const e={"2017年获评“国医大师”称号，为云南中医界之光。":'In 2017, he was awarded the title of "Master of Traditional Chinese Medicine" and is the light of the traditional Chinese medicine community in Yunnan.',"[{ label: '首页', to: '/' }, { label: '传世著作' }]":"[{ label: 'Homepage', to: '/' }, { label: 'Books handed down from ancient times' }]","[{ label: '首页', to: '/' }, { label: '分类检索' }]":"[{ label: 'Home', to: '/' }, { label: 'Category search' }]","[{ label: '首页', to: '/' }, { label: '名医风采' }]":"[{ label: 'Home', to: '/' }, { label: 'Famous Doctor Style' }]","[{ label: '首页', to: '/' }, { label: '杏林医案' }]":"[{ label: 'Home', to: '/' }, { label: 'Xinglin Medical Records' }]","[{ label: '首页', to: '/' }, { label: '资讯动态' }]":"[{ label: 'Home', to: '/' }, { label: 'News' }]","activeCategory = '全部'":"activeCategory = 'All'","activeDepartment = '全部'":"activeDepartment = 'All'","activeEra = '全部'":"activeEra = 'all'","{ 'is-active': activeCategory === '全部' }":"{ 'is-active': activeCategory === 'all' }","{ 'is-active': activeDepartment === '全部' }":"{ 'is-active': activeDepartment === 'all' }","{ 'is-active': activeEra === '全部' }":"{ 'is-active': activeEra === 'all' }","“云南名医馆”数字平台焕新上线，20余位名家医案实现分类检索":`The "Yunnan Famous Doctors' Clinic" digital platform has been relaunched, and more than 20 famous doctors' medical records have been classified and retrieved`,"“夏氏推拿”创立者":`Founder of "Xia's Massage"`,"“宁失其穴，勿失其经”取穴原则详备":'"It is better to lose its acupoints than to lose its meridians" The principle of acupoint selection is detailed',"“方证对应”临证心法系统阐述":'Systematic Explanation of the "Prescription and Syndrome Correspondence" clinical mental method',"《吴佩衡医案》":'"Medical Cases of Wu Peiheng"',"《姚贞白医案》":'"Yao Zhenbai Medical Case"',"《戴丽三医疗经验选》":`"Dai Li's Three Medical Experience Selection"`,"《戴慧芬临床经验》":`"Dai Huifen's Clinical Experience"`,"《滇南本草》药物图谱数字化整理项目启动":'"Southern Yunnan Materia Medica" digital compilation project of drug map launched',"《滇南本草》载滇产药物四百余种，多为他书所未备，如滇重楼、滇黄精、灯盏花等，皆详其性味功用与验方。其书所载方剂多采自民间，简、便、验、廉，至今仍为滇中医家所常用。后世尊先生为“滇南医药之祖”。":'"Southern Yunnan Materia Medica" contains more than 400 kinds of medicines produced in Yunnan, most of which are not included in other books, such as Dian Chonglou, Dian Polygonatum, Erigeron, etc., all of which have detailed descriptions of their properties, taste, functions and prescriptions. The prescriptions contained in his book are mostly collected from the folk, and are simple, convenient, effective and inexpensive. They are still commonly used by Yunnan traditional Chinese medicine practitioners today. Later, Mr. Shizun was regarded as the "ancestor of southern Yunnan medicine".',"《金匮要略》教学名家":'Famous teaching expert on "Synopsis of the Golden Chamber"',"《麻疹发微》":'"Micro Measles"',"一案一世界，一方一乾坤。四诊合参、辨证论治，尽显名家临证心法。":"One case is one world, one party is one universe. The four diagnosis methods combined with ginseng, syndrome differentiation, and treatment fully demonstrate the clinical methods of famous experts.",上一页:"Previous page",下一页:"Next page","下利案 倪某，女，34岁":"Lower interest case: Ni, female, 34 years old","下利案\\n倪某，女，34岁。1983年冬不慎煤气中毒住院抢救，又食生冷而致腹泻，输液3日而下利不止，邀顾氏诊治。日下利十数次，便中带血，干呕烦躁不安，食不下，饮水即吐，面赤肢冷。舌苔淡白，脉微欲绝。治以白通加猪胆汁汤，扶阳育阴：\\n附片100g，干姜24g，葱头3茎，鲜猪胆汁1个，嘱其每服药一次，针刺10余滴兑服。\\n服药1剂，面赤已退，干呕渐平，心烦大减；2剂尽，脉缓有神而诸症渐愈，继以四逆汤、附桂理中汤调理而愈。\\n按：与上案相比，本案除厥逆、脉微、面赤等戴阳证表现外，多了“干呕烦躁不安”之症，恐阳药格拒不纳，因加猪胆汁之苦寒反佐，显示园通之妙。":'Lower interest case\\nNi, female, 34 years old. In the winter of 1983, he was accidentally poisoned by gas and was hospitalized for emergency treatment. He also suffered from diarrhea after eating raw and cold food. After three days of infusion, the pain continued to worsen, so he invited Gu for diagnosis and treatment. There have been more than ten times of diarrhea during the day, with blood in the stool, retching, irritability, inability to eat, vomiting after drinking water, red face and cold limbs. The tongue coating is pale white and the pulse is weak and rapid. Treat with Baitong plus pig bile soup to support yang and nourish yin: 100g of attached tablets, 24g of dried ginger, 3 stalks of green onions, and 1 piece of fresh pig bile. Instruct the patient to take the medicine once and add more than 10 drops of acupuncture. \\nAfter taking 1 dose of medicine, the redness of the face subsided, the retching subsided, and the irritability was greatly reduced; after 2 doses, the pulse was slow and clear, and all the symptoms gradually recovered. Then Sini Decoction and Fugui Lizhong Decoction were used to regulate the condition, and the symptoms were cured. \\nNote: Compared with the previous case, in this case, in addition to the manifestations of Dai Yang syndrome such as convulsions, weak pulse, and red face, there is also the symptom of "retching and irritability". The medicine for fear of Yang is refused, because the bitter cold of pig bile is added as a counter-adjuvant, which shows the wonder of Yuantong.',下痢:"Diarrhea",下肢瘀血阻滞疼痛:"Blood stasis block pain in lower limbs","下肢瘀血阻滞疼痛 （慢性血栓性静脉炎） 杨某，男，三十二岁，昆明…":"Pain caused by blood stasis in lower limbs (chronic thrombophlebitis) Yang, male, 32 years old, Kunming…","下肢瘀血阻滞疼痛 （慢性血栓性静脉炎） 杨某，男，三十二岁，昆明人,省建筑工程局工作。1959年 10月以来，双下肢小腿部血管胀痛,皮色发青,双足冰冷,终 日不能回温，稍多行走,则足软无力，胀痛难忍,步履惟艰。昆 明某医院诊断为“慢性血栓性静脉炎”，疗效不显。该院医生 建议手术治疗，病者不愿接受，因而改服中药。余视之，认为 此系阳气内虚，寒湿凝滞下焦，阳不足以温煦筋脉，遂致寒凝 血瘀，血脉不通而作痛。察其脉沉迟而涩，舌质含青，杂有瘀 斑瘀点，主以温肾助阳，行瘀通络之法。方用： 附片80克，干姜30克，桂枝50克，北细辛10克，伸筋 草10克，桃仁10克（捣），红花8克，甘草8克。 初服则胀痛更甚，再服觉痛麻兼作，疑之，遂来复诊。余 告之此乃阳药温化运行，行瘀通脉之效果，再服无妨。照原方 去桃仁加羌活9克，白芷9克，连服二剂则疼痛渐除,双足回温。三诊，在原方基础上加减散寒除湿活络之剂调治之，数剂 而愈。":'Pain due to blood stasis in the lower limbs (chronic thrombophlebitis) Yang, male, 32 years old, from Kunming, works in the Provincial Construction Engineering Bureau. Since October 1959, the blood vessels in both lower limbs and calves have been swollen and painful, the skin has turned blue, and the feet are cold and unable to warm up all day long. When walking a little more, the feet become weak and weak, the swelling and pain are unbearable, and walking is difficult. A hospital in Kunming diagnosed "chronic thrombophlebitis" and the treatment was not effective. The doctor at the hospital recommended surgical treatment, but the patient was unwilling to accept it, so he took traditional Chinese medicine instead. I looked at it and believed that this was due to internal deficiency of Yang Qi, cold and damp condensation in the lower burner, and Yang was insufficient to warm the muscles and veins, thus causing cold coagulation, blood stasis, and blockage of the blood vessels, resulting in pain. Observe that the pulse is slow and astringent, the tongue is green, and there are bruises and petechiae. The main method is to warm the kidneys, help yang, and remove blood stasis and unblock the collaterals. Recipe: 80 grams of Futian, 30 grams of dried ginger, 50 grams of cinnamon twigs, 10 grams of Asarum, 10 grams of Rhizoma Sinensis, 10 grams of peach kernel (pounded), 8 grams of safflower, and 8 grams of licorice. After taking it for the first time, the swelling and pain became even worse. After taking it again, I felt pain and numbness. I was suspicious, so I came for a follow-up consultation. I told you that this is the warming effect of the yang medicine, which relieves blood stasis and unblocks the meridians. There is no harm in taking it again. According to the original prescription, remove the peach kernels and add 9 grams of Qianhuo and 9 grams of Angelica dahurica. After taking two doses, the pain will gradually disappear and the feet will become warmer. The third diagnosis is based on the original prescription, adding or subtracting agents that dispel cold, remove dampness, and activate collaterals to treat the condition. It will be cured after a few doses.',不孕症:"infertility","不孕症从调经入手之治验与心悟。":"Experience and understanding of the treatment of infertility starting with menstruation regulation.","不孕诸案多从温经暖宫入手，谓胞宫寒者，譬之冰地不生草木，温养冲任而摄精成孕，其理平实而效验确凿。":"Most cases of infertility start with warming the meridians and warming the uterus. It is said that if the uterus is cold, for example, no vegetation grows on the ice, warming and nourishing the Chong Ren will ingest sperm and lead to pregnancy. The theory is simple and the effect is confirmed.",中医内科:"Traditional Chinese Medicine Internal Medicine",中医药大健康智能研发中心:"Traditional Chinese Medicine Big Health Intelligent R&D Center",中国中医科学院中医药信息研究所:"Institute of Traditional Chinese Medicine Information, China Academy of Chinese Medical Sciences",中西医结合:"Integrated Traditional Chinese and Western Medicine",中西医结合肝病名家:"Famous expert on liver disease using integrated traditional Chinese and Western medicine",中西医结合肝病学科带头人:"Leader of the Department of Integrated Traditional Chinese and Western Medicine in Hepatology",中风:"Stroke",中风分期论治与针灸方案完整:"Complete stroke staging and treatment and acupuncture plan","中风急性期、恢复期、后遗症期针灸方案。":"Acupuncture programs for the acute phase, recovery phase, and sequelae phase of stroke.","中风按病程分期论治：急性期开窍启闭，恢复期通络起痿。":"Stroke is treated in stages according to the course of the disease: in the acute stage, the orifices open and close, and in the recovery stage, the meridians are unblocked and flaccidity occurs.",中风针治:"Acupuncture treatment for stroke",临床专著:"clinical monographs",临床医案:"clinical medical records","临证之余主持肝病科研课题多项，主张以现代检测手段印证中医辨证，提高辨证的精准度。":"In addition to clinical diagnosis, he presided over a number of scientific research projects on liver diseases, advocating the use of modern testing methods to confirm TCM syndrome differentiation and improve the accuracy of syndrome differentiation.",临证医案:"Clinical Cases",丹瘀证并多发性脓疽:"Danyu syndrome combined with multiple abscesses","丹瘀证并多发性脓疽 代某，云南省宣威县人，住昆明市珠巩街":"Danyu syndrome combined with multiple abscesses Dai, a native of Xuanwei County, Yunnan Province, lives in Zhugong Street, Kunming City","丹瘀证并多发性脓疽 代某，云南省宣威县人，住昆明市珠巩街。有独生子名延 龄，年三岁，于1937年3月出丹痧，初起发热、咳嗽，目赤多 泪，咽痛不思饮食，面赤而颈项隐隐现点疹，细密而皮肤泛 红，色象不鲜，视其胸背亦然。气吸迫促，沉迷无神，脉浮紧， 指纹色赤偏黯，苔薄白，稍糙，拟桂葛汤稍加薄荷、防风一剂 以托表透疹。 葛根12克，桂枝12克，防风6克，薄荷3克，生姜10 克，小枣5枚，甘草6克。 服后疹又渐出，但色象仍不鲜。此因素禀体弱，正气较 虚，外托无力。继以桂甘姜枣麻辛附子汤扶阳透表主之。 附片30克，桂枝12克，麻茸5克，北细辛3克，小枣6 枚，生姜10克，甘草6克。 服一剂后疹即透出。再剂则遍身疹出稠密成片，色转红 活，白苔已不现，舌色红而娇艳，此为疹毒外出之象，继以桂 枝加附子汤加黄芪治之,服后疹出渐灰，脉静身凉而愈。疹退 后周身脱皮如膜片，肢干脱皮有如蛇蜕之状。 其后不几日，忽于耳下肿硬起核，继之两腋下亦肿硬如 卵，其后于两胯缝处又硬结成包块，渐次大如碗许，皮色不 红,按之皆作痛。身不发热，咳嗽而痰多，舌苔白滑而不渴饮, 此为阴疽而非热毒痈疮可比，故不可施以清热苦寒败毒之 剂，宜以扶阳温化，待脓成之后，再行排脓生肌可望而愈。病 家此时延请西医开刀，流出者仅为清淡脓血水，肿痛稍减，伤 口未敛之时,坐骨下软肉处又忽出现肿硬包块,形如覆碗,其 状如前,于胭弯处又生肿块。患儿形神日趋瘦弱，面色黄黯, 唇舌淡，苔仍白滑。因肿块反复而起，又经多处开刀放脓，体 质虚弱已极，断为难治之证。复易数医，皆因病势较重，且系 独子，均未拟方而去。后又再延余往诊视之。证如前述，乃正 气不充，无力生肌托毒。盖脓为血肉败坏而成，久发不愈，气 血耗伤，施以开刀除脓,其法虽是可行，然只治其标，未达其 本,惟有扶阳辅正，正气内充,脓疽方能根除,余仍坚持温热 大剂，方以四逆汤加味治之： 附片60克，炮姜12克，北口芪15克，败酱草15克，薏苡仁15克，甘草10克，桔梗10克。 连服三剂，肿硬处逐渐转红成脓,表面皮色透亮，外以西 医之法轻施刀术,脓熟皮破，涌溢而出，为带血黏稠之脓液， 味极腥臭。继服四逆汤、茂附汤及阳和汤等温固之剂数十余 剂,始得生肌敛口，脓疽亦不再复作。 四逆汤： 附片60克，干姜10克，炙甘草10克。 芪附汤： 北口芪30克，附片60克。 阳和汤： 熟地黄30克，白芥子3克（炒、研），鹿角胶10克（烊化、分次兑服），姜炭10克，麻黄6克，肉桂6克（研末，泡水兑 入），甘草6克。":"Danyu syndrome combined with multiple abscesses Dai is a native of Xuanwei County, Yunnan Province, living in Zhugong Street, Kunming City. There was an only son named Yan Ling, who was three years old. He developed Dansha in March 1937. He had fever and cough at the beginning, red eyes with many tears, sore throat and no desire to eat. His face was red and there were faint rashes on his neck. His skin was fine and red, and the color was not fresh, even on his chest and back. Shortness of breath, lethargy, floating and tight pulse, red and dark fingerprints, thin white fur, slightly rough, add a dose of Gui Ge Decoction with mint and saposhnikovia to relieve the rash. 12 grams of kudzu root, 12 grams of cinnamon twigs, 6 grams of windbreak, 3 grams of mint, 10 grams of ginger, 5 jujubes, and 6 grams of licorice. After taking it, the rash gradually appeared again, but the color was still there. This factor is due to a weak body, relatively weak righteousness, and weak external support. Follow this with Gui Gan Ginger Zao Ma Xin Aconite Decoction to help yang and penetrate the body. 30 grams of Futian, 12 grams of cinnamon twigs, 5 grams of sesame root, 3 grams of asarum, 6 jujubes, 10 grams of ginger, and 6 grams of licorice. The rash will appear after one dose. After another dose, the rash all over the body becomes dense and becomes flakes, the color turns red and lively, the white coating disappears, and the tongue is red and delicate. This is a sign that the rash poison has gone out. Then use Guizhi plus Fuzi Decoction plus astragalus to treat it. After taking the medicine, the rash gradually becomes gray, the pulse is quiet and the body is cool and healed. After the rash subsided, the skin all over the body peeled off like a membrane, and the limbs peeled off like a snake sloughing off. A few days later, he suddenly developed a hard and swollen nucleation under his ears. Then his armpits also became swollen and hard like eggs. Later, a hard lump formed at the seam of his crotch. It gradually became as big as a bowl. The skin was not red, and it hurt when pressed. No fever, cough with excessive phlegm, white and slippery tongue coating but no thirst for drinks, this is a gangrene, not comparable to a heat-toxin carbuncle. Therefore, it is not possible to use heat-clearing, bitter-cold and detoxifying agents. It is better to use Yang to warm up, wait for the pus to form, then drain the pus and promote muscle growth, and it can be expected to be cured. At this time, the patient asked a Western medicine doctor to perform an operation. The bleeding was only light pus, blood, and water, and the swelling and pain were slightly reduced. When the wound was not closed, a hard and swollen mass suddenly appeared in the soft flesh under the ischium, shaped like a bowl, and the shape was the same as before. Another mass appeared in the crook of the cheek. The child becomes increasingly thin physically and mentally, with a yellowish complexion, pale lips and tongue, and the coating remains white and slippery. Because the lumps appeared repeatedly and multiple incisions were made to release the pus, the body was extremely weak and it was determined to be difficult to treat. Fu Yi visited several doctors, but all of them left without formulating a prescription because the illness was serious and he was an only child. Later, I went to the hospital for further examination. The symptoms are as mentioned above, which is insufficient righteousness and inability to generate muscle and support poison. The pus on the cover is caused by the decay of flesh and blood. If it persists for a long time, Qi and blood will be depleted, so it is necessary to perform surgery to remove the pus. Although this method is feasible, it only treats the symptoms and does not reach the root. Only by supporting Yang and supplementing the righteousness, and filling the body with healthy qi can the abscess be eradicated. If you still insist on warming and large doses, you can treat it with Sini Decoction: 60 grams of Fujiang, 12 grams of Paojiang, 15 grams of Beikou Qi, 15 grams of soybean root, 15 grams of coix seed, 10 grams of licorice, and 10 grams of Platycodon grandiflorum. After taking three doses in a row, the hard and swollen area gradually turned red and turned into pus, and the skin on the surface was translucent. After a gentle operation with Western medicine, the pus was cooked and the skin was broken, and it overflowed, turning into bloody and sticky pus with a very fishy smell. After taking more than dozens of doses of Sini Decoction, Maofu Decoction and Yanghe Decoction, which are warming and fixing agents, the muscles can be tightened and the abscess will no longer reoccur. Sini Decoction: 60 grams of Futian, 10 grams of dried ginger, and 10 grams of Zhigancao. Qifu decoction: 30 grams of Beikou Qi and 60 grams of Fuzhi. Yanghe Decoction: 30 grams of Rehmannia glutinosa, 3 grams of white mustard seeds (stir-fried and grinded), 10 grams of antler gum (boiled and mixed in divided doses), 10 grams of ginger charcoal, 6 grams of ephedra, 6 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 6 grams of licorice.","主张“方证对应”，有是证用是方，不执成见，随证治之。":'He advocates "correspondence of prescriptions and syndromes", using the correct prescription according to the syndrome, not holding on to prejudices, and treating it according to the syndrome.',"主张“治外感如将，治内伤如相”，因势利导，中病即止。":'It is advocated that "treating external symptoms is like generals, and treating internal injuries is like looking at signs." By taking advantage of the situation, internal diseases can be cured.',"主张中西互参、优势互补，以现代手段拓展中医诊疗边界。":"It advocates mutual reference and complementary advantages between China and the West, and using modern means to expand the boundaries of TCM diagnosis and treatment.",主持肝病科研课题多项:"Hosted a number of scientific research projects on liver disease",书籍目录:"book catalog","乳 痈":"Breast carbuncle","乳 痈（二） （乳腺炎） 谢某，女，二十四岁，江苏人，住昆明市光华街":"Breast carbuncle (2) (mastitis) Xie, female, 24 years old, from Jiangsu, living in Guanghua Street, Kunming City","乳 痈（二） （乳腺炎） 谢某，女，二十四岁，江苏人，住昆明市光华街。产后六、 七日，因夜间起坐哺乳而受寒,次日即感不适,恶寒、发热、头 身疼痛，左乳房局部硬结，肿胀疼痛。患者当即赴省级某医院 诊治，服银翘散、荆防败毒散等方加减数剂，发热已退，仍有 恶寒,左乳房硬结红肿不散，反见增大，疼痛加剧。一周后，创 口溃破，流出少许黄色脓液及清淡血水,经西医外科引流消 炎治疗,半月后破口逐渐闭合。但乳房肿块未消散,仍红肿疼 痛,乳汁不通，眠食不佳。每日午后低热,慷燻恶寒,历时一月 未愈。1963年某日延余诊视，病如前述,但见患者面色觥白， 精神疲惫，脉沉细而弱，舌质含青色，苔白厚腻。此乃寒邪失 于宣散，郁闭阻滞经脉血络,迁延未愈,血气耗伤,正气内虚， 无力抗邪外出。局部虽成破口而脓根未除尽，创口虽敛而痈患未能全部消除，此即所谓养痈而遗患也。法当温通里阳，排 脓消肿，散结通乳。方用白通汤加味。 附片150克，干姜15克，川芎10克，当归15克，桔梗10 克，皂角刺9克，赤芍10克，通草6克，细辛5克，白术12 克，葱白3茎。 服二剂后，恶寒、低热已解，体温退至正常，左乳房红肿 硬结渐消。惟乳头右下方复觉灼热、刺痛，局部发红,稍见突 起。此系得阳药温运，气血渐复，血脉疏通，正气抗邪，已有托 脓外出之势。脉沉细而较前和缓有力，舌质青色已退,舌心尚 有腻苔。继以上方加香附9克，连服二剂。腐败之血肉，已化 脓成熟，局部皮肤透亮发红。服三剂后,脓包自行溃破，流出 黄色脓液半盅多，疼痛顿减，红肿消退。再以温经扶阳调补气 血之四逆当归补血汤加白术、杭芍、桂枝、川芎等连进四剂， 脓尽肿消,创口愈合,病告痊瘳。":"Breast carbuncle (2) (Mastitis) Xie, female, 24 years old, from Jiangsu, lives in Guanghua Street, Kunming City. Six or seven days after delivery, she caught cold due to sitting up at night to breastfeed. She felt unwell the next day, with aversion to cold, fever, head and body pain, and local induration, swelling and pain in her left breast. The patient immediately went to a provincial hospital for diagnosis and treatment. He took Yinqiao Powder, Jingfang Baidu Powder and other prescriptions plus subtractive doses. The fever subsided, but he still felt aversion to cold. The left breast was indurated, red and swollen but became enlarged and the pain worsened. A week later, the wound burst, and a little yellow pus and light blood flowed out. After Western medicine surgical drainage and anti-inflammatory treatment, the wound gradually closed after half a month. However, the breast lump did not dissipate and was still red, swollen and painful. Her milk was blocked and she could not sleep or eat well. I had low-grade fever in the afternoon every day, with severe fumigation and aversion to cold, which lasted for a month and did not heal. One day in 1963, during a follow-up examination, the patient's condition was as described above, but the patient's complexion was pale, mentally exhausted, his pulse was deep and thin, his tongue was cyan, and his coating was white and thick. This is caused by the loss of cold evil in Xuan San, which blocks the meridians and blood collaterals, causing them to linger and not heal. The blood and Qi are depleted, and the healthy Qi is internally deficient, making it impossible to fight against the evil going out. Although a local wound is broken, the root of the pus has not been completely removed. Although the wound is constricted, the carbuncle cannot be completely eliminated. This is the so-called nourishing the carbuncle but leaving the disease behind. Fadang warms and unblocks the inner yang, expels pus and reduces swelling, and dissipates stagnation and clears the breasts. Add Baitong soup to taste. 150 grams of Aconite, 15 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of Chuanxiong, 15 grams of angelica, 10 grams of platycodon, 9 grams of saponins, 10 grams of red peony root, 6 grams of Tongcao, 5 grams of asarum, 12 grams of Atractylodes macrocephala, and 3 scallions. After taking two doses, the aversion to cold and low fever were relieved, the body temperature returned to normal, and the redness, swelling and induration of the left breast gradually disappeared. However, the lower right side of the nipple felt hot and stinging again, with local redness and slight protrusion. This system uses Yang medicine to warm and transport Qi and blood, gradually restore Qi and blood, dredge blood vessels, upright Qi resists evil, and has the potential to support the passage of pus. The pulse is deep and thin, gentler and stronger than before, the blue color of the tongue has faded, and there is still greasy coating on the center of the tongue. Following the above, add 9 grams of Cyperus rotundus and take two doses. The rotten flesh and blood has matured into pus, and the local skin is translucent and red. After taking three doses, the pustule burst spontaneously, with more than half a cup of yellow pus flowing out. The pain suddenly subsided, and the redness and swelling subsided. Then, four doses of the Sini Danggui Buxue Decoction, which is used to warm the meridians, nourish yang, regulate qi and nourish blood, plus Atractylodes macrocephala, Hangshao, Guizhi, Ligusticum chuanxiong, etc., can eliminate the pus and swelling, heal the wound, and cure the disease.","乳腺炎案 谢某，女,24岁":"Mastitis case Xie, female, 24 years old","乳腺炎案\\n谢某，女,24岁。产后六七日，因夜间起坐哺乳而受寒，次日即感不适，恶寒、发热，头身疼痛，左乳房局部硬结,肿胀疼痛。当即赴省级某医院诊治，服银翘散、荆防败毒散等方加减数剂，发热已退，仍有恶寒，左乳房硬结红肿不散，反见增大，疼痛加剧。1周后，创口溃破，流出少许黄色脓液及清淡血水，经外科引流消炎治疗，半月后破口逐渐闭合。但乳房肿块未消散，仍红肿疼痛，乳汁不通，眠食不佳。每日午后低热，懔懔恶寒，历时1月未愈，延吴佩衡先生诊视。患者面色㿠白，精神疲惫，脉沉细而弱，舌质含青色，苔白厚腻。此乃寒邪失于宣散，阻滞经脉血络，迁延未愈，血气耗伤，正气内虚，无力抗邪外出。局部虽成破口而脓根未除尽，创口虽敛而痈患未能全部消除，此即所谓养痈而遗患也。法当温通里阳，排脓消肿，散结通乳，方用白通汤加味：\\n附片150g，干姜15g，川芎10g，当归15g，桔梗10g，皂刺9g，赤芍10g，通草6g，细辛5g，白术12g，葱白3茎。\\n2剂后，恶寒、低热已解，体温退至正常，左乳房红肿硬结渐消。惟乳头右下方复觉灼热、刺痛，局部发红，稍见突起。此系得阳药温运，气血渐复，血脉疏通，正气抗邪，已有托脓外除之势。脉沉细而较前和缓有力，舌质青色已退，舌心尚有腻苔。继以上方加香附9g，连服2剂。腐败之血肉已化脓成熟，局部皮肤透亮发红。服3剂后，脓包自行溃破，流出黄色脓液半盅多，疼痛顿减，红肿消退。再以四逆汤合当归补血汤加白术、杭芍、桂枝、川芎等，连进，4剂，脓尽肿消，创口愈合，病告痊瘳。\\n按：此症乳房红肿疼痛，午后低热，容易认作阳热之证。观其“面色㿠白，精神疲惫，脉沉细而弱，舌质含青色，苔白厚腻”，则是一派阴象，因此断为虚阳外越所致，径用附子150g大剂治之，非吴氏这等大家，难以有此手眼。审其用药，含有当归四逆汤之意。":`Mastitis case\\nXie, female, 24 years old. Six or seven days after delivery, she caught cold due to sitting up at night to breastfeed. She felt unwell the next day, with aversion to cold, fever, head and body pain, and local induration, swelling and pain in her left breast. He immediately went to a provincial hospital for diagnosis and treatment. He took Yinqiao Powder, Jingfang Baidu Powder and other prescriptions plus subtracted doses. The fever subsided, but he still had aversion to cold. The left breast was indurated, red and swollen, but became enlarged and the pain worsened. One week later, the wound burst, and a little yellow pus and light blood flowed out. After surgical drainage and anti-inflammatory treatment, the wound gradually closed half a month later. However, the breast lump did not dissipate and was still red, swollen and painful. Her breast milk was blocked and she had trouble sleeping and eating. She developed low-grade fever and aversion to cold every afternoon in the afternoon. It lasted for one month and did not heal. She was referred to Mr. Wu Peiheng for consultation. The patient's complexion is pale, mentally exhausted, his pulse is thin and weak, his tongue has a bluish color, and his fur is white and thick. This is caused by the loss of cold pathogenic dispersion, which blocks the meridians and blood collaterals, causing them to linger and not heal. The blood and Qi are depleted, the healthy Qi is internally deficient, and it is unable to resist the pathogenic factors. Although a local wound is broken, the root of the pus has not been completely removed. Although the wound is constricted, the carbuncle cannot be completely eliminated. This is the so-called nourishing the carbuncle but leaving the disease behind. Fadang warms and clears the yang, drains pus and reduces swelling, disperses knots and clears the breasts. Add the Baitong decoction with the following flavors: 150g of Atractylodes, 15g of dried ginger, 10g of Ligusticum chuanxiong, 15g of Angelica sinensis, 10g of Platycodon, 9g of Saponaria sinensis, 10g of red peony root, 6g of Tongcao, 5g of Asarum, 12g of Atractylodes macrocephala, and 3 scallion stalks. \\nAfter 2 doses, the aversion to cold and low fever were relieved, the body temperature returned to normal, and the redness, swelling and induration of the left breast gradually disappeared. However, the lower right side of the nipple felt hot and stinging again, with local redness and slight protrusion. This system uses yang medicine to warm and transport the qi and blood, gradually restore the qi and blood, unblock the blood vessels, strengthen the qi and resist evil, and have the potential to remove pus. The pulse is deep and thin, gentler and stronger than before, the blue color of the tongue has faded, and there is still greasy coating on the center of the tongue. Following the above, add 9g of Cyperus rotundus and take 2 doses. The rotten flesh and blood has suppurated and matured, and the local skin is translucent and red. After taking 3 doses, the pustule burst spontaneously, with more than half a cup of yellow pus flowing out. The pain suddenly subsided, and the redness and swelling subsided. Then take Sini Decoction combined with Danggui Buxue Decoction plus Atractylodes, Hangshao, Guizhi, Chuanxiong, etc. for 4 doses, the pus and swelling will disappear, the wound will heal, and the disease will be cured. \\nNote: This disease has red, swollen and painful breasts and low fever in the afternoon, which is easily recognized as a sign of Yang heat. Judging from his "white complexion, mental fatigue, deep and weak pulse, cyan tongue, and white and thick greasy coating", it was a yin sign. Therefore, it was concluded that it was caused by deficient yang and external overflow, and he was treated with a large dose of 150g of aconite. It would be difficult for anyone other than Wu to have such skill and eyes. After reviewing the medicine, it contains the meaning of Danggui Sini Decoction.`,"二十位云岭名家，六百年薪火相传。从扶阳宗师到针灸圣手，以仁心仁术泽被苍生。":"Twenty famous Yunling masters have been passed down from generation to generation for six hundred years. From the master of Fuyang to the master of acupuncture, he has benefited the people with his benevolent heart and benevolent skills.","二十位云岭名家，自明代兰茂至当代名宿，各擅专长，蔚为大观。":"Twenty famous Yunling masters, from Lan Mao in the Ming Dynasty to contemporary celebrities, each specializes in their own expertise and is a sight to behold.","于江震，男，55岁，中共西南局书记处书记":"Yu Jiangzhen, male, 55 years old, Secretary of the Southwest Bureau Secretariat of the Communist Party of China","于江震，男，55岁，中共西南局书记处书记。1966年4月16日初诊。患慢性肺源性心脏病多年，经常住院治疗，去冬受寒后症状加重，住院经各种抗菌消炎针药治疗后病趋加重。由专家会诊组进行抢救，病势危笃。吴佩衡受云南省委派遣，由儿子吴生元陪同，紧急飞赴成都参加抢救。\\n4月16日抵达病房，见患者面部浮肿晦黯，口唇乌黑，十指连甲青乌，神疲，嗜卧懒言，胸闷，心悸气短，动则喘甚。喉间痰鸣，咳痰无力，恶寒发热，体温37.6℃，汗出肢冷，下肢浮肿过膝，纳呆拒食不思饮，终日吸氧，有时烦躁不安，咳喘甚时小便自遗，大便溏而不畅。脉微欲绝，舌紫黯苔白滑而腻。\\n此系肺寒脾湿日久，累及心肾，致使心肾阳气衰极，已成肺脾心肾之阳俱虚之候。急宜扶阳化饮，强心温肾，以大回阳饮加味：\\n附片200g，干姜30g，上肉桂10g（泡水兑入），法半夏15g，广陈皮10g，茯苓20g，甘草6g。4剂，每日1剂，日服2次。\\n4剂后咳喘渐减，咳岀较多黏痰，胸闷，心悸减，小便已能控制。尚嗜卧无神，不思饮食，喉间仍有痰阻，余症无明显改善。脉微细，舌紫黯稍减，苔白滑腻稍退。此药不胜病，仍以上方加重剂量治之：\\n附片400g，干姜40g，上肉桂12g（泡水兑入），法半夏15g，广陈皮10g，茯苓30g，白蔻仁10g，甘草10g。4剂。\\n三诊：服上方后，吐痰已不费力，吐较多脓痰；胸闷、心悸、喘促等症大为减轻，面黯唇乌减，仅短时吸氧，可平卧，已思食，小便较畅，大便已不溏。唯阳神尚虚，仍少气懒言。上方再加重附片剂量为500g，稍佐杏仁8g。4剂。\\n半月来随症加减，附片剂量增为600g，脓痰转为大量痰涎，各症大为减轻，纳渐增，已不吸氧，口唇已不紫黯，面色渐转红润，可在室内活动。\\n经一月余的紧张抢救，患者已脱离危险，各项指标均改善趋于正常，唯咽部痰液培养有绿脓杆菌，认为仍有炎症，重新用抗生素，并给服重庆中医研究所同道所拟之剂，内有人参、黄芪、黄连、黄芩、天葵子等。\\n2日后病情反复，原有之各症一一出现，且恶寒发热，体温38.6℃。专家组焦急万分，又邀请吴氏“大会诊”。是时患者咳喘频作，气短难续，喉间痰声辘辘，面唇复现紫黯，各种症状如初，且四肢逆冷，二便不禁。脉沉细而紧滑，舌晦黯苔白滑而腻。此为心肾之阳未复，复遭寒凉，致阳气虚衰，饮邪上泛。当回阳化饮，强心固肾为治。急以大剂回阳饮加味：\\n附片400g，干姜40g，上肉桂15g，桂枝15g，茯苓30g，法半夏20g，吴萸6g，甘草10g。每日1剂，日服2次。\\n连日巡诊，附片逐日增至每日800g，随证酌加公丁、砂仁等。\\n10余日后，各症减轻，已不咳喘，饮食正常，精神渐增，二便调，活动自如，每日可外出散步。患者病情稳定，日趋康复。（顾树华提供）按：此案症情严重，阳虚已极，吴氏径以大回阳饮投治，因痰湿壅滞而合以二陈汤，附片逐日增加，最后加至每日800g，凸显吴氏胆识。其间曾有曲折反复，吴氏薏眼明辨，据理力争，终于挽此重症。请参看“吴佩衡逸事”中“胆识救治于书记”一节。":`Yu Jiangzhen, male, 55 years old, secretary of the Secretariat of the Southwest Bureau of the Communist Party of China. First diagnosis on April 16, 1966. I have suffered from chronic pulmonary heart disease for many years and was often hospitalized for treatment. The symptoms worsened after catching cold in the winter. After being treated in the hospital with various antibacterial and anti-inflammatory injections, the disease became worse. An expert consultation team conducted rescue operations, and his condition was critical. Wu Peiheng was dispatched by the Yunnan Provincial Party Committee, accompanied by his son Wu Shengyuan, and flew to Chengdu urgently to participate in the rescue. \\nWhen I arrived at the ward on April 16, I found that the patient's face was swollen and dull, his lips were black, his nails were blue, he was tired, he was prone to lying down and talking lazily, chest tightness, palpitations, shortness of breath, and severe wheezing when moving. Phlegm in the throat, weakness in expectoration, aversion to cold and fever, body temperature 37.6°C, sweating and cold limbs, edema of the lower limbs above the knees, indigestion, refusal to eat and drink, inhalation of oxygen all day long, sometimes irritability, coughing and wheezing, sometimes spontaneous urination, and loose stools. The pulse is weak, the tongue is purple, dark and the coating is white, slippery and greasy. \\nThis is caused by long-term coldness in the lungs and dampness in the spleen, which affects the heart and kidneys, causing the yang energy of the heart and kidneys to decline to the extreme, and it has become a condition where both the yang of the lungs, spleen, heart and kidneys are deficient. In an emergency, it is advisable to drink the drink to help yang, strengthen the heart and warm the kidneys, and add the Dahuiyang drink with the following flavors:\\n200g of Fuyang, 30g of dried ginger, 10g of cinnamon (soaked in water and mixed in), 15g of Pinellia ternata, 10g of Citrus tangerine peel, 20g of Poria, and 6g of licorice. 4 doses, 1 dose per day, 2 times a day. \\nAfter 4 doses, the coughing and wheezing gradually subsided, more sticky phlegm was coughed up, chest tightness, palpitations subsided, and urination was now under control. He is still addicted to sleeping and lacks energy, and does not want to eat. There is still phlegm obstruction in the throat, and the remaining symptoms have not been significantly improved. The pulse is fine and thready, the purple color of the tongue is slightly reduced, and the white and greasy coating is slightly reduced. The disease is not cured by this medicine, but the above-mentioned aggravating dosage is still used to treat the disease:\\n400g of Fu Pian, 40g of dried ginger, 12g of cassia cinnamon (soaked in water and mixed in), 15g of Pinellia ternata, 10g of Citrus tangerine peel, 30g of Poria cocos, 10g of white cardamom kernels, and 10g of licorice. 4 doses. \\nThird diagnosis: After taking the medicine, spitting becomes effortless and more purulent phlegm is produced; chest tightness, palpitations, shortness of breath and other symptoms are greatly alleviated, the face becomes dull, the lips are darkened, and oxygen can only be breathed for a short period of time. Only Yang Shen is still weak and still lacks energy and is lazy to talk. The dosage of additional tablets above is 500g, with 8g of almonds. 4 doses. \\nIn the past half month, the dosage of the tablets was increased to 600g. The purulent sputum turned into a large amount of phlegm and saliva, and the symptoms were greatly alleviated. My appetite gradually increased, I no longer breathed oxygen, my lips were no longer purple and dark, my complexion gradually turned rosy, and I could move around indoors. \\nAfter more than a month of intensive rescue, the patient was out of danger, and all indicators improved to normal. However, the pharyngeal sputum culture showed Pseudomonas aeruginosa. It was believed that inflammation was still present, so antibiotics were restarted and the medicine prepared by colleagues from the Chongqing Institute of Traditional Chinese Medicine was given, which included ginseng, astragalus, coptis, skullcap, and geranium seed. \\nThe condition recurred 2 days later, with all the original symptoms appearing one by one. She also had aversion to cold and fever, with a body temperature of 38.6°C. The expert team was extremely anxious and invited Wu for a "conventional consultation". At this time, the patient had frequent coughing and wheezing, shortness of breath, gurgling phlegm in the throat, dark purple color on the face and lips, all the symptoms were the same as before, and the limbs were cold and uncontrollable. The pulse is deep, thin, tight and slippery, and the tongue is dark, dark and has white, slippery and greasy coating. This is because the yang of the heart and kidneys has not recovered, and the cold and coolness are encountered again, resulting in deficiency and decline of yang qi, and excessive drinking evil. When the Yang is restored, the drink is used to strengthen the heart and strengthen the kidneys. Urgently use a large dose of Huiyang drink to add flavor:\\n400g of Futian, 40g of dried ginger, 15g of cinnamon, 15g of cinnamon twig, 30g of poria, 20g of pinellia, 6g of Wuyu, and 10g of licorice. 1 dose per day, 2 times a day. \\nI have been doing rounds for several days, and the tablets have been increased to 800g per day, and the dosage of fenugreek, amomum villosum, etc. can be added according to the condition. \\nMore than 10 days later, all symptoms were relieved, he no longer coughed and wheezed, his diet was normal, his energy gradually increased, his bowel movements were adjusted, he could move freely, and he could go out for a walk every day. The patient's condition is stable and he is recovering day by day. (Provided by Gu Shuhua) Note: The condition of this case was serious and the yang deficiency was extremely severe. Wu Shi Jing treated it with Da Hui Yang Drink. Due to phlegm-dampness stagnation, he combined with Erchen Decoction. The pills were increased day by day, and finally increased to 800g per day, which highlighted Wu's courage. There were twists and turns during this period, but Wu's eyes were clear and she argued with reason, finally saving her from this serious illness. Please refer to the section "The Courage Saved the Secretary" in "The Anecdotes of Wu Peiheng".`,云南中医儿科名家:"Yunnan Traditional Chinese Medicine Paediatrics Expert",云南中医名家:"Famous Traditional Chinese Medicine Masters from Yunnan",云南中医学院原院长:"Former Dean of Yunnan College of Traditional Chinese Medicine","云南中医学院原院长 · 内妇名家":"Former President of Yunnan College of Traditional Chinese Medicine · Famous Housewife",云南中医学院教授:"Professor at Yunnan College of Traditional Chinese Medicine",云南中医学院首任院长:"The first president of Yunnan College of Traditional Chinese Medicine",云南中医药大学:"Yunnan University of Traditional Chinese Medicine",云南会泽:"Huize, Yunnan",云南名医馆:"Yunnan Famous Physicians","云南名医馆 · 云岭杏林 | 名医 · 医案 · 著作分类检索":"Yunnan Famous Doctors Hospital · Yunling Xinglin | Famous Doctors · Medical Records · Book Classification Search","云南名医馆 · 云岭杏林数字平台":"Yunnan Famous Medical Center · Yunling Xinglin Digital Platform","云南名医馆 · 典藏":"Yunnan Famous Medical Center · Collection",云南四大名医之一:"One of the four famous doctors in Yunnan","云南四大名医之一 · 姚氏妇科传人":"One of the four famous doctors in Yunnan · Successor of Yao’s gynecology department","云南四大名医之一 · 扶阳大家":"One of the four famous doctors in Yunnan · Fuyang Master","云南四大名医之一 · 温病大家":"One of the four famous doctors in Yunnan · Everyone with febrile diseases","云南四大名医之一 · 经方名家":"One of the Four Famous Doctors in Yunnan · Famous Classical Prescription Master",云南嵩明:"Yunnan Songming",云南推拿学科带头人:"Yunnan Massage Discipline Leader",云南昆明:"Kunming, Yunnan",云南省中医中药研究院研究员:"Researcher at Yunnan Academy of Traditional Chinese Medicine",云南针灸名家:"Yunnan Acupuncture Famous Master",云岭医派:"Yunling Medical School",云岭杏林:"Yunling Apricot Forest","云木香、香茅、艾纳香等芳香药物的功用与配伍。":"Functions and compatibility of aromatic medicines such as agarwood, citronella, and incense.","云木香行气止痛，书中详其与砂仁、陈皮配伍治脘腹胀满之法；香茅煎汤浴身，可祛风除湿，为滇民夏月常备之物；石菖蒲开心窍、化痰浊，合远志治健忘怔忡。":"Yunmuxiang promotes qi and relieves pain. The book details how to use it with amomum villosum and tangerine peel to treat abdominal distention; lemongrass decoction for body bathing can dispel wind and dehumidify, and is a common food for Yunnan people in summer; Acorus calamus can open up the mind, resolve phlegm and turbidity, and combine with polygala root to treat forgetfulness and fatigue.","产后失血 苏某，女，三十五岁，住昆明某医院妇产科":"Postpartum blood loss Su, female, 35 years old, admitted to the obstetrics and gynecology department of a hospital in Kunming","产后失血 苏某，女，三十五岁，住昆明某医院妇产科。分娩第三胎, 产后子宫收缩无力，遂致流血不止。经医院施以针药及输血 治疗，出血仍不见终止。病已三日，病势日趋危重，于1952年 某日邀余前往会诊。患者卧床，已人事不省，面色苍白，目眶 凹陷，形容憔悴，呼吸微弱，唇干色淡。掰开口唇，见齿枯舌淡 而少津，脉细弱沉伏欲绝，手足冰冷。阴道流血仍未止，色淡 而清，浸透垫褥。此系阳弱气虚，气不摄血，血不归经所致。患 者失血过多，气血两亏，病势沉重，危在旦夕。若继续出血，恐 有气随血脱之虑。补血及输血之法，固属必要,然已虚之阳无 力摄血，无力生血,血亦不能归经循行。此证急当扶阳益气， 方能止血固脱。拟大剂回阳饮加味主之。 附片120克，炮黑姜15克，上肉桂15克（研末，泡水兑 入），黄芪30克，当归15克，炒艾9克，炙甘草9克。 因病情较重,嘱早晚各煎服一剂,多次徐徐喂之。 次日复诊。昨日方药浓煎频频喂服，服后，今日流血已减 其半，神识恢复，能饮葡萄糖水二、三口，呼吸稍觉平稳，手足 开始回温。唇、舌仍淡，脉沉细弱，已不似昨日欲绝之状。此阳 气已回，有望生机。继上方加阿胶珠9克,炒白术9克连服五 剂，流血已止，神识清明、面色渐润，并能背靠床头坐卧，进牛 奶及半流质饮食。惟气血尚虚，阳神尚弱，久坐则感头昏无 力，夜寐多梦，气短心慌，声低懒言。舌质已稍现红润色，脉沉 细而缓，两尺较弱。拟四逆汤加味治之。 附片90克，干姜12克，砂仁9克，黄芪24克，白术15克，茯苓15克，补骨脂12克，甘草3克。 上方连服八剂，患者食思倍增，面色润泽,精神恢复。继 后以四逆当归补血汤及黄芪桂枝五物汤数剂调理善后，住 院一月痊愈出院。其后于1964年相遇，询及十余年来，身体 健康。":"Postpartum blood loss Su, female, 35 years old, was admitted to the obstetrics and gynecology department of a hospital in Kunming. After giving birth to her third child, the uterus contracted weakly after delivery, resulting in non-stop bleeding. The hospital administered injections and blood transfusions, but the bleeding still did not stop. He had been ill for three days and became increasingly critical. One day in 1952, he invited me for consultation. The patient was bedridden and unconscious, with a pale complexion, sunken eyes, haggard appearance, weak breathing, and dry and pale lips. When he opened his lips, he saw that his teeth were dry, his tongue was pale and there was little fluid, his pulse was thin and weak, his hands and feet were cold. The vaginal bleeding has not stopped, the color is light and clear, and the mattress is soaked. This is caused by weak yang and qi deficiency, the qi does not absorb the blood, and the blood does not return to the menstruation. The patient lost too much blood, was deficient in both qi and blood, and was seriously ill and in critical condition. If the bleeding continues, there is a fear that the Qi will escape with the blood. Methods of blood replenishment and blood transfusion are absolutely necessary, but the deficient yang cannot absorb blood, produce blood, and the blood cannot return to the meridians. If this syndrome is urgent, you should strengthen Yang and replenish Qi to stop bleeding and cure prolapse. It is recommended to use a large dose of Huiyang Drink with added flavor. 120 grams of Aconite slices, 15 grams of black ginger, 15 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 30 grams of astragalus, 15 grams of angelica root, 9 grams of fried mugwort, and 9 grams of roasted licorice. Because the condition is serious, he is advised to decoct and take one dose in the morning and evening, and feed him slowly several times. Follow-up visit the next day. I decocted the prescription and took it frequently yesterday. After taking it, today's bleeding has been reduced by half, my consciousness has recovered, I can drink two or three sips of glucose water, my breathing feels slightly stable, and my hands and feet have begun to warm up. The lips and tongue are still pale, and the pulse is deep and thin, no longer like the desperate state of yesterday. This Yang Qi has returned and is expected to be revitalized. After adding 9 grams of donkey hide gelatin beads and 9 grams of stir-fried Atractylodes macrocephala for five consecutive doses, the bleeding stopped, the consciousness became clear, the complexion gradually became moist, and the patient was able to sit and lie with his back on the bedside and take milk and semi-liquid diet. However, the qi and blood are still weak, and the yang spirit is still weak. If you sit for a long time, you will feel dizzy and weak, have many dreams during the night, shortness of breath, palpitation, and low voice and laziness. The tongue is slightly red, the pulse is thin and slow, and is weak at two feet. It is treated by adding Sini Decoction. 90 grams of Futian, 12 grams of dried ginger, 9 grams of amomum villosum, 24 grams of astragalus, 15 grams of Atractylodes, 15 grams of Poria, 12 grams of psoralen, and 3 grams of licorice. After taking eight doses of the medicine, the patient's food cravings doubled, his complexion was moist, and his spirit was restored. After several doses of Sini Danggui Buxue Decoction and Astragalus Guizhi Wuwu Decoction, the patient recovered and was discharged from the hospital after being hospitalized for one month. Later, they met in 1964 and asked about his good health for more than ten years.","产后诸疾本产后多虚多瘀之旨，养血兼逐瘀，慎用苦寒，恐伤生生之气，其用药之谨慎如此。":"Postpartum diseases: The main purpose of this medicine is to nourish blood and remove blood stasis due to excessive postpartum deficiency and blood stasis. It is bitter and cold when used with caution, as it may damage the qi of life. This is how to use the medicine with caution.","产后诸疾本产后宜温之旨，养血化瘀，慎用苦寒攻伐，而于生化汤之加减运用尤具心得。":"Postpartum diseases should be treated with warmth after delivery to nourish blood and remove blood stasis, and be careful to use bitter and cold medicines to attack them, and I have special experience in the addition and subtraction of Shenghua Decoction.","产褥热案 罗某，女，31岁，云南人":"Puerperal fever case Luo, female, 31 years old, from Yunnan","产褥热案\\n罗某，女，31岁，云南人。1959年1月30日初诊：患糖尿病多年，临产住某医院。剖腹产后20余日，一直高热不退，服西药、注射抗生素，体温未退，人弱已极。寒入少阴，格阳于外，下午体温39.8℃，小腹冷痛，食欲不振，大便溏泻色绿，脉沉而紧，舌苔白滑而厚腻。此乃少阴寒化之证，急宜扶阳收纳主之，否则阳脱危殆费治。以白通汤加肉桂主之：附片150g，筠姜80g，上肉桂（研末，泡水兑入）10g，葱白6茎。\\n二诊：服前方2剂后，六脉均已和缓，发热已退，脉静身凉，舌苔已退七八，唯里寒未净，小腹作痛，稍能食，人无神，以四逆汤加味治之：\\n附片100g，吴茱萸8g，筠姜30g，茯苓20g，北细辛8g，生草8g。\\n服此方4剂后，诸症悉退，食增神健，痊愈出院。（顾树华提供）":"Puerperal fever case\\nLuo, female, 31 years old, from Yunnan. First diagnosis on January 30, 1959: She had been suffering from diabetes for many years and was admitted to a certain hospital during labor. More than 20 days after the caesarean section, the fever persisted. She took western medicine and injected antibiotics, but her body temperature did not go down and she was extremely weak. Cold enters Shaoyin and Yang is outside. In the afternoon, the body temperature is 39.8°C. The lower abdomen is cold and painful, loss of appetite, loose stools and diarrhea, green color, deep and tight pulse, and white, slippery and thick greasy tongue coating. This is a sign of Shaoyin becoming cold. It is urgent to support the Yang and absorb it, otherwise the Yang will be out of danger and it will be very expensive to treat. Use Baitong soup with cinnamon as the main ingredient: 150g of Fu slices, 80g of Junjiang, 10g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix in), and 6 white scallions. \\nSecond diagnosis: After taking 2 doses of the above medicine, the six pulses have softened, the fever has subsided, the pulse is quiet and cool, and the tongue coating has retreated seven or eight times, but the internal cold is not clear, the lower abdomen is painful, and the person can't eat a little, and the person is lethargic. The disease is treated with Sini Decoction: \\nAdditional Sini Decoction: 100g, Evodia 8g, Junjiang 30g, Poria 20g, Asarum 8g, Shengcao 8g. \\nAfter taking 4 doses of this prescription, all symptoms subsided, food increased, mental health increased, and he was discharged from the hospital. (Provided by Gu Shuhua)","代某，3岁":"Dai, 3 years old","代某，3岁。1937年3月出丹痧，初起发热、咳嗽，目赤多泪，咽痛不思饮食；面赤而颈项隐隐现点疹，细密而皮肤泛红，色象不鲜，视其胸背亦然；气吸迫促，沉迷无神；脉浮紧，指纹色赤偏黯；苔薄白，稍糙。拟桂葛汤稍加薄荷、防风以托表透疹：\\n葛根12g，桂枝12g，防风6g，薄荷3g，生姜10g，小枣5枚，甘草6g。\\n服后疹又渐出，但色象仍不鲜。此因素禀体弱，正气较虚，外托无力。继以桂甘姜枣麻辛附子汤扶阳透表主之：\\n附片30g，桂枝12g，麻茸5g，北辛3g，小枣6枚，生姜10g，甘草6g。\\n服1剂后疹即透出；再剂则遍身疹出稠密成片，色转红活，白苔已不现，舌色红而娇艳，此为疹毒外出之象；继以桂枝加	附子汤加黄芪治之，服后疹出渐灰，脉静身凉而愈。疹退后周身脱皮如膜片，肢干脱皮有如蛇蜕之状。":"Dai, 3 years old. Dansha appeared in March 1937. At the beginning, he had fever, cough, red eyes and tearful eyes, sore throat and no desire to eat. His face was red and there were faint rashes on his neck. The skin was fine and red, and the color was not fresh, even on his chest and back. He had shortness of breath and was lethargic. His pulse was floating and tight, and his fingerprints were red and dark in color. His fur was thin and white, slightly rough. Gui Ge Decoction with a little mint and fangfeng to relieve rash:\\nPudzu root 12g, cinnamon twig 12g, fangfeng 6g, mint 3g, ginger 10g, 5 jujubes, licorice 6g. \\nAfter taking the medicine, the rash gradually appeared again, but the color was still there. This factor is due to a weak body, relatively weak righteousness, and weak external support. Followed by Gui Gan Jiang Zao Ma Xin Aconite Decoction to help yang and penetrate the table: \\n30g of Aconite slices, 12g of cinnamon twigs, 5g of moose, 3g of Beixin, 6 jujubes, 10g of ginger, and 6g of licorice. \\nAfter taking 1 dose, the rash will appear; after taking another dose, the rash will appear all over the body and form dense patches. After the rash subsides, the skin all over the body peels like a membrane, and the limbs peel like a snake sloughing off.","以「名医 · 医案 · 著作」分类检索，让经典惠及当代临床。":'Search by category "Famous Doctors·Medical Records·Writings" to benefit classics from contemporary clinical practice.',传世医案:"Medical records handed down from ancient times",传世著作:"Works","传世著作 | 云南名医馆":"Works handed down from generation to generation | Yunnan Famous Medical Center",传承精华:"The essence of inheritance",伤寒坏病:"Typhoid fever",伤寒救逆篇:"Chapter on rescuing typhoid fever",伤寒杂病:"Typhoid and miscellaneous diseases",伤寒病:"Typhoid fever",伤寒病少阴寒化证:"Typhoid fever Shaoyin cold syndrome","伤寒病少阴寒化证 曾某，男，17岁，当时昆明市市长曾某之子":"Typhoid fever with Shaoyin cold syndrome Zeng, male, 17 years old, son of Zeng, the mayor of Kunming at the time","伤寒病少阴寒化证 曾某，男，十七岁，住昆明市环城东路":"Typhoid fever syndrome of Shaoyin-cold transformation Zeng, male, 17 years old, lives at Huancheng East Road, Kunming City","伤寒病少阴寒化证 曾某，男，十七岁，住昆明市环城东路。始因饮食后受寒 起病,发热,恶寒,头体痛,延某中医诊视，以清凉解表药二剂 无效，当即送入本市西山脚下高峣某医院住院治疗。住院已 十九日，施以针药，发热虽退，然病势则日益沉重，延请数医 会诊，一致诊断为“肠伤寒”且有肠出血或肠穿孔之虞，决定 施用输血方法挽救。输血后病势未减，愈见危笃，竟宣告无 救，遂于1943年10月25日延余诊视。余到达该医院，已是 晚间九时，询知患者病已十九日，身已不发热，但腹中鼓胀， 小腹疼痛,不时呻吟,小便短赤,大便有七、八日不通,饮食不 进，日夜眼不交睫，卧床身不能转侧，但见护士随时以矿泉水 与饮之。舌苔白滑而厚腻,不渴饮，脉搏弦紧,重按则无力而 空。诊毕，当即告以病势十分危重，系伤寒坏病，病邪深入少 阴之脏寒证，阳气内虚，阴寒太盛,寒水阴气内结如冰霜，腹 内阴霾四布，发热虽退但里寒已极。二便不通，乃系阴寒凝结，真阳大虚，无力运行,非热结之证可比也。一线生阳有将 脱之势，病势垂危，颇为费治。惟有扶阳抑阴温化之法，使在 上之寒水邪阴，由口中吐出，中下之寒水邪阴，由二便排泄使 除，阳回阴退，方可转危为安。拟以仲景通脉四逆汤加吴茱 萸、上桂治之。并告知病家，倘若服药后发生呕吐涎痰或大便 泻下切勿惊疑,为病除之兆,一线生机,可望挽回。 白附片160克，干姜30克，上肉桂16克（研末，泡水兑 入），茯苓26克，吴茱萸6克，甘草6克。 10月26日再诊。昨服上方后，旋即呕吐涎水碗许，系病 除之兆。脉搏弦紧已退而转和缓，大便溏泻一次，小便解三 次，惟小腹尚痛，时作时缓。缘病程日久，阳神太亏，里寒太 重，虽已见效,然病重药轻，力不胜病,犹兵不胜敌,犹幸气不 喘,痰不鸣，手足温暖,脉和缓较有神,继以大剂扶阳温化,务 使阳回阴退，渐可转危为安。 白附片260克，干姜60克，吴茱萸20克，上肉桂16克 （研末，泡水兑入），公丁香6克，茯苓30克，西砂仁6克。 10月27日三诊。昨日清晨服药后,又呕吐涎水约两碗， 下午服药后又吐一次,大便泻利数次,均属“冰霜化行”,病毒 邪阴由上下窍道溃退。舌苔仍厚腻，舌质红活,面唇色泽亦转 红润，体温如常,脉搏和缓较有神根,腹胀微痛，鼓胀已减去 十之六、七。大关已过，然病久阳神太亏,邪阴尚未除净，仍以 大剂扶阳辅正主之。 白附片300克，干姜60克，上肉桂16克（研末，泡水兑 入），甜马槟榔6克（去壳，捣），吴茱萸6克，台鸟药4克，西 砂仁6克，茯苓30克。 10月28日四诊，服药后昨日夜共排泄大便十六次，每次 多少不一,今晨又大便二次,均为夹水分之稀薄粪便,始而色乌如酱，今晨渐转黄色，此系胃中生阳渐复之兆。体温37℃, 脉搏每分钟80次。今日解小便六次，色淡黄而清,但于每次 小便时,均觉茎中刺痛，良由病毒下泄刺激作痛，非热盛之证 可比也。昨夜见渴喜热饮，缘腹中阴霾四布，水邪滔天，今得 离照当空，阴霾四散，寒水化行,惟以阳神太虚，无力化气生 津，滋润缺乏，故喜热饮灌溉滋养百骸，非热甚灼阴之渴饮 也。偶尔喜食冷物者，厥阴之气不相顺接，阴阳不和也。矢气 连连，府道已通,浊气下降也。病状虽已大减，险象已脱，惟肝 肾之阴气尚未肃清，元阳正气尚未全复，故左腹留有痞块作 痛。最可欣慰者，今晨已略进食物,显见胃气转和，生阳来复， 可期痊愈矣。大病初退,贵宜调护谨慎,勿使过食伤胃，过劳 伤神，避受风寒为要。仍以扶阳辅正主之。 白附片300克，干姜50克，茯苓30克，薏苡仁16克，上 肉桂18克（研末，泡水兑入），波蔻仁3克（捣），西砂仁6克 （捣），甘草10克，白胡椒2.6克（捣）。 另合服乌梅丸二枚。 10月29日五诊。脉已和缓，每分钟72次，体温37.6℃， 大便六次。小便已较清长而淡黄，茎中微觉刺痛，腹中痞块已 全消，面色渐转红润，鼻准亦现光泽,舌苔已退去十之六、七， 胃口已开，食量较增，腹痛已愈，此时则见遍体出白寤。大病 已退，元阳渐复，可逐步转入善后调养,病退药减，仍以扶阳 辅正主之。并嘱其忌服生冷水果、酸寒食物、嫩鸡蛋、甜酒及 一切黏腻之品，慎风寒，节饮食为调护之责，则可望期而日复 健康矣。 白附片160克，干姜30克，茯苓16克，上肉桂10克（研 末，泡水兑入），波蔻仁5克（捣），薏苡仁16克，甘草6克，桂 圆肉5克，大枣3枚。 10月30日六诊。今晨体温正常，脉搏和缓，舌根仍白腻, 大便二次,稀溏量少,小便淡黄清长,腹中微觉膜胀不舒,食 量日增，考虑其脾胃尚虚，消化力弱，每餐均与定量粥食。因 大病初愈,余寒邪阴尚未肃清,元阳正气亦未全复,仍坚守扶 阳辅正之大法，数剂即克，决无生变之虑。拟方之后，书引四 言一首以为志。 阴云四合日光微，转眼真龙便欲飞， 辛甘化阳离火现,何愁大地不春归。 白附片300克，干姜50克，甘草10克，上肉桂16克（研 末，泡水兑入），吴茱萸6克，波蔻仁6克（捣），茯苓30克，白 胡椒3克（捣）。 10月31日七诊。今晨体温、脉搏均正常，便泻已止，此乃 腹中病毒陈埜已排泄殆净，小便亦清长，腹中胀痛已全消，食 量较佳,惟舌根尚白腻，寒湿余邪尚未全清，元阳正气尚待继 续温扶。拟方： 白附片300克，干姜30克，甘草10克，上肉桂10克（研 末，泡水兑入），西砂仁10克（捣），薏苡仁10克。 11月1日八诊。舌腻苔已退，稍有薄白苔，脉搏、体温正 常,小便清长，腹部宽舒，无他痛楚，食量日佳,每餐节制仅食 至六、七分，以免过食有伤脾胃，睡眠转佳，惟阳神初复，尚不 能固守而多梦，正气未充，起坐感到头昏足软无力。仍以扶阳 辅正，使真阳旺盛，邪阴消尽为度。温扶真阳绝不会伤其真 阴，真阳回复反而有助于滋生真阴也。此即“阳生阴长”、“天 一生水”的道理。阴阳调平则诸证可愈。 白附片300克，干姜36克，甘草10克，西砂仁10克，朱 衣茯神30克，炙远志10克，上肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑入）。":`Symptoms of typhoid fever caused by Shaoyin-cold transformation: Zeng, male, 17 years old, lived on Huancheng East Road, Kunming City. The onset of the disease was fever, aversion to cold, headache and body pain due to cold after eating and drinking. Yan was examined by a traditional Chinese medicine doctor, and two doses of cooling and external medicine were ineffective, so he was immediately sent to a hospital in Gaojiao at the foot of Xishan Mountain in this city for hospitalization. Nineteen days after being hospitalized, injections were given. Although the fever subsided, the condition became increasingly serious. Several doctors were consulted, and they were unanimously diagnosed with "enteric typhoid fever" and there was a risk of intestinal bleeding or intestinal perforation. It was decided to use blood transfusion to save the patient. After the blood transfusion, his condition did not subside, and he became more and more critical. He was declared hopeless, and his medical examination was postponed on October 25, 1943. When I arrived at the hospital, it was already nine o'clock in the evening. I learned that the patient had been ill for 19 days. He had no fever, but had a bulging abdomen, pain in the lower abdomen, moaning from time to time, short and red urine, and had been unable to pass stool for seven or eight days. He could not eat and drink, could not close his eyelids day and night, and could not turn his side in bed. However, he saw a nurse who would give him mineral water at any time. The tongue coating is white, slippery, thick and greasy, and there is no thirst to drink. The pulse is stringy and tight, and becomes weak and empty when pressed hard. After the diagnosis, he was immediately told that the condition was very critical, caused by typhoid fever. The disease pathogens penetrated deep into Shaoyin's viscera-cold syndrome. Yang Qi was internally deficient and Yin-cold was too strong. Cold water and Yin Qi formed in the body like ice. There was a haze in the abdomen. Although the fever subsided, the internal cold was extremely cold. The obstruction of bowel movement is caused by the condensation of yin and cold, and the true yang is greatly deficient and unable to move, which is not comparable to the syndrome of heat knot. The first line of yang has the potential to escape, and the condition is critical, which is quite expensive to treat. Only by supporting yang, suppressing yin and warming it up, so that the cold water and evil yin in the upper part can be spit out from the mouth, and the cold water and evil yin in the middle and lower part can be excreted through the two stools, and the yang can return and the yin can retreat, can the crisis be turned into peace. It is planned to treat it with Zhongjing Tongmai Sini Decoction plus Evodia and Shanggui. We also inform the patient not to be alarmed if vomiting, sputum, or diarrhea occurs after taking the medicine. This is a sign of cure and a glimmer of hope for recovery. 160 grams of Baifu slices, 30 grams of dried ginger, 16 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 26 grams of Poria, 6 grams of Evodia, and 6 grams of licorice. Will see you again on October 26th. After taking the above medicine yesterday, I immediately vomited a bowlful of saliva, which is a sign that the disease is cured. The tight pulse has subsided and become gentle, with loose stools and diarrhea once, and urination three times. However, the lower abdomen still has pain, which comes and goes slowly. The reason is that the course of the disease is long, the yang spirit is too deficient, and the internal cold is too strong. Although the effect has been achieved, the disease is severe and the medicine is light, and the disease is weak and the enemy is still invincible. Fortunately, the breath is no longer breathless, the phlegm is no longer, the hands and feet are warm, and the pulse is gentle and energetic. Afterwards, a large dose is used to support the yang and warm it up, so as to make the yang return to the yin and retreat, and the crisis can gradually be turned into peace. 260 grams of Baifu slices, 60 grams of dried ginger, 20 grams of Evodia, 16 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 6 grams of cloves, 30 grams of Poria, and 6 grams of amomum villosum. Third consultation on October 27. After taking medicine yesterday morning, I vomited about two bowls of saliva again. After taking medicine in the afternoon, I vomited again and had diarrhea several times. This was all due to "frozen melting", and the virus evil yin collapsed from the upper and lower orifices. The tongue coating is still thick and greasy, the tongue is red and lively, the color of the face and lips has also turned rosy, the body temperature is as normal, the pulse is gentle and has a strong pulse, the abdominal distension is slightly painful, and the bulging has reduced by 6-7%. The critical period has passed, but the Yang Shen has been too weak due to long-term illness, and the evil Yin has not yet been eliminated, so a large dose of Fuyang is still used to supplement the main body. 300 grams of Baifu slices, 60 grams of dried ginger, 16 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 6 grams of sweet maple nut (shelled and pounded), 6 grams of Evodia, 4 grams of bird medicine, 6 grams of Amomum villosum, and 30 grams of Poria. On the fourth visit on October 28, after taking the medicine, I passed out 16 stools last night, each time with different amounts. This morning I had two stools, both of which were thin stools filled with water. They were black in color at first, but gradually turned yellow this morning. This is a sign that the yang in the stomach is gradually returning. The body temperature is 37°C and the pulse is 80 beats per minute. I urinated six times today, and the color was light yellow and clear. However, every time I urinated, I felt a tingling pain in the stem. It was caused by the stimulation of the virus and was not caused by excess heat. Last night, I felt thirsty and liked hot drinks because of the haze in my belly and the water evil. Today, when I shine in the sky, the haze disperses and the cold water turns into water, but the Yang spirit is too weak to turn Qi into fluid and lacks moisture, so I like hot drinks to irrigate and nourish the body. It is not a thirsty drink caused by heat or burning Yin. For those who occasionally like to eat cold food, the Qi of Jueyin is not in harmony with each other, and the Yin and Yang are not in harmony. The arrows are flowing continuously, the palace roads are open, and the turbid qi is declining. Although the symptoms of the disease have been greatly reduced and the danger signs have been eliminated, the yin qi of the liver and kidneys has not been cleared away, and the yang and righteousness have not been fully restored, so there is still a lump in the left abdomen causing pain. The most gratifying thing is that I have eaten a little food this morning, and my stomach qi has calmed down, my yang has returned, and I can expect to recover. At the beginning of a serious illness, it is advisable to be cautious in taking care of the patient. Do not overeat to damage the stomach, overwork to damage the mind, and avoid wind and cold. Fuyang is still used to assist the main body. 300 grams of Baifu slices, 50 grams of dried ginger, 30 grams of Poria cocos, 16 grams of coix seed, 18 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 3 grams of Bokou kernel (pounded), 6 grams of amomum villosum (pounded), 10 grams of licorice, and 2.6 grams of white pepper (pounded). Also take two black plum pills. Five clinics on October 29th. The pulse has become gentle, 72 times per minute, the body temperature is 37.6°C, and the patient has six bowel movements. The urine is clearer, longer and light yellow, there is a slight tingling sensation in the stem, the lump in the abdomen has completely disappeared, the complexion gradually turns rosy, the nose is also shiny, six to seven tenths of the tongue coating has receded, the appetite has increased, the food intake has increased, the abdominal pain has subsided, and at this time, white plaques can be seen all over the body. The serious illness has subsided and the yang gradually recovers. You can gradually switch to aftercare. When the illness is gone and the medicine is reduced, it is still mainly to support the yang to supplement the body. He was also told to avoid eating raw and cold fruits, sour and cold foods, tender eggs, sweet wine, and all sticky foods, to be careful of wind and cold, and to maintain a healthy diet. 160 grams of Baifu slices, 30 grams of dried ginger, 16 grams of Poria, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind, soak in water and mix), 5 grams of Bokou kernel (pounded), 16 grams of coix kernels, 6 grams of licorice, 5 grams of longan meat, and 3 jujubes. Six consultations on October 30. This morning, the body temperature is normal, the pulse is gentle, the base of the tongue is still white and greasy, the stool is two times, the volume is small, the urine is yellowish and clear, the membranes in the abdomen are distended and the food intake is increasing day by day. Considering that the spleen and stomach are still weak and the digestion is weak, each meal should be eaten with a certain amount of porridge. Because the serious illness has just recovered, the residual cold and evil yin have not been eliminated, and the original yang and righteousness have not been fully restored. We still adhere to the method of supporting yang and auxiliary righteousness. It can be overcome after a few doses, and there is no worry about changes. After drawing up the prescription, the book introduces four words and one poem to express the ambition. The clouds are gathering and the sun is dimming. In a blink of an eye, the real dragon is about to fly. The sweetness turns into yang and the fire appears. Why worry about the earth not returning in spring? 300 grams of Baifu slices, 50 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of licorice, 16 grams of cinnamon (grind, soak in water and mix), 6 grams of Evodia, 6 grams of Poria kernels (pounded), 30 grams of Poria, and 3 grams of white pepper (pounded). Seven consultations on October 31st. This morning, the body temperature and pulse are normal, and the diarrhea has stopped. This is because the virus in the abdomen has been completely excreted, the urine is clear and long, the abdominal distension and pain have completely disappeared, and the food intake is good, but the base of the tongue is still white and greasy, the remaining evils of cold and dampness have not been completely cleared, and the yang righteousness needs to be continued to be warmed and supported. Preparation: 300 grams of Bai Fu Pian, 30 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of licorice, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10 grams of amomum villosum (pounded), and 10 grams of coix seed. Eight clinics on November 1st. The greasy coating on the tongue has subsided, with slightly thin white coating, the pulse and body temperature are normal, the urine is long and clear, the abdomen is relaxed and comfortable, and there is no other pain. The food intake is getting better, and each meal should be limited to six or seven minutes to avoid overeating that may damage the spleen and stomach. Sleep has improved, but the yang spirit has begun to return, but it is still unable to hold on and has many dreams. The righteousness is not sufficient, and I feel dizzy and weak when sitting up. It is still necessary to support the Yang and supplement the Zheng, so that the true Yang is strong and the evil Yin is eliminated. Warming and supporting the true yang will never damage the true yin, but restoring the true yang will help to breed the true yin. This is the principle of "Yang produces Yin and grows" and "Heaven produces water". When yin and yang are balanced, all syndromes can be cured. 300 grams of Baifu slices, 36 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of licorice, 10 grams of amomum villosum, 30 grams of Zhu Yi Fu Shen, 10 grams of Zhi Polygala, and 10 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed in).`,"伤寒病少阴阴极似阳证 原云南省某医院院长秦某，有独子名念祖，13岁":"Symptoms of typhoid fever in which the Yin pole of Shaoyin resembles Yang. Qin, the former director of a hospital in Yunnan Province, has an only son named Nianzu, who is 13 years old.","伤寒病少阴阴极似阳证\\n原云南省某医院院长秦某，有独子名念祖，13岁。患伤寒病发热20余日不退。秦精于西医，邀数位同道会诊，均断言无法挽救。1948年1月7日邀吴氏诊视。发热不退已20余日，晨轻夜重，面色青黯，两颧微发红；口唇焦燥起血壳，日夜不寐，人事不省。呼吸喘促，时而发迷无神，时又烦乱谵语，两手乱抓有如撮空理线，食物不进.小便短赤，大便已数日不通，舌苔黑燥.不渴饮，喂水仅下咽二三口，多则不吮。脉象浮而空，重按无力。此系伤寒转人少阴，阴寒太盛，阴盛格阳，致成外假热而内真寒之阴极似阳证。外虽现一派燥热之象，内则阴寒已极，逼阳外浮，将有脱亡之势。法当大剂扶阳抑阴，回阳收纳，交通心肾。拟方白通汤加上肉桂主之：附子250g，干姜50g，葱白4茎，肉桂15g（研末，泡水兑入）\\n当晚服后，稍见安静，得寐片刻，面部青黯色稍退而略润，脉象不似昨日空浮，烦躁谵语稍宁。但见欲寐愈甚，现出少阴虚寒本象。又照原方煎服一次，以下为逐日诊治记录：\\n1月8日：热度稍降，唇舌已较润，烦乱止。但有时仍说昏话，曾呕吐涎痰一次。仍以白通汤加味主之：\\n附子300g，干姜30g，茯苓30g，肉桂15g（研末，泡水兑入），葱白4茎。\\n上方服后，整夜烦躁不宁，不能入寐。\\n1月9日：脉稍有力，热度较前稍降，神情淡漠，不渴饮。此系阴寒太盛，阳气太虚，虽得阳药以助.然病重药轻，药力与病邪相攻，力不胜病，犹兵不胜敌。虽见烦躁不宁，乃药病相争之兆，不必惊疑，尚需加重分量始能克。大剂四逆汤加味治之：\\n附子400g，干姜150g，肉桂20g（研末，泡水兑入），朱衣茯神50g，炙远志20g，丁香5g，生甘草20g。\\n此方药力较重，为救危急，嘱煎透后一小时服药一次。当天下午5时又视之，病势已大松，烦躁平定，人已安静，小便转较长。病有转机，是夜又照原方连进，大便始通，泻出酱黑稀粪3次，发热已退去大半，烦乱谵语已不再作，且得熟寐4〜5小时。\\n1月10日：脉浮缓，唇舌回润，黑苔退去十之六七，身热退去十之八九，照第三方加砂仁10g，苍术I0g，吴茱萸8g治之。\\n1月11日：大便又畅泻数次，其色仍酱黑。身热已退净，唇上焦黑血壳已脱去，黑苔更见减少，津液满口。日夜泄泻10余次，秦君夫妇为此担心，认为有肠岀血危险，每见其子排泻大便，即流泪惊惶不已。当即解释，良由寒湿阴邪内盛，腹中有如冰霜凝聚.今得阳药温化运行，阴邪溃退.真阳返回而使冰霜化行。所拟方药皆非泻下之剂，其排泻者为内停寒湿污秽之物，系病除佳兆。病家疑虑始减，继以大剂温化日夜连进。\\n附子400g，干姜80g，肉桂20g（研末，泡水兑入），砂仁10g，茯苓50g，薏苡仁20g，白豆蔻8g，甘草30g。\\n1月12日：大便又泻10余次，色逐渐转黄，小便已较清长，黑苔全退，尚有白滑苔，食思恢复，随时感到腹中饥饿而索饮食，继拟下方调治：\\n附子400g，干姜80g，肉桂20g（研末，泡水兑入），砂仁10g，黄芪30g，炙甘草20g，龙眼肉30g。\\n1月13日：大便仅泻2次，色黄而溏；唇色红润，白滑苔已退净，神识清明，食量较增，夜已能熟寐，脉静身凉。大病悉退，但阳神尚虚，起动则有虚汗出。拟黄芪建中汤加桂附调理：\\n附子300g，黄芪80g，桂枝20g，白芍30g，炙甘草20g，肉桂20g（研末，泡水兑入），生姜30g，大枣4枚，饴糖30g（烊化兑入）。\\n1月14日：脉沉缓而有神，唇舌红润，大便泻利已止，小便清长，有轻微咳嗽，腹中时或作痛。拟四逆汤加味治之：\\n附子300g，干姜100g，细辛8g，肉桂11g（研末，泡水兑入），陈皮10g，法半夏10g，甘草10g。\\n1月15日：咳嗽、腹痛已止，惟正气尚虚，起卧乏力，继以四逆汤加参、芪作善后调理，服五六剂而愈，体质健康如常。\\n按：此症发热、口唇焦燥、双颧微红、烦乱不寐、小便短赤、大便不通、舌苔黑燥等颇似阳热之象，怎么看都是热证；但从面色青黯，人事不省，不渴，脉浮而空等症判为内真寒而外假热，“阴寒已极，逼阳外浮，将有脱亡之势”，其认证之准确，令人钦佩。毅然投以大剂白通汤，不夹一味阴药，每日一诊，随时调方，附子从250g增加到400g，且日进2剂就是800g，如此危症终得救治，确实惊世骇俗，真善用附子大家也。当时有一门生曾题嵌字联盛赞吴氏：“济世全凭寸心无任钦佩，处方独具斗胆谁能抗衡。”":`Symptoms of typhoid fever in which the Yin pole of Shaoyin resembles Yang\\nQin, the former director of a hospital in Yunnan Province, has an only son named Nianzu, who is 13 years old. Suffering from typhoid fever, the fever persisted for more than 20 days. Qin was skilled in Western medicine and invited several colleagues for consultation, all of whom concluded that there was no way to save the disease. On January 7, 1948, Wu was invited for consultation. The fever has not subsided for more than 20 days, and it is light in the morning and heavy at night. His complexion is blue and gloomy, and his cheekbones are slightly red. His lips are dry and bloody, and he is sleepless day and night. He is unconscious. Shortness of breath, sometimes confusion, sometimes irritability and delirium, hands grabbing at the empty space, unable to eat, short red urine, constipation for several days, black and dry tongue coating. Not thirsty to drink, only swallowing two or three mouthfuls of water, and often not sucking. The pulse is floating and empty and cannot be pressed again. This is a syndrome where typhoid fever transfers to Shaoyin, and the Yin-cold is too strong, and the Yin-sheng counteracts the Yang, causing false heat on the outside and true cold on the inside. Although there is a sign of dryness and heat on the outside, the yin and cold are extremely cold on the inside, forcing the yang to float outward, and there will be a tendency to escape. Fa Dang is a large dose that supports yang and suppresses yin, restores yang and absorbs it, and communicates with the heart and kidneys. The proposed recipe of Baitong Decoction plus cinnamon is as follows: 250g of aconite, 50g of dried ginger, 4 stalks of scallions, and 15g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix in)\\nAfter taking it that night, I felt a little quieter and fell asleep for a while. However, the desire to sleep becomes more severe, and the original symptoms of Shaoyin deficiency and cold appear. Decoct the original prescription and take it once. The following is the daily diagnosis and treatment record: \\nJanuary 8: The fever dropped slightly, the lips and tongue became moister, and the restlessness stopped. But sometimes he still talks faintly and once vomited saliva and phlegm. Baitong decoction is still the main flavoring: 300g aconite, 30g dried ginger, 30g poria, 15g cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 4 white scallions. \\nAfter taking the above medicine, I felt restless all night and couldn't fall asleep. \\nJanuary 9: Pulse is slightly stronger, fever is slightly lower than before, expression is indifferent, no thirst for drink. This is because the yin and cold are too strong and the yang qi is too weak. Although the yang medicine can be used to help, the disease is severe and the medicine is weak. Although irritability and restlessness are seen, it is a sign of conflict between medicine and disease. There is no need to be alarmed. It still needs to be aggravated before it can be overcome. A large dose of Sini Decoction can be treated with: 400g of aconite root, 150g of dried ginger, 20g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 50g of Zhu Yi Fu Shen, 20g of Zhi Polygala, 5g of cloves, and 20g of raw licorice. \\nThis prescription is more powerful. To save the patient in a critical situation, please take the medicine once an hour after decoction. At 5 o'clock in the afternoon of the same day, I looked again and found that the condition had improved significantly, the irritability had subsided, the person was quiet, and the urination became longer. The disease took a turn for the better, and he took the original prescription again that night. His bowel movements began to pass, and he had black and loose stools 3 times. Most of the fever had subsided, and he no longer had irritability and delirium, and he could sleep for 4 to 5 hours. \\nJanuary 10th: The pulse is slow and slow, the lips and tongue are moisturized, the black coating has receded in 60% to 90%, and the body heat has receded in 90% to 10%. Treat the condition by adding 10g of Amomum villosum, 10g of Atractylodes, and 8g of Evodia. \\nJanuary 11th: I had loose bowel movements several times, but the color was still black. The body heat has subsided, the burnt black blood crust on the lips has fallen off, the black coating has been reduced, and the mouth is full of body fluids. He had diarrhea more than 10 times day and night. Qin Jun and his wife were worried about this and believed that there was a danger of intestinal bleeding. Every time they saw their son having diarrhea, they shed tears and were frightened. He immediately explained that due to the accumulation of cold and dampness, the yin evils were accumulated in the abdomen, and it was like frost condensing in the abdomen. Now that the yang medicine was used to warm the body, the yin evils retreated. The true yang returned and the ice and frost melted. The proposed prescriptions are not purgative agents. The purgative agents are those that stop cold, dampness and filth in the body, which is a good sign for the cure of the disease. The patient's doubts began to subside, and he continued to treat the patient with large doses of warming day and night. \\n400g aconite, 80g dried ginger, 20g cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10g amomum villosum, 50g poria, 20g coix kernel, 8g white cardamom, 30g licorice. \\nJanuary 12th: The stool had diarrhea more than 10 times, and the color gradually turned yellow. The urine became clearer and longer, the black fur disappeared completely, and there was still white slippery fur. The appetite returned, and I felt hungry at any time and asked for food. The following treatment was planned:\\nAconite 400g, 80g dried ginger, 20g cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water), 10g amomum villosum, 30g astragalus, 20g roasted licorice, and 30g longan meat. \\nJanuary 13: The stools were only 2 times, yellow and loose; the lips were rosy, the white slippery coating had receded, the consciousness was clear, the food intake was relatively increased, the patient was able to sleep well at night, and the pulse was quiet and the body was cool. All serious illnesses have subsided, but the yang spirit is still weak. If it starts, there will be sweating due to deficiency. Prepare the Astragalus Jianzhong Decoction with Guifu: 300g aconite, 80g astragalus, 20g cassia twig, 30g white peony root, 20g licorice, 20g cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 30g ginger, 4 jujubes, 30g caramel (blended and mixed). \\nJanuary 14th: Pulse is slow and energetic, lips and tongue are red, diarrhea has stopped, urine is long and clear, slight cough, and occasional pain in the abdomen. Treat it with the modified Sini Decoction: 300g aconite, 100g dried ginger, 8g asarum, 11g cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10g tangerine peel, 10g pinellia, and 10g licorice. \\nJanuary 15th: The cough and abdominal pain have stopped, but the righteousness is still deficient, and the patient is unable to get up or lie down. He then uses Sini Decoction with ginseng and qi for aftercare. After taking five or six doses, he is healed and his body is as healthy as usual. \\nNote: Fever, dry lips, reddish cheekbones, restlessness and insomnia, short red urine, blocked stools, black and dry tongue coating, etc. are quite similar to signs of yang heat. No matter how you look at it, it is a heat syndrome; I resolutely took a large dose of Baitong decoction, without adding any Yin medicine. I had a consultation every day and made prescriptions at any time. I increased the aconite from 250g to 400g, and took 2 doses a day to get 800g. Such a critical illness was finally cured, which is really shocking. Everyone is really good at using aconite. At that time, a student once wrote a couplet with inlaid words praising Wu: "It is all about caring and admiration. Who can compete with his unique and bold prescriptions?"`,"伤寒病少阴阴极似阳证（一） 杨某，男，三十一岁，云南省姚安县人":"Syndrome of typhoid fever in which the Yin pole of Shaoyin resembles Yang (1) Yang, male, 31 years old, from Yao'an County, Yunnan Province","伤寒病少阴阴极似阳证（一） 杨某，男，三十一岁，云南省姚安县人。1923年3月，已病 廿日。始因微感风寒，身热头痛,连进某医方药十余剂，每剂 皆以苦寒凉下并重加犀角、羚羊角、黄连等,愈进愈剧，犹不 自反，殆至危在旦夕，始延余诊视。斯时病者目赤，唇肿而焦， 赤足露身,烦躁不眠,神昏谵语,身热似火,渴喜滚烫水饮，小 便短赤，大便已数日不解，食物不进，脉浮虚欲散,此乃风寒 误治之变证。缘由误服苦寒凉下太过，已将真阳逼越于外而 成阴极似阳之症,外虽现一派热象,是为假热，而内则寒冷已 极，是为真寒。如确系阳证，内热熏蒸，应见大渴饮冷，岂有尚 喜滚饮乎？况脉来虚浮欲散，是为元阳有将脱之兆，苦寒凉 下,不可再服，惟有大剂回阳收纳，或可挽回生机。病象如此, 甚为危笃。急拟白通汤加上肉桂一剂治之。 附片60克，干姜26克，上肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑入）, 葱白4茎。 拟方之后，病家云及是晚因无人主持，未敢煎服。次晨, 又急来延诊,余仍执前方不变,并告以先用上肉桂泡水试服, 若能耐受,则照方煎服,舍此别无良法。病家乃以上肉桂水与 服之。服后旋即呕吐涎痰碗许，人事稍清，自云内心爽快，遂 进上方。服一剂后，病情较减，即现出恶寒肢冷之象。午后再 诊，身热约退一二，已不作烦躁请语之状,且得熟寐片刻，乃 以四逆汤加上肉桂主之。 附片100克，干姜36克，甘草12克，上肉桂10克（研 末，泡水兑入）。 服上方后，身热退去四、五，脉稍有神，小便赤而长,略进 稀粥。再剂则热退七、八,大便始通，色黑而硬，惟咳嗽痰多， 痰中兼带有血。病家另延数医诊视，皆云热证,出方总不离苦 寒凉下之法。由于前医所误之鉴，又未敢轻试。后因病人吃梨 一个，当晚忽发狂打人,身热大作，有如前状,又急邀余诊治, 始言吃梨之事。余视之，舌白而滑，仍喜滚饮，此阳神尚虚，阴 寒未净，急欲扶阳犹不及，反与滋阴清凉之水果，又增里寒， 病遂加重。即告以禁服生酸水果冷物及清凉苦寒之药为幸， 余仍主以大剂回阳祛寒之剂治之。照第二方加倍分量，并加 茯苓30克、半夏16克、北细辛4克，早晚各服一剂，共连服 六剂。三日后再诊，身热已不作，咳痰渐愈,饮食增加,小便淡 黄而长，大便转黄而滴。又照方去半夏、细辛，加砂仁、白术、 黄芪，每日一剂，连进十余剂，诸病俱愈。后体健胜于前。按：凡病有真热证与真寒证之分，又有真热假寒证与真寒假热证之别。然真者易识，而假者难辨。《内经》曰：“治病必求于本。”即凡病当须辨明阴阳之意也。":`Syndrome of typhoid fever in which the Yin pole of Shaoyin resembles Yang (1) Yang, male, 31 years old, from Yao'an County, Yunnan Province. In March 1923, he had been ill for 20 days. At the beginning, he had a slight cold, body heat and headache, so he took more than ten doses of a certain medical prescription. Each dose was cooled with bitter cold and added rhinoceros horn, antelope horn, coptis, etc. As the symptoms progressed, the condition became more severe and unreflexive, and he was almost in danger, so he postponed further examination. At this time, the patient suffers from red eyes, swollen and burnt lips, bare feet, irritability and sleeplessness, coma and delirium, body heat like fire, thirst for boiling water, short red urine, indigestible stool for several days, inability to eat, and a floating and weak pulse that wants to disperse. This is a syndrome caused by mistreatment of wind-cold. The reason is that if you mistakenly take bitter cold and cool it too much, it will force the true yang to the outside, resulting in a syndrome of yin pole resembling yang. Although there is a heat phenomenon on the outside, it is false heat, but it is extremely cold inside, which is true cold. If it is indeed a yang syndrome and the internal heat is fumigated, you should be very thirsty and drink cold drinks. How can you still like to drink boiling water? If the pulse is weak and dissipates, it is a sign that the yang is about to disappear. It is bitter, cold and cool, so you should not take it anymore. Only a large dose can restore the yang and absorb it, which may save your vitality. The symptoms of the disease are like this, which is very dangerous. Take a dose of Baitong Decoction and cinnamon to cure it. 60 grams of attached slices, 26 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 4 white stalks of scallions. After the prescription was drawn up, the patient said that it was late because no one was in charge, so he did not dare to cook it and take it. The next morning, I came to the doctor urgently, but I still insisted on the same condition. I was told to soak cinnamon in water and try it first. If I can tolerate it, I can decoct it and take it. There is no other way. The patient takes the above cinnamon water with it. Immediately after taking it, I vomited a bowlful of saliva and phlegm. I felt a little clearer and felt refreshed, so I went to the top. After taking one dose, the condition subsided, and symptoms of aversion to cold and cold limbs appeared. After another consultation in the afternoon, the body heat had subsided by about one or two, the patient was no longer irritable and asked for words, and he could sleep for a while, so he took Sini Decoction plus cinnamon as the main treatment. 100 grams of Fu Fian, 36 grams of dried ginger, 12 grams of licorice, and 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix). After taking the above medicine, the body heat subsided for four to five days, the pulse was slightly clearer, the urine was red and long, and the urine was slightly gruel. After another dose, the fever will subside for seven to eight days, and the stool will become clear, black and hard in color, but the cough will produce a lot of phlegm, and the phlegm will also contain blood. The patient consulted several other doctors, all of whom found that the patient had heat syndrome, and the prescription was always based on the method of treating cold and cool conditions. Because of the mistakes made by previous doctors, I did not dare to try it lightly. Later, because the patient ate a pear, he suddenly went crazy and hit someone that night, and his body was very hot, just like before. He urgently invited Yu to diagnose and treat him, and he started to talk about eating pear. When I look at it, my tongue is white and slippery, and I still like to drink. This is because the yang spirit is still weak, and the yin cold is not purified. I am eager to support the yang but fail to do so. Instead, the yin-nourishing and cooling fruits increase the internal cold, and the disease worsens. Fortunately, I was told not to take sour fruits, cold foods, and cool, bitter and cold medicines, but I still treated it with large doses of medicines that restore Yang and dispel cold. Double the amount of the second recipe, and add 30 grams of Poria cocos, 16 grams of Pinellia pinellia, and 4 grams of Asarum. Take one dose in the morning and evening for a total of six doses. Three days later, he was diagnosed again. The body heat was gone, the sputum was gradually getting better, he was eating more, his urine was light yellow and long, and his stool turned yellow and dripping. Then follow the prescription to remove Pinellia ternata and Asarum, add Amomum villosum, Atractylodes macrocephala, and Astragalus. Take one dose a day for more than ten doses, and all diseases will be cured. The back body is stronger than the front. Note: All diseases are divided into true heat syndrome and true cold syndrome, and there is also a difference between true heat and false cold syndrome and true winter and false cold syndrome. However, what is true is easy to recognize, but what is false is difficult to distinguish. "Nei Jing" says: "To treat a disease, we must look at the root." That is, the meaning of yin and yang must be distinguished for all diseases.`,"伤寒病少阴阴极似阳证（二） 原云南省某医院院长秦某，住昆明市小南…":"Syndrome of typhoid fever in which the Yin pole of Shaoyin resembles Yang (2) Qin, the former director of a hospital in Yunnan Province, lives in Xiaonan, Kunming City…","伤寒病少阴阴极似阳证（二） 原云南省某医院院长秦某，住昆明市小南门内绣衣街， 有独子名念祖,年十三岁，患伤寒重证，发热二十余日不退。秦精于西医，对其子曾以多种针药施治，未效。又邀约徐、应 等数位西医同道会诊，均断言无法挽救。后由秦之门生李某 君推荐，邀余于1948年1月7日前往诊视。患儿已发热不退 二十余日，晨轻夜重，面色青黯，两额微发红，口唇焦燥而起 血壳，日夜不寐，人事不省。呼吸喘促，时而发迷无神,时又见 烦乱请语，两手乱抓有如撮空理线。食物不进，小便短赤，大 便已数日不通，舌苔黑燥,不渴饮，喂水仅下咽二、三口，多则 不吮。脉象浮而空，重按无力。此系伤寒转入少阴，阴寒太盛， 阴盛格阳，心肾不交，致成外假热而内真寒之阴极似阳证。外 虽现一派燥热之象，内则阴寒已极，逼阳外浮，将有脱亡之 势。法当大剂扶阳抑阴，回阳收纳，交通心肾，方可挽回，若误 认热证，苦寒下咽,必危殆莫救。拟方白通汤加上肉桂主之。 附片250克，干姜50克，葱白4茎，上肉桂15克（研末， 泡水兑入）。 处方之后，秦对中医药怀有疑虑,见此温热大剂，更不敢 用，且对余说，他还有一特效办法，即抽取一伤寒病刚愈患 者之血液输给病儿，可望有效。殊料是日输血后，身热尤甚， 腹痛呻吟不止，更加烦乱谵语。至此，秦已感到束手无策，始将余所拟方药煎汤与其子试服。当晚服后，稍见安静，得寐 片刻，面部青黯色稍退而略润，脉象不似昨日之空浮，烦躁谵语稍宁。但见欲寐愈甚，现出少阴虚寒本象，又照原方煎 服一次。 1月8日复诊，热度稍降，唇舌已较润，烦乱止。但有时仍 说昏话，曾呕吐涎痰一次，仍以白通汤加味扶阳抑阴，交通心 肾兼化气行水主之。 附片300克，干姜30克，茯苓30克，上肉桂15克（研 末，泡水兑入），葱白4茎。 上方服后，当晚整夜烦躁不宁,不能入寐,秦君为此又生 疑似，次日促余急往诊视，见到正用硼酸水给患儿洗口。详査 病情，脉稍有力,热度较前稍降，神情淡漠，不渴饮。断定此系 阴寒太盛，阳气太虚，虽得阳药以助，然病重药轻，药力与病 邪相攻，力不胜病,犹兵不胜敌。虽见烦躁不宁，乃药病相争 之兆,不必惊疑，尚需加重分量始能克之,拟用大剂四逆汤加 味治之。 附片400克，干姜150克,上肉桂20克（研末，泡水兑入）， 硃衣茯神50克，炙远志20克，公丁香5克，生甘草20克。 此方药力较重，为救危急，嘱煎透后一小时服药一次。当 天下午五时又诊视之，病势已大松,烦躁平定，人已安静，小便 转较长。病有转机，是夜又照原方连进，大便始通，泻出酱黑稀 粪三次，发热已退去大半,烦乱请语已不再作,且得熟寐四、五 小时。 10日清晨，脉浮缓，唇舌回润，黑苔退去十之六、七，身热 退去十之八、九,大有转危为安之象。照第三方加西砂仁10 克，苍术10克,吴茱萸8克治之。 11日复诊。大便又畅泻数次,其色仍酱黑。身热已退净,唇上焦黑血壳已脱去，黑苔更见减少，津液满口。日夜一个对 时大便共泄泻十余次，秦君夫妇为此担心害怕，认为有肠出 血或肠穿孔的危险,每见其子排泻大便,即流泪惊惶不已。余 当即详加解释，良由寒湿邪阴内盛，腹中有如冰霜凝聚，今得 阳药温化运行，邪阴溃退，真阳返回而使冰霜化行。所拟方 药，皆非泻下之剂，其排泻者为内停寒湿污秽之物，系病除佳 兆，邪去则正自能安，方保无虞。于是，病家疑虑始减,继续接 受治疗。仍以大剂温化日夜连进。 附片400克，干姜80克，上肉桂20克（研末，泡水兑 入），西砂仁10克，茯苓50克，薏苡仁20克，波蔻仁8克，甘 草30克。 12日诊。服药后大便又泻十余次，色逐渐转黄，小便已较 清长,黑苔全退，尚有白滑苔，食思恢复，随时感到腹中饥饿 而索求饮食。因伤寒后期，阳神未复，脾胃亦虚，须当注意调 摄，以防食复、劳复等证发生，只宜少量多餐,继拟下方调治。 附片400克，干姜80克，上肉桂20克（研末，泡水兑入）， 西砂仁10克，北口芪30克，炙甘草20克，桂圆肉30克。 13日诊。大便仅泻二次，色黄而滴，唇色红润，白滑苔已 退净，神识清明,食量较增，夜已能熟寐，脉静身凉，大病悉 退，但阳神尚虚，形体瘦弱，起动则有虚汗而出，遂拟黄芪建 中汤加桂附调理之。 附片300克，黄就80克，桂枝尖20克，杭白芍30克，炙 甘草20克，上肉桂20克（研末，泡水兑入），生姜30克，大枣 4枚，饴糖30克（烊化兑入）。 14日诊。脉沉缓而有神，唇舌红润,大便泻利已止，小便 清长,有轻微咳嗽,腹中时或作痛,拟四逆汤加味治之。 附片300克，干姜100克，北细辛8克，上肉桂11克（研末，泡水兑入），广陈皮10克，法半夏10克，甘草10克。 15 日诊。咳嗽、腹痛已止，唯正气尚虚，起卧乏力，继以 四逆汤加参、英作善后调理,服五、六剂而愈,其后体质健康 如常。":"Syndrome of typhoid fever in which the yin pole of Shaoyin resembles yang (2) Qin, the former director of a hospital in Yunnan Province, lived in Xiuyi Street, Xiaonanmennei, Kunming City. He had an only son named Nianzu, who was 13 years old. He suffered from severe typhoid fever and had a fever that did not go away for more than 20 days. Qin was proficient in Western medicine and had treated his son with a variety of acupuncture and medicine, but to no avail. They also invited Xu, Ying and other Western medicine colleagues for consultation, and they all concluded that it was impossible to save the disease. Later, he was recommended by Qin's protégé Li Moujun and invited me to go for a consultation on January 7, 1948. The patient has been having fever for more than 20 days, which has been light in the morning and heavy at night. His complexion is blue and gloomy, his forehead is slightly red, his lips are burnt and have blood crusts, he is sleepless day and night, and he is unconscious. He has shortness of breath, sometimes he is in a daze, and sometimes he is agitated and asking for words, and his hands are grasping at random as if he were trying to sort out the threads in the air. Not eating, short and red urine, constipation for several days, black and dry tongue coating, no thirst for water, only two or three mouthfuls of water, and most often not sucking. The pulse is floating and empty and cannot be pressed again. This is caused by the transfer of typhoid fever to Shaoyin, excessive yin-cold, excessive yin, and disharmony between the heart and kidneys, resulting in false heat on the outside and true cold on the inside. Although there is a sign of dryness and heat on the outside, the yin and cold are extremely cold on the inside, forcing the yang to float outward, and there will be a tendency to escape. A large dose of method should be used to support Yang and suppress Yin, restore Yang and absorb it, and communicate with the heart and kidneys, so that it can be restored. If you misunderstand the heat syndrome and swallow it bitterly and coldly, you will be in danger and cannot be saved. Make a recipe of Baitong soup and add cinnamon. 250 grams of attached slices, 50 grams of dried ginger, 4 white stalks of scallions, and 15 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix in). After the prescription, Qin had doubts about traditional Chinese medicine, and he did not dare to use it after seeing this powerful warm medicine. He also told Yu that he had a special method, which was to extract the blood of a patient who had just recovered from typhoid fever and infuse it into the sick child, which was expected to be effective. Unexpectedly, after the blood transfusion that day, he became extremely hot, suffered from abdominal pain, moaned, and became even more upset and delirium. At this point, Qin felt at a loss what to do, so he decoctioned the prescription I proposed and gave it to his son to try it. After taking it that night, I felt a little calmer and fell asleep for a while. The dark blue color on my face faded a little and became slightly moist. My pulse was not as empty as yesterday, and my irritability and delirium calmed down a little. However, when the sleepiness worsened and the symptoms of Shaoyin deficiency and cold appeared, I decoction and took it again according to the original prescription. I went back for a follow-up visit on January 8. The fever dropped slightly, my lips and tongue became moister, and the restlessness stopped. But sometimes he still talks faintly, and once vomited saliva and phlegm. He still uses Baitong Decoction with a flavor to support yang and suppress yin, connect the heart and kidneys, and transform qi and water. 300 grams of Fu slices, 30 grams of dried ginger, 30 grams of Poria cocos, 15 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), and 4 white stalks of scallions. After taking the above medicine, he was restless and restless all night and could not fall asleep. Qin Jun was suspicious of this again. The next day, he rushed to the doctor for a check-up and saw that the child was washing his mouth with boric acid water. After detailed examination of the condition, the pulse was slightly stronger, the fever was slightly lower than before, the expression was indifferent, and he was not thirsty to drink. It is concluded that this is caused by excessive yin and cold and too weak yang. Although the yang medicine can be used to help, the disease is severe and the medicine is weak, and the medicine's power is in conflict with the disease. Although irritability and restlessness are seen, it is a sign of conflict between medicine and disease. There is no need to be alarmed. It still needs to be increased to overcome the problem. It is planned to use a large dose of Sini Decoction with added flavor to treat it. 400 grams of Fu Shen, 150 grams of dried ginger, 20 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 50 grams of Zhu Yi Fu Shen, 20 grams of Zhi Polygala, 5 grams of male cloves, and 20 grams of raw licorice. This prescription has a relatively strong potency. To save yourself from a critical situation, please take the medicine once an hour after decoction. At five o'clock in the afternoon of the same day, he was examined again. His condition was greatly relieved, his irritability had subsided, he was quiet, and his urination became longer. The disease took a turn for the better, and he continued to take the original prescription again that night. His bowel movements began to pass, and he had black and loose stools three times. The fever had mostly subsided, he no longer made fussy words, and he could sleep for four or five hours. In the early morning of the 10th, my pulse was slow and slow, my lips and tongue were moist, six to seven out of ten black coatings had receded, eight to nine out of ten body heat had receded, and it seemed that the crisis was over. According to the third party, add 10 grams of Amomum villosum, 10 grams of Atractylodes, and 8 grams of Evodia. Follow-up visit on the 11th. He had loose bowel movements several times and was still black in color. The body heat has subsided, the burnt black blood crust on the lips has fallen off, the black coating has been reduced, and the mouth is full of body fluids. Qin Jun and his wife had diarrhea more than ten times at the same time day and night. Qin Jun and his wife were worried about this, thinking that there was a danger of intestinal bleeding or intestinal perforation. Every time they saw their son having diarrhea, they shed tears and were frightened. Yu immediately explained in detail that due to the accumulation of cold, dampness and evil yin in the abdomen, it was like frost condensing in the abdomen. Now the Yang medicine is warming and operating, the evil yin collapses, and the true yang returns to melt the ice. The proposed prescriptions are not purgative agents. The purgative agents are those that stop cold, dampness and dirt in the body. They are a good sign of getting rid of the disease. If the evil spirits are removed, the body will be able to be healthy and safe, so there will be no danger. As a result, the patient's doubts began to subside and he continued to receive treatment. Still use large doses of warming day and night. 400 grams of Aconite slices, 80 grams of dried ginger, 20 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 10 grams of amomum villosum, 50 grams of poria, 20 grams of coix kernels, 8 grams of bokor kernels, and 30 grams of licorice. Clinic on the 12th. After taking the medicine, I had diarrhea more than ten times, and the color gradually turned yellow, and my urine became clearer and longer. All the black coating disappeared, and there was still white slippery coating. My food cravings returned, and I felt hungry at any time and asked for food. Because in the late stage of typhoid fever, the yang spirit has not recovered and the spleen and stomach are also weak, attention must be paid to regulating food intake to prevent the occurrence of symptoms such as resumption of food and work, etc. It is only advisable to eat small amounts and frequently, and follow the treatment as described below. 400 grams of Aconite slices, 80 grams of dried ginger, 20 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 10 grams of amomum villosum, 30 grams of Beikou Qi, 20 grams of licorice, and 30 grams of longan meat. Clinic on the 13th. The stool was yellow and dripping only twice, the lips were rosy, the white slippery coating had disappeared, the consciousness was clear, the food intake was increased, the patient was able to sleep well at night, the pulse was still and the body was cool, the serious illness had subsided, but the yang spirit was still weak, the body was thin, and there was sweating at the onset, so the patient was treated with Huangqi Jianzhong Decoction and Guifu. 300 grams of Aconite slices, 80 grams of Huangjiu, 20 grams of Guizhi tip, 30 grams of Hangzhou white peony root, 20 grams of roasted licorice, 20 grams of cassia cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 30 grams of ginger, 4 jujubes, 30 grams of maltose (blended and mixed in). Clinic on the 14th. The pulse is slow and energetic, the lips and tongue are red, the diarrhea has stopped, the urine is long and clear, there is a slight cough, and there may be pain in the abdomen, it is recommended to add Sini Decoction to treat it. 300 grams of Aconite, 100 grams of dried ginger, 8 grams of Asarum, 11 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10 grams of Citrus tangerine peel, 10 grams of Pinellia ternata, and 10 grams of licorice. Clinic on the 15th. The cough and abdominal pain have stopped, but the righteousness is still weak, and there is difficulty in getting up and lying down. Then Sini Decoction with ginseng and Ying is used as aftercare. After taking five or six doses, the condition is cured. After that, the body is as healthy as usual.","伤寒病少阴阴盛格阳案 马某，13岁":"Case of typhoid fever with Shaoyin Yin excess and Ge Yang case: Ma Mou, 13 years old","伤寒病少阴阴盛格阳案\\n马某，13岁。患伤寒已廿余日，“身热夜重，体温40℃余，反不恶寒，两颧发赤，唇焦而起血壳，头昏不食，欲寐无神，饮水不多，心烦胸闷，冒逆欲呕，小便短赤，大便数日不通，白㾦遍体如麻，脉沉而紧，舌苔白腻”。此症身热夜重，两颧发赤，唇焦而起血壳，心烦，小便短赤，大便不通，极易认作实热：但吴氏综合分析，从脉沉而紧，舌苔白腻、“欲寐无神，饮水不多”着眼，认为“寒邪引入阴分，格拒真阳浮越于外”，系阳虚阴盛之象，法当扶阳温化，破阴回阳，以白通汤治之而愈。按：在尿赤便秘、舌红津枯、唇焦起壳、目赤而肿等一派热象中辨出真寒，投以大剂附子取效。":`Case of typhoid fever with Shaoyin Yin Sheng and Ge Yang cases\\nMou, 13 years old. I had been suffering from typhoid fever for more than 20 days. "My body is hot at night, with a body temperature of more than 40℃, but I am not averse to cold. My cheeks are red, my lips are scorched and crusted with blood, I am dizzy and can't eat, I feel sleepy, I don't drink much water, I feel upset and have tightness in my chest, I feel an urge to vomit, my urine is short and red, my stool has been blocked for several days, my body is numb and white, my pulse is heavy and tight, and my tongue has a greasy coating." This symptom is characterized by severe body heat at night, red cheekbones, burnt lips with bloody crusts, upset, short red urine, and blocked stools, which can easily be regarded as excess heat. However, Wu's comprehensive analysis, based on the pulse is heavy and tight, the tongue coating is white and greasy, and the "drowsiness and lack of energy, and not drinking much" believe that "cold evil introduces yin, and the grid rejects the true yang and floats outside." Note: Identify the true cold among the heat symptoms such as red urine, constipation, red tongue, dry lips, scorched lips, red and swollen eyes, etc., and administer a large dose of aconite to get the effect.`,"伤寒病少阴阴盛格阳证 马某之子,十三岁，住昆明市":"Typhoid fever syndrome with excess of yin and yang in Shaoyin. Ma’s son, 13 years old, lives in Kunming.","伤寒病少阴阴盛格阳证 马某之子,十三岁，住昆明市。1945年11月22日，患伤 寒病已廿余日，医者诊治未愈，寒邪引入阴分,格拒真阳浮越 于外,致身热夜重,体温摄氏四十余度,反不恶寒,两额发赤， 唇焦而起血壳,头昏不食,欲寐无神,饮水不多,心烦胸闷,胃 逆欲呕,小便短赤,大便数日不通，白瘩遍体如麻,脉沉而紧， 舌苔白腻。此阳虚阴盛之象,法当挟阳温化，破阴回阳主之。 附片26克，干姜10克，上肉桂3克（研末，泡水兑入）， 茯苓10克，葱白4茎。 23日复诊。服昨方后呕吐涎水数碗，属温药运行，病除之 兆。仍身热头昏无神,不渴饮，此伤寒寒极之证，阴寒内盛，阳 不胜阴，决无热证，治法不变。 附片50克，干姜13克，上肉桂3克（研末，泡水兑入）， 茯苓10克，麦芽6克，葱白4茎。 24日三诊。舌苔白腻而润，脉较和缓，昨夜曾大便一次， 色黑，初硬而后滴，此里寒内重，阳气尚虚，阳不潜藏，仍潮 热，晨轻夜重,头昏欲寐无神，以大剂扶阳抑阴主之。 附片60克，干姜13克，上肉桂5克（研末，泡水兑入）， 茯苓10克，西砂仁3克，公丁香1.3克，甘草3克。 25日四诊。今晨诊脉，一息五至，状若平脉，舌苔白滑尚 厚腻,体温稍降至39.5℃，昨夜又解大便一次,心烦胸闷稍减, 已得熟寐。惟病久里寒尚重，隔拒真阳，浮游于外而潮热，额 赤,多虚汗，头昏无神。此乃中阳不运，阴寒阻遏，胸腹胀闷仍 不能食,热饮仅三、四口而已，势必驱尽里寒邪阴，真阳始得 返归其舍,潮热诸痒,焉有不退之理乎! 附片100克，干姜16克，上肉桂5克（研末，泡水兑入）, 茯神10克，甘草10克。 26日五诊。服昨方二次,于夜晚服药后,反见心中烦躁不 安,此乃重剂温药，逐动阴寒，药力与病邪相攻之象。待至清 晨，得天阳以助，遂见宁静得寐。刻诊，体温降至38.7℃，呼吸 平和，脉搏一息五至,舌苔仍白腻而滑润。胃寒日久,仍不思 饮食，痰多而夹黑血，属寒痰瘀血化行溃退，非热甚灼阴可 比。所喜者，两额赤色减退，白瘩渐詹，体温已有下降,为病退 佳兆。此病虚寒已极，决无热象足征，余乃抱定宗旨,仍以扶 阳温化辅正主之。 附片180克，干姜16克，上肉桂5克（研末，泡水兑入）， 甘草10克。 30日六诊。昨前三日，病家曾请西医诊治，医者以病情危 重又无特效药而告退，又复延余以求尽力挽救之。刻诊脉缓 弱无力，舌苔白润，小便已较清长,夜间仍有潮热，病者虚弱 已极。此三阴虚寒之证，病情日久，阳神极虚，缓迨延误，恐有 虚脱亡阳之虞，仍以扶阳抑阴，强心辅正主之。 附片130克，干姜16克，上肉桂6克（研末，泡水兑入）， 西砂仁5克，丁香3克，甘草10克。 12月1曰七诊。体温已降至37℃,脉象缓弱，一息四至， 面额赤色全退，现出虚寒病容，晦暗无华，昨夜得汗，身热退后,反畏寒，属阴退阳回，阳气虽已来复，尚虚弱而无力以卫外 所致。昨夜大便一次，色酱黑而滴，虽唇焦有黑血壳,然始终 不见渴饮,此三阴寒极之证,阳神太亏,仍以扶阳扶正主之。 附片130克，干姜20克，上肉桂5克（研末，泡水兑入）, 西砂仁10克，茯神10克，薏苡仁20克，甘草10克。 2日八诊。今晨诊视，体温37.2℃，脉象缓弱，一息四至, 舌白润，各节病情均见好转，口淡无味，不思饮食。此乃病久 中宫太寒，脾胃阳虚，司运失权，俟邪阴逐尽，中阳来复，则渐 可思食矣。仍以扶阳扶正主之。 附片130克，干姜25克，上肉桂6克（研末，泡水兑入）， 西砂仁10克，老白扣仁3克，炙甘草10克。 3日九诊，体温37.8℃,脉和缓，唇上黑血壳已脱去，舌苔 较退,唇舌均转红润，不渴饮，胃气渐复,刻有思饮之意,入夜 微有咳声。乃里寒尚未肃清，元阳仍虚,仍以扶阳辅正主之, 稍佐治咳，切忌过早施用滋补之剂。 附片130克，千姜25克,上肉桂6克（研末，泡水兑入），西 砂仁5克，法半夏10克，炙冬花5克，吴茱萸6克，炙甘草10 克 。 4日十诊。体温降至36.7℃，咳已止，阳神尚虚，照昨方 再进一剂。 5日十一诊。脉缓弱，苔已退，唇舌红润,不渴饮，小便清 长，晨间体温36.5℃,惟睡眠少，胃口不开，头上时有冷汗，阳 神太亏，继以扶阳健胃，养心安神主之。 附片160克，干姜65克，西砂仁6克（捣），上肉桂5克 （研末，泡水兑入），老白豆蔻3克（捣），炙远志6克，硃衣茯 神10克，炒酸枣仁10克，琥珀3克（研末，兑服），甘草6克。 6日十二诊。脉象、体温已正常，唇舌红润，昨日已进饮食，睡眠转佳，阳神尚虚，仍以扶阳辅正主之 附片130克，干姜20克，上肉桂5克（研末，泡水兑入）， 西砂仁6克，明党参20克，甘草6克。 7日十三诊。脉、舌，体温均如常，二便通畅，饮食、精神转 佳，大病已退，渐加调补，可期痊愈。遂拟扶阳建中调理善后， 数剂而后恢复健康。 附片100克，干姜16克，西砂仁6克（捣），老白豆蔻3克 （捣），上肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑入），北口芪20克，明党参20 克,炙甘草6克。":"Symptoms of typhoid fever with excess of yin and excess of yin and yang. Ma’s son, 13 years old, lives in Kunming. On November 22, 1945, I had contracted typhoid fever for more than 20 days, but the doctor had not recovered. The cold evil was introduced into the yin component, and the true yang was blocked from floating outside, causing the body to be hot at night. The body temperature was more than 40 degrees Celsius. Instead, I was not averse to cold, my forehead was red, my lips were burnt and bloody, I was dizzy, I couldn't eat, I felt sleepy, I didn't drink much water, I was upset, chest tightness, stomachache Desire to vomit, short red urine, constipation for several days, white spots all over the body like numbness, deep and tight pulse, white and greasy tongue coating. This phenomenon of yang deficiency and yin excess should be used to warm the yang, break the yin and return it to yang. 26 grams of Fu Lian, 10 grams of dried ginger, 3 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10 grams of Poria cocos, and 4 green onion stalks. Follow-up visit on the 23rd. After taking yesterday's prescription, I vomited several bowls of saliva, which is a sign that the warm medicine will work and the disease will be cured. Still feeling hot, dizzy, and not thirsty to drink, this is a symptom of typhoid fever. Yin and cold are excessive in the body, and yang cannot overcome yin. There is absolutely no heat syndrome, and the treatment method remains unchanged. 50 grams of Fu Lian, 13 grams of dried ginger, 3 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10 grams of Poria cocos, 6 grams of malt, and 4 white scallions. Three consultations on the 24th. The tongue coating is white and greasy, and the pulse is gentle. Last night, I had a bowel movement, which was black in color, hard at first and then dripping. The place is cold and heavy, the yang energy is still weak, the yang is not hidden, and there are still hot flashes. It is light in the morning and heavy at night, and it is dizzy and sleepy. Use a large dose to support yang and suppress yin. 60 grams of Fu Lian, 13 grams of dried ginger, 5 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10 grams of Poria, 3 grams of amomum villosum, 1.3 grams of cloves, and 3 grams of licorice. Four consultations on the 25th. Checking the pulse this morning, the pulse is five times at a time, and the pulse is flat, the tongue coating is white and slippery but still thick and greasy, the body temperature has dropped slightly to 39.5°C, I had another bowel movement last night, the upset and chest tightness have slightly subsided, and I have fallen into a deep sleep. However, when the disease lasts for a long time, the cold inside is still severe, the true Yang is blocked, floating outside, causing hot flashes, red forehead, excessive sweating, dizziness and lack of energy. This is because the middle yang is not moving, the yin and cold are blocked, the chest and abdomen are bloated and stuffy, and you still can't eat. Just three or four sips of hot drinks will drive away the cold and evil yin inside, and the true yang will return to its home. Hot flashes and itching, there is no reason to stop it! 100 grams of Fu Shen, 16 grams of dried ginger, 5 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water), 10 grams of Fushen, and 10 grams of licorice. Five consultations on the 26th. I took yesterday's prescription twice, but after taking it at night, I felt irritable and restless. This is a sign that a heavy dose of warming medicine is used to activate the yin and cold, and the medicine's power is at odds with the pathogenic factors. In the early morning, with the help of the sun, I found peace and fell asleep. Upon examination, the body temperature dropped to 38.7°C, the breathing was gentle, the pulse was five to five, and the tongue coating was still white, greasy and smooth. If the stomach is cold for a long time and still does not want to eat and drink, there is excessive phlegm with black blood, which is a sign of cold phlegm and blood stasis, causing ulceration and retreat, and is not comparable to heat or even burning of yin. For those who are happy, the redness on the forehead has subsided, the white spots are getting thicker, and the body temperature has dropped, which is a good sign that the disease is cured. This disease is extremely deficient and cold, and there are absolutely no signs of heat. Therefore, with a determined purpose, I still use Fuyang and warming to supplement the main treatment. 180 grams of Fu slices, 16 grams of dried ginger, 5 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), and 10 grams of licorice. Six consultations on the 30th. Three days ago yesterday, the patient asked Western doctors for diagnosis and treatment, but the doctor resigned because his condition was critical and there was no effective medicine, and he delayed again in order to try his best to save the patient. Upon diagnosis, the pulse is slow and weak, the tongue coating is white and moist, the urine is clear and long, and there are still hot flashes at night, indicating that the patient is extremely weak. In the syndrome of deficiency and cold of the three yin, if the condition lasts for a long time, the yang spirit will be extremely weak, and the recovery will be delayed. There is a risk of deficiency and loss of yang, so it is still necessary to support the yang and suppress the yin, and strengthen the heart to assist the main function. 130 grams of Aconite slices, 16 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 5 grams of amomum villosum, 3 grams of cloves, and 10 grams of licorice. Seven consultations on December 1st. The body temperature has dropped to 37°C, the pulse is slow and weak, and the breath is four times. The redness of the face and forehead has completely disappeared, and the appearance of a weak and cold disease is dull and dull. I sweated last night, the body heat subsided, and I felt chills. This is caused by the retreat of yin and the return of yang. Although the yang energy has returned, it is still weak and unable to defend the outside. I had a bowel movement last night, and it was black and dripping. Although my lips were scorched and there were black blood crusts, I still didn't feel thirsty to drink. This is a sign of extreme coldness of the three yin and the Yang Shen is too deficient, so I still need to strengthen the Yang and strengthen the body. 130 grams of Fushen, 20 grams of dried ginger, 5 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10 grams of amomum villosum, 10 grams of Fushen, 20 grams of coix seed, and 10 grams of licorice. Eight clinics on the 2nd. During the examination this morning, the body temperature was 37.2°C, the pulse was slow and weak, the breaths came four times, the tongue was white and moist, the condition in all joints had improved, the mouth was tasteless, and he had no desire to eat. This is caused by a long-term illness in which the palace is too cold, the spleen and stomach yang are deficient, and the movement of the body is out of control. Once the evil yin is driven away and the middle yang returns, you will gradually be able to think about food. Still use Fuyang and Fuzheng as the main method. 130 grams of Aconite slices, 25 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10 grams of Amomum villosum, 3 grams of Laobaikou kernel, and 10 grams of Zhigancao. On the 3rd day of the ninth examination, the body temperature was 37.8°C, the pulse was gentle, the black blood crust on the lips had fallen off, the tongue coating had receded, the lips and tongue had turned red, and she was no longer thirsty to drink. The stomach qi gradually returned, indicating a desire to drink, and there was a slight cough at night. If the internal cold has not been eliminated and Yuanyang is still deficient, it is still necessary to use Fuyang to supplement the main function, and to treat cough slightly. Do not use nourishing agents too early. 130 grams of Futian, 25 grams of ginger, 6 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 5 grams of amomum villosum, 10 grams of pinellia, 5 grams of winter flowers, 6 grams of Evodia, and 10 grams of licorice. Ten consultations on the 4th. The body temperature has dropped to 36.7℃, the cough has stopped, and the yang spirit is still weak. I will take another dose according to yesterday's prescription. Clinic on the 11th on the 5th. The pulse is slow and weak, the coating has receded, the lips and tongue are red, not thirsty to drink, the urine is clear and long, the body temperature in the morning is 36.5°C, but the patient sleeps little, has poor appetite, and sometimes has cold sweat on the head, and the yang spirit is too deficient. Follow up with supporting the yang and strengthening the stomach, nourishing the heart and calming the spirit. 160 grams of Aconite slices, 65 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of amomum villosum (pounded), 5 grams of cassia cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water), 3 grams of old white cardamom (pounded), 6 grams of Zhi Polygala, 10 grams of Zhu Yifu Shen, 10 grams of fried jujube kernels, 3 grams of amber (pulverized, mixed with water), and 6 grams of licorice. 12 consultations on the 6th. The pulse and body temperature are normal, the lips and tongue are red, I have eaten yesterday, my sleep has improved, and the yang spirit is still weak, I still take 130 grams of Fuyang Fu Pian, 20 grams of dried ginger, 5 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 6 grams of amomum villosum, 20 grams of Codonopsis pilosula, and 6 grams of licorice. 13th consultation on the 7th. The pulse, tongue, and body temperature are all normal, the bowel movements are unobstructed, the diet and spirit are getting better, the serious illness has subsided, and by gradually increasing the tonic, recovery can be expected. So I planned to use Fuyang Jianzhong to treat the aftermath and restore health after a few doses. 100 grams of Aconite, 16 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of amomum villosum (pounded), 3 grams of old white cardamom (pounded), 10 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 20 grams of Beikou Qi, 20 grams of Codonopsis pilosula, and 6 grams of Zhigancao.",伤寒病并肠出血:"Typhoid fever and intestinal bleeding",伤寒论讲义:"Lecture Notes on Treatise on Febrile Diseases",伤寒验案:"Typhoid fever test case",位:"Bit",余位:"Remaining seats","余八女儿1岁，体质较弱，忽又发热而加咳嗽":"Yu Ba’s daughter is 1 year old and has a weak constitution. She suddenly has fever and cough.","余八女儿1岁，体质较弱，忽又发热而加咳嗽。以为感冒风寒，即以桂枝汤治之，不料服后更觉发热而加惊烦。值余出诊，内人以为内有伏热，即以芍药甘草汤加麦冬煎汤喂之。发热虽退，但脉来紧急，呼吸迫促，不喜吮乳，观之则面项上隐隐现出紫黑疹点，始告之为麻疹，绝不能再服寒凉之剂。若不设法将麻疹升提发泄出来，必至危殆。白附片300g加入甘草数钱，煮沸后与服两茶盏。隔约1小时之后，麻疹渐出，色亦转红活。又复发热，再加干姜30g，频频喂之。其喘促更甚，鼻翼胸部均扇动，咳嗽声哑，哼挣不息。每半小时喂药1次，均呕吐涎痰（寒痰温化由上窍排除）。\\n下午又煎附片300g，干姜30g.上肉桂6g（泡水兑入），日夜频频喂之。病势虽如是沉重，但麻疹逐渐透达。每日仅服汤药，乳食不进。次晨仍照原方早1剂，晚1剂，3日夜共服附片6个300g，仍继续呕吐痰涎和泄泻稀粪，疹方出透渐灰，鼻扇喘挣始平，发热亦退，且乳食已进，遂平息而愈。（《麻疹发微》）":`Yu Ba's daughter is 1 year old and has a weak constitution. She suddenly has a fever and cough. Thinking that he had a cold and wind-cold, he treated it with Guizhi Decoction. Unexpectedly, he felt even more feverish and irritated after taking it. When I was on duty for a consultation, my wife thought that there was latent heat in her body, so she fed her with peony and licorice decoction plus Ophiopogon japonicus decoction. Although the fever has subsided, but the pulse is urgent, the breathing is short, and the patient does not like to suck breasts, and if he looks at it, purple and black rash spots appear faintly on his face, he is diagnosed as measles, and he must not take cold medicine anymore. If you don't try to raise and vent the measles, you will be in danger. Add 300g of Baifu Pian to licorice, boil it and take two cups of tea. After about an hour, the hives gradually appeared and the color turned red. If the fever recurs, add 30g of dried ginger and feed it frequently. His breathing became more severe, his nose and chest were flaring, his cough was hoarse, and he kept humming. After taking medicine every half hour, all patients vomited salivary phlegm (cold phlegm that has become warm is eliminated by the upper orifices). \\nIn the afternoon, fry 300g of Fu slices, 30g of dried ginger, and 6g of cinnamon (soak in water and mix in), and feed them frequently day and night. Although the disease was severe, the measles gradually became clear. He only takes decoction and medicine every day and does not eat milk. The next morning, I continued to take one dose in the morning and one dose in the evening. I took 6 300g tablets for three days and nights. I still continued to vomit phlegm and diarrhea and had loose feces. The rash gradually became grey, my nose became flat, my fever also subsided, and I had taken milk and food, so it subsided and recovered. ("Micro Measles")`,便秘:"constipation",儿科:"Pediatrics",儿科名家:"Pediatric experts","元阳不足，冲任俱虚":"Insufficient Yuanyang means that all tasks are in vain","先期多热，后期多寒，然姚氏必参脉证、不拘成说，热者清之，寒者温之，虚者补之，郁者疏之，绝无执一而论之弊。":"There is a lot of heat in the early stage, and there is a lot of cold in the later stage. However, Yao's theory must be based on the pulse syndrome and is not limited to the theory. If it is hot, it will be cleared, if it is cold, it will be warmed. If it is deficient, it will be replenished. If it is depressed, it will be sparse.","先生临证六十余年，尤以救治阴盛格阳、真寒假热诸危候见长。常于高热烦躁、脉大无根之际，断为戴阳之证，投白通汤、四逆汤重加肉桂、吴萸，每起沉疴。其用附子必依法炮制、久煎去毒，先试后进，胆大而心细，世称“吴附子”。":'Mr. Wang has been clinically diagnosed for more than 60 years, and is particularly good at treating critical symptoms such as yin excess and yang deficiency, as well as true winter holiday fever. Often when there is high fever and irritability, and a large and rootless pulse, it is diagnosed as Dai Yang syndrome. Baitong Decoction and Sini Decoction plus cinnamon and Wuyu are added to the treatment, and every time the disease develops, the disease develops. When using Aconite, one must prepare it according to the law, decoct it for a long time to remove the poison, try it before proceeding, be bold and careful, and it is known as "Wu Fuzi" in the world.',"先生临证讲究“因时制宜”，按时取穴，针必中穴，穴必中经。":'When treating symptoms, Mr. Xiang pays attention to "adapting measures to the current conditions", selecting acupoints on time, the needle must hit the acupoint, and the acupoint must hit the meridian.',"先生主张“儿科古称哑科”，诊察须耐心细致，望诊为先。":'My husband advocated that "pediatrics was called mute medicine in ancient times" and diagnosis must be patient and meticulous, with inspection first.',"先生兼通音韵之学，著有《韵略易通》；又著《医门揽要》，论脉理方治，简明扼要。":'He is also knowledgeable in the study of phonology, and is the author of "Yun Lue Yi Tong"; he is also the author of "Yi Men Lan Yao", which discusses the pulse theory and prescription, which is concise and to the point.',"先生创办昆明市中医医院并长期主理院务，倡“中西互参、以中为本”，为昆明中医事业奠基之人。":'He founded the Kunming Traditional Chinese Medicine Hospital and has been in charge of hospital affairs for a long time. He advocated "interaction between Chinese and Western medicine and put China as the foundation", and he laid the foundation for the cause of traditional Chinese medicine in Kunming.',"先生尝治一水肿患者，诸医迭进清利而病益甚。先生据其畏寒肢冷、小便不利、脉沉细，断为少阴阳虚水泛，投真武汤加减，温阳利水，数剂而肿消。又治久痢滑脱不禁者，以桃花汤合真人养脏汤收功，皆经方活用之范。":"The gentleman tried to treat a patient with edema. Various doctors repeatedly used Qingli to cure the disease, and the patient benefited greatly. Based on his fear of cold and cold limbs, difficulty in urination, and deep and thready pulse, he diagnosed the condition as deficiency of yin and yang and swelling of the water. He took Zhenwu Decoction, which warmed the yang and diuretic, and the swelling disappeared after a few doses. To treat chronic dysentery and slippery syndrome, use Peach Blossom Decoction combined with Zhenren Yangzang Decoction to achieve the desired effect. Both prescriptions can be used flexibly.","先生提出“证候层级辨证”学说，为中医辨证规范化作出重要贡献。":'He proposed the theory of "syndrome level differentiation" and made important contributions to the standardization of syndrome differentiation in traditional Chinese medicine.',"先生毕生致力于中医教育事业，参与创办云南中医学院并出任院长，主张“经典为根、临床为本”，培养了大批中医药骨干人才。":'He devoted his life to the education of traditional Chinese medicine. He participated in the founding of Yunnan College of Traditional Chinese Medicine and served as the dean. He advocated "classics as the root and clinical practice as the basis" and cultivated a large number of key talents in traditional Chinese medicine.',"先生治不孕症，每从调经入手，辨其寒热虚实，或温经汤以暖胞宫，或逍遥散以舒肝郁，或养精种玉汤以填真阴，因人而异。尝谓：“种子必先调经，调经必先理气。”其治痛经、崩漏、癥瘕诸疾，亦皆以调气血、和冲任为要。":'When treating infertility, I always start with regulating menstruation, distinguishing the deficiency and excess of cold and heat, or warming the menstruation soup to warm the uterus, or Xiaoyao Powder to soothe liver stagnation, or nourishing essence and Zhongyu Decoction to fill the true yin, which varies from person to person. Taste said: "The seeds must first regulate menstruation, and to regulate menstruation must first regulate qi." The key to treating dysmenorrhea, metrorrhagia, and abdominal mass diseases is to regulate qi and blood, and to regulate Chong and Ren.',"先生治中风后遗症，上肢不遂取肩髃、曲池、合谷、外关，下肢不遂取环跳、风市、足三里、阳陵泉、太冲，口眼歪斜加地仓、颊车、翳风，每配合梅花针叩刺与艾灸。又治寒湿痹证，以温针灸深刺，务令温热之气透达病所。":"Mr. Wang treats the sequelae of stroke. For upper limb failure, Jianqi, Quchi, Hegu, and Waiguan are used. For lower limb failure, Huantiao, Fengshi, Zusanli, Yanglingquan, and Taichong are used. For mouth and eye deformity, Dicang, Jieche, and Yifeng are used. Each time, plum blossom needle tapping and moxibustion are used. To treat cold-dampness syndrome, use warm acupuncture and deep needling to ensure that the warm Qi reaches the diseased area.","先生治偏头痛，按子午流注择时开穴，配风池、太阳、率谷、外关、足临泣，少而精，针到痛减。尝治一顽固性三叉神经痛，发作有时，先生据其发作时辰循经开穴，再配局部缪刺，数诊而愈。":"To treat migraine, Mr. Zhang opened acupuncture points at the right time according to Ziwu Liuzhu, and used Fengchi, Taiyang, Shuigu, Waiguan, and Zulinqi. The acupuncture was small but precise, and the pain was reduced by acupuncture. Trigeminal treatment of a case of intractable trigeminal neuralgia with occasional attacks. The teacher opened acupuncture points along the meridian according to the time of the attack, and then used local acupuncture. After several diagnoses, the patient was cured.","先生治小儿咳嗽，风寒以止嗽散加减，风热以桑菊饮化裁，痰多者佐二陈；治小儿厌食，以七味白术散合保和丸健脾开胃，兼以捏脊疗法，家长称便。尝诫：“小儿用药，贵在轻灵，一服知，二服已，不效者，更方也。”":'To treat cough in children, use Zhisou Powder for wind-cold, Sangju Decoction for wind-heat, and use Erchen for those with excessive phlegm. To treat anorexia in children, use Qiwei Atractylodes Powder combined with Baohe Pills to strengthen the spleen and appetite, and also use chiropractic therapy. Parents are satisfied. Taste admonishment: "The most important thing when using medicine for children is to be gentle and alert. You will know after one dose, and it will be over after the second dose. If it does not work, try a new prescription."',"先生治春温重症，见壮热烦渴、汗出脉洪者，仿白虎汤意而重用石膏，配银翘透表；若舌绛神昏，则清营透热转气，兼以开窍。其治肝胃不和之胃脘痛，以柴胡疏肝散为主方，随证加左金、金铃，每获良效。":"To treat severe cases of spring fever, with strong heat, polydipsia, sweating, and rapid pulse, use gypsum to imitate the meaning of Baihu Decoction, and add Yinqiao to penetrate the surface; if the tongue is red and faint, use the method to clear the body, penetrate the heat, turn the Qi, and open up the orifices. For the treatment of epigastric pain caused by disharmony between the liver and stomach, Bupleurum Shugan Powder is the main prescription, and Zuojin and Jinling are added according to the syndrome, and good results are obtained every time.","先生治疑难杂症，善以大方复法合治。如治慢性萎缩性胃炎，从益气健脾、疏肝和胃、活血通络、清热解毒四法入手，分层递进；治顽固性失眠，交通心肾、调和肝脾、安神定志诸法并行，条理井然。其辨证之细腻、立法之周全，识者叹服。":"Mr. Wang treats difficult and complicated diseases and is good at using comprehensive methods to treat them. For example, to treat chronic atrophic gastritis, we should start with the four methods of replenishing qi and strengthening the spleen, soothing the liver and stomach, activating blood circulation and unblocking collaterals, and clearing away heat and detoxification, and progress in layers; to treat intractable insomnia, the methods of communicating with the heart and kidneys, harmonizing the liver and spleen, and calming the mind and calming the mind should be used in parallel and in a well-organized manner. Those who know him will be impressed by his delicate diagnosis and comprehensive legislation.","先生行医滇中七十载，遇时疫流行辄挺身而出，活人无算，乡里德之。":"Mr. Wang has been practicing medicine in central Yunnan for seventy years. He often comes forward when epidemics occur.","先生行医滇中，以针灸起大症、愈痼疾，求诊者踵相接，声名远播。":"He practiced medicine in central Yunnan. He used acupuncture to cure serious symptoms and cure chronic diseases. He received many patients seeking treatment and his reputation spread far and wide.","先生诊余设帐授徒，从游者众，常训弟子曰：“经方者，医道之规矩也；不以规矩，不能成方圆。”":`After the doctor's work, he set up a tent to teach disciples, and there were many tourists. He often taught his disciples: "Those who give prescriptions are the rules of medicine. If you don't follow the rules, you can't make a circle."`,"先生诊务之余笔耕不辍，著有《麻疹发微》《伤寒论讲义》《吴佩衡医案》等，其医案理法方药丝丝入扣，为后学临证之津梁。":`In addition to his clinical work, Mr. Wang kept writing, and wrote "The Micronization of Measles", "Lecture Notes on Febrile Diseases", "Wu Peiheng's Medical Cases", etc. His medical cases, methods, prescriptions and medicines are very detailed, and they are the basis for later studies in clinical diagnosis.`,"先生遍尝滇南百草，访诸彝、白各族药农，汇成《滇南本草》三卷，收载滇产药物四百余种。":'Mr. Li tasted all kinds of herbs in southern Yunnan and interviewed drug farmers of the Yi and Bai ethnic groups. He compiled the three volumes of "Southern Yunnan Materia Medica", which contains more than 400 kinds of medicines produced in Yunnan.',全书阅读:"Read the whole book",全屏:"full screen",全部:"All",全部医案:"All medical records",全部名医:"All famous doctors",全部著作:"All works",六百年医脉:"Six hundred years of medical pulse",六经辨证体系讲解条理清晰:"The Six Classics Syndrome Differentiation System is clearly explained","六经辨证验案，以经方起大症。":"The six meridians are used to differentiate the syndrome and verify the case, and use the meridians to cause serious symptoms.",兰茂:"Lan Mao","兰茂1397年生于云南嵩明杨林，隐居不仕，躬耕著述，世称“兰隐君”。":'Lan Mao was born in Yanglin, Songming, Yunnan in 1397. He lived in seclusion and was not an official, devoted himself to farming and writing, and was known as "Lanyinjun" in the world.',"兰茂谓方不在多、中病则灵，药不在贵、对证则验，此编之宗旨也。书中又嘱采药须识土宜、制药须遵古法，勿以伪乱真、以生代熟，其慎于医药如此。":"Lan Mao said that it does not matter if there are too many prescriptions, it will cure the disease; it does not matter if the medicine is expensive, it will prove the symptoms. This is the purpose of this compilation. The book also instructs you to know the appropriate soil when picking medicines, and to follow ancient methods when making medicines. Do not mix fakes with real ones, or substitute raw materials for cooked ones. This is the same as medicine.","兰茂，字廷秀，号止庵，云南嵩明人。明代著名医药学家、音韵学家，所著《滇南本草》为现存最早的区域性本草专著，早于《本草纲目》百余年。":`Lan Mao, courtesy name Tingxiu and nickname Zhi'an, was born in Songming, Yunnan. A famous medical scientist and phonologist in the Ming Dynasty, his "Southern Yunnan Materia Medica" is the earliest existing regional monograph on materia medica, predating the "Compendium of Materia Medica" by more than a hundred years.`,"共 {n} 条":"Total {n} items",共建单位:"Co-constructed unit",关闭:"close","其“夏氏推拿”手法刚柔相济，以“稳、准、轻、巧”著称。":'His "Xia massage" technique combines hardness and softness, and is famous for being "stable, accurate, light and skillful".',"其临证医案由门人整理成帙，辨证用药之精，识者谓得温病三昧。":"His clinical medical records were compiled into a collection by his disciples. The essence of syndrome differentiation and medication was known by those who knew him to be the samadhi of febrile disease.","其时间针法之应用经验，为云南针灸界所重。":"His experience in the application of time acupuncture is valued by the acupuncture community in Yunnan.",典:"classic","养心安神，润燥舒郁":"Nourish the heart and calm the mind, moisturize dryness and relieve depression","养血填精，温通奇经，调经种子":"Nourishes blood and replenishes essence, warms and regulates irregular menstruation, regulates menstruation seeds","内、外、妇、儿各科民间验方汇编，简便廉验。":"A compilation of folk prescriptions for internal medicine, surgery, gynecology, and pediatrics, simple and easy to test.","内伤杂病重视肝胃，善以调和肝胃之法愈久病痼疾。":"Internal injuries and miscellaneous diseases attach great importance to the liver and stomach. The method of harmonizing the liver and stomach can cure chronic diseases.",内妇儿科:"Internal Medicine and Pediatrics",内妇儿科篇:"Internal Medicine and Pediatrics",内容提要:"Executive summary",内科:"Internal Medicine","内科 · 妇科 · 儿科":"Internal Medicine · Gynecology · Pediatrics","内科、妇科疑难杂症治验丰富":"Rich experience in treating difficult and complicated diseases in internal medicine and gynecology",内科杂病:"Internal medicine miscellaneous diseases","内科杂病、妇科调经、儿科痘疹之验案。":"Case studies on miscellaneous internal diseases, gynecological menstruation regulation, and pediatric acne.","内科杂病重视脾肾，妇科诸疾重在调肝肾、和冲任。":"Internal medicine and miscellaneous diseases focus on the spleen and kidneys, while gynecological diseases focus on regulating the liver and kidneys and regulating the kidneys.","内科痰饮、水肿诸案，温中化饮不离苓桂术甘、真武法；妇科痛经、崩漏多从冲任虚寒论治，温经养血而经自调；儿科痘疹治法与麻疹相发明，皆以保阳气、助透发为要。":"For cases of phlegm and edema in internal medicine, warming and resolving fluids is inseparable from the sweetness of Linggui and Zhenwu. Gynecological dysmenorrhea and metrorrhagia are often treated based on Chong Ren deficiency and cold theory, which warms the menstruation and nourishes the blood and regulates the menstruation. The treatment of pediatric acne is similar to that of measles, both of which focus on protecting yang qi and helping to penetrate the hair.",内科篇:"Internal Medicine",内科经验:"Internal Medicine Experience","再如治昆明市长曾某之子伤寒重症，认为“一线生阳有将脱之势，病势垂危，颇为费治":'Another example is the treatment of the son of Kunming Mayor Zeng who suffered from severe typhoid fever. He believed that "the first line of yang has the potential to escape, and the disease is critical, which is quite expensive to treat."',"再如治昆明市长曾某之子伤寒重症，认为“一线生阳有将脱之势，病势垂危，颇为费治。惟有扶阳抑阴温化之法，使在上之寒水阴邪，由口中吐出，中下之寒水阴邪，由二便排泻使除.，阳回阴退，方可转危为安”。以通脉四逆汤加吴萸、上桂治之，白附片用至160g，“并告知病家，倘若服药后发生呕吐涎痰或大便泻下切勿惊疑，为病除之兆，一线生机可望挽回”。服上方后，果呕吐涎水碗许，大便溏泻1次，手足温暖，脉和缓较有神，系病除之兆。继以大剂扶阳温化，白附片用至260g。服药后，又呕吐涎水约两碗，大便泻利数次，“均属冰霜化行，病毒阴邪由上下窍道溃退”之兆。继守原法调理至痊。":'Another example is the treatment of the son of Kunming Mayor Zeng who was seriously ill with typhoid fever. He believed that "the first line of yang has the potential to escape, and the disease is critical, so it is quite expensive to treat." Only by supporting the yang and suppressing the yin and warming it up, so that the cold water yin evil in the upper part can be spit out from the mouth, and the cold water yin evil in the middle and lower part can be eliminated by defecation and diarrhea. Only when the yang returns and the yin retreats can the crisis be turned into peace." Add Wuyu and Shanggui to the Maisini Decoction, and use Baifu Tablets up to 160g. "And tell the patient not to be alarmed if vomiting, sputum, or diarrhea occurs after taking the medicine. It is a sign of cure. The first line is "The vitality is expected to be restored." After taking the medicine, he vomited about two bowls of saliva and had loose stools once, his hands and feet were warm, and his pulse was gentle and energetic, which was a sign that the disease was cured. Then he used a large dose of Fuyang to warm up, and used Baifu Tablets up to 260g. After taking the medicine, he vomited about two bowls of saliva and had loose stools several times.',"冷水奇治春温病 李某，女，年五旬，住四川省会理县":"Cold water can cure spring fever. Li, female, 50 years old, lives in Huili County, Sichuan Province","冷水奇治春温病\\n李某，女，年五旬，住四川省会理县。1920年2月患春温病已5日，延吴佩衡诊视之时，见其张目不寐，壮热烦渴而饮冷，舌苔白厚而燥，舌尖绛，唇焦齿干，脉来洪数，恶热头痛，小便短赤。据云已服发表之剂未愈。查前所服之方，系用羌活、独活、苏叶、荆芥、防风、柴胡、葛根之剂。服后但见头汗出，身热尤甚，气粗而喘，烦渴引饮。\\n吴氏断为春温病误用辛温发散，耗劫阴液所致。急须清热养阴生津为治。因居处远乡僻壤，药材缺乏，未能如愿配方。但见患者烦渴索饮之状，遂与冰凉之冷水任意饮之。饮一碗尽，自言心中爽快，又求再饮。饮至四碗，顿觉清凉不烦，竟然闭目熟睡。俄顷则见汗出淋漓，湿透内衣。约半个时辰后再诊，已脉静身凉，津液满口，诸症悉除。\\n吴氏总结到：春温初起，客邪内传与阳明燥气相合，误投辛散发表，不但邪不得解，反致伤阴劫液，内热燔炽，水源涸竭。今得冷水相济，补阴救焚，从而阴阳调平，气机通达，则汗出而引邪外散。此为饮冷水救阴液之例，当与人参白虎汤清热生津救焚之意谋同，故能获此良效。\\n温热病证，内热如焚，真阴欲竭之际，急需清凉之剂以济之。西瓜汁、鲜梨汁，甚至清凉冷饮，皆可以滋添阴液。某些病家或医者囿于习俗，以为凡病皆须忌生冷，虽病热者苦索无已，尚不知其相宜而须投之。实热病情，以硝、黄、石膏为治，其效若灵，滋阴清热苦寒之品在所必用，又何须拘禁于生凉哉！（《吴佩衡医案》）":`Cold water can cure spring fever\\nLi, female, in her fifties, lives in Huili County, Sichuan Province. In February 1920, he suffered from spring febrile disease for 5 days. When Yan Wu Peiheng examined him, he found that he could not sleep with his eyes open, had strong fever and polydipsia and drank cold drinks, thick white and dry tongue coating, reddish tip of tongue, burnt lips and dry teeth, rapid and rapid pulse, aversion to heat and headache, and short and red urine. According to the cloud, the patient has not recovered after taking the published medicine. The prescription taken before the examination was based on Qianghuo, Duhuo, Suye, Schizonepeta, Fangfeng, Bupleurum and Pueraria. After taking it, I noticed sweating on my head, especially body heat, shortness of breath and wheezing, and polydipsia leading to drinking. \\nWu's diagnosis is that spring fever disease is caused by misuse of pungent and warm medicine, which consumes Jie Yin fluid. Urgent treatment requires clearing away heat, nourishing yin and promoting fluid production. Because I lived in a remote area and lacked medicinal materials, I was unable to achieve the desired formula. But when the patient is thirsty and wants to drink, he drinks it with icy cold water as he pleases. After finishing the bowl, he said that he felt refreshed and begged to drink again. After drinking four bowls, I suddenly felt cool and relieved, and fell asleep with my eyes closed. After a while, he was sweating profusely and his underwear was soaked through. When I checked again about half an hour later, my pulse was stagnant, my body was cool, my mouth was full of body fluids, and all symptoms were gone. \\nWu concluded: At the beginning of the spring temperature, the internal heat of guest evil coincides with the dryness of Yangming. If you mistakenly add Xin powder to release, not only will the evil be unsolved, but it will damage the Yin Jie liquid, burn the internal heat, and dry up the water source. Today, cold water can be used to supplement the yin and relieve the burning, so that the yin and yang are balanced and the qi is unobstructed, causing sweating and attracting evil spirits to disperse. This is an example of drinking cold water to save Yin liquid. It should be consistent with the purpose of Ginseng Baihu Decoction to clear away heat, promote fluid production and save Yin, so it can achieve this good effect. \\nIn the syndrome of warm-heat disease, when the internal heat is burning and the true yin is exhausted, there is an urgent need for a cooling agent to relieve it. Watermelon juice, fresh pear juice, and even refreshing cold drinks can nourish Yin fluid. Some patients or doctors are limited by customs and believe that raw and cold should be avoided in all diseases. Although those who are sick with heat are suffering endlessly, they still do not know the appropriateness and need to treat them. For the condition of excessive heat, saltpeter, Huang, and gypsum are used to treat the disease. They are very effective. Products that nourish yin, clear away heat and bitter cold are a must, so there is no need to confine yourself to cold! ("Medical Cases of Wu Peiheng")`,分类导航:"Category navigation",分类检索:"Search","分类检索 | 云南名医馆":"Category Search | Yunnan Famous Medical Center",刘以敏:"Liu Yimin","刘以敏先生1935年生，专攻儿科数十载，活儿无算，滇中父老呼为“刘一帖”。":'Mr. Liu Yimin was born in 1935. He has specialized in pediatrics for decades. He has no job and is called "Liu Yitie" by his elders in central Yunnan.',"刘以敏，云南中医儿科名家，擅治小儿咳喘、厌食、泄泻诸疾，处方轻清平和，尤重小儿脾胃之护养。":"Liu Yimin is a famous pediatrician of traditional Chinese medicine in Yunnan. He is good at treating cough, asthma, anorexia, diarrhea and other diseases in children. His prescriptions are light and gentle, and he pays special attention to the care of children's spleen and stomach.",刘氏小儿止嗽方:"Liu's Children's Cough Recipe",则:"rule",则医案:"medical records",创办昆明市中医医院:"Founded Kunming Traditional Chinese Medicine Hospital","创立“证候层级辨证”理论":'Created the theory of "syndrome level differentiation"',"初热期、见形期、收没期三期透发法度。":"There are three phases of revealing the method: the initial heat period, the visible period, and the withdrawal period.",前往检索:"Go to search","力主“以透为顺、以陷为逆”的麻疹治疗总纲":'Advocating the general outline of measles treatment of "taking penetration as smooth and sinking as reverse"',功效:"Efficacy","包卉的堂舅，就是在20世纪40年代患伤寒厥脱重症的曾道坚，当时先…":"Bao Hui’s cousin was Zeng Daojian, who recovered from severe typhoid fever in the 1940s. At that time...","包卉的堂舅，就是在20世纪40年代患伤寒厥脱重症的曾道坚，当时先被送到范秉哲博士的医院，经相关检查后诊断为“肠伤寒”，使用各种抗菌针药近20日，仍剧烈腹痛难忍，随时有肠出血及肠穿孔的危险，真是命悬一线，危在旦夕。群医无策，嘱备后事。范院长的挚友徐彪南建议邀请吴佩衡先生前来诊治。范秉哲（1901-1993），曾道坚夫人的伯父，毕业于法国里昂大学医学院，获医学博士学位。1937年亲自主持创办了国立云南大学医学院（今昆明医学院）并任院长。1942〜1943年任国立云南大学医学院附属医院院长兼外科主任。新中国成立后回国，受到周恩来总理亲切接见，之后任北京友谊医院外科主任、肿瘤研究所所长，是我国著名的胸外科专家。\\n徐彪南，内科专家，医学教育家，云南医学医药发展事业的奠基人和开拓者，曾任南京中央医院主治医师。新中国成立后任昆华医院院长、云南省卫生厅副厅长、中华医学会常务理事。据包卉转述其舅母（曾道坚夫人）的回忆，吴佩衡赶到医院时已是晚上9点钟，当时病人嘴唇发青，腹痛难忍，不停地呻吟，身体不能转侧，已多日不能入睡，痛苦不堪。吴佩衡详细了解了病情经过，仔细诊过脉舌后，即以大剂量的附片、干姜、肉桂等药施治。1日后，曾道坚腹痛缓解、转危为安（吴佩衡就留在医院每日诊视，每日1剂中药，每剂附片好几两）。第2日，每剂附片又增加剂量，病情明显减轻。5日后已不腹痛，饮食增加，脸色转红润。10日后，曾道坚精神、饮食、睡眠都已恢复如常，病已痊愈，但身体仍较瘦弱。吴佩衡又先后开了一些建中气、培脾胃、补气血的中药，连续调理了10余天，曾道坚已完全恢复健康，体质比生病前还健康。\\n整个救治过程惊心动魄，令人拍案叫绝。范柄哲先生亦西医名家，曾惊叹为“神”。":`Bao Hui's cousin, Zeng Daojian, was seriously ill with typhoid fever in the 1940s. He was first sent to Dr. Fan Bingzhe's hospital. After relevant examinations, he was diagnosed with "enteric typhoid". After taking various antibacterial injections for nearly 20 days, he still suffered from severe abdominal pain and was in danger of intestinal bleeding and intestinal perforation at any time. His life was hanging by a thread. The doctors were at a loss and asked to prepare for the future. Dean Fan's close friend Xu Biaonan suggested inviting Mr. Wu Peiheng to come for diagnosis and treatment. Fan Bingzhe (1901-1993), the uncle of Mrs. Zeng Daojian, graduated from the School of Medicine of the University of Lyon in France and received a doctorate in medicine. In 1937, he personally presided over the establishment of the National Yunnan University Medical College (now Kunming Medical College) and served as its dean. From 1942 to 1943, he served as the dean and chief of surgery of the Affiliated Hospital of National Yunnan University School of Medicine. After the founding of New China, he returned to China and was cordially received by Premier Zhou Enlai. He later served as director of surgery at Beijing Friendship Hospital and director of the Oncology Institute. He is a famous thoracic surgery expert in my country. \\nXu Biaonan, an internal medicine expert, medical educator, founder and pioneer of medical development in Yunnan, once served as the attending physician of Nanjing Central Hospital. After the founding of New China, he served as president of Kunhua Hospital, deputy director of the Yunnan Provincial Department of Health, and executive director of the Chinese Medical Association. According to the memories of her aunt (Mrs. Zeng Daojian) relayed by Bao Hui, it was already 9 o'clock in the evening when Wu Peiheng rushed to the hospital. At that time, the patient's lips were blue, his abdomen was in unbearable pain, he kept moaning, he could not turn his body sideways, and he had been unable to sleep for many days and was in excruciating pain. Wu Peiheng learned about the condition in detail, and after carefully diagnosing the pulse and tongue, he treated it with large doses of Fu Pian, dried ginger, cinnamon and other medicines. One day later, Zeng Daojian's abdominal pain was relieved and the crisis was over. (Wu Peiheng stayed in the hospital for daily check-ups, one dose of traditional Chinese medicine a day, and several taels of tablets for each dose). On the second day, the dose of Futian was increased after each dose, and the condition was significantly relieved. After 5 days, she no longer had abdominal pain, was eating more food, and her face turned rosy. Ten days later, Zeng Daojian's energy, diet, and sleep returned to normal, and his illness was cured, but his body was still thin. Wu Peiheng successively prescribed some traditional Chinese medicines to build the central qi, strengthen the spleen and stomach, and replenish qi and blood. After more than 10 days of continuous conditioning, Zeng Daojian has completely recovered and his body is healthier than before the illness. \\nThe entire treatment process was thrilling and amazing. Mr. Fan Pingzhe is also a famous Western medicine expert and was once praised as a "god".`,化裁:"Chemical tailoring",医:"doctor",医案:"medical records",医案来源:"Medical record source","医案详情 | 云南名医馆":"Medical record details | Yunnan Famous Medical Center",医案集:"Medical records collection","医案集 · 本草方书":"Collection of Medical Records · Materia Medica Prescriptions",医案条目:"Medical record entries",动态数据:"Dynamic Data","馆藏医案分类数据一览，覆盖九大科室，数据持续更新。":"An overview of the collection's medical records across nine major departments, with data updated continuously.","医药与音韵、儒学相通，博学而后能精于医。":"Medicine is connected with phonology and Confucianism. After being knowledgeable, one can be good at medicine.","十二经筋、奇经八脉辨证取穴纲要。":"An outline of syndrome differentiation and acupoint selection for the twelve tendons and eight extra meridians.","午后发热案 杨某，女，30岁，2008年11月28日诊":"Case of fever in the afternoon: Yang, female, 30 years old, diagnosed on November 28, 2008","午后发热案\\n杨某，女，30岁，2008年11月28日诊。午后发热已20	多日，一直用抗生素输液治疗未效。症见面色㿠白无华，头昏神疲体倦，少气懒言，经化验检查，排除“伤寒”“肺结核”。舌淡苔薄白，脉沉细无力。诊为阳虚发热。法当回阳收纳，引阳归舍，方用白通汤加味治之：\\n附片40g，干姜15g，北细辛6g，葱头3枚。2剂（第1剂以生姜代干姜）。 \\n3日后相告，服第1剂药后发热渐退；2剂服完热未再发，精神恢复。\\n原按：阳虚发热，时有发生，临床治十数例，皆以此法治之，2剂收功，无一不效。此方妙在细辛配合姜、附，可把外浮之阳纳之归舍。":'Case of fever in the afternoon\\nYang, female, 30 years old, diagnosed on November 28, 2008. I have had fever in the afternoon for more than 20 days and have been treated with antibiotic infusions to no avail. Symptoms include pale complexion, dizziness and fatigue, lack of breath and laziness. After laboratory examination, "typhoid fever" and "tuberculosis" were ruled out. Pale tongue with thin white coating, slow and weak pulse. The diagnosis was Yang deficiency and fever. When the method is to return the yang and absorb it, and induce the yang to return to the body, use Baitong Decoction with the following ingredients: 40g of Fu Pian, 15g of dried ginger, 6g of Asarum, and 3 green onions. 2 doses (for the first dose, substitute fresh ginger for dried ginger). \\nI told you 3 days later that the fever gradually subsided after taking the first dose of medicine. After taking the second dose, the fever did not reoccur and I recovered. \\nOriginal note: Fever due to yang deficiency occurs from time to time. Dozens of clinical cases were treated with this method. After 2 doses, all of them were ineffective. The magic of this recipe lies in the combination of Asarum and Ginger and Fu, which can absorb the floating yang and return it to its home.',半产血崩:"Hemipartum hemirrhage","半产血崩 （流产失血） 方某夫人，年三十五岁，罗平县人,住云南省…":"Semipartum hemorrhagic metrorrhagia (blood loss from miscarriage) Mrs. Fang, 35 years old, from Luoping County, lives in Yunnan Province...","半产血崩 （流产失血） 方某夫人，年三十五岁，罗平县人,住云南省昆明市红栅 子十号，素患半产。1923年5月12日，孕五月又堕。初起腰腹 坠痛,继则见红胎堕,血崩盈盆成块,小腹扭痛，心慌目眩，气 喘欲脱，脉芤虚无力，两寸且短。唇淡红，舌苔白滑，舌质夹青 乌。据其夫云,是晚曾昏绝二次。由于素患半产，肾气大亏,气 虚下陷，无力摄血，阳气有随血下脱之势。以气生于肾，统于 肺,今肺肾之气不相接,故气喘欲脱。拟四逆当归补血汤加枣 艾治之。方中四逆汤扶阳收纳，启坎阳上升，佐以黄芪、当归， 补中益气而生过伤之血，干姜、艾、枣制黑,能温血分之寒，引 血归经。 黑附片160克，炮黑姜50克，炙甘草24克，北口芪60 克，当归26克，蕲艾6克（炒黑存性），大枣5枚（烧黑存性）。 13日服一剂后，血崩止,气喘平，病状已去六、七,精神稍 增。仍守原方,14日次剂服完，证遂全瘳。":"Hemorrhagic metrorrhagia (blood loss from miscarriage) Mrs. Fang, 35 years old, from Luoping County, lives at No. 10, Hongzhazi, Kunming City, Yunnan Province. She has always suffered from hemorrhagic metrorrhagia. On May 12, 1923, she gave birth again in the fifth month of pregnancy. It starts with pain in the waist and abdomen, followed by red abortion, bleeding in the basin and lumps, twisting pain in the lower abdomen, palpitation and dizziness, breathlessness, weak and weak pulse, two inches and short. The lips are light red, the tongue coating is white and slippery, and the tongue is blue and black. According to her husband, she fainted twice that night. Due to the condition of partial labor, the kidney qi is greatly depleted, the qi is deficient and sagging, and it is unable to absorb blood, and the yang qi has the tendency to fall off with the blood. Qi is generated in the kidneys and is unified in the lungs. Now the qi in the lungs and kidneys are not connected, so you have asthma and want to escape. It is treated with Sini Danggui Buxue Decoction plus jujube and moxibustion. In the prescription, Sini Decoction is used to support the yang and activate the yang to rise. It is supplemented with astragalus and angelica to replenish the qi and generate blood due to injury. Dried ginger, mugwort and jujube are used to make black, which can warm the cold in the blood and guide the blood to return to the menstruation. 160 grams of Black Fu slices, 50 grams of Paohei ginger, 24 grams of Zhigancao, 60 grams of Beikou stilbene, 26 grams of Angelica sinensis, 6 grams of Qi Ai (roasted black for its properties), and 5 jujubes (for its black properties when roasted). After taking one dose on the 13th, the bleeding stopped, the asthma subsided, the symptoms disappeared for 6-7 days, and the energy level increased slightly. Still sticking to the original prescription, after taking the first dose on the 14th, the symptoms disappeared completely.","半产血崩案 方夫人，35岁，罗平县人":"Hemipartum hemorrhagic collapse Mrs. Fang, 35 years old, from Luoping County","半产血崩案\\n方夫人，35岁，罗平县人。素患半产，此次怀孕5月又堕。初起腰腹坠痛，继则见红胎堕，血崩盈盈成块，小腹扭痛，心慌目眩，气喘欲脱；脉芤虚无力，两寸且短；唇淡红，舌苔白滑，舌质夹青乌。据云，是晚曾昏厥2次。由素患半产，肾气大亏，气虚下陷，无力摄血，阳气有随血脱之势。以气生于肾，统于肺，今肺肾之气不相接，故气喘欲脱。以四逆汤扶阳收纳，启坎阳上升为君，佐以当归补血汤补中益气而生过伤之血，艾、枣温血分之寒，引血归经：\\n黑附片150g，炮黑姜45g，炙草24g，北口芪60g，当归24g，蕲艾叶6g（炒），大枣5枚（烧黑存性）。\\n1剂后，血崩止，气喘平，病状十之已去六七，精神稍增，仍用原方1剂服完，证遂痊愈。\\n按：下部出血诸症如血崩、便血等，以四逆汤启坎阳上升为君，佐以当归补血汤补中益气而生过伤之血，艾叶、大枣温血分之寒，此案用药堪作范例。":"Semi-partum hemorrhagic collapse\\nMrs. Fang, 35 years old, from Luoping County. I had always suffered from partial labor, but this time I had another miscarriage in May. It starts with pain in the waist and abdomen, followed by red abortion, bleeding and lumps, lower abdominal twisting pain, palpitation, dizziness, and breathlessness; pulse is weak and weak, two inches and short; lips are light red, tongue coating is white and slippery, and the tongue is green and black. According to the cloud, he fainted twice that night. Due to Su suffering from partial labor, the kidney qi is greatly depleted, the qi is deficient and sagging, and the yang qi tends to be lost with the blood. Qi originates from the kidneys and is controlled by the lungs. Now the qi in the lungs and kidneys are not connected, so the breath is breathless. Use Sini Decoction to support the yang, Qi Kan Yang ascends to the king, and use Danggui Buxue Decoction to replenish the middle and replenish qi to produce the blood of the injury. Mugwort and jujube warm the blood and lead the blood to return to the menstruation: 150g of black fusilli slices, 45g of black ginger, 24g of zhicao, 60g of Beikouqi, 24g of angelica, 6g of mugwort leaves (fried), 5 jujubes (burned black to preserve the properties). \\nAfter 1 dose, the bleeding stopped, the asthma subsided, 67% of the symptoms were gone, and the energy level increased slightly. I still took 1 dose of the original prescription, and the symptoms were cured. \\nNote: For symptoms of bleeding in the lower part, such as bleeding, hematochezia, hematochezia, etc., use Sini Decoction to activate Kanyang and ascend to the throne, and use Danggui Buxue Decoction to replenish qi and produce blood due to injuries. Mugwort leaves and jujube warm the blood and make it cold. This case of medicine can be used as an example.","半产血崩案\\n方夫人，35岁，罗平县人。素患半产，此次怀孕五月又堕。初起腰腹坠痛，继则见红胎堕，血崩盈盈成块，小腹扭痛，心慌目眩，气喘欲脱。脉芤虚无力，两寸且短；唇淡红，舌苔白滑，舌质夹青乌。据其丈夫云，是晚曾昏厥2次。由素患半产，肾气大亏，气虚下陷，无力摄血，阳气有随血脱之势。以气生于肾，统于肺，今肺肾之气不相接，故气喘欲脱。以四逆汤扶阳收纳，启坎阳上升为君，佐以当归补血汤，补中益气而生过伤之血，艾、枣温血分之寒，引血归经：\\n黑附片150g，炮黑姜45g，炙草24g，北口芪60g，当归24g，薪艾叶6g（炒），大枣5枚（烧黑存性）。\\n1剂后，血崩止，气喘平，病状已去十之六七，精神稍增；仍用原方1剂服完，证遂痊愈。\\n按：下部出血诸症如血崩、便血等，以四逆汤启坎阳上升为君，佐以当归补血汤，补中益气而生过伤之血，艾叶、大枣温血分之寒，2剂即收痊愈之功，吴氏此案用药堪作范例。":"Semi-partum hemorrhagic collapse\\nMrs. Fang, 35 years old, from Luoping County. She was suffering from partial labor, and she had another miscarriage in May of this pregnancy. It starts with pain in the waist and abdomen, followed by red fetal abort, bleeding in lumps, twisting pain in the lower abdomen, palpitations, dizziness, and panting. The pulse is weak and weak, two inches and short; the lips are light red, the tongue coating is white and slippery, and the tongue is green and black. According to her husband, she fainted twice that night. Due to Su suffering from partial labor, the kidney qi is greatly depleted, the qi is deficient and sagging, and the yang qi tends to be lost with the blood. Qi originates from the kidneys and is controlled by the lungs. Now the qi in the lungs and kidneys are not connected, so the breath is breathless. Use Sini Decoction to support the Yang, Qi Kan Yang ascends to the king, and use Danggui Buxue Decoction to replenish the middle and replenish the qi to generate the blood of the injury. Mugwort and jujube warm the blood and lead the blood to return to the menstruation:\\nBlack Fu Shen 150g, Paohei Jiang 45g, Zhicao 24g, Beikou Qi 60g, Angelica 24g, 6g mugwort leaves (fried), 5 jujubes (burned black to preserve the properties). \\nAfter 1 dose, the bleeding stopped, the asthma subsided, 60% of the symptoms were gone, and the energy level increased slightly. After taking 1 dose of the original prescription, the symptoms were cured. \\nNote: For symptoms of bleeding in the lower part, such as hemorrhagic collapse, hematochezia, etc., use Sini Decoction to activate Kanyang and ascend to the throne, and supplement it with Danggui Buxue Decoction, which can replenish the middle and replenish the qi and generate blood from the injury. Mugwort and jujube warm the blood and separate it from the cold. 2 doses will cure the disease. Wu's use of medicine in this case can be used as an example.","卫分证甚者，加桑叶、菊花；气分大热者，石膏加至90g，加知母；入营分者，加犀角、生地、玄参":"If the Wei syndrome is severe, add mulberry leaves and chrysanthemums; if the Qi syndrome is severe, add gypsum to 90g and add anemarrhena; if the Ying syndrome is severe, add rhinoceros horn, rehmannia root, and scrophulariaceae.","危急重症之果断处置与经方救逆。":"Decisive treatment of critical and severe cases and rescue with classic prescriptions.","卷一 · 山草部":"Volume 1 · Mountain and Grass Department","卷三 · 毒草部":"Volume 3 · Poisonous Weeds Department","卷二 · 芳草部":"Volume 2·Fragrant Grass Department",历代名医:"Famous doctors of all ages",厌食:"anorexia",厥阴病篇:"Jueyin disease",厥阴病缩睾证:"Jueyin disease and testicle shrinkage syndrome","厥阴病缩睾证 马某，男，二十七岁，门诊号9546":"Jueyin disease and testicle shrinkage syndrome: Ma, male, 27 years old, clinic number 9546","厥阴病缩睾证 马某，男，二十七岁，门诊号9546。患者右侧睾丸肿痛二 月余,治疗后肿痛逐渐消退。某日夜间，右侧睾丸突然收引回 缩至少腹。少腹拘挛疼痛不已，牵引腰部，痛不能伸,痛剧之 时，连及脐腹，直至四肢挛急难以屈伸。颜面发青，冷汗淋漓。 其亲友略知医理,认为此证系肾精亏损所致，拟滋阴补肾之 剂，服后未见缓解，遂送中医学院附设门诊部就诊。刻诊患者 面色发青，腹痛呻吟，愁容不展，两目无神，白睛发蓝，唇、舌、 指甲均含青色。舌苔白腻，手足冰冷，脉来沉细弦紧。已两日 水米不进。此系肝肾阳虚，厥阴阴寒太盛，阳不足以温熙筋 脉。《内经》云“肝是厥阴之脉……循股阴，入毛中，过阴器，抵 小腹……”经脉失养，故拘挛收引，致使睾丸回缩而痛，即所 谓“寒则收引”之意。法当温扶肝肾之阳,温经散寒,经脉之挛 急自能舒缓。方用当归四逆汤加味。 当归15克，桂枝12克，杭白芍9克，细辛6克，通草6 克，大枣5枚，干姜12克，吴茱萸6克，川椒5克（炒黄），乌 梅4枚，附片60克。 上方服一剂后，疼痛缓解。再剂，则阴囊松缓，睾丸回复。 面目、唇舌青色俱退。手足回温，诸痛皆愈。唯阳神尚虚，照原 方去川椒,加砂仁9克，连服二剂,精神、饮食均恢复正常。":`Jueyin disease testicle shrinkage syndrome: Ma, male, 27 years old, clinic number 9546. The patient's right testicle had been swollen and painful for more than two months, and the swelling and pain gradually subsided after treatment. One night, the right testicle suddenly retracted and retracted to the abdomen. The pain is endless due to spasm in the lower abdomen, which pulls the waist, making it impossible to stretch. When the pain is severe, it reaches the umbilicus and abdomen, until the limbs are so tight that it is difficult to bend or extend. His face turned blue and he was dripping with cold sweat. His relatives and friends knew a little about medical science and believed that the syndrome was caused by the loss of kidney essence. They took a medicine intended to nourish yin and nourish the kidney. However, no relief was found after taking the medicine, so they sent him to the outpatient department of the College of Traditional Chinese Medicine for treatment. During the examination, the patient's complexion was blue, he was moaning with abdominal pain, his face was sad, his eyes were dull, his white eyes were blue, and his lips, tongue, and nails were all blue. The tongue coating is white and greasy, the hands and feet are cold, and the pulse is heavy, thin and stringy. It has been two days without water or rice. This is due to deficiency of liver and kidney yang, excessive yin and coldness in Jueyin, and insufficient yang to warm the tendons and veins. "Nei Jing" says that "the liver is the pulse of Jueyin... it follows the femoral yin, enters the hair, passes through the vagina, and reaches the lower abdomen..." The meridians are out of nourishment, so they contract and contract, causing the testicles to retract and hurt, which is the so-called "cold causes contraction". The method should warm and support the yang of the liver and kidneys, warm the meridians and dispel cold, and soothe the contraction and urgency of the meridians. Add Danggui Sini Decoction to taste. 15 grams of angelica root, 12 grams of cinnamon twig, 9 grams of white peony root, 6 grams of asarum, 6 grams of Tongcao, 5 jujubes, 12 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of Evodia, 5 grams of Sichuan pepper (fried yellow), 4 ebony plums, and 60 grams of Futian. After taking one dose above, the pain was relieved. After another dose, the scrotum will relax and the testicles will recover. The blue color of the face, lips and tongue all faded away. The hands and feet are warmed back, and all pains are relieved. Only the yang spirit was still weak, so I removed the Sichuan pepper and added 9 grams of amomum villosum according to the original prescription. After taking two doses, my spirit and diet returned to normal.`,厥阴证:"Jueyin syndrome","厥阴证 （耐药性金黄葡萄球菌 性急性严重型肺脓疡） 海某，女,十…":"Jueyin syndrome (drug-resistant Staphylococcus aureus acute severe lung abscess) Hai, female, ten years old...","厥阴证 （耐药性金黄葡萄球菌 性急性严重型肺脓疡） 海某，女,十九岁，昆明人,因病住昆明某医院。1959年1 月3日邀余会诊。 患者行剖腹产失血过多，经输血抢救后,突然高热40℃ 以上。经用青霉素、链霉素等治疗，数日后体温降低,但一般 情况反见恶化，神识昏瞰，出现严重呼吸困难，白细胞高达二 万以上。因病情危重，不敢搬动,故未做X线检査。当时西医 未做出明确诊断,继续以大量广谱抗生素治疗,并配合输液 及吸入氧气，均未效。延某医则投以麻杏石甘汤一剂,病情更 趋险峻,西医会诊亦提不出有效方案,乃延余诊视。 患者神志不清，面唇青紫灰黯，舌质青乌，鼻翼扑扑煽 动，呼吸忽起忽落,似潮水往复，十指连甲青乌，脉弦硬而紧, 按之无力而空。盖此病已人厥阴，肝肾之阴气内盛，非传经 病，系真脏病,心肾之阳衰弱已极，下焦之真阳不升，上焦之 阴邪不降，一线残阳将绝，已现衰脱之象，危殆费治。唯有扶 阳抑阴，强心固肾，尽力抢救垂危。主以大剂回阳饮（即四逆 汤加肉桂）。 附片150克，干姜50克，上肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑入） 甘草20克。 因附片需要先煨三、四小时,方能煨透无毒,故让患者先 服上肉桂泡水，以强心急救之。并预告病家，服此方后可能 有呕吐反应，如呕吐之后喉间痰声不响，气不喘促，舌质色 较转红，尚有一线生机可以挽回。若不如此，则为难治，请注 意为幸！ 复诊。昨日服上方后果如余言，呕吐涎痰后已见转机，神 识较前清醒，嗜卧无神，已能缓慢回答询问，可以吃流汁，舌 尖已见淡红色，舌苔白滑厚腻，口唇青紫较退，两颊紫红，鼻 翼不再煽动，呼吸仍有困难，但已不再起伏如潮，开始咳嗽， 咯大量脓痰,脉仍弦滑而紧，按之而空。衰脱危候大为减轻， 仍以扶阳温化主之。 附片150克，千姜50克，上肉桂10克（研末，池水兑 入），法半夏10克，茯苓20克，甘草8克。 三诊。神智清醒，语音清楚,面颊微转润红，指甲唇舌青 紫已退十之八、九，鼻头，目眶微青，午后潮热，喘咳气短，咯 大量脓痰，惟喉间时有痰阻，脉弦滑,病情已有转危为安之象,再以上方加减主之。 附片200克，干姜100克，茯苓30克，上肉桂10克（研 末，泡水兑入），公丁香5克，法半夏10克，橘红10克，甘草8 克，细辛5克。 四诊。面颊微红润，口唇、舌质青紫已退，呼吸渐趋平稳, 午后潮热已退，咳嗽、咯脓痰稍减少，胃气已开,能进食，人事 言语已近常态。大便溏泻,系病除之兆。夜卧多梦，此系阳不 胜阴，邪阴扰乱,神驰不宁所致。脉转和缓。大病已初退，惟坎 阳尚虚，寒温邪阴未净,再以扶阳温化主之。连服三、四剂可 望康复。 此时患者情况好转，可以搬动，经X线检查发现双肺有 多个大小不等的圆形空洞，内容物已大半排空。血液细菌培 养报告，检出耐药性金黄色葡萄球菌。医院西医最后诊断为 “耐药性金黄色葡萄球菌性急性严重型肺脓疡” 。拟方： 附片150克，干姜50克，广陈皮8克，杏仁8克（捣），炙 麻茸8克。 连服四剂，一周后诊视,患者喜笑言谈自如，精神、饮食 业已恢复，病状若失，至此痊愈。按：病至危笃之时，处方用药非大剂不能奏效。若病重药轻，犹兵不胜敌，不能克服。因此，处方用药应当随其病变而有不同。惟临床辨证，务须察明阴阳、表里、虚实、寒热，然后再针对证候之实据而下药。只要诊断确切，处方对证，药董充足，即能克敌制胜，转危为安。古有“病大药大，病毒药毒”之说，故面临危重证候勿须畏惧药“毒”而改投以轻剂。否则，杯水车薪敷衍寒责，贻误病机，则危殆难挽矣。":`Jueyin syndrome (drug-resistant Staphylococcus aureus acute severe lung abscess) Hai, female, 19 years old, from Kunming, was admitted to a hospital in Kunming due to illness. On January 3, 1959, I was invited for consultation. The patient suffered excessive blood loss during a caesarean section. After blood transfusion for rescue, she suddenly developed a high fever of over 40°C. After treatment with penicillin, streptomycin, etc., the body temperature dropped after a few days, but the general condition worsened, with confusion, severe difficulty breathing, and white blood cells reaching more than 20,000. Because his condition was critical and he did not dare to move, no X-ray examination was performed. At that time, Western medicine did not make a clear diagnosis and continued to treat the patient with large amounts of broad-spectrum antibiotics, along with infusion and oxygen inhalation, but to no avail. Doctor Yan gave me a dose of Maxing Shigan Decoction, and the condition became more serious. Western medical consultation could not come up with an effective plan, so I was delayed for examination. The patient is unconscious, his face and lips are blue and purple, his tongue is blue and black, his nose is fluttering, his breathing rises and falls like the tide, his fingers are blue and black, his pulse is hard and tight, and it is weak and empty when pressed. This disease means that the person has lost yin, and the yin energy in the liver and kidneys is excessive. It is not a menstrual disease, but a real internal disease. The yang in the heart and kidneys has been extremely weakened. The true yang in the lower burner does not rise, the yin evil in the upper burner does not fall, and the residual yang is about to die. It has been weakened and is in danger of being treated. We can only support the yang and suppress the yin, strengthen the heart and strengthen the kidneys, and try our best to rescue the dying person. Mainly use a large dose of Huiyang drink (i.e. Sini decoction plus cinnamon). 150 grams of Aconite slices, 50 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix) and 20 grams of licorice. Because the attached piece needs to be simmered for three to four hours before it can be thoroughly simmered and non-toxic, the patient is asked to take cinnamon soaked in water first to strengthen the heart. It also warns patients that they may have vomiting reactions after taking this prescription. For example, after vomiting, there is no sound of phlegm in the throat, shortness of breath, and the color of the tongue turns red. There is still a glimmer of hope for recovery. If not, it will be difficult to treat, please be careful! Follow-up visit. The results after taking the above medicine yesterday were as I said. After vomiting and spitting phlegm, I have improved my consciousness. I am more conscious than before. I feel sleepy and lethargic. I can answer questions slowly. I can eat fluids. The tip of my tongue is light red. The coating on my tongue is white and slippery. The purple lips have faded. My cheeks are purple and my nose is no longer inflamed. I still have difficulty breathing, but it is no longer undulating. I start to cough and cough up a lot of purulent phlegm. My pulse is still slippery and tight and becomes empty when I press it. The symptoms of decline and crisis are greatly alleviated, and the main method is still to support Yang and warm up. 150 grams of Fu Fian, 50 grams of ginger, 10 grams of cinnamon (ground into powder, mixed with pond water), 10 grams of pinellia, 20 grams of Poria, and 8 grams of licorice. Three diagnoses. She is conscious and clear, her voice is clear, her cheeks are slightly flushed, eight or nine tenths of the purple on her nails, lips and tongue has faded, her nose and eye sockets are slightly blue, she has hot flashes in the afternoon, wheezing and coughing, shortness of breath, and a large amount of purulent phlegm, but there is sometimes obstruction of phlegm in the throat, and her pulse is stringy and slippery. The condition has shown signs of turning into a stable condition, so the patient can be treated by adding or subtracting the above. 200 grams of Aconite, 100 grams of dried ginger, 30 grams of Poria, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 5 grams of cloves, 10 grams of Pinellia ternata, 10 grams of orange, 8 grams of licorice, and 5 grams of asarum. Four diagnoses. The cheeks are slightly rosy, the bruises on the lips and tongue have subsided, the breathing has gradually stabilized, the afternoon hot flashes have subsided, the cough and purulent phlegm have slightly decreased, the stomach qi has been relaxed, and I can eat, and my speech has become almost normal. Loose stools and diarrhea are a sign of cure. Sleeping at night and having many dreams are caused by Yang not prevailing over Yin, disturbance of evil Yin, and restlessness. The pulse is gentle and slow. The serious illness has begun to subside, but the Kan yang is still weak and the cold and warm evil yin have not been purified, so it can be controlled by supporting the yang and warming it. Recovery is expected after taking three or four doses. At this time, the patient's condition improved and he could be moved. X-ray examination revealed that there were multiple circular cavities of varying sizes in both lungs, and most of the contents had been emptied. Blood bacterial culture report detected drug-resistant Staphylococcus aureus. The hospital’s Western medicine doctor finally diagnosed the patient as “acute severe lung abscess caused by drug-resistant Staphylococcus aureus.” Preparation: 150 grams of Fu slices, 50 grams of dried ginger, 8 grams of dried tangerine peel, 8 grams of almonds (pounded), and 8 grams of roasted sesame seeds. After taking four doses, the patient was seen after a week. He was smiling and talking freely, and his energy and diet had recovered. If his symptoms were gone, he was fully recovered. Note: When the disease is in critical condition, prescription drugs cannot be effective unless large doses are used. If the disease is serious and the medicine is weak, it will still be invincible and cannot be overcome. Therefore, the prescribed medication should vary according to the disease. However, in clinical syndrome differentiation, it is necessary to identify yin and yang, exterior and interior, deficiency and excess, cold and heat, and then prescribe medicine according to the actual evidence of the syndrome. As long as the diagnosis is accurate, the prescription is correct, and the medicine is sufficient, the enemy can be defeated and the crisis can be turned into safety. There is an ancient saying that "the medicine is powerful for treating a disease, but the medicine is poisonous for viruses." Therefore, when faced with critical syndromes, there is no need to be afraid of the "poison" of the medicine and switch to a lighter dose. Otherwise, it will be a drop in the bucket to cope with the cold responsibilities, delaying the pathogenesis of the disease, and the crisis will be irreversible.`,"又举滇中误治救逆验案数则，以明过汗亡阳、误下结胸之戒，使学者知经方之用，差之毫厘则谬以千里。":"He also cited several cases of mistaken treatment and treatment in central Yunnan, which showed that excessive sweating destroyed the yang and mistakenly prescribed the warning of knotting the chest, so that scholars can understand the use of classic prescriptions. If there is a slight difference, the error will be thousands of miles away.","又如治省立昆华医院院长秦某独子之伤寒重症，四诊时仍用大剂四逆汤，…":"Another example is the treatment of severe typhoid fever in the only son of Mr. Qin, director of the Provincial Kunhua Hospital, who still used a large dose of Sini decoction during the fourth diagnosis...","又如治省立昆华医院院长秦某独子之伤寒重症，四诊时仍用大剂四逆汤，附子用至400g，患儿日夜泄泻10余次，“秦君夫妇为此担心害怕，认为有肠出血或肠穿孔的危险，每见其子排泻大便，即流泪惊惶不已”。吴氏当即详加解释，此由寒湿内盛，腹中有如冰霜凝聚，今得阳药温化运行，阴邪溃退，真阳返回而使冰霜化行。所拟方药皆非泻下之剂，其排泻者为内停寒湿污秽之物，系病除佳兆，邪去则正自能安，方保无虞。于是，病家疑虑始减，继续接受治疗，终至痊愈。":`Another example is the treatment of severe typhoid fever in the only son of Mr. Qin, director of the Provincial Kunhua Hospital. He still used large doses of Sini decoction and 400g of Aconite during the fourth diagnosis. The child had diarrhea more than 10 times day and night. "Qin Jun and his wife were worried about this and thought there was a danger of intestinal bleeding or intestinal perforation. Every time they saw their son passing stool, they shed tears and were frightened." Wu immediately explained in detail, this is due to the cold and dampness in the body, which is like frost condensation in the abdomen. Now the Yang medicine is used to warm and operate, the Yin evil retreats, and the true Yang returns to melt the frost. The proposed prescriptions are not purgative agents. The purgative agents are those that stop cold, dampness and dirt in the body. This is a good sign that the disease will be cured. If the evil spirits are removed, the body will be in good health and there will be no danger. As a result, the patient's doubts began to subside, and he continued to receive treatment, and finally recovered.`,"又论有是证用是药之旨，谓药无偏性，偏性即药之用，医家不可存寒热好恶于胸中，一存成见，则辨证必偏，此全书之总纲也。":"It also discusses the purpose of medicine based on the syndrome and its use, saying that the medicine has no bias, and the bias is the purpose of the medicine. Doctors should not keep the likes and dislikes of cold and heat in the chest. If there is prejudice, the syndrome differentiation will be biased. This is the general outline of the whole book.","又论标本根结、气街四海在临证取穴中的运用，使远道取穴、局部取穴各有理法可循，层次井然。":"It also discusses the application of specimen root knot and Qi Street in selecting acupoints for clinical symptoms, so that the selection of remote acupoints and local acupoints can be followed in a logical and orderly manner.","又论滇中湿盛之体，阳明多挟湿，用白虎须佐芳化，不可纯用寒凉冰伏，此因地制宜之变通也。":"Also talking about the body with abundant dampness in central Yunnan, Yangming mostly takes the dampness, and white tiger whiskers are used to help aromatize it. Cold and cold ice cannot be used purely, so it is adaptable according to local conditions.","又论蛔厥与脏厥之别、久利与热利之辨，皆以条文为纲、验案为目，深入浅出，最便初学。":"It also discusses the difference between roundworm and viscera, and the difference between Jiuli and heat. All of them are based on the article as the outline and the case examination as the purpose. They explain it in a simple and profound way, which is the most convenient for beginners to learn.","又论针刺禁忌、晕针处理与针后调护，示人以规矩，所谓针家之慎，尽在此篇。":"It also discusses the taboos of acupuncture, treatment of needle fainting and post-acupuncture care, and shows people the rules. The so-called caution of acupuncture masters is all in this article.","又谆谆告诫求子夫妇宜怡情志、节房事、慎起居，谓药治之外更需人和，此身心同治之义也。":"He also earnestly warned Qiuzi and his wife that they should be happy with their emotions, be careful in sexual intercourse, and be careful in their daily lives. He said that in addition to medical treatment, they also need humaneness, which means that the body and mind can be treated together.","又载艾纳香制艾绒之法，谓其火力温和、灸治寒湿痹痛优于他处所产。诸药皆附采收时月与阴干之法，示人以保全药性之意。":"It also describes the method of making moxa velvet from moxa incense, saying that its firepower is mild and moxibustion is better than other products in treating cold-damp paralysis. All medicines are accompanied by the method of harvesting in the moon and drying in the shade, showing the intention of preserving the medicinal properties.","又载误服寒凉冰伏致疹毒内陷者救逆诸案，读之可知辨证一差、生死立判之险，临证者可不慎欤。":"It also contains cases of rescuing people who mistakenly took cold and ice packs and caused rash and poison invagination. From reading this, we can see that a mistake in syndrome differentiation can lead to a judgment of life and death. Those who are diagnosed with the disease may not be careful.","又驳麻喜清凉之俗说，谓清凉仅宜于热毒壅盛之顺证，若不辨寒热而一概清凉，最易冰伏疹毒，变证蜂起，此立言之微旨也。":"It also refutes the common saying that Ma likes coolness, saying that coolness is only suitable for those with excessive heat and toxins. If cold and heat are not distinguished and all coolness is used, it is most likely to freeze the rash and poison, and the symptoms will become more severe. This is the purpose of this statement.",反映扶阳学派研习伤寒的独特视角:"Reflecting the Fuyang School’s unique perspective on studying typhoid fever","取穴主张局部与循经并重，必求针下得气、气至病所而后效，此管氏针灸之要诀也。":"When selecting acupuncture points, it is recommended to pay equal attention to the local area and along the meridians. It is necessary to obtain Qi under the needle, and the Qi will reach the disease site and then have effective effects. This is the key to Guan's acupuncture.","取穴少而精，讲究“以指代针”，进针必求得气。":"The acupuncture points should be selected with few but precise points, and the point should be pointed to refer to the needle. When inserting the needle, the Qi will be released.",右图吴氏亲笔方笺亦为阑尾炎治案:"The note on the right handwritten by Wu is also a treatment for appendicitis.","右图吴氏亲笔方笺亦为阑尾炎治案。患者庄先生因阑尾炎拟定当日5点“开刀”手术。吴氏以吴萸四逆汤加味，“一剂已效”，免去手术之苦。可知类似案例，治了不少。":`The note on the right handwritten by Wu is also a treatment for appendicitis. The patient, Mr. Zhuang, planned to undergo surgery at 5 o'clock that day due to appendicitis. Wu added Wuyu Sini Decoction, "one dose is effective", eliminating the pain of surgery. It can be seen that many similar cases have been cured.`,同流派名医:"Same School",名医:"famous doctor","名医详情 | 云南名医馆":"Details of famous doctors | Yunnan Famous Medical Center",名医风采:"Doctors","名医风采 | 云南名医馆":"Famous Doctor Style | Yunnan Famous Medical Center",名家著作:"Works by famous writers","后人整理其临证心得，编成《戴丽三医疗经验选》《戴丽三医案》，风行滇中，为习经方者必读之书。":'Later generations compiled his clinical experience and compiled it into "Selected Medical Experiences of Dai Li" and "Three Medical Cases of Dai Li", which became popular in central Yunnan and became a must-read book for those who practice prescriptions.',吴佩衡:"Wu Peiheng","吴佩衡先生1888年生于云南会泽，幼承家学，及长师从当地名医，日夜研习《伤寒论》《金匮要略》，弱冠即以善治伤寒重症名噪乡里。":'Mr. Wu Peiheng was born in Huize, Yunnan in 1888. He inherited his family education at an early age and studied under local famous doctors for a long time. He studied "Treatise on Febrile Diseases" and "Synopsis of the Golden Chamber" day and night. He became well-known in his hometown for his good treatment of severe typhoid fever.',"吴佩衡先生临证医案精选，尤以伤寒危急重症救逆诸案著称。案中理法方药丝丝入扣，附子运用之胆识与法度跃然纸上，为扶阳学派必读之书。":"Mr. Wu Peiheng has selected clinical medical cases, and is especially famous for his cases of treating critical and severe cases of typhoid fever. The theory, methods and medicines in the case are incisive, and the courage and method of Fuzi's application are vividly displayed on the paper. It is a must-read book for the Fuyang School.","吴佩衡先生执教云南中医学院时编撰之《伤寒论》讲义。以六经辨证为纲，条文讲解结合滇中临证验案，深入浅出，为习伤寒者之津梁。":'The lecture notes of "Treatise on Febrile Diseases" compiled by Mr. Wu Peiheng when he was teaching at Yunnan College of Traditional Chinese Medicine. Based on the syndrome differentiation of the Six Meridians, the article explanations are combined with clinical evidence verification in central Yunnan to explain the disease in a simple and profound way, which is a good reference for those who are familiar with typhoid fever.',"吴佩衡先生论治麻疹之专著。力主麻疹“以透为顺”，对麻疹各期辨治、透疹法度与救逆诸法阐述精详，为中医儿科麻疹论治之重要文献。":`Mr. Wu Peiheng's monograph on the treatment of measles. It advocates that measles should be treated "by clearing it up", and elaborates on the diagnosis and treatment of each stage of measles, the methods for clearing up the rash, and the methods for relieving the disease. It is an important document on the treatment of pediatric measles in traditional Chinese medicine.`,吴佩衡医案:"Wu Peiheng’s medical records",吴佩衡扶阳学术思想研讨会在昆明举行:"Wu Peiheng's Fuyang Academic Thought Seminar was held in Kunming","吴佩衡，字佩衡，云南会泽人。毕生精研《伤寒论》，临证善以大剂附子救治阴盛格阳之危重证候，人称“吴附子”，为云南扶阳学派的一面旗帜。":'Wu Peiheng, courtesy name Peiheng, was born in Huize, Yunnan. He studied "Treatise on Febrile Diseases" all his life, and was good at using large doses of Aconite to treat critical syndromes of yin excess and Yang. He was known as "Wu Fuzi" and became a banner of Yunnan Fuyang School.',"吴某，男，15岁":"Wu, male, 15 years old","吴某，男，15岁。于1921年3月延余诊视：发热不退已11H，面红唇赤而焦，舌红苔黄而无津，虚烦不得卧，食物不进，渴喜冷饮，小便短赤，大便不解，脉来沉细而数。查其先前所服之方，始而九味羌活汤，继则服以黄连、梔子、连翘、黄芩、银花、薄荷等未效。\\n此系春温病误以辛温发散，又复苦燥清热，耗伤真阴，邪热内蕴，转为少阴热化证，拟黄连阿胶鸡子黄汤治之：\\n黄连10g，黄芩12g，杭芍24g，阿胶I。 g（烊化兑入），鸡子黄2枚。\\n先煎苓、连、芍药为汤，稍凉，兑入已悻化之阿胶.再搅入生鸡蛋黄2枚和匀而服。服1剂后即得安静熟寐，烦渴已止， \\n唇舌转润，脉静身凉。继以生脉散加生地、玄参、黄连：\\n米洋参10g，寸冬15g，五味子5g，甘草6g，玄参10g，生地12g，黄连5g。 \\n上方连进2剂而愈。\\n吴佩衡治瘟疫3例，皆投达原饮，均加石膏、大黄两味峻药，剂量亦重，同样显现出胆识。":"Wu, male, 15 years old. In March 1921, he underwent a follow-up examination: the fever persisted for 11 hours, his face was red and his lips were red and burnt, his tongue was red and yellow with no fluid, he was tired and could not lie down, he could not eat, he was thirsty and liked cold drinks, his urine was short and red, his stools were indigestible, and his pulse was heavy and thready. After checking the prescriptions he had taken before, he started with Jiuwei Qianghuo decoction, and then took Coptis chinensis, gardenia, forsythia, skullcap, Yinhua, mint, etc., but no effect. \\nThis is caused by spring-warm disease mistakenly expelled by pungent warmth, and then returns to bitter dryness and clearing heat, which consumes the true yin, and the evil heat is inherent, and turns into a Shaoyin heat syndrome. It can be treated with Coptis Lian Ejiao Jizihuang Decoction:\\nCoptis 10g, Scutellaria baicalensis 12g, Hangshao 24g, donkey hide gelatin I. g (added when cooked), 2 pieces of chicken roe. \\nFirst decoct lings, lian, and peony into a soup, let it cool slightly, and mix in the melted donkey hide gelatin. Then stir in 2 raw egg yolks and mix well before taking. After taking 1 dose, you will have a peaceful and sound sleep, your polydipsia will have stopped, your lips and tongue will become moist, your pulse will be quiet and your body will be cool. Follow with Shengmai Powder and add Radix Rehmanniae, Scrophulariaceae and Coptis Rhizome: \\nPax 10g, Cundong 15g, Schisandra chinensis 5g, Licorice 6g, Scrophulariaceae 10g, Radix Rehmanniae 12g, Coptis 5g. \\nThe patient recovered after taking 2 doses in a row. \\nWu Peiheng treated 3 cases of plague, all of which were treated with Da Yuan drink, with two strong medicinal herbs, gypsum and rhubarb added to them. The dosage was also heavy, and he also showed his courage.","吴氏以临证所验阐释条文，谓太阳主表、治之以汗，然汗法之要在识表虚表实，表虚不可峻汗，表实不可不汗，其间分际不可不究。":"Wu explained the provisions based on his clinical experience, saying that the sun controls the surface and sweating is the treatment. However, the key to sweating is to recognize the deficiency in the symptoms and the reality in the syndrome. The symptoms of deficiency must not be severe, and the symptoms of reality must be sweating. The distinction between them must be studied.",吴氏回阳救逆汤:"Wu's Huiyangjiu Ni Tang","吴氏谓厥阴为阴尽阳生之地，辨证之要在分阴阳之胜负：厥多热少为病进，热多厥少为病退，据此可断预后。":"Wu said that Jueyin is the place where yin is exhausted and yang is generated. The key to syndrome differentiation is to distinguish between yin and yang: more and less heat means the disease is progressing, more and less heat means the disease has retreated, and the prognosis can be determined based on this.","吴氏谓顺证之眼目在神清、热匀、疹活，疹色红活、颗粒分明、依期透布者，虽热甚不惧，切忌妄用寒凉遏其出路，所谓见疹莫止疹，即是此意。":"Wu said that if the eyes of Shun syndrome are clear, the heat is uniform, the rash is active, the rash is red and active, the particles are clear, and the rash is spread according to the schedule, although the heat is very strong, it is not afraid of it, and it is forbidden to use cold and cool to stop its way out. This is the saying that when the rash is seen, do not stop the rash.","吴氏谓麻疹为胎毒蕴于肺脾、触时行之气而发，其病位在肺胃，其出路在皮毛，故治疗始终不离透字，透之一法，贯串三期。":'Wu said that measles is caused by fetal poison accumulating in the lungs and spleen and touching the current qi. The location of the disease is in the lungs and stomach, and its outlet is in the skin. Therefore, the treatment is always inseparable from the word "penetrating", and the method of "penetrating" runs through the three stages.',吴氏麻疹三豆汤:"Wu's measles three bean soup","吴附子．吴佩衡2017":"Wu Fuzi. Wu Peiheng2017",呃逆:"hiccup","呃逆 黄某，女，二十五岁，归国华侨，云南某大学学生":"Hiccup Huang, female, 25 years old, returned overseas Chinese, student at a university in Yunnan","呃逆 黄某，女，二十五岁，归国华侨，云南某大学学生。患呃逆 证已一年余，曾经多方治疗，效果不显。每于精神紧张之时， 呃逆更甚。自觉胃中饱闷，时有逆气上冲，气冲有声,声短而 频,不能自制。近来逐渐加剧，以致情绪不安,心情烦闷，睡眠 差，影响听课学习。1964年夏，患者来中医学院就诊于余，呃 逆频作，面色少华，舌淡质嫩，苔腻微黄，脉象沉缓而弦。《景 岳全书》曰：“致呃之由，总由气逆。”此系阳虚胃寒，中焦气机 升降失调，寒气上逆，胃气不降所致。治宜温中降逆，调和气 机，方用旋覆代赭汤加味。 旋覆花9克，代赭石12克，法半夏9克，明党参15克， 砂仁9克，厚朴9克，生姜3片，大枣5枚，甘草6克。 服二剂后，呃逆减少,间隔时间有所延长,皖闷气逆亦感 减轻。患者自知服药有效,情绪亦好转,睡眠、饮食均有改善。 脉沉缓，关部尚弦。腻苔已退，苔薄白而润。继以温中益气，和 胃降逆治之。用前方，明党参增至30克，加入公丁香3克，柿 蒂6克，连服四剂，呃逆不再发作。 按：“呃逆之由，总由气逆”，乃中焦气机升降失司，逆气 上冲所致。阳虚有寒者，宜温中降逆为主。阴虚有热者，宜苦 寒降逆为主。总不离乎调理升降气机为原则。若久病之人，突 发呃逆，则为脾肾气机将绝，宜以大剂回阳降逆，如吴萸四逆 汤、白通汤、人参干姜附子汤乏类，以求挽回生机。若徒治其 标而忽弃其本，不但呃逆难止，生命亦难保无虞矣。":'Hiccup Huang, female, 25 years old, returned overseas Chinese, student at a university in Yunnan. I have been suffering from hiccup syndrome for more than a year. I have been treated with various methods, but the effect is not obvious. Whenever I feel stressed, my hiccups get worse. Feeling that the stomach is full and stuffy, and sometimes the adverse qi rushes up, and the qi rushes loudly, the sound is short and frequent, and it is impossible to control it. Recently, it has gradually worsened, resulting in emotional restlessness, depression, and poor sleep, which affects listening to classes and studying. In the summer of 1964, the patient came to the College of Traditional Chinese Medicine for treatment. He suffered from frequent epileptic seizures, a pale complexion, a pale and tender tongue, greasy and yellowish fur, and a slow and stringy pulse. "Jingyue Quanshu" says: "The cause of hiccups is always Qi inversion." This is caused by yang deficiency and stomach cold, imbalance in the rise and fall of the middle Jiao Qi machine, cold Qi ascending and inversion, and stomach Qi not falling. To treat the disease, it is appropriate to warm the middle and reduce the adverse effects, and harmonize the qi. Use Xuanfu Daizhe Decoction to add flavor. 9 grams of Inula, 12 grams of ocher, 9 grams of Pinellia ternata, 15 grams of Codonopsis pilosula, 9 grams of Amomum villosum, 9 grams of Magnolia officinalis, 3 slices of ginger, 5 jujubes, and 6 grams of licorice. After taking the second dose, the hiccups were reduced, the intervals were lengthened, and the feeling of suffocation was also alleviated. The patient knew that the medication was effective, his mood also improved, and his sleep and diet improved. The pulse is slow and slow, and the key part is stringy. The greasy coating has receded and the coating is thin, white and moist. Then treat it by warming the middle and replenishing qi, harmonizing the stomach and lowering the qi. After using the medicine, increase the amount of Codonopsis pilosula to 30 grams, add 3 grams of male cloves and 6 grams of persimmon peduncle. After taking four doses, hiccups no longer occur. Note: "The cause of hiccups is always Qi inversion", which is caused by the imbalance of Qi movement in the center of the burner and the upthrust of Qi in the middle part of the body. For those with yang deficiency and cold, it is advisable to warm the body and reduce the adverse effects. Those with yin deficiency and heat should mainly treat cold and cold. The principle of adjusting the air lift is always the same. If a person who has been ill for a long time suddenly develops hiccups, the spleen and kidney qi will be exhausted. It is advisable to use large doses to restore yang and reduce the qi, such as Wuyu Sini Decoction, Baitong Decoction, Ginseng Ganjiang Fuzi Decoction, etc., in order to restore vitality. If you only treat the symptoms and neglect the root cause, not only will the hiccups be difficult to stop, but life will also be difficult to protect.',"咯血案 张某，男，25岁":"Hemoptysis case Zhang, male, 25 years old",'咯血案\\n张某，男，25岁。虚劳咳嗽已经数月，始因盗汗，遗精，食少难寐，求医无效。近则午后恶寒，发热如潮。面颊及口唇色赤如艳，自汗、盗汗，夜间尤甚；痰嗽不爽，咳声嘶嘎，咯血盈碗；耳鸣，眼花，头常昏晕，气短而喘，精神疲惫，不能入寐；脉来虚数无力，舌根白腻。查所服之方，均以阴虚有热为治，病势反见沉重。盖此病良由素禀不足，肾气太亏，真阳内虚不能镇纳阴邪，阴寒水湿夹痰浊上逆于肺，阻遏肺肾升降气机。表阳失固，营阴不敛，则汗易外泄；虚阳无力统摄血液，则散漫游溢脉外而咯血；阴阳相执，虚阳被阴寒格拒于外，发为潮热。虽发热而有恶寒相伴，脉见数，然其体状虚软无力，全属一派阳虚阴寒之象，非阴虚火旺之肺燥咯血可比。往日所治南辕而北辙，徒劳无功。唯有依照甘温除热之旨，方可挽冋生机，方用甘草干姜汤加附子。\\n炙甘草24g，炮黑姜15g，附片45g，大枣3枚（烧黑存性）。\\n服1剂，咯血止；再剂则喘咳稍平，精神较增，再拟四逆汤加味治之：附片60g，干姜、炮黑姜各15g，西砂仁15g，炙甘草15g，大枣4枚（烧黑存性）。\\n服后痰多而兼杂黑血，此乃得阳药温化运行，既已离经之血随痰浊而排除。连进4剂，潮热退半，血痰已不见，各症均有所减。泻下黑酱稀粪为浊阴下降。脉转缓，稍有力，饮食略增。病情大有转机，照前方去大枣加倍分量，加茯苓30g，白术18g。连进5剂，颊唇赤色已退，喘定八九，潮热微作，竟得熟寐，咳痰有减，咳声较洪，此肺气之通达也。再进数剂则潮热已不作，食思倍增，咳痰更减。唯其周身骤然浮肿，面足尤甚。病家因见肿象，不知为阴邪始退，元气来复之兆，突生疑惧，改延他医诊视，断言“误服附子中毒”所致，主以绿豆、贝母、寸冬、熟地、洋参等药。服后是晚喘咳顿作，气滞痰涌，身热再燃。惊惶失措又复促吴氏往诊。知病家不识医理，朝夕更医，几使前功尽弃，吴以诚言相告，力主大剂辛温，逆流挽舟以回颓绝，方用：\\n附片200g，干姜60g，北细辛6g，麻茸4g，上肉桂12g（研末，泡水兑入），茯苓60g，甘草24g。\\n服后微汗，身热始退。连进3剂后，小便畅通，浮肿尽消。遂照原方去麻茸加砂仁15g。5剂后，咳痰减去七八，饮食、精神转增。去细辛加口芪、白术各30g，再进10剂，诸症悉除，以黄芪建中汤加味善后：\\n口芪l00g，桂尖24g，杭芍24g，附片150g，党参20g，，白术20g，西砂仁15g，大枣4枚，生姜30g，饴糖30g（烊化兑入）。\\n按：此案四逆汤“服后痰多而兼杂黑血，此乃得阳药温化运行，既已离经之血随痰浊而排除……各症均有所减，泻下黑酱稀粪，为浊阴下降”，解释合乎情理。“唯其周身骤然浮肿，面足尤甚”，本是“阳药运行，阴邪化去”之正常反应。无奈病家不识，“突生疑惧，改延他医”，误投滋补，导致病情反复。吴氏重予温阳，立即改观，说明治法正确，绝非“误服附子中毒”。郑钦安曾专门指明：“服辛温10余剂后，忽然周身面目浮肿，或发现斑点，痛痒异常，或汗出，此是阳药运行，阴邪化去，从七窍而出也。"':`Hemoptysis case\\nZhang, male, 25 years old. She had been suffering from fatigue and cough for several months. She started to suffer from night sweats, spermatorrhea, difficulty sleeping due to lack of food, and medical treatment was ineffective. In the near afternoon, there is aversion to cold and fever like tide. The cheeks and lips are as red as bright colors, spontaneous sweating and night sweats, especially at night; the phlegm is not good, the cough is hissing, and the bowl is filled with blood; tinnitus, dizziness, dizziness, shortness of breath and wheezing, mental exhaustion, and inability to fall asleep; the pulse is weak and weak, and the base of the tongue is white and greasy. After checking the prescriptions taken, they all treated Yin deficiency and heat, but the condition turned out to be serious. This disease is caused by insufficient elemental endowments, too much kidney qi, and internal deficiency of true yang that cannot suppress and absorb yin evils. Yin, cold, water, and dampness combined with phlegm and turbidity go against the lungs, blocking the lungs and kidneys from ascending and descending qi. If the superficial yang is not solid and the nutrient yin is not restrained, the sweat will easily leak out; if the yang is deficient and unable to control the blood, it will scatter outside the overflowing vessels and cause hemoptysis; if the yin and yang are in conflict, the deficient yang will be rejected by the yin-cold pattern, causing hot flashes. Although the fever is accompanied by aversion to cold and the pulse is rapid, the body is weak and weak, which is all signs of yang deficiency and yin cold, which is not comparable to lung dryness and hemoptysis caused by yin deficiency and fire exuberance. In the past, the governance was in the opposite direction, which was in vain. Only by following the purpose of removing heat with sweetness and warmth can we restore vitality, and use licorice and dried ginger soup plus aconite. \\n24g of roasted licorice, 15g of black ginger, 45g of Fu slices, and 3 jujubes (burned black). \\nTake 1 dose and the hemoptysis will stop; another dose will make the wheezing and coughing slightly subside and the spirit will increase. Then add Sini Decoction to treat it: 60g of Fu Pian, 15g each of dried ginger and black ginger, 15g Amomum villosum, 15g Zhigancao, and 4 jujubes (the symptoms of burning black are present). \\nAfter taking it, there is a lot of phlegm mixed with black blood. This is due to the warming operation of the yang medicine, and the blood that has left the menstruation will be eliminated with the turbid phlegm. After taking 4 doses, the hot flashes subsided by half, bloody sputum disappeared, and all symptoms were reduced. Diarrhoea, black sauce and loose stools indicate a decrease in turbid yin. The pulse is slow and slightly strong, and the diet is slightly increased. The condition has improved greatly. I removed the jujube and doubled the amount, added 30g of Poria cocos and 18g of Atractylodes macrocephala. After taking 5 doses, the redness of the cheeks and lips has subsided, the wheezing has stabilized, the hot flashes are mild, and I feel sleepy, the phlegm is reduced, and the coughing sound is louder. This indicates that the lung qi is clear. After a few more doses, the hot flashes no longer occur, food cravings double, and phlegm cough decreases. However, his whole body suddenly became swollen, especially his face and feet. Because the patient saw swelling and did not realize that it was a sign of Yin evil beginning to subside and regaining his vitality, he suddenly became suspicious and fearful, so he postponed a consultation with another doctor and concluded that it was caused by "mistake of aconite poisoning". He mainly prescribed mung beans, Fritillaria, Cun Dong, Rehmannia glutinosa, American ginseng and other medicines. After taking it, I experienced shortness of breath and sudden onset of cough, stagnation of qi and phlegm, and renewed body heat. Panicked, Wu was urged to go to the hospital again. Knowing that the patient did not know medical science, he kept on treating day and night, almost all his previous efforts were wasted. Wu Yicheng told the truth and advocated a large dose of pungent and warm medicine to reverse the decline. The prescription was:\\n200g of Fu Pian, 60g of dried ginger, 6g of Asarum, 4g of moose, 12g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed in), 60g of Poria, and 24g of licorice. \\nAfter taking it, I sweat slightly and the body heat begins to subside. After taking 3 doses, my urine became smooth and the swelling disappeared. Then follow the original recipe, remove the semen antler and add 15g of amomum villosum. After 5 doses, the sputum expectoration decreased by 70 to 80%, and the diet and energy improved. Remove asarum and add 30g each of Qi Qi and Atractylodes, and then add 10 doses. All symptoms will be eliminated. Use Huangqi Jianzhong Decoction to treat the aftermath:\\nQi 100g, Guijian 24g, Hangshao 24g, 150g of Futian, 20g of Codonopsis pilosula, 20g of Atractylodes macrocephala, 15g of Amomum villosum, 4 jujubes, 30g of ginger, and 30g of maltose (blended and mixed). \\nNote: In this case, Sini Decoction "After taking the Sini Decoction, there was a lot of phlegm mixed with black blood. This is due to the warming operation of the yang medicine. The blood that has left menstruation is eliminated with the turbid phlegm... All symptoms are reduced. The diarrhea of ​​black sauce and thin stools is due to the decrease of turbid yin." "Only his whole body suddenly swelled, especially his face and feet." This is a normal reaction of "the Yang medicine is running and the Yin evil is gone". Unfortunately, the patient was unaware of the problem, "suddenly suspected and fearful, and delayed treatment elsewhere" and mistakenly administered supplements, resulting in recurrence of the disease. Wu's treatment immediately changed her mind after re-warming the yang, indicating that the treatment method was correct and it was definitely not "accidental aconite poisoning". Zheng Qin'an once specifically pointed out: "After taking more than 10 doses of Xinwen, suddenly the whole body is swollen, or spots are found, abnormal pain and itching, or sweating. This is the movement of yang medicine, the yin evil is transformed, and comes out from the seven orifices."`,咳嗽:"cough",咳嗽兼便秘:"Cough and constipation",咽痛:"sore throat","哮 喘":"Asthma","哮 喘 郑某，女，二十五岁，已婚，云南省人":"Asthma Zheng, female, 25 years old, married, from Yunnan Province","哮 喘 郑某，女，二十五岁，已婚，云南省人。患慢性哮喘病已十 四年之久,现身孕四月余，住昆明军区某医院，于1959年10 月9日邀余会诊。询其病史,始因年幼体弱，感风寒而起病， 药、食调理不当，风寒内伏，夹湿痰上逆于肺,经常喘咳,值天 寒时令尤甚,迄今病已多年，转成慢性哮喘。证见咳嗽短气而 喘，痰多色白，咽喉不利，时发喘息哮鸣。面色淡而少华，目 眶、口唇含青乌色。胸中闷胀、少气懒言，咳声低弱，咳时则由 胸部牵引小腹作痛。食少不思饮,溺短不清,夜间喘咳尤甚， 难于平卧入寐。舌苔白滑厚腻，舌质含青色，脉现弦滑，沉取 则弱而无力，此系风寒伏于肺胃，久咳肺肾气虚，阳不足以运 行，寒湿痰饮阻遏而成是证。法当开提肺寒，补肾纳气，温化 痰湿治之,方用小青龙汤加附片。 附片100克，杭白芍10克，麻黄10克，北细辛6克，干 姜30克，桂枝20克，五味子5克，法半夏10克，甘草10克。 服上方二剂后，咳吐大量清稀白痰，胸闷、气短及喘咳均 已较减,能入睡四、五小时，食思见增，唇舌转红，仍微带青 色,厚腻白苔退去其半。上方虽见效，然阳气未充，寒湿痰饮 尚未肃清，继以温化开提之剂治之。方用四逆、二陈合方加麻、辛、桂。 附片200克，干姜40克，茯苓30克，法半夏15克，广陈 皮10克，北细辛8克，麻茸10克（蜜炙），上肉桂10克（研 末，泡水兑入），甘草10克。 服上方后喘咳皆有减少。治法不变，仍用此方，随证加减 药味及分量，共服二十余剂后,哮喘咳嗽日渐平息。再服十余 剂,病遂痊愈,身孕无恙,至足月顺产一子,娩后母子均健康。按：昔有谓妇人身孕，乌、附、半夏皆所禁用，其实不然。盖乌、附、半夏，生者具有毒性，固不能服，只要炮制煎煮得法，去除毒性，因病施用，孕妇服之亦无妨碍。妇人怀孕，身为疾病所缠，易伤胎气而不固。因证立方用药，务使邪去而正安，此实为安胎、固胎之要义。《内经》云：“妇人重身，毒之何如……有故无殒，亦无殒也。”此乃有是病而用是药，所谓有病则病当之，故孕妇无殒，胎亦无殒也。余临证数十年，思循经旨，多有所验,深感得益不少。":'Asthma Zheng, female, 25 years old, married, from Yunnan Province. I had been suffering from chronic asthma for fourteen years. I was now more than four months pregnant and was admitted to a hospital in the Kunming Military Region. I was invited for consultation on October 9, 1959. After asking about his medical history, it was found that he was young and frail, and started to get sick due to wind and cold. He had improper medicine and food preparation, and the wind and cold were internal, and dampness and phlegm were trapped in the lungs. He often wheezed and coughed, especially during cold weather. He has been ill for many years and has turned into chronic asthma. Symptoms include coughing, shortness of breath and wheezing, white phlegm, indigestion in the throat, and occasional wheezing and wheezing. The complexion is light and lustrous, with bluish-black eyes and lips. There is tightness in the chest, lack of breath and laziness in speaking, and a weak cough. When coughing, pain in the lower abdomen is caused by pulling from the chest. He eats little and does not want to drink. He suffers from shortness of breath and confusion, especially wheezing and coughing at night. It is difficult to lie down and fall asleep. The tongue coating is thick and white, the tongue is green, the pulse is stringy and slippery, and if it sinks, it is weak and weak. This syndrome is due to wind and cold in the lungs and stomach, chronic cough, lung and kidney qi deficiency, insufficient yang movement, and blockage of cold-damp phlegm. Fadang can be used to relieve lung coldness, nourish the kidneys and absorb qi, warm up phlegm and dampness, and treat it with Xiao Qinglong Decoction plus Fu Tablets. 100 grams of Aconite, 10 grams of white peony root, 10 grams of ephedra, 6 grams of asarum, 30 grams of dried ginger, 20 grams of cinnamon twigs, 5 grams of Schisandra chinensis, 10 grams of Pinellia ternata, and 10 grams of licorice. After taking two doses of the above medicine, I coughed up a lot of thin and white phlegm. My chest tightness, shortness of breath and wheezing and coughing were all reduced. I was able to fall asleep for four or five hours. My food cravings increased. My lips and tongue turned red but were still slightly green. Half of the thick and greasy white coating had receded. Although the above treatment is effective, the yang qi is not sufficient and the cold, damp and phlegm fluid has not been cleared away, so it can be treated with warming and activating agents. The prescription is composed of Sini and Erchen combined with Ma, Xin and Gui. 200 grams of Aconite slices, 40 grams of dried ginger, 30 grams of Poria, 15 grams of Pinellia ternata, 10 grams of Citrus tangerine peel, 8 grams of Asarum, 10 grams of moose (roasted with honey), 10 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), and 10 grams of licorice. After taking the above medicine, the wheezing and coughing were reduced. The treatment method remains unchanged, I still use this prescription, and add or subtract the taste and dosage according to the syndrome. After taking more than 20 doses in total, the asthma and cough gradually subsided. After taking more than ten doses, the disease was cured, the pregnancy was fine, and a baby was delivered to term, and both mother and baby were healthy after delivery. Note: In the past, it was said that when a woman was pregnant, Acutis, Fu, and Pinellia ternata were all forbidden, but this is not true. Gai Wu, Fu, and Pinellia ternata are toxic to living people and cannot be taken. As long as they are prepared and boiled properly to remove the toxicity, they can be used due to illness, and there is no problem in taking them by pregnant women. When a woman is pregnant, her body is entangled with diseases, which can easily damage the fetal energy and prevent it from solidifying. The use of prescription medicine according to the syndrome must make the evil go away and the body be in good health. This is actually the key to treating the fetus and stabilizing the fetus. "Nei Jing" says: "A woman has a heavy body, and the poison is like this...there is a reason why there is no death, and there is no death." This is because there is a disease and the medicine is used. It is said that if there is a disease, the disease should be treated, so the pregnant woman does not die, and the fetus does not die. I have been practicing for decades, thinking about the sutras, and have experienced many things, and I feel that I have benefited a lot.',"善用灸法温通经脉，寒痹必灸，热痹不忌刺络。":"Make good use of moxibustion to warm and unblock the meridians. Moxibustion is necessary for cold paralysis, but pricking is not advisable for hot paralysis.",善用附子:"Make good use of Aconite","善用附子、干姜、肉桂温扶元阳，胆识过人而剂量讲究，必嘱先煎去麻。":"Make good use of aconite, dried ginger, and cinnamon to warm and support the yang. You are very courageous and careful about the dosage. You must decoct it first to remove the numbness.","四诊合参，辨证论治。每则医案皆是名家临证心法的凝结。":"The four diagnosis methods are combined with ginseng, syndrome differentiation and treatment. Each medical case is the condensation of the clinical methods of famous experts.","回阳固脱，救逆复脉":"Restore yang, stabilize the condition, rescue the nihilistic pulse and restore the pulse",国医大师:"Master of Traditional Chinese Medicine","国医大师 · 云岭医派代表":"Master of Traditional Chinese Medicine·Representative of Yunling Medical School",在线阅读:"Read online",地方药物:"local medicine","处方严谨，加减有法，于经方化裁中见家学渊源。":"The prescription is rigorous, and the addition and subtraction are methodical. The origin of family learning can be seen in the classic prescriptions.","处方轻灵平和，忌蛮补呆攻，贵在拨动机枢。":"The prescription is light and gentle, avoid excessive and dull attacks, the key is to turn the mechanism.","处方轻灵平和，拨动机枢之妙尽显":"The prescription is light and gentle, and the magic of turning the mechanism is fully demonstrated.",夏惠明:"Xia Huiming","夏惠明教授1945年生，专攻推拿数十载，博采众长而自成一家。":"Professor Xia Huiming was born in 1945. He has specialized in massage for decades and has drawn on the strengths of others to form his own brand.","夏惠明，云南中医学院教授，云南推拿学科带头人。创立“夏氏推拿”手法体系，擅治颈肩腰腿诸疾。":`Xia Huiming is a professor at Yunnan College of Traditional Chinese Medicine and the leader of massage in Yunnan. He created the "Xia's Massage" technique system, which is good at treating neck, shoulder, waist and leg diseases.`,夏氏推拿:"Xia massage","太阳中风、伤寒与兼变证之辨治。":"Differentiation and treatment of Taiyang stroke, typhoid fever and concurrent syndrome.",太阳伤寒表实证:"Taiyang typhoid syndrome","太阳伤寒表实证 王某，男，四十二岁，某厂干部":"Evidence of Taiyang Typhoid fever Wang, male, 42 years old, cadre of a factory","太阳伤寒表实证 王某，男，四十二岁，某厂干部。患者于昨夜发热，体温 38.9℃，今晨来诊仍发热，头痛，颈项强直,肢体酸楚而痛，流 清涕，心泛欲呕、食减而不渴，脉浮紧，舌苔薄白。此系风寒伤 及太阳肤表所致。《内经》云“其在皮者，汗而发之”，照仲景 法,当以辛温发散以解表邪,拟麻黄汤加味主之。 麻黄6克，桂枝10克，杏仁10克，法半夏6克，防风6 克，甘草6克，生姜3片。 嘱温服而卧，取汗自愈。殊料病者家属畏忌麻黄一药之 温，恐燥热伤津，自行将药中麻黄减除,服一碗，未得汗。见其 躁烦，热势反增，体温升至39.7℃。继服第二碗,则头痛如裂， 身痛如被杖，恶寒较昨日更甚，疑为药不对症，邀余急往诊 视,脉来浮紧急促，苔白腻，呼痛呻吟，虽言失治,幸喜表寒证 型未变，释明其意，即嘱仍用原方，万不能再去麻黄。经照方 服药二次后，温覆而卧,稍顷汗出热退,表邪解,遂得脉静身 凉而愈。按：世有畏麻、桂如蛇蝎者，以为其性温而易伤津化燥，不知表寒实证无麻黄之辛散，何以开发滕理，驱邪外出？无桂枝之温通，何以助阳温经而散寒？不畏邪之伤于人，而畏药性之辛温，实为姑息养奸之弊也。盖用药不在医家之喜恶，而在于审证之明确，有是证用是药，用之得当则药到病除。用之不当，易变化莫测。阳热偏胜者，辛温固不宜用，营血不足，里虚内伤等证，亦不宜汗。倘确属寒邪束表之证，当用而不用，反以清凉苦寒抑其热，势必助邪伤正，表寒不解，热势更张，斯时宜以麻桂等剂因势利导，驱邪外出，切勿坐失良机而至表邪传里为患，此乃祛邪即所以扶正之法也。麻黄开玄府，通达滕理。桂枝辛温通阳，助其疏泄。杏仁利肺气，降逆平喘，甘草保中气而生津液。方药化合，专发太阳伤寒肤表之汗，效如檸鼓。然服此方一、二碗后，覆卧得汗即可，不必尽剂，更勿令其大汗淋漓以致伤津而耗气。俗云“方是死方，法是活法”。欲求其效，宜潜心钻研意旨，无异于辱锤之非易也。":`Evidence of Taiyang Typhoid fever: Wang, male, 42 years old, a cadre in a factory. The patient had a fever last night with a body temperature of 38.9°C. When he came to the doctor this morning, he still had a fever, headache, stiff neck, soreness and pain in the limbs, clear runny nose, a feeling of nausea, loss of appetite but no thirst, a loose and tight pulse, and a thin white tongue coating. This is caused by wind-cold damage and sun damage to the skin. "Nei Jing" says that "it is on the skin and is caused by sweating". According to Zhongjing's method, it should be dispersed with pungent and warm substances to relieve external evils, and it should be treated with the flavor of Mahuang Decoction. 6 grams of ephedra, 10 grams of cinnamon twigs, 10 grams of almonds, 6 grams of pinellia, 6 grams of parsnips, 6 grams of licorice, and 3 slices of ginger. Instruct him to take warm clothes and lie down, and he will recover by sweating. Unexpectedly, the family members of the patient were afraid of the warmth of the ephedra medicine, fearing that the dryness and heat would damage the body fluids, so they removed the ephedra from the medicine themselves and took a bowl without sweating. Seeing that he was irritable, the heat increased, and his body temperature rose to 39.7°C. After taking the second bowl, I had a splitting headache, body pain like a stick, and aversion to cold that was worse than yesterday. I suspected that the medicine was not treating the symptoms, so I invited Yu Ji to see a doctor. My pulse was floating and rapid, the coating was white and greasy, and I was moaning with pain. Although it was said that it was not cured, I was glad that the syndrome of cold syndrome had not changed. I explained the meaning and ordered to still use the original prescription. Never remove ephedra again. After taking the medicine for two times according to the prescription, the patient should be warm and lie down, and the fever will subside after sweating for a while. Note: There are people who are afraid of hemp and osmanthus like snakes and scorpions, thinking that they are warm in nature and can easily injure body fluids and turn into dryness. They don’t know that there is no pungent powder of ephedra when the symptoms are cold, so how can they develop Tengli and expel evil spirits? Without the warmth of cinnamon twig, how can it help the yang to warm the meridians and dispel cold? Not being afraid of harm caused by evil, but being afraid of the pungent and warm nature of the medicine, is actually tolerating the disadvantages of fostering adultery. The use of medicine does not depend on the doctor's likes and dislikes, but on the clearness of the syndrome. If the syndrome is present, the right medicine should be used. If used properly, the medicine will cure the disease. If used improperly, it can easily change unexpectedly. It is not suitable for people with excessive yang heat, pungent and warm conditions, insufficient nourishment and blood, internal deficiency and internal injury, etc. It is also not suitable to sweat. If it is true that the cold evil is confined to the outside, it should not be used. Instead, use cool, bitter cold to suppress the heat, which will inevitably help the evil and harm the body. The cold outside will not be resolved, and the heat will become more severe. At this time, it is appropriate to use Ma Gui and other agents to take advantage of the situation to expel the evil. Do not miss the opportunity to cause evil from the outside to spread to the inside. This is the way to dispel evil and strengthen the body. Ephedra opens Xuanfu and leads to Tengli. Guizhi is pungent and warm to relieve yang and help relieve diarrhea. Almonds benefit lung qi, lower qi and relieve asthma, while licorice protects qi and produces body fluids. The combination of prescription and medicine is specially designed to relieve sweat caused by typhoid fever on the skin surface, and is as effective as lemon drum. However, after taking one or two bowls of this prescription, it is enough to lie down until the patient is sweating. It is not necessary to use up the dose, and it is not necessary to make the patient sweat profusely, which may damage body fluids and consume energy. As the saying goes, "The method is the method of death, and the method is the method of living." If you want to get its effect, you should concentrate on studying the intention, which is tantamount to insulting the hard work of hammering.`,太阳少阴两感于寒证:"The two senses of Taiyang and Shaoyin are in cold syndrome","太阳少阴两感于寒证 （重感冒） 张某，年四十二岁，住云南省昆明市武庙下南联升巷底":"Syndrome of both Taiyang and Shaoyin due to cold (severe cold) Zhang, 42 years old, lives at the bottom of Liansheng Lane, Xianan Liansheng Lane, Wumiao, Kunming City, Yunnan Province","太阳少阴两感于寒证 （重感冒） 张某，年四十二岁，住云南省昆明市武庙下南联升巷底。 肾气素亏，于1929年9月2日返家途中，时值阴雨，感冒风 寒而病。初起即身热恶寒，头疼体痛，沉迷嗜卧（即少阴病但 欲寐之病情也），兼见渴喜热饮不多，脉沉细而兼紧象。舌苔 白滑，质夹青紫，由于肾气素亏，坎阳内弱，无力卫外固表以 抵抗客邪，以致寒风乘虚直入少阴，阻塞真阳运行之机,而成 是状。以仲景麻辛附子汤，温经解表、扶正除邪治之。 黑附片36克，麻黄10克（先煮数沸，去沬），北细辛6 克，桂枝尖13克。 3日，服上方一剂即汗，身热已退，唯觉头晕咳嗽、神怯。 表邪虽解,肺寒尚未肃清，阳气尚虚，以四逆合二陈加细辛、 五味子，扶阳温寒主之。 黑附片50克，干姜26克，甘草10克，陈皮10克，法半 夏13克，茯苓13克，北细辛4克，五味子2克。 一剂尽,咳嗽立止，食量增加,精神恢复,病遂痊愈。":"Syndrome of both Taiyang and Shaoyin due to cold (severe cold) Zhang, 42 years old, lives at the bottom of Nanliansheng Lane, Wumiaoxia, Kunming City, Yunnan Province. The kidney qi was deficient, and on September 2, 1929, on his way home, it was rainy and he fell ill with a cold. At the beginning, the symptoms include body heat, aversion to cold, headache and body aches, addiction to sleeping (i.e., Shaoyin disease but a desire to sleep), thirst and a lack of hot drinks, and a heavy, thready and tight pulse. The tongue coating is white and slippery, and the texture is bluish-purple. Due to the deficiency of kidney qi, the Kanyang is weak internally and unable to defend the external surface to resist guest evil, so the cold wind takes advantage of the deficiency and goes straight into Shaoyin, blocking the movement of true yang, resulting in this condition. Treat it with Zhongjing Maxin Fuzi Decoction, which can warm the meridians and relieve the symptoms, strengthen the body and eliminate evil. 36 grams of Black Fu slices, 10 grams of Ephedra (boil for several times and remove the phlegm), 6 grams of Asarum, and 13 grams of Guizhijian. On the 3rd, I started sweating after taking just one dose. My fever had subsided, but I only felt dizzy, coughing and timid. Although the external evils have been resolved, the cold in the lungs has not been cleared away, and the yang energy is still weak. Combine the four inverses with the two chen and add asarum and schisandra to support the yang and warm the cold. 50 grams of black peel, 26 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of licorice, 10 grams of tangerine peel, 13 grams of Pinellia ternata, 13 grams of Poria, 4 grams of Asarum, and 2 grams of Schisandra chinensis. After one dose, the cough immediately stops, the food intake increases, the spirit recovers, and the disease is cured.",太阳病篇:"Taiyang disease",失眠:"insomnia",头痛:"headache",女:"female","如太阳误下致结胸者用陷胸汤，少阴下利厥逆者投四逆汤，方证对应丝丝入扣，绝无拖泥带水之笔。":"For example, if the sun goes down accidentally and causes breast knots, use Xianxiang Decoction. If Shaoyin relieves jueni, use Sini Decoction.","如治瘴疟用常山配草果，治湿热痢以马齿苋捣汁合蜜，治乳痈以蒲公英外敷内服并行，治跌打损伤以七叶莲、叶下花酒浸外擦，皆屡试屡验之方。":"For example, to treat miasma and malaria, use Changshan with grass and fruit; to treat damp and hot dysentery, use purslane pounded juice and honey; to treat mastitis, use dandelion for external application and oral administration; to treat bruises and injuries, use Aesculus aesculata and flower leaves soaked in wine and rubbed externally, all of which are tried and tested.","如阳脱危证大剂四逆加人参，亡阳谵妄投桂枝去芍药加蜀漆龙牡救逆汤，皆生死俄顷之际的决断，稍一迟疑则不及救。":"For example, for the syndrome of yang relief, a large dose of Sini is added with ginseng, for delirium due to yang, cinnamon twigs are removed and peony is added, and Shuqi Longmu Jiu Ni Decoction is used to make a decision at the moment of life and death. If you hesitate for a moment, it will be impossible to save.",妇科:"Gynecology","妇科以肝为先天，重在调畅气血，气行则血行。":"Gynecology takes the liver as its congenital factor and focuses on regulating qi and blood. When qi moves, blood moves.",妇科经验:"Gynecological experience",妇科验案:"Gynecological examination case",妊娠胎漏:"pregnancy loss","妊娠胎漏 （先兆流产） 范某之妻，年二十八岁，四州省会理县人":"Pregnancy miscarriage (threatened abortion) Fan’s wife, 28 years old, from Huili County, Sizhou Province","妊娠胎漏 （先兆流产） 范某之妻，年二十八岁，四州省会理县人。身孕六月，某 日因家务不慎，忽而跌仆，遂漏下渐如崩状，腰及少腹坠痛难 忍，卧床不起。因其夫公务未归，无资以疗,延至六、七日，仍 漏欲堕。余往诊之，气血大伤，胎恐难保,惟幸孕脉尚在，以大 补气血，扶阳益气引血归经为治，纵虽胎堕，可保产母无损 矣。拟方四逆当归补血汤加味治之。 附片100克，北口芪60克，当归身24克，阿胶12克（烊 化兑入），炙艾叶6克，炙甘草10克，大枣5枚（烧黑存性）。 服一剂，漏止其半，再剂则全止,三剂霍然，胎亦保住，至 足月而举一子，母子均安。按：附子补坎中一阳，助少火而生气，阳气上升，胎气始固。英、术补中土之气，脾气健运，则能统摄血液以归其经，入当归、阿胶以资既伤之血。艾、附相伍，能温暖下元以止腰腹之疼痛。姜、枣烧黑取其温经止血，且烧黑变苦，得甘草之甘以济之，苦甘化阴，阴血得生。阳气温升，阴血能补，则胎不堕矣。《内经》云：“治病必求其本。”本固而标自立矣，若只以止血为主，而不急固其气，则气散不能速回，其血何由而止？":'Pregnancy miscarriage (threatened abortion) Fan’s wife, 28 years old, is from Huili County, Sizhou Province. I was six months pregnant. One day due to carelessness in housework, I suddenly fell down. The leakage gradually became like a collapse. The pain in my waist and lower abdomen was unbearable and I was bedridden. Because her husband had not returned from his official duties, he had no money for treatment. It was delayed until six or seven days, and he still had leakage and was about to fall. I went to the hospital for diagnosis and found that the qi and blood were severely injured, and the fetus might not be saved. Fortunately, the pregnancy pulse was still there, so it could be treated by replenishing the qi and blood, supporting the yang and replenishing the qi and guiding the blood into the menstruation. Even if the fetus was aborted, the mother could be safe. Prepare the prescription Sini Danggui Buxue Decoction with added flavor to treat it. 100 grams of Fu Pian, 60 grams of Beikou Qi, 24 grams of Angelica sinensis, 12 grams of donkey-hide gelatin (blended and added), 6 grams of roasted mugwort leaves, 10 grams of roasted licorice, and 5 jujubes (burned black to preserve the properties). Taking one dose will stop half of the leakage, another dose will stop it all. After three doses, the fetus will be preserved. When the baby is brought to full term, both mother and baby are safe. Note: Aconite replenishes the yang in Kan, helps the less fire to enrage the body, the yang qi rises, and the fetal qi begins to solidify. Ying and Shu can supplement the qi of the middle earth and strengthen the spleen and movement, so they can control the blood and return it to its meridians, and add angelica and donkey-hide gelatin to relieve the injured blood. Moxa moxa and Fu Xiangwu can warm the lower yuan and relieve pain in the waist and abdomen. When ginger and jujube are burned black, they warm the menstrual flow and stop bleeding. If they are burned black and become bitter, the sweetness of licorice can be used to relieve the problem. When the Yang temperature rises and the Yin blood can replenish it, the fetus will not be aborted. "Nei Jing" says: "To treat a disease, we must seek its root." The root is solid and the standard is self-established. If we only focus on stopping bleeding and do not rush to consolidate the qi, then the scattered qi cannot be recovered quickly, and how can the bleeding be stopped?',"姚某，3岁":"Yao, 3 years old","姚某，3岁。初病发热咳嗽，某医以升提表散而佐清凉之剂。2剂后，麻疹隐隐现点，色象不鲜，发热已五六日，尚未出透延吴氏诊视。患儿昏迷无神，判为邪陷少阴而呈但欲寐之情，麻疹不能透达，若再迁延，势必转危。即以白通汤1剂：\\n附片60g，干姜15g，葱白4茎连须根。\\n服后，疹出透而色转红活，再剂则疹已渐灭，脉静身凉，食增神健而愈。":"Yao, 3 years old. When the patient has fever and cough at the beginning of the disease, a certain doctor uses Shengtibiao Powder and a cooling agent. After 2 doses, the measles appeared faintly, the color was not fresh, and the fever had been going on for five or six days, but there was no translucence yet. Wu's examination was carried out. The child is comatose and lacks consciousness. It is judged that the disease is trapped in the Shaoyin and the feeling of sleepiness is present. The measles cannot penetrate it. If it is delayed any longer, it will definitely become critical. That is, take 1 dose of Baitong Decoction:\\n60g of attached slices, 15g of dried ginger, 4 white scallions with fibrous roots. \\nAfter taking it, the rash appears clear and turns red and active. After another dose, the rash gradually disappears, the pulse is quiet and the body is cool, and the patient recovers after eating more.",姚氏妇科:"Yao's Gynecology","姚氏妇科“女子以血为本”学术思想集中呈现":`Yao's gynecology "women are blood-based" academic thoughts presented in a concentrated manner`,姚氏妇科流派代表:"Representative of the Yao School of Gynecology","姚氏妇科流派传承工作室正式揭牌，将系统整理姚氏妇科验案验方，推动流派学术经验的数字化传承。":"Yao's Gynecology School Inheritance Studio was officially unveiled, which will systematically organize Yao's Gynecology School's verified cases and prescriptions, and promote the digital inheritance of academic experience in the school.",姚氏妇科流派传承工作室落户昆明市中医医院:"Yao's gynecological school inheritance studio settled in Kunming Traditional Chinese Medicine Hospital",姚氏调经种子方:"Yao's Menstrual Regulation Seed Recipe",姚贞白:"Yao Zhenbai","姚贞白先生1910年生于昆明，姚氏世代业医，先生幼承家学，尽得姚氏妇科心传，又广涉温病、内科诸籍。":"Mr. Yao Zhenbai was born in Kunming in 1910. The Yao family has been practicing medicine for generations. Mr. Yao inherited his family's education at a young age. He has learned all about Yao's gynecology and has extensive knowledge of febrile diseases and internal medicine.","姚贞白先生妇科及内科验案精选，集中体现姚氏妇科“调气血、和冲任、重肝肾”的学术思想，为姚氏妇科流派传承之本。":`The selected cases of Mr. Yao Zhenbai's gynecology and internal medicine examinations embody Yao's gynecology academic thoughts of "regulating Qi and blood, harmonizing Chong and Ren, and rejuvenating the liver and kidneys", and are the foundation of the inheritance of Yao's gynecology school.`,姚贞白医案:"Yao Zhenbai medical case","姚贞白，昆明人，姚氏妇科流派第三代传人，以妇科名世。创办昆明市中医医院并任院长，滇中妇女赖以起疾者不可胜数。":"Yao Zhenbai, a native of Kunming, is the third generation descendant of the Yao School of Gynecology and is famous for her gynecology. He founded Kunming Traditional Chinese Medicine Hospital and served as its director. Countless women in central Yunnan relied on him to relieve their illnesses.",子午流注:"Ziwu Liuzhu",子午流注针法临床大家:"Clinical Master of Ziwu Flow Acupuncture","孕妇哮喘案 郑某，25岁":"Asthma case of pregnant woman Zheng, 25 years old","孕妇哮喘案\\n郑某，25岁。慢性哮喘病已14年，现身孕4月余。症见咳嗽短气而喘，痰多色白，咽喉不利，时发喘息哮鸣。面色淡而少华，目眶、口唇含青乌色。胸中闷胀，少气懒言，咳声低弱，咳时则由胸部牵引小腹作痛。舌苔白滑厚腻，舌质含青色；脉现弦滑，沉取则弱而无力。判为风寒伏于肺胃，久咳肺肾气虚，阳不足以运行，寒湿痰饮阻遏而成是证。法当开提表寒，补肾纳气，温化痰湿。方用小青龙汤加附片。附片开手即用100g。2剂后，咳喘各症均减。继用四逆、二陈合方加麻、辛、桂，附片加至200g，服后喘咳皆减轻。共服30余剂，哮喘咳嗽日渐平息痊愈。身孕无恙.至足月顺产一子。原按：昔有谓妇人身孕，乌、附、半夏皆所禁用，其实不然。盖乌、附、半夏，生者具有毒性，固不能服，只要炮制煎煮得法，去除毒性，因病施用，孕妇服之亦无妨碍。妇人怀孕，身为疾病所缠……务使邪去而正安，此实为安胎、固胎之要义。《素问•六元正纪大论》云：“妇人重身，毒之何如……有故无殒，亦无殒也。”此乃有是病而用是药，所谓有病则病当之，故孕妇无殒，胎亦无殒也。":'Asthma case of pregnant woman\\nZheng, 25 years old. I have been suffering from chronic asthma for 14 years and am now more than 4 months pregnant. Symptoms include coughing, shortness of breath and wheezing, white phlegm, indigestion in the throat, and occasional wheezing and wheezing. The complexion is light and lustrous, with bluish-black eyes and lips. There is tightness and swelling in the chest, little breath and laziness to speak, and a weak cough. When coughing, the chest pulls the lower abdomen and causes pain. The tongue coating is white, slippery and greasy, and the tongue texture is cyan; the pulse is stringy and slippery, and when it sinks, it is weak and weak. It is diagnosed as wind-cold lying in the lungs and stomach, chronic cough, lung and kidney qi deficiency, insufficient yang movement, and cold-damp phlegm blocking the syndrome. Fadang can be used to remove cold from the surface, nourish the kidneys and absorb qi, and warm and resolve phlegm and dampness. Use Xiaoqinglong Decoction and add the slices. The attached tablet is 100g ready to use. After 2 doses, all symptoms of cough and asthma were reduced. Following the use of Sini and Erchen combined prescriptions with Ma, Xin, Gui, and additional tablets to 200g, the asthma and cough were relieved after taking the medicine. After taking more than 30 doses in total, the asthma and cough gradually subsided and recovered. The pregnancy was fine and a baby was delivered to term. Original note: In the past, it was said that when a woman is pregnant, Wu, Fu, and Pinellia ternata are all forbidden, but this is not true. Gai Wu, Fu, and Pinellia ternata are toxic to living people and cannot be taken. As long as they are prepared and boiled properly to remove the toxicity, they can be used due to illness, and there is no problem in taking them by pregnant women. When a woman is pregnant and is troubled by illness...it is necessary to get rid of the evil and bring peace of mind. This is actually the key to keeping the fetus safe and stable. "Su Wen·Liu Yuan Zheng Ji Da Lun" says: "A woman has a heavy body, and the poison is like this... There is a reason why there is no death, and there is no death." This is because there is a disease and the medicine is used. It is said that if there is a disease, the disease should be treated. Therefore, the pregnant woman will not die, and the fetus will not die.',学术思想:"Academic Thoughts",学术讲义:"academic handouts","学生严某，门牙肿痛，口唇牙龈高凸，恶寒特甚，头痛体困，手足逆冷，…":"Student Yan suffered from swollen and painful front teeth, protruding lips and gums, severe aversion to cold, headache and feeling sleepy, cold hands and feet,...","学生严某，门牙肿痛，口唇牙龈高凸，恶寒特甚，头痛体困，手足逆冷，口不渴；唇龈虽高肿，但皮色乌青；舌苔白滑质青，脉沉细而紧。请吴老师诊治，处予大剂四逆汤加肉桂、麻黄、细辛。附片90g，干姜45g，炙甘草9g，肉桂12g，麻黄12g，北细辛6g。\\n服后诸症旋即消失而愈（《著名中医学家吴佩衡诞辰一百周年纪念专集》）。\\n按：牙痛一症，方书多认为热证，特别是急性者，最易误诊。吴氏辨为阴证夹表，处予大剂四逆汤加肉桂引火归原，略加麻黄、细辛辛散开表，药精剂重，可圈可点。":'Student Yan suffered from swollen and painful front teeth, raised lips and gums, severe aversion to cold, headache and body drowsiness, cold hands and feet, and no thirst. Although his lips and gums were swollen, his skin was black and blue; his tongue coating was white, slippery and green, and his pulse was deep, thin and tight. Ask Teacher Wu for diagnosis and treatment, and give a large dose of Sini Decoction plus cinnamon, ephedra, and asarum. 90g of Futian, 45g of dried ginger, 9g of licorice, 12g of cinnamon, 12g of ephedra, and 6g of asarum. \\nAll symptoms disappeared immediately after taking it ("Special Collection Commemorating the 100th Anniversary of the Birth of Famous Chinese Medicine Scientist Wu Peiheng"). \\nNote: As a symptom of toothache, many prescriptions believe that heat syndrome, especially acute ones, is most likely to be misdiagnosed. Wu diagnosed it as yin syndrome with superficial symptoms, and prescribed a large dose of Sini Decoction plus cinnamon to bring the fire back to its original state, and a little addition of ephedra and asarum to disperse the superficial symptoms. The medicinal essence was heavy and remarkable.',守正创新:"Keeping integrity and innovation","宣肺降气，化痰止嗽":"Xuanfei, lowering qi, resolving phlegm and relieving coughs","寒 疟 阎某之妻，患疟证二十余日，每日午后发作，先寒而后 热，寒…":"Cold Malaria Yan's wife has been suffering from malaria syndrome for more than 20 days, with attacks every afternoon, with cold first and then hot, cold...","寒 疟 阎某之妻，患疟证二十余日，每日午后发作，先寒而后 热，寒甚则颤栗鼓颌，热退则汗出如洗，发作之时头痛如劈， 饮食不进，呕吐酸苦涎沫，大便溏泻，两胁撑胀而痛、惟喜滚 饮。脉细迟无力。舌苔白滑，质含青色，曾服消食清热平肝等 十余剂未效。此乃阳气内虚，阳不胜阴，肝邪夹寒水之气上 逆,午后之时，阴盛阳虚，真阳被阴邪格拒,浮越于外,遂成是 状。拟四逆汤加味治之。 天雄片60克，干姜30克，公丁香5克，上肉桂10克（研 末，泡水兑入），法半夏12克，茯苓30克，甘草6克。 并嘱先吞服乌梅丸二粒,是晚服药一剂，次晨又一剂，午 后遂不复作。后照原方加砂仁10克，两剂而愈。":"Cold malaria Yan's wife suffered from malaria syndrome for more than 20 days, with attacks in the afternoon every day. She was cold first and then hot. If the cold was severe, she would tremble and bulge her jaw. When the heat subsided, she would sweat profusely. When the attack occurred, she would have a headache like splitting, inability to eat, vomiting, sour and bitter saliva, loose stools, and bloated and painful flanks, but she liked to drink water. Thready and weak pulse. The tongue coating is white and slippery, with a bluish texture. I have taken more than ten doses of Xiaoshi, heat-clearing and liver-calming products, but no effect. This is the internal deficiency of yang energy, the yang cannot overcome the yin, the liver evil and the cold water qi are reversed. In the afternoon, the yin is excessive and the yang is deficient. The true yang is rejected by the yin evil grid and floats to the outside, resulting in this condition. It is treated by adding Sini Decoction. 60 grams of Tianxiong slices, 30 grams of dried ginger, 5 grams of cloves, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 12 grams of pinellia, 30 grams of Poria, and 6 grams of licorice. He was also instructed to swallow two black plum pills first, one dose in the evening, and another dose in the next morning, and no more in the afternoon. Then add 10 grams of amomum villosum according to the original prescription, and it will heal after two doses.","寒 闭":"cold closed","寒 闭 （误服蚕沙酒引发危证） 1924年2月，曾治一奇证，颇险":"Han Shuan (Dangerous Syndrome Caused by Mistaken Use of Silkworm Sand Wine) In February 1924, a strange syndrome was treated, which was quite dangerous.","寒 闭 （误服蚕沙酒引发危证） 1924年2月，曾治一奇证，颇险。有姚姓之女，年十八岁， 因上年患白喉证服寒凉药过多以致信期不调，三、五月一至， 时时“发瘀” 。此系阳虚血寒已极无疑。该女因天癸数月不至， 用蚕沙二两泡酒服之，冀使通达，殊料服两小盏后，经亦未 通，骤发危象。始延某医诊视，断言无救，未拟方而去。随即延 余诊视之,六脉俱绝,唇爪俱黑，面目全身皆发青，牙关紧闭， 用物拨开,见口舌亦青黑，四肢厥逆，不省人事，气喘欲脱。缘 由体素虚寒,且服过量蚕沙酒,亦系寒凉之物，致成纯阴无阳 之候，病情险恶。余始疑无救，然口中气息尚存，不忍坐视而 归。若用他药,恐为时不及,急以上肉桂泡水灌之,偶咽下一、 二口，觉气稍平。又速频频灌喂,喘息渐定，稍识人事，目珠偶 动，呼之乃应。继而复诊,脉仍不见应指。余思寻之，暴病无脉 系闭，久病无脉乃绝。此乃暴病所致，肉桂强心温暖血分之 寒,服之气机稍回,必有生机。约两小时方过,病者始能言语， 言其周身麻木，腹中扭痛,忽而大泻酱黑稀便。再诊,脉隐隐欲现，色象稍转,气微喘，扶之以卧，试其舌，青黑冰指，乃以 大剂回阳饮治之。 黄附片60克，干姜20克，上肉桂20克（研末，泡水兑 入），甘草10克。 次日诊视，六脉俱回，轻取弦紧重按无力而空。唇舌青黑 悉退，唯面部仍稍带青绿色，觉头晕，体痛，腹中冷痛，喜滚 饮。此阳气尚虚，里寒未净，宜击鼓直追，方能定夺。继以上方 加味治之，连服数剂，厥疾遂瘳。 天雄片60克，干姜12克，黑姜12克，上肉桂心10克 （研末，泡水兑入），桂枝尖12克，炒吴茱萸6克，法半夏12 克，茯苓15克，甘草6克。":`Han Shuan (Dangerous Syndrome Caused by Mistaking Silkworm Sand Wine) In February 1924, he was treated for a strange syndrome, which was quite dangerous. There is an eighteen-year-old daughter surnamed Yao. She suffered from diphtheria last year and took too many cold and cooling medicines, which caused irregularities in her period. Between March and May, she would suffer from "blood stasis" from time to time. This is undoubtedly due to Yang deficiency and blood coldness. Since Tiangui was not coming for several months, the woman soaked two ounces of silkworm excrement in wine and drank it in the hope that her menstruation would be smoothened. However, after taking two small cups of the special material, her menstrual flow was not clear either, and she suddenly developed a crisis. Shi Yan was examined by a certain doctor, who concluded that there was no cure and left without formulating a prescription. Immediately after further examination, the six pulses were dead, the lips and claws were all black, the face and the whole body were blue, the teeth were closed, and when they were removed with something, the mouth and tongue were also blue and black, the limbs were reversed, unconscious, and he was panting. The reason is that the body is deficient and cold, and excessive consumption of silkworm excrement wine, which is also a cold and cool thing, leads to a state of pure yin without yang, and the condition is dangerous. Yu Shi doubted that there was no way to save him, but he still had breath in his mouth and couldn't bear to sit back and watch. If you use other medicines, it may be too late, so soak the above cinnamon in water and drink it. Occasionally, you swallow one or two mouthfuls and feel a little flat. He was fed again and again quickly, his breathing gradually calmed down, he became a little aware of people, his eyes occasionally moved, and he responded to calls. After a follow-up visit, the pulse was still missing. After thinking about it, I found that there is no pulse in sudden illness and the system is closed, and if there is no pulse in long-term illness, it will be terminal. This is caused by a sudden illness. Cinnamon strengthens the heart and warms the cold blood. If you take it, the Qi will be slightly restored, and you will have vitality. About two hours passed before the patient could speak. He said that his whole body was numb, his abdomen was sprained, and he suddenly had heavy diarrhea and black and loose stools. After further diagnosis, the pulse was faint, the color changed slightly, and the breath was slightly wheezing. I helped him lie down and tested his tongue. He found blue and black ice fingers, so he treated it with a large dose of Huiyang Drink. 60 grams of Huangfu slices, 20 grams of dried ginger, 20 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), and 10 grams of licorice. On examination the next day, all six pulses returned, and they were weak and empty after lightly picking up the string and pressing firmly. The blue and black lips and tongue have completely subsided, but the face is still slightly green. I feel dizzy, have body pain, have cold pain in my abdomen, and like to drink water. This yang energy is still weak and the internal cold is not purified. It is better to beat the drum and pursue it directly to make a decision. Following the above treatment with added flavor, take several doses, and the disease will subside. 60 grams of Tianxiong slices, 12 grams of dried ginger, 12 grams of black ginger, 10 grams of cinnamon core (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 12 grams of cinnamon branch tip, 6 grams of fried Evodia, 12 grams of pinellia, 15 grams of Poria, and 6 grams of licorice.`,寒凉冰伏之误治救逆法度详备:"Detailed instructions for mistreatment of cold, cold, and ice-free conditions.",寒湿胃痛:"cold dampness stomachache","寒湿胃痛 顾某，男，年四旬，云南省鲁甸县人,住上海马斯南路息 庐三号":"Stomach pain caused by cold and dampness. Gu, male, 40 years old, from Ludian County, Yunnan Province, lives at No. 3, Xilu, Masnan Road, Shanghai","寒湿胃痛 顾某，男，年四旬，云南省鲁甸县人,住上海马斯南路息 庐三号。肾气虚，脾湿素重，时值酷暑炎热季节，常食西瓜凉 饮，夜卧贪凉，复受冷风所袭，遂致皖腹疼痛不止，痛极则彻 及心胸腰背、水米不下，汗出淋漓，辗转反侧睡卧不安，时时 呻吟。余诊之，颜面青黯，舌苔白滑质含青色，脉来一息两至 半，沉迟无力，手足厥冷。此乃肝肾之阴夹寒水脾湿凝聚三 焦，凑卜犯胃，阳不足以运行，而成是状。先以上肉桂10克研 末泡水与服之。服后旋即呕吐涎沫碗许,此为寒湿外除佳兆， 继以吴萸四逆汤加味治之。 附片100克，干姜30克，上肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑入） 公丁 6克，白胡椒6克（捣末，分次吞服），吴茱萸10克，甘草 10克。 服一剂，涌吐酸苦涎水两大碗,痛减其半。再服一剂，又 吐涎水两大碗，其痛大减，遂得安卧。次晚续诊，脉已一息四 至，汗止厥回，诸痛俱瘥。继以桂附理中汤二剂调理而愈。":"Stomach pain due to cold and dampness. Gu, male, in his forties, from Ludian County, Yunnan Province, lives at No. 3 Xilu, Masnan Road, Shanghai. Kidney qi is deficient and spleen dampness is heavy. It is a hot season. People often eat watermelon and drink cold drinks. They lie down at night and are hit by cold winds. This causes endless pain in the abdomen and abdomen. When the pain is extreme, it reaches the chest, waist and back, and the water is not enough. The patient is sweating profusely, tossing and turning in bed, restless, and moans from time to time. Upon further examination, the patient's face was blue and gloomy, the tongue coating was white and slippery with cyan color, the pulse was slow and weak, and the pulse was slow and weak, and the hands and feet were cold. This is the result of the combination of cold water and spleen dampness in the liver and kidneys and the condensation of the three burners, which interfere with the stomach and the yang is insufficient to circulate, resulting in this condition. First, grind 10 grams of cinnamon into powder, soak it in water and take it. Immediately after taking it, you vomited a bowlful of saliva, which is a good sign that the cold and dampness have been eliminated. You can then treat it with Wu Yu Sini Decoction. 100 grams of Aconite, 30 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 6 grams of male diced, 6 grams of white pepper (mash into powder, swallow in batches), 10 grams of Evodia, and 10 grams of licorice. Take one dose and vomit two large bowls of sour and bitter saliva, and the pain will be reduced by half. After taking another dose and spitting out two large bowls of saliva, the pain was greatly reduced and he could sleep peacefully. After a follow-up examination the next night, the pulse had stopped flowing and returned, and all the pains had subsided. After taking two doses of Guifuli Zhongtang, the condition was cured.","寒热错杂、厥热胜复之辨析。":"Differentiation and analysis of mixed cold and heat, and the combination of cold and heat.","寒痹、热痹、顽痹之温针灸与刺络法。":"Warm acupuncture and pricking method for cold paralysis, heat paralysis and stubborn paralysis.","寒痹温针灸，热痹刺络放血，顽痹兼用火针，并详述各法之适应证与禁忌，使学者知所取舍。":"Warming acupuncture is used for cold paralysis, bloodletting is used for hot paralysis, and fire acupuncture is used for stubborn paralysis. The indications and contraindications of each method are described in detail, so that scholars know what to choose.","寒闭案 姚女，18岁，因上年患白喉服寒凉药过多，以致信期不调，三…":"Hanguan case: Yao Nv, 18 years old, suffered from diphtheria last year and took too many cold and cold medicines, which caused irregularity in her period of study. Three...","寒闭案\\n姚女，18岁，因上年患白喉服寒凉药过多，以致信期不调，三五月一至，时时“发痧”，此系阳虚血寒已极无疑。因天癸数月不至，用蚕砂60g泡酒服之，冀使通达。殊料服2小盏后，经亦未通，骤发危象，急延吴氏诊视：六脉俱绝.唇爪俱黑，面目全身皆发青，牙关紧闭；用物拨开，见口舌亦青黑；四肢厥逆，不省人事，气喘欲脱，缘由素体虚寒，且过服蚕砂酒，系寒凉之物，致成纯阴无阳之候。若用他药为时不及，急以上肉桂泡水灌之，偶咽下一二口，觉气稍平；频频灌喂，喘息渐定，稍识人事，目珠偶动，呼之乃应，脉仍不见应指。因思暴病无脉系闭，久病无脉乃绝。此乃暴病所致，肉桂强心温暖血分之寒，服之气机稍回，必有生机。约2小时始能言语，言其周身麻木，腹中扭痛，忽而大泻酱黑稀便。诊脉隐隐欲现，舌象稍转，气微喘，试其舌青黑冰指，乃以大剂回阳饮治之：\\n黄附片60g，干姜20g，上肉桂20g（研末，泡水兑入），甘草10g。\\n次日六脉俱冋，轻取弦紧重按无力而空。唇舌青黑悉退，唯面部仍稍带青绿色。觉头晕，体痛，腹中冷痛，喜滚饮。此阳气尚虚，里寒未净，宜击鼓直追，继以上方加味治之：\\n天雄片60g，干姜12g，黑姜12g，上肉桂心10g（研末，泡水兑入），桂尖12g，炒吴萸6g，半夏12g，茯苓15g，甘草6g。\\n连服数剂，厥疾遂廖。\\n按：厥证无论闭脱，均系急危重症，用附子需要久煎，恐怕缓不济急。骤发危象之际，吴氏先用肉桂泡水灌服救急，然后以大回阳饮回阳救逆，药精量重，典型的经典火神派风格。":`Hanguan case\\nNv Yao, 18 years old, suffered from diphtheria last year and took too many cold and cooling medicines, which caused the irregularity of her period. She often suffered from "sha" during March and May. This was undoubtedly caused by Yang deficiency and blood cold. Since Tiangui is not here for a few months, I soaked 60g of silkworm sand in wine and drank it in the hope that it would lead to enlightenment. After taking 2 small cups of the special medicine, the menstrual flow was not clear, and a crisis suddenly appeared. Wu's diagnosis showed that all six pulses were dead, the lips and claws were all black, the face and body were all blue, and the teeth were shut; when the object was removed, the mouth and tongue were also black and blue; the limbs were reversed, unconscious, and the breath was about to escape. If it is too late to use other medicines, soak the above cinnamon in water and pour it. Occasionally swallow one or two mouthfuls, and feel that the breath is slightly flat. After frequent feeding, the wheezing gradually subsides, and a little awareness of people, the eyes occasionally move, and the call is answered, but the pulse is still missing. Due to sudden illness, there is no pulse and the system is closed, and if there is long-term illness, there is no pulse. This is caused by a sudden illness. Cinnamon strengthens the heart and warms the cold blood. If you take it, the Qi will be restored a little, and you will have vitality. He could not speak until about 2 hours later. He said that his whole body was numb, his abdomen was sprained, and he suddenly had heavy diarrhea with black and loose stools. The pulse is vague, the tongue is slightly turned, and the breath is slightly wheezing. Test the tongue with green and black ice, and treat it with a large dose of Huiyang Drink:\\n60g of Huangfu Pian, 20g of dried ginger, 20g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), and 10g of licorice. \\nThe next day, all six meridians were suppressed. I picked up the string lightly and pressed it tightly, feeling weak and empty. The blue and black lips and tongue have all receded, but the face is still slightly green. Feeling dizzy, body ache, cold pain in abdomen, like to drink water. If the yang energy is still deficient and the internal cold is not purified, it is better to beat the drum and treat it with the following additions: 60g Tianxiong tablets, 12g dried ginger, 12g black ginger, 10g cinnamon core (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 12g Guijian, 6g fried Wuyu, 12g Pinellia ternata, 15g Poria, and 6g licorice. \\nAfter taking several doses in a row, he died of illness. \\nNote: Regardless of whether the abscess syndrome is severe or severe, aconite needs to be decoctioned for a long time, which may not relieve the emergency. When a crisis suddenly occurred, Wu first soaked cinnamon in water and drank it to relieve the emergency, and then used the Dahuiyang drink to restore the Yang. The medicine was heavy in essence, typical of the classic Vulcan style.`,封底:"back cover",封面:"cover","尊崇《伤寒论》，以六经辨证为临证之纲，主张“辨证务求其本”。":'He respects "Treatise on Febrile Diseases", takes the syndrome differentiation of the Six Meridians as the guideline for clinical diagnosis, and advocates "seeking the root of syndrome differentiation".',"小儿“脾常不足、肺常虚”，治病须时时顾护脾胃。":'In children, "the spleen is often deficient and the lungs are often deficient." To treat the disease, the spleen and stomach must be taken care of at all times.',"小儿伤寒病并肠出血危证 张某之子,年八岁，云南省宾川县人":"Children with typhoid fever and dangerous intestinal bleeding Zhang's son, eight years old, from Binchuan County, Yunnan Province","小儿伤寒病并肠出血危证 张某之子,年八岁，云南省宾川县人。1945年4月，患伤 寒病已十余日，住原昆华医院治疗，病势日趋严重，遂将病儿 移回家中。4月23日，改延余诊视。面青唇白而焦，舌质红而 润，无苔，脉象弦紧,按之则空虚无力，体温潮热，日轻夜重， 神识昏愦，言语昏乱,腹胀如蛊，曾大便下血二次,小便短少 而赤，形体瘦羸。此系患伤寒病，寒入阴分，致腹中阴霾四布， 元阳大虚，已成危证,恐有生阳将脱之虞。当以扶阳抑阴治 之。然温热之药服后，触动阴寒,必有吐泻之状，由于正气太 虚，一线残阳将脱，唯恐吐泻之时，又易痰鸣气喘虚脱，思维 再三,只有背城一战,方有挽回之机,犹豫迟疑,错过病机,则 追之莫及矣。急以通脉四逆汤加上肉桂主之。 黑附片100克，干姜26克，生甘草10克，上肉桂10克 （研末，泡水，兑入），葱白2茎。 是晚七时，张君复来寓告知，服药二次，旋即呕吐涎水， 继则泄泻黑粪，腹胀已消去其半，幸未气喘痰鸣，唯精神太 弱。当即告之，已有转机，宜原方再进一剂。 24日晨复诊。昨日服药后吐泻，腹胀若失，弦紧脉象已 平，潮热亦退。缘伤寒大病日久，元阳太耗，鼓胀虽消，而邪阴 未净，阳神未充,散乱无主，尚见沉迷无神，时有烦乱说昏话。 然病情已有转机，毋须置疑,仍以扶阳抑阴主之。 附片130克，干姜26克，上肉桂13克（研末，泡水兑 入），西砂仁4克，茯神16克，炙远志3克，生甘草4克。 25日三诊。服昨方后已不再吐，大便溏泻三次，色已转 黄,此系胃阳来复之兆。烦乱已乎，神识亦清明，体温、脉搏已 转正常。稍进食物,病势逐渐减退，大有转危为安之象，可期 痊愈矣。唯阳神尚虚，邪阴未净,仍以扶阳扶正主之。 附片130克，干姜26克，上肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑入）， 西砂仁6克，法半夏6克，炙远志6克，炙冬花6克，茯神15 克，甘草6克。 26日四诊。唇舌红润,脉较有神,精神较佳,饮食大增，已 无他痛苦，继用黄芪四逆汤加味调理数剂而愈。 附片130克，干姜26克，上肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑 入），北口芪15克，炙远志6克，生甘草6克。":"Childhood typhoid fever complicated by intestinal bleeding risk: Zhang's son, eight years old, from Binchuan County, Yunnan Province. In April 1945, he had been suffering from typhoid fever for more than ten days. He was admitted to Kunhua Hospital for treatment. However, his condition became increasingly serious, so he moved the sick child home. On April 23, the examination was postponed. Blue face, white and burnt lips, red and moist tongue without coating, stringy and tight pulse that feels empty and weak when pressed, body temperature and hot flashes, light days and heavy nights, dizzy consciousness, confused speech, abdominal distension like a gu, blood in the stool twice, short and red urine, and thin body. This is a syndrome caused by typhoid fever, in which cold enters the yin component, causing haze to spread all over the abdomen, and Yuanyang is greatly deficient. This has become a critical syndrome, and there is a risk that Yang will be lost. It should be treated by supporting Yang and suppressing Yin. However, after taking the warm medicine, if the yin and cold are touched, there will be vomiting and diarrhea. Because the righteousness is too weak, the remaining yang will disappear. I am afraid that when the vomiting and diarrhea occur, it will be easy to cause phlegm, asthma, and collapse. I think over and over again that the only way to recover is to fight against the city. If you hesitate and miss the opportunity, you will be out of reach. For urgent treatment, use Tongmai Sini Decoction plus cinnamon. 100 grams of black monkshood slices, 26 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of raw licorice, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water, and mix in), and 2 white stalks of scallions. At seven o'clock in the evening, Zhang Jun came back to the apartment and told him that after taking the medicine for the second time, he immediately vomited saliva, followed by diarrhea and black feces. Half of the abdominal distension had disappeared. Fortunately, he did not have asthma or phlegm, but he was too weak. Immediately tell him that there has been a turn for the better and he should take another dose of the original prescription. Follow-up visit on the morning of the 24th. After taking the medicine yesterday, I had vomiting and diarrhea, and the abdominal distension was gone, my pulse was tight and my pulse has subsided, and my hot flashes have subsided. It is due to the serious illness of typhoid fever that the Yuan Yang is too depleted. Although the bulging subsides, the evil Yin is not purified, the Yang Shen is not fully charged, and it is scattered and without a master. It is still seen as indulging and lack of energy, and sometimes it is agitated and talks faintly. Although the condition has improved, there is no doubt that the main method is to support Yang and suppress Yin. 130 grams of Fu Shen, 26 grams of dried ginger, 13 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 4 grams of Amomum villosum, 16 grams of Fushen, 3 grams of Polygala, and 4 grams of raw licorice. Three consultations on the 25th. After taking yesterday's prescription, I stopped vomiting, had loose stools and had diarrhea three times, and the color turned yellow, which is a sign of the recovery of stomach yang. I am no longer disturbed, my consciousness is clear, and my body temperature and pulse have returned to normal. With a little food intake, the condition of the disease will gradually subside, and the situation seems to be turning around, and recovery can be expected. Only the Yang God is still weak and the evil Yin has not been purified, so it is still the main thing to support the Yang and rectify it. 130 grams of Futian, 26 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 6 grams of amomum villosum, 6 grams of pinellia, 6 grams of polygala, 6 grams of winter flowers, 15 grams of poria, and 6 grams of licorice. Four consultations on the 26th. The lips and tongue are rosy, the pulse is more energetic, the spirit is better, the diet has increased significantly, and there is no other pain. After a few doses of Huangqi Sini Decoction, the condition was cured. 130 grams of Aconite, 26 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 15 grams of Beikou Qi, 6 grams of Polygala, and 6 grams of raw licorice.","小儿伤寒病并肠出血危证案 张某之子，8岁":"A critical case of typhoid fever and intestinal bleeding in a child: Zhang’s son, 8 years old","小儿伤寒病并肠出血危证案\\n张某之子，8岁。1945年4月，患伤寒病已十余日，住原昆华医院，病势日趋严重，遂将病儿移回家中。\\n4月23日改延余诊视。面青唇白而焦，舌质红而润无苔，脉象弦紧，按之则空虚无力。潮热，日轻夜重，神识昏愦，言语昏乱，腹胀如蛊。曾大便下血2次，小便短少而赤，形体瘦羸。此系患伤寒病寒入阴分，致腹中阴霾四布，元阳大虚，已成危证，恐有生阳将脱之虞。当以扶阳抑阴治之。然温热之药服后，触动阴寒，必有吐泻之状，由于正气太虚，一线残阳将脱，唯恐吐泻之时，又易痰鸣气喘虚脱，思考再三，只有背城一战，方有挽回之机，犹豫迟疑，错过病机，则追之莫及矣。急以通脉四逆汤加上肉桂主之：黑附片100g，干姜26g，生草10g，上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），葱白2茎。\\n是晚7时，张君来寓告知，服药2次旋即呕吐涎水，继则泄泻黑粪，腹胀已消去其半，幸未气喘痰鸣，唯精神太弱。当即告之已有转机，宜原方再进1剂。\\n24日复诊：服药后吐泻、腹胀若失，弦紧脉象已平，潮热亦退。缘伤寒大病日久，元阳大耗，鼓胀虽消而阴邪未净，阳神未充，散乱无主，尚见沉迷无神，时有烦乱说昏话。然病情已有转机毋庸置疑，仍以扶阳抑阴主之。\\n附片130g，干姜26g，上肉桂13g（研末，泡水兑人），西砂仁4g，茯神16g，炙远志3g，生草4g。\\n25日三诊：服昨方后已不再吐，大便溏泻3次，色已转黄。此系胃阳来复之兆。烦乱已平，神识亦清明，体温、脉搏已转正常，稍进食物。病势逐渐减退，大有转危为安之象，可期痊愈矣。唯阳神尚虚，阴邪未净，仍以扶阳扶正主之。\\n附片130g，干姜26g，上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），西砂仁6g，法夏6g，炙远志6g，炙冬花6g，茯神15g，甘草6g。\\n26日四诊：唇舌红润，脉较有神，精神较佳，饮食大增，已无痛苦。继用黄芪四逆汤加味调理数剂而愈：\\n附片130g，干姜26g，上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），北艾15g，炙远志6g，生草6g。\\n不仅在成人中投用大剂量附子，对婴幼儿童也敢于放手加量，胆识确非常医可及。":"A critical case of typhoid fever and intestinal bleeding in a child\\nZhang’s son, 8 years old. In April 1945, he had been suffering from typhoid fever for more than ten days. He was admitted to the original Kunhua Hospital. The illness became increasingly serious, so the sick child was moved back home. \\nOn April 23, the remaining medical examinations will be postponed. The face is blue, the lips are white and burnt, the tongue is red and moist without coating, the pulse is stringy and tight, and feels empty and weak when pressed. Hot flashes, light days and heavy nights, dizzy consciousness, confused speech, abdominal distension like a gu. He had blood in his stool twice, his urine was short and red, and he was thin and emaciated. This is caused by the cold entering the yin component of typhoid fever, causing haze to spread all over the abdomen, and the primordial yang is greatly deficient. It has become a dangerous syndrome, and there is a fear that the yang will be lost. It should be treated by supporting Yang and suppressing Yin. However, after taking the warm medicine, if the yin and cold are touched, there will be vomiting and diarrhea. Because the righteousness is too weak, the remaining yang will disappear. I am afraid that when the vomiting and diarrhea occur, I will easily suffer from phlegm, asthma, and collapse. I think over and over again. Only by fighting against the city can I have a chance to recover. If I hesitate and miss the opportunity, I will be out of reach. For urgent treatment, use Tongmai Sini Decoction plus cinnamon: 100g of black Fu slices, 26g of dried ginger, 10g of raw grass, 10g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), and 2 white stalks of scallion. \\nAt 7 o'clock in the evening, Zhang Jun came to the apartment and told him that he vomited saliva immediately after taking the medicine twice, and then had black stools. Half of the abdominal distension had disappeared. Fortunately, he did not have asthma or phlegm, but he was too weak. Immediately tell him that there has been a turnaround and he should take another dose of the original prescription. \\nRevisited on the 24th: After taking the medicine, the vomiting, diarrhea and abdominal distension disappeared, the pulse was tight and flat, and the hot flashes subsided. Due to a serious illness caused by typhoid fever, the Yuanyang is greatly depleted. Although the bulge has disappeared, the Yin evil has not been purified, the Yang spirit has not been fully charged, and it is scattered and without a master. It is still seen as indulging and lack of energy, and sometimes it is agitated and talks in a daze. However, there is no doubt that the condition has improved, and the main method is to support Yang and suppress Yin. \\n130g of attached pieces, 26g of dried ginger, 13g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 4g of amomum villosum, 16g of Poria, 3g of Polygala, and 4g of raw grass. \\nThird consultation on the 25th: After taking yesterday's prescription, I no longer vomited, had loose stools and diarrhea 3 times, and the color has turned yellow. This is a sign of the return of stomach yang. The agitation has subsided, the consciousness is clear, the body temperature and pulse have returned to normal, and I have eaten a little food. The condition of the disease is gradually subsided, and there are signs that the crisis is over, and recovery can be expected. Only the Yang God is still weak and the Yin evil has not been purified, so it is still the main thing to support the Yang and rectify it. \\n130g of attached pieces, 26g of dried ginger, 10g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 6g of amomum villosum, 6g of farsia, 6g of polygala, 6g of winter flower, 15g of poria, and 6g of licorice. \\nFourth consultation on the 26th: The lips and tongue are red, the pulse is more energetic, the spirit is better, the diet has increased significantly, and there is no pain. Then add several doses of Astragalus Sini Decoction with seasonings to heal:\\n130g of Fu Pian, 26g of dried ginger, 10g of cassia cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 15g of mugwort, 6g of Polygala, and 6g of raw grass. \\nNot only do adults use large doses of aconite, but they also dare to increase the dosage for infants and young children. The courage is indeed extraordinary.",小儿咳喘:"Cough and asthma in children",小儿咳嗽:"Cough in children",小儿急惊风:"Infantile convulsions","小儿急惊风(一) 柯某之长子，年一岁半，住云南省昆明市原铁道分扃":"Infantile convulsions (1) Ke's eldest son, one and a half years old, lives in the former railway branch of Kunming City, Yunnan Province","小儿急惊风(一) 柯某之长子，年一岁半，住云南省昆明市原铁道分扃。 1922年阴历九月初六日晨，寐醒抱出，冒风而惊，发热，自汗 沉迷，角弓反张，手足抽搐，目上视，指纹赤而浮，唇赤舌淡 白，脉来浮缓。由于风寒阻遏太阳经气运行之机，加以小儿营 卫未充,脏腑柔嫩,不耐风寒，以致猝然抽搐而成急惊风证。 此为太阳肌表之证，以仲景桂枝汤主之，使中于太阳肌膜之 邪,得微汗而解。 桂枝尖10克，杭芍10克，甘草6克，生姜10克，小枣7 枚。 入粳米一小撮同煎，嘱服后温覆而卧,使得微汗。 一剂尽，即熟寐，汗出热退，次日霍然。 按：此证利在急治，倘迁延日久，别生变故，难以逆料。 案内桂枝全方，力量甚足，故效如桴鼓。":"Infantile convulsions (1) Ke's eldest son, one and a half years old, lives in the former railway branch of Kunming City, Yunnan Province. On the morning of the sixth day of the ninth lunar month in 1922, I woke up from sleep and was taken out. I was frightened by the wind, had fever, suffered from spontaneous sweating, opisthotonus, twitching of my hands and feet, my eyes looked upward, my fingerprints were red and floating, my lips were red and white, my tongue was white, and my pulse was slow and slow. Because the wind and cold block the movement of the solar meridian qi, the child's Yingwei is not fully replenished and the internal organs are tender and intolerant to the wind and cold, resulting in sudden convulsions and wind syndrome. This is a symptom of the sun muscle membrane. Zhongjing Guizhi Decoction can be used to treat the evil in the sun muscle membrane and relieve it with slight sweating. 10 grams of Guizhijian, 10 grams of peony root, 6 grams of licorice, 10 grams of ginger, and 7 jujubes. Add a handful of japonica rice and fry together. After taking it, you should warm it up and lie down to make you sweat slightly. After one dose, you will fall into a deep sleep, sweat, and fever will subside, and you will feel dizzy the next day. Note: The advantage of this syndrome is urgent treatment. If it is delayed for a long time, other changes will occur, which is difficult to predict. There are all kinds of cassia twigs in the case, and they are very powerful, so they are as effective as a drum.","小儿急惊风（二） （风寒误治救逆） 朱小弟，生甫两月，禀赋单薄":"Children with acute convulsions (Part 2) (Rescue caused by mistreatment of wind-cold) Zhu Xiaodi was only two months old and had a weak endowment.","小儿急惊风（二） （风寒误治救逆） 朱小弟，生甫两月，禀赋单薄。某日因感风寒而病,身热 咳嗽，不思乳食，多啼声。医以清热解表之剂，热不退，发惊 惕。又复以追风清热镇惊等法以治之，竟沉迷不乳，体若燔 炭，自汗肢冷,咳嗽喘挣不已，痰声漉漉，时作角弓抽掣，奄奄 一息。后延余诊之，指纹青黑透关,面唇均含青象，舌白而腻。 此为风寒误治引邪入于阴分，阳不胜阴，虚阳浮越于外，法当 扶阳驱寒。 附片20克，炮姜6克，京半夏6克，北细辛2克，生麻茸 2克，茯苓10克，甘草3克。 频频喂服,一剂尽，汗出，热退其半，已不发惊抽掣，喘咳 减，始能吮乳。再剂病退七、八。去麻、辛，又服二剂后，诸证 悉除。":"Children with acute convulsions (2) (Rescue caused by mistreatment of wind-cold) Little brother Zhu was only two months old and had a weak endowment. One day, he fell ill due to a cold. He had a fever, coughed, did not want to eat or drink, and cried a lot. Treat the patient with an agent that clears away heat and relieves the external symptoms. The fever does not go away and the patient becomes frightened and alert. He was treated again with methods such as chasing wind, clearing away heat and calming convulsions, but he became addicted to breast milk, his body was like burning coals, his limbs were cold due to spontaneous sweating, he was coughing and wheezing, his phlegm was dripping, and he was dying. After further examination, the patient's fingerprints were blue and black, the face and lips were all blue, and the tongue was white and greasy. This is caused by incorrect treatment of wind and cold, which causes evil to enter the yin component. The yang cannot overcome the yin, and the deficient yang floats to the outside. The method should be to support the yang and drive away the cold. 20 grams of Fujiang, 6 grams of Paojiang, 6 grams of Pinellia ternata, 2 grams of Asarum, 2 grams of raw mochi, 10 grams of Poria, and 3 grams of licorice. Feed and take it frequently. After one dose is used up, you will sweat, half of the fever will subside, you will no longer have twitching, wheezing and coughing, and you will be able to suck milk. After another dose, the disease will be cured by seven or eight. After removing the numbness and pungency, and taking two doses, all symptoms were eliminated.",小儿慢惊风:"Slow convulsion in children","小儿慢惊风 张某之次子，生甫一岁，住四川省会理县鹿厂街":"Infantile Slow Convulsion Zhang's second son, just one year old, lives in Luchang Street, Huili County, Sichuan Province","小儿慢惊风 张某之次子，生甫一岁，住四川省会理县鹿厂街。1914年 3月，患小儿惊风证,病颇危笃,三日来抽搐不已。余诊视之， 指纹青黑透达三关，脉沉细而弱，舌苔白滑，面唇青黯，闭目 沉迷不省，时而手足拘挛抽掣，乳食不进，夜间发热，大便泄 泻绿色稀粪。询及病由，其母述及，患儿始因受寒感冒起病， 初有发热咳嗽，大便溏泻。某医以清热解表药二剂，服后白昼 身热见退,夜晚又复发热，咳、泻未止。继又拟消食清热药二 剂，服后病不减，忽而风动抽搐。该医以为肝经风热,又以平 肝驱风镇惊药二剂，病情反见日趋沉重而成是状。时病已十 余日，按脉证病情诊察，余思寻之，良由小儿气血未充，脏腑 娇嫩，不耐克伐。风寒初起,只须轻宣透表，其病当愈。尔乃误 以清热之剂，又复以消食、平肝、驱风等法，元阳受损，正不胜 邪,遂致寒痰内壅而成三阴虚寒之慢惊风证。病势已危重，若 辞不治,实非我医者应尽之责，力主逐寒荡惊汤挽救之。 上肉桂6克（研末，泡水兑入），公丁香3克，炮姜10克， 白胡椒3克（捣），灶心土 130克（烧红淬水，澄清后以水煎 药）。 上方喂服二次，稍顷，呕吐涎痰一小盏，风状略减，抽搐 较轻，两眼已睁，目珠已能转动寻视。再喂药一次，又吐涎痰 盏许，风状已定,抽搐不再发作，咳嗽亦平，夜晚已不再发热。 患儿之父母见病已恢复,甚为欣慰,但见其子体质羸弱,认为 宜培补脾胃，自拟理中地黄汤一剂喂服。殊料服后移时，风动 抽搐又起。余往视之，询问缘由，方知患儿大病虽有转机，然 寒痰阴邪尚未逐尽，滋补过早，固必增邪，且有碍于阴邪外 祛，寒痰内阻，遂致慢风复作。此时，病家始知误施补剂亦有 弊端。余仍以逐寒荡惊汤并加附片15克，喂服后又吐涎痰盏 许,畅泻酱黑色稀便二次，抽搐平息，且能吮乳，并闻啼声。照 原方去胡椒、公丁香，加砂仁6克、甘草6克，附片增至30 克，煎汤频频喂服。二剂尽，诸证痊愈。":"Infantile convulsion Zhang's second son, just one year old, lives in Luchang Street, Huili County, Sichuan Province. In March 1914, he suffered from infantile convulsions and became critically ill. He had been having convulsions for three days. Upon examination, the patient's fingerprints were blue and black, reaching all three levels, the pulse was thin and weak, the tongue coating was white and slippery, the face and lips were blue and dark, the patient was unconscious with his eyes closed, and sometimes cramps and cramps in the hands and feet, inability to feed and feed, fever at night, and loose green stools. When asked about the cause of the disease, his mother mentioned that the child first fell ill due to a cold, with fever, cough, and loose stools. A certain doctor gave two doses of heat-clearing and superficial relieving medicine. After taking it, the body heat subsided during the day, but the fever recurred at night, and the cough and diarrhea did not stop. After taking two doses of digestion and heat-clearing medicine, the illness did not subside after taking it, and he suddenly developed wind and convulsions. The doctor believed that the liver meridian was wind-heat, so he prescribed two doses of medicine to soothe the liver, dispel wind, and calm convulsions. However, the condition became increasingly severe and became the same as before. I had been ill for more than ten days. I checked the pulse syndrome and looked for it. The good reason was that the child's qi and blood were not sufficient, and the internal organs were delicate and could not be cut. When wind-cold first appears, just spread it lightly on the surface and the disease will be cured. If you mistakenly use heat-clearing agents, and then use methods such as digestion, calming the liver, and driving wind, the primordial yang will be damaged, and the righteousness will not be able to overcome the evil, causing cold phlegm to accumulate in the body, resulting in chronic convulsions with three yin deficiency and cold. The condition is critical, and if he refuses to be cured, it is really not my duty as a doctor. I strongly recommend Zhuhan Dangjing Decoction to save him. Add 6 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 3 grams of cloves, 10 grams of ginger, 3 grams of white pepper (pounded), and 130 grams of Zaoxin soil (boil red and quench the water, clarify and decoct in water). After feeding the patient twice, he vomited and vomited a small amount of saliva and phlegm for a while, the wind was slightly reduced, the convulsions were mild, the eyes were opened, and the eyes were able to move and look. After another dose of medicine, he spitted out a few sputum again, the wind pattern had settled down, the convulsions no longer occurred, the cough subsided, and he no longer had fever at night. The patient's parents were very pleased to see that the child had recovered from the illness. However, seeing that their son was in a weak constitution, they thought it was appropriate to strengthen the spleen and stomach and fed him a dose of Zhongdihuang Decoction. When the special material was moved back, the wind stirred and the convulsions started again. I looked at it and asked about the reason, and found out that although the serious illness of the child had improved, the cold phlegm and yin evil had not been eliminated, and nourishing it too early would definitely increase the evil, and it would hinder the external removal of yin evil and cause the cold phlegm to block the internal obstruction, causing the recurrence of chronic wind. At this time, patients began to realize that misadministering supplements also has disadvantages. I still took Zhuhan Dangjing Decoction and added 15 grams of tablets. After taking it, I spit a lot of phlegm and had black and loose stools for two times. The convulsions subsided, and I was able to suck breasts and hear the cry. Follow the original recipe and remove the pepper and cloves, add 6 grams of amomum villosum, 6 grams of licorice, and increase the amount of fenugreek to 30 grams. Decoction and feed frequently. After the two doses are used up, all symptoms will be cured.",小儿推拿:"Pediatric Massage",小儿斜颈:"Torticollis in children",小儿时疫痢:"childhood dysentery","小儿时疫痢 （小儿志贺杆菌性痢疾） 张小妹，女，一岁，于1961…":"Childhood dysentery (Shigella dysentery in children) Zhang Xiaomei, female, one year old, born in 1961…","小儿时疫痢 （小儿志贺杆菌性痢疾） 张小妹，女，一岁，于1961年8月19日因发热一日，腹 泻十多次,粪便带红白黏液,经昆明市红十字会医院诊断为 “菌痢”收住儿科病房治疗。 据入院病历所载,患儿发育较差，营养中等,未出牙，前因 未闭合,颈部淋巴可触及。咽喉、心、肺及腹部未见异常,体温 39℃（肛表）。8月20日血象，红细胞3.4x10Q/L（340万/毫米3）， 血红蛋白66%,白细胞总数5.3xl0^9L（5 300/毫米3）,中性68%, 淋巴27%,单核3%。8月22日大便培养报告检出志贺痢疾杆 菌。8月23日起用氯霉素治疗。8月24日加用多黏菌素，并内服清热解毒止痢中药。但腹泻不止，体温仍在39.5℃左右（肛 表）。8月28日血象，红细胞3.15x10^12/L（315万/毫米³）血红蛋 白60%,白细胞总数13.6xl0^9/L（3 600/毫米³）中性68%,淋巴 30%,单核2%。病孩住院十日，经用多种抗菌药物及中药治疗, 仍未见好转，于8月29日邀余会诊。 当日下午诊视，见患儿卧床，正在输液，面赤身热，体温 40.5℃（肛表）,衰弱无神，唇口干燥，眼瞠凹陷。但见其母频频 喂饮，时闻啼声，气息低弱，不思乳食，自汗出，稍动则易惊 怖。询及今日大便已泻十余次,每次便量不多，红白黏液混 杂，小便短少。指纹色赤而浮，舌苔粉白。此系内伤饮食，复感 表邪,表证不解,邪气又陷入阳明，遂成太阳阳明合病下痢之 证。如过早施用清热止痢及苦寒泻下之剂,易伤里气,若表邪 深陷,则痢无止期。此证已属二阳合病，当以解表兼以升提陷 入阳明经邪之法治之。建议暂停前面所用中西药物，拟桂葛 汤一剂。 桂枝10克，葛根10克,杭白芍6克，生姜2小片，小枣3 枚，甘草3克。 当晚喂服二次，至夜有微汗出，身热稍退，体温39℃（肛 表）。次晨又煎服第三次，日内照方服完二剂。每次喂药后片 刻，均有热汗徐徐外出。于30日晚体温已降至37.8℃（肛 表），大便终日未见泻利。 9月1日复诊。体温37.2℃（肛表），大便解二次，已为粪 质，色黄而滴薄，未见脓血状物。据其母所诉,患儿热退之后 已不再发惊，能安静熟睡，稍进乳食。此时虽然发热已退，腹 泻已止，但见面色转淡，嗜卧无神，指纹色淡仅隐隐可见，口 唇回润，干渴之状已不见，舌苔薄白转润。此系病邪已退，中 焦脾胃虚弱，须当调补中气，健运脾胃以善其后，拟归芍理中汤加味治之。 潞党参10克，炮姜6克，肉桂5克，当归6克，杭白芍5 克，白术6克，砂仁3克，公丁香7粒，甘草3克。 上方连服三剂，9月4日诊视，患儿于服药后第二、三两 日，均未解大便，一切情况尚好，今日则大便二次，色黄微 滴，体温已平，精神转佳，乳食如常。9月1日和5日曾各取 大便标本做病菌培养，均未检出痢疾杆菌，遂调理数日，痊 愈出院。":`Childhood Epidemic Dysentery (Pediatric Shigella Dysentery) Zhang Xiaomei, female, one year old, suffered from fever for one day on August 19, 1961, and had diarrhea more than ten times with red and white mucus in her feces. She was diagnosed as "bacillary dysentery" by Kunming Red Cross Hospital and was admitted to the pediatric ward for treatment. According to the admission medical records, the child had poor development, moderate nutrition, no teeth, antecedents that were not closed, and cervical lymph nodes were palpable. There were no abnormalities in the throat, heart, lungs and abdomen, and the body temperature was 39°C (anal surface). The blood picture on August 20th showed red blood cells 3.4x10Q/L (3.4 million/mm3), hemoglobin 66%, total white blood cells 5.3x10^9L (5 300/mm3), neutral 68%, lymph 27%, and mononuclear 3%. On August 22, the stool culture report detected Shigella dysentery. Treatment with chloramphenicol started on August 23. On August 24, polymyxin was added, and traditional Chinese medicine for clearing away heat, detoxifying and stopping dysentery was taken orally. But the diarrhea didn't stop and the body temperature was still around 39.5℃ (anal surface). The blood picture on August 28 showed red blood cells 3.15x10^12/L (3.15 million/mm³), hemoglobin 60%, total white blood cells 13.6x10^9/L (3 600/mm³) neutral 68%, lymph 30%, and mononuclear 2%. The sick child was hospitalized for ten days and was treated with a variety of antibacterial drugs and traditional Chinese medicine, but still did not improve. He was invited for consultation on August 29. During the examination in the afternoon of that day, the patient was seen lying in bed and undergoing infusion. His face was naked and his body was hot. His body temperature was 40.5°C (anal surface). He was weak and listless, with dry lips and mouth, and sunken eyes. However, he saw his mother frequently feeding him and drinking, hearing cries from time to time, his breath was weak, he did not want to feed, he sweated spontaneously, and he was easily frightened when he moved the slightest. I asked about having diarrhea more than ten times today. Each time the stool was not large, with mixed red and white mucus, and the urine was short. The fingerprints are red and floating, and the tongue coating is pink and white. This is caused by internal injury due to diet, re-infection of external evils, unexplained external syndromes, and evil spirits trapped in Yangming, thus forming a syndrome of diarrhea caused by Taiyang-Yangming syndrome. If the medicines used to clear away heat and stop dysentery and those with bitter cold and diarrhea are used too early, it is easy to damage the internal Qi. If the external evils are deeply trapped, the dysentery will last indefinitely. This syndrome is already a syndrome of two Yang meridian syndromes, and should be treated with the method of relieving the superficial symptoms and promoting Yangming meridian evil. It is recommended to suspend the Chinese and Western medicines used previously and take a dose of Guige Decoction. 10 grams of cassia twig, 10 grams of kudzu root, 6 grams of white peony root, 2 small slices of ginger, 3 jujubes, and 3 grams of licorice. The patient was fed twice that night. By the end of the night, he was sweating slightly, and the body heat subsided slightly, with a body temperature of 39°C (anal surface). The next morning, decoct the medicine and take it for a third time, and finish the second dose within the same day. Moments after each dose of medicine, hot sweating would occur slowly. On the evening of the 30th, the body temperature had dropped to 37.8°C (anal surface), and there was no diarrhea in the stool all day long. Follow-up visit on September 1st. The body temperature was 37.2°C (anal surface). The stool was resolved twice and was of fecal matter. The color was yellow and the drops were thin, with no pus or blood. According to his mother's complaint, the child no longer frightened after the fever subsided, and was able to sleep peacefully and take a small amount of milk. At this time, although the fever has subsided and the diarrhea has stopped, the complexion of the face has turned pale, the patient is sleepy and sleepy, the fingerprints are pale and only faintly visible, the lips are moisturized, the signs of thirst have disappeared, and the tongue coating is thin and white and has become moist. This is because the pathogenic factors have subsided and the spleen and stomach are weak in the middle burner. It is necessary to regulate and replenish the middle qi and strengthen the spleen and stomach to improve the aftermath. It is planned to be cured by adding Shao Lizhong Decoction. 10 grams of Codonopsis pilosula, 6 grams of ginger, 5 grams of cinnamon, 6 grams of angelica root, 5 grams of white peony root, 6 grams of Atractylodes macrocephala, 3 grams of amomum villosum, 7 cloves, and 3 grams of licorice. Shang Shang took three doses in a row, and was examined on September 4th. On the second and third days after taking the medicine, the child had no bowel movements, and everything was in good condition. Today, he had two stools, which were yellow in color and had droplets. His body temperature has calmed down, his energy has improved, and his milk and food intake are as usual. Stool samples were taken for bacterial culture on September 1st and 5th, but no Shigella dysenteriae was detected, so he was nursed back to health for several days and was discharged after recovery.`,"小儿湿热痢 （三阳合病下痢） 李某，女孩，一岁半，1964年4月8日来诊（中医学院附 属医院门诊号136651）。患儿患麻疹免后，大便下利红白已十 余日，发热39.8℃,寒热交作,面赤气促,多啼哭,夜不入睡，口 渴而喜饮。每日大便泻十七、八次，量不多，色绿而赤白黏液 间杂，欲便时啼闹不休（腹中痛），哭甚方解，解便不畅（里急 后重,滞下不爽）,小便短赤,脉细数,指纹青紫而浮，苔白腻， 曾服止痢西药数日未见愈。此乃三阳合病下痢之证,拟方。 桂枝15克，葛根10克，柴胡6克，黄芩3克，黄连3克， 榔片3克，杭白芍10克，小枣5枚，生姜2片，甘草7克。 昨日一剂连续煎服六次，得微汗。今日已热退身凉，大便 三次，色黄半干，稍带黏液，赤色已不见，小便转清，口已不 渴，能食软饭。脉转缓，指纹青紫已退，色淡而细，苔薄白质红 润。此痢证已止，尚需调理，以桂枝汤加味一剂而收功。 苏条参6克，杭白芍6克，法半夏6克，砂仁3克，桂枝 10克，小枣5枚，生姜2片，甘草5克。":"Damp-heat dysentery in children (dysentery caused by three yang syndromes) Li, a girl, one and a half years old, came to the clinic on April 8, 1964 (outpatient clinic number of the Affiliated Hospital of the College of Traditional Chinese Medicine: 136651). After the child contracted measles, he had constipated red and white stools for more than ten days. He had a fever of 39.8°C, alternating cold and heat, flushed face, shortness of breath, crying a lot, not sleeping at night, thirsty and fond of drinking. Seventeen or eight times a day, the stool was small, with green and reddish-white mucus interspersed. He cried endlessly when he wanted to defecate (abdominal pain), cried a lot before he could relieve himself, and had difficulty in defecation (tenesmus, lag, and discomfort). His urine was short and red, his pulse was thready and rapid, his fingerprints were blue and purple, and his fur was greasy. He had taken Western medicine to stop dysentery for several days, but it was not cured. This is the syndrome of dysentery caused by the combination of three yangs, and the prescription is formulated. 15 grams of cinnamon twig, 10 grams of kudzu root, 6 grams of bupleurum, 3 grams of skullcap, 3 grams of coptis, 3 grams of palm slices, 10 grams of white peony root, 5 jujubes, 2 slices of ginger, and 7 grams of licorice. Yesterday I took one dose of decoction for six times in a row and I felt slightly sweaty. Today, the fever has subsided and the body is cold. I have three bowel movements. The color is yellow and semi-dry, with a little mucus. The red color is gone. The urine has become clear. I am no longer thirsty and can eat soft rice. The pulse is slow, the cyanosis of the fingerprints has faded, the color is light and thin, the fur is thin, white and red. The dysentery syndrome has stopped and still needs to be treated. One dose of Guizhi Decoction will be effective. 6 grams of Su Tiao Shen, 6 grams of white peony root, 6 grams of Pinellia ternata, 3 grams of Amomum villosum, 10 grams of Guizhi, 5 jujubes, 2 slices of ginger, and 5 grams of licorice.","小儿湿热痢 （三阳合病下痢） 李某，女孩，一岁半，1964年4月…":"Damp-heat dysentery in children (dysentery caused by three yang diseases) Li, a girl, one and a half years old, April 1964…","小儿湿热痢（三阳合病下痢）案 李某，女孩，1岁半":"Case of damp-heat dysentery in children (dysentery caused by three yang syndromes) Li, girl, 1 and a half years old","小儿湿热痢（三阳合病下痢）案\\n李某，女孩，1岁半。1964年4月8日来诊。患麻疹免后，大便下利红白已十余日，发热39.8℃，寒热交作.面赤气促，多啼哭，夜不入睡，口渴而喜饮。每日大便泻十七八次，量不多，色绿而赤白黏液间杂，欲便时啼闹不休（腹中痛），哭甚方解，解便不畅（里急后重，滞下不爽）；小便短赤，脉细数，指纹青紫而浮，苔白腻，曾服止痢西药数日未见愈，此乃三阳合病下痢之证，拟方：\\n桂枝15g，葛根10g，柴胡6g，黄芩3g，黄连3g，榔片3g，杭芍10g，小枣5枚，生姜2片，甘草7g。\\n昨日1剂连续煎服6次，得微汗。今日已热退身凉，大便3次，色黄半干，稍带黏液，赤色已不见；小便转清，口已不渴，能食软饭。脉转缓，指纹青紫已退，色淡而细；苔薄白质红润。此痢证已止，尚须调理，以桂枝汤加味一剂而收功。\\n苏条参6g，杭芍6g，法夏6g，砂仁3g，桂枝10g，小枣5枚，生姜2片，甘草5g。\\n按：此证三阳合病下痢，吴氏化裁桂葛汤、柴胡剂于一炉，用药娴熟，充分表明吴氏治疗痢疾，经验丰富。":"Case of damp-heat dysentery in children (dysentery caused by three Yang syndromes)\\nLi, a girl, 1 and a half years old. Came for treatment on April 8, 1964. After suffering from measles, the stool has been red and white for more than ten days, and the fever is 39.8°C, with alternating cold and heat. The face is red, shortness of breath, crying a lot, not sleeping at night, thirsty and fond of drinking. 17 or 18 times a day, small amount of stools, with green and reddish white mucus interspersed, constant crying (abdominal pain) when trying to defecate, heavy crying, and difficulty in defecation (tenesmus, lag and discomfort); short red urine, thready and rapid pulse, bluish-purple and floating fingerprints, white and greasy coating, and After taking western medicine to stop dysentery for a few days, the patient has not recovered. This is a symptom of dysentery due to the combination of three yangs. The recipe is as follows:\\nCinnamomum twig 15g, Pueraria lobata 10g, Bupleurum 6g, Scutellaria baicalensis 3g, Coptidis 3g, 3g Fructus Scutellariae, 10g peony root, 5 jujubes, 2 slices of ginger, and 7g licorice. \\nYesterday, I took 1 dose of decoction for 6 consecutive times and I felt slightly sweaty. Today, the fever has subsided and the body is cool. I have 3 bowel movements, which are yellow and semi-dry, with a little mucus, and the red color is gone. My urine has become clear, I am no longer thirsty, and I can eat soft rice. The pulse is slow, the cyanosis of the fingerprints has faded, the color is light and thin, the fur is thin, white and ruddy. The dysentery syndrome has stopped and still needs to be treated. One dose of Guizhi Decoction will be effective. \\nSu Tiao Shen 6g, Hangshao 6g, Farxia 6g, Amomum villosum 3g, Guizhi 10g, 5 jujubes, 2 slices of ginger, 5g licorice. \\nNote: This syndrome is caused by the combination of three yangs and causes dysentery. Wu's combination of Guige decoction and Bupleurum root in one pot, and his skill in using the medicine fully shows that Wu has rich experience in treating dysentery.",小儿热极生风证:"Wind syndrome caused by extreme heat in children",小儿目赤肿痛:"Red, swollen and painful eyes in children","小儿目赤肿痛 1923年腊月，朱某之次子，诞生十余日，忽目赤而肿…":"Red, swollen and painful eyes in children In the twelfth lunar month of 1923, more than ten days after the birth of Zhu’s second son, his eyes suddenly became red and swollen…","小儿目赤肿痛 1923年腊月，朱某之次子，诞生十余日，忽目赤而肿，乳 后即吐，大便色绿，夜啼不休。舌白，指纹含青。因儿母素体虚 寒，小儿先天禀赋不足，脾阳虚弱，健运失司，无以制水，里寒 夹肝气横逆而侮脾，元阳不潜，附肝而上，冲及于目，此虚阳 浮越所致。法宜回阳收纳为要,拟附子甘草汤加生姜治之。 附片10克，甘草3克，生姜2小片。 服一剂，啼声止，二剂则目肿渐消，大便转黄，如此四 剂痊愈。按：世习一见目病赤肿，功辄言火，其实不尽如此。眼科病证，名目繁多，括其要，总不离乎外感、内伤两法以判之。不论内外感伤，若见目赤肿痛，雾障羞明，其证各有虚实寒热之不同，必须按六经、八纲之理明辨施治，不可固守一法以邀幸中。余非专于目疾者，然其治法要领，经旨互通矣。":"Red, swollen and painful eyes in children In the twelfth lunar month of 1923, more than ten days after the birth of Zhu's second son, his eyes suddenly became red and swollen, he vomited immediately after breastfeeding, his stools were green, and he cried endlessly at night. The tongue is white and the fingerprints are blue. Because the mother's body is weak and cold, the child's innate endowment is insufficient, the spleen yang is weak, the movement is lost, and the water is unable to be controlled. The cold inside causes the liver qi to go against the spleen and insult the spleen. The main method is to restore Yang and absorb it, so Aconite Licorice Decoction plus ginger is proposed to treat it. 10 grams of Fu Fian, 3 grams of licorice, and 2 small slices of ginger. After taking one dose, the crying stopped. After two doses, the eye swelling gradually disappeared and the stool turned yellow. After four doses, the patient was cured. Note: The world is accustomed to talking about redness and swelling of eye diseases, but this is not the case. There are many types of ophthalmic diseases and syndromes, including the main ones, which can always be diagnosed by external factors and internal injuries. Regardless of the internal and external symptoms, if you see redness, swelling and pain in the eyes, blurred vision, or mist, the syndromes are different in terms of deficiency, excess, cold and heat, and treatment must be based on the principles of the Six Meridians and the Eight Cardinal Guides, and you cannot stick to one method to get lucky. I am not specialized in eye diseases, but the essentials of their treatments are interoperable with each other.",小儿脾胃病:"Spleen and stomach disease in children",少阴咽痛:"Shaoyin sore throat","少阴咽痛 王某，女，成年":"Shaoyin sore throat Wang, female, adult","少阴咽痛 王某，女，成年。始因受寒起病，恶寒，咽痛不适,误服苦 寒清热养阴之剂后转成危证。余诊视之,患者头痛如劈，恶寒 发热，体痛。咽痛,水浆不能下咽，痰涎涌甚，咽部红肿起白泡而破烂。舌苔白滑，脉沉细而兼紧象。不渴饮，此系寒入少阴， 误用苦寒清热，致使阴邪夹寒水上逼,虚火上浮而成是状。取 扶阳祛寒,引阳归舍之法，以加味麻黄细辛附子汤治之。 附片40克，干姜26克，北细辛6克，麻黄5克，上肉桂6 克，（研末，泡水兑入），甘草6克。 服一剂后寒热始退，咽部肿痛减去其半,再剂则痛去七、 八,三剂尽,诸证霍然而愈。按：少阴受寒误用苦寒清热养阴之剂，无异于雪上加霜。《内经》云：“足少阴之脉……循喉咙，挟舌本。”风寒闭束少阴经络不通，虚火上浮冲于咽喉而肿痛者，宜用麻黄细辛附子汤治之。方中附子能扶阳驱寒，麻黄开发腠理，解散表寒，得细辛之辛温，直入少阴以温散经脉寒邪，并能协同附子纳阳归肾，邪去正安，少阴咽痛自然获愈。":'Shaoyin sore throat Wang, female, adult. The disease started due to cold, aversion to cold, sore throat and discomfort, and turned into a critical syndrome after accidentally taking a bitter cold-clearing, heat-nourishing, yin-nourishing agent. Upon further examination, the patient had a headache, aversion to cold, fever, and body pain. Sore throat, inability to swallow water and slurry, heavy phlegm and saliva, pharynx red and swollen with white blisters and tatters. The tongue coating is white and slippery, and the pulse is deep, thin and tight. If you are not thirsty to drink, this is caused by cold entering Shaoyin, and misusing bitter cold to clear away heat, causing yin evil and cold water to push up, and the deficiency fire rises to form this condition. Take the method of supporting yang, dispelling cold, and inducing yang to return to the body, and treat it with the flavored Ephedra Asarum and Fuzi Decoction. 40 grams of Futian, 26 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of Asarum, 5 grams of ephedra, 6 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), and 6 grams of licorice. After taking one dose, the cold and heat begin to subside, and the swelling and pain in the throat are reduced by half. After another dose, the pain disappears for seven or eight times. After three doses, all symptoms will be cured. Note: When Shaoyin catches cold, misuse of bitter cold medicine to clear away heat and nourish yin is just adding insult to injury. "Nei Jing" says: "The pulse of Foot Shaoyin... runs along the throat and holds the base of the tongue." If the Shaoyin meridians are blocked due to wind-cold, and the deficient fire rises and rushes into the throat, causing swelling and pain, it should be treated with Ephedra and Xixin Fuzi Decoction. Aconite in the prescription can support yang and expel cold, ephedra develops interstitial muscles, dissolves superficial cold, and obtains the pungent warmth of asarum, and directly enters Shaoyin to warm the meridians to dissipate cold evil. It can also cooperate with aconite to absorb yang and return it to the kidney. The evil is removed and the sore throat in Shaoyin is naturally cured.',少阴头痛:"Shaoyin headache","少阴头痛 邓某，男，成年":"Shaoyin headache Deng, male, adult","少阴头痛 邓某，男，成年。初因受寒而起病，误服辛凉之剂，未效。 病经十余日，头痛如斧劈,势不可忍，午后则恶寒体痛，脉沉 弱无力，舌苔白滑而不渴饮。此乃寒客少阴，阻碍清阳不升， 复以辛凉耗其真阳，正虚阳弱，阴寒遏滞经脉。头为诸阳之 会，今为阴邪上僭攻于头，阳不足以运行，邪正相争，遂成是 状。以辅正除邪之法,加味麻黄细辛附子汤治之。 附片100克，干姜36克，甘草6克，麻黄10克，细辛5 克，羌活10克。 服一剂,痛减其半,再剂霍然而愈。按：少阴头痛，依本法治之其效如响。方内寓一四逆汤，能温扶阳气上交于头，麻黄、羌活、细辛祛客寒达于太阳，由膀胱而化，此乃温经散寒，辅正除邪之实效矣。六经病皆有头痛，遵仲景六经辨证方法施治，均能获效，出方有绳，庶不至误。":"Shaoyin headache Deng, male, adult. The disease first started due to cold, and I mistakenly took pungent and cool medicine, but it didn't work. The disease lasted for more than ten days, and the headache was like an axe, unbearable. In the afternoon, he felt aversion to cold and body aches, his pulse was weak and weak, his tongue coating was white and slippery, and he was not thirsty to drink. This is caused by the cold guest Shaoyin, which blocks the clear Yang from rising, and consumes its true Yang with pungent coolness. The positive is deficient and the Yang is weak, and the cold Yin stagnates the meridians. The head is the meeting point of all the yangs, but now the yin and evil superiors are attacking the head. The yang is not enough to move, and the evil and the righteous are fighting each other, so this is the case. Treat it with the method of supplementing the righteousness and removing the evil, and add the flavored Ephedra Asarum and Fuzi Decoction. 100 grams of Futian, 36 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of licorice, 10 grams of ephedra, 5 grams of asarum, and 10 grams of Qianhuo. Take one dose and the pain will be reduced by half, and another dose will make the pain disappear. Note: Shaoyin headache can be treated according to this method and the effect will be as good as the sound. The formula contains Yisini Decoction, which can warm and support Yang Qi in the head. Ephedra, Qianghuo, and Asarum dispel the cold and reach the sun, and are transformed by the bladder. This is the effective effect of warming the meridians and dispersing cold, assisting the righteousness and eliminating evil. Six-meridian diseases all have headaches. If you follow Zhongjing's six-meridian syndrome differentiation method to treat them, you can get effective results.",少阴热化证:"Shaoyin heat syndrome",少阴病篇:"Shaoyin Disease","少阴阳虚寒化证与四逆、真武类方运用。":"The syndrome of Shaoyin and Yang deficiency and cold transformation is treated with Sini and Zhenwu prescriptions.",少阴阴极似阳证:"Shaoyin Yin pole resembles Yang syndrome",少阴阴盛格阳证:"Shaoyin yin excess and yang syndrome","尹某，25岁":"Yin, 25 years old","尹某，25岁。产后6日，因右侧乳房患急性乳腺炎经用青霉素等针药治疗，病情不减。改延中医诊治，投以清热解毒之剂，外敷清热消肿软膏。诊治10余日，寒热不退，乳房红肿疼痛反而日渐增剧，遂延吴氏诊视。刻诊：发热而恶寒，体温37.4℃，午后则升高至39℃左右。头疼，全身酸痛。右乳房红肿灼热而硬，乳汁不通，痛彻腋下，呻吟不止。日不思饮食，夜不能入眠，精神疲惫，欲寐无神。脉沉细而紧，舌质淡而含青，苔白厚腻。辨为产后气血俱虚，感受风寒，经脉受阻，气血凝滞。又误服苦寒之剂，伤正而助邪，遂致乳痈加剧。法当扶正驱邪，温经散寒，活络通乳。方用麻黃附子细辛汤加味：附片30g，麻黄9g，细辛5g，桂枝15g，川芎9g，通草6g，王不留行9g，炙香附9g，生姜15g，甘草6g。\\n连服上方2次，温覆而卧，遍身漐漐汗出，入夜能安静熟寐，次晨已热退身凉，头身疼痛已愈，乳房红肿热痛减半，稍进稀粥与牛奶，脉已和缓。舌青已退而转淡红，苔薄白根部尚腻。继以扶阳温化之茯苓桂枝汤加味调之。乳房硬结全部消散，乳汁已通，眠食转佳，照常哺乳。\\n按：此证乳房红肿疼痛，发热，极易判为热证，但是“投以清热解毒之剂，外敷清热消肿软膏，诊治10余日，寒热不退”，可知并不支持热毒判断；而从恶寒，头疼，全身酸痛来看，当有表证；再从精神疲惫，欲寐无神，脉沉细而紧，舌质淡而含青来看，显系阳虚之兆。外见表邪，内已阳虚，故投麻黄附子细辛汤而收效，药证相符，自然取效。整个治疗未用一味凉药，识证之准，用药之确，确显功力。":`Yin, 25 years old. On the 6th day after delivery, she suffered from acute mastitis in the right breast and was treated with penicillin and other injections, but her condition did not abate. Diagnosis and treatment with traditional Chinese medicine was performed, with heat-clearing and detoxifying agents and external application of heat-clearing and swelling ointment. After more than 10 days of diagnosis and treatment, the cold and heat did not subside, but the redness, swelling and pain in the breast became increasingly severe, so Wu's diagnosis was postponed. Immediate diagnosis: Fever with aversion to chills, body temperature 37.4°C, rising to around 39°C in the afternoon. Headache, body aches. The right breast was red, swollen, hot and hard, the milk was blocked, the pain in the armpit was painful, and she kept moaning. I don't think about food during the day, I can't sleep at night, I'm mentally exhausted, and I feel sleepy. The pulse is deep, thin and tight, the tongue is light and green, and the coating is white and thick. It is diagnosed as postpartum deficiency of Qi and blood, feeling of wind and cold, obstruction of meridians, and stagnation of Qi and blood. In addition, taking bitter and cold medicine by mistake can damage the righteousness and help the evil, thus aggravating the mastitis. The method should strengthen the body and expel evil spirits, warm the meridians and dispel cold, activate the meridians and clear the breasts. Add the following flavorings: Ephedra, Aconite and Asarum Decoction: 30g of Aconite, 9g of Ephedra, 5g of Asarum, 15g of Guizhi, 9g of Chuanxiong, 6g of Tongcao, 9g of Wangbuliuxing, 9g of Roper Cyperus, 15g of ginger, and 6g of licorice. \\nTake the above medicine for 2 times. When you lie down with a warm blanket, you will sweat all over your body. You can fall asleep quietly and soundly at night. The heat has subsided and the body is cool in the next morning. The pain in your head and body has healed. The redness, swelling, heat and pain in your breasts have been reduced by half. Add a little gruel and milk, and your pulse has softened. The green tongue has receded and turned light red, and the tongue coating is thin and white, and the roots are still greasy. Then add Fuyang-warmed Poria and Guizhi Decoction to taste. All the induration in the breasts has dissipated, milk flow has been released, sleeping and eating are getting better, and breastfeeding can be carried out as usual. \\nNote: This syndrome is characterized by red, swollen and painful breasts and fever, which can easily be diagnosed as a heat syndrome. However, "administration of heat-clearing and detoxifying agents, external application of heat-clearing and swelling ointment, and diagnosis and treatment for more than 10 days, but the cold and heat persist" does not support the judgment of heat and poison. From the aversion to cold, headache, and body aches, there are superficial symptoms; and from the mental fatigue, sleepiness, heavy and tight pulse, and the pale and green tongue, it is a sign of yang deficiency. External evils are seen on the outside, and internal yang is already deficient, so the patient takes Ephedra, Fuzi and Xixin Decoction and the effect is achieved. The medicine matches the syndrome and takes effect naturally. The whole treatment did not use any cold medicine. The identification of symptoms was accurate and the medicine was used accurately, which really showed the power of the medicine.`,"居处宜温暖避风，饮食宜清淡流质，忌生冷油腻闭塞腠理，尤忌骤减衣被强令出汗，致疹毒不得透发而内陷。":"The living place should be warm and sheltered from wind, and the diet should be light and liquid. Avoid raw, cold, greasy, and occlusive interstitial joints. Avoid sudden loss of clothes and quilts to force sweating, which may cause the rash to not penetrate and become indented.","山草部收载滇南高山所产药物八十余种，以滇重楼、滇黄精、滇贝母为大宗。兰茂论药首重道地，谓滇省山高雾重，得天地阴寒之气，故山草多具清润之性，非他处所产可比。":"The Department of Mountains and Herbs contains more than 80 kinds of medicines produced in the mountains of southern Yunnan, among which Dian Zhonglou, Dian Polygonatum, and Dian Fritillaria are the major ones. Lan Mao's theory of medicine is based on the principle that the mountains in Yunnan Province are high in mountains and foggy, which captures the cold and cold air from the heaven and earth. Therefore, many mountain grasses have a clear and moist property that cannot be compared with those produced in other places.",崩漏:"metrorrhagia",带下:"Take it off","带下案辨色质气味，分寒湿湿热论治，健脾升阳为常法，而用药轻灵，不事滋腻。":"Take the case to distinguish the color, quality and smell, distinguish cold, dampness, dampness and heat for treatment. It is a common method to strengthen the spleen and raise yang, and the medicine is used lightly and does not cause greasiness.",年:"year",年代:"era","张某，42岁，昆明市人":"Zhang, 42 years old, from Kunming City","张某，42岁，昆明市人。某日返家途中，时值阴雨，感冒寒风。初起即身热恶寒，头疼体痛，沉迷嗜卧（即少阴但欲寐之病情也），兼见渴喜热饮不多。脉沉细而兼紧像，舌苔白滑，质夹青紫。由肾气素亏，坎内阳弱，无力卫外固表以抵抗客邪，寒风乘虚直入少阴，阻塞真阳运行之机而成是状。以麻辛附子汤温经解表主之：黑附片36g（先煮透），麻黄9g（先煮数沸去沫），北细辛6g，桂尖12g。 \\n1剂即汗，身热已退，惟觉头晕咳嗽，神怯而已。然表邪虽 \\n解，肺寒尚未肃清，阳气尚虚，以四逆合二陈加辛、味，扶阳温寒王之。\\n黑附片45g，筠姜24g，生甘草9g，广陈皮9g，法夏12g，茯苓12g，北细辛4g，五味子1.2g0\\n开水先煮附片2小时再入余药煎服。1剂尽，咳嗽立止，食量增加，精神恢复，病遂痊愈。（《医药简述》）\\n按：本案肾气素亏，少阴感寒而致太少两感局面。方用麻辛附子汤，另加桂尖增强开表之力；取汗退热之后，以四逆汤合二陈汤再加细辛、五味，温肺化痰，因表证已解，故去掉麻黄；虽用五味子与筠姜、细辛成仲景化痰定式（姜辛味），因防其敛邪，仅用五味子1.2g，显出医律之细。":`Zhang, 42 years old, from Kunming City. On the way home one day, it was rainy and I caught a cold and a cold wind. At the beginning, the symptoms include body heat, aversion to cold, headache and body aches, addiction to sleeping (that is, the condition of Shaoyin but wanting to sleep), and thirst and not much hot drinks. The pulse is deep, thin and tight, the tongue coating is white and slippery, and the texture is bluish-purple. This condition is caused by the deficiency of kidney qi, weak internal yang, and inability to defend the external surface to resist guest evil. Cold wind takes advantage of the deficiency and goes straight into Shaoyin, blocking the movement of true yang. The main method is to use Ma Xin Aconite Decoction to warm the meridian and resolve the symptoms: 36g of black monkshood slices (boil thoroughly first), 9g of ephedra (boil for several times to remove the foam), 6g of Asarum, and 12g of Guijian. \\nI feel sweaty after 1 dose and the body fever has subsided. I only feel dizzy, coughing and timid. However, although the external evils have been resolved, the cold in the lungs has not been cleared away, and the yang energy is still weak. Combine the four inverses with the two chen and add pungent and flavor to support the yang and warm the cold. \\n45g of black fusian slices, 24g of ginger, 9g of raw licorice, 9g of orange peel, 12g of faxia, 12g of poria, 4g of asarum, 1.2g of schisandra chinensis.\\n Boil the fusilli slices in boiling water for 2 hours, then add the remaining medicine and decoct it. After 1 dose, the cough immediately stopped, the food intake increased, the spirit recovered, and the disease was cured. ("Brief Introduction to Medicine") \\nNote: In this case, the kidney qi is deficient, and Shaoyin feels cold, resulting in too little and two senses. The recipe uses Ma Xin Aconite Decoction, and adds Guijian to enhance the ability to open the epidermis; after removing sweat and reducing fever, combine Sini Decoction with Erchen Decoction and add Asarum and Wuwei to warm the lungs and resolve phlegm. Since the external syndrome has been resolved, the ephedra is removed; although Schisandra chinensis is used with Junjiang and Asarum to form Zhongjing's phlegm-reducing formula (ginger-spicy flavor), only 1.2g of Schisandra chinensis is used to prevent it from astringing evil, which shows the meticulousness of medical rules.`,"张某，男，22岁，四川会理县军士":"Zhang, male, 22 years old, sergeant in Huili County, Sichuan","张某，男，22岁，四川会理县军士。1921年3月值瘟疫流行，被染而发病。发高热已10日，延余往诊。刚到该处，见另一军士搀扶病者出门外小解，小便清长如水.旋即目珠上视，其势欲脱。速诊其脉，沉数而细，唇焦口燥，苔黄黑而起刺;以手试之，则口气蒸手。仓卒之时药石不济，恐阴液脱绝，急以冷水灌之，连喂二碗.目珠始返回如常，神识转清。\\n询及病已10日，壮热烦渴.大便不通，小便短赤，曾服发 \\n表退热药数剂，汗后身热不退，反见溺多清长。此系邪热内盛，复被发表劫汗，重伤阴液，逼阴外脱之险象。急宜凉下以救真阴，主以承气白虎汤治之：\\n生石膏30g（碎，布包），知母13g，枳实13g（炒，捣），生大黄16g（泡水兑入），厚朴13g（炒），芒硝10g，川黄连10g，粳米10g。 \\n次日复诊，大便已通，下出酱黑燥屎若干；身热已退六七，小便反见短赤。此邪热已经溃退，阴液尚未恢复，脉仍沉数，喜饮清凉。照原方去黄连，加麦冬26g。\\n再诊，舌苔已退净，津液满口，渴饮止，神食较增，小便已清利如常。遂照原方去石膏，加口芪26g，生地改为熟地15g0连服3剂而愈。":"Zhang, male, 22 years old, sergeant in Huili County, Sichuan. In March 1921, the plague was prevalent, and he became ill after being infected. It has been 10 days since I had high fever and I delayed going to the doctor. As soon as I arrived at the place, I saw another sergeant helping the patient to go out to urinate. His urine was clear and long like water. Immediately, he looked up and felt that he was about to escape. Diagnose the pulse quickly and find that it is several and thin, the lips are burnt and the mouth is dry, and the fur is yellow and black and thorny; if you try it with your hands, your breath will be steaming. In a hurry, the medicine and stone were not enough, and I was afraid that the Yin liquid would disappear, so I hurriedly poured cold water into it and fed it two bowls in a row. The eyes began to return to normal, and the consciousness became clear. \\nThe patient has been ill for 10 days. He has severe fever and polydipsia. He has difficulty in defecation and short and red urine. He has taken several doses of antipyretic drugs. However, the body heat does not subside after sweating. This is a dangerous sign of excessive internal heat causing excessive sweating, severe damage to the yin fluid, and forcing the yin to prolapse. If it is urgent, it should be cooled down to save the true yin. The main treatment is Chengqi Baihu Decoction: 30g of raw gypsum (crushed, wrapped in cloth), 13g of Anemarrhena, 13g of Citrus aurantium (stir-fried, pounded), 16g of raw rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed with water), 13g of Magnolia officinalis (stir-fried), 10g of Glauber's salt, 10g of Coptis chinensis, and 10g of japonica rice. \\nAfter a follow-up visit the next day, the stool was clear, with some black and dry feces coming out. The body fever had subsided and the urine was short and red. This evil heat has subsided, the Yin fluid has not yet recovered, and the pulse is still heavy and rapid, so you like to drink cool drinks. Follow the original recipe and remove Coptis chinensis and add 26g of Ophiopogon japonicus. \\nReexamination, the tongue coating has receded, the mouth is full of body fluids, thirst has been quenched, the appetite has increased, and the urine has become clear and clear as usual. Then the gypsum was removed according to the original prescription, 26g of stilbene was added, and the raw rehmannia was changed to 15g of the rehmannia glutinosa. After taking 3 doses, the condition was cured.","张某，男，50岁":"Zhang, male, 50 years old","张某，男，50岁。始因风寒外感，发热恶寒，头身疼痛，全身不适。次日双目发赤，红肿疼痛，畏光而多眵。察脉沉细而紧，舌淡苔薄白而润。此乃风寒袭表，经脉血络受阻，凝滞不通所致。治以温经解表，发寒通络。方用加味麻黄附子细辛汤。附片30g，麻黄6g，细辛5g，桂枝9g，防风9g，橘络5g，沙苑蒺藜9g，甘草6g，生姜3片。\\n煎服1次，温覆而卧，得微汗出。1剂尽，表证已解.目赤肿痛均已消退。惟阳神尚虚，头昏肢软，双目略感发胀。继以益气通络明目之剂治之。\\n口芪24g，细辛3g，橘络3g，沙苑蒺藜6g，蝉退5g，藁本9g，女贞子9g，益智仁9g，茺蔚子6g，干姜9g，甘草6g。\\n上方服2剂而痊。\\n按：本案目赤肿痛而见风寒表证，吴氏以太少两解法，1剂而表解，目赤肿痛均消，洵为高手。":"Zhang, male, 50 years old. It started with exogenous wind and cold, fever, aversion to cold, head and body pain, and general malaise. The next day, both eyes were red, swollen, painful, and photophobic. The pulse is thin and tight, the tongue is pale and has a thin white coating. This is caused by wind and cold attacking the surface, causing the meridians and blood vessels to be blocked and blocked. The treatment is to warm the meridians and relieve the superficial symptoms, and to relieve cold and dredge collaterals. Use flavored ephedra, aconite and asarum soup. 30g of Aconite, 6g of Ephedra, 5g of Asarum, 9g of Guizhi, 9g of Fangfeng, 5g of Juluo, 9g of Tribulus terrestris, 6g of licorice, and 3 slices of ginger. \\nDecoct it and take it once, warm it while lying down, and you will sweat slightly. After 1 dose, the superficial symptoms have been resolved. The redness, swelling and pain in the eyes have subsided. However, the yang spirit is still weak, the limbs are dizzy and the limbs are weak, and the eyes are slightly swollen. Then treat it with an agent that replenishes qi, unblocks collaterals and improves eyesight. \\nOral Qi 24g, Asarum 3g, Juluo 3g, Tribulus terrestris 6g, Cicada 5g, Ligusticum 9g, Ligustrum lucidum 9g, Aizhiren 9g, Asarum 6g, dried ginger 9g, licorice 6g. \\nThe patient recovered after taking 2 doses. \\nNote: In this case, the symptoms of redness, swelling and pain in the eyes were symptomatic of wind and cold. Wu used the two solutions of Taishao. One dose was enough to relieve the symptoms. The redness, swelling and pain in the eyes were all gone. Xun is a master.","张某，男，年30岁":"Zhang, male, 30 years old","张某，男，年30岁。 1924年3月，感瘟疫之邪而病，服前医之方香苏散合升麻葛根汤等2剂未效。病已八九日，延余诊视：壮热烦渴饮冷，请语烦躁，大便不通，小便短赤，脉来洪数，舌苔黄而生芒刺，唇赤而焦，鼻如烟煤而干燥。此系瘟疫邪气传里入腑之证，邪热内甚，形成亢阳灼阴，真阴涸竭。急当釜底抽薪凉下以救真阴，拟白虎合承气汤方加减治之：\\n生石膏30g，知母13g，生甘草6g，白粳米13g，寸冬16g，生大黄13g（泡水兑入），芒硝，10g，厚朴13g（炒），枳实12g（炒、捣碎），生地13g0\\n服后下出硬结燥屎1次。次日复诊，病状已减，壮热较退，口津略生，因嘱照原方再进1剂。\\n三日复诊：服药后又解润大便3次，身热退去其半，谑语止，烦渴已减。拟用加味人参白虎汤，养阴生津并除余热：\\n人参24g，生石膏24g（碎，布包），知母12g，寸冬15g，生地15g，黄连5g，玄参10g，枳壳12g，大黄6g（泡水兑入），甘草6g，粳米一撮。\\n服后当晚夜半，忽而肢冷畏寒，继则抖战不可忍，旋即大汗如洗.热退肤冷，脉微欲绝。斯时病家惶恐不已，促余再诊。视之则患者脉来缓弱，舌润，口生津液，渴饮已止.呼吸平和。当即告之，此名“战汗”，为病退之兆，切勿惊扰，但可温覆，否则战汗出而中止，病当不愈。\\n四日清晨续诊：唇舌润，苔皮脱，津液满口，已脉静身凉:大病悉退，进稀粥二碗，继以生脉散加当归、生地、杭芍养阴生津，服2剂而愈。\\n原按：“壮火食气”为本病之症结所在。邪热太盛，亢阳灼阴，真阴涸竭，患者危在旦夕，今得凉下连进，邪热溃退，真阴来复，正气胜邪，“战汗”之作，实为病愈佳兆。吴又可《瘟疫论》曰：“……忽得战汗，经气输泄，当即脉静身凉，烦渴顿除。”证诸临床，乃切实之经验。":`Zhang, male, 30 years old. In March 1924, he contracted the evil of plague and became ill. He took two doses of Xiangsu Powder and Cimicifuga Gegen Decoction, which were prescribed by his former doctor, but they did not work. The patient has been ill for eighty-nine days and has been examined for the following symptoms: strong heat, polydipsia and cold drinking, irritability when speaking, obstruction of stool, short red urine, rapid and rapid pulse, yellow tongue coating with thorns, red and burnt lips, and dry and soot-like nose. This is a sign that the evil spirit of plague spreads into the internal organs, and the evil heat is severe, causing hyperactive yang and burning of yin, and the exhaustion of true yin. If you have to draw firewood from the cauldron and let it cool down to save the true yin, use Baihu Hechengqi decoction to treat it: \\nGypsum 30g, Anemarrhena 13g, licorice 6g, white japonica rice 13g, Cundong 16g, 13g of raw rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed with water), 10g of Glauber's salt, 13g of Magnolia officinalis (stir-fried), 12g of Citrus aurantium (stir-fried and mashed), 13g of raw rehmannia glutinosa. 0\\nAfter taking it, I had hard and dry stool once. After a follow-up visit the next day, the symptoms had subsided, the strong fever had subsided, and the mouth was slightly raw, so I was told to take another dose according to the original prescription. \\nRevisited on the third day: After taking the medicine, the stool was moisturized 3 times, half of the body heat subsided, the gibbering stopped, and the polydipsia was reduced. It is planned to use flavored ginseng and white tiger soup to nourish yin and promote fluid and remove residual heat: 24g ginseng, 24g gypsum (crushed, wrapped in cloth), 12g anemarrhena, 15g cundong, 15g raw rehmannia, 5g coptis, 10g scrophulariaceae, 12g aurantium aurantium, 6g rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed), 6g licorice, and a pinch of japonica rice. \\nAt midnight after taking it, I suddenly felt cold in my limbs, followed by unbearable trembling and shaking, and then sweating profusely. The heat subsided, my skin became cold, and my pulse was weak and weak. At this time, the patient was panic-stricken and urged me to see him again. The patient's pulse is slow and weak, his tongue is moist, his mouth produces fluid, his thirst has ceased, and his breathing is peaceful. Immediately tell him that this is called "war sweat", which is a sign that the disease is resolving. Do not disturb him, but he can be treated with warmth, otherwise the war sweat will stop and the disease will not be cured. \\nRevisited in the early morning of the fourth day: Lips and tongue are moist, fur and skin are peeling off, mouth is full of body fluids, pulse is quiet and body is cool: serious illness subsides, take two bowls of gruel, then add Shengmai Powder with Angelicae Sinensis, Radix Rehmanniae, and Hangshao to nourish yin and promote body fluid, take 2 doses and recover. \\nOriginal note: "Strengthening fire and breathing gas" is the crux of the disease. If the evil heat is too strong, the yang will scorch the yin, and the true yin will dry up, the patient will be in danger. Today, the cold will continue to advance, the evil heat will collapse, the true yin will come back, and the righteous energy will defeat the evil. The "fighting sweat" is actually a good sign of recovery. Wu Youke's "Treatise on Plague" said: "...Suddenly, you will suffer from sweating, menstrual qi will be released, your pulse will become stagnant, your body will become cool, and your polydip will be relieved immediately." The clinical symptoms are real experience.`,张氏益气健脾活血方:"Zhang's Recipe for Replenishing Qi, Strengthening the Spleen and Huoxue",张沛霖:"Zhang Peilin","张沛霖先生1927年生，专攻针灸数十载，深研子午流注、灵龟八法等古代时间医学。":"Mr. Zhang Peilin was born in 1927. He has specialized in acupuncture for decades and has studied deeply in ancient time medicine such as Ziwu Liuzhu and Linggui Bafa.","张沛霖，云南针灸名家，擅用子午流注、灵龟八法等时间针法，针灸治疗痛证与神经系统疾病，屡起沉疴。":"Zhang Peilin, a famous acupuncture master in Yunnan, is good at using time acupuncture methods such as Ziwu Liuzhu and Linggui Bafa to treat pain syndromes and neurological diseases with acupuncture, and he often suffers from serious illnesses.",张震:"Zhang Zhen","张震先生1928年生，毕生从事中医临床与科研，学贯中西，尤邃于中医辨证理论研究。":"Mr. Zhang Zhen was born in 1928. He has been engaged in clinical and scientific research of traditional Chinese medicine all his life. He has learned both Chinese and Western medicine, and is especially proficient in the theory of syndrome differentiation of traditional Chinese medicine.","张震，国医大师，云南省中医中药研究院研究员。倡“证候层级辨证”理论，擅治内科疑难杂症，为云岭医派之代表。":'Zhang Zhen is a master of traditional Chinese medicine and a researcher at the Yunnan Academy of Traditional Chinese Medicine. He advocates the theory of "syndrome level differentiation" and is good at treating difficult and complicated internal diseases. He is a representative of the Yunling School of Medicine.',当代:"contemporary","当归20g，川芎12g，白芍20g，熟地25g，菟丝子20g，枸杞子15g，香附15g，艾叶6g":"Angelica sinensis 20g, Chuanxiong rhizome 12g, white peony root 20g, Rehmannia glutinosa 25g, Cuscuta 20g, wolfberry 15g, Cyperus rotundus 15g, mugwort leaves 6g","彭某，男，年35岁":"Peng, male, 35 years old","彭某，男，年35岁。禀赋素强，偶停宿食，兼有湿热，于1929年9月15日夜起入厕，感受风寒而起病。初起即发热吐泻，头疼体痛，自汗而畏寒；继则下痢赤白，小腹痛甚，里急后重，每便仅一二匙，日夜无度；小便短赤，噤口不食，脉来浮弦而兼紧象，舌苔白腻，舌尖绛。\\n按：病原系湿热夹食积阻遏肠胃，复感风寒外邪，闭束太阳经气运行之机，表寒外束，又有湿热内逼，以致身热下痢，此即所谓“协热痢”。法当表里双治。以桂葛汤解肌表之邪，佐小承气汤加黄连下宿食而清湿热。\\n葛根12g，桂尖10g，杭芍20g，大黄10g（泡水兑入），油朴12g，枳实10g（捣），黄连5g，生姜10g，小枣7枚，甘草3g。\\n服上方1剂始尽，即见汗出，汗后热退脉平。表邪已解，痢亦减轻，惟湿热食积尚阻遏胃肠，湿热内逼，痢未全止，每痢仍腹痛后重。遂以通因通用之法，拟大承气汤合槟芍顺气汤急下宿食兼清湿热。 \\n生杭芍24g，生大黄12g（泡水兑入），枳实10g（炒、捣），厚朴10g（炒），槟榔12g，麦冬12g，广木香5g，芒硝5g，黄连4g。\\n上方服后，得快利稀粪二三便，腹痛后重及赤白痢均减去十之七八，腻苔已退，稍进稀粥。惟小便仍短赤，思食冷物水果。此病状虽减而湿热痢毒未净，仍照原方加减主之：\\n生杭芍20g，生大黄6g（泡水兑入），黄连5g，厚朴10g，麦冬12g，玄明粉5g.广木香4g。\\n服后又下出溏薄粪便2次，痢遂止，肛门稍坠，食量较增，小便尚赤。余热尚未全清，继拟下方治疗。\\n沙参13g，寸冬13g，木通10g，生杭芍13g，酒炙大黄5g，厚朴10g。 \\n服上方后饮食复常，神形健如，痢止溺清，腹痛若失而瘥。\\n原按：余遇下痢之证，身热头体痛有表证者，当即以桂葛汤先解表邪；若无表邪，则当头以凉下为急。如此疗法，无不效如桴鼓。苟不解除表邪，则身热不退，易转危笃。故《内经》云：“利证身热不休者死。”不行攻下，邪热痢毒亦不能除。若属久痢虚寒者，又当以温固之法治之。":`Peng, male, 35 years old. He had a strong natural endowment and occasionally stopped eating and had dampness and heat. On the night of September 15, 1929, he went to the toilet and felt wind and cold and became ill. It starts with fever, vomiting and diarrhea, headache and body aches, spontaneous sweating and chills; followed by red and white diarrhea, severe pain in the lower abdomen, severe tenesmus, only one or two spoonfuls in each stool, day and night; short red urine, mouth shut and not eating, floating and tight pulse, white and greasy tongue coating, and red tongue tip. \\nNote: The pathogenic factor is dampness and heat trapped in food that blocks the intestines and stomach, causing wind and cold external evils to block the movement of the sun meridian. The external cold is bundled outward, and dampness and heat are forced inward, resulting in diarrhea caused by body heat. This is the so-called "heat-assisted dysentery". The law should treat both the outside and the inside. Use Guige Decoction to relieve the evils on the skin surface, and use Xiaochengqi Decoction and Coptis chinensis to remove dampness and heat. \\n12g Pueraria lobata, 10g Guijian, 20g peony root, 10g rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed with water), 12g Youpu, 10g Citrus aurantium (pounded), 5g Coptis chinensis, 10g ginger, 7 jujubes, 3g licorice. \\nSweat will appear immediately after taking the first dose above, and the fever will subside after sweating and the pulse will be flat. The external evils have been resolved, and the dysentery has also been relieved. However, the accumulation of damp and hot food still blocks the gastrointestinal tract. Therefore, using the general method of relieving the cause, the Dachengqi Decoction and the Binshao Shunqi Decoction were used to relieve the symptoms and clear away dampness and heat. \\n 24g of raw Hangzhou peony, 12g of raw rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed with water), 10g of Citrus aurantium (stir-fried and pounded), 10g of Magnolia officinalis (stir-fried), 12g of betel nut, 12g of Ophiopogon japonicus, 5g of agarwood, 5g of Glauber's salt, and 4g of coptis. \\nAfter taking the above medicine, two or three loose stools can be obtained quickly. Abdominal pain, redness and white diarrhea are reduced by 70-80%. The greasy coating has receded and a little gruel has been obtained. But the urine is still short and red, and I want to eat cold fruits. Although the symptoms of the disease have subsided but the damp-heat dysentery poison has not been eliminated, the original prescription is still added and subtracted: 20g of raw peony root, 6g of raw rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed in), 5g of coptis, 10g of Magnolia officinalis, 12g of Ophiopogon japonicus, 5g of Xuanming powder, and 4g of Aleica grandiflora. \\nAfter taking it, I had loose and thin stools twice. The dysentery stopped, my anus dropped slightly, my food intake increased, and my urine was still red. The remaining heat has not completely cleared up yet, so we plan to continue the treatment below. \\nAdenophora 13g, Cundong 13g, Akebia 10g, raw peony root 13g, wine-roasted rhubarb 5g, Magnolia officinalis 10g. \\nAfter taking the above, the diet returns to normal, the body and mind are as healthy as possible, the diarrhea is relieved and the abdominal pain is relieved. \\nOriginal note: If you encounter symptoms of dysentery, body heat, headache, or body pain with external symptoms, you should immediately use Guige Decoction to relieve the external evils; if there are no external evils, treat the cold as the first priority. This kind of treatment is as effective as a drum. If the external evil is not eliminated, the body heat will not subside and it will easily turn into a serious condition. Therefore, the "Nei Jing" says: "Those who suffer from persistent body heat will die." If it cannot be attacked, the evil heat and dysentery poison cannot be eliminated. If it is a person with chronic dysentery, deficiency and cold, it should be treated with methods of warming and strengthening.`,"心烦失眠重者，加酸枣仁、远志、茯神；情志郁结甚者，加合欢皮、郁金、柴胡":"For those with severe upset and insomnia, add Ziziphus jujube, Polygala, and Poria; for those with severe emotional depression, add Albizia bark, Yujin, and Bupleurum.",快速链接:"Quick links","急性期醒脑开窍，取水沟、内关、三阴交为主，手法宜重；恢复期通经活络，取手足阳明经穴为主，配合电针；后遗症期调补气血，灸药并施。":"In the acute stage, Shuigou, Neiguan, and Sanyinjiao are the main ones, and the techniques should be heavy; in the recovery stage, the Yangming meridian points of the hands and feet are mainly used to unblock the meridians and activate collaterals, combined with electroacupuncture; in the sequelae stage, qi and blood are adjusted and replenished, and moxibustion is used together.","急惊风案 柯某之子，1岁半，住昆明市":"Emergency case: Ke’s son, 1 and a half years old, lives in Kunming City","急惊风案\\n柯某之子，1岁半，住昆明市。清晨寐醒抱出，冒风而惊，发热，自汗沉迷，角弓反张，目上视。纹赤而浮，唇赤舌淡白，脉来浮缓。由风寒阻塞太阳运行之机，加以小儿营卫未充，脏腑柔嫩，不耐风寒，以致猝然抽搐而成急惊，此为风中太阳肌表之证。以仲景桂枝汤主之，使太阳肌腠之风寒，得微汗而解。桂尖9g，杭芍9g，生草6g，生姜9g，小枣7个。\\n入粳米一小撮同煎，服后温复，微汗。一剂即熟寐，汗出热退，次日霍然。\\n按：此案认证准确，选方切当，虽见猝然抽搐，并未用止痉定惊套药，而是认定“风中太阳肌表之证”，以桂枝汤治之，把好太阳关。仲景服桂枝汤惯例，服药后啜热稀粥，以助胃气。本例则将粳米一小撮同煎，已含医圣之意，此善用经方者也。":`Urgent convulsion case\\nKe’s son, 1 and a half years old, lives in Kunming. Waking up in the morning, I was frightened by the wind, had fever, suffered from spontaneous sweating, opisthotonus, and looked up. The lines are red and floating, the lips are red and the tongue is pale, and the pulse is slow and slow. The wind and cold block the movement of the sun, and the child's internal organs are not fully replenished, and the internal organs are tender and intolerant to the wind and cold, resulting in sudden convulsions and panic. This is the sign of the wind in the sun's skin. Take Zhongjing Guizhi Decoction as the main treatment to relieve the wind-cold in the sun muscles and induce slight sweating. Guijian 9g, Hangshao 9g, raw grass 6g, ginger 9g, 7 jujubes. \\nAdd a handful of japonica rice and fry together. After taking it, it will warm up and make you sweat slightly. One dose will make you sleep well, sweating and fever will subside, and then you will feel restless the next day. \\nNote: The certification of this case is accurate and the selection of prescription is accurate. Although there was a sudden convulsion, the anticonvulsant and anticonvulsant medicine was not used. Instead, it was determined that "the syndrome of wind in the sun's skin surface" was treated with Guizhi Decoction to control the sun. Zhongjing takes Guizhi Decoction as usual. After taking the medicine, he sips the hot gruel to relieve stomach qi. In this example, a handful of japonica rice is fried together, which already contains the meaning of medical sage. This is also a good use of the classic prescription.`,"恶阻、胎漏、产后诸疾治验。":"Treatment experience for obstruction, fetal leakage, and postpartum diseases.","恶阻以和胃降逆为法，用药轻清，不令胎气受伤；胎漏辨寒热虚实，热者清热养血，虚者固肾益气，且嘱静养慎动。":"For severe obstruction, the method is to harmonize the stomach and lower the qi. Use light and clear medicine so as not to hurt the fetal gas. For fetal leakage, distinguish between cold and heat, deficiency and excess. If it is hot, it can clear away heat and nourish blood. If it is deficient, it can strengthen the kidneys and replenish qi. It is also advised to rest and be careful in moving.","您可以更换关键词，或试试以下热门检索：":"You can change keywords, or try the following popular searches:","您所寻访的典籍暂未收录于此，或链接已有所变迁。":"The book you are looking for is not yet included here, or the link has changed.","慢性肝病重在“疏、养、清、化”四法，缓缓图功，不求速效。":'Chronic liver disease focuses on the four methods of "sparing, nourishing, clearing, and transforming", trying to achieve results slowly rather than seeking quick results.',"慢性肾炎合并腹水案 沈某，男，30岁":"Chronic nephritis combined with ascites case Shen, male, 30 years old","慢性肾炎合并腹水案\\n沈某，男，30岁。患慢性肾炎1年余，后因发生腹水肿胀，体虚弱极而送昆明某医院治疗，其效不显，于1958年12月12日邀吴氏会诊：面部浮肿，目下浮起如卧蚕，面色苍白晦滞，口唇青乌，欲寐无神，神情倦怠已极；腹内水鼓作胀，其状如匏；下肢浮肿，胫附以下按之凹陷而不易复起；身重卧床，难于转侧；语声低弱，腹中撑胀，腰背酸胀痛楚不止，小腹亦坠胀作痛；口淡不思食，不渴饮，小便短少；舌润而色淡夹青，苔滑而灰黑，脉沉迟无力。此系脾肾阳虚、水\\n寒土湿、寒水泛滥所致。法当扶阳温寒化气利水主之，方用四逆五苓散加减：\\n附片100g，干姜40g，花椒7g（炒去汗），猪苓15g，茯苓30g，条桂15g。\\n服4剂，小便遽转清长畅利，面足浮肿消退，腹水消去十之六七，体重减轻21市斤，腰背痛已大为减轻，仍有酸胀；稍能食，精神较增；舌苔灰黑已退，呈现白滑苔，脉转和缓。仍以扶阳温化主之：\\n附片100g，干姜50g，吴萸10g，桂枝30g，苡仁10g，猪苓10g，茯苓30g。\\n连服4剂，腹水消去十之七八，面色转好，精神、饮食较增；舌质青色已退，淡红而润，苔薄白滑，脉和缓有神根。大病悉退，阳神尚虚，余邪未净，唯有增强心肾之阳，始能效奏全功。上方加减治之：\\n附片150g，干姜50g，上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），砂仁10g，黑丑20g，茯苓50g，公丁10g。\\n服4剂后，寒水阴邪消除殆尽，善后调理1周，病愈出院。\\n按：此案腹水且周身浮肿，用药不过六七味，方简量重，不愧为经典火神派风格。三诊时，“腹水消去十之七八”“大病悉退”，附片由100g增加到150g；因“余邪未净”，加用黑丑峻药以攻之，俱显胆识。":'Case of chronic nephritis combined with ascites\\nShen, male, 30 years old. He suffered from chronic nephritis for more than a year. Later, he developed ascites and swelling and was extremely weak, so he was sent to a hospital in Kunming for treatment. The effect was not obvious. On December 12, 1958, Wu was invited for consultation: his face was swollen, his eyes were floating like silkworms, his face was pale and dull, his lips were blue, he was sleepy, and his expression was extremely tired; there was water in his abdomen. Swelling, which looks like a belly; lower limbs are swollen, and the shin joints are sunken when pressed and are difficult to get up; the body is heavy in bed and difficult to turn to the side; the voice is weak, the abdomen is distended, the waist and back are sore and painful, and the lower abdomen is also swollen and painful; the mouth is light and does not want to eat, is not thirsty to drink, and the urine is short and infrequent; the tongue is moist and pale and green, the coating is slippery and gray-black, and the pulse is slow and weak. This is caused by spleen and kidney yang deficiency, water\\ncold earth-dampness, and overflow of cold water. Fadang is the main method of nourishing yang, warming cold, transforming qi and diluting water, and uses Si Ni Wuling Powder to add and subtract: 100g of Fu Pian, 40g of dried ginger, 7g of Zanthoxylum bungeanum (fried to remove sweat), 15g of Poria, 30g of Poria, and 15g of Guizhou. \\nAfter taking 4 doses, the urine suddenly became clear and smooth, the edema of the face and feet subsided, ascites disappeared 60% of the time, and the weight decreased by 21 pounds. The back pain was greatly relieved, but there was still soreness and swelling. Fuyang warming is still the main method: 100g Fuyang, 50g dried ginger, 10g Wuyu, 30g Guizhi, 10g Yiren, 10g Polyporus, and 30g Poria. \\nAfter taking 4 doses, 70% of the ascites disappeared, the complexion improved, and the energy and diet increased; the cyan color of the tongue has faded, becoming light red and moist, with thin white slippery coating, and a gentle pulse with a deep pulse. All serious illnesses have subsided, the yang spirit is still weak, and the remaining evils have not been eliminated. Only by strengthening the yang of the heart and kidney can the full effect be achieved. Treat it by adding and subtracting from the above:\\n150g of Futian, 50g of dried ginger, 10g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10g of Amomum villosum, 20g of Heichou, 50g of Poria, and 10g of male penis. \\nAfter taking 4 doses, the cold-water yin evil was completely eliminated. After one week of aftercare, I was discharged from the hospital. \\nNote: This case had ascites and edema all over the body. The medicine was only six or seven flavors, and the prescription was simple and heavy. It was worthy of the classic Vulcan style. During the third consultation, "70% of the ascites disappeared" and "all major illnesses subsided", and the number of attached tablets was increased from 100g to 150g. Because "remaining evils were not purified", Heichoujun medicine was added to attack them, which showed their courage.',戴丽三:"Dai Lisan","戴丽三先生1897年生于昆明中医世家，幼承庭训，熟读经典，弱冠悬壶，即以善用经方名于乡里。":"Mr. Dai Lisan was born in a family of traditional Chinese medicine in Kunming in 1897. He inherited the training from the court at an early age and was familiar with the classics. He was known in his hometown for his good use of classics.","戴丽三先生临证验案汇编。案语简明，方药精当，经方活用之妙尽显于字里行间，为滇中习经方者必读之本。":"A compilation of Mr. Dai Lisan's clinical verification cases. The text is concise, the prescriptions are accurate, and the wonderful use of the classic prescriptions is fully demonstrated between the lines. It is a must-read for those who practice classics and prescriptions in central Yunnan.",戴丽三医案:"Dai Li's third medical case",戴丽三医疗经验选:"Dai Lisan’s medical experience selection","戴丽三，昆明人，出身中医世家。毕生笃嗜《伤寒论》《金匮要略》，临证善用经方，药简效宏，于疑难重症屡起沉疴。":'Dai Lisan, a native of Kunming, comes from a family of traditional Chinese medicine. He has devoted his whole life to "Treatise on Febrile Diseases" and "Synopsis of the Golden Chamber". He makes good use of the classic prescriptions for clinical symptoms. The medicines are simple and effective, and he has repeatedly suffered from serious illnesses.',戴慧芬:"Dai Huifen","戴慧芬教授1926年生于昆明，幼承家学，尽得戴氏医学心传，后入医学院校系统深造。":"Professor Dai Huifen was born in Kunming in 1926. She inherited her family's medical education at an early age and gained Dai's medical inheritance. Later, she entered the medical school system for further study.","戴慧芬，戴丽三先生之女，承家学而有所发挥。长期从事中医内科、妇科临床与教学，曾任云南中医学院院长。":"Dai Huifen, the daughter of Mr. Dai Lisan, inherited the family's learning and made great use of it. He has been engaged in clinical and teaching of internal medicine and gynecology of traditional Chinese medicine for a long time, and once served as the dean of Yunnan College of Traditional Chinese Medicine.",戴氏医学传人:"Dai's medical successor",戴氏甘麦大枣汤加味:"Dai's Ganmai Jujube Soup with Flavor",戴氏真武汤加味:"Dai's Zhenwu Soup with flavor","戴氏谓伤寒之法，辨证在前、方药在后，证辨得准、方自然稳，此卷足以证之。":"Dai Shi said that the method of typhoid fever is to differentiate the syndrome first and the prescriptions later. If the syndrome identification is accurate, the prescription will be natural and stable. This volume is enough to prove it.","戴氏谓经方之妙，不在药味之奇，而在配伍之严，用经方贵在辨证精确，方证相合则效如桴鼓，方证不合则虽良方亦无功。":"Dai said that the beauty of the classic prescriptions lies not in the strange taste of the medicine, but in the strict compatibility. The key to using the classic prescriptions lies in accurate syndrome differentiation. If the prescriptions and syndromes are consistent, the effect will be like a drum. If the prescriptions and syndromes are not consistent, even a good prescription will have no effect.","戴阳、格阳、亡阳诸危候之辨识与救逆验案。":"Identification of critical signs of Dai Yang, Ge Yang, and Sui Yang and verification of rescue cases.","房颤案 李某，女，72岁":"Atrial fibrillation case Li, female, 72 years old","房颤案\\n李某，女，72岁。2014年4月5日初诊：房颤1年半，心率50〜100次/分。几乎每天发作心悸，发时觉得心颤身亦颤，眩晕，乏力，便溏，纳差，耳鸣，鼻干，眠差，后半夜睡眠差，动则汗出；舌胖润，脉沉滑，时有结代。心电图示：阵发性房颤。前服某中医之药不效，视之乃经方炙甘草汤。查其脉证乃系心脾肾三脏阳气不足，水湿偏盛。治当温扶心肾之阳，祛除湿气。方拟补坎益离丹扶助心阳，合真武汤温肾利水：\\n桂心30g，白芍25g，附子30g，白术30g，炮姜30g，海蛤粉30g，茯神30g，红参10g，炙甘草15g，龙骨30g，牡蛎30g，生姜10片，大枣10枚。7剂。\\n复诊：心悸发作减少，余症亦轻。附子加至45g，服后感觉头痛而胀，遂减至40g，同时出入药物尚有黄芪、肉桂、枣仁、砂仁、丹参等，服药2个月，症情稳定，偶有发作，程度亦轻。（《关东火神张存悌医案医话选》）\\n按：本案房颤前医用炙甘草汤不效，这里大有学问。在有关《伤寒论》的研究中，有人主张“方证对应”论，有是证用是方，对有证有方的条文拿来就用。如“伤寒，脉结代，心动悸，炙甘草汤主之”，凡见脉结代、心动悸之症，无问其他，即可投之，称之为“方证辨证”，胡希恕先生“把辨方证称之为最高级辨证”。\\n考炙甘草汤组成以滋补阴血为主（生地、麦冬、阿胶、炙甘草、人参、麻仁、大枣、生姜、桂枝），但是临床上，心之阳气不足，无力推动血脉亦可以造成心动悸、脉结代之症，而且此类恐怕更多。沈阳前辈刘冕堂即曾指出：“按他经亦有此症（脉结代，心动悸），是阳分大虚，虚极生寒，非姜附辛热不为功，若用此药（炙甘草汤），是速其死也。”本例即是如此。患者所现之症皆属阳虚阴盛之象，前医用炙甘草汤不效势在必然，而且这种误治较为普遍，关键是这里有阴阳之异。":`Atrial fibrillation case\\nLi, female, 72 years old. First diagnosis on April 5, 2014: atrial fibrillation for one and a half years, heart rate 50 to 100 beats/min. Heart palpitations occur almost every day. During the onset, the heart and body tremble, dizziness, fatigue, loose stools, poor appetite, tinnitus, dry nose, poor sleep, poor sleep in the second half of the night, and sweating when moving; a fat and moist tongue, a slow and slippery pulse, and occasional knotting. Electrocardiogram: paroxysmal atrial fibrillation. I took a certain traditional Chinese medicine medicine before but it didn't work, so I decided to treat it with Zhigancao Decoction. Checking the pulse syndrome shows that the three internal organs of the heart, spleen and kidney are deficient in yang energy and water and dampness are excessive. Treatment should be to warm and support the yang of the heart and kidneys, and to remove dampness. The prescription is intended to nourish Kan Yi Li Dan to support heart yang, and combine Zhenwu Decoction to warm the kidneys and diuretic: 30g Guixin, 25g White Peony, 30g Aconite, 30g Atractylodes, 30g Paojiang, 30g Sea Clam Powder, 30g Poria God, 10g red ginseng, 15g Zhigancao, 30g dragon bone, 30g oyster, 10 slices of ginger, and 10 jujubes. 7 doses. \\nFollow-up visit: The episodes of heart palpitations have decreased and remaining symptoms have become milder. Aconite was added to 45g. After taking it, I felt a headache and bloated, so I reduced it to 40g. At the same time, other medicines were taken as astragalus, cinnamon, jujube kernel, amomum villosum, salvia miltiorrhiza, etc. After taking the medicine for 2 months, the symptoms were stable, with occasional attacks, which were also mild. ("Selected Medical Records of Guandong Fire God Zhang Cunti") \\nNote: In this case, the medical Zhigancao Decoction was not effective before atrial fibrillation. There is a lot of knowledge here. In the research on "Treatise on Febrile Diseases", some people advocate the theory of "correspondence of prescriptions and syndromes", which means that if there is a syndrome, use the prescription, and use the provisions that have the syndrome and prescription. For example, "Typhoid, knotted pulses, and palpitations can be treated by Zhigancao Decoction." If you see symptoms of knotted pulses and palpitations, you can treat them without asking anything else. It is called "prescription syndrome differentiation". Mr. Hu Xishu "calls prescription syndrome differentiation the highest level of syndrome differentiation." \\nThe composition of Kaozhigancao Decoction is mainly to nourish yin and blood (rehmannia glutinosa, Ophiopogon japonicus, donkey hide gelatin, Zhigancao, ginseng, hemp seeds, jujube, ginger, cassia twigs). However, clinically, insufficient yang energy in the heart and inability to promote blood vessels can also cause heart palpitations and pulse knotting, and there may be more such symptoms. Liu Miantang, a senior in Shenyang, once pointed out: "This syndrome (pulse knotting, palpitations) can also occur according to other meridians. It is caused by a great deficiency of the yang component, and extreme deficiency produces cold. It is not due to the pungent heat of ginger, but if you use this medicine (Zhigancao Decoction), your death will be hastened." "This is the case in this case. The symptoms presented by the patient are all signs of yang deficiency and yin excess. It is inevitable that the Zhigancao decoction used in previous medicine will not be effective, and this kind of mistreatment is relatively common. The key is that there is a difference between yin and yang.`,"所举验案附子用量大而煎法严谨，于服药反应、转归判断言之凿凿，为习扶阳者之津梁。":"The cited cases of Aconite used a large amount and the decoction method is rigorous, and it is conclusive in judging the reaction and prognosis of taking the medicine. It is a favorite for those who practice Yang Fu.","所论或一药之用法，或一证之鉴别，或古人立言之得失，如论柴胡劫肝阴之非、论石膏生用煅用之别，皆有独到见解。":"The discussion may be about the use of a medicine, or the identification of a syndrome, or the pros and cons of what the ancients said, such as the discussion on the faults of Bupleurum to rob liver yin, and the difference between the raw and calcined use of gypsum, all of which have unique insights.","所载救逆诸案剂量峻、见效捷，按语中反复叮咛阳气一回、疹自透发之理，扶阳托透之旨贯彻始终。":"The cases of rescuing and reversing diseases contained in it are of high dosage and quick effect. The notes repeatedly exhort the principle that once the yang energy returns, the eruption will occur on its own, and the purpose of supporting the yang and supporting it is implemented throughout.","所载方剂简、便、验、廉，多采自民间":"The prescriptions contained are simple, convenient, effective, and inexpensive, and are mostly collected from folk sources.","所载治验数则，详述针刺次序、得气要求与疗程安排，可操作性极强，堪为临床程式。":"The treatment rules contained in it detail the acupuncture sequence, deqi requirements and treatment schedule, which are highly maneuverable and can be regarded as clinical procedures.","所载验案或温经暖宫，或疏肝养血，或健脾化痰，皆以调经为先着，经调而后议种子，法度井然。":"The documented cases include warming the menstruation and warming the uterus, soothing the liver and nourishing the blood, or strengthening the spleen and resolving phlegm. They all focus on regulating menstruation first, then regulate the menstruation, and then discuss the seeds. The method is well-organized.",手法要旨:"The gist of the technique","手法轻巧，补泻分明，务求气至病所。":"The technique is light and has clear replenishing and reducing effects, aiming to bring Qi to the location of the disease.",扶阳学派在滇代表人物:"Representative figures of Fuyang School in Yunnan",扶阳派:"Fuyang Sect","扶阳派 · 经方派":"Fuyang Sect · Jingfang Sect","承戴氏“方证对应”之说，主张读经典、做临床、勤思辨。":`Adhering to Dai's theory of "correspondence between prescriptions and syndromes", he advocates reading classics, practicing clinical practice, and diligent thinking.`,"抗肝纤维化每于辨证方中佐以活血软坚之品。":"Anti-hepatic fibrosis prescriptions are often supplemented with blood-activating and softening products in syndrome differentiation prescriptions.","按「名医 · 医案 · 著作」三大分类检索云岭杏林数字馆藏。":'Search the Yunling Xinglin digital collection according to the three major categories of "Famous Doctors·Medical Records·Works".',"按语中详析辨证关键与用药时机，谓急证用药如将之用兵，当机立断、不可迟疑，然亦须胆大心细，方能无误。":"The note explains in detail the key to syndrome differentiation and the timing of medication. It is said that using medication for acute syndrome is like using a military force. You must make a decisive decision without hesitation. However, you must be bold and careful in order to be correct.","推崇“女子以血为本”，调经种子必先养血填精、温通奇经。":'It is advocated that "women are based on blood", and the seeds for regulating menstruation must first nourish blood, replenish essence, and warm and unblock menstruation.',推拿:"Massage","推拿之要，“机触于外，巧生于内，手随心转，法从手出”。":'The essence of massage is "the machine touches the outside, skillfully arises from the inside, the hands turn according to the heart, and the method comes out of the hands."',"推拿名家 · 云南推拿学科带头人":"Massage Master · Yunnan Massage Discipline Leader",推拿科:"Massage Department","搜索医案病名、辨证、方剂、药物……":"Search medical records for disease names, syndrome differentiation, prescriptions, drugs...","搜索名医姓名、学术流派、临床专长……":"Search for names of famous doctors, academic schools, clinical expertise...","搜索著作名称、作者、内容提要……":"Search for title, author, abstract...","擅治中风、痹证":"Good at treating stroke and paralysis syndrome","擅治小儿咳喘、厌食":"Good at treating cough, asthma and anorexia in children",擅治痛证:"Good at treating pain syndrome","收录危急重症救逆验案，辨证剖析入微":"Collects critical and severe rescue cases and provides detailed analysis of syndrome differentiation","收载滇产药物四百余种，多为他书所未备":"It contains more than 400 kinds of medicines produced in Yunnan, most of which are not included in other books.",放大:"Zoom in","救治危急重症主张“药专力宏”，反对轻描淡写、贻误病机。":'In the treatment of critical and severe cases, we advocate "exclusive use of medicines to treat serious diseases" and oppose understatement and delaying the pathogenesis of the disease.',"教授临证每以经方起大症。治妇人脏躁以甘麦大枣汤，治妊娠恶阻以干姜半夏人参丸，治内科痰饮以苓桂术甘汤，皆平淡中见功力。常诫学生曰：“经方之妙，在乎对证；对证之要，在乎读书。”":'The professor always uses classic prescriptions to cause serious symptoms. Use Ganmai Dazao Decoction to treat impotence in women, use Ganjiang Banxia Ginseng Pills to treat pregnancy obstruction, and use Lingguishugan Decoction to treat internal medicine phlegm. He often admonishes his students: "The beauty of classic prescriptions lies in verification; the key to verification lies in reading."',"教授主持云南省推拿重点学科建设，编写推拿教材多部。":"The professor presides over the construction of key massage disciplines in Yunnan Province and has written many massage textbooks.","教授执教数十载，主讲《金匮要略》《中医妇科学》，教学临证并重。":'The professor has been teaching for decades and lectures on "Synopsis of the Golden Chamber" and "Traditional Chinese Medicine Gynecology", with equal emphasis on clinical practice.',"教授治慢性乙型肝炎，辨其湿热蕴结、肝郁脾虚、气滞血瘀诸证，分别投以茵陈蒿汤、逍遥散、膈下逐瘀汤化裁，配合现代保肝降酶之法，每使肝功复常、纤维化指标改善。尝谓：“治肝须缓图，欲速则不达。”":'The professor treats chronic hepatitis B by identifying the syndromes of accumulation of dampness and heat, liver stagnation and spleen deficiency, qi stagnation and blood stasis, and administers Yinchenhao Decoction, Xiaoyao Powder, and Diaphragm Zhuyu Decoction respectively, combined with modern liver-protecting and enzyme-lowering methods, which can restore liver function to normal and improve fibrosis indicators. Taste said: "To treat the liver, you must slow down, haste makes waste."',"教授治神经根型颈椎病，先以㨰法、一指禅放松项背肌群，再行颈椎定点旋转扳法整复错位，最后以拿肩井、点天宗收功，配合“米字操”导引。又治小儿肌性斜颈，以揉、捏、扳等轻柔手法，每获良效。":'The professor treats cervical spondylotic radiculopathy by first using the 㨰 method and one-finger meditation to relax the muscles of the neck and back, and then performs fixed-point rotation and pulling of the cervical vertebrae to correct the misalignment. Finally, Naijianjing and Tianzong points are used to complete the exercise, combined with the guidance of "Mi Zi Exercise". It is also used to treat muscular torticollis in children, with gentle techniques such as kneading, pinching, and pulling, which always achieve good results.',"教授长期执教于云南中医学院，主讲中西医结合内科学，桃李遍滇中。":"The professor has been teaching at Yunnan College of Traditional Chinese Medicine for a long time, specializing in internal medicine integrating traditional Chinese and Western medicine, and has gained fame throughout Central Yunnan.",方药心得篇:"Tips on prescriptions and medicines",明代:"Ming Dynasty","明代医药学家 · 《滇南本草》作者":'Medical scientist of the Ming Dynasty, author of "Southern Yunnan Materia Medica"',"春温案 曾某，男，年20岁":"Chunwen case Zeng, male, 20 years old","春温案\\n曾某，男，年20岁。于1924年2月患春温病3日，脉来浮数，发热微恶寒，头疼体痛；面垢，唇赤而焦，舌苔白而燥，尖绛；渴喜冷饮，小便短赤。此系春温病邪热内壅，外有表邪闭束，遂成表寒里热之证，以麻杏甘石汤主之。\\n麻黄12g，生石膏30g（碎，布包），杏仁10g，甘草6g。\\n服1剂后，俄而汗出淋漓，脉静身凉，霍然而愈。\\n按：本例春温选用麻杏甘石汤，原方4味药不加不减，堪称简练；1剂即霍然而愈，是谓神效。":"Chunwen Case\\nZeng, male, 20 years old. In February 1924, he suffered from spring febrile disease on the 3rd day. He had a floating pulse, fever, slight aversion to cold, headache and body aches; his face was dirty, his lips were red and burnt, his tongue coating was white and dry, with a sharp purple tip; he was thirsty and liked cold drinks, and his urine was short and red. This is due to the internal obstruction of the evil heat caused by spring warm disease, and the obstruction of external evils externally, resulting in a syndrome of cold externally and hot internally, which can be treated with Maxing Ganshi Decoction. \\nEphedra 12g, gypsum 30g (broken, wrapped in cloth), almond 10g, licorice 6g. \\nAfter taking 1 dose, I was sweating profusely, my pulse was still and my body was cold, and I suddenly recovered. \\nNote: In this example, Maxing Ganshi Decoction is used for spring warming. The four herbs in the original prescription are neither added nor subtracted, which is simple and concise; one dose can cause immediate relief, which is said to be a miraculous effect.",春温病:"spring fever","春温病冷水治愈案 李某，女,年五旬，住四川省会理县南乡农村":"Case of cold water cure for spring febrile disease Li, female, 50 years old, living in rural area of ​​Nanxiang, Huili County, Sichuan Province","春温病冷水治愈案 李某，女,年五旬，住四川省会理县南乡农村。于1920年2 月患春温病已五日，延余诊视之时，见其张目不寐，壮热烦渴 而饮冷,舌苔白厚而燥,舌尖绛,唇焦齿干,脉来洪数,恶热头 痛，小便短赤。据云已服发表之剂未愈。査前所服之方,系用羌 活、独活、紫苏叶、荆芥、防风、柴胡、葛根之剂。殊服后但见头 汗出，身热尤甚，气粗而喘，烦渴引饮。余诊后断为春温病误 用辛温发散,耗劫阴液所致，急须清热养阴生津为治。因患者 居处远乡僻壤,药材缺乏,未能如愿配方,但见患者烦渴索饮 之状,遂与冰凉之冷水任意饮之。患者饮一碗尽，自言心中爽 快，又求再饮，饮至四碗，顿觉清凉不烦，竟然闭目熟睡。俄 顷，则见汗出淋漓，湿透内衣。约半个时辰后再诊，已脉静身 凉，津液满口，诸证悉除。按：春温初起，客邪内传与阳明燥气相合，误投辛散发表，不但邪不得解,反致伤阴劫液，内热燔炽，水源涸竭。今得冷水相济，补阴救焚，从而阴阳调平，气机通达，则汗出而引邪外散。此为饮冷水救阴液之例，当与人参白虎汤清热生津救焚之意谋同，故能获此良效。再按：温热病证，内热如焚，真阴欲竭之际，急需清凉之剂以济之。西瓜汁、鲜梨汁，甚至清凉冷秋，皆可以滋添阴液。但见某些病家或医者，习俗为常，以为几病皆须忌生冷，戒之最严，虽病热者苦索无已，尚不知其相宜而须投之。实热病情，以硝黄石膏为治，其效若灵，滋阴、清热、苦寒之品，在所必用，又何须拘禁于生冷哉。":"Case of cold water cure for spring febrile disease Li, female, 50 years old, lives in rural area of ​​Nanxiang, Huili County, Sichuan Province. In February 1920, he suffered from spring febrile disease for five days. During the follow-up examination, he was found to be insomnia with open eyes, excessive heat and polydipsia and cold drinking, thick white and dry tongue coating, red tongue tip, burnt lips and dry teeth, rapid and rapid pulse, aversion to heat, headache, and short and red urine. According to the cloud, the patient has not recovered after taking the published medicine. The prescription taken before the examination was based on the preparations of Qianghuo, Duhuo, Perilla leaves, Schizonepeta, Fangfeng, Bupleurum and Pueraria. After taking this medicine, I noticed sweating on my head, especially body heat, shortness of breath and wheezing, and polydipsia leading to drinking. After further diagnosis, it was determined that spring fever disease was caused by misuse of pungent and warm substances, which depleted the yin fluid. It was urgent to clear away heat, nourish yin and promote fluid production. Because the patient lived in a remote area and lacked medicinal materials, the formula could not be obtained as expected. However, he saw that the patient was thirsty and wanted to drink, so he drank as much as he wanted with ice-cold water. The patient drank one bowl and said he felt refreshed, and asked for more. After drinking four bowls, he suddenly felt cool and relieved, and fell asleep with his eyes closed. After a while, he was sweating profusely and his underwear was soaked through. About half an hour later, he was diagnosed again. His pulse was stagnant, his body was cold, his mouth was full of body fluids, and all symptoms were gone. Note: At the beginning of the spring temperature, the internal heat of guest evil is combined with the dryness of Yangming, and if you mistakenly add Xin and San Qi, not only will the evil be unresolved, but the Yin Jie liquid will be damaged, the internal heat will burn, and the water source will dry up. Today, cold water can be used to supplement the yin and relieve the burning, so that the yin and yang are balanced and the qi is unobstructed, causing sweating and attracting evil spirits to disperse. This is an example of drinking cold water to save Yin liquid. It should be consistent with the purpose of Ginseng Baihu Decoction to clear away heat, promote fluid production and save Yin, so it can achieve this good effect. Press again: Warm fever syndrome, internal heat is burning, and true yin is exhausted, and a cooling agent is urgently needed to relieve it. Watermelon juice, fresh pear juice, and even cool and cold autumn water can nourish Yin fluid. However, it is common practice among some patients or doctors to believe that coldness and rawness should be avoided in all diseases, and the most stringent precautions are taken. Although those suffering from fever are suffering endlessly, they still do not know how appropriate they are and must treat them. For conditions of excessive heat, use yellow gypsum to treat it. It is very effective. It is a product that nourishes yin, clears away heat, and is bitter and cold. It must be used wherever it is needed. There is no need to limit it to raw and cold medicine.","春温病少阴热化证 吴某，昆明人，住昆明市绣衣街，有长子年十五岁，…":"Spring febrile disease with Shaoyin-heat syndrome. Wu is from Kunming and lives in Xiuyi Street, Kunming City. He has an eldest son who is fifteen years old...","春温病少阴热化证 吴某，昆明人，住昆明市绣衣街，有长子年十五岁，于 1921年3月患病延余诊视,发热不退已十一日，面红唇赤而焦，舌红苔黄而无津，虚烦不得卧。食物不进，渴喜冷饮，小 便短赤，大便不解，脉来沉细而数。査其先前所服之方，始而 九味羌活汤，继则服以黄连、梔子、连翘、黄芩、金银花、桑 叶、薄荷等未效。此系春温病误以辛温发散，又复苦燥清热， 耗伤真阴，邪热内蕴，转为少阴阴虚热化证。拟黄连阿胶鸡 子黄汤治之。 黄连10克，黄芩12克，杭白芍24克，阿胶10克（烊化 兑入），鸡子黄2枚。 先煎、连、芍药为汤，稍凉，兑入已悸化之阿胶，再搅入 生鸡蛋黄二枚和匀而服。 服一剂后即得安静熟寐，烦渴已止，唇舌转润，脉静身 凉。继以生脉散加生地黄、玄参、黄连。 米洋参10克，麦冬15克，五味子5克，甘草6克，黑玄 参10克，生地黄12克，黄连5克。 上方连进二剂而愈。":"Syndrome of spring febrile disease with Shaoyin heat transformation: Wu, a native of Kunming, lived in Xiuyi Street, Kunming City. His eldest son was 15 years old. He fell ill in March 1921 and had to wait for a medical examination. The fever persisted for 11 days. His face was red and his lips were red and burnt, his tongue was red and yellow with no fluid, and he was tired and could not lie down. Not eating, thirsty and liking cold drinks, short and red urine, indigestible stools, and a heavy, thready and rapid pulse. After checking the prescriptions he had taken before, he started with Jiuwei Qianghuo decoction, and then took coptis, gardenia, forsythia, skullcap, honeysuckle, mulberry leaves, mint, etc., but no effect. This is caused by spring-warm disease mistakenly expelling pungent warmth, returning to bitterness, dryness and clearing away heat, consuming true yin and damaging the evil heat, turning into a syndrome of Shaoyin yin deficiency and heat. Treat it with Coptidis Ejiao Chicken Zihuang Decoction. 10 grams of Coptis chinensis, 12 grams of Scutellaria baicalensis, 24 grams of white peony root, 10 grams of donkey-hide gelatin (blended and mixed), and 2 pieces of chicken rooster. First, decoct the glutinous rice and peony root into a soup, let it cool slightly, add the melted donkey hide gelatin, then stir in two raw egg yolks and mix well before taking it. After taking one dose, you will have a quiet and sound sleep, your polydipsia will have stopped, your lips and tongue will become moist, and your pulse will be calm and your body will be cool. Follow with Shengmai Powder and add Rehmannia glutinosa, Scrophulariaceae and Coptidis rhizome. 10 grams of Panax quinquefolius, 15 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 5 grams of Schisandra chinensis, 6 grams of licorice, 10 grams of Black Scrophulariaceae, 12 grams of Rehmannia glutinosa, and 5 grams of Coptis chinensis. The patient was cured after taking two doses in a row.","春温病表寒里热证 曾某，男，年二十岁，住四川省会理县南街":"Spring febrile disease with cold exterior and heat interior Zeng, male, 20 years old, lives in South Street, Huili County, Sichuan Province","春温病表寒里热证 曾某，男，年二十岁，住四川省会理县南街。于1920年2 月患春温病三日，脉来浮数，发热微恶寒，头疼体痛。面垢，唇 赤而焦，舌苔白而燥，尖绛，渴喜冷饮，小便短赤。此系春温病 邪热内壅,外有表邪闭束，遂成表寒里热之证，以麻黄杏仁甘 草石膏汤主之。 麻黄12克，生石膏30克（碎，布包），杏仁10克，甘草 6克。 服一剂后，俄而汗出淋漓，脉静身凉，霍然而愈。":"Spring febrile disease with cold exterior and heat interior Zeng, male, 20 years old, lives in South Street, Huili County, Sichuan Province. In February 1920, he suffered from spring febrile disease for three days. He had a floating pulse, fever, mild aversion to cold, headache and body aches. Stain on the face, red and burnt lips, white and dry tongue coating, sharp crimson, thirst for cold drinks, short and red urine. This is a syndrome caused by the evil heat caused by spring fever, which is blocked internally and blocked by external evils, resulting in cold exterior and heat inside. Ephedra, almond, licorice and gypsum decoction is the main treatment. 12 grams of ephedra, 30 grams of gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 10 grams of almonds, 6 grams of licorice. After taking one dose, I felt sweating profusely, my pulse was still and my body was cold, and I suddenly recovered.","春温病阳明经热证 王某，男，年廿五岁，住四川省会理县北关，于1920年2 月患温病已四日，前医以九味羌活汤加葛根、柴胡、紫苏叶等 与服之，服后汗出未解，发热更甚。延余诊视，病者壮热，恶热 而烦渴喜冷饮，头疼,但头汗出，面赤而垢,鼻干而喘,唇赤口 燥，苔黄而无津，小便短赤，大便三日不解。此系春温病误用 辛温发汗，耗伤阴液而成阳明经热之证，以人参白虎汤加麦 冬治之。 生石膏30克（碎，布包），知母20克，沙参15克，麦冬12 克，甘草6克，粳米10克。 连服二盏，竟仰卧而寐，数刻则全身大汗淋漓，热势渐 退。次日复诊烦渴已止，脉静身凉,继以生脉散加生地黄、杭 芍，一剂霍然。 沙参16克，麦冬13克，五味子5克，生地黄13克，杭白 芍13克，甘草6克。":"Spring Febrile Disease Yangming Meridian Heat Syndrome Wang, a 25-year-old male, lived in Beiguan, Huili County, Sichuan Province. He had been suffering from febrile disease for four days in February 1920. The former doctor took Jiuwei Qianghuo Decoction with kudzu root, bupleurum, perilla leaves, etc. After taking it, he sweated and the fever became worse. After further examination, the patient showed strong fever, aversion to heat, polydipsia and a preference for cold drinks, headache but with sweating head, red and dirty face, dry nose and breath, red lips and dry mouth, yellow coating and no fluid, short red urine, and undigested stool for three days. This is a syndrome caused by the misuse of pungent warm sweat in spring febrile disease, which consumes yin fluid and causes Yangming meridian heat. It can be treated with Ginseng Baihu Decoction plus Ophiopogon japonicus. 30 grams of raw gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 20 grams of Anemarrhena, 15 grams of Adenophora, 12 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 6 grams of licorice, and 10 grams of japonica rice. After taking two cups in a row, I fell asleep on my back. Within a few moments, I was sweating profusely and the fever gradually subsided. The next day's follow-up visit showed that the polydipsia had subsided and the pulse was quiet and the body was cool. Shengmai Powder was then added with Rehmannia glutinosa and Hangshao for one dose. 16 grams of adenophora, 13 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 5 grams of Schisandra chinensis, 13 grams of Rehmannia glutinosa, 13 grams of white peony root, and 6 grams of licorice.","春温病阳明经热证 王某，男，年廿五岁，住四川省会理县北关，于19…":"Spring febrile disease Yangming Meridian Heat Syndrome Wang, male, 25 years old, lives in Beiguan, Huili County, Sichuan Province. He died on 19...","晚年将其家传验方与临证心得公之于众，成《姚贞白医案》，为姚氏妇科传世之本。":`In his later years, he made his family's prescriptions and clinical experience public, and compiled "Yao Zhenbai's Medical Records", which is the foundation of Yao's gynecology.`,"晚年总结毕生针法心得，形成管氏针灸流派特色，为云南针灸学科发展奠定基础。":"In his later years, he summarized his lifelong acupuncture experience and formed the characteristics of Guan's acupuncture school, laying the foundation for the development of acupuncture in Yunnan.","晚年整理毕生儿科经验，为滇南儿科留下宝贵财富。":"In his later years, he compiled his lifelong experience in pediatrics and left a valuable legacy for the Department of Pediatrics in Southern Yunnan.",暂停:"pause","暑 证":"summer certificate","暑 证(一) 廖某，男，年三十一岁，四川省会理县人,住云南省昆明 市海潮巷八号":"Summer Certificate (1) Liao, male, 31 years old, from Huili County, Sichuan Province, lives at No. 8 Haichao Lane, Kunming City, Yunnan Province","暑 证(一) 廖某，男，年三十一岁，四川省会理县人,住云南省昆明 市海潮巷八号。1928年5月16日出外郊游，值酷暑炎热，畏 热贪凉，返家时临风脱衣，当晚觉闷热而思饮，全身倦怠违 和，次日则有微寒而发热,头昏痛，肢体酸困疼痛。因平素体 质较健，向少生病,对此小病不以为然。不日则热势突增，发 为壮热烦渴饮冷之证,小便短赤,食思不进,经西法针药施治未效，延余诊视。斯时病已三日，脉来浮弦而数，面赤唇红而 焦，舌红苔燥，肌肤皆热，但不见有汗，气息喘促，呻吟不已。 良由暑邪伤阴，邪热内壅,复被风寒闭束,膜理不通而成表寒 里热之证。法当表里两解，拟仲景麻黄杏仁甘草石膏汤辛凉 解表主之。 生麻黄12克，生石膏24克（碎，布包），杏仁10克，甘草 10克。 17日一剂，即汗出如洗，热势顿除，脉静身凉，头疼体痛 已愈。然表邪虽解，里热未清，仍渴喜冷饮，再剂以人参白虎 汤合生脉散培养真阴清解余热。 沙参24克，生石膏15克（碎，布包），知母12克，麦冬24 克，五味子3克，甘草6克，粳米10克。 服后渴止津生，食量增加，溺尚短赤，照上方去石膏加滑 石40克、生地黄40克。服后溺清而长，余热已尽，真阴复元， 诸证全瘳。按:昔人谓暑忌麻桂,其实亦不尽然。此证里热被表寒所束,非麻黄何能解表。妙在次方即转用白虎生脉,养阴清热，故而收效甚速。":"Summer Certificate (1) Liao, male, 31 years old, from Huili County, Sichuan Province, lives at No. 8 Haichao Lane, Kunming City, Yunnan Province. On May 16, 1928, I went out for an outing. In the scorching heat, I was afraid of heat and greedy for cold. When I returned home, I took off my clothes in the wind. I felt hot and stuffy that night and I wanted to drink. My whole body was tired and unnatural. The next day, I had fever due to slight cold, dizziness and pain, and soreness and pain in my limbs. Because he usually has a relatively healthy constitution, he rarely gets sick, and he doesn't take this minor illness seriously. After a few days, the heat suddenly increased, with symptoms of strong heat, polydipsia, and cold drinking, short red urine, and poor food and thinking. Western acupuncture treatment was ineffective, and further examination was delayed. I had been ill for three days. My pulse was stringy and rapid, my face was red and my lips were red and burnt, my tongue was red and dry, my skin was hot, but there was no sweat, my breath was short of breath, and I was moaning endlessly. Liang Yin is damaged by heat evil, and the evil heat is blocked internally, which is blocked by wind and cold, and the membrane is blocked, resulting in the syndrome of cold on the outside and heat on the inside. The method should be used to explain the exterior and interior. Zhongjing's ephedra, almond, licorice, and gypsum decoction is pungent and cool to explain the exterior. 12 grams of raw ephedra, 24 grams of raw gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 10 grams of almonds, and 10 grams of licorice. One dose on the 17th, the sweating will be as smooth as washing, the heat will be eliminated immediately, the pulse will be quiet, the body will be cool, and the headache and body aches will be cured. However, although the external evils have been resolved, the internal heat has not been cleared, and the patient is still thirsty and prefers cold drinks. Another dose is to use Ginseng Baihu Decoction and Shengmai Powder to cultivate the true yin to clear away the residual heat. 24 grams of Adenophora, 15 grams of gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 12 grams of Anemarrhena, 24 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 3 grams of Schisandra chinensis, 6 grams of licorice, and 10 grams of japonica rice. After taking it, thirst is relieved, food intake is increased, and the symptoms are still short and red. Take the above treatment to remove the plaster and add 40 grams of talc and 40 grams of raw rehmannia glutinosa. After taking it, the symptoms are clear and long-lasting, the residual heat has been exhausted, the true yin has recovered, and all symptoms have disappeared. Note: In the past, people said that Ma Gui should be avoided during summer heat, but this is actually not the case. In this syndrome, the internal heat is restrained by the external cold. How can it be relieved without ephedra? The wonderful thing is that the next step is to use White Tiger to generate pulses, nourish yin and clear away heat, so the effect is very fast.","暑 证（二） 甘某，男，年二十岁，云南姚安县人，住昆明市武成路":"Summer Certificate (2) Gan, male, 20 years old, from Yao'an County, Yunnan, living on Wucheng Road, Kunming City","暑 证（二） 甘某，男，年二十岁，云南姚安县人，住昆明市武成路。 体素健壮，1928年6月12日，值暑热天气，外出旅行，汗多 渴饮，因畏热贪凉,遂避暑休息于大树阴凉之下，汗出则腠理 疏泄，复被凉风吹袭,感冒而起病。初起即慷慷憎寒，口渴思 饮,头身不适,返家后渐次发热,渴饮更甚,头身疼痛，小便短 赤。延余诊视,脉来浮弦而数,面赤唇红，舌红而燥，良由酷暑 伤阴，邪热内壅，复被表寒闭束，騰理不通而成表寒里热之 证,拟仲景麻黄杏仁甘草石膏汤表里两解以治之。 生麻黄10克，生石膏24克（碎，布包），杏仁10克，甘草 10克。 13日复诊。服上方一剂后即汗出淋漓，发热退，头体疼 痛已愈，继以清热养阴之剂肃清余热，拟方人参白虎汤合生 脉散。 沙参20克，生石膏15克（碎，布包），知母12克，麦冬15 克，生地黄12克，甘草6克，粳米10克。 14日复诊。原已脉静身凉，今又身反灼热，渴饮更甚，唇 焦舌干而起芒刺，脉来洪数。何以服清热养阴之剂，病反沉 重,邪热更甚?是投药失宜,抑或余邪再燃?询及由来,病者三、 四日来大便不通，经亲友介绍服通便丸一包，内有巴豆温下 等药,服后大便虽泻通数次,但反而热势再张而成是状,始知 为错服温热丸药所致。当即急以人参白虎汤加重分量，并加 黄连、麦冬、玄参以清心肺之热而滋水生津，佐绿豆以解巴豆 之热毒。 土人参24克，生石膏36克（碎，布包），知母12克，黑玄 参12克，川黄连6克，麦冬21克，小绿豆15克，生甘草6 克，白粳米12克。 15日复诊。此方服后,尽然汗出热退，口津回生,舌苔芒 刺变软，小便色虽黄赤但已较长，脉沉细而带数象，手心尚 热，仍喜冷饮。此乃大病已退，邪热未净，真阴尚虚，再以养阴 生津而清余热治之。方用： 黑玄参12克，生地黄15克，麦冬15克，知母12克，沙 参15克，杭芍15克，石膏12克（碎，布包），小绿豆10克，甘 草6克。 16日复诊。脉已和缓，手心热退,渴饮止，津液满口，小便 清长,神食较增，继以生脉散加黄芪、当归、杭芍,两剂而痊。 沙参15克，麦冬12克，五味子3克，当归12克，黄跌24 克，杭芍12克，甘草6克。 甘某暑证痊愈后，随即介绍其同窗学友李某来诊。李亦 患暑证，病已六、七日，脉来浮洪，面赤多汗,壮热烦渴而喜冷 饮。唇焦舌红苔白而燥，食物不进，小便短涩而赤。曾服黄连、 黄芩、枳壳、梔子、连翘、薄荷、木通、滑石、董香、香需等药无 效。此系暑邪伤阴，津液枯燥，内热如焚，误服此等苦燥辛散 之剂,更增伤津耗液之弊。虽有苦寒之药夹杂其方,犹如杯水 无力以救车薪，遂拟人参白虎汤加味治之。 沙参24克，生石膏60克（碎，布包），知母12克，麦冬24 克，生地黄15克，玄参12克，杭芍12克，甘草6克，粳米12 克。 次日复诊。一剂后即汗出淋漓，邪热溃退，真阴来复，唇 舌较润，烦渴已减少，小便转长，但色仍赤。继以清暑解热，养 阴生津之法,原方加减主之。 沙参15克，石膏12克（碎，布包），麦冬12克，五味子3 克，知母10克，杭白芍12克，川贝母10克，竹叶5克，甘草6 •克。 上方服后，脉静身凉，舌润和，口津生，烦渴止，小便清 长，食量渐增，以生脉散加当归、杭芍、生地黄。连服二剂，邪 去正安，食增神健而愈。":"Summer Certificate (2) Gan, male, 20 years old, from Yao'an County, Yunnan, lives on Wucheng Road, Kunming City. The body is strong. On June 12, 1928, it was a hot summer day and he went out for a trip. He sweated a lot and was thirsty for water. Because he was afraid of heat and greedy for cold, he took shelter from the summer heat and rested under the shade of a big tree. When he sweated, his body was loosened, and he was hit by the cool wind again, which caused him to catch a cold. At the beginning, he felt aversion to cold, was thirsty and wanted to drink, and felt uncomfortable in his head and body. After returning home, he gradually became feverish, his thirst became even worse, he had pain in his head and body, and he had short and red urine. After diagnosis and examination, the pulse is stringy and rapid, the face is red, the lips are red, and the tongue is red and dry. The symptoms are due to the severe heat damaging the yin, and the evil heat causing internal blockage, which is blocked by the external cold, and the flow is blocked, resulting in the syndrome of external cold and internal heat. Zhongjing Ephedra, Almond, Licorice and Gypsum Decoction can be used to treat the problem. 10 grams of raw ephedra, 24 grams of raw gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 10 grams of almonds, and 10 grams of licorice. Follow-up visit on the 13th. After taking the above dose, you will sweat profusely, the fever subsides, and the pain in your head and body has healed. Then use a heat-clearing and yin-nourishing agent to clear away the residual heat, and the prescription of Renshen Baihu Decoction and Shengmai Powder is formulated. 20 grams of Adenophora, 15 grams of Gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 12 grams of Anemarrhena, 15 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 12 grams of Rehmannia glutinosa, 6 grams of licorice, and 10 grams of japonica rice. Follow-up visit on the 14th. The pulse had been quiet and the body was cool, but now the body is burning and the thirst is even worse. The lips are scorched and the tongue is dry and thorny, and the pulse is rapid and rapid. Why is it that after taking a heat-clearing and yin-nourishing agent, the disease becomes severe and the evil heat is even worse? Is it inappropriate to administer the medicine, or is the lingering evil rekindled? When asked about the reason, the patient has been unable to pass stools for three or four days. He was recommended by relatives and friends to take a pack of laxative pills, which contained Croton Wenxia and other medicines. Immediately increase the dosage with Ginseng Baihu Decoction, and add coptis, Ophiopogon japonicus, and Scrophulariaceae to clear away the heat in the heart and lungs, nourish water and promote body fluids, and add mung beans to relieve the heat and poison of Croton. 24 grams of native ginseng, 36 grams of raw gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 12 grams of anemarrhena, 12 grams of black scrophulariaceae, 6 grams of Coptis chinensis, 21 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 15 grams of small mung beans, 6 grams of raw licorice, and 12 grams of white japonica rice. Follow-up visit on the 15th. After taking this prescription, the sweating and fever subsided, the mouth and fluids returned to life, the tongue coating and prickles became soft, the urine was yellowish red but longer, the pulse was heavy and thin with several signs, the palms of the hands were still hot, and I still like cold drinks. This is because the serious disease has subsided, the evil heat has not been eliminated, and the true yin is still weak. It can be treated by nourishing yin and promoting fluid production to clear the remaining heat. Recipe: 12 grams of black scrophulariaceae, 15 grams of raw rehmannia glutinosa, 15 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 12 grams of Anemarrhenae, 15 grams of Adenophora adenophora, 15 grams of peony root, 12 grams of gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 10 grams of mung beans, and 6 grams of licorice. Follow-up visit on the 16th. The pulse has become gentle, the heat in the palms has subsided, thirst has been quelled by drinking, the mouth is full of body fluids, the urine is clear and long, and the spirit food has increased. After two doses of Shengmai Powder plus astragalus, angelica, and peony root, the patient recovered. 15 grams of Adenophora adenophora, 12 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 3 grams of Schisandra chinensis, 12 grams of Angelica sinensis, 24 grams of Huangdi, 12 grams of Hangshao, and 6 grams of Licorice. After Gan recovered from his summer syndrome, he immediately introduced his classmate Li to the clinic. Li Yi suffered from heat syndrome. He had been ill for six or seven days and had a rapid pulse, flushed face and excessive sweating. He had strong heat, polydipsia, and a preference for cold drinks. Burnt lips, red tongue, white and dry coating, inability to eat, short, astringent and red urine. I have taken Coptis chinensis, Scutellaria baicalensis, Citrus aurantium, Gardenia, Forsythia suspensa, Mint, Akebia, talc, Dongxiang, Xiangxu and other medicines but to no avail. This is due to the heat pathogen damaging the yin, drying up the body fluid, and causing internal heat to burn. If you mistakenly take these bitter, dry and pungent powders, it will increase the disadvantages of damaging the body fluid and consuming fluid. Although there were bitter and cold medicines mixed into the prescription, it was like a glass of water that could not save the car, so I added Ginseng Baihu Decoction to treat it. 24 grams of Adenophora, 60 grams of raw gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 12 grams of Anemarrhena, 24 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 15 grams of Rehmannia glutinosa, 12 grams of Scrophulariaceae, 12 grams of peony root, 6 grams of licorice, and 12 grams of japonica rice. Follow-up visit the next day. After one dose, you will sweat profusely, the evil heat will subside, the true yin will return, your lips and tongue will be moister, polydipsia will be reduced, and your urine will become longer, but the color will still be red. Following the method of clearing heat, relieving fever, nourishing yin and promoting fluid production, the original prescription is mainly added or subtracted. 15 grams of Adenophora, 12 grams of gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 12 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 3 grams of Schisandra chinensis, 10 grams of Anemarrhenae, 12 grams of white peony root, 10 grams of Fritillaria fritillary, 5 grams of bamboo leaves, and 6 grams of licorice. After taking the above medicine, the pulse is calm and the body is cool, the tongue is moist and mellow, the mouth is full of fluid, polydipsia is stopped, the urine is clear and long, and the food intake gradually increases. Take Shengmai Powder plus Angelicae Sinensis, Hangshao and Shengdihuang. Take two doses in a row, the evil will be eliminated, the body will be healthy, and the body will be healthy after eating.","暑证案 廖某，男，年31岁，四川会理县人":"Summer Certificate Case Liao, male, 31 years old, from Huili County, Sichuan","暑证案\\n廖某，男，年31岁，四川会理县人。1928年5月郊游，值酷暑炎热，畏热贪凉，返家时临风脱衣，当晚觉闷热而思饮，全身倦怠违和。次日则有微寒而发热，头昏痛，肢体酸困疼痛。不日则热势突增.发为壮热烦渴饮冷之症。小便短赤，食思不进.经西法针药施治未效，延余诊视。病已三日，脉来浮弦而数，面赤唇红而焦，舌红苔燥，肌肤皆热，但不见有汗，气息喘促，呻吟不已。良由暑邪伤阴，邪热内壅，复被风寒闭束，腠理不通而成表寒里热之证。法当表里两解，拟仲景麻杏甘石汤辛凉解表主之：生麻黄12g，生石膏24g（碎，布包），杏仁10g，甘草10g。	1剂即汗岀如洗，热势顿除，脉静身凉，头疼体痛已愈。然表邪虽解，里热未清，仍渴喜冷饮。再剂以人参白虎汤合生脉散培养真阴清解余热：\\n沙参24g，生石膏15g（碎，布包），知母12g，寸冬24g，五味子3g，甘草6g.粳米10g。\\n服后渴止津生，食量增加，溺尚短赤，照上方去石膏加滑石40g.生地40g，服后溺清而长，余热已尽，真阴复元，诸症全廖。\\n原按：昔人谓暑忌麻桂，其实亦不尽然。此证里热被表寒所束，非麻黄何能解表？妙在次方即转用白虎、生脉，养阴清热，故而收效甚速。\\n按：“此证里热被表寒所束”，不见有汗，虽有“暑忌麻桂”之说，仍不忌用麻黄，是为开表之设也。":'Summer Certificate Case\\nLiao, male, 31 years old, from Huili County, Sichuan. In May 1928, I went on an outing. In the scorching heat, I was afraid of heat and greedy for cold. When I returned home, I took off my clothes in the wind. I felt hot and thirsty that night and wanted to drink. My whole body was tired and unnatural. The next day, he had slight cold and fever, dizziness and pain, and limb aches and pains. After a few days, the heat suddenly increases and symptoms of strong heat, polydipsia, and cold drinking occur. Short and red urine, difficulty eating and thinking. Western acupuncture treatment was ineffective, and further examination was delayed. I have been ill for three days. My pulse is stringy and rapid, my face is red and my lips are red and burnt, my tongue is red and has dry coating, my skin is warm but there is no sweat, my breath is short of breath, and I moan incessantly. Yin is damaged by heat evil, evil heat is blocked internally, and it is blocked by wind and cold again, and the internal organs are blocked, resulting in the syndrome of cold on the outside and heat on the inside. The method is to explain both the exterior and interior. Zhongjing Maxing Ganshi Decoction is used to explain the pungent and cool nature of the exterior: 12g of raw ephedra, 24g of raw gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 10g of almonds, and 10g of licorice.	After 1 dose, sweating is as strong as washing, the heat is suddenly eliminated, the pulse is still and the body is cool, and the headache and body aches have been cured. However, although the external evils have been resolved, the internal heat has not been cleared, and the patient is still thirsty and prefers cold drinks. The next dose is to use Renshen Baihu Decoction and Shengmai Powder to cultivate Zhenyin and clear away residual heat: 24g of Adenophora adenophora, 15g of Gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 12g of Anemarrhena, 24g of Cundong, 3g of Schisandra chinensis, 6g of licorice, and 10g of japonica rice. \\nAfter taking it, thirst is quenched and body fluids are increased, food intake is increased, and the symptoms are still short and red. Remove the plaster and add 40g of talc and 40g of raw rehmannia root. \\nOriginal note: People in the past said that Ma Gui is taboo in summer, but this is actually not the case. In this syndrome, the internal heat is restrained by the external cold. How can it be relieved without ephedra? The wonderful thing is that the next prescription is to use Baihu, Shengmai, nourish yin and clear away heat, so the effect is very fast. \\nNote: "In this syndrome, the internal heat is restrained by the external cold." There is no sweating. Although there is a saying that "Ma Gui is contraindicated in summer," ephedra is not contraindicated. This is to open the exterior.',暑邪伤阴:"Summer evil damages yin","曾任云南中医学院院长，为云南中医高等教育殚精竭虑。":"He once served as the dean of Yunnan College of Traditional Chinese Medicine and devoted himself to the higher education of traditional Chinese medicine in Yunnan.",月经不调:"Irregular menstruation","月经不调、带下、不孕诸案。":"Irregular menstruation, vaginal discharge, and infertility cases.","月经不调以温经汤、桂枝茯苓丸随证化裁；不孕多从冲任虚寒、肝郁气滞论治，温养与疏泄并行，不专恃补益。":"Irregular menstruation can be treated with Wenjing Decoction and Guizhi Fuling Pills according to the syndrome; infertility is mostly treated with Chong Ren deficiency and cold, liver stagnation and qi stagnation. Warming and nourishing should go hand in hand with catharsis, without relying exclusively on tonics.","月经先期、后期、痛经、闭经验案。":"Cases of early and late menstruation, dysmenorrhea, and amenorrhea.",月经病:"menstrual disease","有案为证： 张某次子，生甫一岁，住会理县鹿厂街":"There is evidence in the case: Zhang’s second son, just one year old, lives in Luchang Street, Huili County","有案为证：\\n张某次子，生甫一岁，住会理县鹿厂街。1914年3月，患小儿惊风证，病颇危笃，三日来抽搐不已。余诊视之，指纹青黑透达三关，舌苔白滑，面唇青黯，闭目沉迷不省，时而手足拘挛抽掣，乳食不进，夜间发热，大便泄泻绿色稀粪。询及病由，患儿始因受寒感冒起病，初有发热咳嗽，大便溏泻。某医以清热解表药2剂，服后白昼身热见退，夜晚又复发热，咳、泻未止。继又拟消食清热药2剂，服后病不减，忽而风动抽搐。该医以为肝经风热，又以平肝驱风镇惊药2剂，病情反趋沉重而成是状。时病已十余日，按脉证病情诊察，良由小儿气血未充，脏腑娇嫩，不耐克伐。风寒初起，只须轻宣透表，其病当愈。乃误以清热之剂，又复以消食、平肝、驱风等法，元阳受损，正不胜邪，遂致寒痰内壅而成三阴虚寒之慢惊风证。病势已危重，若辞不治，实非我医者应尽之责，力主逐寒荡惊汤挽救之：\\n上肉桂6g（研末，泡水兑入），公丁3g，炮姜10g，白胡椒3g（捣），灶心土130g（烧红淬水，澄清后以水煎药）。\\n上方喂服2次，稍顷呕吐涎痰一小盏，风状略减，抽搐较轻，两眼已睁，目珠已能转动寻视。再喂1次，又吐涎痰盏许，风状已定，抽搐不再发作，咳嗽亦平，夜晚已不再发热。患儿父母见病已恢复，甚为欣慰，但见其子体质羸弱，认为宜培补脾胃，自拟理中地黄汤1剂喂服，殊料移时风动抽搐又起。余往视之，询问缘由，方知患儿大病虽有转机，然寒痰阴邪尚未逐尽，滋补过早，固必增邪，且有碍于阴邪外祛，寒痰内阻遂致慢风复作。病家始知误施补剂亦有弊端。余仍以逐寒荡惊汤并加附片15g，服后又吐涎痰盏许，畅泻酱黑色稀便2次，抽搐平息，且能吮乳，并闻啼声。照原方去胡椒、公丁，加砂仁6g，甘草6g，附片增至30g，煎汤频频喂服。2剂尽，诸症痊愈。":"There is evidence in the case: \\nZhang's second son was just one year old and lived in Luchang Street, Huili County. In March 1914, he suffered from infantile convulsions and became critically ill. He had convulsions for three days. Upon further examination, the patient's fingerprints were blue and black, reaching all three levels, the tongue coating was white and slippery, the face and lips were blue and dark, the eyes were closed and she was unconscious, and sometimes the hands and feet were spasmodic, unable to eat or drink, had fever at night, and had loose green stools. When asked about the cause of the disease, the child first fell ill due to cold, fever, cough, and loose stools. A certain doctor gave 2 doses of heat-clearing and superficial relieving medicine. After taking it, the body heat subsided during the day, but the fever recurred at night, and the cough and diarrhea did not stop. After taking 2 doses of digestion and heat-clearing medicine, the illness did not subside after taking it, and he suddenly developed wind and convulsions. The doctor believed that the liver meridian was wind-heat, so he prescribed 2 doses of liver-calming, wind-relieving and anticonvulsant medicine, but the condition became more severe and became the same. I had been ill for more than ten days, and upon examination based on pulse syndrome, it was found that the child's Qi and blood were not sufficient, and the internal organs were delicate and could not be deflated. When the wind-cold first arises, you only need to gently spread it through the skin, and the disease will be cured. By mistake, heat-clearing agents are used, and methods such as digestion, calming the liver, and expelling wind are used again. The original yang is damaged, and the righteousness cannot overcome the evil, causing cold phlegm to accumulate in the body, resulting in chronic convulsions with three yin deficiency and cold. The condition is critical, and if he refuses to cure it, it is really not the responsibility of our doctors. I strongly recommend Zhuhan Dangjing Decoction to save the patient: \\n 6g cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 3g male diced, 10g ginger, 3g white pepper (pounded), 130g Zaoxin soil (boil red, quench the water, clarify and then decoct the medicine in water). \\nThe patient was fed twice and after a while he vomited and vomited a small amount of sputum. The wind was slightly reduced and the convulsions were mild. His eyes were opened and he could move to look. After another feeding, he spitted out a small amount of phlegm again, the wind pattern was settled, the convulsions no longer occurred, the cough became subdued, and he no longer had fever at night. The patient's parents were very pleased to see that the child had recovered from the disease. However, seeing that their son was in a weak constitution, they thought it was appropriate to strengthen the spleen and stomach, and fed him a dose of Zhongdihuang decoction. However, unexpectedly, the wind and convulsions started again. I went to look at it and inquired about the reason, and found out that although the serious illness of the child had improved, the cold phlegm and yin evil had not been eliminated, and nourishing it too early would definitely increase the evil and hinder the external removal of yin evil, and the internal obstruction of cold phlegm would cause the recurrence of chronic wind. Patients are beginning to realize that misadministering supplements also has disadvantages. I still took Zhuhan Dangjing Decoction and added 15g of tablets. After taking it, I spit a lot of phlegm and had black and loose stools for 2 times. The convulsions subsided, and I could suck breasts and hear the cry. According to the original recipe, remove the pepper and male cubes, add 6g of amomum villosum, 6g of licorice, and increase the amount of fenugreek to 30g, decoct it and feed it frequently. After 2 doses, all symptoms were cured.","服使君子仁呃逆治验 张某，四川人，住昆明市，有子十岁，常患蛔虫腹…":"Fushi Junziren’s experience in treating hiccups. Zhang, a native of Sichuan, lives in Kunming City. He has a ten-year-old son who often suffers from roundworm abdomen...","服使君子仁呃逆治验 张某，四川人，住昆明市，有子十岁，常患蛔虫腹痛，面黄 肌瘦，纳呆食少，夜卧常口齿流涎。渠在药店购得使君子2市 两与子服食，意欲驱杀蛔虫，然不知该服何许剂量，随其子剥 去外壳而食之。因使君子仁，其味香甜,小儿子一日内服食达 一市两之多,遂发呃逆不止,连声频频而作,心泛欲呕而不思 饮食，无法止住，来舍向余求教。余思及早年从师习业，曾闻 师言，服使君子仁致呃逆作呕者，其壳可解。余当即介绍此法 以试之。渠返家后，照法用使君子外壳1市两煎汤与其子服, 连服数次，次日则呃逆顿除。按:使君子仁甘温入脾胃，常用以驱除蛔虫，多食则易致眩晕呃逆作呕，脾胃虚弱者尤甚，然使君子壳又可解之。此系民间单方效验，若遇此者，不妨一试。":"Experience of treating hiccups by taking Junziren. Zhang, a native of Sichuan, lives in Kunming City and has a 10-year-old son. He often suffers from roundworm abdominal pain, has a yellow face and thin muscles, has poor appetite and eats little, and often drools when lying down at night. He bought Shijunzi 2 Shiliang from a drugstore and took it with his son, hoping to drive away roundworms. However, he didn't know what dose to take, so he peeled off the outer shell of the drug and ate it with his son. Because of the sweet taste of Junziren, my younger son took as much as one liang in one day, and then he suffered from hiccups and frequent vomiting. His heart felt like vomiting and he did not think about food. He could not stop, so he came to ask me for advice. Yu Siji was studying as a teacher in his early years. He once heard the teacher's words and said that if a gentleman is benevolent and causes hiccups and vomiting, his shell can be broken. Yu immediately introduced this method to try it out. After he returned home, he took 1 liang of decoction of Zhijunzihuike to his son as prescribed. After taking it several times, the hiccups were cured the next day. Note: Junzi Ren is sweet and warm to the spleen and stomach, and is often used to expel roundworms. Eating too much can easily cause dizziness, hiccups and vomiting, especially in those with weak spleen and stomach. However, Junzi Keren can also be used to relieve this. This is a folk unilateral effect. If you encounter this, you might as well give it a try.","本卷录月经不调、带下、不孕诸案二十余则。戴氏治妇科善用经方化裁，调肝和血贯穿始终。":"This volume records more than twenty cases of irregular menstruation, vaginal discharge, and infertility. Dai's treatment of gynecology makes good use of classic prescriptions to regulate the liver and blood.","本卷收痰饮、水肿、胃脘痛、泄泻等内伤杂病治验四十余则，皆平正通达之治，而愈病之速出人意表。":"This volume collects more than forty treatments for internal injuries and miscellaneous diseases such as phlegm, edema, epigastric pain, diarrhea, etc. All of them are treated in a fair and accessible way, and the speed of recovery is unexpected.","本卷汇辑六经辨证验案三十余则，皆以经方起大症。案语简明，先叙证候，次出方药，末附转归与按语。":"This volume compiles more than 30 cases of differentiation and verification of the six classics, all of which use classic prescriptions to cause serious illnesses. The case is concise and concise. It first describes the symptoms and symptoms, then gives the prescriptions, and finally attaches the consequences and notes.","本卷载危急重症之果断处置与经方救逆验案，最见胆识，非学验俱丰者不能为。":"This volume contains the most courageous and courageous cases of decisive treatment of critical and severe cases and the rescuing cases of classic prescriptions, which cannot be done by those who are not knowledgeable and experienced.","本站所载医案与著作内容仅供学术研究与交流使用，不构成诊疗建议。":"The medical records and writings contained on this website are for academic research and communication purposes only and do not constitute diagnosis and treatment advice.","本章专论麻疹期饮食起居之宜忌，谓三分治疗、七分调护，护理得宜，则顺证可保，逆证可减。":"This chapter is dedicated to the dietary and daily taboos during the measles period. It is said to be three points of treatment and seven points of care. With proper care, normal symptoms can be ensured and negative symptoms can be reduced.","本章为读书临证随笔与门人问答录，信手拈来而医理自见，最见先生平日工夫。":"This chapter is a collection of clinical essays on reading and questions and answers from disciples. It is easy to pick up and the medical principles can be seen clearly, and the best is the teacher's daily work.","本章分初热期、见形期、收没期三期，详述顺证透发法度。初热期宣肺透表，见形期清热透疹，收没期养阴益气，三期井然不紊。":"This chapter is divided into three phases: the initial heat period, the visible period, and the withdrawal period, detailing the method of revealing the evidence. In the initial heat stage, it clears the lungs and penetrates the surface, in the visible stage, it clears away heat and penetrates the rash, and in the subsidence stage, it nourishes yin and replenishes qi. The three stages are in an orderly manner.","本章列中风急性期、恢复期、后遗症期完整针灸方案。管氏分期论治，法度谨严，不以一方一法概治全程。":"This chapter lists the complete acupuncture plan for the acute phase, recovery phase, and sequelae phase of stroke. Guan's treatment is divided into stages, and the laws are strict. He does not treat the whole process with one method and one method.","本章系统阐述戴氏方证对应临证心法，以桂枝汤、真武汤、柴胡类方为纲，逐一剖析主治证候与加减法度。":"This chapter systematically explains the clinical methods of Dai's prescriptions and syndromes, taking Guizhi Decoction, Zhenwu Decoction, and Bupleurum prescriptions as the outline, and analyzes the main syndromes and addition and subtraction methods one by one.","本章考镜源流，自《麻疹专书》以降历代论麻之说，辨析麻疹与时行温毒、天花之别，使学者先明其名实。":'This chapter examines the origins of the theories on measles in the past dynasties since the "Special Book on Measles", and analyzes the differences between measles, tepid poison, and smallpox, so that scholars can first understand its name and reality.',"本章规范进针、得气、补泻诸手法操作，为管氏针灸之根基，学者由此入门，庶几不误。":"This chapter standardizes the operations of acupuncture, qi-retaining, and tonifying and reducing techniques, which is the foundation of Guan's acupuncture. Scholars can get started with it without any mistakes.","本章论寒痹、热痹、顽痹之温针灸与刺络放血法。管氏治痹重在温通，谓痹者闭也、通则不痛。":"This chapter discusses the warm acupuncture and bloodletting methods for cold paralysis, heat paralysis and stubborn paralysis. Guan's treatment of paralysis focuses on warming and clearing it, which means that if the paralysis is closed, there will be no pain.","本章论疹陷、喘促、神昏诸危候之救逆，为全书之重心。吴氏谓逆证十之七八由误治而来，寒凉冰伏居其大半，可为临证者戒。":"This chapter discusses the treatment of rash, shortness of breath, and coma, which is the focus of the whole book. Wu said that seventy-eight out of ten adverse syndromes are caused by mistreatment, and cold and cold conditions occur in most of them, which can be a warning for those who are experiencing the syndrome.","本章论调经、种子、产后诸疾之经方化裁。戴氏谓女子以肝为先天、以血为用，治妇科不离调肝和血四字。":"This chapter discusses the prescriptions for regulating menstruation, seeds, and postpartum diseases. Dai said that women are born with the liver and use the blood, and the treatment of gynecology cannot be separated from the four words of regulating the liver and blood.","本章载痰饮、水肿、泄泻、消渴诸病治验。戴氏治内伤杂病首重脾胃，谓脾胃一伤、百病由生，脾胃一复、生机自旺。":"This chapter contains experiences in treating phlegm, edema, diarrhea, and thirst. Dai's treatment of internal injuries and miscellaneous diseases focuses primarily on the spleen and stomach. It means that once the spleen and stomach are injured, all diseases will arise, but once the spleen and stomach are restored, vitality will flourish.","本章述十二经筋、奇经八脉辨证取穴纲要。管氏针灸以经络辨证为先，谓宁失其穴、勿失其经，取穴必先明病在何经。":"This chapter describes the outline of syndrome differentiation and acupoint selection for the twelve tendons and eight extra meridians. Guan's acupuncture focuses on meridian syndrome differentiation, saying that it is better to lose its acupoints than to lose its meridians. When selecting acupoints, you must first understand where the disease is located.","本篇为吴氏最所擅场，论少阴阳虚寒化证与四逆、真武、麻附细辛诸方之运用，扶阳心法于此尽见。":"This article is Wu's best specialty, discussing the syndrome of Shaoyin and Yang deficiency and cold transformation and the application of Sini, Zhenwu, Mafu Xixin, and the method of supporting yang.","本篇录内科杂病、妇科调经、儿科痘疹验案四十余则，可见吴氏平脉辨证、随证治之的深厚功夫。":"This article records more than 40 cases of miscellaneous diseases in internal medicine, gynecological menstrual regulation, and pediatric acne, which shows Wu's profound skills in differentiating syndromes and treating them according to the syndrome.","本篇录温病、肝胃诸病验案。姚氏治温病善用轻清透达之品，谓治上焦如羽、非轻不举，药味少而分量轻，取其轻可去实。":"This article records the examination cases of febrile diseases, liver and stomach diseases. Yao makes good use of light, clear and clear medicines to treat febrile diseases, saying that it can treat burnt skin like a feather and is not light enough. The medicine has little flavor and light weight. Use the light medicine to remove the excess.","本篇收月经先期、后期、痛经、闭经诸验案。姚氏谓调经之要，首在理气，次在和血，气顺血和、经候自调。":"This article collects various empirical cases of early and late menstruation, dysmenorrhea, and amenorrhea. Yao said that the key to regulating menstruation is to regulate qi first and harmonize blood secondly.","本篇收麻疹、春温、暑温等时病验案三十余则。吴氏治温病不废温阳，谓温病亦有阳虚之体，透发全赖阳气，不可概以寒凉为能事。":"This article collects more than 30 cases of measles, spring fever, summer fever and other seasonal diseases. Wu's treatment of febrile diseases does not waste warm yang, saying that febrile diseases also have yang deficiency in the body, and the development of hair depends entirely on yang qi, and it cannot be said that cold and cool are the cure.","本篇汇辑戴阳、格阳、亡阳诸危候救逆验案二十余则。吴氏辨阴证重在脉舌与神气，谓阴证眼目，全在但欲寐、脉沉微、舌润不渴六字。":"This article compiles more than 20 cases of rescuing people from danger in Dai Yang, Ge Yang and Sui Yang. Wu's differentiation of yin syndrome focuses on the pulse, tongue and spirit. The yin syndrome of the eyes is all in six words: desire to sleep, deep and weak pulse, moist tongue but no thirst.","本篇讲解太阳病提纲、中风伤寒之别及桂枝、麻黄二汤之运用法度，旁及蓄水、蓄血诸兼变证，条分缕析。":"This article explains the outline of Taiyang Disease, the differences between stroke and typhoid fever, and the application methods of Guizhi and Mahuang decoctions, as well as the syndromes of water storage and blood storage, analyzed in detail.","本篇论不孕症从调经入手之治验与心悟。姚氏谓种子先调经、经调子自至，反对一味蛮补，蛮补则气血壅滞，反成障碍。":"This article discusses the experience and understanding of the treatment of infertility starting with menstrual regulation. Yao said that the seeds first regulate the menstruation, and the menstrual regulation will come naturally, and he is opposed to blindly tonic, which will cause qi and blood to be stagnant, which will become an obstacle.","本篇论阳明经证、腑证之辨及白虎、承气诸方之运用。吴氏谓阳明无死证，死皆死于失下，然亦申明可下不可下之辨，不以猛浪从事。":"This article discusses the Yangming Meridian syndrome, the differentiation of Fu-organ syndrome, and the application of Baihu and Chengqi prescriptions. Wu said that there was no death certificate for Yangming, and that all deaths were caused by falling. However, he also stated that there was no distinction between what could be done and what was not, and he would not engage in violent waves.","本篇载恶阻、胎漏、产后诸疾治验。姚氏安胎本胎气系于肾、养于脾、赖于血之旨，补肾健脾养血并行。":"This article contains experiences in treating obstruction, fetal leakage, and postpartum diseases. The purpose of Yao's anti-fetal medicine is that the fetal qi is tied to the kidneys, nourishes the spleen, and depends on the blood. It nourishes the kidneys, strengthens the spleen, and nourishes the blood.","本篇辨厥阴寒热错杂、厥热胜复之理，解乌梅丸、当归四逆汤诸方之奥义。厥阴为六经之末，证情最为复杂。":"This article differentiates the principles of Jueyin, cold and heat, the combination of Jueyin and heat, and explains the secrets of Wumei Wan and Danggui Sini Decoction. Jueyin is at the end of the six meridians and has the most complex symptoms.","本篇集吴氏用药心法，以附子、肉桂、吴萸、细辛诸温热药为主，旁及石膏、大黄等寒凉药的对证运用。":"This article collects Wu's method of using medicine, mainly focusing on warm and hot medicines such as aconite, cinnamon, Wuyu, and asarum, and the use of cold and cool medicines such as gypsum and rhubarb.",本草:"Materia Medica","本草之学贵在亲尝亲验，不徒以文献为据。":"The importance of learning herbal medicine lies in personal taste and experience, not just relying on literature as evidence.",本草方书:"Materia Medica","朱小弟，生甫两月，禀赋单薄":"Zhu Xiaodi is only two months old and has little talent.","朱小弟，生甫两月，禀赋单薄。因感风寒而病，身热咳嗽，不思乳食，多啼。医以清热解表之剂，热不退，发惊惕；又复以追风清热镇惊等法以治之，竟沉迷不乳，体若燔炭，自汗肢冷，咳嗽喘挣不已，痰声辘辘，时作角弓抽掣，奄奄一息。后延余诊之。指纹青黑透关，面唇均含青象，舌白而腻。此为风寒误治引邪入于阴分，阳不胜阴，虚阳浮越于外，法当扶阳驱寒。附片20g，炮姜6g，京夏6g，北辛2g，生麻茸2g，茯苓10g，甘草3g。\\n频频喂服，1剂尽，汗出，热退其半，已不发惊抽掣，喘咳减，始能吮乳。再剂病退七八。去麻、辛，又服2剂后，诸症悉除。":"Zhu Xiaodi is only two months old and has little talent. Sick due to wind and cold, body heat and cough, not wanting to eat or drink, and crying a lot. The doctor used medicine to clear away heat and relieve external symptoms, but the heat did not go away, causing panic and vigilance. He also tried to treat it with methods such as chasing wind to clear away heat and calm down the convulsions. However, he was addicted to milk, his body was like burning coal, spontaneous sweating and cold limbs, coughing and wheezing, phlegm, and sometimes twitching, and he was dying. The diagnosis was later postponed. The fingerprints are blue and black, the face and lips are blue, and the tongue is white and greasy. This is caused by incorrect treatment of wind and cold, which causes evil to enter the yin component. The yang cannot overcome the yin, and the deficient yang floats to the outside. The method should be to support the yang and drive away the cold. 20g of Futian, 6g of Paojiang, 6g of Jingxia, 2g of Beixin, 2g of raw sesame root, 10g of Poria, and 3g of licorice. \\nFeed frequently, after one dose is used up, sweating occurs, half of the fever subsides, twitching and twitching no longer occurs, wheezing and coughing subside, and then you can suck milk. After another dose, the disease will be cured by 70 to 80%. After removing the numbness and pungency, and taking 2 more doses, all symptoms were eliminated.",杂病验案:"Miscellaneous disease examination records","李某，男，32岁":"Li, male, 32 years old","李某，男，32岁。平素血压高，于1958年11月14日头昏重，跌仆昏倒，不省人事，家人急送其来诊。牙关紧闭，口眼㖞斜，痰涎壅盛，面白唇黯，四肢逆冷，脉弦滑。当即以上好肉桂10g开水泡服。服数次后，牙关即渐松，能张口咽药，人渐苏醒，但不能言，右半身不遂，右手足全不能动。\\n此系内体元阳过衰，又遇外邪侵袭，以致突然昏倒而成中风之证。以白通汤合三生饮加味主之：\\n生附片80g，生川乌80g，生南星20g，筠姜30g，葱头3茎，天麻10g，北细辛10g，上肉桂（研末，泡水兑入）l0g。附子、川乌、南星三味以开水先煨4小时。4剂。\\n二诊：口已能张，咽药已易，略能言语，但仍謇塞不明，左侧头疼，手足稍能活动。仍以上方加减：\\n附片200g，筠姜80g，上肉桂（研末，泡水兑入）15g，桂枝40g，川乌80g，北细辛10g，法半夏15g，羌活10g，麻黄10g，生草10g。4剂。\\n三诊：说话已清，右手足仍麻木痿软。调方：\\n附片200g，筠姜80g，天麻10g，伸筋草10g，五加皮10g，羌活6g，桂枝30g，北细辛10g，生草10g。4剂。\\n四诊：精神增，食量佳，足稍能行动而较慢，右手仍软。处方：\\n附片200g，白术20g，炙麻根20g，上肉桂（研末.泡水兑人）15g，砂仁8g，伸筋草10g，北细辛10g，生草10g。\\n五诊：右手已能举动，但尚软而无力，已能行走，说话已明八九，体质增强，面红润，舌亦红活。继服下方调理善后。\\n附片200g，天麻10g，桂枝30g，五加皮15g，上肉桂15g（研末，泡水兑入），伸筋草10g，石枫丹15g，北细辛10g，生草10g。（顾树华提供）\\n按：本例虽未提续命汤，但在白通汤合三生饮的基础上，选加麻黄、桂枝等开表之药，似含续命汤之意。":"Li, male, 32 years old. He usually had high blood pressure. On November 14, 1958, he became dizzy, fell down, and fell unconscious. His family rushed him to see a doctor. The teeth are closed, the mouth and eyes are slanted, the phlegm and saliva are blocked, the face is white and the lips are dark, the limbs are cold, and the pulse is stringy and slippery. Immediately soak 10g of the above good cinnamon in boiling water and take it. After taking it several times, the teeth gradually loosen and the person can open his mouth and swallow the medicine. The person gradually wakes up, but cannot speak. The right side of the body is paralyzed and the right hand and foot cannot move at all. \\nThis is a symptom of stroke caused by excessive decline of internal yang and invasion by external evils, resulting in sudden fainting. Combine Baitong Tang with Sansheng Drink and add the following: 80g of raw Aconite slices, 80g of raw Sichuan Wu, 20g of raw Nanxing, 30g of Junjiang, 3 stalks of green onion, 10g of Gastrodia elata, 10g of Asarum, and 10g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water). Simmer Aconite, Sichuan Aconite and Nanxing in boiling water for 4 hours. 4 doses. \\nSecond diagnosis: The mouth can be opened, swallowing medicine is easy, and the patient can speak a little, but the pain is still unclear, the left side has a headache, and the hands and feet can move slightly. Add or subtract from the above:\\n200g of attached slices, 80g of Junjiang, 15g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 40g of cassia twig, 80g of Aconite, 10g of Asarum, 15g of Pinellia, 10g of Qiang Huo, 10g of Ephedra, and 10g of raw grass. 4 doses. \\nThird diagnosis: Speech has become clearer, but the right foot is still numb and flaccid. Recipe: \\n200g Fu Pian, 80g Junjiang, 10g Gastrodia elata, 10g Shenjincao, 10g Acanthopanax bark, 6g Qianghuo, 30g Guizhi, 10g Asarum, and 10g raw grass. 4 doses. \\nFourth diagnosis: Increased energy, good food intake, slightly able to move but slowly, and the right hand is still soft. Prescription: \\n200g of Atractylodes, 20g of Atractylodes, 20g of Asarum root, 15g of Cinnamon (grind into powder and soak in water for mixing), 8g of Amomum villosum, 10g of Asarum, 10g of Asarum, and 10g of raw grass. \\nFifth diagnosis: The right hand can already move, but is still soft and weak. It can already walk, can speak clearly, has improved physical fitness, has a rosy face, and has a red and active tongue. Continue to take the lower part for conditioning and aftercare. \\n200g of attached piece, 10g of Gastrodia elata, 30g of cinnamon twig, 15g of Acanthopanax bark, 15g of cassia cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10g of Herba elata, 15g of Fengdan, 10g of Asarum, and 10g of raw grass. (Provided by Gu Shuhua)\\nNote: Although this example does not mention Xuanming Decoction, on the basis of Baitong Decoction and Sansheng Yin, the addition of ephedra, cassia twig and other prescribed medicines seems to imply the meaning of Xuanming Decoction.","李某，男，年四旬余":"Li, male, more than 40 years old","李某，男，年四旬余。患痰饮咳喘病已八九年，中西医屡治未愈。脉左弦右滑，两尺弱，心脉细短，肺脉滑大，按之则空；舌苔白滑而腻，面色青黯，目下浮起如卧蚕；咳痰气喘而短，胸闷痰滞，头疼目眩。食少无神，畏食酸冷，渴喜热饮而不多，小便短赤，咳时则遗；入夜难眠，行卧惟艰，值阴雨天寒尤甚。此由脾肾阳虚，饮邪内泛，上逆犯肺则作痰作咳；肾虚不纳，则短气喘息而遗溺；痰湿阻遏，清阳不升，浊阴不降，肺肾之气不相接，遂成痰饮咳喘之证。《金匮要略》曰：“病痰饮者，当以温药和之。”拟方小青龙汤加减主之：附片20g，北细辛4g，麻茸3g，干姜15g，法夏15g，五味子1.5g，甘草3g。\\n次日复诊：头疼、咳痰稍减，痰较易咯，乃照原方分量加倍。服后痰多咳吐如涌，胸闷减，喘息较平。2剂后，头痛若失，喘息平其大半。3剂后，稍能食，行卧已较轻便，唯痰多，气仍短，小便转长而色仍赤。盖湿痰饮邪得阳药运行，在上由咽喉气道而出，在下则随小便而去，乃病退之兆。仍照前方加减治之：\\n附片100g，北细辛10g，半夏10g，干姜40g，上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），茯苓30g，桂尖20g，五味子3g，甘草10g。\\n2剂后，喘咳平，痰已少。3剂后，胸闷气短均愈，饮食倍增，弦滑之脉已平，腻苔已退，唯精神未充。苓桂术甘汤加附子、口芪，连进10剂，遂得痊瘳。\\n附片150g，口芪30g，茯苓20g，桂尖20g，自术20g，甘草10g。\\n按：吴氏用小青龙汤加附子，减去白芍，意其碍阳。初诊方各药包括附子的剂量均系平剂小量；得效后，“乃照原方分量加倍”，附子一再加大剂量。":'Li, male, in his forties. He has been suffering from cough and asthma due to phlegm retention for 89 years, and has not been cured after repeated treatments with traditional Chinese and Western medicine. The pulse is stringy on the left and slippery on the right, weak in two feet, the heart pulse is thin and short, the lung pulse is slippery and large, and is empty when pressed; the tongue coating is white, slippery and greasy, the complexion is blue and gloomy, and the eyes are floating like lying silkworms; expectoration is short and short, chest tightness and phlegm stagnation, headache and dizziness. He eats less and lacks energy, is afraid of food that is sour and cold, is thirsty and likes hot drinks but not much, has short and red urine, which is passed out when coughing; it is difficult to sleep at night, and it is difficult to walk or lie down, especially when it is rainy and cold. This is caused by spleen and kidney yang deficiency, drinking evil internally, rising in opposition to the lungs, resulting in phlegm and coughing; kidney deficiency, shortness of breath, wheezing and drowning; phlegm and dampness blocking, clear yang does not rise, turbid yin does not fall, and the qi of the lungs and kidneys are not connected, resulting in phlegm, water retention, cough and asthma. "Jingui Synopsis" says: "Those who are sick and have phlegm should be treated with warm medicine." The proposed prescription of Xiaoqinglong Decoction is as follows: 20g of Fu Pian, 4g of Asarum, 3g of Asarum, 15g of dried ginger, 15g of Faxia, 1.5g of Schisandra chinensis, and 3g of licorice. \\nRevisited the next day: The headache and phlegm cough were slightly reduced, and the phlegm was easier to cough up, so the dosage of the original prescription was doubled. After taking it, the cough with excessive phlegm and vomiting is like gushing, the chest tightness is reduced, and the wheezing is less severe. After 2 doses, the headache disappeared and most of the wheezing subsided. After 3 doses, I can eat a little and can walk and lie more easily. However, I have a lot of phlegm, my breath is still short, and my urine becomes longer and still red in color. When dampness, phlegm and evil are absorbed, the yang medicine circulates. It comes out from the throat and airway at the top, and goes with the urine at the bottom, which is a sign of the disease retreating. Treat it as before with addition and subtraction: \\n100g of Fu Pian, 10g of Asarum, 10g of Pinellia ternata, 40g of dried ginger, 10g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 30g of Poria, 20g of Guijian, 3g of Schisandra chinensis, and 10g of licorice. \\nAfter 2 doses, the wheezing and cough subsided and there was less phlegm. After 3 doses, the chest tightness and shortness of breath were all cured, my diet doubled, my stringy and slippery pulse became smooth, and the greasy coating receded, but my energy was not yet full. Lingguishugan decoction plus aconite and qiqi was taken for 10 consecutive doses, and the disease was cured. \\n150g of Fu Pian, 30g of Orchid Qili, 20g of Poria, 20g of Guijian, 20g of Zishu, and 10g of Licorice. \\nNote: Wu used Xiaoqinglong Decoction plus aconite and subtracted white peony root, meaning that it hinders yang. The dosage of each medicine in the initial diagnosis prescription, including aconite, is a small, flat dose; after it is effective, "the dosage of the original prescription is doubled," and the dosage of aconite is increased.',李氏温病透解方:"Li's prescription for treating febrile diseases",李继昌:"Li Jichang","李继昌先生1890年生于昆明，早年攻举子业，后弃儒从医，深研叶、薛、吴、王温病诸家之说。":"Mr. Li Jichang was born in Kunming in 1890. In his early years, he worked in the medical field. Later, he abandoned Confucianism and became a doctor. He studied the theories of Ye, Xue, Wu and Wang about Wenbing.","李继昌，昆明人，精于温病与内科杂病。辨证细腻入微，用药轻灵见长，于滇中时疫之治多有建树。":"Li Jichang, a native of Kunming, specializes in febrile diseases and miscellaneous internal diseases. His syndrome differentiation is delicate and subtle, and he is good at using medicine lightly. He has made many achievements in the treatment of epidemic diseases in central Yunnan.",杏林传承:"Xinglin inheritance","杏林典籍 · 数字典藏":"Xinglin Classics · Digital Collection",杏林医案:"Cases","杏林医案 | 云南名医馆":"Xinglin Medical Records | Yunnan Famous Medical Center","杏林新事，传承纪闻。":"Xinglin new things, inherited records.","杏林新事，传承纪闻。记录云南中医药的当代动态、学术研讨与流派传承。":"Xinglin new things, inherited records. Record the contemporary trends, academic discussions and school inheritance of traditional Chinese medicine in Yunnan.","条文与验案互证，学以致用":"Provisions and case verification mutually prove each other and apply what you have learned","来自全国的扶阳学派学者齐聚昆明，围绕吴佩衡先生“阳主阴从”学术思想与附子临床应用展开研讨。":`Scholars of the Fuyang School from all over the country gathered in Kunming to conduct discussions around Mr. Wu Peiheng's academic thought of "yang dominates and yin follows" and the clinical application of Aconite.`,查看更多:"View more",查看详情:"View details","柴胡15g，郁金12g，白术20g，茯苓25g，当归15g，白芍20g，太子参20g，垂盆草30g，炒麦芽30g":"Bupleurum 15g, Turmeric 12g, Atractylodes 20g, Poria 25g, Angelica sinensis 15g, White peony root 20g, Radix Pseudostellariae 20g, Atractylodes sinensis 30g, Fried malt 30g","桂枝汤、真武汤、柴胡类方之运用法度。":"Methods for using Guizhi Decoction, Zhenwu Decoction, and Bupleurum decoction.",案:"case","案中处处以脾胃为念，温中、化饮、和胃、健脾诸法运用裕如，于平淡方中见神奇。":"The spleen and stomach are taken into consideration throughout the case, and all the methods of warming the body, transforming Yin, harmonizing the stomach, and strengthening the spleen are used fluently, and magic can be seen in ordinary prescriptions.","案中每见误用寒凉而致阴阳离决者，吴氏辄以大剂四逆、白通、通脉四逆力挽狂澜。附子用量自一两递增至半斤，必嘱久煎去麻，且详载服药后烦躁、鼻衄等反应为阳回佳兆，非深明药性者不能下此断语。":"Whenever she saw cases where the misapplication of cold and cool substances caused separation of yin and yang, Wu would always turn the tide with large doses of the Four Nis, Baitong, and Tongmai Sini. The dosage of aconite is increased from one liang to half a catty, and it must be decoctioned for a long time to remove the numbness. It is also stated in detail that reactions such as irritability and epistaxis after taking the medicine are good signs of yang return. Those who do not understand the properties of the medicine cannot make this conclusion.",'案中虽分科论治，而辨证之理一贯，吴氏所谓"万病不离六经，万治不离阴阳"者，于此篇可证。':`Although the cases are divided into different disciplines, the principles of syndrome differentiation are consistent. Wu's saying that "all diseases are inseparable from the six meridians, and all treatments are inseparable from yin and yang" can be proved in this article.`,"案中见其顾护阴液之用心，凡用香燥理气，必佐养阴和胃之品，防其劫伤肝阴，此大家之法度也。":"In the case, we can see his intention to protect the yin fluid. Whenever he uses aromatic drying to regulate qi, he must supplement it with products that nourish yin and stomach to prevent it from damaging the liver yin. This is the law of everyone.",检索:"Search","此卷未载 · 页面未找到":"This volume is not loaded · Page not found",'此部体例与前两卷略异，每药先列毒性反应，次述炮制，再述主治，末附解毒之法，示人以谨慎之意，无愧乎"毒药"之名。':'The format of this volume is slightly different from that of the first two volumes. The toxic reactions of each medicine are listed first, followed by the preparation, and then the main treatments. The detoxification method is not included at the end, showing people to be cautious, and it is worthy of the name of "poison".',"每方之下先列仲景原文，次述辨证眼目，再附本人验案，层层递进，最便初学。":"Under each formula, Zhongjing's original text is listed first, followed by a description of the eye for syndrome differentiation, and then a personal verification of the case, which is advanced step by step, most convenient for beginners.","每期均列主方加减示例，用药轻清灵动，以桑、蝉、升、葛之属宣透为常法，使邪有出路而正不受伤。":"Each issue lists examples of additions and subtractions of the main prescriptions. The use of medicine is light, clear and flexible, and the attributes of mulberry, cicada, sheng and kudzu are used as a regular method, so that the evil can have a way out and the good will not be hurt.","每案末附按语，或辨疑似，或论药量，或诫误治，扶阳心法尽在其中。学者合案与按语互参，自可得其心传。":"There are notes at the end of each case, either to identify suspicions, to discuss the dosage of medicine, or to warn against mistreatment, all of which contain the Yang-supporting method. Scholars can combine the case and the notes to get their own personal biography.","每案辨证眼目分明，方证对应清晰":"Each case has a clear eye for syndrome differentiation and clear correspondence between prescriptions and syndromes.","每案附按语，揭示辨证眼目":"Notes are attached to each case to reveal the eye for diagnosis","每药之下必附民间验方一二首，用药多不过四五味，取其简便易行，山乡村寨皆可自疗。此山草部之体例也。":"Each medicine must be accompanied by one or two folk prescriptions. There are no more than four or five medicinal herbs. They are simple and easy to use and can be used for self-treatment in villages and villages. This is the style of Shancao Department.","毒草部收附子、草乌、雪上一枝蒿等毒烈之品二十余种。兰茂再三申明毒药治病、中病即止之旨，于炮制、用量、禁忌三事言之尤详。":"The poisonous weed department contains more than 20 kinds of poisonous and powerful products, such as aconite, Aconite, and Artemisia on snow. Lan Mao repeatedly stated the purpose of using poison to cure diseases and stop the disease immediately, and was particularly detailed in the preparation, dosage, and contraindications.","民航局长自筹附子 1965年，北京民航局局长赵某，来请吴老诊病":"The director of the Civil Aviation Administration of China raised Fuzi himself. In 1965, Zhao, the director of the Beijing Civil Aviation Administration, came to ask Mr. Wu to diagnose his illness.","民航局长自筹附子\\n1965年，北京民航局局长赵某，来请吴老诊病。赵局长患风湿关节炎疼痛数年，在北京曾请多位著名中西医诊治，服过中西药，效验不显，特慕名远道而来请吴老为治。患者来时拄手杖上楼，步履艰难，须赖护理人员搀扶。吴老诊后说：须用大量附子配方为治。但当时昆明药材公司川附片供应紧缺，难以大量买到。赵局长回答说：我可以到成都购买。买回一小布袋约5000g。吴老说：可以够用了。于是开始治疗。用川附片配方，从60g开始，复诊又加至90g，再加到120g为止。一共煎服了近30剂。患者上楼到吴老客厅，已经不必拄手杖，也不必要人搀扶而获愈。（《著名中医学家吴佩衡诞辰一百周年纪念专集》）":`The director of the Civil Aviation Administration raised his own money\\nIn 1965, Zhao, director of the Beijing Civil Aviation Administration, came to ask Mr. Wu for diagnosis. Director Zhao had been suffering from rheumatoid arthritis pain for several years. He had been treated by many famous Chinese and Western medicine doctors in Beijing. He had taken Chinese and Western medicines, but the effect was not obvious, so he came all the way to see Mr. Wu for treatment. When the patient arrived, he used a cane to go upstairs and had difficulty walking. He had to rely on the support of nursing staff. After diagnosis, Mr. Wu said: A large amount of aconite formula should be used to treat it. However, at that time, Kunming Medicinal Materials Company was in short supply of Chuanfu Tablets and it was difficult to buy them in large quantities. Director Zhao replied: I can go to Chengdu to buy it. I bought a small cloth bag worth about 5000g. Mr. Wu said: It is enough. So treatment began. Use the Chuanfu Tablet formula, start with 60g, increase to 90g during follow-up visits, and then increase to 120g. I took nearly 30 doses in total. The patient went upstairs to Mrs. Wu's living room and recovered without the need for a cane or support. ("Special Collection Commemorating the 100th Anniversary of the Birth of Famous Chinese Medicine Scientist Wu Peiheng")`,气虚不摄:"Deficiency of Qi",气虚便秘:"Qi deficiency and constipation","气虚便秘 张某，男，三十二岁，昆明人,患便秘证已一年余":"Constipation due to Qi deficiency Zhang, male, 32 years old, from Kunming, has been suffering from constipation for more than a year.","气虚便秘 张某，男，三十二岁，昆明人,患便秘证已一年余。初起大 便难解，凡二、三日一行，干结不爽。头昏食少，院腹痞闷不 适,时常啰气上逆，冲口而出。医者以为阴虚肠燥，胃腑有热， 连续治以清热苦寒、滋润通下之剂。每服一剂，大便通泻一 次，其后又复秘结如故，脫腹痞闷终不见减。如此往复施治数 月之久，愈见便秘，甚者六、七日始一行。口苦咽干纳呆食减， 体瘦面黄，精神倦怠。余诊其脉，沉迟而弱，舌苔厚腻,色黄少 津，口气微臭，思饮不多。如此并非肠胃燥热之证，乃是气虚 之便秘。因长期服用苦寒通下之品，脾肾之阳受戕，睥气虚 弱，无力运化，肾气不足,难以化气生津,气机壅滞，胃肠传化 失司，遂成便秘。当以温下之法，务使枢机运转，腑气自能通 达。方用温脾汤加味。 附片45克，大黄9克（后放），明党参15克，厚朴9克， 杏仁9克（捣），干姜12克，甘草6克。 煎服一次后，则腹中肠鸣，气窜胸胁，自觉欲转矢气而不 得。再服二次,则矢气频作,便意迫肛，旋即解出大便许多,干 黑硬结如栗，其臭无比。顿觉腹中舒缓，如释重负，呕啰已不 再作。连服二剂后，大便隔日可解。口苦咽干已愈，食思转佳， 腹中痞胀消去。厚腻黄苔已退，呈现薄白润苔，脉仍沉缓。遂 照原方加肉桂9克增其温化运转之力，连服四剂后，大便通 调如常，精神、饮食明显好转,面色呈润泽。为巩固疗效，继以 吴茱萸汤加肉桂、甘松温中健胃，调理二十余日，并瞩其常服 桂附理中丸。三年后相遇，询及便秘之证已痊愈，迄今未复 发。":"Constipation due to qi deficiency Zhang, male, 32 years old, from Kunming, has been suffering from constipation for more than a year. It is difficult to pass stool at the beginning, and every second or third day, the stool becomes dry and constipated. Dizziness, eating less, abdominal pain and discomfort, and rales often coming out of the mouth. Doctors believe that there is yin deficiency, dryness of the intestines, and heat in the stomach and intestines, and the patient is treated with an agent that clears away heat, bitter cold, and moisturizes the lower intestines. After taking one dose, the patient had diarrhea once, and then the constipation returned to the same state, and the abdominal distension and tightness did not subside. After several months of repeated treatment, constipation became more and more frequent, and constipation only started to occur on the sixth or seventh day. Bitter mouth, dry throat, indigestion, decreased appetite, thin body, yellow face, and mental fatigue. I checked the pulse, which was slow and weak, the tongue coating was thick and greasy, yellow in color and less fluid, the breath was slightly smelly, and the urge to drink was not much. This is not a sign of gastrointestinal dryness and heat, but constipation due to Qi deficiency. As a result of long-term use of bitter and cold products, the yang of the spleen and kidneys will be suppressed, resulting in weak Qi and inability to transport and transform. Insufficient kidney Qi makes it difficult to transform Qi and produce fluid, resulting in stagnation of Qi machinery and loss of gastrointestinal transmission, resulting in constipation. The method of warming should be used to make the cardinal organs move, so that the fu qi can flow naturally. Use Wenpi Decoction to add flavor. 45 grams of Aconite slices, 9 grams of rhubarb (put later), 15 grams of Codonopsis pilosula, 9 grams of Magnolia officinalis, 9 grams of almonds (pounded), 12 grams of dried ginger, and 6 grams of licorice. After taking the decoction once, there will be bowel rumbling in the abdomen, qi rushing to the chest and side, and the conscious desire to turn the qi away cannot be achieved. After taking it for a second time, the qi will flow frequently and the anus will be forced, and soon the stool will be large, black and hard as chestnuts, and the smell is extremely bad. Suddenly I felt soothed in my stomach, relieved, and the vomiting no longer occurred. After taking two doses, the stool will be relieved the next day. The bitterness in the mouth and dry throat have improved, the appetite has improved, and the abdominal distension has disappeared. The thick and greasy yellow coating has receded, and the coating appears thin and white, and the pulse is still slow. Then I added 9 grams of cinnamon according to the original prescription to increase its warming and circulation power. After taking four doses, my bowel movement became normal, my energy and diet improved significantly, and my complexion became moist. In order to consolidate the curative effect, the patient was treated with Evodia Fructus Decoction plus cinnamon and nard to warm the stomach and strengthen the stomach for more than 20 days. He was also prescribed Guifulizhong Pills regularly. We met three years later and was informed that the constipation had been cured and has not recurred so far.","气虚便秘案 刘某，年过六旬":"Case of Qi deficiency and constipation: Liu, over sixty years old","气虚便秘案\\n刘某，年过六旬。病已月余，咳嗽哮喘而多痰。腹胀且痛，不思食，大便秘结20日不更衣，小便赤而长，喜热饮，夜难入寐，精神极弱。六脉沉迟无力，舌苔白腻。查前所服方药，均以清热消食降气为主，且以硝、黄峻剂通下，仍不能便，其势较危。此系脾肾阳虚，中土失运，痰湿水饮阻逆于肺，清肃不降，致痰喘咳嗽，传导失司，无力输送。加之阳虚则气不化津，无以滋润肠道，致成气虚寒凝之便秘不通。宜扶阳温化主之，拟真武汤加味：附片100g，茯苓30g，白术20g，杭芍10g.干姜30g，北细辛6g，五味子5g。\\n1剂见效，2剂后喘、咳约去十之六七。3剂照原方去杭芍，服后痰喘咳嗽若失，略进饮食。第3日以四逆汤加茯苓、上肉桂、砂仁、北芪：\\n附片l00g，干姜50g，茯苓50g.砂仁10g，上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），北芪60g。\\n上方服1剂后，是晩便意迫肛，解出干结黑色粪便半痰盂	许，腹中顿觉舒缓。然因年老气虚，解便时用力过盛，旋即昏晕不省人事。急诊之，气短欲绝，脉沉迟无力，但见白苔已退，唇舌已转红润，此乃气虚下陷之故。当即以煎好之汤药喂服，俄顷人事已省，脉转有神。原方连服3剂，食增神健，咳喘不作，二便通达。\\n按：此证咳喘而兼便秘，用真武汤加姜、辛、五味，自是仲圣成法。唯虽见便秘“20日不更衣”，仍不予硝、黄攻下，是因其属寒凝便结，故予大剂姜、附温通化结，治之但扶其真元，一剂而“解出干结黑色粪便半痰盂许，腹中顿觉舒缓”，确显扶阳心法。":`Case of Qi deficiency and constipation\\nLiu, over sixty years old. I have been ill for more than a month and have cough, asthma and excessive phlegm. Abdominal distension and pain, no desire to eat, constipation, not changing clothes for 20 days, red and long urine, liking hot drinks, difficulty falling asleep at night, and extremely weak energy. The six pulses are slow and weak, and the tongue coating is white and greasy. The prescriptions taken before the examination were all aimed at clearing away heat, digesting and lowering qi, and even though the patient was still unable to defecate after taking saltpetre and Huangjun agents, the condition was dangerous. This is due to the deficiency of spleen and kidney yang and the loss of earth in the middle. The phlegm-dampness and water drinking are blocked by the lungs and cannot be purified, causing phlegm, wheezing and coughing, loss of conduction, and inability to transport. In addition, when Yang is deficient, Qi cannot transform into body fluids and cannot moisten the intestines, resulting in constipation and obstruction due to Qi deficiency, coldness and coagulation. It is suitable to focus on Fuyang warming, and add the following flavors: 100g Fuyang, 30g Poria, 20g Atractylodes, 10g Hangshao, 30g dried ginger, 6g Asarum, and 5g Schisandra chinensis. \\nOne dose is effective, and after two doses, the wheezing and coughing are about 60 to 70% gone. Take 3 doses of the original prescription to remove the peony root. If the phlegm, wheezing and cough disappear after taking the medicine, add a small amount of food. On the 3rd day, add poria cocos, cinnamon, amomum villosum, and astragalus to Sini decoction:\\n100g of Fu Pian, 50g of dried ginger, 50g of poria, 10g of amomum, 10g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water), and 60g of astragalus. \\nAfter taking 1 dose of the above, I felt my anus was pressed in the evening, about half a cup of dry and black feces was released, and I suddenly felt relieved. However, due to his old age and weak energy, he exerted too much force when defecating, and soon became faint and unconscious. In emergency, shortness of breath, slow and weak pulse, but the white coating has receded and the lips and tongue have turned red, this is due to qi deficiency and depression. Immediately take the boiled decoction and take it. Within a short time, you have been relieved and your pulse has improved. After taking 3 doses of the original prescription, food will increase your mental health, your cough and wheezing will stop, and your bowel movements will be clear. \\nNote: For this syndrome, cough and asthma combined with constipation, use Zhenwu Decoction with ginger, pungent, and five flavors, which is Zhongsheng's method. Although constipation was seen and "did not change clothes for 20 days", the patient was still not treated with saltpetre or Huang because it was caused by cold condensation. Therefore, a large dose of ginger was given to warm the constipation and relieve the constipation. The cure was to strengthen the essence. One dose "resolved half of the phlegm of dry black feces, and the abdomen suddenly felt soothing", which is indeed a method of supporting yang.`,"气血不调，营卫失谐,":"Imbalance of qi and blood, imbalance of camp and body,","气血素亏，阴阳不相为守":"Qi and blood elements are deficient, and yin and yang do not maintain each other.",水肿:"Edema",汉族:"Han nationality","汤某，28岁":"Tang, 28 years old","汤某，28岁。1938年正月，患中风不语，半身不遂，西法曰“脑充血”。唇焦舌缩，不省人事，奄奄一息。延某大博士诊视，断定无救，未拟方而去。延余诊视，仍以旧的理论，判断病源，以三生饮、续命汤、白通四逆汤加减配合，旬余痊愈，此症经余治愈颇多，以后详载。（《驳冯友兰论中西医药》）\\n按：本例虽未列出具体药物，但明确提出用续命汤，确系该病良方。孙思邈云：“卒中风欲死，不醒人事，口眼喝斜，半身不遂，言塞不能语，亦治风湿痹痛。夫风为百病之长，诸急卒病多是风，宜速与续命汤。”力主中风卒发选用本方。":`Tang, 28 years old. In the first month of 1938, he suffered a stroke that left him speechless and hemiplegic. Westerners called him "cerebral congestion". His lips were burnt, his tongue was shrinking, he was unconscious and dying. Doctor Yan examined the patient and concluded that it was hopeless, so he left without formulating a prescription. After more than ten days of diagnosis and examination, I still used the old theory to determine the cause of the disease. I used Sanshengyin, Xuming Decoction and Baitong Sini Decoction with a combination of additions and subtractions, and I was cured in more than ten days. There are many cures for this disease after menstruation, which will be detailed later. ("Refutation of Feng Youlan's Theory of Chinese and Western Medicine")\\nNote: Although this example does not list specific drugs, it is clearly stated that Xuming Decoction is a good prescription for this disease. Sun Simiao said: "Stroke is like death, unconsciousness, mouth and eyes are slanted, hemiplegia, and speech is blocked. It can also treat rheumatism and arthralgia. Wind is the common cause of all diseases, and most of the acute stroke diseases are wind. It is advisable to take Xuanming Decoction." He strongly recommends using this prescription for stroke.`,"治上焦如羽，非轻不举；用药轻清灵动，忌早投寒凉冰伏。":"Treating Jiao Ru Yu should not be done lightly; the medicine should be used lightly, clear and flexible, and it is avoidable to put it in the cold and ice in the early stage.","治咳喘重在宣降肺气、化痰顺气，兼以健脾杜痰之源。":"The treatment of cough and asthma focuses on dispersing and lowering lung qi, resolving phlegm and smoothing qi, and also strengthening the spleen and eliminating the source of phlegm.",泄泻:"diarrhea","注重“因地制宜”，开地域本草之先河":'Pay attention to "adapting measures to local conditions" and pioneer regional herbal medicine',泰:"Thailand","活人无算，乡里称颂":"A living person has no calculation, and the villagers praise him","活儿无算，乡里称颂":"Work is futile, praised by the villagers",流派:"genre",消化科:"Gastroenterology","消渴分上中下三消而以肾气丸收功，谓苦寒泻火仅可暂用，久服必损中阳，反致缠绵不愈。":"It is divided into upper, middle and lower three eliminations for quenching thirst, and Shenqi Pills are used to complete the function. It is said that bitter cold and purging fire can only be used temporarily. Taking it for a long time will damage the middle yang and cause lingering lingering.","清热解毒，活血祛风，养肝润肺，滋燥生津":"Clear away heat and detoxify, activate blood circulation and dispel wind, nourish liver and lungs, nourish dryness and promote body fluids","清透卫气，解毒生津":"Clear and healthy Qi, detoxify and promote body fluids",温热病:"febrile disease",温病:"febrile disease","温病、肝胃诸病之验案。":"Examination of febrile diseases, liver and stomach diseases.","温病与妇科互参，产后、经期感邪每仿温病立法而化裁。":"Febrile diseases and gynecology are closely related, and pathogenic factors after childbirth and menstruation are often eliminated by imitating febrile diseases legislation.",温病学派:"febrile disease school",温病学派滇中代表:"Representative of central Yunnan school of febrile disease school",温病篇:"Febrile Diseases","温病辨证以卫气营血为纲，重“透邪外达”，不令邪气内陷。":'Syndrome differentiation of febrile diseases is based on the principle of protecting qi and nourishing blood, emphasizing on "penetrating evil and spreading it outward", and preventing evil qi from sinking in.',"温针灸、刺络放血等手法操作规范":"Operating instructions for warm acupuncture, pricking and bloodletting",温阳化气利水:"Warming yang, transforming qi and diluting water",温阳托透法开麻疹治法之新境:"The Wenyang Tuopu method opens up a new realm of measles treatment","湿 疹":"Eczema","湿 疹 李某，女，二十五岁，广东人，大学教师，住昆明市":"Eczema Li, female, 25 years old, Cantonese, university teacher, living in Kunming","湿 疹 李某，女，二十五岁，广东人，大学教师，住昆明市。身体 健康，向少生病，1965年4月，赴滇南某化肥厂出差，当地气 候炎热，暑湿氤氲。某日下班出厂，迎面微风吹拂而来，顿觉 面部烘热，身发寒噤。次日颜面皮肤细密丘疹遍起，皮肤嫌 红，绷紧灼热，奇痒难忍。工厂医务所诊断为“过敏性湿疹”， 给服盐酸苯海拉明及静脉注射葡萄糖酸钙等治疗,面部痒疹 未退，于两肘弯处又复发生，稍轻拭则有清淡黄水渗出，夜间 作痒尤甚，眠食不安。5月1日回昆明，来舍就诊于余。脉浮 缓,舌淡苔薄白，此气血不调，营卫失谐,受暑湿之气熏腾,复 为风邪所感，发为湿疹。法当调和营卫、疏风除湿固表主之， 方用桂枝汤玉屏风散合方加味。 黄芪30克，防凤15克，白术20克，桂枝20克，杭白芍 10克，蝉蜕5克，红毛五加10克，刺疾藜10克，广蛇床10 克，生姜3片，大枣3枚，甘草10克。 不日返回该厂，照方煎服二剂而愈，此后未再复发。":'Eczema Li, female, 25 years old, from Guangdong, university teacher, lives in Kunming. He was in good health, but Xiang Shao fell ill. In April 1965, he went on a business trip to a fertilizer factory in southern Yunnan. The local climate was hot and humid. One day when I left the factory after get off work, I was greeted by a gentle breeze. My face suddenly felt hot and my body felt chilly. The next day, the skin on the face was covered with fine papules, the skin was red, tight, burning, and itched unbearably. The factory clinic diagnosed it as "allergic eczema" and treated it with diphenhydramine hydrochloride and intravenous injection of calcium gluconate. However, the facial itching did not go away and recurred in the elbow bends. Light yellow water oozed out after a slight swab. The itching was especially severe at night, causing restlessness in sleeping and eating. I returned to Kunming on May 1st and came to Sheshe for medical treatment. Floating and slow pulse, pale tongue with thin white coating, imbalance of qi and blood, imbalance of qi and health, inflamed by heat-damp qi, combined with wind evil, leading to eczema. The method is to harmonize Yingwei, dispel wind, remove dampness and solidify the surface. Use Guizhi Decoction and Yu Pingfeng Powder to add flavor. 30 grams of astragalus, 15 grams of Fangfeng, 20 grams of Atractylodes, 20 grams of cinnamon twigs, 10 grams of white peony root, 5 grams of cicada slough, 10 grams of eleuthero, 10 grams of tribulus terrestris, 10 grams of snake bed, 3 slices of ginger, 3 jujubes, and 10 grams of licorice. He returned to the factory the next day and recovered after taking two doses of the prescription. There has been no recurrence since then.',"湿热偏重者，加茵陈、栀子；气滞血瘀者，加丹参、赤芍、鳖甲；脾虚甚者，加黄芪、山药":"For those with severe damp-heat, add artemisia and gardenia; for those with qi stagnation and blood stasis, add salvia miltiorrhiza, red peony root, and turtle shell; for those with severe spleen deficiency, add astragalus and yam.",湿热痢:"Damp-heat dysentery",滇:"Yunnan",滇南儿科:"Southern Yunnan Pediatrics",滇南医药:"Southern Yunnan Medicine",滇南医药之祖:"The ancestor of southern Yunnan medicine","滇南地气特殊，物产药物多与中土异，用药当“因地制宜”。":'Southern Yunnan has a special climate, and many of its products and medicines are different from those in China. The use of medicines should be "adapted to local conditions."',滇南本草:"Southern Yunnan Materia Medica","滇重楼、滇黄精、滇贝母等山地药材之性味主治与验方。":"Indications and prescriptions for the nature and taste of mountain medicinal materials such as Dian Zhonglou, Dian Polygonatum, and Dian Fritillaria.","滇重楼一味，性苦微寒，清热解毒、消肿止痛，书中载其治痈疽疔毒、虫蛇咬伤甚效，并附醋磨外敷之法。滇黄精甘平润肺、补脾益气，谓其得坤土之精，久服轻身。滇贝母清热化痰、开郁散结，尤宜于燥咳痰黏之证。":"Dian Chonglou is bitter in nature and slightly cold in nature. It clears away heat and detoxifies, reduces swelling and relieves pain. The book states that it is very effective in treating carbuncle, furuncle, insect bites and snake bites, and the method of rubbing it with vinegar for external application is also included. Polygonatum d'unnanensis is sweet, flat, moisturizing the lungs, tonifying the spleen and replenishing qi. It is said that it can obtain the essence of the earth and take it for a long time to lighten the body. Fritillaria yunnanensis clears away heat and resolves phlegm, relieves stagnation and dissipates stagnation, and is especially suitable for those with dry cough and sticky phlegm.","炙紫菀10g，炙冬花10g，杏仁8g，桔梗8g，陈皮8g，法半夏8g，川贝母6g（研末冲服），生甘草4g":"10g of roasted aster, 10g of roasted winter flower, 8g of almond, 8g of platycodon, 8g of tangerine peel, 8g of pinellia, 6g of fritillary (grind and drink), 4g of raw licorice",热深厥深阳极似阴证:"Syndrome of deep heat and deep yang pole resembling yin",热盛逼阴证:"Hot and strong syndrome",热门检索:"Popular searches","燥 咳":"Dry cough","燥 咳 吴某，男，二十四岁，昆明医学院学生":"Dry cough Wu, male, 24 years old, student at Kunming Medical College","燥 咳 吴某，男，二十四岁，昆明医学院学生。1963年10月感秋 令燥邪而病咳嗽，咳声频频，干咳声响无痰无涕，唇干，舌苔 薄白少津，脉浮濡,服西药止咳药未效。此为阴虚肺燥之证， 宜养阴润肺止咳，拟二冬二母汤加味，一剂尽，津液回生，咳 声立止。 麦冬15克，天冬12克，川贝母10克，知母10克，百合 12克，黄芩10克，生杭白芍12克，百部10克，桑白皮12克， 玄参10克，五味子3克，甘草6克。":"Dryness and cough Wu, male, 24 years old, student at Kunming Medical College. In October 1963, he suffered from a cough caused by autumn dryness evil. He coughed frequently and dryly without phlegm or runny eyes. His lips were dry, his tongue coating was thin and white, and he had less fluid. His pulse was loose and wet. Taking western medicine to relieve cough was not effective. This is a syndrome of yin deficiency and dryness of the lungs. It is advisable to nourish yin, moisten the lungs and relieve coughs. Add the flavored Erdongermu Decoction. After one dose, the body fluids will regenerate and the coughing will stop immediately. 15 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 12 grams of Asparagus Asparagus, 10 grams of Fritillaria fritillaris, 10 grams of Anemarrhenae, 12 grams of Lily, 10 grams of Scutellaria baicalensis, 12 grams of white peony root, 10 grams of Rhizoma Rhizoma, 12 grams of Mulberry bark, 10 grams of Scrophulariaceae, 3 grams of Schisandra chinensis, and 6 grams of licorice.",燥热内结证:"Internal syndrome of dry heat",牙痛:"toothache","牙痛案 孙某，男，38岁":"Toothache case Sun, male, 38 years old","牙痛案\\n孙某，男，38岁。受寒感冒，服辛凉解表银翘散1剂，旋即牙痛发作，痛引头额，夜不安寐，其势难忍；牙龈肿痛，齿根松动，不能咬合，以致水米不进，时时呻吟；舌尖红，苔薄白而润，脉虚数无力。辨为表寒误服辛凉，寒邪凝滞经络，里阳受损，虚火上浮。治宜宣散经络凝寒，引火归元，纳气归肾，方用潜阳封髓丹加味：	:\\n附片45g，炙龟板9g，肉桂9g（研末，泡水兑入），砂仁9g，细辛5g，黄柏9g，白芷9g，露蜂房6g，生姜12g，甘草9g。\\n煎服1次，牙痛减轻，夜能安寐；再服则疼痛渐止，2剂服毕，牙龈肿痛痊愈。\\n按：此属阴火上浮所致牙痛，极易误为实火。论其牙龈肿痛、舌尖赤红，似属外感火热。然从病史看，受寒感冒，服辛凉之剂旋即牙痛，显然不符。舌尖虽红，但苔薄白而润，脉虚数无力，综合判断，属于“里阳受损，虚火上浮”，说到底是阴火。潜阳封髓丹正为此类证候而设，另加细辛、白芷、露蜂房止痛治标，标本兼顾，2剂痊愈，效如桴鼓。":`Toothache case\\nSun, male, 38 years old. After catching a cold, I took 1 dose of Xinliang Jiebiao Yinqiao Powder. Immediately, toothache broke out, causing pain in my head and forehead, making me restless and unbearable at night. The gums were swollen and painful, the roots of teeth were loose, and I couldn't bite, so I couldn't eat water or rice, and I moaned all the time. The tip of the tongue was red, the coating was thin, white and moist, and the pulse was weak and weak. If the external cold is mistakenly taken as pungent and cool, the cold evil will stagnate the meridians, damage the inner yang, and cause the deficiency fire to rise. The treatment is suitable for dispersing the cold in the meridians, inducing fire to return to the yuan, and absorbing the qi to return to the kidneys. The recipe is supplemented with Qianyang Marrow-sealing Pill: :\\n45g of Fu Shen, 9g of turtle shell, 9g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 9g of amomum villosum, 5g of asarum, 9g of Phellodendron, 9g of Angelica dahurica, 6g of honeycomb, 12g of ginger, and 9g of licorice. \\nAfter taking the decoction once, the toothache is relieved and you can sleep peacefully at night; if you take it again, the pain will gradually stop. After taking 2 doses, the gum swelling and pain will be cured. \\nNote: This is toothache caused by rising yin fire, which can easily be mistaken for real fire. His gums were swollen and painful, and the tip of his tongue was red, which seemed to be caused by exogenous heat. However, judging from the medical history, it is obviously inconsistent to have a cold, toothache immediately after taking a pungent and cool medicine. Although the tip of the tongue is red, the coating is thin, white and moist, and the pulse is weak and weak. Based on comprehensive judgment, it is "damaged internal yang and deficient fire", which is ultimately yin fire. Qianyang Marrow-Sealing Pill is designed for this type of syndrome. It is also added with Asarum, Angelica dahurica and Lufengxing to relieve pain and treat the symptoms. It takes into account both the symptoms and the symptoms. After 2 doses, the disease is cured and the effect is like a drumbeat.`,牙龈出血:"Bleeding gums","牙龈出血 王某，男，年三十二岁，患龈缝出血已久，牙床破烂，龈肉 …":"Bleeding gums Wang, male, 32 years old, has been suffering from gum bleeding for a long time, his gums are in tatters, and his gums…","牙龈出血 王某，男，年三十二岁，患龈缝出血已久，牙床破烂，龈肉 萎缩，齿摇松动，且痛而痒，屡服滋阴降火之品罔效。余诊之, 脉息沉弱无力，舌质淡，苔白滑,不思水饮。此系脾肾气虚,无 力统摄血液以归其经。齿为骨之余，属肾，肾气虚则齿枯而动 摇。脾主肌肉，开窍于口，脾气虚而不能生养肌肉，则龈肉破 烂而萎缩。气者，阳也。血者，阴也。阳气虚则阴不能潜藏而 上浮，阴血失守而妄行于血脉之外。法当扶阳以镇阴，固气以 摄血，俾阴阳调和则血自归经而不外溢矣。拟方潜阳封髓丹 加黑姜、肉桂治之。 附片60克，西砂仁20克（研），炮黑姜26克，上肉桂10 克（研末，泡水兑入），焦黄柏6克，炙甘草10克，龟板13克 （酥，打碎）。 服一剂稍效，三剂血全止，四剂后痛痒若失。连服十剂， 牙肉已长丰满，诸证全瘳。按：附子、肉桂温补下焦命门真火,扶少火而生气，砂仁纳气归肾，龟板、黄柏敛阴以潜阳，黑姜、炙甘草温中益脾，伏火互根，并能引血归经，故此方能治之而愈。余遇此等病症,屡治屡效，如见脉数饮冷，阴虚有热者，又须禁服也。":"Bleeding gums Wang, male, 32 years old, has been suffering from gingival seam bleeding for a long time. His gums are tattered, his gums have shrunk, his teeth are loose, and he is painful and itchy. He has repeatedly taken products that nourish yin and reduce fire, but have no effect. Upon further examination, the patient's pulse was deep and weak, the tongue was pale, the coating was white and slippery, and he did not want to drink water. This is caused by spleen and kidney qi deficiency, which means that the blood cannot be absorbed and returned to its meridians. Teeth are bones and belong to the kidneys. If kidney qi is deficient, the teeth will become dry and shaky. The spleen governs muscles and opens into the mouth. If the spleen is weak and unable to grow muscles, the gums will become tattered and atrophy. Qi means Yang. Blood is Yin. If Yang Qi is deficient, Yin cannot hide and floats up, causing Yin blood to lose control and travel outside the blood vessels. The method should support the yang to calm the yin, consolidate the qi to absorb the blood, and harmonize the yin and yang so that the blood will return to the meridians without overflowing. The proposed prescription Qianyang Fengsui Dan is treated by adding black ginger and cinnamon. 60 grams of Aconite slices, 20 grams of amomum villosum (grind), 26 grams of black ginger, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 6 grams of burnt cypress, 10 grams of roasted licorice, 13 grams of tortoise shell (crisp, smashed). One dose gave a slight effect, three doses stopped the bleeding completely, and after four doses the pain and itching disappeared. After taking ten doses in a row, the gums on the teeth had grown plump and all symptoms were gone. Note: Aconite and cinnamon warm and tonify the lower Jiao Mingmen True Fire, support the Shaohuo and bring qi to the kidneys, Amomum villosum attracts Qi and returns it to the kidneys, Tortoiseshell and Phellodendron collect yin to subdue yang, black ginger and roasted licorice warm the middle and benefit the spleen, subdue the mutual roots of fire, and induce blood to return to the menstruation, so it can be cured and cured. In case of such symptoms, repeated treatments have been effective. For example, if the pulse is rapid and the drink is cold, or there is heat due to yin deficiency, it is necessary to refrain from taking the medicine.","狂病案 某男，20余岁.体质素弱":"Madness case: a man in his 20s. Physically weak","狂病案\\n某男，20余岁.体质素弱。始因腹痛便秘而发热，医者诊为瘀热内滞，以桃仁承气汤下之，病情反重，岀现发狂奔走，言语错乱。延吴氏诊视，脉沉迟无力，舌红津枯但不渴，微喜热饮而不多；气息喘促而短，有欲脱之势。断为阴证误下，逼阳暴脱之证。拟大剂回阳饮与服：附片130g，干姜50g，上肉桂13g（研末，泡水兑入），甘 \\n草10g。 \\n服后鼻孔流血，大便亦下黑血。认为非服温热药所致，实由桃仁承气汤误下，致血脱成瘀，已成离经败坏之血。今得温运气血，不能再行归经，遂上行下注而致鼻衄、便血。次日复诊见脉微神衰，嗜卧懒言，神识已转清，原方再服1剂，衄血、便血均止，口微燥，此系阳气已回，营阴尚虚，继以四逆汤加人参，连进4剂而愈。\\n按：此症舌红津枯、发狂奔走，颇似阳证。但脉沉迟无力，微喜热饮，参考误下之后，病情反重，气息喘促，判为阴证误下，逼阳暴脱之证，用大回阳饮收效。确实有胆有识，见解高超。":"Madness case\\nA man in his 20s with a weak constitution. He started to have fever due to abdominal pain, constipation, and the doctor diagnosed it as internal stagnation of blood stasis and heat. He prescribed Taoren Chengqi Decoction. The condition worsened, and he started to run around wildly and his speech was confused. After Yan Wu's examination, the pulse was slow and weak, the tongue was red and dry but not thirsty, and he liked hot drinks but not much; the breath was short and short, and there was a tendency to want to escape. It is definitely a sign that the yin syndrome is mistakenly lowered and the yang is forced out violently. A large dose of Huiyang drink should be taken: 130g of Fu tablets, 50g of dried ginger, 13g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), and 10g of licorice. \\nAfter taking the medicine, my nostrils bleed and black blood was found in my stools. It is thought that it was not caused by taking warm medicine, but actually the Taoren Chengqi Decoction was mistakenly taken, which caused the blood to break off and become blood stasis, which has become the blood that has been separated from the menstruation and corrupted. Now that the blood has warmed the blood, it can no longer return to the menstrual flow, so it goes up and down, causing epistaxis and bloody stools. The next day's follow-up examination showed that the pulse was weak, the patient was prone to lying down and talking, and the consciousness had become clear. He took another dose of the original prescription, and the bleeding in the nose and stool stopped, and the mouth was slightly dry. This was because the Yang Qi had returned, and the Yin Yin was still weak. He then added Sini Decoction with ginseng, and the patient was cured after taking 4 doses in a row. \\nNote: This disease has a red tongue, dry tongue, and frantic running around, which is quite similar to Yang syndrome. However, the pulse is slow and weak, and the patient prefers hot drinks. After mistakenly taking the reference, the condition worsens and the breath becomes short. It is judged that the yin syndrome is mistakenly taken, forcing the yang to burst, and the use of Dahuiyang Drink will be effective. He is indeed courageous, knowledgeable and insightful.","王某，女，成年":"Wang, female, adult","王某，女，成年。始因受寒起病，恶寒，咽痛不适，误服清热养阴之剂而症情加重。头痛如劈，恶寒发热，体痛。咽痛，水浆不能下咽，痰涎涌甚，咽部红肿起白泡而溃烂。舌苔白滑，不渴饮，脉沉细而兼紧象。此系寒入少阴，误用苦寒清热，致使阴邪夹寒水上逼，虚火上浮而成是状。取扶阳祛寒，	引阳归舍之法，以加味麻黄附子细辛汤治之：附片40g，干姜26g，北细辛6g，麻黄5g，上肉桂6g（研末，泡水兑入），甘草6g。 \\n1剂后寒热即退，咽部肿痛减去其半，再剂则痛去七八。3剂尽，诸症霍然而愈。\\n按：吴氏指出，少阴受寒误用苦寒清热养阴之剂，无异于雪上加霜。方中附子能扶阳驱寒；麻黄开发腠理，解散表寒，得细辛之辛温，直入少阴以温散经脉寒邪，并能协同附子纳阳归肾，邪去正安，少阴咽痛自然获愈。":"Wang, female, adult. The disease started due to cold, aversion to cold, sore throat and discomfort, and the symptoms worsened after mistakenly taking a heat-clearing and yin-nourishing agent. Headache like splitting, aversion to cold, fever, body aches. Sore throat, inability to swallow water and slurry, excessive phlegm and saliva, pharynx red and swollen with white blisters and ulceration. The tongue coating is white and slippery, and there is no thirst to drink. The pulse is heavy, thin and tight. This is caused by cold entering Shaoyin, misusing bitter cold to clear away heat, causing yin evil and cold water to push up, and the deficiency fire rises to form this condition. Use the method of supporting yang to dispel cold and inducing yang to return to the body, and treat it with the flavored Ephedra, Aconite and Asarum Decoction: 40g of Futian, 26g of dried ginger, 6g of Asarum, 5g of Ephedra, 6g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed), and 6g of licorice. \\nAfter one dose, the cold and heat will subside, and the swelling and pain in the throat will be reduced by half, and after another dose, the pain will be reduced by seven to eight. After 3 doses, all symptoms suddenly healed. \\nNote: Wu pointed out that if Shaoyin catches cold and misuses bitter cold medicine to clear away heat and nourish yin, it is tantamount to adding insult to injury. The aconite in the prescription can support yang and expel cold; ephedra develops interstitial muscles, dissolves superficial cold, and obtains the pungent warmth of asarum, and directly enters Shaoyin to warm the meridians and dissipate cold evil.",现存最早区域性本草专著作者:"The earliest extant author of a regional Materia Medica monograph","现存最早的区域性本草专著，成书早于《本草纲目》百余年。收载滇南道地药物四百余种，详其性味功用，附民间验方，是滇南医药学的奠基之作。":"The earliest existing regional Materia Medica monograph was written more than a hundred years before the Compendium of Materia Medica. It contains more than 400 kinds of local medicines in southern Yunnan, detailing their properties, tastes and functions, as well as folk prescriptions. It is the foundation of southern Yunnan medicine.","甘某之女，2岁":"Gan’s daughter, 2 years old","甘某之女，2岁。1924年3月岀麻疹，发热，涕清咳嗽，目赤多泪；耳指冷，面部隐隐已现红点。因上年冬季曾患慢脾风症，经吴氏治疗，体质尚未复元，故未敢用发表寒凉之剂，乃主以桂枝汤加附子、细辛：\\n桂枝6g，杭芍6g，甘草3g，生姜10g，大枣2枚，附片15g，细辛3g。\\n服1剂麻疹渐出，2剂透齐，3剂渐灰。但微见烦躁，因当时经验不足，竟疑为服温热药后之燥象，即用上方减去辛、附，倍芍药加当归以补阴血，加麦冬而清烦热。\\n次日复诊：服上方后脉反紧急，发热烦乱，喘挣痰鸣，鼻翼扇动，唇色青乌，舌苔白滑；指纹青黑出二关，有欲作惊风之状。此已有阴盛逼阳于外之势，当即以扶阳抑阴之四逆汤加肉桂、茯苓治之：\\n附片24g，干姜10g，甘草5g，上肉桂6g（研末，泡水兑入），茯苓12g，公丁香1.5g。 \\n服后旋即风动，手足抽掣，角弓反张，喘挣痰鸣，鼻扇不乳，以药饮之，则涌吐涎沫，泄泻绿粪，颇属危笃。诊其脉象，已较前和缓，身热约退十分之二三。此是药与病相争之兆，亦即“若药不瞑眩，厥疾弗瘳”之瞑眩现象，告其勿疑惧，当即照原方增量主之：\\n附片50g，干姜15g，甘草6g，上肉桂6g（研末，泡水兑入），茯苓12g，公丁香1.5g。连夜煎服。\\n次日复诊，见其脉静身凉，已能吮乳，惟尚咳嗽略挣，大便尚泻而色渐转黄，面唇指纹青乌之色已退。照原方再服1剂，泄泻止，喘挣平。复以上方加口芪12g.砂仁6g，去公丁香、茯苓，连服5剂，遂得痊愈。\\n原按：此等病症，若认为阳毒热重，以清热解毒之品投之，势必变症危笃，此时虽有识者用温热药以补救之，但如剂量过轻，或配伍不当，亦难生效。故应辨别阴阳，分析寒热，随症施治，则可免误治也。":`Gan's daughter, 2 years old. In March 1924, he developed measles, fever, cough with clear discharge, red eyes and many tears; cold ears and fingers, and faint red spots appeared on his face. Because I suffered from chronic spleen wind in the winter last year, my body has not recovered after Wu's treatment, so I dare not use any cold-cooling agent. Instead, I mainly use Guizhi Decoction with Fuzi and Asarum:\\nGuizhi 6g, Hangshao 6g, licorice 3g, ginger 10g, 2 jujubes, 15g Futian, and 3g Asarum. \\nAfter taking 1 dose, the measles gradually came out, after 2 doses, it cleared up completely, and after 3 doses, it gradually became gray. However, there was a slight irritability. Due to lack of experience at the time, I suspected it was dryness after taking warm medicine. I used the above to subtract the pungent and attached symptoms, added peony and angelica to nourish yin and blood, and added Ophiopogon japonicus to clear away the irritability and heat. \\nRevisit the next day: After taking the medicine, the pulse becomes urgent, fever and irritability, wheezing and phlegm, nose flaring, lips are blue and black, tongue coating is white and slippery; fingerprints are blue and black with two passes, and there is a feeling of convulsion. This has the potential to force yang to the outside, so immediately treat it with the Sini Decoction of supporting yang and suppressing yin, adding cinnamon and poria:\\n24g of Fu Pian, 10g of dried ginger, 5g of licorice, 6g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed in), 12g of Poria, and 1.5g of male clove. \\nImmediately after taking it, there will be wind movement, twitching of hands and feet, opisthotonus, wheezing and phlegm, and nostrils. If you drink the medicine, you will spit out saliva and have diarrhea of ​​green feces, which is quite dangerous. After checking his pulse, he found that it had become gentler than before, and his body heat had subsided by about 20-30%. This is a sign of conflict between the medicine and the disease, that is, the dizziness phenomenon of "if the medicine does not cure the dizziness, the disease will not be cured", tell them not to be afraid, and immediately increase the dosage according to the original prescription:\\n50g of Fu Pian, 15g of dried ginger, 6g of licorice, 6g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed in), 12g of Poria, and 1.5g of cloves. Decoction and take it overnight. \\nAfter a follow-up visit the next day, it was found that his pulse was quiet and his body was cool. He was able to suck milk, but he still coughed a little. His stools continued to have diarrhea and were gradually turning yellow. The blue and black color of his face, lips, and fingerprints had faded. Take another dose according to the original prescription, and the diarrhea stops and the asthma subsides. Add 12g of Qi Qi and 6g of Amomum villosum to the above, remove clove and poria, and take 5 doses in a row, and the patient was cured. \\nOriginal note: For these diseases, if it is believed that the Yang poison is severe and the heat is severe, taking heat-clearing and detoxifying products will inevitably turn the disease into a critical condition. At this time, although knowledgeable people can use warming medicine to remedy the disease, it will be difficult to be effective if the dosage is too light or the compatibility is improper. Therefore, yin and yang should be distinguished, cold and heat should be analyzed, and treatment should be carried out according to the symptoms, so as to avoid mistreatment.`,"甘某之子，3岁":"Gan's son, 3 years old","甘某之子，3岁。1924年3月出麻疹，初时发热咳嗽，请某医诊治，服升提表散而佐清凉之药2剂后，麻疹隐隐现点，色象不鲜，发热已五六日，尚未出透。吴氏诊之，见其昏迷无神（少阴证但欲寐之病情）。发热已五六日，麻疹尚未出透，若再迁延，势必转危，即以白通汤1剂：附片60g，干姜15g，葱白4茎（连须根）。\\n服后，疹已出透而色转红活；再剂疹渐灰，脉静身凉，食增神健，霍然而愈。\\n原按：体弱发迷无神，疹出性慢，色象不鲜，服白通汤一二剂，即能使疹子出齐，平安而愈。此种治法，在麻疹方书上虽不易见，但麻疹既不得发越外出而现阴盛阳衰之象，投以白通汤扶助心肾之阳，疗效甚速。倘再误施寒凉，则正愈虚而阳愈弱，无力托毒外出，反而内攻，必致衰脱.故无论痧麻痘疹，一旦病势沉重，务须体会《内经•阴阳应象大论》“治病必求其本”之精神，认真辨别阴阳，不可固守一法。症现阴象，必须救阳；症现阳象，必须救阴，方有挽回之望。\\n按：此案麻疹“既不得发越外出而现阴盛阳衰之象，投以白通汤扶助心肾之阳，疗效甚速”。症现阴象，必须救阳，足以显现火神派理念。":`Gan's son, 3 years old. Measles occurred in March 1924. He had fever and cough at the beginning. He asked a doctor for diagnosis and treatment. After taking 2 doses of Shengtibiao Powder combined with cooling medicine, the measles appeared faintly, and the color was not fresh. He had been having fever for five or six days and had not yet cleared up. Wu diagnosed him and found that he was comatose and unconscious (a condition in which Shaoyin syndrome requires sleepiness). It has been five or six days since the fever, but the measles has not yet emerged. If it persists any longer, the disease will definitely turn critical. Take 1 dose of Baitong decoction: 60g of Aconite tablets, 15g of dried ginger, and 4 white scallions (with fibrous roots). \\nAfter taking it, the rash has appeared and turned red. After taking another dose, the rash gradually turned gray, the pulse was still and the body was cool. After eating, the spirit became strong and the symptoms suddenly improved. \\nOriginal note: If you are weak, confused and lackadaisical, the rash is slow to appear, and the color is not fresh, take one or two doses of Baitong Decoction, which can make the rash appear and heal safely. Although this kind of treatment method is not easy to see in measles prescription books, measles should not spread out and show signs of yin excess and yang decline. Baitong decoction can be used to support the yang of the heart and kidneys, and the curative effect is very fast. If cold and cool are applied by mistake again, the righteousness will become more deficient and the yang will become weaker, unable to support the poison from going out, but attacking internally, which will inevitably lead to degeneration. Therefore, no matter whether it is Sha, measles or acne, once the disease is severe, it is necessary to understand the spirit of "Treatment must seek its root" in "Nei Jing·Yin and Yang Ying Xiang Da Lun", carefully distinguish yin and yang, and do not stick to one method. If the symptoms appear to be yin, the yang must be rescued; if the symptoms appear to be yang, the yin must be rescued before there is any hope of recovery. \\nNote: In this case, the measles "should not spread out and cause signs of yin excess and yang decline. Baitong Decoction was given to support the yang of the heart and kidneys, and the effect was very rapid." When the disease manifests a yin phenomenon, the yang must be rescued, which is enough to manifest the concept of the Vulcan Sect.`,"甘草12g，浮小麦30g，大枣10枚，小麦30g，百合20g，苏叶10g，姜半夏12g":"12g licorice, 30g floating wheat, 10 jujubes, 30g wheat, 20g lily, 10g perilla leaves, 12g ginger pinellia","用于麻疹初起，证偏阳热者：加桑叶、薄荷、蝉蜕、香薷；若疹出顺畅、发热渐退，改用赤小豆汤加南沙参、麦冬、玄参":"For those with yang fever at the beginning of measles: add mulberry leaves, mint, cicada slough, and fragrant grass; if the rash breaks out smoothly and the fever gradually subsides, use Chixiaodou Decoction with Nansha Shen, Ophiopogon japonicus, and Scrophulariaceae.","用药禁忌亦详列之：疹未透齐慎用寒凉，收没期慎用辛散，一切大苦大寒、峻补滋腻之品皆非所宜，末附家常食疗数则，以助药力之所不逮。":"Medication contraindications are also listed in detail: use cold and cool ingredients with caution before the rash is fully absorbed, and use pungent powder with caution during the recovery period. All products that are severe in severe pain, cold, severe, nourishing, and greasy are not suitable. At the end of the article, a few rules of home-based dietary therapy are included to help where the medicine fails.","用药精纯，剂量讲究，于平凡方中见神奇。":"The medicine is pure, the dosage is exquisite, and the magic is found in ordinary prescriptions.","用药轻清平和，中病即止，忌大苦大寒伐生生之气。":"The medicine is gentle and gentle, and the disease will be stopped immediately. Avoid severe bitterness and severe cold, which can reduce the vitality.","由中国中医科学院中医药信息研究所中医药大健康智能研发中心与云南中医药大学合作建设的“云南名医馆”完成改版，支持名医、医案、著作三大分类检索。":'The "Yunnan Famous Doctors Museum", jointly built by the Traditional Chinese Medicine Health Intelligence R&D Center of the Institute of Traditional Chinese Medicine Information of the China Academy of Chinese Medical Sciences and Yunnan University of Traditional Chinese Medicine, has completed its revision and supports retrieval of famous doctors, medical records, and works.',男:"male","疏肝健脾，清热利湿":"Soothe the liver and strengthen the spleen, clear away heat and promote dampness",疑难杂症:"Intractable diseases","疑难杂症多“虚实夹杂、寒热交错”，治当复方图之，攻补兼施。":'Many difficult and complicated diseases are "mixed with deficiency and excess, and mixed with cold and heat". They should be treated with compound prescriptions, using both attack and supplement.',疑难重症:"Difficult and severe cases",疟证:"malaria syndrome",疳积:"malnutrition","疹陷、喘促、神昏诸危候之救逆验案。":"A proven case for rescuing and treating critical symptoms such as rash, shortness of breath, and coma.","疹陷色暗、面白肢冷者，急投麻附细辛汤温阳托透；喘促痰鸣者，小青龙加附子温肺涤饮；神昏者辨闭脱，闭者透邪开窍，脱者回阳固脱，不容毫厘之差。":"For those with dark rash, white face and cold limbs, immediately use Mafu Xixin Decoction to warm the yang and clear it up; for those with asthma and phlegm, add Xiaoqinglong plus Aconite to warm the lungs and purify the drink; for those with coma, identify closure and detachment; for closure, clear evil and open the orifices; for detachment, restore yang and solidify the detoxification; no difference is allowed.","痄 腮":"gills","痄 腮 （急性腮腺炎） 李某，男孩，五岁":"Mumps (acute mumps) Li, boy, five years old","痄 腮 （急性腮腺炎） 李某，男孩，五岁。1964年2月患腮腺炎，已四五日。发热 恶寒,两腮于耳下赤肿疼痛。其母用臭灵丹叶捣烂外敷，另服 六神丸，效果不明显,反觉服六神丸后腹中冷痛不适,延余诊 视。初诊，患儿寒热未退,两腮仍肿痛，腹内亦痛，不思饮食, 精神疲惫,脉弦细，舌苔薄白，根部稍显黄腻。此乃风寒外袭, 邪遏太阳、少阳两经，经气受阻,脉络不通所致,亦属太少二 阳合病之证。拟用桂枝、柴胡合方加味治之。 柴胡6克，黄芩6克，明党参9克，桂枝9克，杭芍6克， 法半夏6克，生姜3片，大枣3枚,板蓝根9克，甘草6克。 服一剂，发热退，恶寒减轻,两腮肿痛消退大半，腹痛亦 止，已思饮食。脉细缓，舌根部黄腻苔已退。继上方去黄芩加 山甲珠6克、败酱草6克，连服二剂而愈。":"Mumps (acute mumps) Li, a boy, five years old. He contracted mumps in February 1964 and had been there for four or five days. Fever, aversion to cold, redness, swelling and pain in cheeks below ears. His mother mashed up the leaves of Xiuling Dan and applied them externally, and also took Liushen Pills, but the effect was not obvious. Instead, she felt cold pain and discomfort in the abdomen after taking Liushen Pills, and she delayed further examination. At the initial diagnosis, the child's cold and heat had not subsided, his cheeks were still swollen and painful, and there was pain in the abdomen. He did not want to eat, was mentally exhausted, had a stringy and thready pulse, and had a thin white tongue coating with a slightly yellowish greasy coating at the root. This is caused by the external attack of wind and cold, and the evil restrains the Taiyang and Shaoyang meridians, causing the meridian Qi to be blocked and the meridians to be blocked. It is also a syndrome of the combination of too little and two yang. It is planned to treat it with a combination of Guizhi and Bupleurum. 6 grams of Bupleurum, 6 grams of Scutellaria baicalensis, 9 grams of Codonopsis pilosula, 9 grams of Guizhi, 6 grams of peony root, 6 grams of Pinellia ternata, 3 slices of ginger, 3 jujubes, 9 grams of Radix isatidis, and 6 grams of licorice. After taking one dose, the fever subsided, the aversion to cold was alleviated, the swelling and pain in the cheeks subsided by most of the time, the abdominal pain also stopped, and I can now think about eating. The pulse is thin and slow, and the yellow and greasy coating on the base of the tongue has receded. Following the above procedure, remove Scutellaria baicalensis and add 6 grams of Scutellaria baicalensis and 6 grams of Scutellaria baicalensis. Take two doses and the symptoms will be cured.","痄腮案 李某，男孩，5岁":"Gill case: Li, boy, 5 years old","痄腮案\\n李某，男孩，5岁。1964年2月患腮腺炎已四五日.发热恶寒，两腮于耳下赤肿疼痛。其母用臭灵丹叶捣烂外敷，另服六神丸，效果不明显，反觉腹中冷痛不适，延余诊视。寒热未退，两腮仍肿痛，腹内亦痛，不思饮食，精神疲惫，脉弦细，舌苔薄白根部稍显黄腻。此乃风寒外袭，邪遏太阳少阳两经，经气受阻，脉络不通所致，亦属太少二阳合病之证。拟用桂枝、柴胡合方加味治之：柴胡6g，黄芩6g，明党参9g，桂枝9g，杭芍6g，法夏6g，板蓝根9g，甘草6g，生姜3片，大枣3枚。\\n服1剂，发热退，恶寒减轻，两腮肿痛消退大半，腹痛亦止，已思饮食。脉细缓，舌根部黄腻苔已退。继上方去黄芩，加甲珠6g，败酱草6g，连服2剂而愈。\\n按：痄腮多按热毒辨治，前服六神丸即着眼于此。吴氏从寒热未退、两腮肿痛等脉症辨析，认为风寒外袭，邪遏太阳、少阳两经，用柴胡桂枝汤解此二阳合病之证，体现“把好太阳关”之旨。":'Gill case\\nLi, boy, 5 years old. In February 1964, I suffered from mumps for four to five days. I had fever and aversion to cold, and my cheeks were red, swollen and painful under my ears. His mother pounded the leaves of Xiulingdan and applied them externally, and also took Liushen Pills. The effect was not obvious, and she felt cold pain and discomfort in her abdomen, and she delayed further examination. The cold and heat have not subsided, the cheeks are still swollen and painful, and there is also pain in the abdomen. There is no desire to eat, mental fatigue, stringy and thin pulse, and the tongue coating is thin and white, and the root is slightly yellow and greasy. This is caused by the external attack of wind and cold, which suppresses the Yang and Shao Yang meridians, causing obstruction of the meridian Qi and blockage of the meridians. It is also a syndrome of the combination of too little and two Yang meridians. It is planned to use a combination of Guizhi and Bupleurum to treat the disease: Bupleurum 6g, Scutellaria baicalensis 6g, Codonopsis pilosula 9g, Guizhi 9g, Hangshao 6g, Faxia 6g, Isatis 9g, Licorice 6g, 3 slices of ginger, 3 jujubes. \\nAfter taking 1 dose, the fever subsided, the aversion to cold was relieved, the swelling and pain in the cheeks subsided by most of the time, the abdominal pain also stopped, and I started thinking about eating. The pulse is thin and slow, and the yellow and greasy coating on the base of the tongue has receded. Following the above procedure, remove Scutellaria baicalensis, add 6g of Scutellaria baicalensis and 6g of Scutellaria baicalensis, and take 2 doses in a row to heal. \\nNote: Cheeks should be treated based on the differentiation of heat and toxins. Taking Liushen Pills beforehand will focus on this. Based on the analysis of pulse symptoms such as persistent cold and heat, swollen and painful cheeks, Wu believed that when wind and cold attack externally, the evils inhibit the two yang meridians, the taiyang and shaoyang meridians, and used Bupleurum Guizhi Decoction to resolve this syndrome of combined yang and yang, embodying the purpose of "keeping the sun in check".',"病后体弱出麻疹变证严重 甘某之女，两岁余,姚安人，住昆明市":"After the illness, she became weak and developed measles, which turned into serious symptoms. Gan’s daughter, more than two years old, is from Yao’an and lives in Kunming City.","病后体弱出麻疹变证严重 甘某之女，两岁余,姚安人，住昆明市。患儿于1924年3 月出麻疹，延余诊治。其症发热，涕清咳嗽，目赤多泪，耳指冷, 面部隐隐已现红点。因上年冬季曾患慢脾风症，经余治疗，体 质尚未复元,故未敢用发表寒凉之剂，乃主以桂枝汤加附子、细辛。 桂枝6克，杭白芍6克，甘草3克，生姜10克，大枣2枚， 附片15克，细辛3克。 服一剂，麻疹渐出，二剂透齐，三剂渐灰。但微见烦躁，因 当时余经验不足，竟疑为服温热药后之燥象，即用上方减去 辛、附，倍芍药加当归以补阴血，加麦冬而清烦热。 桂枝6克，杭白芍12克，甘草3克，生姜10克，大枣2 枚，当归10克，麦冬10克。 次日复诊。服上方后患儿脉反紧急，发热烦乱，喘挣痰 鸣，鼻翼扇动，唇色青乌，舌苔白滑，指纹青黑出二关,有欲作 惊风之状。此种病情，已有阴盛逼阳于外之势，当即以扶阳抑 阴之四逆汤加肉桂、茯苓治之。 附片24克，干姜10克，甘草5克，上肉桂6克（研末，泡 水兑入），茯苓12克，丁香1.5克。 服后，旋即风动，延余再诊。见其手足抽掣，角弓反张，喘 挣痰鸣，鼻扇不乳，以药饮之，则涌吐涎沫，泄泻绿粪。此种症 状，颇属危笃。但诊其脉象，已较前和缓，身热约退十分之二、 三。此是药与病相争之兆,亦即“若药不瞑眩,厥疾弗瘳”之瞑 眩现象，告其希勿疑惧。当即照原方增量主之。 附片50克，干姜15克，甘草6克，上肉桂6克（研末，泡 水兑入），茯苓12克，丁香1.5克。 嘱病家连夜煎服。次日复诊,见其脉静身凉，已能吮乳， 惟尚咳嗽略挣,大便尚泻而色渐转黄，面唇指纹青乌之色已 退。照原方再服一剂，泄泻止，喘挣平。复以上方加北口芪12 克、砂仁6克，去公丁香、茯苓，连服五剂，遂得痊愈。按：此等病症，若认为阳毒热重，以清热解毒之品投之，势必变证危笃，此时虽有识者用温热药以补救之，但如剂量过轻，或配伍不当，亦难生效。故应辨别阴阳，分清虚实寒热，随症施治，则可免误治也。":`After the illness, she became weak and developed measles, which turned into serious symptoms. Gan's daughter is more than two years old, from Yao'an, and lives in Kunming City. The child developed measles in March 1924 and was delayed in diagnosis and treatment. Symptoms include fever, cough with clear discharge, red eyes and tearful eyes, cold ears and fingers, and faint red spots on the face. Because I suffered from chronic spleen wind in the winter last year, and after the treatment, my body has not yet recovered, so I did not dare to use any cold-cooling agent. Instead, I mainly used Guizhi Decoction with Aconite and Asarum. 6 grams of cassia twig, 6 grams of white peony root, 3 grams of licorice, 10 grams of ginger, 2 jujubes, 15 grams of Asarum, and 3 grams of asarum. After taking one dose, the measles will gradually come out, after the second dose, the symptoms will clear up, and after the third dose, the symptoms will gradually fade away. However, there was a slight irritability. Due to lack of experience at the time, I suspected it was dryness after taking warm medicine, so I used the above to subtract the pungent and attached, doubled the peony and angelica to nourish yin and blood, and added Ophiopogon japonicus to clear away the irritability and heat. 6 grams of cassia twig, 12 grams of white peony root, 3 grams of licorice, 10 grams of ginger, 2 jujubes, 10 grams of angelica root, and 10 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus. Follow-up visit the next day. After taking the above medicine, the child has an urgent pulse, fever and irritability, wheezing and phlegm, flaring nose, blue lips, white and slippery tongue coating, blue and black fingerprints, and a feeling of convulsion. In this condition, the yin is exuberant and the yang is forced out, so the Sini decoction of supporting yang and suppressing yin plus cinnamon and poria is immediately treated. 24 grams of Aconite, 10 grams of dried ginger, 5 grams of licorice, 6 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 12 grams of Poria, and 1.5 grams of cloves. Immediately after taking it, I felt windy and had to wait for further consultation. He had twitching in his hands and feet, opisthotonus, wheezing and phlegm, and no nasal discharge. If he drank the medicine, he would vomit saliva and have diarrhea. Such symptoms are quite dangerous. However, upon examination, his pulse condition was gentler than before, and his body heat had subsided by about two to three tenths. This is a sign of the conflict between medicine and disease, that is, the phenomenon of dizziness that "if the medicine does not treat the disease, the disease will not be cured." Please do not be afraid of this. Immediately follow the original method and increase it. 50 grams of Fu Fian, 15 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of licorice, 6 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 12 grams of Poria, and 1.5 grams of cloves. Instruct the patient to decoction and take it overnight. After a follow-up visit the next day, it was found that her pulse was quiet and her body was cool, and she was able to suck breasts. However, she still coughed a little, and her stools continued to have diarrhea and gradually turned yellow in color. The blue and black color of her face, lips, and fingerprints had faded. Take another dose according to the original prescription, and the diarrhea will stop and the asthma will subside. Add 12 grams of Beikou Qi and 6 grams of Amomum villosum to the above, remove cloves and poria, and take five doses in a row, and the patient was cured. Note: For these diseases, if it is believed that the Yang poison is severe and the heat is severe, and the medicine is used to clear away heat and detoxify, the symptoms will inevitably become critical. At this time, although knowledgeable people can use warm medicine to remedy the problem, it will be difficult to be effective if the dosage is too light or the compatibility is improper. Therefore, yin and yang should be distinguished, cold and heat should be distinguished between deficiency and excess, and treatment should be carried out according to the symptoms, so that mistreatment can be avoided.`,"病毒性心肌炎案 李某，女，39岁":"Viral myocarditis case Li, female, 39 years old","病毒性心肌炎案\\n李某，女，39岁。因病毒性心肌炎住院治疗月余，现已病危，医院已下4次病危通知书，邀我前往诊治。患者平卧在床，两眼微闭，面红，已输液红霉素近20余天仍高烧不退，无力答话，睁眼或稍偏头则眩晕大作，饮食不下；脉沉微细数无力，舌淡苔白，边尖有齿痕；四肢厥冷。辨为阳虚欲脱，已成戴阳证，拟白通汤回阳收纳，以挽一线生机：\\n附片100g，干姜24g，葱头3茎。2剂。\\n药尽发热渐退，面红已消，能起坐食粥，欲脱之阳已渐复，仍短气乏力，心悸时眩晕作，更以真武汤温肾扶阳，镇水宁心：\\n附片100g，生姜3片，白术15g，杭芍10g，茯苓30g。.\\n服药2剂后，大有好转，已能起床自理，露出笑容，心悸眩晕未作。续投以大回阳饮强心固肾：\\n附片100g，干姜24g，上肉桂10g，甘草10g。服药一周出院，调理月余恢复工作。\\n按：本例阳脱于上，危在旦夕，万不可误认高烧、面红为阳证。生死之间，差以毫厘，谬之千里，全在神情萎靡、四肢厥冷处着眼。急用白通汤回阳固脱，继以真武汤温肾扶阳，后用大回阳饮挽回生机。皆以经方投用，用药之简净，实有乃祖风格（《经典火神派医案点评》，下同）":`Viral myocarditis case\\nLi, female, 39 years old. I have been hospitalized for viral myocarditis for more than a month and I am now critically ill. The hospital has issued critical illness notices four times and invited me to come for diagnosis and treatment. The patient was lying on his back in bed with his eyes slightly closed and his face was red. He had been infused with erythromycin for nearly 20 days and still had a high fever. He was unable to answer. He suffered from dizziness when he opened his eyes or tilted his head slightly. He could not eat or drink. His pulse was slow and weak, his tongue was pale and white with white coating, and there were tooth marks on the edges. His limbs were cold. It is diagnosed as Yang deficiency and the patient wants to take off the disease, which has become a syndrome of Dai Yang. Baitong Decoction can be used to restore Yang and absorb it, so as to save a glimmer of life:\\n100g of attached slices, 24g of dried ginger, and 3 stalks of green onion. 2 doses. \\nAfter the medicine is used up, the fever gradually subsides, the flushing disappears, and I can sit up and eat porridge. The yang that wants to be shed has gradually recovered, but I am still short of breath and weak, and feel dizzy during palpitations. I use Zhenwu Decoction to warm the kidneys and support yang, calm the water and calm the heart:\\n100g of attached pieces, 3 slices of ginger, 15g of Atractylodes, 10g of peony root, and 30g of poria. .\\nAfter taking 2 doses of the medicine, I have greatly improved. I can get up and take care of myself, smile, and my heart palpitations and dizziness have not gone away. Continue to use Dahuiyang Drink to strengthen the heart and strengthen the kidneys:\\n100g of Fu Pian, 24g of dried ginger, 10g of cinnamon, and 10g of licorice. After taking medicine for a week, he was discharged from hospital and returned to work after a month of recuperation. \\nNote: In this case, the yang is detached from the upper body, which is very dangerous. Do not mistake high fever and flushed face for yang syndrome. The difference between life and death is just a hair's breadth, a thousand miles away, all based on looking at the sluggish look and cold limbs. Urgently use Baitong Decoction to restore yang and stabilize the condition, then use Zhenwu Decoction to warm the kidneys and support yang, and finally use Dahuiyang Drink to restore vitality. All medicines are administered based on classic prescriptions, and the medication is simple and clean, truly in the style of ancestors ("Commentary on Classic Vulcan School Medical Records", the same below)`,痛经:"Dysmenorrhea","痛经案辨经前经后、痛之拒按喜按，分气滞、血瘀、寒凝、气血虚四端论治，用药轻灵平和，不恃攻伐。":"The case of dysmenorrhea is divided into premenstrual and postmenstrual pain, pain that refuses to be pressed and prefers to be pressed. The treatment is divided into four aspects: qi stagnation, blood stasis, cold coagulation, and qi and blood deficiency. The medication is gentle and gentle, and does not rely on attacks.",痛证:"Pain syndrome","痛证论治首辨经络归属，循经取穴与按时取穴并用。":"The first step in the treatment of pain syndrome is to identify the meridians, select acupoints along the meridians and select acupoints on time.","痰喘咳嗽兼气虚便秘 刘某之父，年过六旬":"Phlegm, asthma, cough and constipation due to Qi deficiency. Liu’s father is over sixty years old.","痰喘咳嗽兼气虚便秘 刘某之父，年过六旬。1924年9月，病已月余，六脉沉迟 无力，舌苔白腻,喜热饮，咳嗽哮喘而多痰。腹胀且痛，不思 食，大便秘结二十日不更衣,小便赤而长,夜难入寐,精神极 弱。查前所服方药，均以清热消食降气为主，且以硝、黄峻剂 通下之，仍不能便，其势较危。此系脾肾阳虚，中土失运，痰湿 水饮阻逆于肺，清肃不降，致痰喘咳嗽，传导失司，无力输送。 加之阳虚则气不化津，无以滋润肠道,致成气虚寒凝之便秘 不通，此太阴、阳明经气不相传也。宜扶阳温化主之,拟真武 汤加味。 附片100克，茯苓30克，白术20克，杭白芍10克，干姜 30克，北细辛6克，五味子5克。 一剂见效，二剂后喘、咳约去十之六、七，三剂则照原方 去杭芍,服后痰喘咳嗽若失，略进饮食。第三日以四逆汤加茯 苓、上肉桂、砂仁、北口芪。 附片100克，干姜50克，茯苓50克，砂仁10克，上肉桂 10克（研末，泡水兑入），北口芪60克。 上方服一剂后，是晚便意迫肛，解出干结黑色粪便半痰 盂许，腹中顿觉舒缓。然因年老气虚，解便时用力过盛，旋即昏晕不省人事。急诊之，气短欲绝，脉沉迟无力，但见白苔已 退，唇舌已转红润,此乃气虚下陷之故。当即以煎好之汤药喂 服。俄顷，人事已省，脉转有神。原方连服三剂，食增神健，咳 喘不作，二便通达。":"Phlegm, asthma, cough and constipation due to Qi deficiency. Liu's father is over sixty years old. In September 1924, he had been ill for more than a month. His six pulses were slow and weak, his tongue coating was white and greasy, he liked hot drinks, and he had cough, asthma and excessive phlegm. Abdominal distension and pain, no desire to eat, constipation, not changing clothes for twenty days, red and long urine, difficulty falling asleep at night, and extremely weak spirit. The prescriptions taken before the examination were all aimed at clearing away heat, digesting and lowering qi, and even after taking them with nitrate and Huangjun agents, the patient was still unable to have bowel movements, and the condition was dangerous. This is due to deficiency of spleen and kidney yang, loss of luck in the middle earth, phlegm-dampness and water drinking are blocked by the lungs, and the purification does not fall, causing phlegm, wheezing and coughing, loss of conduction, and inability to transport. In addition, when Yang is deficient, Qi cannot transform into body fluids and cannot moisten the intestines, resulting in constipation and obstruction due to Qi deficiency, coldness and coagulation. This is because the Taiyin and Yangming meridians do not pass Qi to each other. It is better to use Fuyang to warm it up, and add the flavor of Zhenwu Decoction. 100 grams of Futian, 30 grams of Poria, 20 grams of Atractylodes, 10 grams of white peony root, 30 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of Asarum, and 5 grams of Schisandra chinensis. One dose is effective. After the second dose, about 60% or 70% of the cough and wheezing will disappear. After the third dose, follow the original prescription to remove Hangshao. If phlegm, wheezing and cough disappear after taking it, add a little more food. On the third day, add Poria cocos, cassia cinnamon, Amomum villosum and Beikou Qi to Sini decoction. 100 grams of Fu Feng, 50 grams of dried ginger, 50 grams of Poria, 10 grams of amomum villosum, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), and 60 grams of Beikou Qi. After taking one dose of the above medicine, I had a late bowel movement and felt forced to the anus. Half a cup of dry black feces was released, and I suddenly felt relieved. However, due to his old age and weak energy, he exerted too much force when defecating, and soon became faint and unconscious. In emergency, shortness of breath, slow and weak pulse, but the white coating has receded and the lips and tongue have turned red, this is due to qi deficiency and depression. Take the decoction immediately. In a matter of seconds, people and things have been saved, and the pulse has changed. After taking three doses of the original prescription, food will increase your mental health, your cough and breath will stop, and your bowel movements will be smooth.","痰喘咳嗽兼气虚便秘案 刘某，年过六旬":"Case of phlegm, asthma, cough and constipation due to Qi deficiency: Liu, over sixty years old","痰喘咳嗽兼气虚便秘案\\n刘某，年过六旬。病已月余，咳嗽哮喘而多痰。腹胀且痛，不思食，大便秘结20日不更衣，小便赤而长，喜热饮，夜难入寐，精神极弱。六脉沉迟无力，舌苔白腻。查前所服方药，均以清热消食降气为主，且以硝、黄峻剂通下，仍不能便，其势较危。此系脾肾阳虚，中土失运，痰湿水饮阻逆于肺，清肃不降、致痰喘咳嗽，传导失司，无力输送。加之阳虚则气不化津，无以滋润肠道，致成气虚寒凝之便秘不通。宜扶阳温化主之。拟真武汤加味：\\n附片100g，茯苓30g，白术20g，杭芍10g，干姜30g，北细辛6g，五味子5g。\\n1剂见效；2剂后喘、咳约去十之六七；3剂照原方去杭芍，服后痰喘咳嗽若失，略进饮食。第3日以四逆汤加茯苓、上肉桂、砂仁、北芪。\\n附片100g，干姜50g，茯苓50g，砂仁10g，上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），北芪60g。\\n服1剂后，是晚便意迫肛，解出干结黑色粪便半痰盂许，腹中顿觉舒缓：然因年老气虚，解便时用力过盛，旋即昏晕不省人事。急诊之：气短欲绝，脉沉迟无力，但见白苔已退，唇舌已转红润。此乃气虚下陷之故。当即以煎好之汤药喂服，俄顷人事已省，脉转有神。原方连服3剂，食增神健，咳喘不作，二便通达。\\n按：此证咳喘而兼便秘，用真武汤加姜、辛、五味，自是仲景成法。唯虽见便秘“20日不更衣”，仍未予硝黄攻下，是因其属寒凝便结，故予大剂姜附温通化结，治病求本。1剂而“解出干结黑色粪便半痰盂许，腹中顿觉舒缓”。确显火神心法。":`Case of phlegm, asthma, cough and constipation due to Qi deficiency\\nLiu, over sixty years old. I have been ill for more than a month and have cough, asthma and excessive phlegm. Abdominal distension and pain, no desire to eat, constipation, not changing clothes for 20 days, red and long urine, liking hot drinks, difficulty falling asleep at night, and extremely weak energy. The six pulses are slow and weak, and the tongue coating is white and greasy. The prescriptions taken before the examination were all aimed at clearing away heat, digesting and lowering qi, and even though the patient was still unable to defecate after taking saltpetre and Huangjun agents, the condition was dangerous. This is due to spleen and kidney yang deficiency, loss of earth in the middle, and phlegm-dampness and water drinking are blocked by the lungs. The purification does not fall, causing phlegm, wheezing and coughing, and loss of conduction and inability to transport. In addition, when Yang is deficient, Qi cannot transform into body fluids and cannot moisten the intestines, resulting in constipation and obstruction due to Qi deficiency, coldness and coagulation. It should be controlled by Fuyang and warming. Xiuzhenwu Decoction is flavored with: \\n100g of Futian, 30g of Poria, 20g of Atractylodes, 10g of peony root, 30g of dried ginger, 6g of Asarum, 5g of Schisandra chinensis. \\n1 dose is effective; after 2 doses, the wheezing and coughing are about 60% to 70% better; after 3 doses, follow the original recipe to remove Hangshao. If phlegm, wheezing and cough disappear after taking it, eat a little. On the third day, add Poria cocos, cassia cinnamon, amomum villosum, and astragalus root to the Sini decoction. \\n100g of attached pieces, 50g of dried ginger, 50g of Poria, 10g of amomum villosum, 10g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 60g of astragalus. \\nAfter taking 1 dose, I had a late bowel movement and forced my anus to pass. About half a sputum cup of dry black feces was released, and I suddenly felt relieved. However, due to my old age and weak qi, I exerted too much force when defecating, and I immediately fainted and fell unconscious. Emergency treatment: Shortness of breath, slow and weak pulse, but the white coating has receded and the lips and tongue have turned red. This is due to Qi deficiency and depression. Immediately take the boiled decoction and take it. Within a short time, you have been relieved and your pulse has improved. After taking 3 doses of the original prescription, food will increase your mental health, your cough and wheezing will stop, and your bowel movements will be clear. \\nNote: For this syndrome, cough and asthma combined with constipation, use Zhenwu Decoction with ginger, pungent, and five flavors, which is Zhongjing's method. Although constipation was observed and "didn't change clothes for 20 days", it was still not treated with nitrate yellow. This was because the constipation was caused by cold condensation, so a large dose of ginger was given to warm the constipation and resolve the constipation, in order to cure the disease. After just one dose, "about half of the dry black stool was relieved, and I suddenly felt soothed in my abdomen." It truly shows the mind of Vulcan.`,"痰喘咳嗽，气虚便秘":"Phlegm, asthma, cough, Qi deficiency and constipation","痰饮、水肿、泄泻、消渴诸病治验。":"Treatment of phlegm, edema, diarrhea, and thirst.","痰饮、水肿、胃脘痛等内伤杂病治验。":"Treatment experience for phlegm, edema, epigastric pain and other internal injuries and miscellaneous diseases.",痰饮咳嗽:"Cough due to phlegm","痰饮咳嗽 李某，男，年四旬余，昆明市人，患痰饮咳喘病已八、九 年…":"Cough due to phlegm retention Li, male, in his forties, from Kunming City, has been suffering from cough and asthma due to phlegm retention for eight or nine years...","痰饮咳嗽 李某，男，年四旬余，昆明市人，患痰饮咳喘病已八、九 年，经中、西医屡治未愈。诊其脉左弦右滑，两尺弱，心脉细 短，肺脉滑大，按之则空,舌苔白滑而腻，面色青黯，目下浮起 如卧蚕。咳痰气喘而短，胸闷痰滞，头疼目眩，食少无神，畏食 酸冷,渴喜热饮而不多,小便短赤，咳时则遗,入夜难眠,行卧 惟艰，值阴雨天寒尤甚。良由脾肾阳虚，饮邪内泛，脾不运化， 寒湿水饮上逆犯肺则作痰作咳。肾虚不纳，则短气喘息而遗 溺,痰湿阻遏，清阳不升，浊阴不降，肺肾之气不相接,遂成痰 饮咳喘之证。《金匮要略》曰：“病痰饮者，当以温药和之。”为 痰饮病治本之法,禀承此意拟方小青龙汤加减主之。 附片20克，北细辛4克，麻茸3克，干姜15克，法半夏 15克，五味子1.5克，甘草3克。 次日复诊。昨服一剂，头疼、咳痰稍减，痰较易咯,乃照原 方加倍分量。服后痰多咳吐如涌,胸闷减，喘息较平。服二剂 后,头痛若失，喘息平其大半。服三剂后，稍能食,行卧已较轻 便，唯痰多,气仍短，小便转长而色仍赤。盖湿痰饮邪得阳药 运行，在上由咽喉气道而出，在下则随小便而去，乃病退之 兆。仍照前方加减治之。 附片100克，北细辛10克，法半夏10克，干姜40克，上 肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑入），茯苓30克，桂枝尖203克，五 味子3克，甘草10克。 服二剂后，喘咳平，痰已少。三剂后，胸闷气短均愈，饮食倍增，弦滑之脉已平，腻苔已退。唯精神未充,后以苓桂术甘 汤加附子、北口芪，连进十剂，遂得痊瘳。 附片150克，北口芪30克，茯苓20克，桂枝尖20克，白 术20克，甘草10克。":'Cough due to phlegm retention Li, male, in his forties, from Kunming City, has been suffering from cough and asthma due to phlegm retention for eight or nine years, and has not been cured after repeated treatments with Chinese and Western medicine. The pulse is stringy on the left and slippery on the right, weak in both feet, the heart pulse is thin and short, the lung pulse is slippery and large and empty when pressed, the tongue coating is white, slippery and greasy, the complexion is blue and gloomy, and the eyes are floating like lying silkworms. Coughing up phlegm and shortness of breath, chest tightness and phlegm stagnation, headache and dizziness, little food and lack of energy, fear of sour and cold food, thirst and preference for hot drinks but not much, short and red urine, which is passed out when coughing, difficulty sleeping at night, and difficulty in walking and lying down, especially on rainy days and cold weather. Good symptoms include spleen and kidney yang deficiency, internal drinking evil, inability to transport and transform the spleen, and cold and damp water that invades the lungs and causes phlegm and cough. Deficiency of the kidneys results in shortness of breath, wheezing and drowning, phlegm and dampness are blocked, clear yang does not rise, turbid yin does not fall, and the qi of the lungs and kidneys are not connected, resulting in cough and asthma due to phlegm drinking. "Jingui Synopsis" says: "Those who are sick with phlegm and water retention should be treated with warm medicine." As the root cause of phlegm and water retention disease, I am adhering to this idea to prepare Xiaoqinglong Decoction. 20 grams of Futian, 4 grams of Asarum, 3 grams of sesame root, 15 grams of dried ginger, 15 grams of Pinellia ternata, 1.5 grams of Schisandra chinensis, and 3 grams of licorice. Follow-up visit the next day. After taking one dose yesterday, my headache and phlegm cough were slightly relieved, and the phlegm was easier to cough up, so I doubled the amount of the original prescription. After taking it, the cough with excessive phlegm becomes vomiting, the chest tightness is reduced, and the wheezing becomes less severe. After taking two doses, the headache disappeared and most of the wheezing subsided. After taking three doses, I can eat a little, walk and lie down and have lighter bowel movements, but there is a lot of phlegm, shortness of breath, and the urine becomes longer and still red in color. If dampness, phlegm and evil are absorbed, the yang medicine will circulate. It will come out from the throat and airway at the top, and go with the urine at the bottom, which is a sign of the disease retreating. Still treat it with addition and subtraction according to the front. 100 grams of Fu Lian, 10 grams of Asarum, 10 grams of Pinellia, 40 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 30 grams of Poria, 203 grams of Guizhijian, 3 grams of Schisandra chinensis, and 10 grams of licorice. After taking two doses, the wheezing and cough subsided and there was less phlegm. After three doses, the chest tightness and shortness of breath were all cured, the diet doubled, the stringy and slippery pulses became flat, and the greasy coating disappeared. However, since he was not energetic enough, he took ten doses of Linggui Shugan Decoction plus Aconite and Beikouqi, and the disease was cured. 150 grams of Fu Pian, 30 grams of Beikou Qi, 20 grams of Poria, 20 grams of Guizhijian, 20 grams of Atractylodes, and 10 grams of licorice.',"痰饮善用苓桂术甘、小半夏加茯苓；水肿从肺脾肾三脏论治，开鬼门、洁净府、去菀陈莝三法随证选用；泄泻分暴泻久泻，暴泻化湿，久泻健脾升阳。":"For phlegm and phlegm, it is better to use Linggui Zhugan, Pinellia pinellia and Poria cocos; edema is treated based on the lungs, spleen and kidneys, and the three methods of Kaiguimen, Jiejingfu, and removing Wanchenchenju are selected according to the syndrome; diarrhea is divided into violent diarrhea and long-term diarrhea, violent diarrhea to transform dampness, and long-term diarrhea to strengthen the spleen and raise yang.",痹证:"Bi syndrome",痹证针治:"Acupuncture treatment of Bi syndrome",痿证:"Impotence syndrome",瘟疫病:"plague","瘟疫病小儿热极抽风证 郑某，2岁，住四川省会理县南门外近郊":"Severe fever syndrome in children with plague Zheng, 2 years old, lives in the suburbs outside Nanmen, Huili County, Sichuan Province","瘟疫病小儿热极抽风证\\n郑某，2岁，住四川省会理县南门外近郊。1921年5月，因邻居患时疫而被传染，某医以祛风解表治之，愈进愈危，延余诊视。时高热已6H，壮热渴饮，唇赤而焦，舌苔黄燥，指纹粗而色紫，脉沉数。大便已三四日不解，小便短赤，饮食不进，角弓反张之状，时而瘪疯抽掣，喘挣不已。视其症状颇危.此系疫邪传里与阳明燥气相合，热甚伤阴之证，复被祛风解表，更耗散阴血，以致津枯液涸，血不荣筋.血虚筋急风动遂成是状，所谓热极生风之证也。乃拟达原饮去草果加石膏、大黄清热下结，输转达邪治之：\\n杭芍13g，黄芩6g，榔片6g，知母6g，甘草3g，生石膏13g（碎，布包），大黄6g（泡水兑入）。\\n服1剂，二便通利，病退四五，抽掣筋急已止；再服1剂，则病退七八。继以生脉散加生地、当归、杭芍、石膏，连进2剂而愈。":"Severe fever syndrome in children with plague\\nZheng, 2 years old, lives in the suburbs outside the south gate of Huili County, Sichuan Province. In May 1921, a neighbor suffered from an epidemic and was infected. A certain doctor treated the disease with dispelling wind and relieving superficial symptoms. As the disease progressed, it became more and more dangerous and he was delayed for further examination. The fever has been high for 6 hours, and she is thirsty for drinks due to strong fever. Her lips are red and burnt, her tongue coating is yellow and dry, her fingerprints are thick and purple, and her pulse is heavy and rapid. He has been having unconscionable stools for three or four days. His urine is short and red, he is not eating well, his horns are opisthotonized, and sometimes he has cramps, convulsions, and constant breathing. The symptoms are considered to be quite dangerous. This is a syndrome in which the pathogenic factors are combined with the Yangming dryness, and the heat is extremely harmful to the Yin. The wind is dispelled and the exterior is dissipated, and the Yin and blood are dissipated, causing the body fluids to dry up and the blood to dry up the tendons. Blood deficiency and tendons are twitchy and windy, resulting in this condition. This is the so-called syndrome of wind caused by extreme heat. Naishidayuan drink is used to remove grass and fruit, add gypsum and rhubarb to clear away heat and reduce knots, and inject to treat Dahei: 13g of peony root, 6g of skullcap, 6g of palm slices, 6g of anemarrhena, 3g of licorice, 13g of gypsum (crushed, wrapped in cloth), 6g of rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed in). \\nTake 1 dose, the bowel movement will be relieved, the illness will be relieved by 40-50%, and the cramps and cramps will stop; take 1 more dose, the illness will be 78-80% better. Follow with Shengmai Powder plus Radix Rehmanniae, Angelicae Sinensis, Hangshao, and Gypsum, and it will heal after taking 2 doses in a row.","瘟疫病小儿热极生风证 郑某之子，两岁，四川省会理县南门外近郊农民":"Plague syndrome in children with extreme heat and wind. Zheng’s son, two years old, a farmer in the suburbs of Nanmenwai, Huili County, Sichuan Province","瘟疫病小儿热极生风证 郑某之子，两岁，四川省会理县南门外近郊农民。1921年 5月，因邻居患时疫而被传染，某医以祛风解表治之,愈进愈 危，延余诊视。时高热已六日，壮热渴饮，唇赤而焦，舌苔黄 燥,指纹粗而色紫，脉沉数。大便已三、四日不解，小便短赤， 饮食不进，角弓反张之状，时而疯癒抽掣，喘挣不已,视其证 状颇危。此系疫邪传里与阳明燥气相合,热甚伤阴之证，复被 祛风解表,更耗散阴血，以致津枯液涸，血不荣筋，血虚筋急 风动，遂成是状，所谓热极生风之证也。乃拟达原饮去草果加 石膏、大黄清热下结,输转达邪治之。 杭白芍13克，黄芩6克，榔片6克，知母6克，甘草3 克，生石膏13克（碎,布包），大黄6克（泡水兑入）。 服一剂，二便通利，病退四、五，抽掣筋急已止。再服一 剂，则病退七、八。继以生脉散加生地黄、当归、杭白芍、石膏， 连进二剂而愈。 沙参10克，麦冬10克，五味子3克，甘草3克，生石膏 10克（碎，布包），生地黄6克，当归10克,杭白芍10克。":"Plague syndrome in children with extreme heat and wind. Zheng's son, two years old, is a farmer in the suburbs outside the south gate of Huili County, Sichuan Province. In May 1921, a neighbor suffered from the epidemic and was infected. A certain doctor treated the disease with dispelling wind and relieving superficial symptoms. However, the disease became more and more dangerous and was delayed for further consultation. She had been suffering from high fever for six days. She was very hot and thirsty to drink. Her lips were red and burnt, her tongue coating was yellow and dry, her fingerprints were thick and purple, and her pulse was heavy and rapid. He has been having indigestible stool for three or four days, has short and red urine, is not eating well, has opisthotonus, and sometimes becomes more and more convulsed, and is gasping for breath. His symptoms are considered to be dangerous. This is a syndrome in which the epidemic evil is combined with the Yangming dryness, and the heat is extremely harmful to the yin. It is expelled wind and relieves the surface, and the yin blood is dissipated, so that the body fluids dry up, the blood does not prosper the tendons, and the blood deficiency causes the tendons to move with wind. This is the so-called syndrome of extreme heat causing wind. It is planned to drink the original drink without the grass and fruit, add gypsum and rhubarb to clear away heat and lower the knot, and transfuse it to cure the evil. 13 grams of Hangzhou white peony root, 6 grams of skullcap, 6 grams of palm slices, 6 grams of Anemarrhenae, 3 grams of licorice, 13 grams of gypsum (crushed, wrapped in cloth), 6 grams of rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed with water). Taking one dose will relieve constipation, relieve symptoms for four or five days, and stop cramps and cramps. After taking another dose, the disease will be cured by seven or eight degrees. Then take Shengmai Powder plus Rehmannia glutinosa, Angelica sinensis, Hangzhou white peony root, and Gypsum, and the disease will heal after taking two doses. 10 grams of Adenophora adenophora, 10 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 3 grams of Schisandra chinensis, 3 grams of licorice, 10 grams of gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 6 grams of raw rehmannia glutinosa, 10 grams of angelica root, and 10 grams of white peony root.",瘟疫病战汗:"plague war sweat","瘟疫病战汗 张某,男，年三十岁，住四川省会理县东门外":"Plague War Sweat Zhang, male, 30 years old, lives outside the east gate of Huili County, Sichuan Province","瘟疫病战汗 张某,男，年三十岁，住四川省会理县东门外。1924年3 月，感瘟疫之邪而病，服前医之方香苏散合升麻葛根汤加羌 活、枳壳、白芷、防风、黄芩等二剂未效。病已八、九日，延余诊 视，壮热烦渴饮冷，请语烦躁，大便不通，小便短赤，脉来洪 数，舌苔黄而生芒刺，唇赤而焦，鼻如烟煤而干燥。此系瘟疫 邪气传里人腑之证，邪热内甚，形成亢阳灼阴，真阴涸竭，急 当釜底抽薪凉下以救真阴。拟白虎合承气汤方加减治之。 生石膏30克，知母13克，生甘草6克，白粳米13克，麦 冬16克，生大黄13克（泡水兑入），芒硝10克，厚朴13克 （炒），枳实12克（炒、捣碎），生地黄13克。 服后下出硬结燥屎一次。次日复诊，病状已减，壮热较 退，口津略生，因瞩照原方再进一剂。 三日复诊。服药后又解润大便三次,身热退去其半,诲语 止，烦渴已减。拟用加味人参白虎汤，养阴生津并除余热。 人参24克，生石膏24克（碎，布包），知母12克，麦冬15 克，生地黄15克，黄连5克，玄参10克，枳壳12克，大黄6 克（泡水兑入），甘草6克，粳米一撮。 服后当晚夜半,忽而肢冷畏寒,继则抖战不可忍，旋即大 汗如洗,热退肤冷,脉微欲绝。斯时病家惶恐不已，促余再诊, 视之则患者脉来缓弱，舌润，口生津液，渴饮已止，呼吸平和。 当即告之,此名“战汗”，为病退之兆,切勿惊扰,但可温覆,否 则战汗出而中止，病当不愈。 四日清晨续诊。唇舌润，苔皮脱，津液满口，已脉静身凉。 大病悉退,进稀粥二碗。继以生脉散加当归、生地黄、杭芍养 阴生津，服二剂而愈。按：“壮火食气”为本病之症结所在。邪热太盛，亢阳灼阴，真阴涸竭，患者已危在旦夕，今得凉下连进，邪热溃退，真阴来复，正气胜邪，“战汗”之作，实为病愈佳兆。吴有性《温疫论》曰：“……忽得战汗，经气输泄，当即脉静身凉，烦渴顿除。”证诸临床，乃切实之经验。":`Plague War Zhang, male, 30 years old, lives outside the east gate of Huili County, Sichuan Province. In March 1924, he contracted the evil of plague and became ill. He took the medicine's prescription of Xiangsu powder and Cimicifuga kudzu decoction plus Qianghuo, Citrus aurantium, Angelica dahurica, Fangfeng and Scutellaria baicalensis, but it was not effective. I have been ill for eight or nine days, and after further examination, I have strong fever, polydipsia and cold drinking, irritable speech, obstructed stool, short red urine, rapid and rapid pulse, yellow tongue coating with thorns, red and burnt lips, and a soot-like and dry nose. This is a sign that the evil spirit of the plague spreads to the human internal organs. The evil heat is so severe that it causes hyperactive yang and scorching yin, and the true yin is exhausted. It is urgent to draw fuel from the bottom of the cauldron and let it cool down to save the true yin. Treat it with the addition and subtraction of Baihu Hechengqi Decoction. 30 grams of raw gypsum, 13 grams of Anemarrhena, 6 grams of raw licorice, 13 grams of white japonica rice, 16 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 13 grams of raw rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed in), 10 grams of Glauber's salt, 13 grams of Magnolia officinalis (fried), 12 grams of Citrus aurantium (fried and mashed), and 13 grams of raw Rehmannia glutinosa. After taking it, I had hard and dry stool once. After a follow-up visit the next day, the symptoms had subsided, the strong fever had subsided, and the mouth fluid was slightly raw, so I took another dose according to the original prescription. Follow-up visit in three days. After taking the medicine, the stool was relieved and moisturized three times. Half of the body heat subsided, the diarrhea stopped, and the polydipsia was reduced. It is planned to use flavored ginseng and white tiger soup to nourish yin, promote fluid production and remove residual heat. 24 grams of ginseng, 24 grams of gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 12 grams of Anemarrhena, 15 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 15 grams of Rehmannia glutinosa, 5 grams of coptis, 10 grams of Scrophulariaceae, 12 grams of Citrus aurantium, 6 grams of rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed with water), 6 grams of licorice, and a pinch of japonica rice. In the middle of the night after taking it, I suddenly felt cold in my limbs, followed by unbearable shivering and trembling. Then I sweated profusely, the heat subsided, my skin became cold, and my pulse was weak and weak. At this time, the patient was panic-stricken and asked for another diagnosis. The patient's pulse was slow and weak, his tongue was moist, his mouth was filled with saliva, his thirst for drinking had ceased, and his breathing was calm. Immediately tell him that this is called "war sweat", which is a sign that the disease is resolving. Do not disturb him, but he can be treated with warmth, otherwise the war sweat will stop and the disease will not be cured. Follow-up consultation on the morning of the 4th. The lips and tongue are moist, the fur and skin are peeling off, the mouth is full of fluid, and the pulse is quiet and the body is cool. The serious illness is gone, and I have two bowls of gruel. Then take Shengmai Powder plus Angelica sinensis, Rehmannia glutinosa and Hangshao to nourish yin and promote fluid production. After taking two doses, the condition will be cured. Note: "Strengthening fire and eating qi" is the crux of the disease. The evil heat is too strong, the yang is scorching the yin, and the true yin is exhausted. The patient is in danger. Today, the cold continues to advance, the evil heat collapses, the true yin comes back, and the righteous energy overcomes the evil. The "fighting sweat" is really a good sign of recovery. Wu Youxing's "Treatise on Warm Epidemics" said: "...Suddenly you experience sweating, menstrual qi is released, your pulse becomes stagnant, your body cools immediately, and your polydipsia is suddenly eliminated." The clinical syndromes are based on practical experience.`,"瘟疫病热深厥深阳极似阴证 马某，男，三十岁，成都人，住四川省会理县北街":"Plague fever is profound and the yin pole is similar to yin syndrome. Ma, male, 30 years old, from Chengdu, lives in Beijie, Huili County, Sichuan Province","瘟疫病热深厥深阳极似阴证 马某，男，三十岁，成都人，住四川省会理县北街。1920年 3月患瘟疫病已七、八日，延余诊视，见其张目仰卧，烦躁请 语,头汗如洗，问其所苦不能答,脉象沉伏欲绝，四肢厥逆,遍 身肤冷。唇焦齿枯，舌干苔黑，起刺如铁钉，口臭气粗。以手试 之,则口气蒸手。小便短赤点滴，大便燥结已数日未通，査其 前服之方，系以羌活、紫苏、荆芥、薄荷、山楂、神曲、枳实、厚 朴、梔子、黄连、升麻、麻黄及葛根等药连进四剂，辛散发表过 甚，真阴被劫，疫邪内壅与阳明燥气相合，复感少阴君火，热 化太过,逼其真阴外越,遂成此热深厥深阳极似阴之证,苟不 急为扑灭,待至真阴灼尽,必殆无救,拟下方治之。 大黄26克（泡水兑入），生石膏30克，枳实15克，厚朴 15克，芒硝10克，知母12克，生地黄60克，黄连10克。 服一剂，病情如故。服二剂后大便始通,脉息沉而虚数， 但仍神识蒙胧，问不能答。照方再服二剂，连下恶臭酱黑粪 便，臭不可当，其后口津略生。又照原方再服二剂，大便始渐 转黄而溏，舌钉渐软,惟舌中部黑苔钉刺尚硬，唇齿稍润，略 识人事，始知其证索饮而渴。进食稀粥少许，照前方去枳实、 厚朴，加天冬、麦冬各15克，沙参20克,生地黄12克，甘草6 克，将大黄分量减半。连进四剂后，人事清醒，津液回生，苔皮 渐退而唇舌已润，惟仍喜冷饮。继以生脉散加味，连服三剂而 愈。 人参15克，麦冬15克，当归10克，生地黄15克，杭白 芍15克，五味子3克，生石膏10克，黄连5克，甘草6克。 按：阳明急下之证，惠者已严重昏愦不省人事，不能询及 渴饮与否，如证见壮热面赤，口气蒸手，唇舌焦燥，鼻如烟熏 等则实热证情已具，即当急下，切勿迟疑，以免贻误病机，证 变难挽。":"Plague fever is profound and the yin pole is similar to yin syndrome. Ma, male, 30 years old, from Chengdu, lives in North Street, Huili County, Sichuan Province. In March 1920, he had been ill with the plague for seven or eight days. After a check-up, he was seen lying on his back with his eyes open, asking for words irritably, sweating all over his head, and unable to answer questions about his sufferings. Burnt lips, withered teeth, dry tongue with black coating, thorns like iron nails, bad breath and thick breath. If you try it with your hands, your breath will steam your hands. The urine was short and red, and the stool had been dry and constipated for several days. After checking the prescription, I found the prescription of Qianhuo, Perilla, Schizonepeta, mint, hawthorn, Shenqu, Fructus Aurantii, Magnolia officinalis, Gardenia, Coptidis, Cimicifuga, Ephedra and Puerariae for four doses. If the pungent powder is too much, the true yin is robbed, the internal congestion of the epidemic evil combines with the Yangming dryness, and the Shaoyin Jun fire is reappeared, causing heat. If it is transformed too much, the true yin will be forced to move outward, resulting in a symptom of deep heat and a deep yang pole similar to yin. If you don't rush to extinguish it, when the true yin is burned out, there will be no hope of salvation, so we plan to treat it below. 26 grams of rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed in), 30 grams of raw gypsum, 15 grams of Citrus aurantium, 15 grams of Magnolia officinalis, 10 grams of Glauber's salt, 12 grams of Anemarrhena, 60 grams of Rehmannia glutinosa, and 10 grams of coptis. After taking one dose, the condition remains the same. After taking two doses, his stool became clear, his pulse was heavy and weak, but his consciousness was still hazy and he could not answer questions. Take two more doses according to the prescription, and the feces will be black with foul-smelling sauce. The smell is unbearable, and the mouth will be slightly raw afterwards. After taking two more doses according to the original prescription, the stool began to turn yellow and loose, the tongue nails gradually became soft, but the black coating in the middle of the tongue was still hard, the lips and teeth were slightly moist, and I knew a little about people and affairs, and then I realized that it was thirsty due to drinking. Eat a little porridge, remove Citrus aurantium and Magnolia officinalis as before, add 15 grams each of Asparagus and Ophiopogon japonicus, 20 grams Adenophora adenophora, 12 grams Rehmannia glutinosa, 6 grams licorice, and halve the amount of rhubarb. After taking four doses in a row, I feel awake, my body fluids are regenerated, my coating gradually recedes and my lips and tongue are moist, but I still like cold drinks. Then take Shengmai Powder with added flavor and take three doses in succession to recover. 15 grams of ginseng, 15 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 10 grams of angelica root, 15 grams of raw rehmannia glutinosa, 15 grams of white peony root, 3 grams of Schisandra chinensis, 10 grams of raw gypsum, 5 grams of coptis, and 6 grams of licorice. Note: In the syndrome of Yang Ming's sudden onset, the patient is severely comatose and unconscious, and cannot ask whether he is thirsty or not. If the patient's face is red with strong heat, his breath is steaming his hands, his lips and tongue are scorched, his nose feels like smoke, etc., then the symptoms of severe heat are already present, so he should be treated urgently. Do not hesitate to avoid delaying the onset of the disease and making the syndrome difficult to cure.","瘟疫病热盛逼阴证 张某，男，川北人，年二十二岁，在四川省会理县北…":"Zhang, male, from northern Sichuan, 22 years old, lives in the north of Huili County, Sichuan Province...","瘟疫病热盛逼阴证 张某，男，川北人，年二十二岁，在四川省会理县北街参 熔衙署充当军士。1921年3月，值瘟疫流行，被染者多，其亦 被传染而发病。高热已十日，延余往诊，刚到该处，见另一军 士掺扶病者出门外小解,小便清长如水，旋即目珠上视,其势 欲脱。速诊其脉，沉数而细，唇焦口燥，苔黄黑而起刺，以手试 之，则口气蒸手,仓卒之时,药石不济,恐阴液脱绝，急以冷水 灌之，连喂二碗，目珠始返回如常，神识转清。询及由来，始知 病已十日，壮热烦渴，大便不通，小便短赤，曾服发表退热药 数剂,汗后身热不退，反见溺多清长。又述及前有两个军士， 同患是病，发表之后，亦见小便清长，旋即死去。此系邪热内 盛,复被发表劫汗，重伤阴液，逼阴外脱之险象,幸喜急灌冷 水以救之，水源不涸竭，真阴未致立亡,急宜凉下以救真阴， 主以承气白虎汤治之。 生石膏30克（碎，布包），知母13克，枳实13克（炒， 捣），生大黄16克（泡水兑入），厚朴13克（炒），芒硝10克， 川黄连10克，粳米10克。 次日复诊，大便已通，下出酱黑燥屎若干，身热已退六、 七，小便反见短赤，此邪热已经溃退，阴液尚未恢复，脉仍沉 数，喜饮清凉,照原方去黄连加麦冬26克。 第三日继诊，病者已汗出热退，脉静身凉，烦躁止，口津 生,唇舌转润，舌苔已退去大半，稍能进食,小便渐转清长,但 仍喜冷饮，以生脉散加味养阴生津而清余热。 沙参15克，麦冬15克，五味子6克，当归16克，生地黄 15克,杭白芍15克，生石膏15克（碎,布包），甘草6克。 连服二剂再诊，舌苔已退净，津液满口，渴饮止，神食较 增，小便已清利如常。遂照原方去石膏加口英26克,生地黄 改为熟地黄15克，连服三剂而愈。":"Zhang, male, from northern Sichuan, 22 years old, works as a sergeant at the Shenrong Yamen Office, Beijie, Huili County, Sichuan Province. In March 1921, during the epidemic of plague, many people were infected, and they were also infected and became ill. I had been suffering from high fever for ten days, so I went to see a doctor. When I arrived there, I saw another soldier helping the patient go out to urinate. His urine was clear and long like water. He immediately looked up and felt that he was about to urinate. Diagnose the pulse quickly and find that it is several and thin, the lips are burnt and the mouth is dry, and the fur is yellow and black and prickly. If you try it with your hands, the breath will steam your hands. In a hurry, the medicine and stones are not enough, and you are afraid that the Yin fluid will be lost, so you rush to pour cold water into it and feed it two bowls. The eyes will return to normal and the consciousness will become clear. When asked about the cause, I found out that I had been ill for ten days and had strong fever, polydipsia, constipation, and short and red urine. I had taken several doses of antipyretic drugs, but the body heat did not go away after sweating. He also mentioned that there were two sergeants who suffered from the same disease. After the publication, they also had clear and clear urine and died immediately. This is a dangerous situation where evil heat is excessive in the body, causing excessive sweating, severely damaging the Yin fluid, and forcing the Yin to escape from the outside. Fortunately, the cold water can be poured in quickly to save the condition. 30 grams of raw gypsum (crushed, wrapped in cloth), 13 grams of Anemarrhena, 13 grams of Citrus aurantium (stir-fried, pounded), 16 grams of raw rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed with water), 13 grams of Magnolia officinalis (stir-fried), 10 grams of Glauber's salt, 10 grams of Sichuan coptis, and 10 grams of japonica rice. After a follow-up visit the next day, the stool was clear, with some black and dry feces. The body heat had subsided for 6 or 7 days, and the urine was short and red. The evil heat had subsided, the yin fluid had not recovered, and the pulse was still heavy and rapid. He liked to drink cool drinks, and added 26 grams of Coptis chinensis and Ophiopogon japonicus according to the original prescription. On the third day of follow-up examination, the patient's sweating and fever subsided, his pulse was quiet and his body was cool, his irritability stopped, his mouth was full of fluids, his lips and tongue became moist, and most of the tongue coating had receded. He was able to eat a little, and his urine gradually became clear and long, but he still liked cold drinks. He took Shengmai Powder with a flavor to nourish yin, promote fluid, and clear away residual heat. 15 grams of Adenophora adenophora, 15 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 6 grams of Schisandra chinensis, 16 grams of Angelica sinensis, 15 grams of Rehmannia glutinosa, 15 grams of white peony root, 15 grams of raw gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), and 6 grams of licorice. After taking two doses, the patient was diagnosed again and found that the tongue coating had receded, the mouth was full of body fluids, thirst was relieved by drinking, the food intake increased, and the urine was clear and clear as usual. Then the original prescription was used to remove the gypsum and add 26 grams of kouying, and the raw rehmannia was replaced with 15 grams of cooked rehmannia. The patient recovered after taking three doses.","瘟疫病燥热内结证 谢某之妻，车姓，年十八岁，住四川省会理县南街":"Plague syndrome with internal heat syndrome Xie’s wife, surnamed Che, is 18 years old and lives in South Street, Huili County, Sichuan Province","瘟疫病燥热内结证 谢某之妻，车姓，年十八岁，住四川省会理县南街。于 1920年3月，感瘟疫病邪，发病已二日，起始则见发热而渴， 恶热而不寒,头痛体痛,脉浮弦而数，唇赤面垢,舌白如积粉。 病虽初起,但邪不在经,若发汗,则既伤表气又易耗损津液， 势必热邪愈炽。此乃瘟疫之邪蟠踞募原，有入里化燥伤津之 势,宜输转募原之邪,使之达表而解，以达原饮加石膏主之。 槟榔10克，厚朴10克，草果10克，知母12克，杭白芍 12克，黄芩10克，甘草6克，生石膏15克（碎，布包）。 服一剂后，证情稍减，惟大便已三日燥结不通，于是续前 方加大黄12克，嘱即服。因患者之父略知医理，认为该女素 体虚弱，恐不能耐受寒下之剂，竟私自将大黄、石膏减去未 用。隔日延余再诊，见患者舌苔转黄而燥，胃实胸满,拒按呼 痛,烦渴饮冷,小便短赤,大便仍燥结,壮热未解,时发谵语。 此系邪已入腑，燥热结滞，非清热泻下不能力挽危绝。当即拟 白虎加承气汤合方一剂。其父仍有难色，不敢与服。随后，患 者忽鼻衄不止，色鲜红而量较多，稍顷，衄血即凝而成块。病 家惶恐，另延中医彭某诊视，断为阳虚亡血之证,且谓如系热 证，鼻衄流出之后，必不致凝结成块,主以四逆汤。病家疑虑， 踌躇无决，仍不敢与服之。又复求询于余，余据理解释，力说 病家:此乃邪热亢极灼阴之证,急宜大剂凉下以救真阴，缓则 真阴灼尽，危殆难治。又告之，余素谙于用姜附者，尚不敢以 温热之剂妄投，当此证情,苦寒泻下尤恐不及,倘若误服温热之剂,犹如火上浇油,危亡立至。因余力主,病家始而信服,遂 拟方清热凉下治之。 生石膏60克（碎，布包），生大黄30克（泡水兑入），枳实 20克（捣），厚朴20克，芒硝13克，知母20克，生地黄16克， 甘草6克。 上方煎汤日夜连进之后，鼻衄方止,神识转清,身热退去 六七。次日照原方再服一剂，服后则二便通畅,脉静身凉,惟仍 渴思冷饮,此系余热未净、津液未复所致,以生脉散加味治之。 沙参30克，麦冬13克，五味子6克，当归16克，生地黄 16克，杭白芍16克，石膏16克，大黄6克。 连服三剂，渴饮止，津液满口。其后于此方减去石膏、大黄连服三剂而痊。":"Plague syndrome with internal heat syndrome Xie's wife, surnamed Che, is 18 years old and lives in South Street, Huili County, Sichuan Province. In March 1920, I contracted the plague pathogen. It had been two days since the onset of the disease. At first, I experienced fever and thirst, aversion to heat but not cold, headache and body aches, floating and rapid pulse, red lips and dirty face, and a white tongue like accumulated powder. Although the disease starts at the beginning, the evil is not in the meridians. If sweating occurs, it will not only damage the superficial qi but also easily consume body fluids, and the heat evil will inevitably become more intense. This is because the pathogenic factors of the plague are occupying the source of the disease and have the potential to enter the body and transform into dryness, damaging the body fluids. It is advisable to transfer the evil of the source of the disease to the source of the disease, allowing it to express itself and resolve it, so as to achieve the effect of removing the original evil by drinking gypsum. 10 grams of betel nut, 10 grams of magnolia bark, 10 grams of grass fruit, 12 grams of anemarrhena, 12 grams of white peony root, 10 grams of skullcap, 6 grams of licorice, and 15 grams of gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth). After taking one dose, the symptoms were slightly relieved, but the stool had been dry and blocked for three days, so I continued the prescription and added 12 grams of rhubarb, and took it immediately. Because the patient's father knew a little about medical science, he thought that the woman was weak and might not be able to tolerate the cold medicine, so he secretly subtracted the rhubarb and gypsum without using them. The next day's follow-up examination revealed that the patient's tongue coating had turned yellow and dry, his stomach was full and his chest was full, he refused to press his fingers and had pain when breathing, he was thirsty and drank cold water, his urine was short and red, his stools were still dry and congested, his strong fever was not relieved, and he sometimes suffered from delirium. This type of evil has entered the fu organs, resulting in stagnation of dryness and heat. Unless it is cleared of heat and purged, it is impossible to cure the disease. Immediately prepare a dose of Baihu plus Chengqi Decoction. His father was still embarrassed and did not dare to submit. Subsequently, the patient suddenly suffered from epistaxis, which was bright red in color and large in amount. After a while, the epistaxis coagulated into clumps. The patient was frightened, so another Chinese medicine doctor Peng made a diagnosis and diagnosed the condition as a syndrome of yang deficiency and blood loss. He also said that if it was a heat syndrome, the epistaxis would not coagulate into lumps after it flowed out, so he prescribed Sini Decoction. The patient has doubts, is hesitant, and still dare not accept the treatment. He asked Yu again, and Yu explained it logically and said to the patient: This is a sign of excessive heat and extreme burning of the Yin. If it is urgent, it is better to cool it down with a large dose to save the true Yin. If it is slow, the true Yin will be burned out, making it difficult to treat the critical condition. He also told me that those who are familiar with the use of ginger do not dare to take warm medicines rashly. In this condition, bitter cold and diarrhea are especially fearful. If you accidentally take warm medicines, it will be like adding fuel to the fire, and you will be in danger. Because of the remaining strength, the patient was convinced, so he formulated a prescription to clear away heat and cool down to treat it. 60 grams of raw gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 30 grams of raw rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed with water), 20 grams of Citrus aurantium (pounded), 20 grams of Magnolia officinalis, 13 grams of Glauber's salt, 20 grams of Anemarrhena, 16 grams of Rehmannia glutinosa, and 6 grams of licorice. After decoction above day and night, epistaxis will stop, consciousness will become clearer, and body heat will subside for six to seven days. The next day, take another dose of the original prescription. After taking it, the stools will be unobstructed, the pulse will be quiet, and the body will be cool, but the patient will still be thirsty and long for cold drinks. This is caused by residual heat that has not been purified and the body fluids have not recovered. It can be treated with Shengmai Powder with added flavor. 30 grams of Adenophora, 13 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 6 grams of Schisandra chinensis, 16 grams of Angelicae Sinensis, 16 grams of Rehmannia glutinosa, 16 grams of white peony root, 16 grams of gypsum, and 6 grams of rhubarb. After taking three doses in a row, thirst will be stopped and your mouth will be full of body fluids. Later, the patient recovered after taking three doses of this prescription minus plaster and rhubarb.",瘟疫病狂汗:"Plague Sweat","瘟疫病狂汗 张某，男，四川人，年廿四岁，住四川省会理县北街，禀赋 充盛,1920年4月感瘟疫病邪。病已三日，延余诊视,发热而 渴不恶寒,小便短赤，大便三日未解，脉来洪数,舌苔白腻如 积粉,舌尖绛红而燥，面部垢腻。此系募原疫邪有渐入于里化 热之势,宜输转募原之邪,兼消入里之热,加味达原饮治之。 槟榔13克，厚朴10克，草果10克，知母13克，杭白芍 16克，黄芩13克，甘草6克，生石膏30克，葛根13克，大黄 13克（泡水，兑入）。 服一剂后,病者旋即发狂乱奔,病家以为误服凉药之咎， 促余再行诊视，见其口舌转润，脉象已较前转平，且有微汗。 当即告知病家,此乃“狂汗”，系病退之征，稍待汗出即愈，遂 嘱再服前药。服药一碗，即令使覆卧。俄顷，大汗淋漓,约三刻 钟后,狂躁止,脉静身凉,霍然而愈。 按：吴有性《温疫论》云：“狂汗者，伏邪中溃，欲作汗解， 因其人禀赋充盛，阳气冲击，不能顿开……”今得药力相助， 输转募原之邪以达于表而解，邪随汗去，则狂证焉有再作之 理。":`Plague Disease Sweating Zhang, male, 24 years old, from Sichuan, lived in North Street, Huili County, Sichuan Province, with abundant natural resources. He contracted the plague in April 1920. She has been ill for three days and has not yet been examined. She has fever but no aversion to cold, thirst, short red urine, and unresolved stools for three days. Her pulse is rapid and rapid, her tongue coating is white and greasy like accumulated powder, the tip of her tongue is red and dry, and her face is greasy and dirty. This is because the original epidemic evil has the tendency to gradually enter the interior and transform into heat. It is advisable to transfer the original evil and eliminate the heat entering the interior. It can be cured by adding the original drink with added flavor. 13 grams of betel nut, 10 grams of magnolia bark, 10 grams of grass fruit, 13 grams of anemarrhena, 16 grams of white peony root, 13 grams of skullcap, 6 grams of licorice, 30 grams of gypsum, 13 grams of kudzu root, and 13 grams of rhubarb (soak in water and mix in). After taking one dose, the patient immediately started to run wildly. The patient believed that he had mistakenly taken the cold medicine, so he examined me again and found that his mouth and tongue had become moist, his pulse had become flatter than before, and he had slight sweating. The patient was immediately informed that this was "crazy sweating" and was a sign of remission of the disease. He would be cured after sweating for a while, and he was instructed to take the medicine again. Take a bowl of medicine, even if you lie down. After a while, I was sweating profusely. After about three quarters of an hour, my mania stopped, my pulse was still and my body was cool, and I suddenly recovered. Note: Wu Youxing's "Treatise on Warm Epidemics" says: "Those who sweat violently suffer from subdued evil and want to sweat to relieve it, because the human endowment is full and the yang energy is impacted and cannot be relieved..." Now with the help of medicine, the original evil can be transferred to the surface and resolved. If the evil goes away with sweating, then there is no reason for the recurrence of mad syndrome.`,"瘟疫病狂汗 张某，男，四川人，年廿四岁，住四川省会理县北街，禀赋…":"Sweating violently due to plague Zhang, male, 24 years old, from Sichuan, lives in North Street, Huili County, Sichuan Province, endowed with...","瘟疫病狂汗案 张某，男.四川人，年24岁，禀赋充盛":"Case of plague-related sweating: Zhang, male, from Sichuan, 24 years old, full of talents","瘟疫病狂汗案\\n张某，男.四川人，年24岁，禀赋充盛。1920年4月感瘟疫病邪，病已3日，延余诊视：发热而渴不恶寒，小便短赤，大便3日未解，脉来洪数，舌苔白腻如积粉，舌尖绛红而燥，面部垢腻此系膜原疫邪有渐入于里化热之势，宜输转膜原之邪，兼消入里之热，加味达原饮治之：\\n槟榔13g，厚朴10g，草果10g，知母13g，杭芍16g，黄芩I3g，甘草6g，生石膏30g，葛根13g，大黄13g（泡水兑入）。\\n服1剂后，病者旋即发狂乱奔，病家以为误服凉药之咎，促余再行诊视。见其口舌转润，脉象已较前转平，且有微汗。当即告知病家，此乃“狂汗”，系病退之征，稍待汗出即愈，遂嘱再服前药。服药一碗，即令使覆卧。俄顷，大汗淋漓，约三刻钟后狂躁止，脉静身凉，霍然而愈。\\n原按：吴又可《瘟邪论》云：“狂汗者，伏邪中溃，欲作汗解，因其人禀赋充盛，阳气冲击，不能顿开……。”今得药力相助，输转膜原之邪以达于表而解，邪随汗去，则狂证焉有再作之理。":`Case of plague fever\\nZhang, male, from Sichuan, 24 years old, with abundant talents. In April 1920, I contracted the plague pathogen. I had been ill for 3 days. After a follow-up examination, I found: fever with thirst but no aversion to cold, short red urine, unresolved stool for 3 days, heavy and rapid pulse, white and greasy tongue coating like accumulated powder, red and dry tongue tip, and greasy facial stains. The original evil can also eliminate the heat that enters the body, and can be cured by adding the original drink:\\nBetel nut 13g, Magnolia officinalis 10g, Cao Guo 10g, Anemarrhena 13g, Hangshao 16g, Scutellaria baicalensis 13g, Licorice 6g, Gypsum 30g, Pueraria lobata 13g, Rhubarb 13g (soak in water and mix in). \\nAfter taking 1 dose, the patient immediately ran wildly. The patient believed that he had mistakenly taken the cold medicine and urged me to see him again. His mouth and tongue became moist, his pulse became flatter than before, and he had slight sweating. The patient was immediately informed that this was "crazy sweating" and was a sign of remission of the disease. He would be cured after a short period of sweating, and he was instructed to take the medicine again. Take a bowl of medicine, even if you lie down. For a while, I was sweating profusely. After about three quarters of an hour, the mania stopped. My pulse was still and my body was cool, and I suddenly recovered. \\nOriginal note: Wu Youke's "Treatise on Plague Evils" says: "Those who sweat violently suffer from subdued evils and want to sweat to relieve them. Because the human endowment is full and the yang energy is impacted, it cannot be opened..." Now with the help of medicine, the evils of the original membrane can be transferred to the surface and resolved.`,"瘟疫病误治变证转阳极似阴证 张某之妻，年四旬余，四川省会理县人，…":"Mistreatment of plague causes the syndrome to change from yang to yin. Zhang’s wife, in her forties, is from Huili County, Sichuan Province...","瘟疫病误治变证转阳极似阴证 张某之妻，年四旬余，四川省会理县人，体质素弱，患痰 饮哮喘咳嗽多年，屡服滋阴清肺之药罔效，余拟以小青龙汤 加附子及四逆二陈加麻辛汤等治之，服十多剂后病愈而复健 康。数年后，于1920年3月感染时疫。初起发热而渴、头体 痛。某医以九味羌活汤加麻黄、桂枝一剂，服后，则汗出而昏 厥。延余诊视，脉沉伏欲绝，肢厥肤冷，唇焦齿枯、口不能张， 问其所苦不能答。此系瘟疫误表过汗伤阴，疫邪传入阳明之 腑,复感少阴君火，热化太过，亢阳灼阴，真阴欲绝，邪热内逼 致使真阴外越，遂成阳极似阴之证。急与清热养阴生津之剂， 方用生脉散煎汁、频频喂服。 米洋参10克，麦冬26克，北五味子6克，生甘草6克。 药汤下咽后数刻，脉来沉数，肢厥渐回，口气仍蒸手。邪 热未溃仍照前方加生石膏50克,生地黄40克,知母、贝母各 30克。 是晚再诊视，脉来洪数，人事稍清，视其苔黄黑而生芒 刺，壮热渴喜冷饮,小便短赤,大便燥结不通。《内经》云：“热 深者厥亦深也。”今得前二方以济之，促其真阴内回，阳热始 通，故反呈现壮热烦渴饮冷等证,邪热内炽不退,燥结阳明， 真阴仍有涸竭之虞。当即主以凉下救真阴，拟白虎承气汤加 味一剂。 生石膏26克，知母16克，沙参16克，生大黄10克（泡 水兑入），枳实13克，厚朴13克，芒硝6克，生甘草6克，黄 连5克，生地黄16克。 服一剂后，大便始通,苔刺渐软,身热稍退。又服二剂，热 退六、七，口津稍回，仍渴喜冷饮。续服第三剂，乃下黑燥粪， 恶臭已极,热退七、八，已不见渴，稍进稀粥。又照此方去枳、 朴,加天冬、麦冬各40克,连进二剂后,脉静身凉,津液满口， 惟尚喜冷饮，仍照原方去芒硝，并将石膏、大黄减半，加入当 归16克、杭白芍13克，连进四剂而愈。继以四物汤加党参、 黄苗,调理十余日而康复。":`The plague disease was mistreated and the yang pole turned into a yin syndrome. Zhang's wife was in her forties and a native of Huili County, Sichuan Province. She had a weak constitution and suffered from phlegm-draining asthma and cough for many years. Her repeated use of medicines for nourishing yin and clearing the lungs had no effect. I planned to treat the disease with Xiaoqinglong Decoction plus Aconite and Sini Erchen plus Maxin Decoction. After taking more than ten doses, she recovered and recovered. A few years later, he contracted the epidemic in March 1920. At first, he had fever, thirst, head and body pain. A certain doctor added a dose of Jiuwei Qianghuo Decoction with ephedra and cinnamon twig. After taking it, he would sweat and faint. After further examination, the pulse was deep and weak, the limbs were cold and the skin was cold, the lips were burnt, the teeth were dry, and the mouth could not be opened. When asked about the pain, he could not answer. This is caused by the plague mistakenly manifesting as excessive sweating and damaging the yin. The plague evil is introduced into the Yangming's fu organs, and the Shaoyin king's fire is re-infected. The heat is too high, the yang is overheated and the yin is burnt, and the true yin is extinguished. The evil heat is forced inward, causing the true yin to move outward, thus forming a syndrome where the yang pole resembles yin. For urgent and clearing away heat, nourishing yin and promoting fluid production, use Shengmai Powder decoction and take it frequently. 10 grams of Panax quinquefolius, 26 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 6 grams of Schisandra chinensis, and 6 grams of raw licorice. A few moments after swallowing the medicinal soup, my pulse came and went, my limbs gradually returned, and my breath was still steaming. If the evil heat has not broken down yet, add 50 grams of gypsum, 40 grams of rehmannia glutinosa, 30 grams each of Anemarrhena and Fritillaria. Check again later in the evening. The pulse is strong and rapid, and the body is slightly clear. The coating is yellow and black with thorns, strong heat and thirst, and a preference for cold drinks. The urine is short and red, and the stool is dry and blocked. "Nei Jing" says: "If the heat is deep, the cold will also be deep." Now we can use the first two methods to help it, promote the internal return of true yin, and the yang heat will begin to unblock. Therefore, symptoms such as strong heat, polydipsia, and cold drinking will appear instead. Evil heat will not subside internally, and dryness will bind yang. There is still a risk of true yin drying up. Immediately use cooling to relieve the true yin, and add a dose of Baihu Chengqi Decoction. 26 grams of raw gypsum, 16 grams of Anemarrhena, 16 grams of Adenophora, 10 grams of raw rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed with water), 13 grams of Citrus aurantium, 13 grams of Magnolia officinalis, 6 grams of Glauber's salt, 6 grams of raw licorice, 5 grams of coptis, and 16 grams of raw rehmannia. After taking one dose, the stool becomes clear, the prickly fur gradually softens, and the body heat subsides slightly. After taking two more doses, the fever subsided by six to seven degrees, the mouth fluid returned slightly, and she was still thirsty and preferred cold drinks. After taking the third dose, the feces was black and dry, the stench was extremely bad, the fever subsided for seven to eight days, the thirst was no longer felt, and a little gruel was eaten. Follow this recipe to remove Trifoliate Aurantium and Puccini, add 40 grams each of Asparagus and Ophiopogon japonicus. After taking two doses, the pulse is still and the body is cool, and the body fluid is full of mouth. However, I still like cold drinks, so I still follow the original recipe and remove Glauber's salt, and halve the gypsum and rhubarb. Add 16 grams of Angelica sinensis and 13 grams of Hangzhou white peony root. After taking four doses, it will be cured. After taking Siwu Decoction with Codonopsis pilosula and Huangmiao, the patient recovered after more than ten days of conditioning.`,"瘟疫病阳明急下证 陈某之父，四川省会理县鹿厂牛上坎农民":"Yang Ming urgently confirmed the plague. Chen’s father is a farmer in Niu Shangkan, Luchang, Huili County, Sichuan Province.","瘟疫病阳明急下证 陈某之父，四川省会理县鹿厂牛上坎农民。年虽六旬，体 素康健。1916年4月初，因事赴邻村，值村中时疫流行，遂被 传染。返家数日，忽觉胸闷食少,头昏体困，口燥思饮而起病。 初起即感慷慷憎寒,继则发热，渴思冷饮,头体疼痛，小便短 少，其色如茶，病卧已七、八日，自服发表消导药二剂无效，始 延余诊视。脉来洪数，唇焦口燥，舌苔厚腻，边白中黄而生芒 刺。但头汗出,余处无汗,壮热烦渴饮冷,时发谵语,小便短涩 但又随时点滴遗出。大便已六、七日不通,腹满而不能食。此乃 瘟疫误于表散，大伤真阴，疫毒传入阳明之腑，邪热内蒸而呈 是状,急宜凉下以救真阴,拟仲景大承气汤加石膏、麦冬,急下 救阴,犹釜底抽薪之意,务将胃肠中之邪热疫毒下尽为度。 大黄16克（泡水兑入），芒硝3克（后放），枳实13克（炒， 捣），厚朴13克（炒），生石膏30克（碎,布包），麦冬26克。 此方煎服三次后，畅下黑酱粪半小桶之多,臭不可当，身 热约退七、八，口津渐回,苔刺变软,请语止，小便已不滴遗， 稍见清长,色仍黄,仍渴喜冷饮，当即索取石缸内冰凉冷水一 碗与饮之，饮后病者自云心中爽快，再饮一碗，顿觉全身清 凉,竟得安卧熟寐片刻。余热未尽,继拟小承气汤加清热养阴 生津以治之。 沙参16克，生石膏15克（碎,布包），枳壳10克，麦冬16 克，厚朴10克，生地黄13克，玄参10克，大黄6克（泡水兑 入）。 服二剂后,大便溏泻数次,色由酱黑而渐次转黄,脉静身 凉，津液满口，苔皮退去八、九,烦渴止，已能进稀粥少许。拟 方： 沙参20克，杭白芍10克，生地黄13克，麦冬13克，北 口芪30克，当归13克，甘草6克。 连服三剂，食增神健,诸证全瘳。":"Yang Ming’s urgent diagnosis of the plague Chen’s father is a farmer in Niu Shangkan, Luchang, Huili County, Sichuan Province. Although he is sixty years old, he is in good health. In early April 1916, I went to a neighboring village for business. There was an epidemic in the village and I was infected. After returning home for a few days, he suddenly felt chest tightness, less food, dizziness, sleepiness, dry mouth and craving for drinking. At the beginning, he felt a strong aversion to cold, followed by fever, thirst for cold drinks, pain in the head and body, and short urine with a color like tea. He had been lying in bed for seven or eight days. Two doses of self-administered antibiotics were ineffective, and he was delayed for further examination. The pulse is rapid and rapid, the lips are burnt and the mouth is dry, the tongue coating is thick and greasy, the edges are white and the middle is yellow, and there are thorns. But there is sweating on the head, no sweating in the rest of the body, strong heat, polydipsia and cold drinking, occasional delirium, short and astringent urine but dribbling out at any time. I have been unable to pass stool for six or seven days, and my abdomen is full and I cannot eat. This is because the plague mistakenly dispersed on the surface, severely injuring the true yin. The epidemic poison was introduced into the yangming organs, and the evil heat steamed in the internal organs. It is like this. In an emergency, it is better to cool down to save the true yin. Zhongjing Dachengqi Decoction is added with gypsum and Ophiopogon japonicus, and it is urgently taken to save the yin. It is like drawing fuel from the bottom of the cauldron, so as to eliminate all the evil heat and epidemic poison in the gastrointestinal tract. 16 grams of rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed in), 3 grams of Glauber's salt (added later), 13 grams of Citrus aurantium (fried and pounded), 13 grams of Magnolia officinalis (fried), 30 grams of gypsum (crushed, wrapped in cloth), and 26 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus. After decoction of this prescription for three times, I drank half a small bucket of black sauce feces, which was unbearable. The body heat subsided by about 7 to 8 minutes. The fluid in my mouth gradually returned, and the thorns on the coating became soft. Please stop talking. The urine was no longer dribbling. It was slightly clear and long, but the color was still yellow. I was still thirsty and liked cold drinks. I immediately asked for a bowl of cold water from the stone vat and drank it. After drinking it, the patient felt refreshed. After drinking another bowl, his whole body felt cool, and he could lie down and sleep for a while. If the residual heat is not exhausted, add Xiaochengqi Decoction to clear away heat, nourish yin and produce fluid to treat it. 16 grams of Adenophora, 15 grams of gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 10 grams of Citrus aurantium, 16 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 10 grams of Magnolia officinalis, 13 grams of Rehmannia glutinosa, 10 grams of Scrophulariaceae, and 6 grams of rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed in). After taking two doses, I had loose stools several times, the color gradually turned from black to yellow, my pulse was quiet and cool, my mouth was full of body fluids, my fur had receded eight or nine times, my polydipsia had ceased, and I could eat a little gruel. Preparation: 20 grams of adenophora, 10 grams of white peony root, 13 grams of raw rehmannia root, 13 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 30 grams of Beikou Qi, 13 grams of angelica root, and 6 grams of licorice. Take three doses in a row, the food will increase the spirit and health, and all symptoms will be relieved.","瘟疫病阳明燥实证 李某，男，年二十五岁，四川省会理县南乡农民":"Evidence of plague caused by Yangmingzao Li, male, 25 years old, farmer from Nanxiang, Huili County, Sichuan Province","瘟疫病阳明燥实证 李某，男，年二十五岁，四川省会理县南乡农民。1921年 3月感时疫而病,发热十二日不退，脉来洪数,舌苔黄黑而生 芒刺，唇焦齿干，口气蒸手,值午后则热势更张，澈澈汗出，谵语烦躁不能安卧。小便短赤,大便自病后十余日不通,从心下 至少腹胀满，呻吟呼痛而拒按，仰卧难以转侧，食物不进，惟 烦渴而喜冷饮。此际邪热亢甚，阴津枯涸，燥屎内结，阳明下 证悉具。当急下以救阴，缓则危殆。思及亢热已久，燥屎坚结， 无阴液以润泽，如行舟之乏水,邪热燥结亦无所由出，宜于急 下之剂兼以养阴生津之品以治之,拟加味黄龙汤一剂。 土人参30克，当归26克，生地黄16克，大黄16克（泡 水兑入），芒硝10克（后放），枳实16克，厚朴16克，生石膏 26克（碎，布包）。 当晚服后，病者欲便，但十分费力而难于解出，用力挣 之，则燥屎一节，缓慢而出，长约尺许坚硬不断，色酱黑。余亲 视之,真坚硬如鞭。次晨诊视,其脉已较和缓，发热已退其半， 苔刺变软，口津稍润，腹中胀痛大减，仍渴喜冷饮，嘱照原方 再服一剂。第三日诊，大便畅通，色转黄而溏，斯时已脉静身 凉，能进米粥。査其舌，见苔已退去其半，津液回生，但仍喜冷 饮,此乃邪热始退,阴津尚未完全恢复,拟生脉散加味养阴生 津兼清余热。 沙参26克，麦冬16克，五味子3克，甘草6克，生地黄 16克，玄参13克，黄连5克。 服二剂后，继以六味地黄汤调理阴分，一、二剂而愈。 生地黄26克，粉丹皮10克，山茱萸（枣皮）10克，淮山药 13克，茯苓13克，泽泻10克。":"Evidence of Yangming Dryness of Plague Disease Li, male, 25 years old, a farmer in Nanxiang, Huili County, Sichuan Province. In March 1921, he contracted an epidemic and became ill. He had a fever that did not subside for 12 days, a rapid and rapid pulse, a yellow and black tongue coating with thorns, scorched lips and dry teeth, and breath that made his hands steam. In the afternoon, the fever became more intense, he sweated profusely, he was delirium, irritable, and unable to lie down. The urine is short and red, and the stool has been blocked for more than ten days since the illness. The abdomen is distended and full from the heart down, and the patient moans in pain and refuses to press. It is difficult to turn on the side when lying on the back. He cannot eat, but he is thirsty and prefers cold drinks. At this time, the evil heat is extremely high, the yin and body fluids are dried up, dry feces is accumulated in the body, and the symptoms of yangming are lower. If it is urgent, it will save Yin, if it is slow, it will be in danger. I have been thinking about excessive heat for a long time, dry stools are hard and solid, and there is no Yin liquid to moisten them, just like running out of water, and the evil heat and dryness knots have no source. It is suitable to use a medicine that nourishes yin and promotes body fluid to treat it. I plan to add a dose of Huanglong Decoction. 30 grams of native ginseng, 26 grams of Angelica sinensis, 16 grams of Rehmannia glutinosa, 16 grams of rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed in), 10 grams of Glauber's salt (added later), 16 grams of Citrus aurantium, 16 grams of Magnolia officinalis, and 26 grams of gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth). After taking it that night, the patient wanted to defecate, but it was very laborious and difficult to defecate. If he tried hard to pull it out, a piece of dry feces would come out slowly, about a foot long, hard and continuous, and black in color. Yu Qin looked at it, it was as hard as a whip. Examination the next morning revealed that her pulse was gentler, her fever had subsided by half, her prickly fur had softened, her mouth was slightly moist, her abdominal distension and pain were greatly reduced, and she was still thirsty and preferred cold drinks. She was instructed to take another dose according to the original prescription. On the third day of diagnosis, the stool was smooth, turned yellow and loose, and the pulse was still and the body was cool, and rice porridge could be eaten. Check his tongue and see that half of the coating has receded and the body fluid has returned to life, but he still likes cold drinks. This is because the evil heat has just subsided and the yin and fluid have not fully recovered. Xiushengmai Powder is flavored to nourish yin, generate fluid and clear residual heat. 26 grams of Adenophora, 16 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 3 grams of Schisandra chinensis, 6 grams of licorice, 16 grams of Rehmannia glutinosa, 13 grams of Scrophulariaceae, and 5 grams of coptis. After taking two doses, use Liuwei Dihuang Decoction to regulate the yin, and the symptoms will be cured after one or two doses. 26 grams of raw rehmannia glutinosa, 10 grams of pink bark, 10 grams of dogwood (jujube bark), 13 grams of yam, 13 grams of poria, and 10 grams of Alisma.","白通汤救治县长女 1929年，当时的蒙自县县长之女廖子庚，年15岁":"Baitongtang treated the county magistrate’s daughter. In 1929, Liao Zigeng, the daughter of the then magistrate of Mengzi County, was 15 years old.","白通汤救治县长女\\n1929年，当时的蒙自县县长之女廖子庚，年15岁。冬季患伤寒症，经某西医诊治，身热20余日不退，该医施尽各种方法未效，遂力主注射灌脓针。此前有一张连长，亦患是病，打灌脓针热仍不退，且打针处竟溃烂至骨，逐日流清浓淡血水，形成骷髅，神识昏愦，竟至不起，临死热仍不退。廖女今即由该医诊治，有鉴于此，闻之生惧，故未敢轻试。即延吴佩衡诊视，视其舌黑唇焦，面青颧赤，脉浮大而空，神昏谵语，夜则尤重。判断为伤寒寒入少阴，阴盛格阳之症，以白通加人尿猪胆汁汤为治1剂后即汗出淋漓，脉静身凉；继以扶阳辅正，3剂而痊。（《驳冯友兰论中西医药》）":`Bai Tongtang treats the county magistrate's daughter\\nIn 1929, Liao Zigeng, the daughter of the then magistrate of Mengzi County, was 15 years old. I suffered from typhoid fever in winter. After being diagnosed and treated by a Western doctor, my body fever did not go away for more than 20 days. The doctor tried various methods but failed, so he insisted on injecting pus-filled needles. Previously, there was a company commander who also suffered from this disease. The fever did not go away after the injection of pus, and the injection site actually ulcerated to the bone. He oozed thick and light blood day by day, forming a skeleton. He was unconscious and could not even stand up. The death fever still did not go away. Ms. Liao was diagnosed and treated by this doctor now. In view of this, she was frightened after hearing about it, so she did not dare to try it lightly. Immediately after Yan Wu Peiheng's examination, he found that his tongue was black and his lips were burnt, his face was green and his cheeks were red, his pulse was large and empty, he was dizzy and delirium, especially at night. It was judged that the disease was caused by typhoid fever entering Shaoyin, with excess of Yin interfering with Yang. After one dose of Baitong plus Human Urine and Pig Bile Decoction, the patient started to sweat profusely and the pulse was still and cool. After three doses, the patient recovered. ("Refutation of Feng Youlan's Discussion on Chinese and Western Medicine")`,"益气健脾，活血通络，清热解毒":"Replenishing qi and strengthening the spleen, promoting blood circulation and dredging collaterals, clearing away heat and detoxifying",目录:"Directory",目赤肿痛:"Red, swollen and painful eyes","目赤肿痛 张某，男，五十岁":"Red, swollen and painful eyes Zhang, male, 50 years old","目赤肿痛 张某，男，五十岁。始因风寒外感，发热，恶寒，头身疼痛， 全身不适。次日，双目发赤,红肿疼痛,畏光而多眵。察其脉，沉 细而紧，舌质淡,苔薄白而润。此乃风寒袭表，经脉血络受阻， 凝滞不通所致。治以温经解表，发寒通络。方用加味麻黄附子 细辛汤。 附片30克，麻黄6克，细辛5克，桂枝9克，防风9克， 橘络5克，沙苑蒺藜9克，甘草6克，生姜3片。 煎服一次，温覆而卧，得微汗出。一剂尽，则表证已解，目 赤肿痛均已消退。惟阳神尚虚，头昏肢软，双目略感发胀。继 以益气通络明目之剂治之。 北口芪24克，细辛3克，橘络3克，沙苑蒺藜6克，蝉蜕5 克，藁本9克，女贞子9克，益智仁9克，兖蔚子6克，干姜9 克，甘草6克。 服上方二剂而痊。":"Red, swollen and painful eyes Zhang, male, 50 years old. It started with exogenous wind and cold, fever, aversion to cold, head and body pain, and general malaise. The next day, my eyes were red, swollen, painful, and photophobic. Observe the pulse, which is deep, thin and tight, the tongue is light, and the fur is thin, white and moist. This is caused by wind and cold attacking the surface, blocking the meridians and blood vessels, and causing stagnation. The treatment is to warm the meridians and relieve the superficial symptoms, and to relieve cold and dredge collaterals. Use flavored ephedra, aconite and asarum soup. 30 grams of Futian, 6 grams of Ephedra, 5 grams of Asarum, 9 grams of Guizhi, 9 grams of Fangfeng, 5 grams of Juluo, 9 grams of Tribulus terrestris, 6 grams of licorice, and 3 slices of ginger. Decoct and take it once, warm it while lying down, and you will sweat slightly. After one dose is used up, the superficial symptoms will be resolved and the redness, swelling and pain in the eyes will subside. However, the yang spirit is still weak, the limbs are dizzy and the limbs are weak, and the eyes are slightly swollen. Then treat it with an agent that replenishes qi, unblocks collaterals and improves eyesight. 24 grams of Beikou Qi, 3 grams of Asarum, 3 grams of Tangerine, 6 grams of Tribulus terrestris, 5 grams of Cicada slough, 9 grams of Ligusticum lucidum, 9 grams of Ligustrum lucidum, 9 grams of Aizhirenzi, 6 grams of Yanweizi, 9 grams of dried ginger, and 6 grams of licorice. He recovered after taking two doses of the above.","目赤肿痛案 朱某之次子，1923年腊月诞生10余日":"Case of red, swollen and painful eyes Zhu’s second son was born more than 10 days after the twelfth lunar month in 1923","目赤肿痛案\\n朱某之次子，1923年腊月诞生10余日。忽目赤而肿，乳后即吐，大便色绿，夜啼不休。舌白，指纹含青。儿母素体虚寒，致小儿先天禀赋不足，脾阳虚弱，健运失司，无以制水，里寒夹肝气横逆而侮脾，元阳不潜，附肝而上，冲及于目，此虚阳浮越所致。法宜回阳收纳为要，拟附子甘草汤加生姜治之。附子10g，甘草3g，生姜2小片。\\n服1剂，啼声止；2剂则目肿渐消，大便转黄。如此4剂痊愈。\\n原按：世习一见目病赤肿，动辄言火，其实不尽如此。眼科病证，名目繁多，括其要总不离乎外感、内伤两法以判之，不论内外、感伤，若见目赤肿痛，雾障羞明，其证各有虚实寒热之不同，必须按六经、八纲之理明辨施治，不可固守一法以邀幸中“余非专于目疾者，然其治法要领，经旨互通矣。":`Case of red, swollen and painful eyes\\nZhu’s second son was born on the 10th day of the twelfth lunar month in 1923. Suddenly the eyes become red and swollen, vomiting occurs immediately after breastfeeding, the stool is green, and the patient cries endlessly at night. The tongue is white and the fingerprints are blue. The mother's body is deficient and cold, resulting in the child's innate endowment being insufficient, the spleen yang being weak, the movement losing control, and being unable to control water. The cold inside is holding the liver qi in reverse and insulting the spleen. The primordial yang is not submerged, but attaches to the liver and rises up, rushing to the eyes. This is caused by the floating of the deficient yang. The main method is to restore Yang and absorb it, so Aconite Licorice Decoction plus ginger is proposed to treat it. 10g aconite, 3g licorice, 2 small slices of ginger. \\nAfter taking 1 dose, the crying stopped; after 2 doses, the eye swelling gradually disappeared and the stool turned yellow. He was cured after 4 doses. \\nOriginal note: Shi Xi often complains about the redness and swelling of his eyes when he sees them, but this is not the case. There are many names of eye diseases and syndromes, and their diagnosis is always based on external and internal injuries. Regardless of internal and external injuries, if you see redness, swelling and pain, mist, blindness, etc., each syndrome has different symptoms of deficiency, excess, cold and heat, and must be treated according to the principles of the Six Classics and the Eight Cardinal Guides. You cannot stick to one method to get lucky. "I am not specializing in those with eye diseases, but the essentials of their treatment and the principles of the classics are interoperable.`,真寒假热:"Really hot during winter vacation","石 淋":"stone shower","石 淋 （肾结石虚寒证型） 黄某，男，四十四岁，湖北人，昆明海口某厂军事代表":"Shilin (kidney stone deficiency and cold syndrome) Huang, male, 44 years old, from Hubei, military representative of a factory in Haikou, Kunming","石 淋 （肾结石虚寒证型） 黄某，男，四十四岁，湖北人，昆明海口某厂军事代表。 患者以腰痛数年而住入昆明军区某医院治疗，经X线摄 片检查，发现右肾肾盂有十粒结石影象，小如花椒，大至蚕 豆,诊断为“肾结石”,因身体虚弱不能耐受外科手术，遂于 1958年11月出院延余诊治。言及患腰痛已久，时有所发,痛 如绞作,延及腰腹,下引宗筋,痛甚则神怯而畏寒肢冷。小腹 胀痛，小便短涩。饮食欠佳，精神缺乏。舌苔白滑而厚腻，脉沉 迟无力。此因肾脏寒极，寒湿不化，内结成石，以温肾扶阳温 化之法主之，投以四逆汤加味。 附片60克，杜仲10克，桂枝30克，干姜40克，茯苓30 克，上肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑入），北细辛6克，甘草6克。 服药十一剂后，相继经尿道排出结石四粒，其中曾有一 粒较大者，排出时嵌于尿道口，尿线中断，其痛非常，经该厂 医生用镀子夹出，宛如细包谷粒大小，至使尿道口略为出血。 经X线复査,尚余下六粒结石,但影象均较前为小,原大如蚕 豆者已不复见。此乃温化之剂所致也。唯因肾寒日久，腰尚冷痛，结石未全化解排尽，其法不变,继以扶阳温化主之。 附片100克，干姜50克，狗脊10克，北细辛6克，薏苡仁 30克，桂枝30克，上肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑入），甘草10克。 因服药有效，信心不移，连服不断则病情大减，食增神 健,体质大为好转，于1959年1月开始恢复工作，前后相继 数十余剂，腰痛已不复作，于1959年3月前来复诊，带来X 线复査照片，十粒结石已消去九粒，仅剩下一粒，影象亦较前 缩小。再以上方加减，不离强心温肾，调补气血之原则。数月 后,最后一粒结石亦随尿排出，自此恢复健康,照常工作。":`Shilin (kidney stone deficiency and cold syndrome) Huang, male, 44 years old, from Hubei, military representative of a factory in Haikou, Kunming. The patient suffered from low back pain for several years and was admitted to a hospital in the Kunming Military Region for treatment. After X-ray examination, it was found that there were ten stones in the renal pelvis of the right kidney, ranging from peppercorns to broad beans. The patient was diagnosed as "kidney stones". Because he was too weak to tolerate surgery, he was discharged from the hospital in November 1958 for further treatment. He mentioned that he had been suffering from low back pain for a long time, and it would occur from time to time. The pain was like twisting, extending to the waist and abdomen, and leading to the lower back muscles. If the pain was severe, he would feel timid and afraid of cold, and his limbs would be cold. Distension and pain in the lower abdomen, short and astringent urine. Poor diet and lack of energy. The tongue coating is white, slippery, thick and greasy, and the pulse is slow and weak. This is because the kidneys are extremely cold and the cold and dampness cannot be converted, and stones form in the kidneys. The main method is to warm the kidneys, nourish the yang and warm the kidneys, and add Sini Decoction to add flavor. 60 grams of Futian, 10 grams of Eucommia ulmoides, 30 grams of cinnamon twigs, 40 grams of dried ginger, 30 grams of Poria cocos, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 6 grams of Asarum, and 6 grams of licorice. After taking eleven doses of medicine, four stones were passed out through the urethra one after another. One of them was a larger one. It was embedded in the urethral opening and the urinary string was interrupted. The pain was very painful. The doctor of the factory used a plating tool to pinch out the stones, which were as big as finely wrapped grains, causing slight bleeding at the urethral opening. After X-ray re-examination, six stones remained, but the images were smaller than before, and the original stones as big as broad beans were no longer visible. This is caused by the warming agent. However, because the kidneys are cold for a long time, the waist is still cold and painful, and the stones are not completely dissolved and eliminated, the method remains unchanged, and the main method is to use Fuyang to warm up. 100 grams of Futian, 50 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of dog's spine, 6 grams of asarum, 30 grams of coix seed, 30 grams of cinnamon twigs, 10 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), and 10 grams of licorice. Because the medicine was effective and her confidence remained strong, her condition was greatly reduced as she continued to take it. She was able to eat better and her health improved significantly. She resumed work in January 1959 and took dozens of doses one after another. The above additions and subtractions should be made without departing from the principles of strengthening the heart, warming the kidneys, and regulating qi and blood. A few months later, the last stone was excreted in the urine, and he recovered and returned to work as usual.`,"秋 燥":"Autumn dryness","秋 燥 尚某之女，年十四岁":"Qiuzao, daughter of Shang, fourteen years old","秋 燥 尚某之女，年十四岁。1924年8月感秋令燥邪，身热头 疼，咽干而痛，食物不下，喜饮清凉。脉息弦数,舌尖红，苔白 而燥。此为外邪与阳明燥气相合遂成是状。方用麻黄、杏仁、 甘草、石膏汤加味治之,一剂而愈。 麻黄10克，杏仁10克，生石膏12克（碎,布包），桔梗10 克，连翘6克，麦冬10克。":"Qiuzao is the daughter of Shang, fourteen years old. In August 1924, I felt the dryness evil caused by the autumn weather. I felt hot and had a headache. My throat was dry and painful. I couldn't eat enough and I liked to drink cool drinks. The pulse is stringy and rapid, the tip of the tongue is red, and the coating is white and dry. This is the result of the combination of external evil and Yangming dryness. Treat it with ephedra, almond, licorice and gypsum decoction, and it will be cured in one dose. 10 grams of ephedra, 10 grams of almonds, 12 grams of gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth), 10 grams of platycodon, 6 grams of forsythia, and 10 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus.",种子篇:"Seeds",科室:"Department","童子捞案 张某，8岁，禀赋不足，形体羸弱":"The boy was involved in the case. Zhang, 8 years old, lacks endowment and is weak.","童子捞案\\n张某，8岁，禀赋不足，形体羸弱。受寒起病，脉来浮滑，兼有紧象；指纹色淡而青，舌苔白滑，质含青色；涕清，咳嗽而如痰涌；发热、恶寒，头昏痛，喜热饮。缘由风寒表邪引动内停之寒湿水饮，肺气不利，阻遏太阳经气出入之机。拟小青龙汤加附子助阳解表、化饮除痰，附片用至30g。服后得微汗，身热始退，表邪已解，寒痰未净，守原方去杭芍、麻茸，加茯苓10g，白术12g，连进2剂，饮食已如常。惟仍涕清痰多，面浮，午后潮热，自汗，腹中时而隐痛。孰料病家对吴氏信任不专，另延中医诊视。云误服附子，中毒难解，处以清热利湿之剂，反见病重，出现风动之状，双目上视，唇缩而青，肢厥抽掣，汗出欲绝。又急促吴氏诊视，具述误治经过，乃主以大剂加味四逆汤治之。附片用至100g。连服2次，风状已减，不再抽掣。原方加口芪、白术、茯苓，连进数十余剂始奏全功。\\n8岁小儿前后共服附片量逾5000g，“并无中毒，且患儿病愈之后，身体健康，体质丰盛胜于病前，多年无恙”。\\n又如治3岁甘某“麻疹误服表凉药转阴证案”：发热已五六日，“昏迷无神”，投白通汤，附子用至60g，2剂即愈。":`The boy investigates the case\\nZhang, 8 years old, has insufficient endowment and a weak body. When cold occurs, the pulse is slippery and tight; the fingerprints are light and green, the tongue coating is white and slippery, and the texture is bluish; the mucus is clear, and the cough is like phlegm; fever, aversion to cold, dizziness and pain, and a preference for hot drinks. The reason is that wind-cold external evil causes internal stasis of cold and damp water to drink, which is unfavorable for lung qi and blocks the entry and exit of solar meridian qi. Add Fuzi to Xiaoqinglong Decoction to help relieve yang and relieve phlegm. Use Fuzi tablets up to 30g. After taking it, I feel slight sweating, body heat begins to subside, external evils have been resolved, and cold phlegm has not been purified. I keep the original prescription and remove the peony root and mango root, add 10g of Poria cocos and 12g of Atractylodes macrocephala, and take 2 doses in a row. My diet is as usual. However, she still has clear discharge, phlegm, floating face, hot flashes in the afternoon, spontaneous sweating, and sometimes dull pain in the abdomen. Unexpectedly, the patient did not trust Mr. Wu, so he postponed the traditional Chinese medicine consultation. Yun accidentally took aconite and the poisoning was difficult to cure, so he was given a heat-clearing and dampness-removing agent, but he became seriously ill, with wind-like symptoms, his eyes looking up, his lips shrunken and blue, his limbs twitching, and he was sweating profusely. He also consulted Wu urgently and detailed the mistreatment process. He treated it with a large dose of flavored Sini Decoction. Use up to 100g of attached tablets. After taking it twice, the windiness has subsided and there is no more cramping. The original prescription is added with Qi Qi, Atractylodes Macrocephala, and Poria cocos, and more than dozens of doses are added to achieve the full effect. \\nThe 8-year-old child took more than 5,000g of the tablets before and after. "There was no poisoning, and after the child recovered from the illness, he was in good health and had better physical fitness than before the illness. He has been fine for many years." \\nAnother example is the case of treating 3-year-old Gan's case of "measles that turned to yin by mistake after taking cool medicine": He had been feverish for five or six days and was "unconscious". He took Baitong decoction and 60g of aconite, and he was cured after 2 doses.`,童子痨:"Tuberculosis in children","童子痨 张某之子，云南省永仁县人，年八岁，禀赋不足，形体羸 弱，…":"Child Tuberculosis Zhang’s son, a native of Yongren County, Yunnan Province, is eight years old. He has insufficient endowment and a weak body...","童子痨 张某之子，云南省永仁县人，年八岁，禀赋不足，形体羸 弱，平素多病，时有腹痛，多痰慢咳而少食。此先天不足，脾虚 不运，阴寒挟水湿内渍。1922年6月某日，受寒而起病，脉来 浮滑，兼有紧象,指纹色淡而青，舌苔白滑，质含青色，涕清， 咳嗽而加痰涌。发热、恶寒，头昏痛，喜热饮。缘由风寒表邪， 引动内停之寒湿水饮，肺气不利，清肃不降，脾不健运，水湿 不化，阻遏太阳经气出入之机，拟小青龙汤加附子助阳解表 化饮除痰。 附片30克，桂枝尖10克，麻茸3克，北细辛3克，杭白 芍6克，五味子2克，小枣7枚，生姜10克。 服后得微汗,身热始退，表邪已解，但咳嗽痰多而清稀。 此乃寒痰未净，脾肺之气尚虚,守原方去杭芍、麻茸加茯苓10 克、白术12克连进二剂，饮食已如常。惟仍涕清痰多，面浮， 午后尚有潮热，自汗，腹中时而隐隐作痛。此表邪虽解，寒痰 内饮尚重,今得辛温之剂以运行,逐动内饮欲溃,务期祛尽停 饮寒痰，沉痼始除。殊料张君对余信任不专，另延中医数人诊 视，有云“误服附子，中毒难解”。有云“系湿热阻遏中焦”，处 方均以清热利湿。数剂后，不但原病不减，反见沉重,涕清如 水,午后潮热更甚，汗出淋漓，咳痰气息短弱而兼喘促,食物 不进,形体枯瘦，四肢厥冷，已奄奄一息。又改延某西医诊治， 断言“误服姜附，已将肺液烧干”，（试问：涕为肺之液,如果肺 液已经烧干，焉能涕清如水？）竟主服“保肺药水”，并云有起 死回生之效。服后顷刻，遂现风状，双目上视，唇缩而青，肢厥 抽掣，汗出欲绝，已命在旦夕。张君惊惶不已，又急促余诊视 之,并具述误治经过,余不忍坐视待毙,尽力挽回颓绝，主以 大剂加味四逆汤治之。 附片100克，干姜40克，砂仁10克，上肉桂10克（研 末，泡水兑入），甘草10克。 上方连服二次，风状减，已不抽掣。次日复诊，诸证亦有减 轻。再服二剂,突见周身浮肿，咳嗽多痰，但潮热已退，厥逆回 温,能稍进饮食。乃告之此系阴寒水湿之邪被阳药温运化散， 元气回复之征。现仍阳弱气虚，须待温扶。照原方加黄芪、白 术、茯苓连进数十余剂始奏全功。此证即所谓“童子瘠”也，前 后施治，经余拟方，共服附片约10余市斤,并无中毒反应，亦 未见将阴液烧干,且患儿病愈之后，身体健康,体质丰盛胜于 病前，多年无恙。":`Child Tuberculosis Zhang's son, a native of Yongren County, Yunnan Province, is eight years old. He has insufficient endowment, is weak, and is often sick. He has abdominal pain from time to time, chronic cough with excessive phlegm, and eats less. This is a congenital deficiency, spleen deficiency, poor transportation, cold Yin and water-damp internal stains. One day in June 1922, he became ill due to cold. His pulse was slippery and tight, his fingerprints were light and green, his tongue coating was white and slippery, his texture was green, his mucus was clear, and he coughed with phlegm. Fever, aversion to cold, dizziness and pain, prefer hot drinks. The reason is that wind-cold external evil causes internal stasis of cold and damp water, which is unfavorable for lung qi and cannot be purified. The spleen is not good at transporting water and dampness, which blocks the entry and exit of solar meridian qi. Xiaoqinglong Decoction plus aconite can help relieve yang, dissolve the drink, and remove phlegm. 30 grams of Aconite, 10 grams of Guizhi tip, 3 grams of sesame root, 3 grams of asarum, 6 grams of white peony root, 2 grams of Schisandra chinensis, 7 jujubes, and 10 grams of ginger. After taking it, I feel slightly sweaty, the body heat begins to subside, and the external evils are resolved, but I have a cough with abundant phlegm but clear and thin phlegm. This is because the cold phlegm has not been purified, and the Qi of the spleen and lungs is still weak. Keep the original prescription and remove the peony root and mango root, add 10 grams of Poria cocos, and 12 grams of Atractylodes macrocephala for two consecutive doses. The diet is as usual. However, he still has clear discharge, phlegm, and a floating face. He still has hot flashes in the afternoon, spontaneous sweating, and sometimes a dull pain in the abdomen. Although the external evil has been resolved, the cold phlegm and internal drinking are still heavy. Now we need to use pungent and warm medicine to activate the internal drinking, and gradually remove the internal drinking and stop it. Drink the cold phlegm, and the chronic disease will be removed. Unexpectedly, Zhang Jun did not trust me professionally, and he was consulted by several Chinese medicine practitioners. It was said that "if you take Aconite by mistake, the poisoning will be difficult to cure." It is said that "dampness and heat block the middle burn", and the prescriptions are all aimed at clearing away heat and diluting dampness. After several doses, not only did the original disease remain unabated, but it became heavy and clear as water, and the hot flashes in the afternoon were even worse. The patient was sweating profusely, coughing up phlegm, shortness of breath, and shortness of breath. He was unable to eat, his body was thin, his limbs were cold, and he was dying. He also changed the diagnosis and treatment of a certain Western medicine doctor, asserting that "mistaken ginger powder has dried up the lung fluid" (I want to ask: tears are the fluid of the lungs, if the lung fluid has been dried up, how can the tears be clear as water?) He actually took the "lung-preserving potion", which was said to have the effect of bringing the dead back to life. Immediately after taking it, I felt windy, my eyes were looking up, my lips were shrinking and blue, my limbs were twitching, I was sweating profusely, and I was dying. Zhang Jun was panic-stricken and hurriedly examined Yu's diagnosis and detailed the mistreatment process. Yu couldn't bear to sit back and wait for death, and tried his best to save the disease, so he treated it with a large dose of flavored Sini Decoction. 100 grams of Fu Feng, 40 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of amomum villosum, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), and 10 grams of licorice. After taking the medicine twice, the wind was reduced and the cramps were gone. After a follow-up visit the next day, all symptoms were relieved. After taking two more doses, I suddenly noticed edema all over the body and cough with phlegm, but the hot flashes subsided, my body temperature returned to normal, and I was able to eat a little. It is reported that this is a sign that the evil of yin, cold, water, and dampness is dispersed by the warm movement of yang medicine, and the vitality is restored. Now the yang is still weak and the qi is weak, so it needs to be warmed and supported. Follow the original recipe and add astragalus, atractylodes, and poria for dozens of doses to achieve full effect. This syndrome is the so-called "child's infertility". After treatment, I prepared prescriptions and took about 10 kilograms of Fu tablets in total. There was no poisoning reaction, and no drying of Yin fluid. After the child recovered from the disease, he became healthier and richer than before the disease, and he has been fine for many years.`,"筋骨并重、动静结合，整复手法须在放松基础上施行。":"Pay equal attention to the muscles and bones, combine movement and stillness, and the rehabilitation techniques must be performed on the basis of relaxation.",简:"Jane",简体中文:"Simplified Chinese",管正斋:"Guan Zhengzhai","管正斋先生1895年生，幼入医门，专攻针灸，遍访名师，尽得经络腧穴之妙。":"Mr. Guan Zhengzhai was born in 1895. He entered medicine at a young age and specialized in acupuncture. He visited famous teachers and learned the wonders of meridians and acupuncture points.","管正斋先生毕生针灸治验之汇编，系统整理管氏针灸“辨经取穴、少而精、必得气”的学术特色，尤详于中风、痹证之针灸论治。":"This is a compilation of Mr. Guan Zhengzhai’s lifelong acupuncture treatment experience, and systematically organizes the academic characteristics of Guan’s acupuncture of “meridian differentiation, acupoint selection, few but precise, and sure to obtain qi”, especially in the acupuncture treatment of stroke and paralysis syndrome.",管正斋针灸治验录:"Guan Zhengzhai's acupuncture treatment experience record","管正斋，云南针灸名家，精研经络腧穴之学，创立管氏针灸流派特色，尤擅针灸治疗中风、痹证与痿躄。":"Guan Zhengzhai, a famous acupuncture master in Yunnan, studied meridians and acupuncture points intensively, and created the characteristics of Guan's acupuncture school. He is especially good at acupuncture treatment of stroke, paralysis syndrome and impotence.",管氏针灸:"Guan's Acupuncture",管氏针灸流派创始人:"Founder of Guan's Acupuncture School",类别:"Category","系统整理戴丽三先生毕生医疗经验，突出经方为主、时方为辅的学术特色。辨证细腻，用药精纯，于平凡方中见神奇，为习经方者所重。":"Systematically collates Mr. Dai Lisan's lifelong medical experience, highlighting the academic characteristics of focusing on classic prescriptions and supplementing contemporary prescriptions. The syndrome differentiation is delicate, the medicine is pure, and the magic can be found in ordinary prescriptions, which is highly valued by those who practice prescriptions.",索:"So",繁:"Traditional",繁體中文:"Traditional Chinese",组成:"composition","经 闭":"Amenorrhea","经 闭 宋某，女，二十七岁，河南人，住昆明郊区呈贡飞机场":"Amenorrhea Song, female, 27 years old, from Henan, lives at Chenggong Airport in the suburbs of Kunming","经 闭 宋某，女，二十七岁，河南人，住昆明郊区呈贡飞机场。患 者禀赋素弱，婚后多年未孕。初始月经参差不调，每月均需用 中西药物调治，方能应期而潮。但每次行经，量少而黑，少腹 坠胀冷痛。如是两三年后，经血渐少以至闭结。 后又继用中、西药物治疗,并行人工周期法以诱导之，前 后内服中药百余剂，均未获效，迄今已经闭六年之久。患者于 1959年7月到云南中医学院附设门诊部就诊。证见患者面色 萎黄不泽，神情倦怠，少气懒言，毛发稀疏而焦黄。自月经闭 止以来,常感头昏耳鸣，心中烦闷。日间困倦思睡,入夜又不 能安眠。口淡无味,不思饮食。腰膂酸痛,腿膝酸软无力,手足 蹶逆,少腹亦感冰冷不适。脉象沉涩，舌质淡嫩，色黯夹瘀，苔薄白而润。此系元阳不足，冲任俱虚，血寒气滞，胞宫寒冷所 致。阳虚生寒，气虚易滞，血寒则凝。血寒气虚，瘀滞难行，百 脉不荣，经血无源，故而闭止，亦不孕育。故当温扶下元，温经 活血，散寒暖宫。自拟验方益元暖宫汤治之。 附片100克，当归15克，丹参15克，桂枝12克，吴茱萸 9克，炙香附12克，细辛6克，赤芍9克，炒艾叶12克，干姜 15克，甘草9克。 服上方三剂后复诊,腹部疼痛减去七、八,少腹冰冷感觉 减轻，尚有坠胀感。食思增进,手足四肢回温，心中已不烦闷， 夜已能熟寐。脉仍沉涩,舌质淡，瘀黯稍减,苔薄白。继上方温 化之剂加红花5克以助温经活血之功，并嘱服药时滴酒少许 为引，以促其温行血脉之效。告知患者,如服药后诸证均见好 转,惟腰及少腹又复酸胀痛者,为月经欲潮之兆,幸勿疑误。 上方连服八剂，果如余言。于原方中去赤芍加川芎9克， 阿胶15克（烊化兑服）药炉不辍连服五剂，经水即潮,先行者 为黑色血块，继则渐红。次日，腰腹疼痛随之缓解，行经五日 而净。继以八珍汤加香附、益母、炒艾等调补气血。连服十余 剂后，面色毛发润泽，精神眠食转佳。其后经信通调，应时而 潮，一年后顺产一子。":"Amenorrhea Song, female, 27 years old, from Henan, lives at Chenggong Airport in the suburbs of Kunming. The patient has weak endowments and has not been pregnant for many years after marriage. Menstruation is irregular at the beginning, and needs to be treated with Chinese and Western medicine every month in order to have regular menstruation. But every time I menstruate, the amount is small and dark, and my lower abdomen is distended, cold and painful. After two or three years, the menstrual blood gradually becomes less and even stops. Later, he continued to use Chinese and Western medicines for treatment, and artificial cycle method was used to induce it. He took more than 100 doses of traditional Chinese medicine orally, but none of them were effective. He has been closed for six years so far. The patient went to the outpatient department of Yunnan College of Traditional Chinese Medicine in July 1959. The patient's complexion is sallow and dull, his expression is tired, he is short of breath and lazy to talk, and his hair is sparse and brown. Since menstruation stopped, I often feel dizzy, tinnitus, and depressed. Feeling sleepy during the day and unable to sleep well at night. The mouth is tasteless and does not want to eat. There is soreness in the waist and back, the legs and knees are sore and weak, the hands and feet are slumped, and the lower abdomen also feels cold and uncomfortable. The pulse is heavy and astringent, the tongue is light and tender, dark in color with blood stasis, and the fur is thin, white and moist. This is caused by insufficient Yuanyang, deficiency of both Chong and Ren, cold blood and qi stagnation, and cold uterus. Yang deficiency produces cold, Qi deficiency tends to stagnate, and blood cold causes coagulation. Blood is cold and Qi is deficient, blood stasis is stagnant and it is difficult to move, the pulses are sluggish, and menstrual blood has no source, so it is blocked and sterile. Therefore, it should warm and support Xia Yuan, warm the meridians, activate blood circulation, dispel cold and warm the palace. Treat it with self-made prescription Yiyuan Nuangong Decoction. 100 grams of Futian, 15 grams of Angelica sinensis, 15 grams of Salvia miltiorrhiza, 12 grams of Guizhi, 9 grams of Evodia, 12 grams of roasted Cyperus rotundus, 6 grams of Asarum, 9 grams of red peony root, 12 grams of fried mugwort leaves, 15 grams of dried ginger, and 9 grams of licorice. After taking three doses of the above medicine, I went back for a follow-up consultation. The pain in my abdomen was reduced by 7 to 8 points, the cold feeling in the lower abdomen was relieved, and there was still a feeling of bloating. Food cravings increase, hands, feet and limbs become warmer, my heart is no longer bored, and I can sleep soundly at night. The pulse is still heavy and astringent, the tongue is light, the blood stasis is slightly reduced, and the fur is thin and white. Following the warming agent above, add 5 grams of safflower to help warm the menstrual flow and activate blood circulation, and ask to drink a little wine as a guide when taking the medicine to promote its effect of warming the blood vessels. Inform the patient that if all the symptoms are improved after taking the medicine, but the soreness and distension of the waist and lower abdomen return, it is a sign of menstrual cramps. Fortunately, there is no doubt. I took eight doses in a row, and it was as good as I said. Remove the red peony root and add 9 grams of Chuanxiong root and 15 grams of donkey-hide gelatin to the original prescription. Take five doses in a row. The menstrual fluid will become flushed. The first one will be black blood clots, and then they will become red. The next day, the pain in the waist and abdomen was relieved, and the menstruation was cleared after five days. Then add Bazhen Decoction with Cyperus rotunda, Yi Mu, fried mugwort, etc. to replenish qi and blood. After taking more than ten doses, my complexion and hair are moisturized, and my energy, sleep and eating are getting better. Afterwards, through communication and communication, she was able to respond to the tide and gave birth to a baby one year later.",经方:"Jingfang","经方为主、时方为辅，融会温病之说而无门户之见。":"Mainly based on classic prescriptions, supplemented by seasonal prescriptions, it integrates the theory of febrile diseases without any sectarian views.",经方加减化裁之法度示范性强:"The method of adding, subtracting and reducing classic prescriptions is highly demonstrative",经方学派滇中代表:"Representative of Central Yunnan of Jingfang School",经方应用:"Application of classic prescriptions",经方心悟:"Enlightenment from the Sutra",经方派:"Jingfang sect","经方派（戴氏医学传人）":"Jing Fang Sect (successor of Dai’s medicine)","经筋病候之辨、奇经八脉之主治，条分缕析，配合循经按压以定病所，为取穴之依据。":"The identification of symptoms of meridian diseases and the main treatments of the eight extra meridians are analyzed step by step, combined with massage along the meridians to determine the location of the disease, which is the basis for selecting acupoints.",经络辨证:"Meridian syndrome differentiation",经行血崩:"Menstrual bleeding","经行血崩 杨某,女，四十一岁，住昆明市正义南路教子巷":"Menstrual bleeding, Yang, female, 41 years old, lives in Jiaozi Lane, Zhengyi South Road, Kunming City","经行血崩 杨某,女，四十一岁，住昆明市正义南路教子巷。1953年 秋,适值月经来潮，因抬重物用力过猛，骤然下血如崩。先后 经二医诊治，皆云血热妄行，服用清热、凉血、止血之剂，血未能止，迁延十余日，以致卧床不起，延余诊治。患者面色蜡黄、 精神疲倦，气短而懒言，不思饮食，手足不温。经血仍淋漓不 断,时而如潮涌出，皆清淡血水兼夹紫黑血块,腰及小腹酸胀 坠痛。舌质淡，苔薄白少津，脉沉涩。此乃阳气内虚，冲任不 守，气不纳血，血海不固，致成崩漏之证。方用回阳饮加人参 扶阳固气。 附片120克，吉林红参9克，炮黑姜9克，上肉桂9克 （研末，泡水兑入），甘草9克。 服二剂后，流血减少其半，血色淡红，瘀块减少，呼吸已 转平和，四肢回温。饮食稍增，能进藕粉少许。照原方加炒艾 15克,阿胶24克（烊化分次兑服）,炒白术9克,侧柏炭9克。 连服三剂后，流血大减,仅为少量淡红血水,精神饮食增加， 面色已转润泽，舌质显红润，苔薄白，脉缓弱，已能起床。阳气 回复，气血渐充，欲求巩固，仍须与甘温之剂调补之。以四逆 当归补血汤加味气血两补。 附片90克，黄芪60克，当归30克，干姜15克，上肉桂12 克（研末，泡水兑入），炒艾15克，阿胶12克（烊化，分次兑 服），甘草9克。 连服五剂，流血全止,精神、饮食基本恢复，颜面唇舌已 转红润，脉象和缓，已能下床活动。惟气血未足，阳神尚虚，走 动稍感头昏、腿软，继服四逆当归补血汤加上肉桂、砂仁，服 二十余剂，气血恢复,诸证获愈,恢复健康。":"Menstrual bleeding. Yang, female, 41 years old, lives in Jiaozi Lane, Zhengyi South Road, Kunming City. In the autumn of 1953, at the time of my menstrual period, I suddenly started bleeding like a convulsion due to exerting too much force while lifting heavy objects. After being diagnosed and treated by two doctors one after another, they all reported that the blood-heat was spreading indiscriminately. After taking heat-clearing, cooling, and hemostatic agents, the bleeding failed to stop and persisted for more than ten days, resulting in the patient being bedridden, delaying diagnosis and treatment. The patient's complexion was sallow, mentally tired, short of breath, lazy to talk, unwilling to eat, and his hands and feet were not warm. The menstrual blood is still flowing continuously, sometimes gushing out like a tide, with light blood mixed with purple and black blood clots, and the waist and lower abdomen are sore and painful. The tongue is pale, the fur is thin and white, and there is little fluid. The pulse is heavy and astringent. This is a symptom of internal deficiency of Yang Qi, failure to maintain the charge and control, Qi not receiving blood, and blood sea not solidifying, leading to metrorrhagia. Use Huiyang drink and add ginseng to support Yang and strengthen Qi. 120 grams of Futian, 9 grams of Jilin red ginseng, 9 grams of black ginger, 9 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), and 9 grams of licorice. After taking two doses, the bleeding was reduced by half, the blood was light red, the blood clots were reduced, breathing became gentle, and the limbs became warm. If the diet is slightly increased, a little lotus root powder can be added. Follow the original recipe and add 15 grams of fried mugwort, 24 grams of donkey-hide gelatin (take it in divided doses), 9 grams of fried atractylodes, and 9 grams of arborvitae charcoal. After taking three doses, the bleeding was greatly reduced to only a small amount of light red blood, the mental intake increased, the complexion became moist, the tongue became red, the coating was thin and white, the pulse was slow and weak, and I was able to get up. Yang Qi is restored and Qi and blood are gradually replenished. If you want to strengthen it, you still need to supplement it with sweet and warm medicine. Use Sini Danggui Buxue Decoction to nourish Qi and blood. 90 grams of Fu Fian, 60 grams of Astragalus, 30 grams of Angelicae Sinensis, 15 grams of dried ginger, 12 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 15 grams of fried moxa, 12 grams of donkey-hide gelatin (yellow, drink in divided doses), and 9 grams of licorice. After taking five doses, the bleeding stopped completely, the spirit and diet basically recovered, the face, lips and tongue became rosy, the pulse became gentle, and I was able to get out of bed. However, the qi and blood were not enough, the yang spirit was still weak, and I felt a little dizzy when walking and my legs were weak. I continued to take Sini Danggui Buxue Decoction plus cinnamon and amomum villosum for more than 20 doses. The qi and blood recovered, all symptoms were cured, and health returned.",经行血崩及口鼻出血不止:"Menstrual bleeding and bleeding from mouth and nose","经行血崩及口鼻出血不止 过某之妻,年三十五岁,湖南籍，住昆明市东…":"Menstrual bleeding and persistent bleeding from the mouth and nose. Guo’s wife is 35 years old, from Hunan, and lives in the east of Kunming City...","经行血崩及口鼻出血不止 过某之妻,年三十五岁,湖南籍，住昆明市东庄九十九号，素患 经痛不调，经某医诊治，拟方以破气行瘀之法，方中配伍桃 仁、红花、三棱、莪术、川芎、当归等,并嘱可作常服，冀使经信 通调。如是方药已服十年有余，攻破太过,致气血大伤。1961 年6月下旬，因打骂小孩动气生怒,忽然经行血崩不止,急往 某医院就诊，经治数日，子宫仍出血未止,又复鼻衄仍及牙 龈出血，身发紫斑，病势日重。7月1日，家属主动抬出医院改 请某中医诊治。医者立案为“血不归经之候”,拟方二帖：内服 以酒炒生地黄50克，酥炒侧柏叶30克，艾叶30克，炒杭芍 30克，浙麦冬30克，姜炭30克，藕节二个,生甘草20克，点 童便少许并加发灰为引，嘱服二剂。外治用附子面100克，酒 炒，包足心涌泉穴。殊料服药一次,上、下出血更甚，呻吟不 已，气短欲脱,举家惶恐万状。7月2日清晨来舍促余急诊,见 患者面色淡黄晦黯无华,唇舌亦淡白，苔白滑，唇、舌、口腔内 两颊黏膜均有大小不匀之紫黑血泡，舌心血泡一枚,约拇指 头大,鼻及牙龈仍见出血，色黯红不鲜，用物填塞鼻孔，则血 块阻于咽喉，渐从口中咳吐而出，亦为紫黑血块及血水。四肢 及胸背皮肤起青紫血斑，神情淡漠、声低息短，呻吟不已，但 觉心中慌跳,气虚难接。日不思食,夜不能寐,唯少喜热饮一、 二口。六脉芤虚,重按若无。缘由攻破太过,气血两亏,气虚无 力摄血，阳不守阴，血虚则气无所依，阴不恋阳，以致血不归 经，游溢妄行，气随血耗，散漫无羁。如继续流血不止,恐血尽气亡，阴阳俱脱。盖气血两亏失血之证，当以治气为先，气足 则血自能止，血止之后，方能言补益之法。当此证候,余主以 扶阳收纳，固气止血,方用： 黑天雄150克，炮黑姜30克，黑荆芥6克，上肉桂15克 （研末，泡水兑入），茯神20克，桂枝尖30克，甘草6克，大枣 2枚（烧黑存性）。 7月3日复诊。服上方后已见效，出血减少。然气血太亏, 一时难以尽复，口鼻及下部仍流出淡黑血水，心泛呕逆，仍不 思饮食，神志尚弱。由于气血所亏，原患寒湿痹痛旧疾又复 发，左手肩臂疼痛。照上方佐以温经散寒之剂治之。 附片200克，炮黑姜10克，干姜10克，上肉桂15克（研 末，泡水兑入），西砂仁10克，桂枝尖20克，北细辛6克，吴 茱萸5克，甘草10克。 7月4日三诊。脉象较有神根,各部出血减少十之八、九, 唇舌转红润，口舌血泡已瘪,昨夜得熟寐。小便转长,喜热饮, 稍能进食。惟头部昏重作痛，左肩臂筋肉仍痛,然病势已见大 减，渐可转危为安。处方： 附片200克，炮黑姜10克，干姜15克，上肉桂15克（研 末，泡水兑入），桂枝尖30克，北细辛7克，法半夏15克，公 丁香5克，甘草10克，麻黄根10克。 7月6日四诊。上方连进二付，口鼻出血已止，口舌紫黑 血泡全退。舌质红润，苔尚薄白，下部仍稍流黑血,极腥臭。此 系已离经败坏之血，得阳药温化而下行，非新出之血液也。腑 气已通，数日以来始有大便，色黑而干。精神、食量均较佳，脉 已和缓较有神，惟左臂仍稍掣痛,延及左侧头项，再以扶阳温 化通经散寒治之。 附片200克，干姜50克，北细辛10克，桂枝尖50兑，羌活5克，独活6克，薏苡仁15克，麻黄5克，上肉桂15克（研 末，泡水兑入），甘草15克。 7月8日五诊。病状大减，头疼止，肩臂痛已大为减轻，遂 照原方去麻黄，服二剂后，诸证已愈。再以四逆汤加黄芪、当 归、白术、慧攻仁数剂调理而善后。":`Menstrual bleeding and persistent bleeding from the mouth and nose. Guo's wife, 35 years old, Hunanese, lives at No. 99, Dongzhuang, Kunming City. She has always suffered from irregular menstrual pain. After diagnosis and treatment by a doctor, a prescription was formulated to break Qi and relieve blood stasis. The prescription was combined with peach kernel, safflower, Trigonella, Curcuma, Chuanxiong, Angelica, etc., and was advised to take it regularly in order to regulate the menstrual flow. I have been taking this prescription for more than ten years, but it has broken down too much, causing severe damage to Qi and blood. In late June 1961, I got angry because of beating and scolding a child, and suddenly my menstrual bleeding stopped. I rushed to a hospital for treatment. After several days of treatment, the uterine bleeding still did not stop, epistaxis and gum bleeding continued, and I developed purple spots on my body. My condition became increasingly serious. On July 1, the family took the initiative to take her out of the hospital and consult a traditional Chinese medicine doctor for diagnosis and treatment. The doctor filed a case for "when blood does not return to menstruation" and drew up two prescriptions: Oral administration: stir-fry 50 grams of raw rehmannia glutinosa with wine, 30 grams of fried arborvitae leaves, 30 grams of mugwort leaves, 30 grams of stir-fried peony root, 30 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 30 grams of ginger charcoal, two lotus root joints, 20 grams of raw licorice, a little child's stool and add ash as a guide, and ordered to take two doses. For external treatment, use 100 grams of aconite noodles, stir-fry with wine, and wrap at the Yongquan point in the heart of the foot. After taking the special medicine once, the bleeding from the upper and lower parts became even worse, the patient moaned constantly, was short of breath, and the whole family was in panic. In the early morning of July 2, I came to the emergency room for emergency treatment. The patient's complexion was pale and dull, his lips and tongue were also pale, and the coating was white and slippery. There were purple-black blood bubbles of uneven sizes on the lips, tongue, and oral mucosa. There was one blood bubble on the tongue, about the size of a thumb. Bleeding was still seen in the nose and gums, and the color was dark red. If the nostrils were stuffed with something, the blood clots would block the throat, and they would gradually come out of the mouth as purple-black blood clots and blood. There were purple blood spots on the skin of the limbs and chest and back. His expression was indifferent, his voice was low and his breathing was short, and he kept moaning. However, he felt his heart was racing and his energy was weak and difficult to control. He doesn't think about food during the day and can't sleep at night. He only likes one or two sips of hot drinks. The six meridians are weak and weak, and they feel weak when pressed hard. The reasons are excessive breakthrough, loss of both Qi and blood, Qi deficiency and inability to absorb blood, Yang does not guard Yin, blood deficiency means Qi has no support, and Yin does not love Yang, resulting in blood not returning to the menstrual flow, overflowing and wandering, Qi being consumed along with the blood, and being unruly. If the bleeding continues, there is a fear that the blood will be exhausted and the Qi will be exhausted, and both yin and yang will be lost. To deal with the syndrome of blood loss caused by deficiency of both Qi and blood, treatment of Qi should be the priority. When Qi is sufficient, the bleeding will stop. Only after the bleeding stops can the method of replenishment be discussed. When this syndrome occurs, Yu Zhu uses Fuyang to absorb, consolidate Qi and stop bleeding. Prescription: 150g Hei Tianxiong, 30g Paohei ginger, 6g Black Nepeta, 15g Cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 20g Poria Shen, 30g Guizhi tip, 6g licorice, 2 jujubes (burned to preserve the nature). Follow-up visit on July 3. After taking the above medicine, it has been effective and the bleeding has been reduced. However, the qi and blood were too depleted, and it was difficult to recover for a while. Dark blood still flowed out of the mouth, nose and lower parts, the heart was vomiting, the patient still had no desire to eat, and his consciousness was still weak. Due to the loss of qi and blood, the old disease of cold-damp arthralgia recurred, causing pain in the left shoulder and arm. Treat it by treating it by treating it with the medicine above to warm the meridians and dispel cold. 200 grams of Futian, 10 grams of black ginger, 10 grams of dried ginger, 15 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10 grams of Amomum villosum, 20 grams of Guizhijian, 6 grams of Asarum, 5 grams of Evodia, and 10 grams of licorice. Third consultation on July 4th. The pulse condition is more intense, the bleeding in various parts of the body has decreased by 80-90%, the lips and tongue have turned red, and the blood bubbles in the mouth and tongue have deflated. I had a good sleep last night. His urine becomes longer, he likes hot drinks, and he is less able to eat. However, the head is dizzy and painful, and the muscles of the left shoulder and arm are still painful. However, the condition of the disease has been greatly reduced, and the crisis is gradually turning into peace. Prescription: 200 grams of Fupi, 10 grams of black ginger, 15 grams of dried ginger, 15 grams of cassia cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 30 grams of Guizhijian, 7 grams of Asarum, 15 grams of Pinellia ternata, 5 grams of cloves, 10 grams of licorice, and 10 grams of ephedra root. Four consultations on July 6. After two consecutive injections, the bleeding from the mouth and nose stopped, the mouth and tongue were purple and black, and the blood blisters all subsided. The tongue is red, the coating is still thin and white, and the lower part still bleeds a little black blood, which is extremely fishy. This is the blood that has been separated from the menstruation and has been corrupted. It is warmed by the Yang medicine and then flows down. It is not new blood. The qi in the fu organs has been cleared, and the stool has been dark and dry for several days. His energy level and food intake are both better, and his pulse has become gentler and more energetic. However, there is still a slight pain in his left arm, which extends to the left side of his head. He is treated with Fuyang, warming, dredging menstruation and dispersing cold. 200 grams of Aconite, 50 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of Asarum, 50 grams of Guizhijian, 5 grams of Qianghuo, 6 grams of Duhuo, 15 grams of coix seed, 5 grams of ephedra, 15 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed), and 15 grams of licorice. Five clinics on July 8. The symptoms were greatly reduced, the headache stopped, and the shoulder and arm pain was greatly alleviated. So I followed the original prescription to remove ephedra. After taking two doses, all symptoms were cured. Then use Sini Decoction plus several doses of astragalus, angelica, atractylodes, and Huigongren to treat the aftermath.`,"经行血崩案 杨某，女，41岁":"Menstrual bleeding case: Yang, female, 41 years old","经行血崩案\\n杨某，女，41岁。适值月经来潮，抬重物用力过猛，骤然下血如崩。先后诊治，皆云血热妄行，服用清热、止血之剂，血未能止，迁延10余日以致卧床不起，延吴氏诊治：面色蜡黄，精神疲倦，气短懒言，不思饮食，手足不温；经血仍淋漓不断，时而如潮涌出，皆清淡血水兼夹紫黑血块.腰及小腹酸胀坠痛；舌质淡，苔薄白少津，脉沉涩。此乃阳气内虚，冲任不守，气不纳血，血海不固，致成崩漏之证。方用回阳饮加人参扶阳固气：\\n附片120g，吉林红参9g，炮黑姜9g，上肉桂9g（研末，泡水兑入），甘草9g。\\n服2剂后，流血减少其半，血色淡红，瘀块减少，呼吸已转平和，四肢回温。原方加炒艾15g，阿胶24g（烊化分次兑服）、炒白术9g，侧柏炭9g。连服3剂后，流血大减，仅为少量淡红血水，精神饮食增加，面色已转润泽，舌质显红润，苔薄白，脉缓弱，已能起床。阳气回复，气血渐充，欲求巩固。仍须与甘温之剂调补之。以四逆当归补血汤加味：\\n附片90g，口芪60g，当归30g，干姜15g，上肉桂12g（研末，泡水兑入），炒艾叶15g，阿胶12g（烊化，分次兑服），甘草9g。\\n连服5剂，流血全止，精神、饮食基本恢复，颜面、唇舌已转红润，脉象和缓，能下床活动。继服四逆当归补血汤加上肉桂、砂仁服20余剂，气血恢复，诸症获愈。\\n按：崩漏之症，出手即用附子120g，药仅5味，不加冗药，确为经典火神派风范。大回阳饮再加艾叶、阿胶、肉桂、砂仁等药，俱可借鉴。":"Menstrual bleeding case\\nYang, female, 41 years old. At the time of menstruation, I used too much force to lift heavy objects, and suddenly bleeded like a collapse. After successive diagnosis and treatment, they all showed that blood-heat was indiscriminately, and they took heat-clearing and hemostatic agents, but the bleeding failed to stop, and the condition lasted for more than 10 days and became bedridden. Yan Wu's diagnosis and treatment: sallow complexion, mental fatigue, shortness of breath and laziness, no desire to eat, and lukewarm hands and feet; menstrual blood was still dripping, sometimes gushing out like a tide, all with light blood and purple-black blood clots. The waist and lower abdomen were sore, distended and painful; the tongue was pale, the coating was thin and white, and there was little fluid, and the pulse was deep and stringy. This is a symptom of internal deficiency of Yang Qi, failure to maintain the charge and control, Qi not being able to absorb blood, and a sea of ​​blood that is not solid, leading to metrorrhagia. Use Huiyang drink with ginseng to strengthen yang and strengthen qi:\\n120g of Futian, 9g of Jilin red ginseng, 9g of black ginger, 9g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), and 9g of licorice. \\nAfter taking 2 doses, the bleeding was reduced by half, the blood was light red, the blood clots were reduced, breathing became calmer, and the limbs became warmer. To the original recipe, add 15g of fried moxa, 24g of donkey-hide gelatin (take it in divided doses), 9g of fried atractylodes, and 9g of arborvitae charcoal. After taking 3 doses in a row, the bleeding was greatly reduced to only a small amount of light red blood, the spirit and diet increased, the complexion became moist, the tongue became red, the fur was thin and white, the pulse was slow and weak, and I was able to get up. The yang energy is restored, the qi and blood are gradually filled, and the desire is strengthened. It still needs to be supplemented with sweet and warming ingredients. Add Sini Danggui Blood Replenishing Decoction to taste:\\n90g of Aconite, 60g of Qiqi, 30g of Angelica, 15g of dried ginger, 12g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix in), 15g of fried moxa leaves, 12g of donkey-hide gelatin (yellow, drink in divided doses), and 9g of licorice. \\nAfter taking 5 doses, the bleeding stopped completely, my energy and diet basically recovered, my face, lips and tongue became rosy, my pulse was gentle, and I was able to get out of bed. After taking more than 20 doses of Sini Danggui Buxue Decoction plus cinnamon and amomum villosum, the qi and blood recovered and all the symptoms were cured. \\nNote: For metrorrhagia, use 120g of Aconite as soon as possible. There are only 5 flavors of medicine and no redundant medicine is added. It is indeed a classic Vulcan style. Dahuiyang drink plus mugwort leaves, donkey-hide gelatin, cinnamon, Amomum villosum and other medicines can be used for reference.","经证大热大汗大渴脉洪大者，白虎汤辛凉重剂清之；腑证痞满燥实坚者，三承气随证下之，缓急轻重各有攸当。":"For those with severe fever, profuse sweating, profuse thirst, and strong pulse, a strong dose of Baihu Decoction, which is pungent and cool, can be used to clear it; for those with viscera syndrome of fullness, dryness, and firmness, three Qi can be treated according to the syndrome, and each has its own priority.","经闭案 宋某，女，27岁，住昆明":"Amenorrhea case: Song, female, 27 years old, living in Kunming","经闭案\\n宋某，女，27岁，住昆明。禀赋素弱，婚后多年未孕。初始月经参差不调，每月均需中西药物调治，方能应期而潮。但每次行经量少而黑，少腹坠胀冷痛。如是两三年后，经血渐少以至闭结。曾行人工周期法诱导之，内服中药百余剂，均未获效，迄今经闭6年之久。症见面色萎黄不泽，神情倦怠，少气懒言，毛发稀疏而焦黄；自月经闭止以来，常感头昏耳鸣，心中烦闷；日间困倦思睡，入夜不能安眠；口淡无味，不思饮食;腰膂酸痛，腿膝酸软无力，手足厥逆，少腹亦感冰冷不适；脉象沉涩，舌质淡嫩，色黯夹瘀，苔薄白而润。此系元阳不足，冲任俱虚，血寒气滞，胞宫寒冷所致。阳虚生寒，气虚易滞，血寒则凝，经血无源故而闭止，亦不孕育。当温扶下元，温经活血，散寒暖宫，自拟验方益元暖宫汤治之：\\n附片100g，当归15g，丹参I5g，桂枝12g，吴萸9g，炙香附12g，细辛6g，赤芍9g，炒艾叶12g，干姜15g，甘草9g。\\n服上方3剂后，腹部疼痛减去七八，少腹冰冷感觉减轻，尚有坠胀感。食思增进，手足四肢回温，心中已不烦闷，夜已能熟寐；脉仍沉涩，舌质淡，瘀黯稍减，苔薄白。继上方加红花5g，以助温经活血之功。并嘱服药时滴酒少许为引，以促其温行血脉。如服药后诸症均见好转，惟腰及少腹又复酸胀痛者，为月经欲潮之兆，幸勿疑误。	上方连服8剂，果如余言。于原方中去赤芍，加川芎9g，，阿胶15g（烊化兑服），药炉不辍，连服5剂，经水即潮，先行者为黑色血块，继则渐红。\\n次日，腰腹疼痛随之缓解，行经5日而净。继以八珍汤加香附、益母、炒艾等调补气血。连服10余剂后，面色毛发润泽，精神眠食转佳。其后经信通调，应时而潮，1年后顺产一子。\\n按：6年闭经之症，判为“元阳不足，冲任俱虚，血寒气滞，胞宫寒冷所致”，从温扶下元，散寒暖宫着眼，调理月余而愈。确是火神派风格。":'Suspension case\\nSong, female, 27 years old, lives in Kunming. She has a weak endowment and has not been pregnant for many years after marriage. Menstruation is irregular at the beginning, and requires Chinese and Western medicines every month before menstruation can be expected. But every time my menstrual flow is light and dark, my lower abdomen is distended, cold and painful. After two or three years, the menstrual blood gradually becomes less and even stops. Artificial cycle method was used to induce it, and more than 100 doses of traditional Chinese medicine were taken orally, but none of them were effective. So far, I have had amenorrhea for 6 years. Symptoms include a sallow complexion, a tired look, shortness of breath and laziness, sparse and scorched hair; since menstruation has stopped, I often feel dizzy, tinnitus, and feel depressed; sleepiness during the day and inability to sleep well at night; tasteless mouth and no desire to eat; soreness in the waist and waist, weak legs and knees, retrograde limbs, and cold discomfort in the lower abdomen; heavy pulse, pale tongue, dark color and blood stasis, and thin, white and moist coating. This is caused by insufficient Yuanyang, deficiency of both Chong and Ren, cold blood and qi stagnation, and cold uterus. Yang deficiency produces cold, qi deficiency easily stagnates, cold blood coagulates, menstrual blood has no source, so it stops, and pregnancy is infertile. It should be used to warm the lower yuan, warm the menstrual flow, activate blood circulation, disperse cold and warm the palace, and treat it with the self-prescribed Yiyuan Nuangong Decoction: 100g of Aconite slices, 15g of Angelica sinensis, 15g of Salvia miltiorrhiza, 12g of Guizhi, 9g of Wuyu, 12g of roasted Cyperus rotundus, 6g of Asarum, 9g of red peony root, 12g of fried mugwort leaves, 15g of dried ginger, and 9g of licorice. \\nAfter taking the above 3 doses, the abdominal pain was reduced by 70 to 80%, the cold feeling in the lower abdomen was relieved, and there was still a feeling of bloating. Food cravings increase, the hands, feet and limbs become warmer, the heart is no longer depressed, and the patient can sleep well at night; the pulse is still heavy and astringent, the tongue is pale, the blood stasis is slightly reduced, and the coating is thin and white. Following the above, add 5g of safflower to help warm the menstrual flow and activate blood circulation. He was also instructed to drop a little wine as a guide when taking the medicine to promote warming and circulation of blood vessels. If all symptoms improve after taking the medicine, but pain and soreness in the waist and lower abdomen return, this is a sign of menstrual cramps.	I took 8 doses in a row, and it was as good as I said. Remove the red peony root from the original prescription, add 9g of Chuanxiong, and 15g of donkey-hide gelatin (take it in a boiled form). Take 5 doses in a row. Menstrual fluid will become flushed. The first one will be black blood clots, and then they will become red. \\nThe next day, the pain in the waist and abdomen was relieved, and the menstruation was cleared after 5 days. Then add Bazhen Decoction with Cyperus rotunda, Yi Mu, fried mugwort, etc. to replenish qi and blood. After taking more than 10 doses, my complexion and hair are moisturized, and my energy, sleep and eating are getting better. Afterwards, through information and communication, the baby was born naturally one year later. \\nNote: The symptom of 6-year amenorrhea is diagnosed as "insufficient Yuan Yang, deficiency of both Chong and Ren, cold blood and qi stagnation, and cold uterus". It can be treated by warming and supporting the lower Yuan, dispersing cold and warming the uterus, and it will be cured after a month of conditioning. It is indeed the Vulcan style.',经验方:"Formulas",缩小:"zoom out","缩睾症案 马某，男，27岁":"Testicular shrinkage case: Ma, male, 27 years old","缩睾症案\\n马某，男，27岁。右侧睾丸肿痛2月余，治疗后肿痛逐渐消退。某日夜间，右侧睾丸突然收引回缩至少腹，拘挛疼痛不已，牵引腰部，痛不能伸，痛剧之时，连及脐腹，直至四肢挛急难以屈伸；颜面发青，冷汗淋漓；腹痛呻吟，愁容不展，两目无神，白睛发蓝，唇、舌、指甲均含青色；舌苔白腻，手足冰冷，脉来沉细弦紧；已两日水米不进。此系肝肾阳虚，厥阴阴寒太盛，阳不足以温熙筋脉。所谓“寒则收引”之意。法当温扶肝肾之阳，温经散寒，经脉之挛急自能舒缓。方用当归四逆汤加味：\\n当归I5g，桂枝12g，杭芍9g，细辛6g，通草6g，大枣5枚，干姜12g，吴萸6g，川椒5g‘（炒黄），乌梅4枚，附片60g。\\n1剂后，疼痛缓解；再剂则阴囊松缓，睾丸回复，面目、唇舌青色俱退，手足回温，诸痛皆愈。唯阳神尚虚。照原方去川椒，加砂仁9g，连服2剂，精神、饮食均恢复正常。\\n按：郑钦安谓：“须知肿缩二字，即盈虚之宗旨，肝气有余便是火，即囊丸肿的实据；肝气不足便是寒，即囊丸缩的实据……治缩者，重在破阴以回阳，吴萸四逆加桂、砂、小茴，或乌梅丸倍阳药之类；治肿者，法宜破阳以扶阴，鸡子黄连与泻肝汤可施。”吴氏本案即宗此旨，虽用当归四逆汤，仔细揣摩用药，亦含乌梅丸之意。":`Testicular shrinkage case\\nMa, male, 27 years old. The right testicle was swollen and painful for more than 2 months, and the swelling and pain gradually subsided after treatment. One night, the right testicle suddenly retracted and retracted to the abdomen, causing severe cramping pain. The waist was pulled, and the pain could not be extended. When the pain was severe, it was connected to the umbilicus and abdomen, until the limbs were contracted and difficult to bend and extend; This is due to liver and kidney yang deficiency, excessive yin and cold yin, and insufficient yang to warm the tendons and veins. The so-called "cold leads to withdrawal". The method should warm and support the yang of the liver and kidneys, warm the meridians and dispel cold, and soothe the tightness of the meridians. The recipe is flavored with Danggui Sini Decoction:\\nAngelica I5g, Guizhi 12g, Hangshao 9g, Asarum 6g, Tongcao 6g, 5 jujubes, 12g dried ginger, 6g Wuyu, 5g Sichuan pepper (fried yellow), 4 ebony plums, 60g Fengzhi. \\nAfter one dose, the pain was relieved; after another dose, the scrotum was relaxed, the testicles recovered, the blue color of the face, lips and tongue disappeared, the hands and feet became warm, and all pains were relieved. Only the Yang God is still empty. Follow the original recipe and remove the Sichuan peppercorns, add 9g of amomum villosum, and take 2 doses, and the spirit and diet return to normal. \\nNote: Zheng Qin'an said: "It should be noted that the word "swelling and shrinking" refers to the purpose of excess and deficiency. Excessive liver qi means fire, which is the basis for swelling of the bladder; insufficient liver qi means cold, which is the basis for shrinkage of the bladder... To treat shrinkage, the focus is to break the yin to restore yang, and the four inverses of Wuyu Add cinnamon, sand, cumin, or black plum pills to double the yang. For swelling, the method is to break the yang and support the yin. Chicken Coptis and Xiegan Decoction can be used. This is the purpose of Wu's case. Although she used Danggui Sini Decoction, she carefully thought about the medicine and it also contained the meaning of black plum pills.`,缩睾证:"testicle shrinkage syndrome",翻阅典籍:"Read the classics","肝水肿 （肝硬化腹水） 胡某，男，五十三岁，因患肝硬化腹水臌胀，…":"Hepatic edema (cirrhosis and ascites) Hu, male, 53 years old, suffered from swollen ascites due to cirrhosis of the liver,…","肝水肿 （肝硬化腹水） 胡某，男，五十三岁，因患肝硬化腹水臌胀，住昆明某医 院，于1958年12月12日邀余会诊。 询及由来,病者始因患红白痢证一月余，继后渐感腹胀, 逐渐发展而成腹水肿胀之证。余视之，面色黄暗，神情淡漠， 卧床不起，腹部鼓胀膨窿，已有腹水内积，肝脏肿大，触之稍 硬,小腹坠胀，小便短少,饮食不进。脉象缓弱，舌苔白滑，舌 质含青色。此系下痢日久脾肾阳虚，寒湿内停,肝气郁结而致 肝脏肿大，肺肾气虚，不能行司通调水道、化气利水之职能， 遂致寒水内停，日积月累而成腹水臓胀证。法当温中扶阳化 气逐水,拟四逆五苓散加减主之。 附片80克，干姜30克，上肉桂8克（研末，泡水兑入）， 败酱15克，猪苓15克，茯苓30克，甘草10克。 同时以大戟、芫花、甘遂各等量，研末和匀（即十枣汤粉 剂），日服6~10克。 服后次日，每日畅泻稀水大便数次。泻后腹水大减,精神 稍欠,又继服上方，扶阳温化逐水。 1959年1月二诊。服上方三剂后，腹水已消去一半多，体 重减轻二十市斤。诊其脉来沉缓，右脉较弱，系脾湿阳虚脉 象。左肝脉带弦，系肝寒郁结，寒水内停之象。舌质较转红润， 白苔已退去其半，再照上方加减与服之。 附片80克，干姜40克，川椒6克（炒去汗），上肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑入），吴茱萸10克，茯苓30克，苍术15克， 公丁香5克。 如前法再服十枣汤粉剂二日。 三诊。服药后昨日又水泻十多次，吐一两次，腹水消去十 分之八,体重又减轻10市斤。患者面色已转为红润，精神不 减,舌苔退，舌质亦转红活。小便清长,饮食转佳，已能下床行 动，自行至厕所大小便。唯口中干，但思热饮而不多。系泻水 之后，肾阳尚虚，津液不升所致。继以扶阳温化主之。 附片80克，干姜40克，砂仁10克，枳壳8克，上肉桂8 克（研末，泡水兑入），猪苓10克，茯苓30克。 服此方十余剂后,腹水、肝肿全消,食量增加，即告痊愈。 按:寒水内停为病之标，脾肾阳衰为病之本。标实本虚治 以攻补相兼之法，皆相得宜。所治之法一如离照当空，一如凿 渠引水，寒水坚冰何得不去焉！如不放胆用此峻猛之剂，姑息荞奸，于此危证，终不免肿胀癃闭，衰竭而逝。":"Hepatic edema (cirrhosis and ascites) Hu, male, 53 years old, suffered from cirrhosis and ascites and was admitted to a hospital in Kunming. On December 12, 1958, he invited Yu for consultation. When asked about the cause, the patient had suffered from red and white diarrhea for more than a month, then gradually felt abdominal distension, and gradually developed into ascites and swelling. I looked at him and saw that his complexion was yellow and dark, his expression was indifferent, he was bedridden, his abdomen was distended, he had accumulated ascites, his liver was enlarged and slightly hard to touch, his lower abdomen was swollen, he had little urine, and he couldn't eat well. The pulse is slow and weak, the tongue coating is white and slippery, and the tongue texture is blue. This is a syndrome caused by prolonged diarrhea, spleen and kidney yang deficiency, internal stasis of cold and dampness, stagnation of liver qi, resulting in liver enlargement, and lung and kidney qi deficiency. The function of regulating water channels, transforming qi and diluting water cannot be performed, resulting in internal stasis of cold water, which accumulates over time to form ascites and distension. The method is to warm the middle and support the yang, transform the qi and drive the water, and it is mainly based on the addition and subtraction of Si Ni Wu Ling Powder. 80 grams of Aconite slices, 30 grams of dried ginger, 8 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 15 grams of bean paste, 15 grams of Polyporus, 30 grams of Poria, and 10 grams of licorice. At the same time, take equal amounts of Euphorbia, Daphne, and Kansui, grind them into powder and mix well (i.e. Shizao Decoction powder), and take 6 to 10 grams daily. The next day after taking it, I had diarrhea and watery stools several times a day. After diarrhea, the ascites was greatly reduced and the energy was a little low. I continued to take the above medicine to support the yang and warm up the water. Second consultation in January 1959. After taking the above three doses, more than half of the ascites has disappeared and the weight has dropped by 20 pounds. The patient's pulse was slow and slow, and the right pulse was weak, which was due to spleen dampness and yang deficiency. The stringy left liver vein is a symptom of liver cold stagnation and cold water stasis. The tongue becomes more rosy, and half of the white coating has receded. Then add or subtract the medicine above and take it. 80 grams of Futian, 40 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of Sichuan pepper (fried to remove sweat), 10 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 10 grams of Evodia, 30 grams of Poria, 15 grams of Atractylodes, and 5 grams of cloves. Take Shizao Decoction powder for another two days as before. Three diagnoses. After taking the medicine, I had diarrhea more than ten times yesterday and vomited once or twice. Eight-tenths of the ascites disappeared and my weight lost another 10 pounds. The patient's complexion has turned rosy, his energy has not decreased, his tongue coating has receded, and his tongue has also turned red. His urine is long and clear, his diet has improved, and he is now able to get out of bed and go to the toilet to relieve himself. My mouth is dry, but I want hot drinks but not much. It is caused by the deficiency of kidney yang and failure of body fluid to rise after diarrhea. Followed by Fuyang warming. 80 grams of Aconite slices, 40 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of Amomum villosum, 8 grams of Citrus aurantium husk, 8 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix in), 10 grams of Poria cocos, and 30 grams of Poria cocos. After taking more than ten doses of this prescription, the ascites and liver swelling disappeared, the food intake increased, and the patient was cured. Note: Internal stasis of cold water is the symptom of the disease, and deficiency of spleen and kidney yang is the root of the disease. Treat the actual condition and the underlying deficiency with the method of attack and supplement, both of which are suitable for each other. The method of treatment is the same as clearing the sky from the sun, or digging a canal to divert water. Why not remove the cold water and solid ice! If you don't boldly use this harsh and powerful medicine to treat buckwheat rape, this dangerous syndrome will inevitably lead to swelling, constriction, and death from exhaustion.",肝炎:"hepatitis",肝病:"Liver disease","肝病治脾，见肝之病，知肝传脾，当先实脾。":"Treat liver disease by treating the spleen. When seeing liver disease, knowing that the liver transmits to the spleen, the spleen should be strengthened first.",肝病科:"Hepatology",肝硬化:"Cirrhosis","肝硬化腹水案 方某，男，28岁":"Case of liver cirrhosis and ascites Fang, male, 28 years old","肝硬化腹水案 李某，男":"Case of liver cirrhosis and ascites Li, male","肝硬化腹水案 胡某，男，53岁":"Case of liver cirrhosis and ascites Hu, male, 53 years old","肝硬化腹水案\\n方某，男，28岁。肝脾肿大，全身发黄已8年。先后在军区、省市医院治疗，疗效不显。继而出现腹水，腹围98cm，黄疸指数100U，剖腹探查，诊为“胆汁性肝硬化”。初诊：身形羸瘦，面黄、身黄晦滞无光，巩膜深度黄染，周身皮肤干枯瘙痒而见抓痕。精神倦怠，声低息短，少气懒言，不思食，不渴饮，小便短少，色黄如浓茶，腹胀如鼓，四肢瘦削，颜面及足附浮肿，两胁疼痛，尤以肝区为甚。肝肿大肋下2指，脾肿大肋下3指。脉沉取弦劲而紧，舌苔白滑厚腻而带黄色，少津。辨为阳虚水寒，肝气郁结不得温升，脾虚失其运化，湿浊阻遏中焦，胆汁失其顺降溢于肌肤，故全身发黄。阳虚则湿从寒化，肤色黄晦不鲜，似阴黄之候，即阴痺证。法当扶阳抑阴，疏肝利胆，健脾除湿，以四逆茵陈五苓散加减主之：\\n附片100g，干姜50g，肉桂I5g（研末，泡水兑入），吴萸15g（炒），败酱15g，茵陈30g，猪苓15g，茯苓50g，北细辛8g，苍术20g，甘草8g。\\n二诊：服上方10余剂后，黄疸退去十之八九，肝脾肿大已缩小，小便色转清长，肿胀渐消，黄疸指数降至20U，面部黄色减退，渐现红润之色，食欲增加，大便正常，精神转佳。患病已久，肝肾极为虚寒，脾气尚弱，寒湿尚未肃清。再以扶阳温化主之：\\n附片150g，干姜80g，茵陈80g，茯苓30g，苡仁20g，肉桂15g（研末，泡水兑入），吴萸10g（炒），白术20g，桂尖30g，甘草l0g。\\n三诊：服上方6剂后，肝脾已不肿大，胁痛若失，小便清利如常；面足浮肿及腹水鼓胀已全消退，饮食精神倍增；皮肤及巩膜已不见发黄，黄疸指数降至3U；脉象和缓，舌苔白润，厚腻苔已退。此水湿已除，元阳尚虚。再拟扶阳温化调理，促其正气早复：\\n附片150g，干姜90g，砂仁15g，郁金10g，苡仁30g，肉桂15g（研末，泡水兑入），佛手20g，甘草10g。\\n服上方七八剂后，患者基本恢复健康。1年后随访，未再发作。\\n原按：以上病证，实由阳虚水寒，寒湿内滞，肝气郁结不舒所致。阳虚则水邪泛溢，肝郁则易克伐脾土，脾虚不能健运，湿从寒化，而至肝脾肿大、腹水、黄疸诸症丛生。余所拟用各方，旨在温暖肾寒，疏肝解郁，健运脾湿，化气行水。寒湿内滞之证，施以温化之剂，犹如春和日暖，冰雪消融，故能治之而愈\\n按：病涉肝经，吴氏在用四逆五苓散的同时，常加入厥阴经药品如吴萸、败酱、佛手、川椒等，体现分经用药之旨。":'Case of liver cirrhosis and ascites\\nFang, male, 28 years old. Hepatosplenomegaly and yellowing all over his body have been present for 8 years. He was treated successively in military region, provincial and municipal hospitals, but the effect was not obvious. Ascites then appeared, the abdominal circumference was 98cm, and the jaundice index was 100U. After exploratory laparotomy, he was diagnosed as "biliary cirrhosis". Initial diagnosis: thin body, yellow face and body, deep jaundice of the sclera, dry itching and scratches on the skin all over the body. Mental fatigue, low voice and short breath, lack of breath and laziness, no desire to eat, no desire to drink, short urine, yellow color like strong tea, abdominal distension like a drum, thin limbs, edema of the face and feet, and pain in both flanks, especially in the liver area. Hepatomegaly is 2 fingers below the ribs, and splenomegaly is 3 fingers below the ribs. The pulse is deep, stringy and tight, the tongue coating is white, slippery, thick, greasy and yellow, and there is little fluid. It is identified as Yang deficiency and cold water, stagnation of liver qi that prevents the temperature from rising, spleen deficiency that prevents its transportation and transformation, dampness and turbidity that blocks the middle burner, and bile that fails to descend smoothly and overflows over the skin, so the whole body becomes yellow. When yang is deficient, the dampness turns from cold, and the skin color becomes yellowish and dull, resembling yin-yellow syndrome, that is, yin paralysis syndrome. Fadang supports yang and suppresses yin, soothes the liver and promotes gallbladder, invigorates the spleen and removes dampness. Sini Yinchen Wuling Powder is the main method: 100g of attached tablets, 50g of dried ginger, 5g of cinnamon I (pulverized, soaked water), 15g Wuyu (stir-fried), 15g Baijiang, 30g Yincheng, Polyporus 15g, Poria 50g, Asarum 8g, Atractylodes 20g, Licorice 8g. \\nSecond diagnosis: After taking more than 10 doses of the above medicine, jaundice has receded in nine out of ten cases, hepatosplenomegaly has shrunk, urine color has turned clear and long, swelling has gradually subsided, jaundice index has dropped to 20U, the yellow color of the face has subsided and gradually turned rosy, appetite has increased, stools are normal, and the spirit has improved. I have been ill for a long time, my liver and kidneys are extremely weak and cold, my spleen is still weak, and the cold and dampness have not been cleared away. Then use Fuyang to warm it up: 150g of Fuyang slices, 80g of dried ginger, 80g of Artemisia argyi, 30g of Poria, 20g of Yiren, 15g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10g of Wuyu (stir-fried), 20g of Atractylodes, 30g of Guijian, and 10g of licorice. \\nThird diagnosis: After taking 6 doses of the above, the liver and spleen are no longer swollen, the hypochondriac pain is gone, and the urine is clear and clear as usual; facial and foot edema and ascites bulging have completely subsided, and eating energy has doubled; the skin and sclera have disappeared, and the jaundice index has dropped to 3U; the pulse is gentle, the tongue coating is white and moist, and the thick and greasy coating has receded. This water dampness has been removed, but the Yuanyang is still weak. Then use Fuyang warming and conditioning to promote early recovery of healthy energy: 150g of Fuyang, 90g of dried ginger, 15g of amomum villosum, 10g of turmeric, 30g of yiren, 15g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 20g of bergamot, and 10g of licorice. \\nAfter taking the above seven or eight doses, the patient basically recovered to health. Follow-up visit 1 year later showed no recurrence. \\nOriginal note: The above syndromes are actually caused by yang deficiency and cold water, internal stagnation of cold and dampness, and stagnation of liver qi. Yang deficiency means water evil will overflow, liver stagnation will easily attack the spleen earth, spleen deficiency will not improve transportation, and dampness will change from cold, leading to hepatosplenomegaly, ascites, and jaundice. The various methods I plan to use are aimed at warming the cold kidneys, soothing the liver and relieving stagnation, strengthening the spleen and promoting dampness, and transforming qi and flowing water. For symptoms of internal stagnation of cold and dampness, applying warming agents is like a warm spring day, melting ice and snow, so it can be cured and cured\\nNote: The disease involves the liver meridian. While using Si Ni Wuling Powder, Wu often adds Jueyin meridian medicines such as Wuyu, Baijiang, Bergamot, Sichuan pepper, etc. to reflect the purpose of medication according to the meridians.',"肝硬化腹水案\\n李某，男。1958年6月7日初诊：患病已4月，住某医院3月余，诊为肝硬化，引起腹水鼓胀，病势垂危。眼睛发黄，小便日二三次，量少呈咖啡色；面黄黯，腹胀，右胁下作痛厉害；微咳痰少，腰微痛。脉弦滑，按之无力，左尺较沉弱，右尺几无；舌青紫，苔厚腻带黑色。此系肾虚阳弱，肝寒脾湿而致阴黄疸症。以四逆汤合薏改附子败酱散加减：\\n附片100g，筠姜40g，败酱20g，薏苡仁30g，茵陈20g，花椒10g（炒黄），上肉桂l（）g（研末，泡水兑入），茯苓50g，法夏15g，生草10g。 4剂\\n二诊：腹水已消十之二三，眼睛仍黄，眼眶青色；脉沉滑，左脉较弱，舌质转红润。，仍以上方加减：\\n附片150g，筠姜50g，佛手10g，败酱15g，吴茱萸10g，茯苓40g，上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑人），猪苓20g，泽泻10g，茵陈10g，生草8g。4剂。\\n三诊：腹水消去十分七八，胁痛已大减，大便正常，小便清长，脉沉缓，面色唇舌均转红润。以温寒除湿之剂主之：\\n附片150g，筠姜50g.白术20g，元胡8g，北细辛8g，猪苓15g，花椒10g，广木香4g，生草8g。6剂。\\n四诊：病退八九，唯病久体弱。继以扶阳温肝除湿之剂，连进8剂，大病悉退。\\n附片150g，筠姜40g，砂仁10g，上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），白术20g.青皮8g，生草10g。（顾树华提供）\\n按：吴佩衡用五苓散通常只取3味，诸案大致如此。本案初诊用肉桂、茯苓；二诊用茯苓、猪苓、泽泻；三诊用白术、猪苓，似有意变换选用，唯有附子不断加量。":"Case of liver cirrhosis and ascites\\nLi, male. First diagnosis on June 7, 1958: I had been ill for 4 months and had been admitted to a hospital for more than 3 months. I was diagnosed with cirrhosis of the liver, which caused bulging ascites, and I was in critical condition. The eyes are yellow, and the urination is two or three times a day, and the amount is small and brown; the face is yellow and dull, the abdomen is distended, and the pain under the right hypochondrium is severe; there is a slight cough with little sputum, and slight pain in the waist. The pulse is stringy and slippery, weak when pressed, the left ruler is heavier and weaker, and the right ruler is almost non-existent; the tongue is blue and purple, with thick greasy coating and black coating. This is due to kidney deficiency and weak yang, cold liver and spleen dampness, leading to yin jaundice. Use Sini Decoction and Coix Tears to change Fuzi Baijiang Powder with the following additions and subtractions: 100g Fuzi, 40g Junjiang, 20g Baijiang, 30g Coix Seeds, 20g Yincheng, 10g Zanthoxylum bungeanum (fried yellow), 1 ()g cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 50g Poria, 15g Faxia, and 10g raw grass. 4 doses\\nSecond diagnosis: 23% of the ascites has disappeared, the eyes are still yellow and the eye sockets are cyan; the pulse is heavy and slippery, the left pulse is weak, and the tongue has turned red. , add or subtract from the above: \\nAdd or subtract from the above:\\n150g of Fu Shen, 50g of Junjiang, 10g of Bergamot, 15g of Beijiang, 10g of Evodia, 40g of Poria, 10g of Cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix with people), 20g of Polyporus, 10g of Alisma, 10g of Yincheng, and 8g of raw grass. 4 doses. \\nThird diagnosis: The ascites has disappeared by 70 to 80%, the hypochondriac pain has been greatly reduced, the stool is normal, the urine is long and clear, the pulse is slow and slow, and the complexion, lips and tongue have turned rosy. The main ingredients are those that warm and dehumidify the cold: 150g of Futian, 50g of Junjiang, 20g of Atractylodes, 8g of Radix Asarum, 8g of Asarum, 15g of Polyporus, 10g of Zanthoxylum bungeanum, 4g of Patchouli, and 8g of Radix Asarum. 6 doses. \\nFourth diagnosis: Eighty-nine degrees of illness have subsided, but the patient is weak after being ill for a long time. After taking 8 doses of a medicine that nourishes the Yang, warms the liver and removes dampness, all serious illnesses are cured. \\n150g of attached pieces, 40g of ginger, 10g of amomum villosum, 10g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 20g of Atractylodes, 8g of green bark, and 10g of raw grass. (Provided by Gu Shuhua)\\nNote: Wu Peiheng usually only takes 3 flavors of Wuling Powder, and this is roughly the case in all cases. In this case, Cinnamon and Poria were used for the first diagnosis; Poria, Polyporus, and Alisma were used for the second diagnosis; Atractylodes macrocephala and Polyporus were used for the third diagnosis. It seems that the selection was intentionally changed, but the dosage of Aconite was constantly increased.","肝硬化腹水案\\n胡某，男，53岁。因肝硬化腹水住某医院，邀吴氏会诊。腹部鼓胀膨窿，肝脏肿大，触之稍硬，小腹坠胀，小便短少，饮食不进。脉缓弱，舌苔白滑，舌质含青色。此系寒湿内停，肝气郁结而致肝脏肿大，肺肾气虚，不能行通调水道、化气利水之职，寒水内停而成腹水鼓胀。法当温中扶阳，化气逐水。拟四逆五苓散加减主之：附片80g，干姜30g，上肉桂8g（研末，泡水兑入），败酱草15g，猪苓15g，茯苓30g，甘草10g。\\n同时以大戟、芫花、甘遂各等量，研末和匀（即十枣汤粉剂），日服6〜10g。服后次日，每日畅泻稀水大便数次，腹水大减，精神稍欠，继服上方。\\n二诊：腹水已消去一半多，体重减轻20市斤。再照上方加减与服之：\\n附片80g，干姜40g，川椒6g（炒去汗），上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），吴萸10g，茯苓30g，苍术15g，公丁5g。\\n如前法再服十枣汤粉剂2日。\\n三诊：服药后又水泻10多次，吐一二次，腹水消去十分之八，体重又减轻10市斤。面色已转为红润，精神不减，舌苔退，舌质亦转红活。再经调理10余剂后，腹水、肝肿全消，食量增加，即告痊愈。\\n原按：寒水内停为病之标，脾肾阳衰为病之本。标实本虚治以攻补相兼之法，皆相得宜。所治之法一如离照当空，一如凿渠引水，寒水坚冰何得不去焉！如不放胆用此峻猛之剂，姑息养奸，于此危证终不免肿胀癃闭，衰竭而逝。\\n按：本例在投以四逆五苓散的同时，加用了十枣汤粉剂，攻补相兼，“一如离照当空，一如凿渠引水”“放胆用此峻猛之剂”，胆识兼备。\\n黄煌教授评价本例：“有胆有识，有法有方，不愧为现代经方大家。”（《医案助读》）":`Case of liver cirrhosis and ascites\\nHu, male, 53 years old. He was admitted to a hospital due to liver cirrhosis and ascites, and Wu was invited for consultation. The abdomen is distended, the liver is enlarged and slightly hard to the touch, the lower abdomen is distended, there is insufficient urine, and inability to eat. The pulse is slow and weak, the tongue coating is white and slippery, and the tongue texture is blue. This is due to the internal stasis of cold-dampness and stagnation of liver-qi, leading to liver enlargement. Lung-kidney qi is deficient and unable to regulate water channels, transform qi and diuretic. Internal stasis of cold-dampness results in bulging ascites. The method should warm the body and support the yang, transforming qi and driving away water. The main additions and subtractions of Si Ni Wuling Powder are as follows: 80g of Futian, 30g of dried ginger, 8g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 15g of soybean root, 15g of Polyporus, 30g of Poria, and 10g of licorice. \\nAt the same time, take equal amounts of Euphorbia, Daphne, and Kansui, grind into powder and mix well (i.e. Shizao Decoction powder), take 6 to 10g daily. The next day after taking it, I had loose watery stools several times a day, my ascites was greatly reduced, I was a little less energetic, and I continued to take the medicine. \\nSecond consultation: More than half of the ascites has disappeared, and the weight has dropped by 20 pounds. Then add, subtract and take it as shown above: 80g of Fu Pian, 40g of dried ginger, 6g of Sichuan pepper (stir-fry to remove sweat), 10g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10g of Wuyu, 30g of Poria, 15g of Atractylodes, 5g of male penis. \\nTake Shizao Decoction powder for another 2 days as before. \\nThird diagnosis: After taking the medicine, I had watery diarrhea more than 10 times, vomited once or twice, eight-tenths of the ascites disappeared, and I lost another 10 pounds of weight. The complexion has turned rosy, the energy has not decreased, the tongue coating has receded, and the tongue texture has also turned red. After more than 10 doses of conditioning, the ascites and liver swelling disappeared, the food intake increased, and the patient was cured. \\nOriginal note: Internal stasis of cold water is the symptom of the disease, and the deficiency of spleen and kidney yang is the root of the disease. The methods of treating the actual condition and the underlying deficiency with attack and supplementation are all suitable for each other. The method of treatment is the same as clearing the sky from the sun, or digging a canal to divert water. Why not remove the cold water and solid ice! If you don't boldly use this harsh and powerful agent to appease and support adultery, this dangerous syndrome will inevitably lead to swelling, constriction, and death. \\nNote: In this case, while taking Si Ni Wu Ling Powder, Shi Zao Decoction powder was also added, which has both attack and supplement effects. "It's like digging a canal to divert water." \\nProfessor Huang Huang commented on this case: "He is courageous and knowledgeable, and has methods and methods. He deserves to be a master of modern classics." ("Medical Case Reading Aid")`,肝胃病:"Liver and stomach disease","肝胃诸案以疏肝和胃为纲，逍遥、柴胡疏肝、左金诸方化裁运用，理气而不伤阴，和胃而不碍脾。":"The liver and stomach prescriptions are based on soothing the liver and harmonizing the stomach. Xiaoyao, Bupleurum soothing the liver, and Zuojin are used to regulate qi without damaging yin, and harmonize the stomach without disturbing the spleen.","肝郁气滞者，加柴胡、川楝子；胞宫寒凝者，加肉桂、吴茱萸；阴虚内热者，加生地、地骨皮、女贞子":"For patients with liver qi stagnation, add Bupleurum and Soupeli; for those with cold uterus, add cinnamon and Evodia; for yin deficiency and internal heat, add Rehmannia glutinosa, Digupi and Ligustrum lucidum","肝郁气滞者，加柴胡、白芍；胃阴不足者，加生地、麦冬、石斛；瘀毒胶结者，加半枝莲、藤梨根":"For liver qi stagnation, add Bupleurum and white peony root; for stomach yin deficiency, add Rehmannia glutinosa, Ophiopogon japonicus, and Dendrobium; for stasis and stasis, add Scutellaria baicalensis and Tengli root.",肩周炎:"frozen shoulder","肺脓疡重症案 海某，女，19岁":"Severe lung abscess case Hai, female, 19 years old","肺脓疡重症案\\n海某，女，19岁。行剖腹产失血过多，经输血抢救后，突然高热40℃以上。经用青、链霉素等治疗，体温降低，一般情况反见恶化，神识昏愦，出现呼吸困难，白细胞高达20.0X109/L以上。因病情危重，未做X线检查。继以大量抗生素治疗，配合输液、吸氧均未效，延吴先生会诊。神志不清，面唇青紫灰黯，舌质青乌；鼻翼扇动，呼吸忽起忽落如似潮水，十指连甲青乌；脉弦硬而紧，按之无力而空。辨为肝肾阴气内盛，心肾之阳衰已极，下焦真阳不升，上焦阴邪不降，一线残阳将绝，已现衰脱之象。唯有扶阳抑阴，强心固肾，尽力抢救垂危。主以大剂回阳饮：\\n附片150g，干姜50g，上肉桂l0g(研末，泡水兑入)，甘草20g。\\n因附片需要先煨三四小时，故让患者先服上肉桂泡水，以强心急救。并预告病家，服此方后可能有呕吐反应，如呕吐之后喉间痰声不响，气不喘促，舌质色较转红，尚有一线生机可挽，否则难治。\\n复诊：服上方后果如前言，呕吐涎痰后已见转机，神识较前清醒，嗜卧无神，已能缓慢答问，喝流汁；舌尖已见淡红色，苔白滑厚腻，口唇青紫较退，两颊紫红，鼻翼不再扇动，呼吸仍有困难，咳嗽咯大量脓痰；脉仍弦滑而紧，按之而空。衰脱危候大为减轻，仍以扶阳温化主之：\\n附片150g，干姜50g，上肉桂10g（研末，池水兑入），半夏10g，茯苓20g，甘草8g。\\n三诊：神志清醒，面颊微转润红，指甲唇舌青紫已退十之八九，鼻头、目眶微青，午后潮热，喘咳气短，咯大量脓痰，脉弦滑。病已转危为安，再以上方加减：\\n附片200g，干姜100g，茯苓30g，上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），公丁5g，法夏10g，橘红10g，甘草8g，细辛5g。\\n四诊：面颊微红润，口唇、舌质青紫已退，呼吸渐趋平稳，午后潮热已退，咳嗽、咯脓痰稍减少，胃气已开，能进食。大便溏泻，系病除之兆，脉转和缓。大病初退，情况好转。经X线检查发现双肺有多个大小不等的圆形空洞；细菌培养，检岀耐药性金黄色葡萄球菌，最后诊为“严重型肺脓疡”，拟方：\\n附片l50g，干姜50g，广陈皮8g，杏仁8g（捣），炙麻茸8g。 \\n连服4剂，喜笑言谈自如.病状若失。\\n按：此案认证之独到，令人惊叹。若从白细胞20.0 X 109/L、咯吐脓痰、金黄色葡萄球菌、肺脓疡等现象着眼，势必陷入痰热蕴肺，热毒盛极的认识中，难免大剂黄芩、鱼腥草之类苦寒套方，后果可想而知。吴氏不为其所惑，从神色舌脉断为阴寒内盛，“心肾之阳衰弱已极，一线残阳将绝”，处以大剂回阳饮，附片从150g增至200g，挽起此等重症。其胆识、经验皆非常医所及，不愧火神派大家。\\n黄煌教授评价本案：“又是急危重症，又是四逆汤，又是无可辩驳的疗效，吴氏超人的胆识和丰富的经验，在本例抢救过程中，又一次显露出来。”（《医案助读》）":`Severe lung abscess case\\nHai, female, 19 years old. She suffered excessive blood loss during a caesarean section and suddenly developed a high fever of over 40℃ after blood transfusion for rescue. After treatment with penicillin, streptomycin, etc., the body temperature dropped, and the general condition worsened. He became confused, had difficulty breathing, and had white blood cells as high as 20.0X109/L or more. Due to his critical condition, no X-ray examination was performed. After treatment with a large amount of antibiotics, infusion, and oxygen inhalation, all of which were ineffective, Mr. Yan Wu was consulted. He is unconscious, his face and lips are blue and purple, his tongue is blue and black; his nose flaps, his breathing rises and falls like the tide, his fingers are all blue and black; his pulse is hard and tight, weak and empty when pressed. It is defined as the excessive yin energy in the liver and kidneys, the yang in the heart and kidneys has been extremely weak, the true yang in the lower burner does not rise, the yin evil in the upper burner does not fall, and the residual yang is about to disappear, showing signs of decline. We can only support the Yang and suppress the Yin, strengthen the heart and strengthen the kidneys, and try our best to rescue the dying person. Mainly use a large dose of Huiyang drink: \\n150g of Auxiliary tablets, 50g of dried ginger, 10g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 20g of licorice. \\nSince the epithelial tablets need to be simmered for three to four hours, the patient is asked to drink cinnamon soaked in water first to strengthen the heart. It also warns patients that they may have vomiting reactions after taking this prescription. For example, after vomiting, there is no sound of phlegm in the throat, shortness of breath, and the color of the tongue turns red. There is still a glimmer of hope, otherwise it will be difficult to treat. \\nFollow-up examination: The results of taking the above medicine are as mentioned above. After vomiting and spitting phlegm, things have improved. The consciousness is clearer than before, sleepiness and lethargy, and the patient can answer questions slowly and drink liquid. The tip of the tongue has become light red, the coating is white and slippery, thick and greasy, the purple lips have faded, the cheeks are purplish, the nose no longer flaps, breathing is still difficult, and a large amount of purulent phlegm is coughed up. The pulse is still stringy and tight, but is empty when pressed. The dangers of aging are greatly alleviated, and the main method is still to support Yang and warm them: \\n150g of Fuyang, 50g of dried ginger, 10g of cinnamon (grind into powder, mix with pond water), 10g of pinellia, 20g of Poria, and 8g of licorice. \\nThird diagnosis: She is conscious, her cheeks are slightly rosy, most of the bruising on her fingernails, lips and tongue has faded, her nose and eye sockets are slightly bluish, she has hot flashes in the afternoon, wheezing and coughing, shortness of breath, a large amount of purulent phlegm, and a stringy and slippery pulse. The disease has turned from critical to safe, and then add and subtract from the above:\\n200g of Fu Pian, 100g of dried ginger, 30g of Poria, 10g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 5g of male penis, 10g of faxia, 10g of orange, 8g of licorice, and 5g of asarum. \\nFourth diagnosis: The cheeks are slightly rosy, the bruises on the lips and tongue have subsided, the breathing has gradually stabilized, the afternoon hot flashes have subsided, the cough and purulent phlegm have slightly reduced, the stomach qi has been opened, and you can eat. Loose stools and diarrhea are signs of cure, and the pulse is gentle and gentle. The serious illness has begun to subside and the condition is improving. X-ray examination revealed multiple circular cavities of varying sizes in both lungs; bacterial culture revealed drug-resistant Staphylococcus aureus, and was finally diagnosed as "severe lung abscess." The proposed prescription was: 150g of attached piece, 50g of dried ginger, 8g of dried tangerine peel, 8g of almonds (pounded), and 8g of Zhima antler. \\nAfter taking 4 doses in a row, I can smile and talk freely. My symptoms are gone. \\nNote: The certification of this case is unique and amazing. If we look at phenomena such as leukocyte count 20.0 Wu was not confused by this. From the look on his face, tongue and pulse were broken, he found that the yin and cold in his body were strong. "The yang of the heart and kidneys was extremely weak, and the remaining yang was about to disappear." His courage, wisdom and experience are beyond the reach of doctors, and he is worthy of everyone in the Vulcan Sect. \\nProfessor Huang Huang commented on this case: "It was a critical illness, Sini Decoction, and irrefutable curative effect. Wu's superhuman courage and rich experience were once again revealed during the rescue process of this case." ("Medical Case Reading Aid")`,肾内科:"Nephrology","肾气大亏,气 虚下陷":"Severe kidney qi deficiency, qi deficiency and depression","肾水肿 （慢性肾炎并腹水） 沈某，男，三十岁，浙江人,云南省下关市某机关干部":"Renal edema (chronic nephritis and ascites) Shen, male, 30 years old, from Zhejiang, cadre of a certain agency in Xiaguan City, Yunnan Province","肾水肿 （慢性肾炎并腹水） 沈某，男，三十岁，浙江人,云南省下关市某机关干部。患 “慢性肾炎”已一年余，当地诊治无效。后因发生腹水肿胀,体 虚弱极而转送昆明某医院治疗，住院一周多，其效不显，于 1958年12月12日邀余前往会诊。患者面部浮肿，目下浮起 如卧蚕,面色苍白晦滞，口唇青乌，欲寐无神,神情倦怠已极， 腹内水鼓作胀,其状如匏,下肢浮肿，胫附以下，按之则凹陷 而不易复起,身重卧床，难于转侧。问其所苦,但闻语声低弱， 言及腹中撑胀，腰背酸胀痛楚不止，小腹亦坠胀作痛，口淡不 思食,不渴饮,小便短少。察其舌脉,舌虽润而色淡夹青,苔滑 而灰黑，脉象沉迟无力。此系脾肾阳虚，水寒土湿，寒水泛滥 所致，法当扶阳温寒化气利水主之,方用四逆五苓散加减。 附片100克，干姜40克，花椒7克（炒去汗），猪苓15 克，茯苓30克，条桂15克。 服四剂，小便遽转清长畅利，面足浮肿消退，腹水消去十 之六、七，体重减轻21市斤，腰背痛已大为减轻，仍有酸胀。 稍能食，精神较增。舌苔灰黑已退，呈现白滑苔。脉转和缓，体 尚弱。仍以扶阳温化主之。 附片10O克，干姜50克，吴茱萸10克，桂枝30克，慧该 仁10克，猪苓10克，茯苓30克。 连服四剂，腹水消去十之七、八,面色亦转好,精神、饮食 较增,舌质青色已退，淡红而润，苔薄白滑，脉和缓有神根。大病悉退，阳神尚虚，余邪未净，唯有增强心肾之阳，不变温化 之法,始能效奏全功,照上方加减治之。 附片150克，干姜50克，上肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑 入），砂仁10克，黑丑20克，茯苓50克，丁香10克。 服四剂后，寒水邪阴消除殆尽，善后调理一周，病愈出院。":`Renal edema (chronic nephritis and ascites) Shen, male, 30 years old, from Zhejiang, cadre of a certain agency in Xiaguan City, Yunnan Province. I have been suffering from "chronic nephritis" for more than a year, and local diagnosis and treatment has been ineffective. Later, due to the development of ascites and swelling and extreme physical weakness, he was transferred to a hospital in Kunming for treatment. He was hospitalized for more than a week, but the effect was not obvious. On December 12, 1958, I was invited for consultation. The patient's face is swollen, his eyes are bulging like lying silkworms, his complexion is pale and sluggish, his lips are blue and black, he is sleepy and sleepy, his expression is extremely tired, his abdomen is bulging with water, which looks like a crotch, his lower limbs are swollen, below the tibia, and they are sunken when pressed and it is difficult to get up, and he is heavy in bed and difficult to turn sideways. When asked about the pain, he heard his voice was low and weak, and mentioned abdominal distension, soreness and distension in the lower back, pain in the lower abdomen, pale mouth, no desire to eat, no desire to drink, and lack of urination. Observe his tongue and pulse. Although the tongue is moist, it is light green in color, the coating is slippery and gray-black, and the pulse is slow and weak. This is caused by spleen and kidney yang deficiency, cold water and damp soil, and flooding of cold water. The main method is to strengthen the yang, warm the cold, transform qi and promote water, and use Si Ni Wu Ling Powder. 100 grams of Fu Fian, 40 grams of dried ginger, 7 grams of Zanthoxylum bungeanum (stir-fried to remove sweat), 15 grams of Poria cocos, 30 grams of Poria cocos, and 15 grams of Guizhou Gui. After taking four doses, the urine suddenly became clear, long and smooth, the facial and foot edema subsided, six to seven tenths of the ascites disappeared, the weight dropped by 21 pounds, the back pain was greatly relieved, but there was still soreness and swelling. If you can eat a little, your energy level will increase. The gray and black tongue coating has receded and appears white and slippery. The pulse is gentle and slow, and the body is still weak. It is still mainly controlled by Fuyang and warming. 100 grams of Futian, 50 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of Evodia, 30 grams of Guizhi, 10 grams of Huigairen, 10 grams of Polyporus, and 30 grams of Poria. After taking four doses, 70% to 80% of the ascites disappeared, the complexion also improved, the spirit and diet increased, the cyan color of the tongue had faded, became light red and moist, the coating was thin and white, and the pulse was gentle and had a deep root. All serious illnesses have subsided, the yang spirit is still weak, and the remaining evils have not been eliminated. Only by strengthening the yang of the heart and kidneys without changing the method of warming can the full effect be achieved, and the treatment can be treated with addition and subtraction from above. 150 grams of Fu Feng, 50 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10 grams of Amomum villosum, 20 grams of Heichou, 50 grams of Poria, and 10 grams of cloves. After taking four doses, the cold water evil yin was completely eliminated. After a week of recovery, he was discharged from the hospital.`,"肾结石案 黄某，男，44岁":"Kidney stone case Huang, male, 44 years old",'肾结石案\\n黄某，男，44岁。以腰痛数年而住某医院治疗，经X线摄片检查，右肾肾盂有十粒结石影像，小如花椒，大至蚕豆，诊断为“肾结石”。因身体虚弱不能耐受外科手术，出院延吴氏诊治。腰痛已久，时有所发，痛如绞作，延及腰腹，下引宗筋，痛甚则神怯而畏寒肢冷；小腹胀痛，小便短涩；饮食欠佳，精神缺乏；舌苔白滑而厚腻，脉沉迟无力。辨为肾脏寒极，寒湿不化，内结成石，以温肾扶阳温化之法主之。投以四逆汤加味：附片60g，干姜40g，桂枝30g，茯苓30g，上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），杜仲10g，北细辛6g，甘草6g。\\n服药11剂后，相继经尿道排岀结石4粒，其中1粒较大者，排出时嵌于尿道口，尿线中断，其痛非常，经用银子夹出。X线复查，尚余6粒结石，但影像均较前为小，原大如蚕豆者已不复见。肾寒日久，腰尚冷痛，继以扶阳温化主之：\\n附片100g，干姜50g，北细辛6g，苡仁30g，桂枝30g，狗脊10g，上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），甘草10g。\\n因服药有效，信心不移，连服不断，病情大减，食增神健，体质大为好转，前后相继数十剂，腰痛已不复作，开始恢复工作。再以上方加减，数月后，最后1粒结石亦随尿排出。\\n按：肾结石治疗，一般不离海金沙、金钱草之类利水通淋之品，效果平平。见石不治石，而能成功排石，靠的是“治之但扶其真元"的火神心法。从扶阳入手，用大剂四逆汤加味，全案始终未用一味排石药，专从阴寒湿盛着眼，投以大剂附姜，不治石而治人，竟能愈此结石重症，确实体现了扶阳威力。':`Kidney stone case\\nHuang, male, 44 years old. He was admitted to a hospital for treatment of low back pain for several years. After X-ray examination, it was found that there were ten stones in the renal pelvis of his right kidney, ranging from small as peppercorns to as large as broad beans. He was diagnosed as "kidney stones". Because he was too weak to tolerate surgery, he was discharged from the hospital to Yan Wu's diagnosis and treatment. The pain in the lower back has been present for a long time, and it occurs from time to time. The pain is like twisting, extending to the waist and abdomen, and lowering the tendons. If the pain is severe, the patient will be timid and afraid of cold limbs. The lower abdomen is distended and painful, and the urine is short and astringent. The diet is poor and the energy is lacking. The tongue coating is white, slippery and thick, and the pulse is slow and weak. It is diagnosed as that the kidneys are extremely cold, the cold and dampness cannot be converted, and the kidneys are formed into stones. The method of warming the kidneys, nourishing the yang, and warming the kidneys is the main method. Add the Sini Decoction to taste: 60g of Fu Fian, 40g of dried ginger, 30g of cinnamon twig, 30g of Poria, 10g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10g of Eucommia ulmoides, 6g of Asarum, and 6g of licorice. \\nAfter taking 11 doses of medicine, 4 stones were passed through the urethra one after another. One of the larger stones was embedded in the urethral opening and the urethra was interrupted. X-ray review showed that there were still 6 stones, but the images were smaller than before, and the original stones as big as broad beans were no longer visible. If the kidneys are cold for a long time and the waist is still cold and painful, follow the main method of warming and warming with Yang:\\n100g of Fuyang, 50g of dried ginger, 6g of Asarum, 30g of Yiren, 30g of cinnamon twig, 10g of dog's spine, 10g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water), 10g of licorice. \\nDue to the effectiveness of the medicine, I remained confident and continued to take it. My condition was greatly reduced, I was able to eat better, and my physical condition was greatly improved. After dozens of doses, my back pain no longer occurred and I began to resume work. Adding and subtracting from the above, after a few months, the last stone will be excreted in the urine. \\nNote: In the treatment of kidney stones, it is generally recommended to use products that diuretic and treat stranguria such as Lihaijinsha and Desmodium chinensis, but the effect is mediocre. Seeing a stone without curing it, but being able to successfully remove the stone relies on the Vulcan mentality of "treating it but supporting its true essence". Starting from supporting yang, a large dose of Sini decoction was used to flavor it. No stone-removing medicine was used in the whole case. Focusing on the yin, cold and dampness, a large dose of ginger was added to cure the person without treating the stone. It was able to cure the severe stone disease, which truly reflects the power of supporting yang.`,"胁 痛":"flank pain","胁 痛 （肝炎肝脏肿大疼痛） 魏某，男，廿五岁，原昆明市红十字会医院五官科主任":"Hypochondriac pain (hepatitis, liver enlargement and pain) Wei, male, 25 years old, former director of the facial features department of Kunming Red Cross Hospital","胁 痛 （肝炎肝脏肿大疼痛） 魏某，男，廿五岁，原昆明市红十字会医院五官科主任。 1958年12月30日门诊，患“肝炎”已半年余，右胁内疼痛，双 目白睛发黄,色晦暗，面色亦黄而带青色,大便时溏，小便短 少，其色如茶，右胁肋下触之有硬块作痛，此乃肝脏肿大疼 痛。脉缓弱,舌苔白而厚腻，舌质边夹青色。此系里寒内盛，土 湿木郁，肝木不得温升所致。法当温化寒湿，舒肝达木以治 之，拟方茵陈四逆汤加味。 附片60克，干姜30克，佛手10克，败酱草10克，薏苡仁20克，川椒3克（炒去汗），上肉桂5克（研末，泡水兑入）， 茵陈10克，甘草5克。 服三剂后，脉象沉弱而带弦长,厚腻舌苔已退其半,舌已 转红，小便色转清，较前长,胁下疼痛大有缓减。继上方加减 主之。 附片100克，干姜80克，青皮10克，北细辛10克，茵陈 15克，桂枝30克，茯苓30克，上肉桂6克（研末，泡水兑入）， 甘草6克，川椒6克（炒去汗）。 三诊。服此方四剂后，胁痛肝大已减去十之六、七，脉转 和缓，舌质红活苔薄白而润。面、目黄色退净，小便清长，饮食 如常。继服下方八剂后，即告痊愈。 附片100克，干姜40克,延胡索10克，茯苓36克,广木香 5克，上肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑入），北细辛10克，甘草10克":'Hypochondriac pain (hepatitis, liver enlargement and pain) Wei, male, 25 years old, former director of the facial features department of Kunming Red Cross Hospital. I went to the outpatient clinic on December 30, 1958. I had been suffering from "hepatitis" for more than half a year. I had pain in my right hypochondrium, the whites of my eyes were yellow and dark, and my complexion was yellow with a bluish color. I had loose stools, short and infrequent urine, the color of which was like tea, and there was a hard lump under my right hypochondrium that hurt when I touched it. This was due to enlarged liver and pain. The pulse is slow and weak, the tongue coating is white and thick and greasy, and the edges of the tongue are blue. This is caused by excessive cold inside, damp soil and stagnant wood, and liver wood not being able to warm up. The method should be used to warm and dispel cold and dampness, soothe the liver and damage the wood to treat it. The prescription Yinchen Sini Decoction is prepared and flavored. 60 grams of Sichuan peppercorns, 30 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of bergamot, 10 grams of soybean root, 20 grams of coix seed, 3 grams of Sichuan pepper (fried to remove sweat), 5 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 10 grams of artemisia, 5 grams of licorice. After taking three doses, the pulse was weak and stringy, half of the thick and greasy tongue coating had retreated, the tongue had turned red, the urine became clear and longer than before, and the pain under the hypochondriac was greatly relieved. Following the addition and subtraction above, it is the main one. 100 grams of Aconite slices, 80 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of green peel, 10 grams of Asarum, 15 grams of Yincheng, 30 grams of cinnamon twigs, 30 grams of Poria, 6 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 6 grams of licorice, and 6 grams of Sichuan pepper (stir-fry to remove sweat). Three diagnoses. After taking four doses of this prescription, the hypochondriac pain and hepatomegaly have been reduced by 60% to 70%, the pulse is gentle and gentle, and the tongue is red and has a thin, white and moist coating. The yellow color of the face and eyes has subsided, the urine is clear and long, and the diet is as usual. After taking the following eight doses, he was cured. 100 grams of Futian, 40 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of Corydalis, 36 grams of Poria, 5 grams of Patchouli, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind, soak in water and mix), 10 grams of Asarum, 10 grams of licorice',胁痛:"hypochondriac pain","胁痛（慢性肝炎）案 魏某，男，25岁":"Hypochondriac pain (chronic hepatitis) case Wei, male, 25 years old","胁痛（慢性肝炎）案\\n魏某，男，25岁。患“肝炎”已半年余，右胁疼痛，双目白睛发黄，色晦暗，面色亦黄而带青色；大便时溏，小便短少，其色如茶；右胁肋下触之有硬块作痛。脉缓弱，舌苔白而厚腻，舌质边夹青色。此系里寒内盛，土湿木郁，肝木不得温升所致。法当温化寒湿，疏肝达木。拟茵陈四逆汤加味：\\n附片60g，干姜30g，佛手10g，败酱10g，改仁20g，川椒3g（炒去汗），上肉桂5g（研末，泡水兑入），茵陈10g，甘草5g。 \\n3剂后，脉象沉弱而带弦长，厚腻舌苔已退其半，舌已转红；小便色转清，较前长；胁下疼痛大有缓减。继上方加减主之：\\n附片100g，干姜80g，青皮10g，北细辛10g，茵陈15g，桂枝30g，茯苓30g，上肉桂6g（研末，泡水兑入），甘草6g，川椒6g（炒去汗）。\\n4剂后，胁痛肝大已减去十之六七，脉转和缓，舌质红活苔薄白而润；面、目黄色退净，小便清长，饮食如常。继服下方8剂，即告痊愈：\\n附片100g，干姜40g，元胡10g，茯苓36g，广木香5g，上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），北细辛10g，甘草10g。 \\n按：本例黄疸胁痛，因其寒湿内盛，故予四逆汤大剂为主治之，针对木郁选用了川椒、青皮、北细辛、上肉桂、茵陈等味，剂量不大，主次分明。":'Case of hypochondriac pain (chronic hepatitis)\\nWei, male, 25 years old. I have been suffering from "hepatitis" for more than half a year. I have pain in my right hypochondrium, the whites of my eyes are yellow and dark in color, and my complexion is also yellow with a bluish tint. I have loose stools and short urine, which is the color of tea. There is a hard lump under the ribs of my right hypochondrium that causes pain. The pulse is slow and weak, the tongue coating is white and thick and greasy, and the edges of the tongue are blue. This is caused by excessive internal cold, dampness in the soil and depression of the wood, and a failure of the liver and wood to warm up. Fa Dang warms and resolves cold and dampness, soothes the liver and damages the wood. Add flavor to Yinchen Sini Decoction:\\n60g of attached slices, 30g of dried ginger, 10g of bergamot, 10g of bean paste, 20g of gairen, 3g of Sichuan pepper (fried to remove sweat), 5g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 10g of yinchen, and 5g of licorice. \\nAfter 3 doses, the pulse was weak and stringy, half of the thick and greasy tongue coating had retreated, and the tongue had turned red. The urine became clear and longer than before. The pain under the hypochondriac was greatly relieved. Following the above additions and subtractions:\\n100g of Fenghuan, 80g of dried ginger, 10g of green bark, 10g of Asarum, 15g of Yincheng, 30g of cinnamon twig, 30g of Poria, 6g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 6g of licorice, 6g of Sichuan pepper (stir-fry to remove sweat). \\nAfter 4 doses, the hypochondriac pain and hepatomegaly have reduced by 60-70%, the pulse is gentle and gentle, the tongue is red and has a thin, white and moist coating; the yellow color of the face and eyes has subsided, the urine is clear and long, and the diet is as usual. After taking the following 8 doses, you will be cured:\\n100g of Futian, 40g of dried ginger, 10g of Yuanhu, 36g of Poria, 5g of Patchouli, 10g of Cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 10g of Asarum, and 10g of licorice. \\nNote: This case of jaundice and hypochondriac pain is caused by excessive cold-dampness, so a large dose of Sini decoction is mainly used to treat it. For wood stasis, Sichuan pepper, green bark, asarum, cinnamon, artemisia and other flavors are selected. The dosage is not large and the priority is clear.',胃痛:"stomachache","胃痛案 顾某，男，年四旬":"Stomach pain case: Gu, male, 40 years old","胃痛案\\n顾某，男，年四旬。肾气虚，脾湿素重，时值酷暑炎热季节，常食西瓜凉饮，夜卧贪凉，复受冷风所袭，遂致脘腹疼痛不止，痛极则彻及心胸腰背，水米不下，汗出淋漓，辗转反侧睡卧不安，时时呻吟。吴氏诊之：颜面青黯，舌苔白滑质含青色，脉来一息两至半，沉迟无力，手足厥冷。此乃肝肾之阴寒夹水，脾湿凝聚三焦，凌心犯胃，阳不足以运行而成是状。先以上肉桂10g研末泡水与服之，服后旋即呕吐涎沫碗许，此为寒湿外除佳兆，继以吴萸四逆汤加味治之：\\n附片100g，干姜30g，上肉桂10g(研末，泡水兑入)，公丁6g，白胡椒6g(捣末，分次吞服)，吴萸10g，甘草l0g。\\n服1剂，涌吐酸苦涎水两大碗，痛减其半；再服1剂，又吐涎水两大碗，其痛大减，遂得安卧。次晚续诊，脉已一息四至，汗止厥回，诸痛俱瘥。继以桂附理中汤2剂调理而愈。\\n按：本例胃痛，虽然用“吴萸四逆汤”，考加味中有丁香、白胡椒，显然含有四逆苓桂丁椒汤之意。":`Stomach pain case\\nGu, male, in his forties. Kidney qi is deficient, spleen dampness is heavy, and it is a hot season. People often eat watermelon and cool drinks, sleep in the cold at night, and are repeatedly hit by cold winds, which leads to constant pain in the epigastrium and abdomen. When the pain is extreme, it penetrates into the chest, waist and back. The water is not enough, sweating, tossing and turning, sleeping restlessly, and moaning all the time. Wu's diagnosis showed that the face was blue and gloomy, the tongue coating was white and slippery with a bluish color, the pulse was slow and weak, and the hands and feet were cold. This is caused by the coldness of the liver and kidneys mixed with water, the dampness of the spleen condensing into the triple burner, the Lingxin invading the stomach, and the yang being insufficient to circulate, resulting in this condition. First grind 10g of the above cinnamon into powder and soak it in water and take it. After taking it, you will vomit a bowlful of saliva. This is a good sign that the cold and dampness has been eliminated. Then use Wu Yu Sini Decoction to treat it:\\n100g of Fu Pian, 30g of dried ginger, 10g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 6g of male cubes, 6g of white pepper (pulverized and swallowed in portions), 10g of Wuyu Sini, and 10g of licorice. \\nAfter taking one dose, he vomited two large bowls of sour and bitter saliva, and the pain was reduced by half; after taking another dose, he vomited two large bowls of saliva, and the pain was greatly reduced, and he could sleep peacefully. After a follow-up examination the next night, he found that his pulse had reached four times, the sweating had stopped, and all the pains had subsided. After taking 2 doses of Guifuli Zhong Decoction, the condition recovered. \\nNote: In this case of stomachache, although "Wuyu Sini Decoction" was used, the Kaojia flavor contains cloves and white pepper, which obviously means Sini Ling Guiding Pepper Decoction.`,胃脘痛:"Epigastric pain","胃脘痛一案辨寒热虚实最详，同为痛证，或建中，或泻心，或左金，随证而施，绝无成见存于胸中。":"In the case of epigastric pain, the most detailed distinction is made between cold and heat, deficiency and excess. They are all pain syndromes, either Jianzhong, Xiexin, or Zuojin. It is applied according to the syndrome, and there is absolutely no preconception in the chest.",胆囊炎:"Cholecystitis","胆识救治于书记 1966年春，中共中央西南局书记于江震患肺心病病…":"Courage saved Yu Jiangzhen In the spring of 1966, Yu Jiangzhen, secretary of the Southwest Bureau of the CPC Central Committee, suffered from pulmonary heart disease...","胆识救治于书记\\n1966年春，中共中央西南局书记于江震患肺心病病危，在成都金牛坝宾馆特设病房中抢救。吴佩衡受云南省委派遣，由吴生元陪同，与省委书记阎红彦同机飞赴成都参加救治。当时参与抢救的有戴自英等21位著名的一级教授已先期抵达，包括成都中医学院院长李斯炽、重庆中医研究所所长龚志贤等，专家组组长为四川医学院院长、著名内科专家曹钟梁每天组织会诊，直接向周恩来总理汇报病情。\\n吴佩衡到达时，专家组已决定行气管切开术。他仔细诊查病人后，剖析病情，据理力争，阻止气管切开，力主以中医药治疗。众专家交头接耳，惊叹不语，病床前瞬间的沉默几乎使空气凝滞，吴生元在旁也为父亲揑了一把汗。最后，这一决定得到患者及家属的认可。吴立即书写处方，第1剂用了200g附片（处方见“大回阳饮”一节中于江震案）。然后由吴生元到成都大药店选购最好的上肉桂，并连夜守在3个电炉旁煨煮，试服后，再给病人服用。\\n服药后病情开始缓解，病人对祖父信任有加，只服吴氏开的药。以后附片逐渐增加，15天后病人已能坐起。经一月余的紧张救治，患者已脱离危险，各项指标均趋于正常，遂安排吴氏父子在宾馆休息一日。唯咽部痰液培养有绿脓杆菌，专家组认为有炎症，有人并言“不能再服附子、干姜、肉桂了”。于是重新用抗生素，并给服重庆中医研究所专家所拟之方。\\n2日后病情反复，原有各症又一一出现，且恶寒发热，体温38.6℃。专家组焦急万分，又邀吴氏“大会诊”。有关人员开始不承认给患者服过其他中药，后经检查药渣，内有人参、北芪、黄连、黄芩、天葵子等，才说出已给服此药。\\n吴氏认为此属心肾之阳未复，复用寒凉致阳气衰微，饮邪上泛。急以大剂回阳饮加味投治，附片用400g。此后每日巡诊，附片逐日增至800g，随证酌加公丁、砂仁等。\\n10余日后，各症减轻，已不咳喘，饮食正常，精神渐增，二便调，活动自如，每日可外出散步。一个半月后可以下床走路。患者病情稳定，日趋康复，吴氏父子遂返昆明（据吴生元回忆及《我的祖父——吴荣宗回忆录》）":`Courage to treat Secretary Yu In the spring of 1966, Yu Jiangzhen, Secretary of the Southwest Bureau of the CPC Central Committee, was critically ill with pulmonary heart disease and was rescued in a special ward of Jinniuba Hotel in Chengdu. Wu Peiheng was dispatched by the Yunnan Provincial Party Committee, accompanied by Wu Shengyuan, and flew to Chengdu on the same plane as the Provincial Party Committee Secretary Yan Hongyan to participate in the treatment. At that time, 21 famous first-level professors, including Dai Ziying, had arrived early to participate in the rescue, including Li Sichi, dean of Chengdu College of Traditional Chinese Medicine, and Gong Zhixian, director of Chongqing Institute of Traditional Chinese Medicine. The leader of the expert team was Cao Zhongliang, dean of Sichuan Medical College and a famous internal medicine expert, who organized daily consultations and reported the condition directly to Premier Zhou Enlai. \\nWhen Wu Peiheng arrived, the expert team had decided to perform a tracheotomy. After carefully examining the patient, he analyzed the condition, argued rationally, stopped tracheotomy, and advocated treatment with traditional Chinese medicine. The experts whispered to each other and were silent in admiration. The moment of silence in front of the hospital bed almost made the air stagnant. Wu Shengyuan was also sweating for his father. In the end, this decision was recognized by the patient and his family. Wu immediately wrote a prescription, and used 200g of Futian for the first dose (see Yu Jiang Zhen’s case in the section "Da Huiyang Drink" for the prescription). Then Wu Shengyuan went to a large drug store in Chengdu to buy the best cinnamon, and stayed overnight beside three electric stoves to simmer it. After trying it out, he gave it to the patient. \\nAfter taking the medicine, the condition began to improve. The patient trusted his grandfather more and only took the medicine prescribed by Wu. After that, the number of attachments gradually increased, and the patient was able to sit up after 15 days. After more than a month of intensive treatment, the patient was out of danger and all indicators tended to normal, so Wu and his son were arranged to rest in a hotel for a day. Only the pharyngeal sputum culture showed Pseudomonas aeruginosa, and the expert group believed that there was inflammation. Some people also said, "I can no longer take aconite, dried ginger, and cinnamon." So I started using antibiotics again and took the prescription prepared by the experts from Chongqing Institute of Traditional Chinese Medicine. \\nThe condition recurred 2 days later, with all the original symptoms appearing one after another. She also had aversion to cold and fever, with a body temperature of 38.6°C. The expert team was extremely anxious and invited Wu for a "conference consultation". The relevant personnel initially refused to admit that they had given the patient other traditional Chinese medicines. Later, after checking the medicine residue, which contained ginseng, astragalus root, coptis, skullcap, and Tiankui seeds, they revealed that they had given this medicine. \\nWu believes that this is because the yang of the heart and kidneys has not been restored, and repeated use of cold and cool will cause the yang to weaken and drink evil to rise. Urgently use a large dose of Huiyang drink with flavoring and 400g of attached tablets. After that, daily inspections were carried out, and the tablets were increased to 800g every day, and Gongding, Amomum villosum, etc. were added according to the symptoms. \\nMore than 10 days later, all symptoms were relieved, he no longer coughed and wheezed, his diet was normal, his energy gradually increased, his bowel movements were adjusted, he could move freely, and he could go out for a walk every day. You can get out of bed and walk after one and a half months. The patient's condition was stable and recovering day by day, and the Wu family and his son returned to Kunming (according to Wu Shengyuan's memories and "My Grandfather - Memoirs of Wu Rongzong")`,胎产篇:"Fetal delivery","胎漏案 范某之妻.28岁，身孕6个月":"Fetus leakage case: Fan’s wife. 28 years old, 6 months pregnant","胎漏案\\n范某之妻.28岁，身孕6个月。因家务不慎，忽而跌仆，遂漏下渐如崩状，腰及少腹坠痛难忍，卧床不起。延至六七日，仍漏欲堕。吴氏诊之，认为气血大伤，胎恐难保，惟幸孕脉尚在。以大补气血，扶阳益气，引血归经为法，拟方四逆当归补血汤加味治之：\\n附片100g，北口芪60g，当归身24g，阿胶12g（烊化兑入），炙艾叶6g，炙甘草10g，大枣5枚（烧黑存性）。\\n服I剂，漏止其半；再剂则全止；3剂霍然，胎亦保住。至足月而举一子，母子均安。\\n原按：附子补坎中一阳，助少火而生气，阳气上升，胎气始固；黄芪补中土之气，脾气健运，则能统摄血液以归其经；入当归、阿胶以资既伤之血；艾、附相伍，能温暖下元以止腰腹之疼痛；姜、枣烧黑，取其温经止血，且烧黑变苦，得甘草之甘以济之，苦甘化阴，阴血得生。阳气温升，阴血能朴，则胎不堕矣。《内经云》：“治病必求其本。”本固而标自立矣。若只以止血为主，而不急固其气，则气散不能速回，其血何由而止？\\n按：此案似应有炮姜一药，吴氏称炮黑姜，试看“原按”中有“姜、枣烧黑，取其温经止血”之语可知。查吴氏其他血证案均用黑姜，":`Fetal leakage case\\nFan’s wife is 28 years old and 6 months pregnant. Due to carelessness in housework, he suddenly fell down, and the leakage gradually became like a collapse. The pain in his waist and lower abdomen was unbearable, and he was bedridden. It was postponed to six or seven days, but the leakage was still about to fall. After Wu's diagnosis, he thought that the qi and blood were severely damaged and the fetus might not be safe, but fortunately the pregnancy pulse was still there. The method is to replenish qi and blood, support yang and qi, and induce blood to return to the meridian. The prescription is prepared with Sini Danggui Buxue Decoction with added flavors: 100g of Fu Pian, 60g of Beikou Qi, 24g of Angelicae Sinensis, 12g of donkey hide gelatin (added in yanghua), 6g of roasted mugwort leaves, 10g of roasted licorice, and 5 jujubes (burned black to preserve the nature). \\nAfter taking one dose, half of the leakage was stopped; another dose stopped it completely; after 3 doses, the fetus was still preserved. When the baby reaches full term, both mother and baby will be safe. \\nOriginal note: Aconite replenishes one yang in the Kan, helps less fire to enrage, the yang qi rises, and the fetal qi begins to solidify; Astragalus replenishes the qi of the middle earth, strengthens the spleen, and can control the blood and return it to its meridians; add Angelica sinensis and donkey-hide gelatin to nourish the qi. It is the blood of injury; when combined with moxa and moxa, it can warm the lower yuan and relieve pain in the waist and abdomen; when ginger and jujube are burned black, use them to warm the menstruation and stop bleeding. If they are burned black and become bitter, get the sweetness of licorice to relieve it. The bitterness and sweetness can transform yin, and yin blood can be regenerated. When the Yang temperature rises and the Yin blood becomes pure, the fetus will not be aborted. "Nei Jing" says: "To treat a disease, we must seek its root. "The root is solid and the standard is self-established. If we only focus on stopping bleeding and not urgently fixing the qi, the scattered qi cannot be recovered quickly, and how can the bleeding be stopped?\\nNote: This case seems to have a drug called Paojiang, which Wu called Paoheijiang. It can be seen from the "Original Press" that there is a saying "Ginger and jujube are burned black, and they are used to warm the menstruation and stop bleeding." In Wu's other blood syndrome cases, black ginger was used.`,胸痹:"Chest paralysis","胸痹心痛 杨某,年五十余,某年2月患胸痹心痛证，曾服桂附理中 汤…":"Chest arthralgia and heartache. Yang, who is over 50 years old, suffered from chest arthralgia and heartache in February of a certain year. He once took Guifulizhong decoction...","胸痹心痛 杨某,年五十余,某年2月患胸痹心痛证，曾服桂附理中 汤，重用党参、白术并加当归，服后病未见减。每于发作之时, 心胸撮痛，有如气结在胸,甚则痛彻肩背，水米不进。痛急则 面唇发青，冷汗淋漓，脉息迟弱，昏绝欲毙，危在旦夕。此乃土虚无以制水，阳衰不能镇阴，致下焦肝肾阴邪夹寒水上凌心 肺之阳而成是状。然寒水已犯中宫,骤以参术当归之峻补，有 如高筑堤堰堵截水道,水邪无由所出之路,岸高浪急，阴气上游,势必凌心作痛。斯时不宜壅补过早,法当振奋心阳，使心 气旺盛，则阴寒水邪自散矣。方用四逆汤合瓜篓薤白汤加桂。 天雄片100克，干姜30克，薙白10克，瓜蒌实10克，公 丁香10克，上肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑入），甘草5克。 一剂痛减其半，二剂加茯苓30克以化气行水，则痛减 七、八分,三剂后胸痛若失。":"Chest arthralgia and heartache Yang, who is over 50 years old, suffered from thoracic arthralgia and heartache in February of a certain year. He once took Guifulizhong decoction, which used Codonopsis pilosula, Atractylodes macrocephala and Angelica sinensis, but the symptoms were not relieved after taking the medicine. Whenever an attack occurs, there will be a sharp pain in the heart and chest, as if the Qi is trapped in the chest, and even worse, the pain will go through the shoulders and back, making it impossible to drink water or rice. When the pain is severe, the face and lips will turn blue, dripping with cold sweat, the pulse will be slow and weak, and the patient will feel faint and in danger. This is due to the lack of earth to control water, and the weakened yang cannot calm down the yin, causing the yin evil in the lower liver and kidneys to mix with the cold water and the yang in the heart and lungs, resulting in this condition. However, the cold water has invaded the middle palace, and it is suddenly supplemented by the strong force of Shenshu Danggui, which is like building a high embankment to block the waterway. The water evil has no way out, the bank is high and the waves are strong, and the Yin Qi is upstream, which will inevitably hurt the heart. At this time, it is not advisable to make up for the congestion too early. The method should be to invigorate the heart yang and make the heart qi strong, so that the yin, cold and water evil will dissipate. Use Sini Decoction combined with Guazu Xiebai Decoction and Gui. 100 grams of Tianxiong slices, 30 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of Nagiba, 10 grams of Trichosanthes trichosanthes, 10 grams of cloves, 10 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), and 5 grams of licorice. The pain is reduced by half after one dose, and 30 grams of Poria cocos is added to the second dose to transform qi and move water, and the pain is reduced by seven to eight points. The chest pain disappears after three doses.","胸痹心痛案 杨某之妻，年32岁":"Chest paralysis and heartache case: Yang’s wife, 32 years old","胸痹心痛案\\n杨某之妻，年32岁。于1939年冬，患寒水凌心，胸痹心痛，甚则彻背彻心，经某西医诊治，无效尤重，且断言无救，延余诊视。唇舌淡白，脉来一息两至，形消神惫，水浆不进，气息奄奄，呻吟不已。据云曾昏厥两次。如是险象，危在旦夕，仍照中医的旧理论，判断病源，配合特效方剂，扶阳抑阴，以仲景之乌头赤石脂汤大剂连进，更佐以巴豆霜3g，使排泻寒水由二便而退。1剂后即畅泻数次，病退七八，继以扶阳辅正，3剂全瘥。（《驳冯友兰论中西医药》）按：本例胸痹心痛，形消神惫，气息奄奄，昏厥两次，脉来一息两至，似显虚象，俗医难免用补。吴氏则着眼于阴寒固结，选用乌头赤石脂汤大剂连进，药皆祛寒峻品如乌头、椒姜类，不夹一味补药，尤其“更佐以巴豆霜一钱”排泻寒水，致畅泻数次，病退七八，显现尚攻胆识。":`Case of chest pain and heartache\\nYang’s wife, 32 years old. In the winter of 1939, he suffered from cold water affecting his heart, chest numbness and heartache, which even penetrated his back and heart. He was diagnosed and treated by a certain Western medicine doctor, but it was ineffective and severe. The lips and tongue are pale white, the pulse is coming in and out, the body is exhausted, the water and slurry cannot enter, the breath is dying, and the moaning is endless. It is said that he fainted twice. If this is a dangerous situation, we should still follow the old theory of traditional Chinese medicine to determine the source of the disease, and use special prescriptions to support yang and suppress yin. Take a large dose of Zhongjing's Aconitum Chishizhi Decoction, and add 3g of Croton Cream to make the cold water in the stool disappear. After one dose, the patient had diarrhea several times, and the disease subsided for 70 to 80% of the time. Followed by Fuyang and Zhengzheng, 3 doses were used to cure the disease. ("Refutation of Feng Youlan's Theory of Traditional Chinese and Western Medicine") Note: This case has chest pain and heartache, physical and mental exhaustion, poor breathing, fainting twice, pulse coming and going twice, and it seems to be a virtual phenomenon, so it is inevitable for common doctors to use supplements. Wu focuses on the consolidation of yin and cold, and uses a large dose of Aconitum Chishizhi Decoction. The medicines are all cold-repelling herbs such as Aconitum, pepper and ginger, and do not include any tonics. In particular, "a penny of croton frost" is used to expel cold water, which leads to several times of diarrhea, seven or eight symptoms of illness, and a strong sense of courage.`,"胸痹案 杨某，50余岁":"Chest paralysis case Yang, over 50 years old","胸痹案\\n杨某，50余岁。患胸痹心痛证，曾服桂附理中汤，重用党参、白术并加当归，服后病未见减。每于发作之时，心胸撮痛，有如气结在胸，甚则痛彻肩背：水米不进，面唇发青，冷汗淋漓，脉息迟弱，昏绝欲毙，危在旦夕。认为此乃土虚无以制水，阳衰不能镇阴，致下焦肝肾阴邪夹寒水上凌心肺而成是状，“然寒水已犯中宫，骤以参、术、当归之峻补，有如高筑堤堰堵截水道，水邪无由所出之路，岸高浪急，阴气上游，势必凌心作痛。斯时不宜壅补过早，法当振奋心阳，使心气旺盛，则阴寒水邪自散矣”。方用四逆汤合瓜蒌薤白汤加肉桂：	天雄片100g，干姜30g，薤白10g，瓜蒌实10g，公丁10g，上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），甘草5g。\\n1剂痛减其半；2剂加茯苓30g以化气行水，则痛减七八分；3剂后胸痛若失。\\n按：本例先前治者亦用了桂附理中汤，唯其“重用党参、白术并加当归，服后病未见减”，吴氏喻称“骤以参、术、当归之峻补，有如高筑堤堰堵截水道，水邪无由所出之路，岸高浪急，阴气上游，势必凌心作痛”“斯时不宜壅补过早”，改予四逆汤合瓜篓薤白汤，摒弃参、术、当归之壅补之品，果获良效在应用附子等辛热药物治疗阴证时，是否夹用滋补之晶，是温补派与火神派的重要区别。吴氏在这一点上，表现出鲜明的经典火神派风格。用扶阳诸方，绝少夹用滋补药品，即或补气药也少应用，嫌其掣肘”“正治之方决勿夹杂其他药品，如果加入寒凉之剂则引邪深入；加入补剂则闭门留寇，必致传经变证，渐转危笃费治”（《医药简述》）。":'Chest paralysis case\\nYang, over 50 years old. Suffering from chest pain and heartache, I once took Guifuzhong Decoction, which used Codonopsis pilosula and Atractylodes macrocephala combined with Angelica sinensis. However, the symptoms were not relieved after taking the medicine. Whenever an attack occurs, there will be a sharp pain in the heart and chest, as if Qi is stuck in the chest, and even the pain may go through the shoulders and back: no water or rice can be eaten, the face and lips will turn blue, dripping with cold sweat, the pulse rate is slow and weak, and the person is dizzy and is in danger of death. It is believed that this is because the earth is empty to control water, and the yang is weak and cannot suppress the yin, causing the lower scorch, liver and kidney yin evil and cold water to overpower the heart and lungs. "However, the cold water has invaded the middle palace, and it is suddenly supplemented by ginseng, Shu, and angelica, just like building a high embankment." The weir blocks the waterway, and the water evil has no way out. The bank is high and the waves are strong, and the Yin Qi in the upper reaches is bound to hurt the heart. At this time, it is not advisable to make up for it too early. The method should be to invigorate the Yang of the heart and make the heart Qi strong, then the Yin and cold water evil will dissipate." The recipe uses Sini Decoction combined with Trichosanthes and Trichosanthes Decoction plus cinnamon: 100g of Tianxiong slices, 30g of dried ginger, 10g of Trichosanthes trichosanthes, 10g of Trichosanthes trichosanthes, 10g of male cubes, 10g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed in), and 5g of licorice. \\nAfter 1 dose, the pain is reduced by half; after 2 doses, 30g of Poria cocos is added to transform qi and water, and the pain is reduced by 70-80%; after 3 doses, the chest pain disappears. \\nNote: The previous doctor in this case also used Guifuli Zhong Decoction, but he "emphasized the use of Codonopsis pilosula, Atractylodes macrocephala and Angelica sinensis, and the disease was not relieved after taking it." Wu said that "the sudden use of ginseng, Shu, and Angelica sinensis is like building a high dike to block the waterway, and the water evil has no way out. The shore is high and the waves are strong, and the Yin Qi goes upstream." "It is bound to hurt the heart." "It is not advisable to use tonic and tonic too early at this time." Instead, use Sini Decoction and Guazu Xiebai Decoction, and abandon the tonic products of ginseng, shu, and angelica, and achieve good results. When using pungent and hot drugs such as aconite to treat yin syndrome, whether to use nourishing crystals is an important difference between the warming and tonic school and the fire god school. At this point, Wu shows a distinct classic Vulcan style. When using various prescriptions to support Yang, nourishing medicines are rarely used, and even Qi-tonifying medicines are rarely used, as they are considered to be constraints. "Do not mix other medicines in the correct treatment prescription. If cold and cooling agents are added, the evil will be attracted deep; adding supplements will lead to the secretion of the disease, which will inevitably lead to changes in the transmission of the classics, and will gradually become dangerous and expensive to treat." ("Medical Brief").',"脑膜炎案 戴姓之子，年10岁，万钟街尤家巷七号":"Meningitis case: son surnamed Dai, 10 years old, No. 7, Youjia Lane, Wanzhong Street","脑膜炎案\\n戴姓之子，年10岁，万钟街尤家巷七号。1938年2月，患脑膜炎重症，甚危，经某西医诊治20余日，无效尤重。身热不退，头项强直，不能转侧，耳聋声哑不语，形消神弱，奄奄一息。延余诊视，亦照旧的理论，判断病源，以三生饮、白通四逆等加减配合，大剂连进，涌吐涎水数盆，二便畅利，旬余治愈而复健康。以后学司机，灵动如常。（“驳冯友兰论中西医药”）":`Meningitis case\\nThe son surnamed Dai, 10 years old, No. 7, Youjia Lane, Wanzhong Street. In February 1938, he suffered from severe and critical meningitis. He was diagnosed and treated by a Western doctor for more than 20 days, but it was extremely ineffective. The body heat persists, the head and neck are stiff and unable to turn sideways, the patient is deaf and mute, the body is weak and the spirit is weak, and he is dying. After further diagnosis and examination, we still used the usual theory to determine the cause of the disease. We used Sanshengyin, Baitong and Sini, etc. in addition and subtracted combinations, and took large doses in succession. The patient vomited several basins of saliva and had smooth bowel movements. After ten days, he was cured and healthy again. From now on, learn to drive and be as agile as ever. ("Refutation of Feng Youlan's Discussion on Chinese and Western Medicine")`,脘腹痛:"abdominal pain","脘腹痛 张某之妻，年三十余岁，四川省会理县人":"Abdominal pain Zhang’s wife, over 30 years old, from Huili County, Sichuan Province","脘腹痛 张某之妻，年三十余岁，四川省会理县人。1924年6月患 病，请西医治疗，病情日剧，就诊于余。余视之，舌苔白滑兼灰 黑色，脉细迟欲绝，十余日来饮食不进，微喜滚饮，虽恶寒但 不见发热，心痛彻背。时时感觉腹中有气上冲心胸，心中慌 跳，复见呕吐，触之，腹内有癥坚痞块，痛不可当。缘由前医曾 予腹部注射某药一针，其后针处硬结突起，继而扩展大如碗 口。此乃肝肾阴邪为患，复因针处被寒，阴寒挟水邪上逆，凌 心犯胃，如不急为驱除,绥则必殆无救。遂拟四逆苓桂丁椒汤 治之。 附片130克，干姜60克，茯苓26克，公丁香13克，上肉 桂13克（研末，泡水兑入），白胡椒6克（捣末，分次冲服），甘 草6克。 服一剂则痛减其半，再剂则诸证渐退，痛止七、八，稍进 饮食。唯呕吐未止，此乃肝肾阴寒之邪未净,拟乌梅丸方治 之。 附片130克，干姜60克，当归26克，上肉桂13克（研 末，泡水兑入），黄连13克，黄柏13克，北细辛6克，潞党参 16克，川椒6克（炒去汗），乌梅3枚。 服一剂后，呕吐止。服二剂后，腹痛全瘳，腹内痞块渐散。 继以回阳饮（即四逆汤加肉桂），兼吞服乌梅丸十余剂，始奏 全功。":"Abdominal pain in the abdomen: Zhang’s wife is in her thirties and is from Huili County, Sichuan Province. He fell ill in June 1924 and asked Western medicine for treatment. His condition was revealed in Japanese dramas and he was treated by Yu Yu. Upon further inspection, the tongue coating was white and slippery and gray-black, and the pulse was thready and slow. He had not eaten or eaten for more than ten days, and was slightly fond of drinking water. Although he had an aversion to cold, there was no fever, and his heart ached through his back. I often feel that there is gas in the abdomen rushing up to my heart and chest, my heart is pounding, I feel vomiting again, and there are hard lumps in my abdomen that are painful. The reason is that the previous doctor once injected a certain medicine into the abdomen, and then the needle area became indurated and protruded, and then expanded as big as the mouth of a bowl. This is caused by yin evil in the liver and kidneys. Due to the cold at the needle site, the yin and cold bring water evil upward and reverse, causing the heart to invade the stomach. If it is not expedited urgently, the patient will be hopeless. Then Sini Ling Gui Ding Jiao Decoction was prepared to treat it. 130 grams of Futian, 60 grams of dried ginger, 26 grams of Poria, 13 grams of cloves, 13 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 6 grams of white pepper (pound into powder, drink in divided doses), and 6 grams of licorice. After taking one dose, the pain will be reduced by half. If you take another dose, the symptoms will gradually subside, and the pain will stop for seven or eight days. You should eat a little better. However, if the vomiting does not stop, this is due to the yin-cold evil in the liver and kidneys that has not been purified, and can be treated with the Wumei Wan prescription. 130 grams of Aconite slices, 60 grams of dried ginger, 26 grams of Angelica sinensis, 13 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 13 grams of Coptis chinensis, 13 grams of Phellodendron cypress, 6 grams of Asarum, 16 grams of Codonopsis root, 6 grams of Sichuan pepper (stir-fried to remove sweat), and 3 ebony plums. After taking one dose, the vomiting stopped. After taking the second dose, the abdominal pain subsided and the mass in the abdomen gradually dispersed. After taking Huiyang Drink (i.e. Sini Decoction plus cinnamon) and swallowing more than ten doses of Wumei Pills, the full effect will be achieved.","脘腹痛案 张某之妻，30余岁":"Case of abdominal pain: Zhang’s wife, over 30 years old","脘腹痛案\\n张某之妻，30余岁。心痛彻背，时觉腹中有气上冲心胸，心中慌跳.复见呕吐，触之腹内有癥坚痞块，痛不可当。缘由前医曾予腹部注射某药一针，其后针处硬结突起，继而扩展大如碗口。十余日来饮食不进，微喜滚饮，虽恶寒但不见发热，舌苔白滑兼灰黑色，脉细迟欲绝。此乃肝肾阴邪为患，复因针处被寒，阴寒夹水邪上逆，凌心犯胃，如不急为驱除，缓则必殆无救。拟四逆苓桂丁椒汤治之：\\n附片130g，干姜60g，茯苓26g，公丁13g，上肉桂13g（研末，泡水兑入），白胡椒6g（捣末，分次冲服），甘草6g。\\n1剂则痛减其半，再剂则诸症渐退.痛止七八，稍进饮食。唯呕吐未止，此乃肝肾阴寒之邪未净，拟乌梅丸方治之：\\n附片130g干姜60g，当归26g，上肉桂13g（研末，泡水兑入），黄连13g，黄柏13g，北细辛6g，潞党参16g，川椒6g（炒去汗），乌梅3枚。\\n服1剂后，呕吐止；2剂后，腹痛全瘳，腹内痞块渐散。继	以大回阳饮，兼吞服乌梅丸10余剂，始奏全功。\\n按：本例腹痛而兼呕吐，后选乌梅丸，且“服1剂后，呕吐止”，颇有新意。":'Case of abdominal pain\\nZhang’s wife, over 30 years old. Heartache pierces through the back, and I often feel that there is air in the abdomen rushing up to the chest, and my heart is pounding. I see vomiting again, and there are symptoms and hard lumps in the abdomen that are felt, and the pain is unbearable. The reason was that the previous doctor had injected a certain medicine into the abdomen, and then the needle area became indurated and protruded, and then expanded as big as the mouth of a bowl. He has been unable to eat or drink for more than ten days and prefers drinking water. Although he is averse to cold, he has no fever. His tongue coating is white and slippery and grey-black, and his pulse is thin and slow. This is caused by yin evil in the liver and kidneys. The needle site is cold, and the cold yin and water evil are in reverse, causing the heart to invade the stomach. If it is not expedited urgently, it will be hopeless if it is delayed. Treat it with Siniling Guidingjiao Decoction:\\n130g of Fu Fian, 60g of dried ginger, 26g of Poria, 13g of male cubes, 13g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 6g of white pepper (pound into powder, drink in divided doses), and 6g of licorice. \\nOne dose will reduce the pain by half, and with another dose, the symptoms will gradually subside. The pain will stop for seven or eight times, and you should eat a little better. If the vomiting does not stop, it is because the evil of yin and cold in the liver and kidneys has not been purified. The following is the prescription of Wu Mei Pill: 130g of dried ginger, 26g of angelica root, 13g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 13g of coptis, 13g of Phellodendri, 6g of Asarum, 16g of Codonopsis, 6g of Sichuan pepper (stir-fried to remove sweat), and 3 ebony. \\nAfter taking 1 dose, the vomiting stopped; after 2 doses, the abdominal pain became general and the mass in the abdomen gradually dispersed. After taking Da Hui Yang Drink and swallowing more than 10 doses of Wu Mei Pills, the full effect was achieved. \\nNote: In this case of abdominal pain and vomiting, Wumei Pills were chosen as the last option, and "the vomiting stopped after taking one dose", which is quite innovative.',"脱 发":"hair loss","脱 发 李某，女，二十四岁，未婚，云南大学学生":"Hair loss Li, female, 24 years old, unmarried, student of Yunnan University","脱 发 李某，女，二十四岁，未婚，云南大学学生。1963年以来发 现头发成丛脱落,脱后不见再长,发脱之处圆如钱状,大小不 等，两月余,头发全部脱去，头顶光秃，毫毛不留。患者为此惊 忧不已，寝食不安，日间则心绪不宁，难于静心学习，夜卧又 梦境飘扬，不能安卧熟寐。遍求医药施治，历经数月，未获效 验。于1964年3月由亲友介绍，来余舍求诊，见患者头部用 纱巾缠裹。询其病状，则羞涩含泪欲泣。脉象沉细而弱，舌质 淡，苔薄白润。《内经》云：“肾者……精之处也，其华在发。”肾 受五脏六腑之精而藏之,发为血之余。精与血互为资生,精足 则血充，血充则毛发润泽。故毛发滋荣于血，生长则根源于 肾。此证脱发并非疥癣所致,乃精血不足也，当以补肾荣血之 法为治。方用： 附片60克，炙首乌15克，当归15克，熟地黄15克，肉 桂12克，炒枣仁15克，木蝴蝶（千张纸）9克，益智仁9克 （炒），鹿角胶9克（烊化，分次兑入），甘草6克。 连服八剂后，头部即开始生长银白色短绒毛发，眠食均 见好转。继上方加补骨脂12克、菟丝子9克，药炉不辍，连服 十五剂。一月后，头发已长至一寸多，色泽渐深。照原方，去千 张纸加肉苁蓉12克，又服二十余剂，头发渐长,其色渐转黝 黑,半年后黑发满头,未见再有脱落。":`Hair loss Li, female, 24 years old, unmarried, student at Yunnan University. Since 1963, it has been found that the hair falls out in clusters and does not grow back. The hair loss areas are round and money-shaped and vary in size. After more than two months, all the hair fell off, leaving the top of the head bald, with no hair left. The patient is frightened and anxious because of this, and has restless sleep and eating. During the day, he is restless and has difficulty studying calmly. When he sleeps at night, his dreams are wandering, and he cannot sleep peacefully. I have been seeking medical treatment for several months, but to no avail. In March 1964, he was introduced by relatives and friends and came to Yushe for treatment. He saw that the patient's head was wrapped in gauze. When asked about his symptoms, he was shy and ready to cry. The pulse is thin and weak, the tongue is light, and the fur is thin and white. "Nei Jing" says: "The kidney... is the place where the essence is emitted." The kidney receives the essence from the internal organs and stores it, and the essence is emitted as blood. Essence and blood feed each other. If the essence is sufficient, the blood will be sufficient, and if the blood is sufficient, the hair will be moist. Therefore, hair is nourished by the blood, and its growth originates from the kidneys. Hair loss in this syndrome is not caused by scabies, but caused by insufficient essence and blood. It should be treated with the method of nourishing the kidneys and promoting blood. Ingredients: 60 grams of Fu Shen, 15 grams of Radix Polygoni Multiflori, 15 grams of Angelicae Sinensis, 15 grams of Rehmannia glutinosa, 12 grams of cinnamon, 15 grams of fried jujube kernels, 9 grams of Wood Butterfly (Thousand Sheets of Paper), 9 grams of Pleurotus lucidum (fried), 9 grams of deer antler glue (yawed, added in batches), and 6 grams of licorice. After taking eight doses, silver-white short hair began to grow on the head, and his sleep and eating conditions improved. Following the above, add 12 grams of psoralen and 9 grams of dodder, and continue taking the medicine for fifteen doses. One month later, my hair has grown to over an inch, and its color is getting darker. According to the original prescription, I removed 1,000 pieces of paper and added 12 grams of Cistanche deserticola, and took more than 20 doses. The hair gradually grew longer, and its color gradually turned dark. After half a year, my head was covered with black hair, and no more shedding was seen.`,脾肾气虚:"Spleen and kidney qi deficiency",脾肾阳虚:"Spleen and kidney yang deficiency","脾肾阳虚，寒湿内停,肝气郁结":"Deficiency of spleen and kidney yang, internal stasis of cold and dampness, and stagnation of liver qi",脾胃病:"Spleen and stomach disease","脾虚 不运":"Spleen deficiency and bad luck",腰腿痛:"Low back and leg pain",腹痛:"abdominal pain","腹膜炎案 潘某，广东人，28岁，住南强街七十一号":"Peritonitis case: Pan, a Cantonese, 28 years old, living at No. 71 Nanqiang Street","腹膜炎案 珠市桥恒益店，刘夫人，年20岁":"Peritonitis case: Zhushiqiao Hengyi Store, Mrs. Liu, 20 years old","腹膜炎案\\n潘某，广东人，28岁，住南强街七十一号。1939年9月，患腹膜炎甚剧，住某医院10日，日益加重，该医等均认为腹膜炎，腹内灌脓.肠将溃烂，除开刀外别无二法。因手术费过巨，无力交付，致未签字。旋由军分校李教官介绍，延余到该院诊视。脉来两至，舌苔白腻，胸腹胀痛如鼓，二便不利，用洗便器仍不通；喜冷饮不思食，精神疲惫，势颇垂危。因住院不便诊治，当即出院。即以上肉桂数钱与之，服后约2小时，即畅泻水分数次；继以扶阳抑阴之吴萸四逆汤连进，次日腹膜胀痛如失，配合加减，3剂全愈。（“驳冯友兰论中西医药”）\\n按：以上脑膜炎、腹膜炎案例俱系西医确诊、治疗无效的急重病人，时俗多从热盛毒聚诊治，投以寒凉之药。吴氏不为西医诊断所惑，从神色、舌脉断为阴寒内盛，治以三生饮、白通汤、吴萸四逆汤、姜桂乌附等温热之剂，且“大剂连进”，均于短期内治愈，确显见地。因系“驳冯友兰论中西医药”一文所录病例，故医案中时见“以中医的旧理论，判断病源”等语，含有讥讽之意，特予点明。":`Peritonitis case\\nPan, a 28-year-old Cantonese, lives at No. 71 Nanqiang Street. In September 1939, he suffered from severe peritonitis. He stayed in a certain hospital for 10 days and it got worse day by day. The doctor and others believed that peritonitis was caused by pus filling the abdomen and the intestines would ulcerate, so there was no other way but to operate. Because the surgery fee was too high and I was unable to pay it, I did not sign. Xuan was introduced by instructor Li from the military branch and Yanyu went to the hospital for a consultation. The pulse is coming and going, the tongue coating is white and greasy, the chest and abdomen are distended and painful like a drum, the bowel movement is difficult, and the toilet is still blocked. The patient likes cold drinks but does not want to eat, is mentally exhausted, and is in critical condition. Because hospitalization was inconvenient for diagnosis and treatment, he was discharged immediately. That is, take the above cinnamon with several coins, and about 2 hours after taking it, the water will flow freely for several times; then take the Wuyu Sini Decoction to support yang and suppress yin. The next day, the peritoneal swelling and pain will disappear. After adding and subtracting, the patient will be fully recovered after 3 doses. ("Refutation of Feng Youlan's Discussion on Traditional Chinese and Western Medicine")\\nNote: The above cases of meningitis and peritonitis are all acute and severe patients who have been diagnosed and failed to treat with western medicine. The current common practice is to diagnose and treat the disease based on the accumulation of heat and poison, and the use of cold and cooling medicines. Wu was not confused by the diagnosis of Western medicine. From the diagnosis of facial expression, tongue and pulse, it was yin-cold and internal excess. He treated it with Sanshengyin, Baitong Decoction, Wu Yu Sini Decoction, Jiang Gui Wu Fu and other warm agents. He also used "large doses in succession" to cure the disease in a short period of time, which is indeed an insight. Because these cases were recorded in the article "Refuting Feng Youlan's Theory of Chinese and Western Medicine", the medical records often see phrases such as "using the old theories of Chinese medicine to determine the cause of the disease", which contain a sarcastic meaning and are specially pointed out here.`,"腹膜炎案\\n珠市桥恒益店，刘夫人，年20岁。患腹膜炎，经某西医诊治，月余日益加重，竟断言无救。饮食不进，形消神惫，腹中痞块如石，胀痛不止，奄奄待毙。延余诊视，以中医的旧理论，判断病源，以仲景之乌头赤石脂汤、姜桂乌附加减配合，大剂连进，旬余疗愈而复健康。（“驳冯友兰论中西医药”）":`Peritonitis case\\nMrs. Liu, 20 years old, from Hengyi Store, Qiao, Zhushi. Suffering from peritonitis, after being diagnosed and treated by a Western doctor, the condition became worse and worse over the past month, and he was declared to be hopeless. He was not eating enough, his body was exhausted, his stomach was as lumpy as a stone, he was distended and painful, and he was dying. After a long period of diagnosis and treatment, the old theory of traditional Chinese medicine was used to determine the cause of the disease, and Zhongjing's Aconitum Chishizhi Decoction and Jiang Guiwu were combined with each other in large doses. After ten days, the patient was cured and healthy again. ("Refutation of Feng Youlan's Discussion on Chinese and Western Medicine")`,臌胀:"bloated","自《滇南本草》以降，名家著述薪尽火传，为后学留下临证指南与学术津梁。":`Since the "Compendium of Materia Medica of Southern Yunnan", famous writers' works have been passed down forever, leaving clinical guides and academic resources for future generations.`,自动播放:"Autoplay","芳草部载云木香、香茅、艾纳香、石菖蒲等芳香药物四十余种。兰茂谓芳香之品多入气分，能醒脾开郁、透达经络，滇南湿盛之地尤为要药。":"The Fragrant Grass Department contains more than 40 kinds of aromatic medicines such as yunxiang, citronella, aina incense, and calamus. Lan Mao said that aromatic products can invigorate the spleen and open up the meridians. It is particularly important in southern Yunnan where there is a lot of moisture.",苏氏疏肝理脾方:"Su's prescription for soothing the liver and regulating the spleen",苏涟:"Su Lian","苏涟教授1924年生，早年习现代医学，后系统研修中医，融会中西之长，专攻肝胆疾病。":"Professor Su Lian was born in 1924. He studied modern medicine in his early years. Later, he systematically studied traditional Chinese medicine, integrating the best of Chinese and Western medicine, and specializing in hepatobiliary diseases.","苏涟，云南中医学院教授，长期从事中西医结合肝病临床与科研，倡导“辨病与辨证结合”，为云南肝病学科奠基人之一。":'Su Lian, a professor at Yunnan College of Traditional Chinese Medicine, has long been engaged in the clinical and scientific research of liver diseases integrating traditional Chinese and Western medicine. He advocates "combination of disease differentiation and syndrome differentiation" and is one of the founders of the Yunnan liver disease discipline.',"著《姚贞白医案》":'Author of "Yao Zhenbai Medical Cases"',"著《戴丽三医疗经验选》《戴丽三医案》":'Author of "Selected Medical Experiences of Dai Lisan" and "Medical Cases of Dai Lisan"',"著《滇南本草》《医门揽要》《韵略易通》":'He is the author of "Southern Yunnan Materia Medica", "Medical Essentials" and "Yun Lue Yi Tong"',"著《麻疹发微》《伤寒论讲义》":'Author of "The Micronization of Measles" and "Lecture Notes on Treatise on Febrile Diseases"',著作:"Writings","著作详情 | 云南名医馆":"Book details | Yunnan Famous Medical Center",著者小传:"Author's biography",薪火传承:"Fire inheritance",虚劳咳嗽:"Asthenia cough","虚劳咳嗽 张某，年二十五岁，四川人,1923年患虚劳咳嗽，病经数 月":"Asthenia Cough Zhang, 25 years old, from Sichuan, suffered from asthenia cough in 1923 and lasted for several months.","虚劳咳嗽 张某，年二十五岁，四川人,1923年患虚劳咳嗽，病经数 月。始因盗汗，遗精，食少难寐，求医无效。近则午后恶寒，发 热如潮。面颊及口唇色赤如艳，自汗、盗汗，夜间尤甚。痰嗽不 爽，咳声嘶嘎，咯血盈碗。耳鸣，眼花，头常昏晕，气短而喘，精 神疲惫，不能入寐。脉来虚数无力，舌根白腻。査其所服之方, 均以阴虚有热为治，不外清金润肺止咳、滋阴降火平肝、凉血 止血退骨蒸劳热等百十余剂。又服西药多种，沉疴未起，病势反见日趋沉重。盖此病良由素禀不足，肾气太亏，真阳内虚不 能镇纳阴邪，阴寒水湿夹痰浊上逆于肺，阻遏肺肾升降气机， 表阳失固，营阴不敛，则汗易外泄，已虚之阳无力统摄血液， 则散漫游溢脉外而咯血，阴阳相执,虚阳被阴寒格拒于外：发 为潮热，此午后阴气较盛故虚热愈见浮矣。虽发热而有恶寒 相伴，脉见数，然其体状虚软无力，全属一派阳虚阴寒之象， 非阴虚火旺之肺燥咯血可比也。往日所治,违其证，南辕而北 辙，徒劳无功。如是之证，唯有依照《内经》甘温除热之旨，方 可挽回生机。方用甘草干姜汤加附子。 炙甘草24克，炮黑姜15克，附片45克，大枣3枚（烧黑 存性）。 服一剂，咯血止。再剂则喘咳稍平.，精神较增，再拟四逆 汤加味治之。 附片60克，干姜、炮黑姜各15克，西砂仁15克，炙甘草 15克，大枣4枚（烧黑存性）。 服后痰多而兼杂黑血，此乃得阳药温化运行，既已离经 之血，当随痰浊而排除。遂连进四剂，潮热退其半，血痰已不 见，各节证情均有所减，泻下黑酱稀粪,为浊阴下降。脉转缓， 稍有力，饮食略增。病情已大有转机,照前方去大枣加倍分 量,加茯苓30克、白术18克，连进五剂,颊唇赤色已退，喘定 八、九，潮热微作,竟得熟寐，咳痰有减，咳声较洪,此肺气之 通达也。再进数剂则潮热已不作，食思倍增，咳痰更减，唯其 周身骤然浮肿，面足尤甚。病家因见肿象，不知为阴邪始退、 元气来复之兆，突生疑惧。改延他医诊视，断言“误服附子中 毒”所致，主以绿豆、贝母、麦冬、熟地黄、洋参、枇杷叶、当归、 泽泻、苏子、腹毛、枳壳、炙甘草。殊料服后是晚喘咳顿作，气 滞痰涌，身热再燃。于是惊惶失措，又复促余前往诊视。始知病家苦于不识医理，朝夕更医，几使前功尽弃。余仍以诚言相 告,力主大剂辛温，逆流挽舟，以回颓绝。方用： 附片200克，干姜60克，北细辛6克，麻茸4克，上肉桂 12克（研末，泡水兑入），茯苓60克，甘草24克。 服后出微汗，身热始退。连进三剂后，小便畅通，浮肿尽 消。遂照原方去麻茸加砂仁15克。五剂后，咳痰减去七、八。 饮食、精神转增。去细辛加黄芪、白术各30克，再进十剂，诸 证悉除。唯元气未充，以黄芪建中汤加味调理善后，二十余 剂则体健康复。 黄芪100克,桂枝尖24克,杭白芍24克，附片150克，党参 20克，白术20克,西砂仁15克，大枣4枚，生姜30克，饴糖30克 （烊化兑入）。":`Asthenia Cough Zhang, 25 years old, from Sichuan, suffered from asthenia cough in 1923 and lasted for several months. It started with night sweats, spermatorrhea, difficulty sleeping due to lack of food, and medical treatment was ineffective. In the near afternoon, there is aversion to cold and fever like tide. The cheeks and lips are red and bright, with spontaneous sweating and night sweats, especially at night. Unpleasant cough with phlegm, hoarse cough, and hemoptysis that fills the bowl. Tinnitus, dizziness, dizziness, shortness of breath, mental exhaustion, and inability to fall asleep. The pulse is weak and weak, and the base of the tongue is white and greasy. After checking the prescriptions he had taken, it was found that all of them were used to treat yin deficiency and heat, including more than 100 prescriptions such as Qingjin, moistening the lungs and relieving cough, nourishing yin, lowering fire and calming the liver, cooling blood, stopping bleeding and reducing bone steaming fever. He also took a variety of Western medicines, but the serious illness did not appear, but his condition became increasingly serious. The good cause of this disease is insufficient natural endowments, too deficient kidney qi, internal deficiency of true yang that cannot suppress and absorb yin evils, yin-cold water-dampness and phlegm turbidity go up against the lungs, blocking the lungs and kidneys from ascending and descending qi. The external yang is not solid, and the nutrient yin is not restrained, so sweat is easy to leak. It is hot flashes. The yin energy is stronger in the afternoon, so the deficiency heat becomes more apparent. Although the fever is accompanied by aversion to cold and the pulse is rapid, the body is weak and weak, which is all signs of yang deficiency and yin cold, and is not comparable to lung dryness and hemoptysis due to yin deficiency and exuberance of fire. The treatment in the past was contrary to the evidence and went in the opposite direction, which was in vain. If this is the case, only by following the "Nei Jing"'s purpose of sweetness and warmth to remove heat can the vitality be restored. Use licorice and dried ginger soup plus aconite. 24 grams of roasted licorice, 15 grams of black ginger, 45 grams of Fu slices, and 3 jujubes (burned black for survival). Take one dose to stop hemoptysis. After taking another dose, the wheezing and coughing will subside slightly, and the spirit will increase. Then add Sini Decoction to treat it. 60 grams of attached slices, 15 grams each of dried ginger and black ginger, 15 grams of amomum villosum, 15 grams of roasted licorice, and 4 jujubes (burned black). After taking it, there is a lot of phlegm mixed with black blood. This is due to the warming operation of the yang medicine. The blood that has left the menstruation should be eliminated along with the turbid phlegm. After taking four doses in a row, the hot flashes subsided by half, the bloody sputum disappeared, and all symptoms were reduced. Black sauce and thin feces were purged, indicating a decrease in turbid yin. The pulse is slow and slightly strong, and the diet is slightly increased. The condition has improved greatly. I removed the jujube and doubled the amount, added 30 grams of Poria cocos and 18 grams of Atractylodes macrocephala. After five doses, the redness of the cheeks and lips has subsided, asthma has calmed down for days 8 and 9, hot flashes are mild, and I can sleep well. The expectoration is reduced, and the cough is louder. This shows that the lung qi is clear. After a few more doses, the hot flashes no longer occurred, food cravings doubled, and phlegm coughing decreased, but the whole body suddenly became edematous, especially the face and feet. Because the patient sees swelling, he does not know that it is a sign that the yin evil is beginning to recede and the vitality is returning, and he suddenly becomes suspicious and fearful. The diagnosis was postponed to another doctor, who concluded that the poisoning was caused by "mistaken aconite poisoning", mainly mung beans, fritillaries, Ophiopogon japonicus, Rehmannia glutinosa, American ginseng, loquat leaves, angelica, Alisma, perilla, abdominal hair, Citrus aurantium, and roasted licorice. After taking the special ingredient, I experienced late wheezing and coughing, qi stagnation and phlegm, and body heat rekindled. So panicked, he urged me to go to the clinic again. It turns out that the patient suffers from ignorance of medical principles and has to seek medical treatment day and night, thus almost all the previous efforts have been wasted. I still told him sincerely, urging him to use a large dose of Xinwen to push the boat against the current to reverse his decline. Recipe: 200 grams of Fu Pie, 60 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of Asarum, 4 grams of sesame, 12 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 60 grams of Poria, and 24 grams of licorice. After taking it, I will sweat slightly and my body heat will subside. After taking three doses, the urination became smooth and the swelling disappeared. Then follow the original recipe, remove the semen antler and add 15 grams of Amomum villosum. After five doses, the sputum expectoration decreased by seven or eight. Improvement in diet and spirit. Remove Asarum and add 30 grams each of Astragalus and Atractylodes, and then take ten doses, and all syndromes will be eliminated. However, if the vitality is not sufficient, use Huangqi Jianzhong Decoction to treat the aftermath. After more than 20 doses, the body will be healthy again. 100 grams of Astragalus membranaceus, 24 grams of Guizhijian, 24 grams of white peony root, 150 grams of Futian, 20 grams of Codonopsis pilosula, 20 grams of Atractylodes macrocephala, 15 grams of Amomum villosum, 4 jujubes, 30 grams of ginger, and 30 grams of caramel sugar (added in raw form).`,虚寒胃痛:"Deficiency, cold and stomachache","虚寒胃痛 徐某，男，年四旬余，云南省大姚县人，住滇南个旧市":"Stomach pain caused by deficiency and cold Xu, male, in his forties, from Dayao County, Yunnan Province, living in Gejiu City, southern Yunnan","虚寒胃痛 徐某，男，年四旬余，云南省大姚县人，住滇南个旧市。 1923年10月来昆明治病，就诊于余。询及由来，悉知患心胃 痛证已二十余年，经中西药物屡治未效,近则病情日见增剧， 形体消瘦，面容不展。胸膈痞胀作痛，两胁满闷不舒，院腹灼 痛，痛极则彻于胸背，固定不移，从心下至脐腹窿起板硬如 石，按之亦痛,腰背如负薄冰，慷慷而寒。时而泛酸上冲咽喉， 呕吐黄绿酸苦涎水，心中嘈杂，知饥而不能食，唯喜烫饮，饮 而不多。大便干结难解，小便短涩，手足不温，少气无力，入夜 难寐。舌淡苔白滑腻,脉来沉迟,息间仅两至半,且短而弱。良 由病久阳虚，真火内衰，阴寒内结，脾阳不运，无力以制水邪， 肝郁不疏,挟寒水上逆犯胃凌心。阳虚为病之本，寒水泛溢为 病之标,乃本虚标实之证,法当扶阳温散寒水之邪治之,先拟 乌梅丸方一剂。 附片100克，干姜30克，桂尖30克，细辛10克，黄连10 克，焦柏10克，当归25克，川椒3克（炒去汗），党参3克，乌 梅2枚。 服上方，痛稍减，呕吐酸苦水已少。此病历经二十余载， 根深蒂固，邪实而证顽矣，欲除病根，非大剂辛温连进，方能 奏效。以余多年临床体验，此证每于服药之后，或见院腹增 痛,或吐酸、便泻、小便色赤而浊等征象,可一时有所表露,此 乃药与病相攻，驱邪之兆,若药能胜病,犹兵能胜敌,倘畏惧 不专，虽欲善其事，而器不利也，何以克服！古云：“若药不瞑眩，厥疾弗瘳”。余将此理告病者,务期早除痛苦，渠则严然信 守,遂以吴萸四逆汤加味治之。 附片150克，吴茱萸18克，干姜60克，上肉桂18克（研 末，泡水兑入），公丁香5克，茯苓30克，白胡椒3克（研末, 兑服），甘草15克。 服药后果如余言，一剂则痛反较增，二剂则腹中气动雷 鸣。三剂则涌吐大作，吐出黄绿苦水盈盂，吐后胸胃痞胀舒 缓，白滑苔渐退。更照原方附片量增至200克，每日一剂，连 进十剂，愈服越见吐，痛不减反有所增之势，小便色赤，但较 长，已十余日不大便,诊视则白滑苔已退尽，但舌本透白而无 血色，脉转缓和稍有神,仍喜滚饮而畏寒,正邪交作，势均力 敌。仍照前法，再进不怠。拟方白通汤加上肉桂。 白附片300克，生盐附子150克，干姜150克，葱白9 茎，上肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑入）。 连服二剂，大便始通,色黑如漆,腹痛,痞硬稍减，能略进 饮食。再服数剂，大便则畅泻，色黑绿，臭不可当，皖腹疼痛及 痞硬顿失其半，胃逆作酸已减少。此阴寒溃退，元阳渐复。照 原方去葱白加茯苓30克，砂仁15克，白术30克，甘草18 克。连进数剂，大便由稀而溏，色渐转黄，饮食渐增，舌质已略 显红润之色，脉沉细一息已四至，腹中痞硬已消去八、九，唯 胃皖中仍感灼辣疼痛，时而吐酸水一、二口，复主以乌梅丸 方。服三剂，吐止痛减，食量增加，背寒肢厥已回温。唯形体枯 瘦，正气未充，精神尚差，胃中尚时而隐痛，继以桂附理中汤 加黄芪，并兼服乌梅丸，每日三丸。每服均见好，连服十数余 剂而愈，体健如常。":'Stomach pain caused by deficiency and cold. Xu, male, in his forties, is from Dayao County, Yunnan Province, and lives in Gejiu City, southern Yunnan. In October 1923, he came to Kunming for medical treatment and was treated by Yu Yu. When asked about the reason, I learned that I have been suffering from heart and stomach pain syndrome for more than 20 years. Repeated treatments with Chinese and Western medicines have not been effective. Recently, the condition has become increasingly severe, with a thin body and a dull face. The chest and diaphragm are swollen and painful, the flanks are full and tight, and the abdomen is burning and painful. When the pain is extreme, it penetrates the chest and back and is fixed. From the bottom of the heart to the navel and abdominal cavity, the board is as hard as a stone, and it hurts when pressed. The waist and back feel like carrying thin ice, generous and cold. Sometimes pantothenic acid rushes up the throat, vomiting yellow-green sour and bitter saliva, the heart is noisy, and one feels hungry but cannot eat. He only likes to drink hot water, but not much. Dry and hard stools, short and astringent urine, lukewarm hands and feet, shortness of breath and weakness, and difficulty sleeping at night. The tongue is pale and the coating is white and greasy, and the pulse is slow and slow, with only two to half breaths, short and weak. Good due to long-term illness, Yang deficiency, internal depletion of true fire, internal accumulation of Yin-cold, poor spleen-Yang movement, inability to control water evil, persistent liver stagnation, and cold water invading the stomach and lungs. Deficiency of yang is the root of the disease, and overflowing cold water is the symptom of the disease. This is the syndrome of deficiency in the origin and excess in the disease. The method is to strengthen the yang and warm up the cold water to treat it. First, prepare a dose of Wumei Wan. 100 grams of Aconite slices, 30 grams of dried ginger, 30 grams of Guijian, 10 grams of Asarum, 10 grams of Coptis chinensis, 10 grams of Jiaobai, 25 grams of Angelica sinensis, 3 grams of Sichuan pepper (fried to remove sweat), 3 grams of Codonopsis pilosula, and 2 ebony plums. After taking it, the pain is slightly relieved and the soreness and bitterness of vomiting are reduced. This disease has been going on for more than 20 years, and it is deep-rooted, and the evil is real and stubborn. If you want to get rid of the root of the disease, you can only use a large dose of pungent and warm medicine to be effective. Based on my many years of clinical experience, this symptom may manifest itself temporarily after taking medicine, such as increased abdominal pain, sour vomiting, diarrhea, red and turbid urine, etc. This is a sign that the medicine and the disease are fighting each other to drive away evil spirits. If the medicine can defeat the disease, it is like a soldier who can defeat the enemy. If you are afraid of being incompetent, even if you want to do a good job, but the tools are not good, how can you overcome it? An ancient saying goes: "If the medicine does not cure dizziness, the disease will not be cured." I told the patient this theory to relieve the pain as soon as possible, but he strictly abided by it and treated it with Wu Yu Sini Decoction. 150 grams of Aconite, 18 grams of Evodia, 60 grams of dried ginger, 18 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water), 5 grams of cloves, 30 grams of Poria, 3 grams of white pepper (pulverized, mixed with water), 15 grams of licorice. The consequences of taking the medicine are as Yu said. The first dose will increase the pain, and the second dose will cause thunder and gas in the abdomen. After the third dose, vomiting was severe, and yellow-green bitter water was vomited out to fill the cup. After vomiting, the swelling in the chest and stomach was relieved, and the white slippery coating gradually receded. The dosage of the original prescription was increased to 200 grams, one dose per day, and ten doses in a row. The more I took it, the more I vomited, and the pain did not subside but increased. The urine was red in color, but it lasted for a long time. I had not had a bowel movement for more than ten days. The white slippery coating had receded on examination, but the tongue was completely white without blood color. The pulse was gentle and slightly energetic. I still liked to drink water but was afraid of cold. Good and evil were competing in an evenly matched manner. Still follow the previous method and don’t be lazy if you make further progress. Recipe Baitong soup with cinnamon. 300 grams of white aconite slices, 150 grams of raw salted aconite, 150 grams of dried ginger, 9 white stalks of scallions, and 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix in). After taking two doses, the stool becomes clear, the color is as black as paint, the abdominal pain and constipation are slightly reduced, and the patient can eat a little more. After taking a few more doses, the stool became smooth, dark-green in color, and had an unbearable odor. Half of the abdominal pain and constipation in Anhui were reduced, and gastric reflux acidity was reduced. The yin and cold retreat, and the yang gradually recovers. Follow the original recipe and add 30 grams of Poria cocos, 15 grams of Amomum villosum, 30 grams of Atractylodes macrocephala, and 18 grams of licorice. After several doses, the stool changed from thin to loose, and the color gradually turned yellow. The diet gradually increased, the tongue became slightly red, the pulse was heavy and thready for four breaths, and the hardness in the abdomen had disappeared for eight or nine times. After taking three doses, the vomiting and pain were reduced, the food intake increased, and the cold back and limbs recovered. However, his body was thin, his righteousness was not sufficient, his spirit was still poor, and he still had a dull pain in his stomach from time to time. He then took Guifu Lizhong Decoction plus astragalus root, and also took Wumei Pills, three pills a day. Every time I took it, I felt better. After taking more than ten doses, I recovered and my body was as healthy as usual.',"虚寒胃痛案 徐某，男，年四旬":"Case of stomachache due to deficiency and cold: Xu, male, 40 years old","虚寒胃痛案\\n徐某，男，年四旬。患心胃痛证已20余年，病情日见增剧，形体消瘦，胸膈痞胀作痛，两胁满闷不舒，脘腹灼痛，痛极则彻于胸背，固定不移，从心下至脐腹隆起板硬如石，按之亦痛，腰背如负薄冰，懔懔而寒；时而泛酸上冲咽喉，呕吐黄绿酸苦涎水，心中嘈杂，知饥而不能食，唯喜烫饮，饮而不多；大便干结难解，小便短涩，手足不温，少气无力，入夜难寐；舌淡苔白滑腻，脉来沉迟。判为病久阳虚，真火内衰，阴寒内结，脾阳不运，无力以制水邪，肝郁不舒，夹寒水上逆犯胃凌心。阳虚为病之本，寒水泛溢为病之标，法当扶阳温散寒水之邪治之。先拟乌梅丸方1剂，疼痛稍减，呕吐酸苦水已少。认为此病根深蒂固，非大剂辛温连进不可。\\n但“多年临床体验，此证每于服药之后，或见脘腹增痛，或吐酸、便泻、小便色赤而浊等征象，可一时有所表露，此乃药与病相攻，驱邪之兆。若药能胜病，犹兵能胜敌，倘畏惧不专，虽欲善其事，而器不利也，何以克服？古云：‘若药不瞑眩，厥疾弗瘳 ”。吴氏将此理告于病者.遂以大剂吴萸四逆汤加味治之：\\n附片150g，吴萸18g，干姜60g，上肉桂18g（研末，泡水兑入），公丁5g，茯苓30g，白胡椒3g（研末，兑服），甘草15g。\\n“服药后果然1剂则痛反较增，2剂则腹中气动雷鸣，3剂则涌吐大作，吐出黄绿苦水盈盂。”原方附片增至200g，连进10剂，“愈服越见吐，痛不减反有所增之势”，脉转缓和稍有神，仍喜滚饮而畏寒。仍照前法，再进不怠，白附片用至300g，连服2剂，脘腹疼痛及痞硬顿失其半，胃逆作酸已减少。继续调理10数余剂而愈，体健如常。\\n按：此例吴氏进以大剂姜附，预先告以可能有所反应，令患者有心理准备。及至服药后果然“1剂则痛反较增，2剂则腹中气动雷鸣，3剂则涌吐大作”，进而“愈服越见吐，痛不减反有所增之势”，当此之际，一般医家恐难守持。吴氏“仍照前法，再进不怠”，而且附子加量，让人领略吴氏胆识与经验。":`Case of stomachache due to deficiency and cold\\nXu, male, in his forties. I have been suffering from heart and stomach pain syndrome for more than 20 years. The condition is getting worse day by day. I am losing weight, my chest and diaphragm are distended and painful, my flanks are full and tight, and my epigastrium and abdomen are burning. The pain is very deep and fixed in my chest and back. From the bottom of the heart to the umbilical and abdominal bulge, the board is as hard as a stone, and it hurts when I press it. My waist and back feel like I am carrying thin ice, and I feel numb. And cold; sometimes pantothenic acid rushes up the throat, vomiting yellow-green sour and bitter saliva, a noisy heart, knowing that one is hungry but unable to eat, and only likes to drink hot water, but not much; dry and hard stools, short and astringent urine, lukewarm hands and feet, lack of breath and weakness, difficulty sleeping at night; pale tongue with white and slippery coating, and slow and slow pulse. It is judged that the patient has been ill for a long time and has Yang deficiency, internal internal fire decline, Yin-cold internal knots, spleen-Yang failure, inability to control water evil, liver stagnation and discomfort, and cold water invading the stomach and the heart. Yang deficiency is the root of the disease, and overflowing cold water is the symptom. The method should be to strengthen the yang and warm up the cold water to treat it. I took 1 dose of Wumei Pills first, and the pain was slightly relieved, and the soreness and bitterness of vomiting was reduced. It is believed that this disease is deep-rooted and must be treated with large doses of pungent and warm medicine. \\nHowever, "many years of clinical experience have shown that after taking medicine, this syndrome may cause symptoms such as increased pain in the epigastrium and abdomen, acid vomiting, diarrhea, or red and turbid urine. This is a sign that the medicine and the disease are fighting each other to drive away evil spirits. If the medicine can defeat the disease, it is like a soldier who can defeat the enemy. If you are afraid of not being expert, how can you overcome it even if you want to do it well, but the equipment is not good? An ancient saying goes: 'If the medicine does not cure the dizziness, the disease will not heal." Wu explained this to the patient and treated it with a large dose of Wuyu Sini Decoction: 150g of Futian, 18g of Wuyu, 60g of dried ginger, 18g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed with water), 5g of male penis, 30g of Poria, 3g of white pepper (pulverized, mixed with water), 15g of licorice. \\n"After taking the medicine, the pain increased after taking the first dose. After the second dose, there was thunder and gas in the abdomen. After the third dose, the patient vomited violently and vomited yellow-green bitter water to fill the cup." The original prescription was increased to 200g, and 10 doses were taken. Still following the previous method, continue taking it without delay, and use 300g of Baifu Tablets for 2 doses. The pain in the epigastrium and abdominal pain and constipation have been reduced by half, and gastric acid reflux has been reduced. Continue to take 10 more doses and the condition will heal, and the body will be as healthy as usual. \\nNote: In this case, Wu administered a large dose of ginger to warn the patient of possible reactions in advance so that the patient could be mentally prepared. After taking the medicine, it turned out that "the pain increased after the first dose, the gas in the abdomen was thunderous after the second dose, and the vomiting was severe after the third dose", and then "the more I took the medicine, the more vomiting occurred, and the pain did not decrease but increased." At this time, ordinary doctors may find it difficult to maintain. Wu "still follows the previous method and will not slack off in making further progress", and increases the amount of aconite, allowing people to appreciate Wu's courage and experience.`,虚寒证:"Deficiency and cold syndrome",虚火牙痛:"Toothache due to deficiency of fire","虚火牙痛 孙某，男，三十八岁，某厂干部":"Toothache due to deficiency of fire Sun, male, 38 years old, cadre of a factory","虚火牙痛 孙某，男，三十八岁，某厂干部。始因受寒感冒，服银翘 散一剂，夜晚旋即牙痛发作，痛引头额，持续不休，终夜眼不 交睫,其势难忍。次日，牙龈亦肿痛,齿根浮动，龈满齿长,不 能咬合。冷、热水饮入口，浸及齿冠，其痛尤剧。近日水米不 进，时时呻吟。察其脉，虚数无力，舌尖色红，舌苔薄白而润， 根部稍黄。右下牙龈赤肿，未见嶠洞。此系表寒而误服清凉 之剂，寒邪不散，凝滞经络，里阳受伤，相火不潜，虚火上浮 所致。治宜宣散经络凝寒，引火归原，纳阳归肾。方用潜阳封髓丹加味。 附片45克，炙龟板9克，肉桂9克（研末，泡水兑入），砂 仁9克，细辛5克，黄柏9克，白芷9克，露蜂房6克，生姜12 克，甘草9克。 上方煎服一次，牙痛减轻，夜已能寐。继服二次则疼痛渐 止。二剂尽，牙龈肿胀及疼痛全然消散而愈。":"Toothache caused by weak fire. Sun, male, 38 years old, a cadre in a factory. I took a dose of Yinqiao Powder due to a cold at the beginning. Immediately at night, I suffered from toothache, which caused pain in my head and forehead. The next day, the gums were also swollen and painful, the tooth roots were floating, the gums were full and the teeth were long, making it impossible to bite. Cold or hot water drinks enter the mouth and soak into the crown of the tooth, causing severe pain. Recently, the water and rice have not come in, and I groan all the time. Observe the pulse, which is weak and weak, the tip of the tongue is red, the tongue coating is thin, white and moist, and the root is slightly yellow. The lower right gum was red and swollen with no cavities. This is caused by mistakenly taking cooling agents due to cold external symptoms. The cold evil persists and stagnates the meridians. The internal yang is injured, the phase fire does not submerge, and the deficiency fire rises. The treatment is suitable for dispersing cold in the meridians, bringing fire back to its origin, and absorbing yang and returning it to the kidneys. Use Qianyang Marrow Sealing Pill to flavor the recipe. 45 grams of Aconite, 9 grams of turtle bark, 9 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed), 9 grams of amomum villosum, 5 grams of asarum, 9 grams of Phellodendri, 9 grams of Angelica dahurica, 6 grams of honeycomb, 12 grams of ginger, and 9 grams of licorice. Decoct the above and take it once. The toothache is relieved and you can sleep at night. After taking it for a second time, the pain gradually stopped. After the second dose, the gum swelling and pain completely dissipated and healed.",蛔厥腹痛:"Ascariasis and abdominal pain","蛔厥腹痛 （胆道蛔虫证） 郑某，女，三十六岁，昆明官渡区某公社社员":"Ascariasis and abdominal pain (biliary ascaris syndrome) Zheng, female, 36 years old, member of a commune in Guandu District, Kunming","蛔厥腹痛 （胆道蛔虫证） 郑某，女，三十六岁，昆明官渡区某公社社员。1962年10 月某日夜间，患者突然院胁疼痛,宛如刀绞,彻于右侧肩背， 四肢冰冷，汗出如珠,兼发恶心呕吐，吐出黄绿苦水,并吐蛔 虫一条，胃中灼热嘈杂，脫腹痞胀,烦躁不宁，呻吟不止,终夜 不能入眠。天明,其痛稍有减轻，方才交睫,又复作痛如前，遂 由家人护送至中医学院附属医院急诊。经检査，诊断为“胆道 蛔虫症”，住院治疗。余会诊之时，见患者脉沉弦而紧，舌苔白 腻，舌质青黯，不渴饮。此乃厥阴脏寒，肝胆气机郁结,腹中蛔 虫上扰作痛,属蛔厥之证。照伸景法，以乌梅丸方主之。 附片30克，干姜15克，肉桂9克，当归15克，党参15 克，黄连6克，黄柏9克，川椒5克（炒去汗），细辛5克，乌梅 3枚。 煎一服，疼痛稍减，三服尽疼痛呕吐均止，手足已回温， 夜间已能安静入睡。惟胃中仍嘈杂，皖腹尚感痞闷。口苦，不 思饮食。脉沉弦，已不似昨日兼有紧象，腻苔稍退，舌质仍含 青色。蛔虫虽安,但肝胆寒凝之气尚未祛尽。照原方加川楝 子9克，榔片9克。连服二剂后，便下蛔虫二十余条，腹中感 到舒缓，饮食渐有恢复。脉缓,苔退。再以香砂理中汤加筚茇、高良姜调理二剂，气机恢复，痊愈出院。":`Ascariasis and abdominal pain (biliary ascaris syndrome) Zheng, female, 36 years old, member of a commune in Guandu District, Kunming. One night in October 1962, the patient suddenly suffered from flank pain, like a knife twisting, penetrating into the right shoulder and back. His limbs were cold, sweating like beads, nausea and vomiting, vomiting yellow-green bitter water, and a roundworm. At daybreak, the pain was slightly relieved, and just as he was crossing his eyelashes, the pain returned as before. He was escorted by his family to the emergency department of the Affiliated Hospital of the College of Traditional Chinese Medicine. After examination, he was diagnosed with "biliary ascariasis" and was hospitalized. During the consultation, I found that the patient's pulse was deep and stringy, the tongue coating was white and greasy, the tongue was blue and dark, and he was not thirsty to drink. This is due to coldness in the yin and internal organs, stagnation of the liver and gallbladder qi, and pain caused by the disturbance of roundworms in the abdomen, which is a syndrome of ascariasis. According to the Shenjing method, take the black plum pill prescription as the main method. 30 grams of Aconite slices, 15 grams of dried ginger, 9 grams of cinnamon, 15 grams of angelica root, 15 grams of Codonopsis pilosula, 6 grams of Coptis chinensis, 9 grams of Cortex cypress, 5 grams of Sichuan pepper (fried to remove sweat), 5 grams of asarum, and 3 ebony plums. After one dose of decoction, the pain was slightly relieved. After three doses, the pain and vomiting stopped. My hands and feet became warmer and I was able to fall asleep peacefully at night. But the stomach is still noisy and the abdomen still feels stuffy. Bitter mouth, no desire to eat or drink. The pulse is deep and stringy, no longer tight and tight like yesterday, the greasy coating has receded slightly, and the tongue is still blue. Although the roundworms are safe, the cold and condensed Qi in the liver and gallbladder has not been eliminated. Follow the original recipe and add 9 grams of toodanzi and 9 grams of walnut slices. After taking two doses, I had more than 20 roundworms in my stool, felt soothed in my stomach, and my diet gradually recovered. The pulse is slow and the coating is receding. Then, he took two doses of Xiangsha Lizhong Decoction plus squid and galangal. His Qi was restored and he was discharged from the hospital.`,"血栓性静脉炎案 杨某，男，32岁":"Thrombophlebitis case Yang, male, 32 years old","血栓性静脉炎案\\n杨某，男，32岁。双下肢小腿部血管胀痛，皮色发青，双足冰冷，终日不能回温；稍多行走则足软无力，胀痛难忍，步履维艰。昆明某医院诊断为“慢性血栓性静脉炎”，建议手术治疗，病者改服中药。吴氏视之，认为系阳气内虚，寒湿凝滞下焦，阳不足以温煦筋脉，遂致寒凝血瘀，血脉不通而作痛。察其脉沉迟而涩，舌质含青，杂有瘀斑瘀点。主以温肾助阳，行瘀通络之法，方用：\\n附片80g，干姜30g，桂枝50g，北细辛10g，伸筋草10g，，桃仁I0g（捣），红花8g，甘草8g。\\n初服则胀痛更甚，再服觉痛麻兼作，患者疑之，遂来复诊。告之此乃阳药温化运行，行瘀通脉之效果，再服无妨。照原方去桃仁加羌活9g，吴白芷9g，连服2剂则疼痛渐除，双足回温。在原方基础上加减散寒除湿活络之剂调治之，数剂而愈。\\n按：此例“初服则胀痛更甚，再服觉痛麻兼作，患者疑之”，吴氏胸有定见，“告之此乃阳药温化运行，行瘀通脉之效果，再服无妨”。若无经验者，恐怕只能改弦易辙矣。\\n吴氏温阳案中甚少夹用活血之药，唯此案加入#兆仁、红花，大概因舌“杂有瘀斑瘀点”，主血瘀之故。":`Thrombophlebitis case\\nYang, male, 32 years old. The blood vessels in the lower legs of both lower limbs are swollen and painful, the skin turns blue, and the feet are cold and cannot warm up all day long. When walking a little longer, the feet become weak, the swelling and pain are unbearable, and it is difficult to walk. A hospital in Kunming diagnosed the patient with "chronic thrombophlebitis" and recommended surgical treatment and the patient switched to traditional Chinese medicine. According to Wu's view, it is caused by internal deficiency of yang energy, cold-dampness condensation and stagnation in the lower burner, and insufficient yang to warm the muscles and veins, resulting in cold coagulation and blood stasis, blockage of blood vessels, and pain. His pulse was slow and astringent, his tongue was blue, mixed with ecchymosis and petechiae. The main method is to warm the kidneys and help yang, remove blood stasis and unblock meridians. Recipe: 80g of Futian, 30g of dried ginger, 50g of cinnamon twig, 10g of Asarum, 10g of Shenjincao, 10g of peach kernel (pounded), 8g of safflower, 8g of licorice. \\nAfter taking it for the first time, the swelling and pain became even worse. After taking it again, he felt pain and numbness. The patient was suspicious and came for a follow-up consultation. It is told that this is the effect of warming and transforming Yang medicine, relieving blood stasis and unblocking the meridians, so there is no harm in taking it again. According to the original prescription, remove the peach kernel and add 9g of Qianhuo and 9g of Radix Angelicae. After taking 2 doses, the pain will gradually disappear and the feet will become warmer. On the basis of the original prescription, add or subtract the agent to dispel cold, dehumidify and activate collaterals to treat it, and it will be cured after a few doses. \\nNote: In this case, "the swelling and pain became worse after taking it for the first time, and the pain and numbness increased after taking it again, and the patient was suspicious." Wu's chest had a definite opinion, "I told you that this is the warming effect of the yang medicine, and the effect of removing blood stasis and unblocking the meridians. There is no harm in taking it again." If you don't have experience, you may have to change your mind. \\nIn Wu's Wenyang case, few blood-activating drugs were used. Only in this case, #赵仁 and safflower were added. This may be because the tongue is "mixed with ecchymosis and petechiae," which is responsible for blood stasis.`,"衄 血":"Epistaxis blood","衄 血（二） 秦某，男，六旬有四，广西人，住上海新闸路":"Nasty bleeding (2) Qin, male, 60 years old, Guangxi, living on Xinzha Road, Shanghai","衄 血（二） 秦某，男，六旬有四，广西人，住上海新闸路。秦素多痰 湿，患痰饮咳嗽多年。昨日因咳嗽气急上气，忽而鼻衄不止， 用物堵塞鼻孔则血由口中吐出。经注射止血针药，血未能止 住。曾昏厥一次,喂服白兰地酒少许始回苏。1933年7月11 日延余诊视，患者面色惨淡,鼻鈕不止，口角亦见血迹，冷汗 淋漓，沉迷无神，气息低弱而呈奄奄一息之状。脉来乳虚欲 散，重按无根，二、三至则一止，已现代象。掰开口视其舌，质 淡夹青而少血色。此证良由气虚不摄血，阳虚不守阴，以致阴 血散漫不归于经。复因咳嗽气动，挣破血络而成衄。察其脉 证,病势颇危,有阳气欲随阴血外脱之势，急宜扶阳收纳，如 得血汗均止，始有生机。以参附汤加味急救。 高丽参10克，附片30克，炮黑姜6克，甘草3克，大枣2 枚（烧黑存性）。 服一剂则效,衄血减，神气转佳。再剂则血汗均已得止。 次日又照服一剂，13日复诊，神识已清醒，不再衄血。唇舌已 转红,脉缓弱较有神，但五、六至，间仍有止歇,依原方增量加 北口芪扶阳固气。 高丽参10克，附片60克，炮黑姜15克，北口芪24克， 甘草10克，大枣2枚（烧黑存性）。 连服二付，饮食、精神均有恢复，面唇舌色已红润，脉缓 和有神，惟尚有咳嗽，痰中夹少许黑血,此乃离经之瘀血随痰 咯出之故。原方去参、苗加入法半夏10克、茯苓15克、砂仁3 克，三剂而痊。此后多年,未见再衄。":"Nasty bleeding (2) Qin, male, 60 years old, from Guangxi, living on Xinzha Road, Shanghai. Qin Su has a lot of phlegm and dampness, and has suffered from phlegm-damp cough for many years. Yesterday I was short of breath due to coughing, and suddenly suffered from epistaxis. If I blocked my nostrils with something, blood would come out of my mouth. After injection of hemostatic medicine, the bleeding could not be stopped. I fainted once and had to drink a little brandy before returning to Suzhou. On July 11, 1933, Yan Yu underwent a medical examination. The patient's face was pale, his nose was knotted, blood was seen at the corners of his mouth, he was dripping with cold sweat, he was unconscious, his breath was weak and he was dying. The pulse comes when the pulse is weak and wants to dissipate. When pressed hard, the pulse has no root. The second or third pulse will stop at the second or third pulse. This is a modern phenomenon. Open the mouth and look at the tongue. It is light green and less bloody. This syndrome is caused by deficiency of qi and failure to absorb blood, and deficiency of yang and failure to maintain yin, resulting in yin and blood being scattered and not returning to the meridians. Due to coughing and turbulence, the blood vessels are broken and bleeding occurs. Observe the pulse pattern and you will see that the condition is quite critical and there is a tendency for yang energy to escape with the yin blood. If it is urgent, it is advisable to support the yang and absorb it. Only when the blood and sweat have stopped can there be vitality. Use Shenfu Decoction for first aid. 10 grams of Korean ginseng, 30 grams of Aconite slices, 6 grams of black ginger, 3 grams of licorice, and 2 jujubes (burned black). Take one dose and it will be effective, the epistaxis and blood loss will be reduced, and your mood will improve. Another dose will stop bleeding and sweating. He took another dose the next day and had a follow-up visit on the 13th. His consciousness was clear and he no longer had bleeding. The lips and tongue have turned red, and the pulse is slow and weak, but it still stops at the fifth or sixth lunar hour. According to the original prescription, add Beikou Qi to strengthen Yang and strengthen Qi. 10 grams of Korean ginseng, 60 grams of Aconite slices, 15 grams of black ginger, 24 grams of Beikou stilbene, 10 grams of licorice, and 2 jujubes (burned black). After taking two pills, my diet and energy have recovered, my face, lips and tongue have become rosy, my pulse is slow and energetic, but I still have a cough, and there is a little black blood in the phlegm. This is due to the blood stasis from menstruation being coughed up along with the phlegm. In the original recipe, remove the ginseng and seedlings, add 10 grams of Pinellia ternata, 15 grams of Poria cocos, and 3 grams of Amomum villosum, and the disease will be cured after three doses. After many years, I did not suffer from bleeding again.",衄血:"Epistaxis","衄血（一） 李某，十四岁，素患鼻衄，无他痛苦,故未用药石调理之":"Epistaxis (1) Li, fourteen years old, has always suffered from epistaxis, and he is not as painful as others, so he does not use medicinal stones to treat it.","衄血（一） 李某，十四岁，素患鼻衄，无他痛苦,故未用药石调理之。 某日，感客邪,身热恶寒,头疼体痛,喜冷饮,脉浮而细数,主以 麻杏石甘汤一剂霍然。异日外出，适值阴雨天寒,又复感冒而 病,发热恶寒，头昏疼,肢体酸痛,不渴饮,脉反沉细而弱，主以 麻黄细辛附子汤加桂枝尖、生姜_剂。服后汗出热退。次晨忽 又鼻不止,用物塞鼻孔则血由口中溢出，似有不可止之状。 头晕，腹痛，面色淡而无华，形弱神疲,复诊其脉迟缓而弱。此 乃气血素亏，阴阳不相为守也。血虚散漫妄行，气虚则无力统 摄血液，易致离经外溢。表邪虽解，气血尚虚，主以四逆当归补 血汤。 附片50克，炮黑姜15克，砂仁6克，大枣3枚（烧黑存 性）,北口芪15克，当归10克。 一剂衄血立止，再剂霍然。是夜因大便用力，起身时忽而 气喘咬牙，昏厥欲绝，唇青，面色灰白，脉细迟无力，扶之使 卧,稍定,乃以四逆汤加上肉桂治之,连进四剂而痊。":"Epistaxis (1) Mr. Li, fourteen years old, had always suffered from epistaxis. He was not suffering from other symptoms, so he did not treat it with medicinal stones. One day, I felt guest evil, body heat, aversion to cold, headache and body aches, preference for cold drinks, floating and thready pulse, I took a dose of Maxing Shigan Decoction. Go out on the next day, it is rainy and cold, and you have a cold again and become ill, with fever and aversion to cold, dizziness and pain, sore limbs, no thirst for water, and a heavy and thin pulse. Mainly take Ephedra Asarum Fuzi Decoction plus Guizhijian and Ginger. Sweating and fever subsided after taking it. The next morning, my nose stopped suddenly again. If I stuffed my nostrils with something, the blood would overflow from my mouth, which seemed to be unstoppable. Dizziness, abdominal pain, pale complexion, weak body and mental fatigue. On reexamination, the pulse was slow and weak. This is due to the deficiency of qi and blood elements, and the yin and yang do not maintain each other. Blood deficiency leads to loose and erratic movement, while Qi deficiency makes it impossible to control the blood, which can easily cause menstrual leakage and overflow. Although the external evils have been resolved, Qi and blood are still deficient, so the main treatment is Sini Danggui Buxue Decoction. 50 grams of Fu Fian, 15 grams of black ginger, 6 grams of amomum villosum, 3 jujubes (burned black to preserve the properties), 15 grams of Beikou Qi, and 10 grams of angelica. One dose will immediately stop the bleeding, another dose will cause the pain to fade. That night, due to straining to defecate, he suddenly wheezed and gritted his teeth when he stood up, fainted, had blue lips, pale complexion, and a thready and weak pulse. He helped him lie down and calmed down for a while, so he was treated with Sini Decoction plus cinnamon, and he was cured after taking four doses.",表寒里热证:"Cold on the outside and heat on the inside",论著:"treatises",证候研究:"syndrome research",诊余漫话:"Talk after diagnosis",语言切换:"language switch",误治变证转阳极似阴证:"Syndrome changes due to mistreatment and the yang pole resembles yin syndrome","读书临证随笔与门人问答录。":"A collection of clinical essays on reading and questions and answers from disciples.",调护禁忌:"Contraindications for care","调经、种子、产后诸疾之经方化裁。":"It can be used to regulate menstruation, seeds, and various postpartum diseases.","调经种子、胎产诸疾验案丰富":"There are abundant test cases on menstruation-regulating seeds and fetal birth diseases.",调经篇:"Tiao Jing Chapter","谓少阴病提纲脉微细、但欲寐六字乃辨阴证之眼目，一见此证即当急温，切不可观望迟疑、养痈遗患，温之得法则生机自复。":"It is said that Shao Yin disease has a weak pulse but a desire to sleep. These six words are the key to distinguishing Yin syndrome. As soon as you see this syndrome, you should warm it urgently. You must not wait and hesitate, or treat the residual disease of carbuncle. If you warm it, you will be able to recover your vitality.",资讯动态:"News","资讯动态 | 云南名医馆":"News | Yunnan Famous Medical Center","赤 痢 彭某，男，年三十五岁，四川人，住云南省昆明市珠市桥":"Red dysentery Peng, male, 35 years old, from Sichuan, living in Zhushiqiao, Kunming City, Yunnan Province","赤 痢 彭某，男，年三十五岁，四川人，住云南省昆明市珠市桥。 禀赋素强，偶停宿食，兼有湿热，于1929年9月15日夜起入 厕，感受风寒而起病。初起即发热吐泻，头疼体痛，自汗而畏 寒,继则下痢赤白，小腹痛甚，里急后重，每便仅一、二匙，日 夜无度,小便短赤，噤口不食，脉来浮弦而兼紧象，舌苔白腻， 舌尖绛。按病原系湿热挟食积阻遏肠胃，复感风寒外邪，闭束 太阳经气运行之机，表寒外束，又有湿热内逼，以致身热下 痢，此即所谓“协热痢”。法当表里双治，以桂葛汤解肌表之 邪，佐小承气汤加黄连下宿食而清湿热。 葛根12克，桂枝尖10克，杭白芍20克，大黄10克（泡水 兑入），油朴12克，枳实10克（捣），黄连5克，生姜10克，小枣 7枚，甘草3克。 次日复诊。服上方一剂始尽，即见汗出，汗后热退脉平， 表邪已解，痢亦减轻,惟湿热食积尚阻遏胃肠，湿热内逼，痢 未全止,每痢仍腹痛后重，遂以“通因通用”之法，拟大承气汤 合槟芍顺气汤加减急下宿食兼清湿热。 生杭白芍24克，生大黄12克（泡水兑入），枳实10克 （炒、捣），厚朴10克（炒），槟榔12克，麦冬12克，广木香5 克，芒硝5克，黄连4克。 三诊,上方服后,得快利稀粪二、三便,腹痛后重及赤白痢 均减去十之七、八，腻苔已退，稍进稀粥。惟小便仍短赤，思食 冷物水果。此病状虽减而湿热痢毒未净，仍照原方加减主之。 生杭白芍20克，生大黄6克（泡水兑入），黄连5克，油 朴10克，麦冬12克，玄明粉5克，广木香4克。 服后又下出溏薄粪便二次，痢遂止，肛门稍坠，食量较 增，小便尚赤。余热尚未全清，继拟下方治疗。 沙参13克，麦冬13克，木通10克，生杭白芍13克，酒 炙大黄5克，厚朴10克。 服上方后饮食复常,神形健如,痢止溺清、腹痛若失而瘥。按:余遇下痢之证,身热头体痛有表证者,当即以桂葛汤先解表邪。若无表邪,则当头以凉下为急,如此疗法,无不效如桴鼓。苟不解除表邪,则身热不退,易转危笃。故《内经》云:“利证身热不休者死。”不行攻下,邪热痢毒亦不能除。若属久痢虚寒者,又当以温固之法治之。":`Red dysentery Peng, male, 35 years old, from Sichuan, lives in Zhushiqiao, Kunming City, Yunnan Province. He had a strong natural endowment and occasionally stopped eating and had dampness and heat. On the night of September 15, 1929, he went to the toilet and felt wind and cold and became ill. It starts with fever, vomiting and diarrhea, headache and body pain, spontaneous sweating and fear of cold, followed by red and white diarrhea, severe lower abdominal pain, tenesmus, only one or two spoonfuls in each bowel movement, day and night, short red urine, mouth shut and not eating, floating and tight pulse, white and greasy tongue coating, and red tongue tip. According to the pathogenic factor, damp-heat suppresses food accumulation and blocks the intestines and stomach, causing wind-cold external pathogens to block the circulation of the sun meridian. Cold on the outside is bundled outward, and damp-heat is forced on the inside, resulting in diarrhea caused by heat in the body. This is the so-called "heat-assisted dysentery". The method is to treat both the exterior and the interior, use Guige Decoction to relieve the evils on the surface of the muscle, and use Xiaochengqi Decoction and Coptis chinensis to remove dampness and heat. 12 grams of kudzu root, 10 grams of Guizhijian, 20 grams of white peony root, 10 grams of rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed with water), 12 grams of Youpu, 10 grams of Citrus aurantium (pounded), 5 grams of coptis, 10 grams of ginger, 7 jujubes, and 3 grams of licorice. Follow-up visit the next day. After taking just one dose of the above medicine, you will see sweating, post-sweating heat and pulse are flat, the external evils have been resolved, and the dysentery has also been alleviated. However, the accumulation of damp and hot food still blocks the gastrointestinal tract, causing the damp and hot internal pressure, and the dysentery has not completely stopped. The abdominal pain still worsens every time the dysentery occurs. Therefore, based on the method of "all causes and general use", Dachengqi Decoction and Binshao Shunqi Decoction are proposed to reduce acute diarrhea and relieve dampness and heat. 24 grams of raw Hangzhou white peony root, 12 grams of raw rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed with water), 10 grams of Citrus aurantium (stir-fried and pounded), 10 grams of Magnolia officinalis (stir-fried), 12 grams of betel nut, 12 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 5 grams of agarwood, 5 grams of Glauber's salt, and 4 grams of coptis. After the third examination, after taking the above medicine, the second and third stools were quickly relieved and loose stools. The abdominal pain, redness and white diarrhea were all reduced by 70 to 80%. The greasy coating has receded and the gruel has been slightly reduced. But the urine is still short and red, and I want to eat cold fruits. Although the symptoms of this disease are reduced but the damp-heat dysentery poison has not been eliminated, the original prescription can still be treated with addition and subtraction. 20 grams of raw Hangzhou white peony root, 6 grams of raw rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed with water), 5 grams of Coptis chinensis, 10 grams of Youpu, 12 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 5 grams of Xuanming powder, and 4 grams of Patchouli. After taking it, I had loose and thin stools for two times, and the dysentery stopped. My anus dropped slightly, my food intake increased, and my urine was still red. The remaining heat has not completely cleared up yet, so we plan to continue the treatment below. 13 grams of adenophora, 13 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 10 grams of Akebia, 13 grams of raw white peony root, 5 grams of rhubarb roasted in wine, and 10 grams of Magnolia officinalis. After taking the above medicine, the diet will return to normal, the body and mind will be as healthy as possible, the diarrhea will stop, and the abdominal pain will disappear. Note: If you encounter symptoms of diarrhea, body heat, head pain, or external symptoms, you should immediately use Guige Decoction to relieve the external evils. If there is no external evil, then the first priority is to cool down. Such treatment will be as effective as a drum. If the external evil is not eliminated, the body heat will not subside and it will easily turn into a serious condition. Therefore, the "Nei Jing" says: "Those who suffer from persistent body heat will die." If it cannot be attacked, the evil heat and dysentery poison cannot be eliminated. If it is a case of chronic dysentery, deficiency and cold, it should be treated with the method of warming and strengthening.`,赤痢:"red dysentery","车某，女，18岁，住会理县南街":"Che, female, 18 years old, lives in South Street, Huili County","车某，女，18岁，住会理县南街。1920年3月，感瘟疫病邪，发病已二日，始则见发热而渴，恶热而不寒，头疼体痛，脉浮弦而数，唇赤面垢，舌白如积粉。病虽初起，但邪不在经，若发汗则既伤表气又易耗损津液.势必热邪愈炽。此乃瘟疫蟠踞膜原，有入里化燥伤津之势，宜输转使之达表而解。以达原饮加石膏主之：槟榔10g，厚朴10g，草果10g，知母12g，杭芍12g，黄芩10g，甘草6g，生石膏15g（碎，布包）。\\n服1剂后，证情稍减，惟大便已3日燥结不通，于是续前方加大黄12g。患者之父略知医理，认为该女素体虚弱，恐不能耐受寒下之剂，竟私自将大黄、石膏减去未用。隔日再诊，见舌苔转黄而燥，胃实胸满，拒按呼痛，烦渴饮冷，小便短赤，大便仍燥结，时发谵语。此系邪已入腑，燥热结滞，非清热泻下不能力挽危绝。即拟白虎加承气汤合方1剂其父仍有难色，不敢与服。随后，患者忽鼻衄不止，色鲜红而量较多，稍顷衄血即凝而成块。病家另延中医彭某诊视，断为阳虚亡血之证，且谓如系热证，鼻衄流出之后，必不致凝结成块，主以四逆汤。病家疑虑，仍不敢与服。余据理解释：此乃邪热亢极灼阴之证，急宜大剂凉下以救真阴，缓则真阴灼尽，危殆难治。又告之，余素谙于用姜附者，尚不敢以温热之剂妄投。当此证情苦寒泻下犹恐不及，倘若误服温热之剂，犹如火上浇油，危亡立至。因余力主，病家始而信服，遂拟方清热凉下治之：\\n生石膏60g，（碎，布包）生大黄30g（泡水兑入），枳实20g（捣），厚朴20g，芒硝13g，知母20g，生地16g，甘草6g。\\n上方日夜连进之后，鼻衄方止，神识转清，身热退去六七。次日照原方再服1剂，则二便通畅，脉静身凉。惟仍渴思冷饮，此系余热未净、津液未复所致。以生脉散加味连服3剂：\\n沙参30g，麦冬13g，五味子6g，当归16g，生地16g.杭芍16g，石膏16g，大黄6g。\\n渴饮止，津液满口。其后减去石膏、大黄，连服3剂而痊。\\n按：此案本是瘟疫燥热内结之证，吴用达原饮加石膏自是正治。因患者之父“认为该女素体虚弱，恐不能耐受寒下之剂，竟私自将大黄、石膏减去未用”，致使燥热未解反而加重。吴氏据证乃以白虎加承气汤合方再进。病家“仍不敢与服”，此时“余据理解释：此乃邪热亢极灼阴之证，急宜大剂凉下以救真阴，缓则真阴灼尽，危殆难治。又告之，余素谙于用姜附者，尚不敢以温热之剂妄投”。即便彭医“断为阳虚亡血之证……主以四逆汤”时，仍旧“因余力主，病家始而信服”。\\n整个案情显示，即以吴氏“素谙于用姜附者，尚不敢以温热之剂妄投”，表明他坚持辨证论治的立场，“当凉则凉，当热则热”，绝不“固守一法”。":`Che, female, 18 years old, lives in South Street, Huili County. In March 1920, I contracted the plague pathogen. It had been two days since the onset of the disease. I started to experience fever and thirst, aversion to heat but not cold, headache and body pain, floating and rapid pulse, red lips and dirty face, and white tongue like accumulated powder. Although the disease starts at the beginning, the evil is not in the meridians. If sweating occurs, it will damage the superficial Qi and easily consume body fluids. The heat evil will inevitably become more intense. This is because the plague is lingering on the membrane, and has the potential to enter the interior and transform into dryness, damaging the body fluids. It should be transferred to the outside to relieve the symptoms. Mainly add gypsum to Da Yuan drink: 10g betel nut, 10g Magnolia officinalis, 10g Cao Guo, 12g Anemarrhenae, 12g Hangzhou peony root, 10g Scutellaria baicalensis, 6g licorice, 15g gypsum (broken, wrapped in cloth). \\nAfter taking 1 dose, the symptoms were slightly reduced, but the stool had been dry and blocked for 3 days, so I continued to add 12g of rhubarb. The patient's father, who knew a little about medical science, thought that the woman was weak and might not be able to tolerate the cold medicine, so he secretly subtracted the rhubarb and plaster without using it. The patient was diagnosed again the next day and found that the tongue coating had turned yellow and dry, the stomach was full and the chest was full, the patient refused to press and breathed painfully, he was thirsty and drank cold drinks, the urine was short and red, the stools were still dry and congested, and he sometimes suffered from delirium. This type of evil has entered the fu organs, resulting in stagnation of dryness and heat. Unless it is cleared of heat and purged, it is impossible to cure the disease. Even after taking one dose of Baihu plus Chengqi Decoction, his father was still embarrassed and did not dare to take it. Subsequently, the patient suddenly suffered from epistaxis, which was bright red in color and large in amount, and the blood from the epistaxis immediately coagulated into clumps. The patient further consulted Chinese medicine doctor Peng and determined that it was a syndrome of yang deficiency and blood loss. He also said that if it was a heat syndrome, the epistaxis would not coagulate into lumps after it flowed out, so he prescribed Sini Decoction. The patient was doubtful and still did not dare to take the medicine. Yu rationally explained: This is a sign of excessive heat and excessive burning of the Yin. If it is urgent, it should be cooled down with a large amount to save the true Yin. If it is slow, the true Yin will be burned out, making it difficult to treat the critical condition. He also told me that those who are familiar with the use of ginger do not dare to use warming agents. When this condition is characterized by bitterness, coldness, and diarrhea, it is feared that it will not be enough. If you mistakenly take a warming agent, it will be like adding fuel to the fire, and you will be in danger. Because of the remaining strength, the patient was convinced, so he formulated a prescription to clear away heat and cool down the treatment: 60g of raw gypsum, 30g of raw rhubarb (crushed, wrapped in cloth) (soaked in water and mixed in), 20g of Citrus aurantium (pounded), 20g of Magnolia officinalis, 13g of Glauber's salt, 20g of Anemarrhena, 16g of Rehmannia glutinosa, and 6g of licorice. \\nAfter the day and night treatment above, the epistaxis stopped, the consciousness became clear, and the body heat subsided. Take another dose of the original prescription the next day, then the bowel movements will be smooth, the pulse will be quiet and the body will be cool. However, you are still thirsty for cold drinks, which is caused by the residual heat and body fluids that have not been restored. Take 3 doses of Shengmai Powder with flavored ingredients:\\nAdenophora 30g, Ophiopogon japonicus 13g, Schisandra chinensis 6g, Angelica sinensis 16g, Rehmannia glutinosa 16g. Hangshao 16g, Gypsum 16g, Rhubarb 6g. \\nDrinking will stop your thirst and your mouth will be full of body fluids. After that, the plaster and rhubarb were removed, and the patient recovered after taking 3 doses. \\nNote: This case was originally a sign of internal knots caused by the plague's heat and heat. Wu Yongda Yuan drink plus gypsum is the correct treatment. Because the patient's father "thought that the woman was weak and might not be able to tolerate the cold medicine, he secretly subtracted the rhubarb and gypsum without using them." As a result, the dryness and heat worsened without being relieved. According to Wu's evidence, he used White Tiger plus Chengqi Decoction to combine the prescription. The patient "still didn't dare to take it". At this time, "Yu rationally explained: This is a sign of excessive heat and excessive burning of the Yin. If it is urgent, it should be cooled down with a large dose to save the true Yin. If it is slow, the true Yin will burn out, making it critical and difficult to treat. I also told those who are familiar with the use of ginger and do not dare to use warm medicine." Even when Dr. Peng "diagnosed it as a syndrome of Yang deficiency and blood loss... and prescribed Sini Decoction", "because of his remaining strength, the patient was convinced". \\nThe entire case shows that Mr. Wu "is well versed in the use of ginger, but he still dares not to use warming agents", which shows that he adheres to the stance of syndrome differentiation and treatment, "when it is cold, it will be cool, and when it is hot, it will be hot" and will never "stick to one method".`,"辨病与辨证结合，宏观辨证与微观指标互参。":"Disease differentiation and syndrome differentiation are combined, and macroscopic syndrome differentiation and microscopic indicators are mutually referenced.","辨证当有层级：先辨病位、病性，再辨病势、病机转归。":"Syndrome differentiation should be hierarchical: first identify the location and nature of the disease, and then identify the condition, pathogenesis and outcome.",辨证首重脾胃的学术主张贯穿全书:"The academic proposition that the spleen and stomach are the first priority in syndrome differentiation runs through the entire book.","辨证首重脾胃，谓“脾胃一伤，百药难施”。":'The first priority in syndrome differentiation is the spleen and stomach. It is said that "if the spleen and stomach are injured, hundreds of medicines will be difficult to cure".',近代:"Modern times",返回首页:"Return to home page","这里仅录其中一例：江灿北之第九子，年13岁，住三市街二允巷一号":"Only one example is recorded here: Jiang Canbei’s ninth son, 13 years old, lives at No. 1 Eryun Lane, Sanshi Street","这里仅录其中一例：江灿北之第九子，年13岁，住三市街二允巷一号。廿七年八月患病甚危，右少腹凝结一块，其痛甚剧；形容消瘦，唇舌焦燥，痛甚烦乱，须臾复止，止而复烦。均经四位大名西医诊视，均决断为肓肠炎之危证，力主开刀但不能保险，且云肠内已有脓，肠将溃烂。即延余诊视。即以“中医的旧理论，判断病源，为厥阴证，肝气凝结，蛔虫内扰.以仲景之乌梅丸方，一剂立效，略加减四剂而痊.且免刀术之险”。":`Only one example is recorded here: Jiang Canbei’s ninth son, 13 years old, lived at No. 1, Eryun Lane, Sanshi Street. In August of the 27th year, I became critically ill. A lump formed in my right lower abdomen, and the pain was severe. I was emaciated, my lips and tongue were dry, and the pain was very disturbing. It stopped after a while, but then became annoying again. After being examined by four well-known Western doctors, they all determined that the patient was suffering from enteritis, and they urged surgery, but it was not safe. Moreover, there was pus in the intestines and the intestines would ulcerate. That is, delayed examination. That is to say, "the old theory of traditional Chinese medicine is used to determine the cause of the disease, which is Jueyin syndrome, condensation of liver qi, and internal disturbance of roundworms. Zhongjing's Wumei Pill prescription is effective after one dose, and can be cured by slightly adding or subtracting four doses. It also avoids the risk of surgery."`,"进针、得气、补泻手法操作规范。":"The procedures for acupuncture, deqi, and reinforcing and purging are standardized.","进针讲究快而无痛，得气强调气至而有效，补泻依迎随、呼吸、提插、捻转配合运用，条理清晰。":"The acupuncture should be fast and painless, Deqi should be effective by emphasizing the arrival of Qi. Tonifying and reducing should be done in conjunction with Yingsui, breathing, lifting and inserting, and twisting in a clear manner.",退出全屏:"Exit full screen",逆证救逆:"Adverse evidence and salvation","邓某，男，成年":"Deng, male, adult","邓某，男，成年。初以受寒发病，误服辛凉，病经十几天，头痛如斧劈，势不可忍。午后恶寒身痛，脉沉弱无力，舌苔白滑而不渴饮。辨为寒客少阴，阻碍清阳不升，复因辛凉耗其真阳，正虚阳弱，阴寒遏滞经脉。头为诸阳之会，今为阴邪上攻，阳不足以运行，邪正相争，遂致是症。治以辅正除邪之法，麻黄附子细辛汤加味主之：附片100g，干姜36g，麻黄10g，细辛5g，羌活10g。\\n1剂痛减其半，再剂霍然而愈。\\n按：此案“头痛如斧劈”，据其“午后恶寒身痛，脉沉弱无力，舌苔白滑而不渴饮”，辨为寒客少阴，治以麻黄附子细辛汤加羌活、干姜，用药简练，彰显经典火神派风范。":`Deng, male, adult. The disease first started due to cold, and she mistakenly took pungent cold drinks. The disease lasted for more than ten days, and the headache was like an axe. It was unbearable. In the afternoon, he feels aversion to cold and body aches, his pulse is weak and weak, his tongue coating is white and slippery, and he is not thirsty to drink. It is identified as cold guest Shaoyin, which blocks the clear Yang and does not rise, and its true Yang is depleted due to pungent coolness. Zheng deficiency and Yang are weak, and the cold Yin stagnates the meridians. The head is the meeting place of all the yangs. Now the yin evil is attacking upward. The yang is not enough to move, and the evil and righteousness are competing with each other, which leads to this disease. The main method of treatment is to supplement the body's health and eliminate evil. Ephedra, Aconite and Asarum Decoction is flavored with: 100g of Fuzi, 36g of dried ginger, 10g of ephedra, 5g of Asarum, and 10g of Qianghuo. \\nOne dose reduces the pain by half, and another dose makes the pain heal. \\nNote: This case had a "headache like an axe". According to the patient's "aversion to cold in the afternoon and body aches, a heavy and weak pulse, white and slippery tongue coating but no thirst for drinks", it was diagnosed as cold guest Shaoyin. The treatment was with Ephedra, Fuzi and Asarum Decoction plus Qiang Huo and dried ginger. The medication was simple and demonstrated the classic Vulcan style.`,部:"Department",部著作:"Works",酷暑伤阴:"Heat hurts yin","采撷云南历代名家医案，汇聚滇南传世典籍，":"It collects the medical records of famous Yunnan experts from past dynasties and collects the classics handed down from southern Yunnan.","采撷云岭杏林六百年医脉，汇集名家医案、传世著作与学术经验，以数字化之力延续中医薪火，让经典惠及当代临床。":"Picking up the 600-year-old medical history of Yunling Xinglin, it brings together famous medical records, handed down works and academic experience to continue the flame of traditional Chinese medicine with the power of digitalization, so that classics can benefit contemporary clinical practice.",重感冒:"severe cold",重症救逆案:"Severe rescue case",重置:"reset",重置封面:"reset cover","重视体质因素，“同病异治、异病同治”皆以体质为枢机。":'Attaching importance to physical factors, "treating the same disease with different treatments, and treating different diseases with the same treatment" all take physical constitution as the basis.',"重视阳气，力主“阳主阴从”，认为阳气之存亡关乎生死之机。":'It attaches great importance to Yang Qi and advocates "Yang dominates and Yin follows", believing that the survival of Yang Qi is a matter of life and death.',"金银花30g，连翘25g，淡竹叶15g，荆芥穗12g，牛蒡子15g，薄荷10g（后下），芦根30g，生石膏45g":"30g honeysuckle, 25g forsythia, 15g pale bamboo leaves, 12g nepeta paniculata, 15g burdock, 10g mint (bottom), 30g reed root, 45g gypsum",针灸:"Acupuncture","针灸 · 推拿":"Acupuncture · Massage","针灸之要，首在辨经，“宁失其穴，勿失其经”。":'The key to acupuncture is to differentiate the meridians, "it is better to lose the points than to lose the meridians."',"针灸取穴当合天时，“因天时而调血气”。":'Acupuncture points should be selected when they are in harmony with the sky, which "regulates the blood and qi according to the weather."',"针灸名家 · 时间针灸":"Acupuncture Master · Time Acupuncture","针灸名家 · 管氏针灸传人":"Famous Acupuncture Master · Guan’s Successor of Acupuncture",针灸科:"Acupuncture Department","问答数则尤见心法，如辨证难在取舍、用药难在分量诸语，非久历临证者不能道，学者所宜深味。":"The number of questions and answers especially shows the mental method. For example, it is difficult to distinguish syndromes by choosing and choosing, and it is difficult to use medicine by weighing various words. Those who have not experienced the syndrome for a long time cannot understand it, and scholars should understand it deeply.",闻:"smell","阑尾炎案 江某之第九子，年13岁，住昆明市":"Appendicitis case Jiang’s ninth son, 13 years old, living in Kunming","阑尾炎案\\n江某之第九子，年13岁，住昆明市。1938年年8月患病甚危，右少腹凝结一块，其痛甚剧；形容消瘦，唇舌焦燥，痛甚烦乱，须臾复止，止而复烦。曾请四位大名西医诊视，均决为肓肠炎之危证，力主开刀，但不能保险，且云肠内已有脓，肠将溃烂。延余诊视，即以中医的旧理论，判断病源，为厥阴证，肝气凝结，蛔虫内扰，以仲景之乌梅丸方，1剂立效；略加减4剂而痊，且免刀术之险。（《驳冯友兰论中西医药》）\\n按：归纳吴氏应用乌梅丸，主要指征有三个：腕腹灼痛，呕吐酸苦，胸腹痞块胀痛如治张某之妻，呕吐，腹内有癥坚痞块，痛不可当。拟四逆苓桂丁椒汤治之，1剂则痛减其半，唯呕吐未止，此乃肝肾阴寒之邪未净，拟乌梅丸方治之：附片130g，干姜60g，当归26g，上肉桂13g（研末，泡水兑入），黄连13g，黄柏13g，北细辛6g，潞党参16g，川椒6g（炒去汗），乌梅3枚。服1剂后，呕吐止；2剂后，腹痛全瘳，腹内痞块渐散。继以大回阳饮，兼吞服乌梅丸10余剂，始奏全功。\\n":`Appendicitis case\\nJiang’s ninth son, 13 years old, lives in Kunming. In August 1938, he became seriously ill. A lump formed in his right lower abdomen, and the pain was severe. He was emaciated, his lips and tongue were dry and dry, and the pain was very disturbing. It stopped after a while, but then became annoying again. I asked four famous Western doctors to examine me, and they all determined that it was a critical case of enteritis. They urged surgery, but it was not safe, and there was pus in the intestines, and the intestines would ulcerate. Yanyu's diagnosis and examination was based on the old theory of traditional Chinese medicine to determine the cause of the disease. It was Jueyin syndrome, condensation of liver qi, and internal disturbance of roundworms. Zhongjing's Wumei Pill prescription was used. One dose of Zhongjing's Wumei Pills took immediate effect. Slightly adding or subtracting 4 doses allowed the patient to recover without the risk of surgery. ("Refutation of Feng Youlan's Theory of Traditional Chinese and Western Medicine") \\nNote: In summary, Wu's use of Wumei Pills has three main indications: burning pain in the wrists and abdomen, soreness and pain in vomiting, distended and painful lumps in the chest and abdomen, such as treating Zhang's wife, vomiting, and unbearable pain due to hard lumps in the abdomen. Treat it with Simultaneous Siniling Guidingjiao Decoction. One dose reduces the pain by half, but the vomiting does not stop. This is because the evil of yin and cold in the liver and kidneys has not been eliminated. Treat it with Simultaneous Wumei Pill: 130g of Futian, 60g of dried ginger, Angelica sinensis. 26g, 13g cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 13g Coptis chinensis, 13g Phellodendron cypress, 6g Asarum, 16g Codonopsis pilosula, 6g Sichuan pepper (fried to remove sweat), 3 ebony plums. After taking 1 dose, the vomiting stopped; after 2 doses, the abdominal pain became generalized, and the abdominal mass gradually dispersed. After taking Da Hui Yang Drink and swallowing more than 10 doses of Wu Mei Pills, the full effect was achieved. \\n`,阳弱气虚:"Weak yang and weak qi",阳明急下证:"Yang Ming urgently issued the certificate",阳明燥实证:"Evidence of Yangming dryness",阳明病篇:"Yangming Disease",阳明经热证:"Yangming Meridian Heat Syndrome","阳明经证、腑证与清下法度。":"Yangming Meridian Syndrome, Fu-organ Syndrome and Qingxia Dharma.","阳极似阴证案 张某之妻，年四旬余":"Case of Yang pole resembling Yin syndrome: Zhang’s wife, over 40 years old","阳极似阴证案 马某，男，30岁":"The positive pole resembles the negative evidence case: Ma, male, 30 years old","阳极似阴证案\\n张某之妻，年四旬余。体质素弱，患痰饮哮喘咳嗽多年，屡服滋阴清肺之药罔效。余拟以小青龙汤加附子及四逆二陈加麻辛汤等治之，服10多剂后病愈而复健康。数年后感染时疫，初起发热而渴，头体痛，某医以九味羌活汤加麻黄、桂枝1剂，服后则汗出而昏厥。\\n延余诊视：脉沉伏欲绝，肢厥肤冷，唇焦齿枯，口不能张，问其所苦不能答。此系瘟疫误表过汗伤阴，疫邪传入阳明，复感少阴君火，热化太过，亢阳灼阴，真阴欲绝，邪热内逼致使真阴外越，遂成阳极似阴之证。急与清热养阴生津之剂，方用生脉散煎汁，频频喂服：\\n米洋参10g，麦门冬26g，北五味子6g，生甘草6g。\\n药汤下咽后数刻，脉来沉数，肢厥渐回.口气仍蒸手。邪热未溃，仍照前方加生石膏50g.生地40g，知母、贝母各30g。\\n是晚再诊，脉来洪数，人事稍清，视其苔黄黑而生芒刺，壮热渴喜冷饮，小便短赤，大便燥结不通。《内经》云：“热深者\\n厥亦深也。”今得前二方以济之，促其真阴内回，阳热始通，故反呈现壮热烦渴饮冷等症，邪热内炽燥结阳明，真阴仍有涸竭之虞。当即主以凉下救真阴，拟白虎承气汤加味1剂：\\n生石膏26g，知母16g，沙参16g，生大黄10g（泡水兑入），枳实13g，厚朴13g，芒硝6g，生甘草6g，黄连5g，生地16g。\\n服1剂后，大便始通，苔刺渐软.身热稍退；又服1剂，热退六七，口津稍回，仍渴喜冷饮；续服第3剂，乃下黑燥粪，恶臭已极，热退七八，已不见渴，稍进稀粥。又照此方去枳、朴，加天冬、麦冬各40g，连进2剂后，脉静身凉，津液满口，惟尚喜冷饮。仍照原方去芒硝，并将石膏、大黄减半，加入当归16g，杭芍13g，连进4剂而愈。继以四物汤加党参、口便，调理10余日而康复。\\n原按：此阳极似阴危笃之证，连进凉下9剂，始将疫毒邪火扑灭净尽，转危为安。本证燥热合邪，消灼真阴，津液涸竭，危在旦夕。如不用釜底抽薪之法，连用大凉、大下之剂，万难奏效。诚言有是病，用是药，如方药对证，石膏、大黄亦妙药也。\\n按：吴氏治疗实热之证，用凉药之重不下于用桂附热药，且白虎汤合承气汤，清下并用，即仲景亦未用过，颇见胆识。":`Case of positive pole resembling yin\\nZhang’s wife is in her forties. My constitution is weak and I have been suffering from asthma and cough due to phlegm accumulation for many years. However, I have been taking medicines for nourishing yin and clearing the lungs for many years, but it has no effect. I planned to treat it with Xiaoqinglong Decoction plus Fuzi and Si Ni Erchen plus Maxin Decoction. After taking more than 10 doses, the disease recovered and returned to health. A few years later, he was infected with the epidemic. At first, he had fever, thirst, head and body pain. A certain doctor gave Jiuwei Qianghuo Decoction plus a dose of ephedra and cassia twig. After taking it, he sweated and fainted. \\nAfter further examination: the pulse was deep and weak, the limbs were cold and the skin was cold, the lips were burnt and the teeth were dry, and the mouth could not be opened. When asked about the pain, he could not answer. This is caused by the plague mistakenly manifesting as excessive sweating and damaging the yin. The epidemic evil is introduced into the yangming and re-infects the lord fire of Shaoyin. The heat is excessive, the overactive yang burns the yin, and the true yin is extinguished. The evil heat is forced inward and causes the true yin to move outwards, resulting in a syndrome where the yang pole resembles yin. For urgent and clearing away heat, nourishing yin and promoting fluid production, use the decoction of Shengmai Powder and take it frequently: 10g of American ginseng, 26g of Ophiopogon japonicus, 6g of Schisandra chinensis, and 6g of raw licorice. \\nA few moments after swallowing the medicinal soup, my pulse came and went, and my limbs gradually returned. My breath was still steaming. If the evil heat has not broken down, add 50g of raw gypsum, 40g of raw rehmannia, 30g each of Anemarrhena and Fritillaria. \\nHe was diagnosed again in the evening. His pulse was rapid and rapid, his body was slightly clear, and his fur was yellow and black with thorns. He was suffering from strong fever and thirsty and liked cold drinks. His urine was short and red, and his stool was dry and blocked. "Nei Jing" says: "Those with deep heat will also have deep colds." Now we can use the first two prescriptions to help it, promote the internal return of true yin, and the yang heat will begin to unblock. Therefore, symptoms such as strong heat, polydipsia, and cold drinking will appear instead, and evil heat will cause internal blazing, dryness, and yang, and the true yin is still in danger of drying up. Immediately use cooling to save the true yin, and add 1 dose of Baihu Chengqi Decoction:\\nGypsum 26g, Anemarrhena 16g, Adenophora 16g, Raw rhubarb 10g (soak in water and mix in), Citrus aurantium 13g, Magnolia officinalis 13g, Glauber's salt 6g, Raw licorice 6g, Coptis 5g, Rehmannia glutinosa 16g. \\nAfter taking 1 dose, the stool became clear, and the prickly fur gradually became softer. The body heat subsided slightly; after taking another dose, the fever subsided by 6 to 7 degrees, the mouth fluid returned slightly, and I was still thirsty and liked cold drinks; after taking the 3rd dose, I had black and dry feces, the stench was extremely bad, the fever subsided by 7 to 8 degrees, I no longer felt thirsty, and I had a little gruel. Also follow this recipe to remove Trifoliate Aurantium and Trifoliate Aurantium, add 40g each of Asparagus Asparagus and Ophiopogon japonicus, and after taking 2 doses, the pulse is still and the body is cool, and the mouth is full of body fluids, but I still like cold drinks. Still following the original recipe, remove the Glauber's salt, halve the gypsum and rhubarb, add 16g of angelica root and 13g of peony root, and add 4 doses in a row to heal. After taking Siwu Decoction with Codonopsis pilosula and koufa, he recovered after more than 10 days of conditioning. \\nOriginal note: This is a sign that the Yang pole is like Yin danger. After 9 doses of cooling, the evil fire of epidemic poison can be completely extinguished and the danger can be turned into peace. In this syndrome, dryness and heat combine with evil, the true yin is eliminated, and body fluids dry up, which is a critical situation. If you don't use the method of removing the firewood from the bottom of the cauldron, and use the powerful cold and powerful medicine together, it will never be effective. I sincerely say that if there is a disease, use the medicine, just like prescriptions and medicines to suit the symptoms, gypsum and rhubarb are also wonderful medicines. \\nNote: Wu's use of cold medicine is no less important than the use of Guifu heat medicine in treating excess heat syndrome, and Baihu Decoction and Chengqi Decoction are used together to clear the body. Even Zhong Jing has never used it, which shows his courage.`,"阳极似阴证案\\n马某，男，30岁。1920年3月患瘟疫病已七八日，延余诊视。见其张目仰卧，烦躁谵语，头汗如洗。问其所苦不能答。脉象沉伏欲绝，四肢厥逆，遍身肤冷。唇焦齿枯，舌干苔黑起刺如铁钉，口臭气粗。以手试之，则口气蒸手。小便短赤点滴，大便燥结已数日未通。查其前服之方，系以羌活、紫苏、荆芥、薄荷、山楂、神曲、枳实、厚朴、栀子、黄连、升麻、麻黄及葛根等药连进4剂，辛散发表过甚，真阴被劫，疫邪内壅与阳明燥气相合，复感少阴君火，热化太过，逼其真阴外越，遂成此热深厥深、阳极似阴之证。苟不急为扑灭，待至真阴灼尽，必殆无救。拟下方治之：大黄26g（泡水兑入），生石膏30g，枳实15g，厚朴15g.芒硝10g，知母12g，生地60g，黄连10g。\\n服1剂，病情如故；服2剂后大便始通，脉息沉而虚数，但仍神识蒙睫，问不能答；照方再服2剂，连下恶臭酱黑粪便，臭不可当，其后口津略生；又照原方再服2剂，大便始渐转黄而溏，舌钉渐软，惟舌中部黑苔钉刺尚硬，唇齿稍润；略识人事，始知其症索饮而渴，进食稀粥少许。照前方去枳实、厚朴，加天冬、麦冬各15g，沙参20g，生地12g，甘草6g.将大黄分量减半。连进4剂后，人事清醒，津液回生，苔皮渐退而唇舌已润，唯仍喜冷饮。继以生脉散加味，连服3剂而愈。\\n人参15g，寸冬15g，当归10g，生地15g，杭芍15g，五味子3g，生石膏10g，黄连5g，甘草6g。\\n原按：阳明急下之证，患者已严重昏愦不省人事，不能询及渴饮与否，如证见壮热面赤、口气蒸手、唇舌焦燥、鼻如烟熏等则实热证情已具，即当急下，切勿迟疑，以免贻误病机，证变难挽。":"The positive pole resembles the negative evidence\\nMou, male, 30 years old. In March 1920, he had been ill with the plague for seventy-eight days and was delayed for medical examination. He was seen lying on his back with his eyes open, irritable and delirium, with sweat on his head. When asked about his suffering, he could not answer. The pulse is deep and severe, the limbs are reversed, and the skin is cold all over the body. The lips are scorched, the teeth are dry, the tongue is dry and the coating is black and thorny like iron nails, and the breath is bad and bad. If you try it with your hands, your breath will steam your hands. The urine is short and red, and the stool is dry and constipated for several days. Check the prescription for taking it before taking it. It is based on 4 doses of astragalus, perilla, nepeta, mint, hawthorn, Shenqu, citrus aurantium, magnolia bark, gardenia, coptis, cohosh, ephedra and kudzu root. If it is expressed too much, the true yin will be robbed, and the internal obstruction of the epidemic evil will combine with the Yangming dryness, and the Shaoyin Lord Fire will be felt again, and the heat will be too much, forcing the true yin to escape outwards, resulting in a syndrome of deep heat and deep yin, and the yang pole is like yin. If you don't rush to extinguish it, when the true yin is burned out, you will be completely hopeless. It is planned to treat the disease as follows: 26g of rhubarb (soaked in water and mixed with water), 30g of gypsum, 15g of Fructus Aurantii, 15g of Magnolia officinalis, 10g of Glauber's Salt, 12g of Anemarrhena, 60g of Radix Rehmanniae, and 10g of Coptidis Rhizoma. \\nAfter taking 1 dose, the condition remained the same; after taking 2 doses, the stool became clear, the pulse was heavy and empty, but the consciousness was still blinded, and I could not answer questions; I took another 2 doses according to the prescription, and the feces were black with foul-smelling sauce. The smell was unbearable, and afterwards the mouth was There was a slight increase in body fluids; after taking another 2 doses according to the original prescription, the stool began to turn yellow and loose, the tongue became softer, but the black coating in the middle of the tongue was still hard, and the lips and teeth were slightly moist; after knowing a little about people, I realized that the symptom was thirst after drinking and eating a little gruel. Remove Citrus aurantium and Magnolia officinalis as before, add 15g each of Asparagus and Ophiopogon japonicus, 20g Adenophora adenophora, 12g Rehmannia glutinosa, and 6g licorice. Reduce the amount of rhubarb in half. After taking 4 doses in a row, I felt awake, my body fluids were regenerated, my coating gradually receded and my lips and tongue were moist, but I still liked cold drinks. Then take Shengmai Powder with added flavor and take 3 doses and the symptoms will be cured. \\nGinseng 15g, Cundong 15g, Angelica sinensis 10g, Rehmannia glutinosa 15g, Hangshao 15g, Schisandra chinensis 3g, Gypsum 10g, Coptis 5g, Licorice 6g. \\nOriginal note: In the syndrome of Yangming's sudden illness, the patient is severely comatose and unconscious, and cannot ask whether he is thirsty or not. If the syndrome shows strong heat, flushed face, steaming breath and hands, dry lips and tongue, and a smoky nose, etc., then the symptoms of severe heat are already present, so it is urgent to treat the patient immediately. Don't hesitate to avoid delaying the pathogenesis and making the syndrome difficult to cure.","阳虚甚、畏寒肢冷者，加干姜、上肉桂；小便不利重者，加车前子、泽泻；水肿甚者，加猪苓、大腹皮":"For those with severe yang deficiency and aversion to cold and cold limbs, add dried ginger and cinnamon; for those with severe difficulty in urination, add Psyllium Seed and Alisma; for severe edema, add Polyporus Polyporus and Dabupi.",阳虚胃寒:"Yang deficiency and stomach cold",阳虚阴寒:"Yang deficiency and Yin cold","阴极似阳案 杨某，男，32岁":"Yin pole is like Yang case Yang, male, 32 years old","阴极似阳案\\n杨某，男，32岁。始因风寒，身热头痛，某医连进苦寒凉下方药10余剂，且重加犀角、羚羊角、黄连等，愈进愈剧，病发已20口，危在旦夕，延吴氏诊视，目赤，唇肿而焦，赤足露身，烦躁不眠，神昏谵语，身热似火，渴喜滚烫水饮。小便短赤，大便已数日不解，食物不进，脉浮虚欲散。辨为风寒之证误服苦寒，真阳逼越于外而成阴极似阳之证。外虽现一派热象，是为假热；而内则寒凉已极，是为真寒。如确系阳证，内热熏蒸应见大渴饮冷，岂有尚喜滚饮乎？况脉来虚浮欲散，是为阳气将脱之兆。治之急宜回阳收纳，拟白通汤加上肉桂为方：	附片60g，干姜26g，上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），葱白4茎。\\n方子开好，病家称家中无人主持，未敢服药，实则犹疑不定。次日又延吴氏诊视，“仍执前方不变”。并告以先用肉桂泡水试服，若能耐受，则照方煎服。病家如法试之，服后即吐岀涎痰碗许，人事稍清，内心爽快。遂进上方，病情即减，身热约退一二，出现恶寒肢冷之象，已无烦躁谵语之状，且得熟睡片刻。乃以四逆汤加上肉桂续服：\\n附片100g，干姜36g，甘草12g，上肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入）。\\n服药1剂，身热退去四五，脉稍有神。尿赤而长，略进稀饭；再剂则热退七八，大便已通。唯咳嗽痰多夹血，病家另请数医诊视，皆云热证，出方不离苦寒凉下之法，鉴于前医之误，未敢轻试。其时病人吃梨一个，“当晚忽发狂打人，身热大作，有如前状”。又急邀吴氏诊视，见舌白而滑，“仍喜滚饮”，判为“阳神尚虚，阴寒未净”。仍主以大剂回阳祛寒之法，照第二方剂量加倍，另加茯苓30g，半夏16g，北细辛4g，早晚各1剂，即日进2剂。连服6剂，身热已退，咳嗽渐愈，饮食增加，小便淡黄而长，大便转黄而溏。前方去半夏、细辛，加砂仁、白术、口芪善后，连进10余剂，诸症俱愈。\\n按：此案既显出吴氏辨证准确，又示其用药风格。在一派热象之中，以“舌白而滑，渴喜滚烫水饮，脉浮虚欲散”为阴证辨识眼目。另外，从其服苦寒凉下之药而病“愈进愈剧”，亦可推知绝非阳证。最可奇者，病人吃一梨后，“忽发狂打人，身热大作，有如前状”，此系阴证食凉必然加重，阳气欲脱之象。吴氏加倍重用附子，不夹凉药，挽回此等重症，确有见识。":`Yin pole is like Yang case\\nYang, male, 32 years old. It started with a headache due to wind-cold and body heat. A certain doctor prescribed more than 10 doses of bitter and cold prescription medicines, and added rhinoceros horn, antelope horn, coptis, etc., which became more and more severe. The disease had already occurred 20 times and was in danger. Wu's diagnosis showed red eyes, swollen and burnt lips, bare feet exposed, irritability and sleeplessness, coma and delirium, body heat was like fire, and thirsty for boiling water. The urine is short and red, the stool has been indistinct for several days, food cannot be taken in, and the pulse is floating and weak. Diagnosed as a syndrome of wind and cold, if you mistakenly take bitter cold, the true yang will be forced beyond the outside, resulting in a syndrome of yin pole resembling yang. Although there is some heat outside, it is false heat; while inside it is extremely cold, it is true cold. If it is indeed a yang syndrome, internal heat fumigation will result in severe thirst and cold drinking. How can you still drink boiling water? If the pulse is weak and wants to dissipate, it is a sign that Yang Qi is about to escape. For urgent treatment, it is better to restore Yang and absorb it. Take Baitong decoction and add cinnamon as a recipe: 60g of Fu slices, 26g of dried ginger, 10g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), and 4 white stalks of scallion. \\nAfter the prescription was prescribed, the patient said that no one at home was in charge and he did not dare to take the medicine, but in fact he was hesitant. Wu's diagnosis was postponed the next day, but "the patient's front remains unchanged." He also told me to soak cinnamon in water and take it first. If you can tolerate it, you can decoct it and take it. The patient tested it according to the method. After taking it, he spit out a bowl of phlegm, felt a little clearer, and felt refreshed. Then he went to the upper level, and his condition immediately subsided. The body heat subsided by about one or two, the symptoms of aversion to cold and cold limbs appeared, and the irritability and delirium no longer appeared, and he could fall asleep for a while. Then take Sini Decoction with cinnamon and continue taking: 100g of Fu Pian, 36g of dried ginger, 12g of licorice, and 10g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix). \\nAfter taking 1 dose of medicine, the body fever subsided and the pulse became slightly clearer. The urine will be red and long, and a little porridge will be added; if you take another dose, the fever will subside and the stool will be clear. The patient only had a cough with excessive phlegm and blood, so the patient asked several doctors for examination. They all reported that the patient had heat syndrome, and the prescription was based on bitter cold and cooling. In view of the mistakes of previous doctors, he did not dare to try it lightly. At that time, the patient ate a pear and "suddenly went crazy and beat people that night, and his body became very hot, just like before." He also urgently invited Mr. Wu for a consultation. He found that his tongue was white and slippery, and he "still likes to drink." The main method is still to use a large dose to restore Yang and dispel cold, double the dose of the second prescription, and add 30g of Poria cocos, 16g of Pinellia ternata, and 4g of Asarum, one dose in the morning and one in the evening, and two doses on the same day. After taking 6 doses, the body fever has subsided, the cough has gradually improved, the diet has increased, the urine is light yellow and long, and the stool has turned yellow and loose. Remove Pinellia ternata and Asarum, add Amomum villosum, Atractylodes macrocephala, and Oral Qilin to treat the aftermath. After taking more than 10 doses, all symptoms were cured. \\nNote: This case not only shows Wu’s accuracy in syndrome differentiation, but also his medication style. Among the heat signs of one school, "white and slippery tongue, thirsty to drink boiling water, floating and weak pulse that wants to disperse" are used to identify the eyes as yin syndrome. In addition, from the fact that the disease "progressed and became more severe" after taking bitter, cold and cooling medicine, it can also be inferred that it is definitely not a Yang syndrome. The most surprising thing is that after the patient ate a pear, he "suddenly went crazy and hit people, and his body became very hot, just like before." This is a sign that the yin syndrome will inevitably aggravate when eating cold food, and the yang energy is about to escape. Wu's wisdom in using Aconite aconite more than any other medicine to treat such serious illness can be remedied.`,阴疽核肿:"vaginal gangrene","阴疽核肿 朱某之母，四十九岁，住昆明市珠巩街三四二号":"Gangrene and swollen penis Zhu's mother, 49 years old, lives at No. 342, Zhugong Street, Kunming City","阴疽核肿 朱某之母，四十九岁，住昆明市珠巩街三四二号。1952年 8月，右颈脖处起核如鸡蛋大，肿硬疼痛，肤色如常，咽口津则 痛彻耳咽，饮食难下,神惫无力，曾到某医院诊视，诊断为炎 症化脓，需要开刀排脓，否则听其自然出头而已。渠因惧怕开刀痛楚，来舍就诊于余，脉舌均为阳虚阴寒之象，断为阴疽结 核之证，以温化疏通之剂。 附片100克，干姜30克，细辛6克，败酱50克，薏苡仁 50克，通草6克，桔梗10克，穿山甲10克，延胡索12克，炙 香附12克，甘草12克。 三剂后，核肿消散。":"Gangrene and swollen penis Zhu's mother, 49 years old, lives at No. 342, Zhugong Street, Kunming City. In August 1952, he developed a nucleus as big as an egg on the right side of his neck, which was swollen, hard and painful. His skin color was as normal, and his throat was so painful that it penetrated his ear and throat. He had difficulty eating and drinking, and was exhausted. He went to a hospital for a diagnosis and was diagnosed with inflammation and suppuration. Surgery was needed to drain the pus, otherwise it would just take its course. Because he was afraid of the pain of surgery, he went to see a doctor. His pulse and tongue showed symptoms of yang deficiency and yin cold, so he diagnosed it as gangrene and tuberculosis, so he prescribed warming and dredging medicine. 100 grams of Aconite, 30 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of asarum, 50 grams of bean paste, 50 grams of coix seed, 6 grams of Tongcao, 10 grams of Platycodon, 10 grams of pangolin, 12 grams of Corydalis, 12 grams of Cyperus rotundus, and 12 grams of licorice. After three doses, the nuclear swelling dissipated.",阴瘅证:"Yin syndrome","阴瘅证 （慢性胆汁性肝硬化） 方某，男，二十八岁，未婚，河南省人…":"Genital syndrome (chronic biliary cirrhosis) Fang, male, 28 years old, unmarried, from Henan Province...","阴瘅证 （慢性胆汁性肝硬化） 方某，男，二十八岁，未婚，河南省人，昆明军区某部战 士。患者因肝脾肿大，全身发黄已八年，曾先后住昆明军区某 医院及省市级医院治疗,效果不显著，继而出现腹水肿胀,腹 围达98厘米，黄疸指数高达100单位,经军区医院行剖腹探 査,取肝脏活体组织做病理检验,证实为“胆汁性肝硬化”。遂 于1959年7月由市级某医院转来中医学院门诊部就诊。余 见患者病体羸瘦，面色黄黯晦滞无光,巩膜深度黄染，周身皮 肤亦呈深黯黄色，干枯瘙痒而留见抓痕。精神倦怠，声低息 短，少气懒言，不思食，不渴饮。小便短少，色深黄如浓茶水， 腹水鼓胀，四肢瘦削，颜面及足附以下浮肿，两胁疼痛,尤以 肝区为甚。扪之，肝肿大于右肋沿下约二横指,脾肿大于左肋 沿下约三横指。脉沉取弦劲而紧，舌苔白滑厚腻而带黄色，少 津。因阳虚水寒，肝气郁结不得温升，脾虚失其运化,湿浊阻 遏中焦，胆液失其顺降，溢于肌肤,故全身发黄。阳虚则湿从 寒化，水湿之邪泛滥于内，脾阳失其运化，日久则成为腹水肿 胀之证。肤色黄黯不鲜，似阴黄之象。此病即所谓“阴瘅证”。 法当扶阳抑阴，疏肝利胆，健脾除湿为治则。以四逆茵陈五苓 散加减治之。 附片100克，干姜50克，肉桂15克（研末，泡水兑入）， 吴茱萸15克（炒），败酱草15克，茵陈30克，猪苓15克，茯 苓50克，北细辛8克，苍术20克，甘草8克。 二诊。服上方十余剂后,黄疸已退去十之八九，肝脾肿大 已减小，小便色转清长，外肿内胀渐消，黄疸指数降至20单 位，面部黄色减退，已渐现润红色,食欲增加，大便正常,精神 转佳。然患病已久,肝肾极为虚寒，脾气尚弱,寒湿邪阴尚未 肃清，宜再以扶阳温化主之。 附片150克，干姜80克，茵陈80克，茯苓30克，薏苡仁 20克，肉桂15克（研末，泡水兑入），吴茱萸10克，白术20 克，桂枝尖30克，甘草10克。 三诊。服上方六剂后,肝脾已不肿大,胁痛若失,小便清利 如常,面脚浮肿及腹水鼓胀已全消退,饮食、精神倍增,皮肤及 巩膜已不见发黄色。到市级某医院复査，黄疸指数已降至3单 位。脉象和缓，舌苔白润，厚腻苔已全退。此水湿之邪已除，元 阳尚虚，再拟抉阳温化之剂调理之,促其正气早复，以图巩固 效果。 附片150克，干姜80克，砂仁15克，郁金10克，肉桂15 克（研末，泡水兑入），薏苡仁30克，佛手20克，甘草10克。 服上方七、八剂后，患者已基本恢复健康。一年后询访， 肝脾肿痛及黄疸诸证均未再发作。 按：以上病证，实由阳虚水寒，寒湿内滞，肝气郁结不疏 所致。阳虚则水邪泛溢，肝郁则易克伐脾土，脾虚不能健运， 湿从寒化，而至肝脾肿大、腹水、黄疸诸证丛生。余所拟用各 方，旨在温暖肾寒，疏肝解郁，健运脾湿，化气行水。寒湿内 滞之证，施以温化之剂，犹如春和 日暖，冰雪消融，故能治之 而愈。":`Syndrome of yin syndrome (chronic biliary cirrhosis) Fang, male, 28 years old, unmarried, from Henan Province, a soldier of a certain unit of the Kunming Military Region. The patient had been suffering from hepatosplenomegaly and yellowness all over his body for eight years. He had been admitted to a hospital in the Kunming Military Region and a provincial and municipal hospital for treatment, but the effect was not significant. Then he developed ascites and swelling, with an abdominal circumference of 98 cm and a jaundice index as high as 100 units. After a laparotomy at the military hospital, biopsy of the liver tissue was taken for pathological examination, and it was confirmed to be "biliary cirrhosis." Then in July 1959, he was transferred from a municipal hospital to the outpatient department of the College of Traditional Chinese Medicine. The rest of the patient's body was thin, his complexion was yellow and dull, his sclera was deeply jaundiced, and the skin all over his body was also dark yellow, withered, itchy, and scratched. Mental fatigue, low voice and short breathing, lack of breath and laziness, no desire to eat, no desire to drink. The urine is short, dark yellow in color like strong tea, bulging abdominal fluid, thin limbs, edema on the face and below the feet, and pain in both flanks, especially in the liver area. It can be seen that the hepatoma is larger than about two fingers horizontally below the right rib, and the splenomegaly is larger than about three fingers below the left rib. The pulse is deep, stringy and tight, the tongue coating is white, slippery, thick, greasy and yellow, and there is little fluid. Due to yang deficiency and cold water, stagnation of liver qi prevents the temperature from rising, spleen deficiency loses its transportation and transformation, dampness and turbidity block the middle burner, and bile fluid loses its smooth descent and overflows on the skin, so the whole body becomes yellow. When Yang is deficient, dampness transforms from cold, and the evil of water-dampness floods the inside. Spleen Yang loses its transportation and transformation, and over time, abdominal edema and distension will occur. The skin color is yellowish and dull, like a yin-yellow appearance. This disease is the so-called "yin syndrome". The treatment principles are to strengthen yang and suppress yin, soothe the liver and promote gallbladder, invigorate the spleen and remove dampness. Treat it with addition and subtraction of Sini Yinchen Wuling Powder. 100 grams of Futian, 50 grams of dried ginger, 15 grams of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water), 15 grams of Evodia (stir-fried), 15 grams of soyrel, 30 grams of capsicum, 15 grams of Polyporus, 50 grams of Poria, 8 grams of Asarum, 20 grams of Atractylodes, and 8 grams of licorice. Second diagnosis. After taking more than ten doses of the above medicine, jaundice has receded in nine out of ten cases, hepatosplenomegaly has been reduced, urine color has become clear and long, external swelling and internal swelling have gradually disappeared, the jaundice index has dropped to 20 units, the yellow color of the face has subsided and has gradually turned red, the appetite has increased, the stool is normal, and the spirit has improved. However, the patient has been ill for a long time, the liver and kidneys are extremely weak and cold, the spleen is still weak, and the cold-dampness evil yin has not been cleared away, so it is better to strengthen the yang and warm it up. 150 grams of Futian, 80 grams of dried ginger, 80 grams of Artemisia argyi, 30 grams of Poria, 20 grams of coix seed, 15 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10 grams of Evodia, 20 grams of Atractylodes, 30 grams of Guizhi tip, and 10 grams of licorice. Three diagnoses. After taking six doses of the above, the liver and spleen are no longer swollen, the hypochondriac pain has disappeared, the urine is clear and clear as usual, the edema of the face and feet and the bulging ascites have completely subsided, the diet and energy have doubled, and the yellowing of the skin and sclera has disappeared. I went to a municipal hospital for review and found that the jaundice index had dropped to 3 units. The pulse is gentle, the tongue coating is white and moist, and the thick and greasy coating has completely subsided. The evil of water-dampness has been eliminated, but the Yuanyang is still deficient. Then use the Yang-warming agent to regulate it, to promote the early recovery of the healthy Qi, in order to consolidate the effect. 150 grams of Aconite slices, 80 grams of dried ginger, 15 grams of amomum villosum, 10 grams of turmeric, 15 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 30 grams of coix seed, 20 grams of bergamot, and 10 grams of licorice. After taking seven or eight doses of the above, the patient has basically recovered. After a follow-up visit one year later, the symptoms of liver and spleen swelling and pain and jaundice had not recurred. Note: The above symptoms are actually caused by Yang deficiency, cold water, internal stagnation of cold and dampness, and stagnation of liver qi. Yang deficiency means water evil will overflow, liver stagnation will easily attack the spleen earth, spleen deficiency will not improve transportation, and dampness will change from cold, leading to hepatosplenomegaly, ascites, and jaundice. The various prescriptions I plan to use are aimed at warming the kidney cold, soothing the liver and relieving stagnation, strengthening the spleen and promoting dampness, and transforming qi and flowing water. The syndrome of internal stagnation of cold-dampness can be cured and cured by applying warming agents, just as the ice and snow melt when the sun warms in spring.`,"阴盛格阳、面赤戴阳者，加葱白3茎、猪胆汁少许；脉微欲绝者，加人参30g；大汗不止者，加龙骨、牡蛎各60g":"For those with Yin and Yang, red face and Yang, add 3 white stalks of green onion and a little pig bile; for those with weak and weak pulse, add 30g of ginseng; for those with persistent sweating, add 60g each of keel bone and oyster.",阴虚肺燥:"Yin deficiency and lung dryness",阴证误下救逆:"Yin syndrome mistakenly saves the day","阴证误下救逆案 昔诊一男，廿余岁，系一孀妇之独子，体质素弱":"A case of a man with yin syndrome who mistakenly rescued someone from a bad situation. I once diagnosed a man in his twenties, the only son of a widowed woman, with a weak constitution.","阴证误下救逆案 昔诊一男，廿余岁，系一孀妇之独子，体质素弱。始因腹 痛便秘而发热，医者诊为瘀热内滞，误以桃仁承气汤下之, 便未通而病情反重，出现发狂奔走，言语错乱。延余诊视，脉 沉迟无力，舌红津枯但不渴，微喜热饮而不多，气息喘促而 短,有欲脱之势。据此断为阴证误下，逼阳暴脱之证,遂拟大 剂圈阳饮（即四逆汤加肉桂）与服。 附片130克，干姜50克，上肉桂13克（研末，泡水兑 入），甘草10克。 服后，当天夜晚则鼻孔流血,大便亦下黑血。次日复诊则 见脉微神衰，嗜卧懒言,神识已转清。其所以鼻衄及下黑血 者，非服温热药所致，实由于桃仁承气汤误下后，致血脱成 瘀,今得上方温运气血，既已离经败坏之血,不能再行归经， 遂上行而下注。嘱照原方再服一剂。服后,衄血便血均未再 出，口微燥,此系阳气已回，营阴尚虚,继以四逆汤加人参连 进四剂而愈。方中加人参者，取其益气生津养阴以配阳也。":"A case of a man with yin syndrome who mistakenly saved the patient. I once diagnosed a man in his twenties, the only son of a widowed woman, with a weak constitution. He started to have fever due to abdominal pain, constipation, and the doctor diagnosed it as internal stagnation of blood stasis and heat. He mistakenly prescribed Taoren Chengqi Decoction. As a result, the stool did not pass and the condition worsened. He ran around frantically and had confused speech. After delayed examination, the pulse was slow and weak, the tongue was red and dry but not thirsty, the patient liked hot drinks but not much, the breath was short and short, and there was a tendency to want to escape. Based on this, it was concluded that the yin syndrome was mistakenly suppressed and the yang was forced out, so a large dose of Yang Encircling Drink (i.e. Sini Decoction plus cinnamon) was prepared and taken. 130 grams of Fu slices, 50 grams of dried ginger, 13 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), and 10 grams of licorice. After taking it, I had bleeding from my nostrils and black blood in my stool that night. The next day's follow-up examination showed that the pulse was weak and the patient was weak, prone to lying down and talking lazily, and his consciousness had become clear. The reason why the epistaxis and black blood in the vagina are not caused by taking warm medicine is actually due to Taoren Chengqi Decoction being mistakenly taken, causing the blood to break off and form blood stasis. Please take another dose according to the original prescription. After taking it, the epistaxis and blood in the stool no longer came out, and the mouth was slightly dry. This was because the Yang Qi had returned and the Ying Yin was still deficient. After taking four doses of Sini Decoction and ginseng, the condition was cured. If ginseng is added to the prescription, it should be used to replenish qi, promote fluid and nourish yin to coordinate yang.","阴证误下，逼阳暴脱之证":"The yin syndrome is mistakenly suppressed, forcing the yang to escape violently.","附子150g（先煎），干姜60g，炙甘草30g，上肉桂20g（研末泡水兑入），砂仁15g":"150g aconite (fried first), 60g dried ginger, 30g roasted licorice, 20g cinnamon (grind and soak in water), 15g Amomum villosum","附子30g（先煎），白芍20g，茯苓30g，白术25g，生姜15g，桂枝15g":"30g aconite (fried first), 20g white peony root, 30g poria, 25g atractylodes, 15g ginger, 15g cassia twig","附子、干姜、肉桂等温阳药运用法度详备":"Detailed instructions for using aconite, dried ginger, cinnamon and other yang-warming herbs","附子、肉桂、吴萸等药物的炮制、用量与配伍心得。":"Experience on the preparation, dosage and compatibility of aconite, cinnamon, Wuyu and other medicines.","附子、草乌等毒烈药物的炮制、用量与解毒之法。":"The preparation, dosage and detoxification methods of aconite, aconite and other poisonous drugs.","附子一斤救团长夫人 在吴佩衡诞辰一百周年纪念大会上，云南大理州李…":"A pound of aconite saved the wife of the group leader. At the commemoration meeting for the 100th anniversary of Wu Peiheng’s birth, Li...","附子一斤救团长夫人\\n在吴佩衡诞辰一百周年纪念大会上，云南大理州李宝鍹先生回忆：抗日时期，国军将领薛岳守卫长沙，屡歼日寇。云南组织滇军团长若干人赴湘参观学习。李的表兄方家治亦奉命参加，而其表嫂玉卿正值病危，中西医束手无策。前曾请某中医诊治，不给开方，告诉家人准备后事。其婆母哭泣，遂请吴佩衡诊治。次日清晨，有表姐催促李到方府，老太太说：“吴先生昨晚处方时说不会死，药不重无力，用土锅煨服。已请雷某等亲友斟酌，都不置可否，今请侄儿主病。”李接处方，见用附片一斤，盐附子四两……令人骇然。思考久之说：“今不服药待毙，勿宁服药救生，侄儿虽不知医，但深信吴先生医术无误，请即煮药，”于是连服数剂，终于起死回生。玉卿嫂高龄至今健康，先生之方奇效如此:（《著名中医学家吴佩衡诞辰一百周年纪念专集》）":`Aconite Yijin rescued the leader’s wife\\nAt the commemoration meeting for the 100th anniversary of Wu Peiheng’s birth, Mr. Li Baoquan of Dali Prefecture, Yunnan Province recalled: During the Anti-Japanese War, the national army general Xue Yue guarded Changsha and repeatedly wiped out the Japanese invaders. Yunnan organized several commanders of the Yunnan Army to visit and study in Hunan. Li's cousin Fang Jiazhi was also ordered to participate, but his cousin-in-law Yuqing was critically ill, and Chinese and Western medicine were helpless. I once asked a Chinese medicine doctor for diagnosis and treatment, but he refused to give me a prescription and told my family to prepare for the funeral. His mother-in-law cried and asked Wu Peiheng for diagnosis and treatment. Early the next morning, a cousin urged Li to go to Fang's house. The old lady said: "Mr. Wu gave the prescription last night and said that he would not die. The medicine is not heavy and weak, so he should simmer it in an earthen pot. I have asked Lei and other relatives and friends to consider it, but they are all undecided. Now I ask my nephew to treat the disease." When Li received the prescription, he saw that he would use one pound of Fu tablets and four taels of salt and monkshood... It was shocking. After thinking for a long time, he said: "If I don't take medicine now, I will die. I would rather take medicine to save life. Although my nephew does not know medicine, he is convinced that Mr. Wu's medical skills are correct. Please boil the medicine immediately." So he took several doses and finally brought him back to life. Sister-in-law Yuqing is still healthy at her advanced age, and her husband’s prescription has such miraculous effects: ("Special Collection Commemorating the 100th Anniversary of the Birth of Famous Chinese Medicine Scientist Wu Peiheng")`,"附子条下最详：辨产地、讲炮制、论配伍、明剂量，谓附子乃药中先锋，用之得当，起死回生，并明列久煎、渐增、中病即止三戒，可谓仁术兼至。":"The article on Aconite is the most detailed: identifying the place of origin, processing, compatibility, and dosage. It is said that Aconite is a pioneer among medicines. When used properly, it can bring people back to life. It also lists the three precepts of long-term decoction, gradual increase, and immediate relief of diseases. It can be said that it is both benevolent and skillful.","附子条下详载盐渍、火煨、童便浸诸法，谓生用峻烈、熟用温厚，救阳虚危证非此不为功。草乌必以久煎去毒，且明列中毒解救之方，凡唇舌麻木、心悸呕恶者，急以甘草、绿豆、蜂蜜煎汤解之。":"The aconite article details the methods of salting, stewing in fire, and soaking in children's feces. It is said that the raw method is harsh and the cooked method is mild. This is not the only way to save the dangerous syndrome of Yang deficiency. Caowu must be decoctioned for a long time to remove the poison, and remedies for poisoning are clearly listed. For those with numbness of the lips and tongue, palpitations, and nausea, decoction of licorice, mung beans, and honey can be used urgently to relieve the symptoms.","附录 · 诸病验方":"Appendix · Prescriptions for various diseases","附录汇编内、外、妇、儿各科验方二百八十余首，多采自滇南民间，药皆本地所产，价贱而效捷。":"The appendix compiles more than 280 prescriptions from internal medicine, external medicine, gynecology, and pediatrics. Most of them are collected from the folk in southern Yunnan. The medicines are all locally produced, cheap and effective.","青囊传世，典籍流芳。汇云南历代名医著述，存一方医学之正脉。":"The green bag is handed down from generation to generation, and the classics are famous. It collects the writings of Yunnan famous doctors from past dynasties and preserves the true pulse of medicine.",静音:"mute",面瘫:"Facial paralysis",音效:"Sound effects",音韵医药:"Phonological Medicine","页面未找到 | 云南名医馆":"Page not found | Yunnan Famous Medical Center","项目将对《滇南本草》所载四百余种滇产药物进行本草考证与图谱数字化，为滇南医药研究提供文献支撑。":'The project will conduct materia medica research and digitize the maps of more than 400 Yunnan-produced drugs contained in the "Southern Yunnan Materia Medica" to provide documentary support for southern Yunnan medical research.',顺证辨治:"Syndrome differentiation and treatment",颈椎病:"cervical spondylosis","颈腰疾患主张“三分治、七分养”，授患者导引之法以固疗效。":'For neck and waist diseases, we advocate "three-part treatment and seven-part nourishment", and patients should be taught guidance methods to consolidate the curative effect.',"风寒者加苏叶、荆芥；风热者加桑叶、薄荷、连翘；痰多者加二陈汤；脾虚者加白术、茯苓、神曲":"For those with wind-cold, add perilla leaves and Schizonepeta; for those with wind-heat, add mulberry leaves, mint, and forsythia; for those with excessive phlegm, add Erchen Decoction; for those with spleen deficiency, add Atractylodes macrocephala, Poria cocos, and Shenqu.","风寒袭表，经脉血络受阻":"Wind and cold attack the surface, and the meridians and blood collaterals are blocked",风湿关节痹痛:"Rheumatic joint pain","风湿关节痹痛 田某妻，年三十余，某年9月，患风湿痹证，右手关节疼…":"Rheumatism and joint pain. Tian's wife, who was in her thirties, suffered from rheumatism and joint pain in September of a certain year...","风湿关节痹痛 田某妻，年三十余，某年9月，患风湿痹证，右手关节疼痛 发麻，自觉骨间灼热，但又见寒生畏。病已十余、日，曾服四逆汤加白术、当归等剂,未效,疼痛忽轻忽重，固着肩肘,痛甚不 休。余审其病情，查其方药，此乃风寒湿邪杂合而至，阻遏经 脉，阳不足以运行通利关节,不通则痛，虽应用姜附之辛温以 化散寒湿，然杂以归、术之壅补滋腻,犹如闭门捉寇,遂使邪气 难化。因照前方去归、术加入桂枝、细辛、茯苓治之,一剂显效， 二剂霍然。 附片60克，干姜15克，桂枝24克，细辛5克，茯苓24 克，甘草10克。":"Rheumatic joint arthralgia Tian's wife, who was in her thirties, suffered from rheumatic arthralgia syndrome in September of a certain year. She had pain and numbness in the joints of her right hand. She felt there was burning between the bones, but was afraid of the cold. I have been ill for more than ten days. I have taken Sini decoction plus Atractylodes macrocephala, Angelica sinensis and other medicines, but it has no effect. The pain alternates between mild and severe, and the pain is constant in my shoulders and elbows. I reviewed his condition and checked his prescriptions. It turned out that this was caused by the combination of wind, cold, and damp evils, which blocked the meridians. The yang was not enough to circulate and clear the joints, and the blockage caused pain. Although the pungent warmth of ginger was used to dispel the cold and dampness, the combination returned, and the technique was used to block and nourish the blood, which was like catching a bandit behind closed doors, making it difficult for the evil qi to be transformed. According to the method of removing the disease from the front, adding cinnamon twig, asarum, and poria cocos to treat it, one dose is effective, and the second dose is sudden. 60 grams of Futian, 15 grams of dried ginger, 24 grams of cinnamon twig, 5 grams of asarum, 24 grams of Poria, and 10 grams of licorice.","风湿关节痹痛案 田某之妻，30余岁":"Rheumatic joint pain case: Tian’s wife, over 30 years old","风湿关节痹痛案\\n田某之妻，30余岁。患风湿痹证，右手关节疼痛发麻，自觉骨间灼热，但又见寒生畏。病已10余日，曾服四逆汤加白术、当归等剂未效，疼痛忽轻忽重，固着肩肘，痛甚不休。吴氏审病查方，认为乃风寒湿邪杂合而至，阻遏经脉，阳不足以运行通利关节，不通则痛。“虽应用姜附之辛温以化散寒湿，然杂以归术之壅补滋腻，犹如闭门留寇，遂使邪气难化。因照前方去归、术，加入桂枝、细辛、茯苓治之”，1剂显效，2剂霍然。按：火神派扶阳讲究单刀直入，不夹阴药。作为经典火神派代表，吴氏即或补气药也少应用，嫌其掣肘。本案吴氏以亲身实践诠释了这一点。":`Case of rheumatic joint pain\\nTian’s wife, over 30 years old. Suffering from rheumatism syndrome, the joints of the right hand are painful and numb, and the bones feel hot, but the cold is also frightening. I have been ill for more than 10 days. I have taken Sini decoction plus Atractylodes macrocephala, Angelica sinensis and other medicines, but it has no effect. The pain alternates between mild and severe, and the pain is constant in my shoulders and elbows. After Wu's review of the disease and prescription, he believed that it was caused by the combination of wind, cold, and damp evils, which blocked the meridians, and the yang was not enough to move the joints, and the blockage caused pain. "Although the pungent warmth of ginger is used to dispel cold and dampness, it is mixed with the congestion and nourishment of Gui Shu, which is like leaving a bandit behind closed doors, so it is difficult to change the evil spirit. According to the previous Gui and Shu techniques, cinnamon twig, asarum, and Poria are added to treat it." One dose is effective, and the second dose is sudden. Note: The Vulcan sect’s method of supporting yang emphasizes going straight to the point without inserting yin medicine. As a representative of the classic Vulcan sect, Wu seldom uses qi-tonifying medicines because he thinks they are limiting. In this case, Wu explained this point through personal practice.`,首经验方:"First experience",首页:"Home","验案丰富，涵盖内妇儿科疑难病症":"Rich case studies, covering difficult diseases in gynecology and pediatrics",麻疹:"Measles","麻疹、春温等时病透发与救误之案。":"Cases of sudden onset of measles, spring fever and other seasonal diseases and misguided rescue.",麻疹危证:"measles risk","麻疹危证扶阳救逆二例、顺证一例 陶某，年三十二岁，江西人,住上海…":"Two cases of measles critical syndrome, supporting yang and rescuing the reverse, and one case of normal syndrome. Tao, 32 years old, from Jiangxi, lives in Shanghai...","麻疹危证扶阳救逆二例、顺证一例 陶某，年三十二岁，江西人,住上海，有四子一女，于1932 年3月值麻疹流行，将其长次两子（七至九岁）,送往苏州躲 避。殊料去后均出麻疹，误服寒凉之药相继夭亡。三、四两子， 二至四岁，在上海亦患麻疹,住某广东医院治疗。病至严重 时,该院诊断为“肺炎”，延余到该院诊视。两孩均同卧于小床 内，麻疹虽免，但发热不退，喘咳痰鸣，满口涎痰随时流出口 外，不知曾服何药。见喂入黄果水时，仍从口中外流。颜面青 黯（阴象外露）,两额发赤（虚阳外泄）,唇色青紫,指纹青黑出 二关，脉搏紧急（寒极之象），大便鹫溏（水寒土湿，木邪贼 土）,乳食不进（胃中虚寒，司运失权）。该院认为病势严重,别 无他法，已感束手。余诊视后，当即告以病势危笃，已成三阴 寒极之证,寒痰内壅，真阳外泄，有风动或衰脱之势，急宜扶 阳抑阴，温逐寒痰为主。若服后涌吐寒痰,系病除之兆。如热 退喘平，尚可转危为安。倘若缓治或再施寒凉之药,必危殆无 救。渠因长次两子已夭亡，三、四两孩又复病重，惊慌不已，要 求设法抢救，万分信任，纵虽不起，决无怨言。遂拟四逆二陈 汤加丁香、肉桂，少佐麻,辛,分量加重，与两孩同服（因其病 情相同，故共服一剂）。 附片100克，干姜24克，肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑入）， 法半夏10克，广陈皮6克，茯苓15克，细辛3克，公丁香6 克，炙麻茸3克，甘草10克。 此方服后，均呕吐涎痰碗许，自汗淋漓，大便泄泻。次日复诊，发热已退十之七八，喘平十之五、六，口中涎沫减去十 之八、九,喉间痰鸣亦减去其半，略进乳食。照原方加量去麻 辛治之。 附片130克，干姜36克，肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑入）， 化橘红6克，茯苓15克，法半夏10克，公丁香6克，甘草10 克。 第二方服后，又各吐涎痰碗许。第三日复诊，已脉静身 凉,喘平泻止，眠食较佳，咳减十之六、七,颜面及指纹青紫均 退。照原方去公丁，加细辛、五味子、黄芪，连进三剂，诸病痊 愈。":`Two cases of critical measles syndrome, supporting yang to save the disease, and one case of favorable syndrome. Tao, 32 years old, was from Jiangxi and lived in Shanghai. He had four sons and one daughter. During the measles epidemic in March 1932, his eldest son, his two sons (aged seven to nine years old), were sent to Suzhou to escape. Unexpectedly, they all developed measles after treatment and died young one after another after taking cold and cooling medicines by mistake. The third and fourth sons, aged two to four, also suffered from measles in Shanghai and were admitted to a Guangdong hospital for treatment. When the illness became serious, the hospital diagnosed him with "pneumonia" and he was delayed to the hospital for examination. The two children were both lying on the cot. Although they were free of measles, their fever persisted. They were wheezing and coughing with phlegm, and their mouths were full of saliva and phlegm flowing out of their mouths at any time. It was unknown what medicine they had taken. It was seen that when yellow fruit water was fed, it still flowed out of the mouth. The face is blue and gloomy (the yin sign is exposed), the forehead is red (deficient yang is leaked), the lips are blue and purple, the fingerprints are blue and black, the pulse is urgent (the sign of extreme cold), the stool is loose (water is cold and the soil is damp, the wood evil is stealing the soil), and the milk and food are not taken in (deficiency and cold in the stomach, the movement is lost). The hospital believed that the patient's condition was serious and there was no other way to do it. After I examined the patient, he was immediately told that the condition was critical and had become a syndrome of three yin and extreme cold, cold phlegm was blocked in the body, true yang was leaking out, and there was a tendency of wind movement or decline. In an emergency, it was necessary to support the yang and suppress the yin, and to warm the cold phlegm. If you vomit cold phlegm after taking it, it is a sign that the disease will be cured. If the fever subsides and the asthma subsides, the crisis can still be turned into peace. If the treatment is delayed or cold and cooling medicines are used, the disease will be in danger and there will be no hope of salvation. Because his two sons had died in infancy, and his third and fourth children were seriously ill again, he was panic-stricken and asked for rescue. He trusted him so much that even though he couldn't afford it, he never complained. Then I prepared Sini Erchen Decoction with cloves, cinnamon, and a little bit of numbing, pungent, and heavier weight, and took it with the two children (because they had the same condition, so they took one dose together). 100 grams of Aconite, 24 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water), 10 grams of Pinellia ternata, 6 grams of Citrus tangerine peel, 15 grams of Poria, 3 grams of Asarum, 6 grams of cloves, 3 grams of Zhima antler, and 10 grams of licorice. After taking this prescription, all patients vomited a bowlful of saliva, sweated profusely, and had diarrhea. After a follow-up visit the next day, the fever had subsided by 70% to 80%, the wheezing had subsided by 50% to 60%, the amount of saliva in the mouth had decreased by 80% to 90%, and the phlegm in the throat had also decreased by half, and he had been on a slightly breastfeeding diet. Follow the original prescription and increase the amount to remove numbness and pungent treatment. 130 grams of Aconite, 36 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 6 grams of tangerine, 15 grams of poria, 10 grams of pinellia, 6 grams of cloves, and 10 grams of licorice. After taking the second prescription, everyone spit out a bowl of phlegm. After a follow-up visit on the third day, the pulse was calm and cool, the asthma was subdued and diarrhea stopped, the patient slept and ate better, the cough decreased by 60% to 70%, and the bruises on the face and fingerprints all subsided. According to the original prescription, remove the phlegm, add asarum, schisandra, and astragalus, and take three doses in a row, and all diseases will be cured.`,"麻疹危证扶阳救逆二例、顺证一例渠之另一女孩，约五岁多,亦继出麻疹":"Two cases of critical measles syndrome were treated with Fuyang and reversal, and one case of normal syndrome. Another girl, about five years old, also developed measles.","麻疹危证扶阳救逆二例、顺证一例渠之另一女孩，约五岁多,亦继出麻疹。初起即发热、涕 清，而加咳嗽，呕吐泄泻，目泪盈眶。拟以桂枝葛根汤加防风、 薄荷。 桂枝10克，杭白芍10克，葛根10克，防风6克，薄荷6 克，甘草6克，生姜10克，大枣2枚。 服上方后麻疹渐出。第二剂去葛根加黄芪16克,服后全 身透达。第三剂黄芪桂枝五物汤，服后疹灰脉静身凉，平安而愈。黄芪15克，桂枝10克，生姜10克，大枣2枚，杭白芍10克。按：陶某五个小孩，长次两子，远避隔离不能幸免，误于寒凉之药而夭亡。三、四两子转“肺炎”而严重，得回阳救逆之剂抢救而全活。一女孩用药适当，两、三剂平淡之药而治愈。以此观之，凡治麻疹一证，立方用药，务须细心.审慎。明朝李念莪《内经知要》注《阴阳应象大论》关于“少火生气”云：“特须善为调剂，世之善用苦寒，好行疏伐者，柜非岐黄之罪人哉。”此为医医之言，须熟记之。":`Two cases of critical measles syndrome were treated with Fuyang, and one case of normal syndrome. Another girl, about five years old, also developed measles. Fever and clear nasal discharge are present at the beginning, followed by cough, vomiting and diarrhea, and tears in the eyes. It is planned to add cinnamon twig and kudzu root decoction with windbreak and mint. 10 grams of cinnamon twig, 10 grams of white peony root, 10 grams of pueraria lobata, 6 grams of fanfeng, 6 grams of mint, 6 grams of licorice, 10 grams of ginger, and 2 jujubes. The measles gradually came out after taking the medicine. In the second dose, remove Pueraria lobata and add 16 grams of Astragalus membranaceus. After taking it, it will penetrate the whole body. After taking the third dose of Astragalus Guizhi Wuwu Decoction, the rash, gray veins and veins were calmed down by calming down, and the symptoms healed safely. 15 grams of astragalus, 10 grams of cassia twig, 10 grams of ginger, 2 jujubes, and 10 grams of white peony root. Note: Tao had five children, two of whom were his eldest son. They were unable to survive in isolation and died young due to the mistake of taking cold medicine. The third and fourth sons were diagnosed with "pneumonia" and became serious. They were rescued by the medicine of Hui Yang and Ji Ni and survived. One girl was cured with appropriate medication and two or three doses of ordinary medicine. From this point of view, whenever you treat a single symptom of measles, you must be careful and cautious when using prescription drugs. In the Ming Dynasty, Li Nian'e's "Yin Yang Ying Xiang Da Lun" annotation in "Yin Yang Ying Xiang Da Lun" said: "You must be good at regulating, making good use of bitter cold, and good at sparing, and you are not a sinner of Qi Huang." This is what the doctor said, and you must memorize it.`,"麻疹危证案 严某，4岁":"Measles critical case case Yan, 4 years old","麻疹危证案 陶某，32岁，住上海":"Measles critical case case Tao, 32 years old, lives in Shanghai","麻疹危证案\\n严某，4岁。出麻疹已六七日，疹出已齐渐灰，但发热不退，舌苔白滑，不渴饮，唇色青紫焦燥而起血壳，脉沉细而紧，大便泄泻，小便赤而长，下午夜间发热尤甚，烦躁不寐，咳嗽痰滞难唾，食物不进，精神缺乏。其证已转危笃，复查所服方剂，始而升提发表，继则养阴清热解毒，以致阴寒之气益甚，逼其真阳外越，故见内真寒而外假热，且有衰脱之势。姑拟白通汤加味治之：\\n附片60g，干姜15g，葱白4茎，肉桂6g：\\n次日复诊：服药后旋即呕吐涎痰盏许，咳嗽已松，夜已能寐二三小时，泄泻次数减少，略进稀粥半杯。视其身热渐退，脉较缓和，唇口流血已止且较润，均为大有转机之象。仍宜扶阳抑阴，以四逆汤加味主之：\\n附片90g，干姜25g，甘草9g，法夏9g，上肉桂6g，化橘红6g。\\n三诊：病状已大松，脉静身凉，夜已熟寐，白苔退去十之八九，唇舌红润，津液满口，食量较增，咳嗽亦止。再以四逆汤加北黄芪、砂仁，连进2剂，诸症痊愈。\\n按：此证舌脉、神色一派阴寒之象，再察“始而升提发表，继则养阴清热解毒”，而病势转重，可以判定阴证。其“唇色青紫焦燥而起血壳”“烦躁不寐”，则属虚阳外越之象，极易误解为阴虚燥热。":`Measles critical case\\nYan, 4 years old. It has been six or seven days since the onset of measles, and the rash has gradually turned gray, but the fever has not subsided, the tongue coating is white and slippery, and I am not thirsty to drink. My lips are blue and purple, scorched and dry with blood crust, my pulse is thick and tight, I have diarrhea, and my urine is red and long. I have fever especially in the afternoon and night. I am irritable and sleepless, cough with phlegm that is difficult to spit, I can't eat, and I'm lacking in energy. His symptoms have turned critical, and he reviewed the prescriptions he took, which showed that they first improved the symptoms, and then nourished the yin, cleared heat, and detoxified, so that the yin-cold qi was more beneficial and forced the true yang to cross the outside. Therefore, he saw true cold inside and false heat outside, and there was a tendency of decline. Modified Guxiu Baitong Decoction treats the condition:\\n60g of Aconite slices, 15g of dried ginger, 4 stalks of scallions, and 6g of cinnamon:\\nRevisited the next day: Immediately after taking the medicine, there was vomiting and a small amount of saliva and phlegm, the cough was loosened, and the frequency of diarrhea was reduced, and half a cup of gruel was added. Judging from the fact that the body heat gradually subsides, the pulse becomes gentler, and the bleeding of the lips and mouth has stopped and becomes moister, these are all signs of improvement. It is still suitable to support yang and suppress yin, and the main method is to use Sini Decoction with the following flavors: 90g of Fu Pian, 25g of dried ginger, 9g of licorice, 9g of faxia, 6g of cinnamon, and 6g of tangerine. \\nThird diagnosis: The symptoms are loose, the pulse is quiet, the body is cool, the patient has slept well at night, the white coating has receded in nine out of ten cases, the lips and tongue are red, the mouth is full of fluid, the food intake has increased, and the cough has stopped. Then add Sini Decoction with Astragalus membranaceus and Amomum villosum, and take 2 doses in a row, and all symptoms will be cured. \\nNote: This syndrome shows that the tongue, pulse, and facial expressions are all yin-cold. If you observe that "it begins with lifting and releasing, and then nourishes yin, clears heat, and detoxifies," if the disease becomes more serious, you can determine the yin syndrome. "Lip color is blue and purple, burnt and dry with blood crusts" and "irritability and insomnia" are symptoms of Yang deficiency and external excess, which can easily be misunderstood as Yin deficiency, dryness and heat.`,"麻疹危证案\\n陶某，32岁，住上海。其三四两子，约2〜4岁，在上海患麻疹，住某医院治疗。两孩均同卧于小床内，麻疹虽免，但发热不退，喘咳痰鸣，满口涎痰随时流出口外，不知曾服何药。见喂入黄果水时，仍从口中外流；颜面青黯（阴象外露），两颧发赤（虚阳外泄），唇色青紫，指纹青黑出二关，脉搏紧急（寒极之象），大便鹫溏（水寒土湿，木邪贼土），乳食不进（胃中虚寒，司运失权）。该院认为病势严重，别无他法，已感束手。余诊视后，即告以病势危笃，已成三阴寒极之证，寒痰内壅，真阳外泄，有风动或衰脱之势，急宜扶阳抑阴，温逐寒痰为主。若服后涌吐寒痰，系病除之兆；如热退喘平，尚可转危为安。遂拟四逆二陈汤加丁香、肉桂，少佐麻辛，分量加重，与两孩同服（因其病情相同，故共服1剂）：\\n附片100g，干姜24g，肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），法夏10g，广皮6g，茯苓15g，细辛3g，公丁香6g，炙麻绒3g，甘草10\\n服后均呕吐涎痰碗许，自汗淋漓，大便泄泻。发热已退十之七八，喘平十之五六，口中涎沫减去十之八九，喉间痰鸣亦减去其半，略进乳食。照原方加量去麻辛治之：\\n附片130g，干姜36g，肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），化红6g，茯苓15g，法夏10g，公丁香6g，甘草10g。\\n第二方服后又各吐涎痰碗许。第三日复诊已脉静身凉，喘平泻止，眠食较佳，咳减十之六七，颜面及指纹青紫均退。照原方去公丁，加细辛、五味、黄便，连进3剂，诸症痊愈。":"Measles critical case\\nTao, 32 years old, lives in Shanghai. His third and fourth sons, about 2 to 4 years old, contracted measles in Shanghai and were admitted to a hospital for treatment. The two children were both lying in the cot. Although they were free of measles, their fever did not go away. They were wheezing and coughing with phlegm, and their mouths were full of saliva and phlegm flowing out of their mouths at any time. I don’t know what medicine they had taken. It is seen that yellow fruit water still flows out of the mouth when feeding; the face is blue and dark (yin is exposed), both cheekbones are red (deficiency and yang are leaking), the lips are blue and purple, the fingerprints are blue and black, the pulse is urgent (the sign of extreme cold), the stool is loose (water is cold and the earth is damp, wood evil invades the earth), and the milk and food are not taken in (deficiency and cold in the stomach, the movement is lost). The hospital believed that the patient was seriously ill and had no other option. After further examination, he was told that the condition was critical and had become a syndrome of three yin and cold extremes, cold phlegm was blocked in the body, true yang was leaking out, and there was a tendency of wind movement or weakness. In an emergency, it was necessary to support the yang and suppress the yin, and to warm the cold phlegm. If you vomit cold phlegm after taking it, it is a sign that the disease will be cured; if the fever subsides and the asthma subsides, the crisis can be turned into peace. Then I prepared Sini Erchen Decoction with cloves, cinnamon, and less Ma Xin to increase the weight and take it with the two children (because they have the same condition, so they take 1 dose in total): 100g of attached tablets, 24g of dried ginger, 10g of cinnamon (pulverized , soaked in water and mixed with water), Faxia 10g, Guangpi 6g, Poria 15g, Asarum 3g, Clove 6g, Zhima 3g, Licorice 10\\nAfter taking it, all patients vomited a bowlful of saliva, sweated, and had diarrhea. The fever has subsided by 78%, the wheezing has subsided by 56%, the saliva in the mouth has decreased by 89%, the phlegm in the throat has also decreased by half, and the milk intake has been slightly reduced. Follow the original recipe and add the following dosage to remove the numbing factor: 130g of Aconite slices, 36g of dried ginger, 10g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix in), 6g of Huahong, 15g of Poria, 10g of Faxia, 6g of cloves, and 10g of licorice. \\nAfter taking the second prescription, everyone spit out a bowl of phlegm. On the third day of follow-up examination, the pulse was quiet and the body was cool, the asthma was subdued and diarrhea had stopped, the patient was sleeping and eating better, the cough was reduced by 67%, and the bruises on the face and fingerprints had subsided. According to the original prescription, remove the male penis, add asarum, Wuwei, and yellow stool, take 3 doses in a row, and all symptoms will be cured.",麻疹发微:"Mild measles",麻疹变证:"measles mutation","麻疹变证案 甘某之女，2岁余":"Measles testimonial case: Gan’s daughter, over 2 years old",'麻疹变证案\\n甘某之女，2岁余。1924年3月出麻疹，发热，涕清咳嗽，目赤多泪；耳指冷，面部隐隐已现红点。因上年冬季曾患慢脾风症，经吴氏治疗，体质尚未复元，故未敢用发表寒凉之剂，乃主以桂枝汤加附子、细辛：\\n桂枝6g，杭芍6g，甘草3g，生姜10g，大枣2枚，附片15g，细辛3g。\\n服1剂麻疹渐出，2剂透齐，3剂渐灰。但微见烦躁，因当时经验不足，竟疑为服温热药后之燥象，即用上方减去辛、附，倍芍药加当归以补阴血，加麦冬而清烦热。\\n次日复诊：服上方后脉反紧急，发热烦乱，喘挣痰鸣，鼻翼扇动，唇色青乌，舌苔白滑，指纹青黑出二关，有欲作惊风之状。此已有阴盛逼阳于外之势，当即以扶阳抑阴之四逆汤加肉桂、茯苓治之：\\n附片24g，干姜10g，甘草5g，上肉桂6g（研末，泡水兑入），茯苓12g，公丁香1.5g。\\n服后旋即风动，手足抽掣，角弓反张，喘挣痰鸣，鼻扇不乳，以药饮之，则涌吐涎沫，泄泻绿粪，颇属危笃。诊其脉象，已较前和缓，身热约退十分之二三。此是药与病相争之兆，亦即“若药不瞑眩，厥疾弗瘳”之瞑眩现象，告其勿疑惧，当即照原方增量主之：\\n附片50g，干姜15g，甘草6g，上肉桂6g（研末，泡水兑入），茯苓12g，公丁1.5g。连夜煎服。\\n次日复诊，见其脉静身凉，已能吮乳，惟尚咳嗽略挣，大便尚泻而色渐转黄，面唇指纹青乌之色已退。照原方再服1剂，泄泻止，喘挣平。复以上方加口芪12g，砂仁6g，去公丁、茯苓，连服5剂，遂得痊愈。\\n原按：此等病症，若认为阳毒热重，以清热解毒之品投之，势必变症危笃"此时虽有识者用温热药以补救之，但如剂量过轻或配伍不当，亦难生效。故应辨别阴阳，分析寒热，随症施治，则可免误治也。':`Measles testimonial case\\nGan’s daughter, more than 2 years old. In March 1924, he developed measles, fever, cough with clear discharge, red eyes and many tears; cold ears and fingers, and faint red spots appeared on his face. Because I suffered from chronic spleen wind in the winter last year, my body has not recovered after Wu's treatment, so I dare not use any cold-cooling agent. Instead, I mainly use Guizhi Decoction with Fuzi and Asarum:\\nGuizhi 6g, Hangshao 6g, licorice 3g, ginger 10g, 2 jujubes, 15g Futian, and 3g Asarum. \\nAfter taking 1 dose, the measles gradually came out, after 2 doses, it cleared up completely, and after 3 doses, it gradually became gray. However, there was a slight irritability. Due to lack of experience at the time, I suspected it was dryness after taking warm medicine. I used the above to subtract the pungent and attached symptoms, added peony and angelica to nourish yin and blood, and added Ophiopogon japonicus to clear away the irritability and heat. \\nRevisit the next day: After taking the medicine, the pulse becomes urgent, fever and irritability, wheezing and phlegm, the nose flaps, the lips are blue and black, the tongue coating is white and slippery, the fingerprints are blue and black, and there is a feeling of convulsion. This has the potential to force yang to the outside, so immediately treat it with the Sini Decoction of supporting yang and suppressing yin, adding cinnamon and poria:\\n24g of Fu Pian, 10g of dried ginger, 5g of licorice, 6g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed in), 12g of Poria, and 1.5g of male clove. \\nImmediately after taking it, there will be wind movement, twitching of hands and feet, opisthotonus, wheezing and phlegm, and nostrils. If you drink the medicine, you will spit out saliva and have diarrhea of ​​green feces, which is quite dangerous. After checking his pulse, he found that it had become gentler than before, and his body heat had subsided by about 20-30%. This is a sign of conflict between the medicine and the disease, that is, the dizziness phenomenon of "if the medicine does not cure the dizziness, the disease will not be cured", tell them not to be afraid, and immediately increase the dosage according to the original prescription:\\n50g of Aopian, 15g of dried ginger, 6g of licorice, 6g of cinnamon (pulverized, soaked in water and mixed in), 12g of Poria, and 1.5g of Ginger. Decoction and take it overnight. \\nAfter a follow-up visit the next day, it was found that his pulse was quiet and his body was cool. He was able to suck milk, but he still coughed a little. His stools continued to have diarrhea and were gradually turning yellow. The blue and black color of his face, lips, and fingerprints had faded. Take another dose according to the original prescription, and the diarrhea stops and the asthma subsides. Add 12g of Qi Qi and 6g of Amomum villosum to the above, remove the fennel and Poria, and take 5 doses in a row, and the condition is cured. \\nOriginal note: For these diseases, if it is believed that the yang poison is severe and the heat is severe, using heat-clearing and detoxifying products will inevitably turn the disease into a critical condition. At this time, although knowledgeable people use warming medicine to remedy the disease, it will be difficult to take effect if the dose is too light or the compatibility is improper. Therefore, Yin and Yang should be distinguished, cold and heat should be analyzed, and treatment should be carried out according to the disease, so as to avoid mistreatment.`,麻疹后湿热下痢:"Diarrhea due to damp heat after measles","麻疹后湿热下痢 王某之女，年五岁，麻疹免后,下痢红白，腹痛里急后重, 不思饮食":"Diarrhea caused by damp heat after measles. Wang's daughter, aged five years old, had red and white diarrhea after being cured of measles, abdominal pain, tenesmus, and no desire to eat.","麻疹后湿热下痢 王某之女，年五岁，麻疹免后,下痢红白，腹痛里急后重, 不思饮食。系麻疹后,湿热阻遏所致,以槟芍顺气汤主之。 杭白芍12克，槟榔片6克，枳壳6克，厚朴6克，木香3 克，前仁6克，大黄6克，甘草3克。 服后，大便畅利三、四次。次日复诊,红白痢已减十之八、 九,仍照上方加减治之。 当归12克，杭白芍12克，前仁6克，莱服子5克，槟榔 片6克，黄芩3克，枳壳3克，甘草3克。 第三诊，利止食增，续以下方连服二剂而愈。 党参12克，北口芪12克，西砂仁3克，当归10克，黑姜 6克，桂圆肉10克。":"Diarrhea due to damp heat after measles Wang's daughter, aged five years old, developed red and white diarrhea after being freed from measles, abdominal pain with severe tenesmus, and no desire to eat. It is caused by the suppression of dampness and heat after measles, and the main treatment is Bin Shao Shun Qi Decoction. 12 grams of white peony root, 6 grams of betel nut slices, 6 grams of Citrus aurantium husk, 6 grams of Magnolia officinalis, 3 grams of Acosta, 6 grams of Qianren, 6 grams of rhubarb, and 3 grams of licorice. After taking it, I had smooth bowel movements three or four times. After a follow-up visit the next day, it was found that 80% or 90% of the redness and whiteness of the dysentery had been reduced, and the patient was still treated as above with addition and subtraction. 12 grams of angelica root, 12 grams of white peony root, 6 grams of Qianren, 5 grams of Laifuzi, 6 grams of betel nut slices, 3 grams of skullcap, 3 grams of Citrus aurantium, and 3 grams of licorice. At the third diagnosis, it was helpful to stop the increase in appetite. Continue to take two doses of the following and the symptoms will be cured. 12 grams of Codonopsis pilosula, 12 grams of Beikou Qi, 3 grams of Amomum villosum, 10 grams of Angelica sinensis, 6 grams of black ginger, and 10 grams of longan meat.","麻疹后湿热下痢王某之子,年五岁，出麻疹后，邪热内伏，阴虚阳燥，发…":"Wang's son, five years old, suffered from dysentery due to damp heat after measles. After measles, he suffered from internal evil heat, yin deficiency and yang dryness, and...","麻疹后湿热下痢王某之子,年五岁，出麻疹后，邪热内伏，阴虚阳燥，发热 八、九日不退，脉息沉数,唇焦舌燥，渴思冷饮，虚烦不寐，大 便不解已五、六日，小便短赤。以温补之剂服之，病势更甚。此 系少阴热化之证，拟以黄连阿胶鸡子黄汤主之。 黄连5克，黄芩6克，杭白芍12克，阿胶6克（烊化兑 入）,鸡子黄1枚（搅化兑入）。 待苓、连、芍三味煎汁，稍冷，兑入阿胶、鸡子黄调匀 而服。 次日再诊，患儿烦止得寐，身热退去十之八、九，唇舌已 回润，再以生脉散加味治之。 米洋参5克，麦冬10克，五味子3克，甘草6克，生地黄 6克，玄参6克。 第三日复诊,患儿脉静身凉,津液满口，二便通利，续以 前方去生地黄、玄参，加北口芪20克、当归10克，补中益气， 养阴生血，连服二剂，食增神健，诸病俱愈。":"The son of Wang, a five-year-old man, suffered from dysentery due to damp heat after measles. After the onset of measles, he had internal pathogenic heat, yin deficiency and yang dryness, and the fever did not go away for eight or nine days. His pulse was heavy and rapid, his lips were burnt and his tongue was dry, he was thirsty for cold drinks, he was tired and insomnia. He had not been able to pass stool for five or six days, and his urine was short and red. Taking it with warming and tonic medicine will make the condition worse. This is a syndrome of Shaoyin heat transformation, and it is planned to be treated with Coptis Lian Ejiao Chicken Zi Huang Decoction. 5 grams of Coptis chinensis, 6 grams of Scutellaria baicalensis, 12 grams of white peony root, 6 grams of donkey-hide gelatin (blended and blended), 1 chicken roe (stirred and blended). Decoction the three flavors of Lingcocos, Lianlian and Shaoyao, let it cool slightly, add donkey hide gelatin and chicken yellow, mix thoroughly and take it. The patient was diagnosed again the next day and found that the child's irritability had stopped and he could sleep well. Eighty or ninety percent of the body heat had subsided, and his lips and tongue had become moisturized. He was treated with Shengmai Powder with added flavor. 5 grams of Panax quinquefolius, 10 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 3 grams of Schisandra chinensis, 6 grams of licorice, 6 grams of Rehmannia glutinosa, and 6 grams of Scrophulariaceae. On the third day of follow-up examination, the child's pulse was quiet and cool, his mouth was full of body fluids, and his bowel movements were laxative. He continued to remove Rehmannia glutinosa and Scrophulariaceae from the front, and added 20 grams of Beikou Qi and 10 grams of Angelica sinensis to invigorate Qi, nourish yin and promote blood. He took two doses in a row, and the food increased his mental health, and all diseases were cured.","麻疹后转“肺炎”":"Measles turned into pneumonia","麻疹后转“肺炎”虚寒重证三例 其一： 罗某之子,年三岁，住昆明如意巷":`Three cases of measles followed by "pneumonia" and severe deficiency and cold syndrome. One: Luo's son, three years old, lives in Ruyi Lane, Kunming.`,"麻疹后转“肺炎”虚寒重证三例 其一： 罗某之子,年三岁，住昆明如意巷。患儿于1939年3月 患麻疹，住某医院治疗。因转变为肺炎，病势严重。该院认为 病势危笃，已感束手,遂出院回家。当延余诊视之，患儿麻疹 虽免，但脉搏沉细而紧,颜面含青黯之色，唇口紫乌而焦燥, 舌苔白滑而厚腻，指纹青紫出二关，大便鹜溏,小便短赤。咳 嗽喘促，声音嘶嘎，午后及夜间发热，食少无神。据以上病情, 已成为太少二阴虚寒重证，寒痰邪阴内壅，阳不足以运行，遂 见以上症状。当即用四逆汤加肉桂、公丁香、法半夏、茯苓以 扶阳抑阴治之。 附片36克，干姜15克，甘草6克，公丁香3克，法半夏 10克，茯苓15克。 次日复诊，据病家自述，服药后，旋即呕吐不少涎痰，大 便泄泻数次。视其发热、咳嗽、喘促等证已减轻十之六、七，且 能熟寐,面唇青黯之色稍退,唇亦较润,仍照原方将附片加为 60克,去丁香,加苍术6克。第三日续诊,据病家云，服药后又 吐涎痰二次,发热已退,小便较长,泄泻亦止，喘促已平，并能 进稀粥。视其面唇青黯已退去十之八、九，唇转红润，白苔已 退其半，小便虽黄而长，神食亦较增，声音已恢复正常，尚微 咳稍喘，以四逆汤加砂仁、法半夏连服二剂。 附片60克，干姜15克，砂仁6克，法半夏10克。 第五日续诊，面色已转红润，舌苔全退，喘咳已愈，再以四逆汤加北口茂16克、潞党参13克、砂仁6克，连服二剂, 食增神健，诸病全瘳。":`Three cases of measles followed by "pneumonia" and severe deficiency and cold syndrome. One: Luo's son, three years old, lives in Ruyi Lane, Kunming. The child contracted measles in March 1939 and was admitted to a hospital for treatment. As he turned into pneumonia, his condition became serious. The hospital believed that the patient was in a critical condition and was at the end of his rope, so he was discharged home. After further examination, it was found that although the child had measles, his pulse was heavy and tight, his face was blue and dark, his lips were purple and burnt, his tongue coating was white, slippery and thick, his fingerprints were blue and purple, his stool was loose, and his urine was short and red. Cough, shortness of breath, hoarse voice, fever in the afternoon and night, little food and lack of energy. According to the above condition, it has become a syndrome of too little two yin deficiency and severe cold. The cold phlegm and evil yin are blocked in the body, and the yang is not enough to circulate, so the above symptoms are seen. Immediately use Sini Decoction with cinnamon, clove, pinellia, and poria to support yang and suppress yin. 36 grams of Aconite, 15 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of licorice, 3 grams of cloves, 10 grams of Pinellia ternata, and 15 grams of Poria. After a follow-up visit the next day, the patient reported that immediately after taking the medicine, he vomited a lot of saliva and had diarrhea several times. If the patient's fever, cough, shortness of breath and other symptoms have been alleviated by 60 to 70%, and he can sleep well, and the blue and dark color of his face and lips have faded slightly, and his lips are moister, he should still follow the original prescription and add 60 grams of Atractylodes, remove the cloves, and add 6 grams of Atractylodes. During the follow-up consultation on the third day, according to the patient, she spit out phlegm twice after taking the medicine, the fever has subsided, the urination is longer, the diarrhea has stopped, the shortness of breath has subsided, and gruel can be eaten. It seems that the blueness on the face and lips has receded eight to nine times, the lips have turned red, and the white coating has receded by half. Although the urine is yellow and long, the appetite has increased, the voice has returned to normal, and there is still a slight cough and wheezing. Take two doses of Sini Decoction with Amomum villosum and Banxia. 60 grams of Fu Feng, 15 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of Amomum villosum, and 10 grams of Pinellia ternata. On the fifth day of the follow-up consultation, the complexion had turned rosy, the tongue coating had completely disappeared, and the asthma and cough had recovered. Then Sini Decoction was added with 16 grams of Beikoumao, 13 grams of Ludang Shen, and 6 grams of Amomum villosum. After taking two doses, the patient was in good health and all diseases were relieved.`,"麻疹后转“肺炎”虚寒重证三例 其三： 杨某，住昆明大绿水河，有一…":'Three cases of measles followed by "pneumonia" and severe deficiency and cold syndrome. The third case: Yang, who lived in Dalvshuihe, Kunming, had one...',"麻疹后转“肺炎”虚寒重证三例 其三： 杨某，住昆明大绿水河，有一女生甫半岁，于1958年春 出麻疹，已灰，忽转“肺炎”，发热喘咳，喉间痰鸣，鼻翼扇动， 面含青象，指纹青紫出二关，大便泻绿水，小便短赤。此系疹 后元阳内虚，寒痰壅闭，肺肾之气不接,清肃不降而成是证， 即以小青龙汤加附子主之。 附片30克，干姜12克，法半夏6克，细辛3克，麻黄3克，五味子1.5克，桂枝尖10克,杭白芍6克，甘草6克。 服后旋即呕吐涎痰盏许。次日复诊，喘咳稍减，发热已退 其半,再以四逆二陈汤加肉桂少佐麻绒、细辛主之。 附片50克，干姜12克，法半夏6克，陈皮6克，茯苓13 克，肉桂20克（研末，泡水兑入），甘草10克，炙麻绒3克，细 辛2.5克。 服后，又吐不少涎痰，喘咳已去十之八、九，鼻扇痰鸣已 止，大便转黄而溏，小便已较长而淡黄，并略进稀粥，颜面指 纹已转红润,仍照原方去麻、辛、陈皮，连服二剂而愈。按：“肺炎”系西医病名，中医则应分为肺热、肺寒或肺燥等证。针对寒热虚实之病情实据，灵活处方治疗。如一见“肺炎”，不辨寒热，动辄以清凉解毒之剂任意消炎，则贻误不浅矣。以上三例，均系体质虚寒，湿痰内盛而成肺炎寒极严重之证，故主以扶阳温化之剂，均奏全功。如系邪热肺燥之炎证，又当以养阴清肺、生津润燥之剂治之，方能收效。":`Three cases of measles followed by "pneumonia" and severe deficiency and cold syndrome. The third case: Yang, who lived in Dalvshuihe, Kunming, had a girl who was just half a year old. She developed measles in the spring of 1958 and was already gray. She suddenly turned to "pneumonia", with fever and wheezing and cough, phlegm in the throat, flaring nose, green face, fingerprints with blue and purple eyes, green watery stools, and short red urine. This syndrome is caused by internal deficiency of yang after the rash, cold phlegm blocking the lungs and kidneys, and Qi in the lungs and kidneys not connecting, and the Qi in the lungs and kidneys cannot be reduced. This is treated with Xiaoqinglong Decoction plus Fuzi. 30 grams of Aconite, 12 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of Pinellia, 3 grams of Asarum, 3 grams of Ephedra, 1.5 grams of Schisandra chinensis, 10 grams of Guizhijian, 6 grams of Hangzhou white peony root, and 6 grams of licorice. Immediately after taking the medicine, there was vomiting and a small amount of saliva and phlegm. After a follow-up visit the next day, the wheezing and coughing subsided slightly, and the fever had subsided by half. The patient was treated with Sini Erchen decoction plus cinnamon, ma rong, and asarum. 50 grams of cinnamon, 12 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of pinellia, 6 grams of tangerine peel, 13 grams of poria, 20 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10 grams of licorice, 3 grams of rhizome, and 2.5 grams of asarum. After taking it, I vomited a lot of phlegm again, my wheezing and coughing were gone for eight or nine times out of ten, the phlegm ringing in my nose had stopped, my stool became yellow and loose, my urine was longer and light yellow, and some gruel was included, and my facial fingerprints turned ruddy. I still followed the original prescription to remove the numbness, pungent, and dried tangerine peel, and recovered after taking two doses. Note: "Pneumonia" is the name of the disease in Western medicine. In traditional Chinese medicine, it should be divided into syndromes such as lung heat, lung cold or dryness of the lung. According to the actual evidence of the condition of cold, heat, deficiency and excess, flexible prescription treatment is provided. If you don't distinguish between cold and heat when you see "pneumonia", and you always use cooling and detoxifying agents to reduce inflammation at will, you will make a lot of mistakes. The above three cases were all caused by severe cold syndrome caused by deficiency and cold in the body and excess of dampness and phlegm. Therefore, they mainly used agents that strengthened the yang and warmed them, and they all worked perfectly. If it is an inflammatory syndrome caused by evil heat and dryness of the lung, it should be treated with agents that nourish yin, clear the lungs, promote body fluids and moisturize the dryness, in order to be effective.`,"麻疹后转“肺炎”虚寒重证三例 其二： 朱某之女,年五岁，住昆明市晓东街":`Three cases of measles followed by "pneumonia" and severe deficiency and cold syndrome. The second case: Zhu's daughter, five years old, lives in Xiaodong Street, Kunming City`,'麻疹后转“肺炎”虚寒重证三例 其二： 朱某之女,年五岁，住昆明市晓东街。于1939年春出麻 疹,住某医院诊治,麻疹免后,转为“肺炎",病势沉重,遂出院 回家。延余诊视，见其脉来沉弱，面色青黯,唇口淡红而焦，舌 苔白厚而燥,不渴饮,夜发潮热,形神瘦弱，咳嗽气短而喘促, 腹痛食少。据以上病情,属于素禀不足，麻疹免后，正虚阳弱， 寒湿内伏上逆于肺，阳不足以运行所致。法当温中扶阳，开提 肺气,化痰止咳，以四逆二陈汤加味主之。 附片50克，干姜15克，法半夏10克，陈皮6克，茯苓12 克，肉桂10克（研末，泡水兑入），砂仁6克，细辛3克，五味 2.5克，甘草6克。 次日复诊，喘咳已减轻，唇舌较润，面色青黯稍退,饮食 略增，夜热已退，照原方再服一剂。第三日续诊，喘咳止,精神 饮食较增,白苔退去十之八、九,唇舌已转红润,颜色青黯已 退十之七、八,续以四逆汤加砂仁、肉桂、茯苓连进三剂，津液 满口，食增神健,诸病痊愈。 附片50克，干姜15克，肉桂6克（研末，泡水兑入），砂 仁6克，茯苓12克，甘草6克。':`Three cases of measles followed by "pneumonia" and severe deficiency and cold syndrome. Second: Zhu's daughter, five years old, lives in Xiaodong Street, Kunming City. In the spring of 1939, he developed measles and was admitted to a hospital for treatment. After the measles was cured, he developed pneumonia and became seriously ill, so he was discharged and returned home. After further examination, it was found that his pulse was weak and weak, his complexion was blue and gloomy, his lips were light red and burnt, his tongue coating was white and thick and dry, he was not thirsty to drink, he had hot flashes at night, he was thin physically and mentally, he had cough, shortness of breath and shortness of breath, and he had abdominal pain and little food. According to the above condition, it is caused by insufficient natural endowment, post-measles recovery, weak righteousness and weak yang, internal cold and dampness lying in opposition to the lungs, and insufficient yang movement. The method is to warm the middle and support yang, open up lung qi, resolve phlegm and relieve cough. The main method is to use Sini Erchen Decoction with flavor. 50 grams of Aconite slices, 15 grams of dried ginger, 10 grams of Pinellia ternata, 6 grams of tangerine peel, 12 grams of Poria, 10 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 6 grams of amomum villosum, 3 grams of asarum, 2.5 grams of five spices, and 6 grams of licorice. After a follow-up visit the next day, the wheezing and coughing were relieved, the lips and tongue were moister, the pale complexion had subsided slightly, the diet was slightly increased, and the night fever had subsided, so he took another dose according to the original prescription. On the third day of follow-up examination, the asthma and cough stopped, the energy level increased, the white coating receded 80% to 90%, the lips and tongue had turned red, and the blue color had faded 70% to 80%. I continued to take Sini Decoction with amomum villosum, cinnamon, and poria cocos for three doses. The mouth was full of body fluids, the food improved the spirit, and all diseases were cured. 50 grams of Aconite, 15 grams of dried ginger, 6 grams of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 6 grams of Amomum villosum, 12 grams of Poria, and 6 grams of licorice.`,麻疹后邪热灼肺:"Evil heat burning the lungs after measles","麻疹后邪热灼肺 王某之男孩,年三岁，出麻疹免后，身热不退，喘咳痰…":"Evil heat burns the lungs after measles. Wang, a three-year-old boy, suffered from measles and persistent fever, wheezing and coughing up phlegm...","麻疹后邪热灼肺 王某之男孩,年三岁，出麻疹免后，身热不退，喘咳痰滞， 唇焦，舌苔白厚而燥，指纹紫红，脉洪数，壮热烦渴，小便短 赤，鼻干，目多勝。此系疹后真阴内虚，邪热灼肺，津枯液燥， 以人参白虎汤加味主之。 米洋参5克，生石膏12克，知母10克，甘草6克，麦冬 10克，川贝母3克，五味子5克，粳米一撮。 次日复诊,患儿脉静身凉,烦渴喘咳均减，以生脉散加味 治之。 米洋参6克，麦冬12克，五味子2.5克，甘草3克，生地 黄10克，川贝母5克，杭白芍6克。 第三日复诊，津液满口，喘咳已平，食量较佳，再以黄芪 20克、当归10克、生地黄6克、党参10克、桂圆肉10克、炙 甘草3克,调补气血之剂，连服二剂而愈。":"Evil heat burning the lungs after measles Wang, a three-year-old boy, suffered from persistent fever after measles, wheezing and coughing with stagnant phlegm, burnt lips, thick white and dry tongue coating, purple-red fingerprints, rapid and rapid pulse, strong heat and polydipsia, short red urine, dry nose, and excessive eyesight. This is due to internal deficiency of true yin after the rash, pathogenic heat burning the lungs, dry body fluid, and the main treatment is the flavored Ginseng Baihu Decoction. 5 grams of American ginseng, 12 grams of gypsum, 10 grams of Anemarrhena, 6 grams of licorice, 10 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 3 grams of Fritillaria fritillary, 5 grams of Schisandra chinensis, and a pinch of japonica rice. After a follow-up visit the next day, the child's pulse was quiet and his body was cool, and his polydipsia, wheezing and cough were all reduced. He was treated with Shengmai Powder. 6 grams of Panax quinquefolius, 12 grams of Ophiopogon japonicus, 2.5 grams of Schisandra chinensis, 3 grams of licorice, 10 grams of Rehmannia glutinosa, 5 grams of Fritillaria fritillary, and 6 grams of white peony root. On the third day of follow-up consultation, the mouth was full of body fluids, the wheezing and coughing had subsided, and the food intake was better. Then he took 20 grams of astragalus, 10 grams of angelica root, 6 grams of raw rehmannia root, 10 grams of Codonopsis pilosula, 10 grams of longan meat, and 3 grams of licorice to regulate qi and blood. He was cured after taking two doses.","麻疹期饮食起居调护与用药禁忌。":"Diet, daily care, and medication taboos during the measles period.","麻疹治验二则 其一: 李某之长子九岁，次子七岁，住云南省禄丰县南…":"Two experiences on measles treatment. One: Li's eldest son is nine years old and his second son is seven years old. They live in the south of Lufeng County, Yunnan Province...","麻疹治验二则 其一: 李某之长子九岁，次子七岁，住云南省禄丰县南城外，于 1922年3月同患麻疹。初起发热二日，涕清咳嗽,耳指冷，目 微赤，多泪，面上隐隐现红疹，以桂枝汤加葛根、防风、薄荷、 升麻，两子同服。 桂枝15克，杭白芍15克，葛根12克，防风13克，薄荷6 克，甘草6克，升麻6克，生姜24克，大枣4枚。 服一剂麻疹渐出而红润，继则去葛根、升麻，加广皮、法 半夏、细辛，仍同服。服后,疹即透达渐灰，脉静身凉。再服黄芪建中汤一剂，即告痊愈。 黄芪30克，桂枝15克，杭芍15克，甘草6克，生姜30 克，大枣5枚，饴糖30克。 （本案两孩病状相同，故二人同服一剂，所用药量稍重， 若分服则当减轻使用。）":"Two experiences on the treatment of measles. One: Li's eldest son was nine years old, and his second son was seven years old. They lived outside Nancheng, Lufeng County, Yunnan Province. They both suffered from measles in March 1922. Fever started for two days, with clear discharge and cough, cold ears and fingers, slightly red eyes, excessive tears, and a faint rash on the face. Take Guizhi Decoction plus kudzu root, sapsroot, peppermint, and cohosh. Take the two pills together. 15 grams of cinnamon twig, 15 grams of white peony root, 12 grams of kudzu root, 13 grams of parsnips, 6 grams of mint, 6 grams of licorice, 6 grams of cohosh, 24 grams of ginger, and 4 jujubes. After taking one dose, the measles will gradually appear and become rosy, then remove Pueraria lobata and Cimicifuga, add Guangpi, Banxia, ​​and Asarum, and still take the same medicine. After taking it, the rash becomes clear and gradually becomes gray, the pulse is quiet and the body is cool. Take another dose of Huangqi Jianzhong Decoction and you will be cured. 30 grams of astragalus, 15 grams of cassia twig, 15 grams of peony root, 6 grams of licorice, 30 grams of ginger, 5 jujubes, and 30 grams of caramel. (In this case, the symptoms of the two children were the same, so they both took one dose at the same time. The dose used was slightly heavier. If they were given separately, the dosage should be lighter.)","麻疹治验二则 其二： 陈某之子，二岁，住云南省禄丰县南城外":"Two experiences on measles treatment. Second: Chen’s son, two years old, lives outside Nancheng, Lufeng County, Yunnan Province.","麻疹治验二则 其二： 陈某之子，二岁，住云南省禄丰县南城外。患儿于1922 年3月出麻疹，已发热四日，头面隐隐现红疹，色淡红不鲜， 兼见昏迷咳嗽，大便泄泻。因其体弱未敢过于表凉，乃与麻辛 附子汤加二陈汤及生姜以温经解表，辅正除邪而止咳泻。 附片24克，麻黄5克，细辛3克，广陈皮6克，法半夏6 克，甘草3克，生姜10克。 服后，疹渐出，色已较红润，但仍发迷无神，继以白通 汤一剂。 附片30克，干姜13克，葱白4茎。 服后疹即出透，身热渐退，仍见咳嗽。再照上方去葱白加 细辛3克，法半夏6克，化红6克，甘草6克。服后，麻疹渐 灰,脉静身凉,神识清爽，顺利痊愈。按：以上患儿三人，均出麻疹，未经误治，服药后，遂顺利痊愈。倘恣意寒凉或任施表散，焉得不变证而促其夭折乎！":"Two experiences in treating measles. Second: Chen’s son, two years old, lives outside Nancheng, Lufeng County, Yunnan Province. The child developed measles in March 1922 and had been feverish for four days. A faint rash appeared on his head and face, which was light red in color and not fresh. He also suffered from coma, cough, and diarrhea. Because he is weak and does not dare to cool the surface too much, he adds Ma Xin Fuzi Decoction, Erchen Decoction and ginger to warm the meridians and relieve the surface, assist in correcting the disease and eliminate evil, and relieve cough and diarrhea. 24 grams of Futian, 5 grams of ephedra, 3 grams of Asarum, 6 grams of Citrus tangerine peel, 6 grams of Pinellia ternata, 3 grams of licorice, and 10 grams of ginger. After taking it, the rash gradually appeared and became more rosy, but still dizzy and listless, so I took a dose of Baitong Decoction. 30 grams of attached slices, 13 grams of dried ginger, and 4 white stalks of scallions. The rash breaks out immediately after taking it, the body heat gradually subsides, and cough is still seen. Then remove the white scallions and add 3 grams of asarum, 6 grams of pinellia, 6 grams of red pepper, and 6 grams of licorice. After taking it, the measles gradually turned gray, my pulse was quiet and my body was cool, my consciousness was refreshed, and I recovered smoothly. Note: The above three children all had measles. They were not treated incorrectly and recovered smoothly after taking medicine. If you indulge in cold or cold medicine or give it external powder, how can you get the same evidence and promote its premature death?",麻疹溯源:"Measles traceability","麻疹病因病机与历代医家论述述要。":"The etiology and pathogenesis of measles and the summary of discussions by doctors of past dynasties.","麻疹误服表凉药转阴证 甘某之子，三岁，姚安人，住昆明市土主庙街巷内":"Measles turned yin syndrome after accidentally taking cool medicine. Gan's son, three years old, from Yao'an, lives in Tuzhumiao Street, Kunming City","麻疹误服表凉药转阴证 甘某之子，三岁，姚安人，住昆明市土主庙街巷内。患儿 于1924年3月出麻疹，延余诊治。据其父云，初时发热咳嗽, 请某医诊治,服升提表散而佐清凉之药二剂后，麻疹隐隐现 点，色象不鲜,发热已五六日，尚未出透。余诊视之，见其昏迷 无神（少阴证但欲寐之病情）。发热已五、六日，麻疹尚未出 透,若再迁延,势必转危，即以白通汤一剂。 附片60克，干姜15克，葱白4茎（连须根）。 服后，疹已出透而色转红活,再剂疹渐灰，脉静身凉,食 增神健，霍然而愈。按：体弱发迷无神，疹出性慢，色象不鲜，服白通汤一、二剂，即能使疹子出齐，平安而愈。此种治法,在麻疹方书上，虽不易见，但麻疹既不得发越外出而现阴盛阳表之象，投以白通汤扶助心肾之阳，故疗效甚速。倘再误施寒凉，则正愈虚而阳愈弱，无力托毒外出，反而内攻，必致衰脱。故无论疹麻痘疹，一旦病势沉重，务须体会《内经•阴阳应象大论》“治病必求其本”之精神，认真辨别阴阳，不可固守一法，症现阴象，必须救阳，症现阳象，必须救阴，方有挽回之望。":`Measles turned yin syndrome after mistakenly taking cool medicine. Gan's son, three years old, was from Yao'an and lived in Tuzhumiao Street, Kunming City. The child developed measles in March 1924 and was delayed in diagnosis and treatment. According to his father, he had a fever and cough at the beginning. He asked a doctor for diagnosis and treatment. After taking two doses of Shengtibiao Powder combined with cooling medicine, the measles appeared faintly. I examined him and found that he was comatose and unconscious (Shaoyin syndrome, in which he is sleepy but unable to sleep). The fever has been present for five or six days, but the measles has not yet broken out. If it persists any longer, the disease will definitely turn critical, so take a dose of Baitong Decoction. 60 grams of attached slices, 15 grams of dried ginger, and 4 white stalks of scallion (including fibrous roots). After taking it, the rash has appeared and turned red and active. After taking another dose, the rash gradually turned gray, the pulse was still and the body was cool. After eating, the spirit and health were improved, and the symptoms were cured. Note: If the patient is weak, confused and lacks energy, the rash appears slowly and the color is not fresh, taking one or two doses of Baitong Decoction can make the rash appear uniformly and heal safely. Although this kind of treatment method is not easy to see in the measles prescription book, the measles cannot spread out and show signs of yin and yang. Baitong decoction is used to support the yang of the heart and kidneys, so the curative effect is very fast. If cold and cool are applied by mistake again, the positive will become more deficient and the yang will become weaker, unable to support the poison from going out. Instead, it will attack internally, which will inevitably lead to degeneration. Therefore, no matter it is measles, measles, or rash, once the disease is serious, we must understand the spirit of "Treatment must seek its root" in "Nei Jing·Yin and Yang Ying Xiang Da Lun", carefully distinguish yin and yang, and do not stick to one method. If the symptoms appear yin, the yang must be rescued, and if the symptoms appear yang, the yin must be rescued, in order to have any hope of recovery.`,"麻疹诸案力主以透为顺，见疹陷色暗、面白肢凉者，即断为寒遏，径投麻附细辛、四逆辈温阳托透，与世俗专事寒凉者迥异。春温案则详析新感伏气之辨，透邪存津并行不悖。":"In all cases of measles, it is recommended to use penetration as a smooth treatment. If the rash is dark in color and the face is white and the limbs are cold, it should be diagnosed as cold and restrained. Directly treat hemp with asarum and four negative generations of warming and yang to support penetration, which is very different from those who specialize in cold and cool in the world. Chunwen Case analyzes in detail the differentiation of new feelings and subdued qi, and it is consistent to eliminate evil and store fluid.","麻疹转肺炎案 朱女，5岁，住昆明市":"Measles-to-pneumonia case: Zhu daughter, 5 years old, living in Kunming","麻疹转肺炎案 杨女，岀生甫半岁，住昆明大绿水河":"Case of Measles Converting to Pneumonia: Ms. Yang, just half a year old, lives in Dalvshuihe, Kunming","麻疹转肺炎案\\n朱女，5岁，住昆明市。于1939年春出麻疹，住某医院诊治，麻疹免后，转为“肺炎”，病势沉重，遂出院回家。延余诊视，见其脉来沉弱，面色青黯，唇口淡红而焦，舌苔白厚而燥，	不渴饮，夜发潮热，形神瘦弱，咳嗽气短而喘促，腹痛食少。据以上病情，属于素禀不足，麻疹免后，正虚阳弱，寒湿内伏上逆于肺，阳不足以运行所致。法当温中扶阳，开提肺气，化痰止咳。以四逆二陈汤加味主之\\n附片50g，干姜I5g，法夏10g，陈皮6g，茯苓12g，肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），砂仁6g，细辛3g，五味2.5g，甘草6g，\\n次日复诊：喘咳已减轻，唇舌较润，面色青黯稍退，饮食略增，夜热已退，照原方再服1剂。\\n第三日续诊：喘咳止，精神饮食较增，白苔退去十之八九，唇舌已转红润，颜色青黯已退十之七八。续以四逆汤加砂仁、肉桂、茯苓，连进3剂，津液满口，食增神健，诸症痊愈。":"Measles-to-pneumonia case\\nNv Zhu, 5 years old, lives in Kunming. He developed measles in the spring of 1939 and was admitted to a hospital for treatment. After the measles was cured, he developed pneumonia and became seriously ill, so he was discharged and returned home. After further examination, it was found that his pulse was weak and weak, his complexion was blue and gloomy, his lips were light red and burnt, his tongue coating was white and thick and dry, he was not thirsty to drink, he had hot flashes at night, he was thin physically and mentally, he had cough, shortness of breath and shortness of breath, and abdominal pain and little food. According to the above condition, it is caused by insufficient natural endowment, post-measles recovery, weak righteousness and weak yang, internal cold and dampness lying in opposition to the lungs, and insufficient yang movement. The method is used to warm the middle and support yang, open and lift lung qi, resolve phlegm and relieve cough. Use Sini Erchen Decoction to flavor it.\\n50g of Fengzi, 5g of dry ginger, 10g of faxia, 6g of tangerine peel, 12g of poria, 10g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 6g of amomum villosum. , asarum 3g, Wuwei 2.5g, licorice 6g, \\nRevisited the next day: the wheezing and coughing have been relieved, the lips and tongue are moist, the pale complexion has subsided slightly, the diet has increased slightly, the night fever has subsided, take another dose according to the original prescription. \\nFollow-up consultation on the third day: the wheezing and coughing have stopped, the spirit and diet have increased, the white coating has receded in nine out of ten cases, the lips and tongue have turned ruddy, and the blue and dark color has receded in nine out of ten cases. Continue to take Sini Decoction with Amomum villosum, cinnamon, and Poria cocos for 3 doses. The mouth will be filled with body fluids, the mind will be strengthened after eating, and all symptoms will be cured.","麻疹转肺炎案\\n杨女，岀生甫半岁，住昆明大绿水河。1958年春出麻疹，已灰，忽转“肺炎”，发热喘咳，喉间痰鸣，鼻翼扇动，面含青象，指纹青紫出二关，大便泻绿水，小便短赤。此系疹后元阳内虚，寒痰壅闭，肺肾之气不接，清肃不降而成是证即以小青龙汤加附子主之：\\n附片30g，干姜12g，法夏6g，细辛3g，麻黄3g，五味子1.5g，桂尖10g，杭芍6g，甘草6g。\\n服后旋即呕吐涎痰盏许。\\n次日复诊：喘咳稍减，发热已退其半。再以四逆二陈汤加肉桂少佐麻绒、细辛主之：\\n附片50g，干姜12g，法夏6g，陈皮6g，茯苓13g，肉桂20g（研末，泡水兑入），甘草10g，炙麻绒3g，细辛2.5g。\\n服后又吐不少涎痰，喘咳已去十之八、九，鼻扇、痰鸣已止，大便转黄而溏，小便已较长而淡黄，并略进稀粥，颜面指纹已转红润。仍照原方去麻辛、陈皮，连服2剂而愈。\\n原按：“肺炎”系西医病名，中医则应分为肺热、肺寒或肺燥等证。针对寒热虚实之病情实据，灵活处方治疗。如一见“肺炎”，不辨寒热，动辄以清凉解毒之剂任意消炎，则贻误不浅矣。以上3例，均系体质虚寒，湿痰内盛而成肺炎寒极严重之证，故主以扶阳温化之剂，均奏全功。如系邪热肺燥之炎证，又当以养阴清肺生津润燥之剂治之，方能收效。":`Measles-to-Pneumonia Case\\nNv Yang was just half a year old and lived in Dalushuihe, Kunming. In the spring of 1958, measles appeared, which turned gray, and suddenly turned into pneumonia. She had fever, wheezing and coughing, phlegm in the throat, flaring nose, a green face, blue and purple fingerprints, green watery stools, and short red urine. This syndrome is caused by internal deficiency of yang after the rash, cold phlegm blockage, lack of connection of Qi in the lungs and kidneys, and inability to reduce the purification. This syndrome is treated with Xiaoqinglong Decoction plus Aconite: \\nAconite 30g, dried ginger 12g, farsia 6g, asarum 3g, ephedra 3g, Schisandra chinensis 1.5g, Guijian 10g, Hangshao 6g, licorice 6g. \\nI immediately vomited and spit a lot of phlegm after taking it. \\nRevisited the next day: the wheezing and coughing subsided slightly, and the fever was reduced by half. Then add Sini Erchen Decoction with cinnamon, basil, asarum, and asarum: 50g of Fu slices, 12g of dried ginger, 6g of faxia, 6g of tangerine peel, 13g of poria, 20g of cinnamon (grind into powder, soak in water and mix), 10g of licorice, 3g of licorice, 3g of asarum, and 2.5g of asarum. \\nAfter taking it, I vomited a lot of saliva and phlegm, my wheezing and coughing have gone away eight or nine times out of ten, my nose and phlegm have stopped, my stool has turned yellow and loose, my urine has become longer and light yellow, and there is a little gruel, and my face and fingerprints have turned ruddy. Follow the original prescription to remove the spicy and dried tangerine peel, and heal after taking 2 doses. \\nOriginal note: "Pneumonia" is the name of the disease in Western medicine. In traditional Chinese medicine, it should be divided into syndromes such as lung heat, lung cold, or lung dryness. According to the actual evidence of the condition of cold, heat, deficiency and excess, flexible prescription treatment is provided. If you don't distinguish between cold and heat when you see "pneumonia", and you always use cooling and detoxifying agents to reduce inflammation at will, you will make a lot of mistakes. The above 3 cases were all caused by severe cold syndrome caused by weak and cold constitution and excessive accumulation of dampness and phlegm. Therefore, they were mainly treated with agents that strengthened the yang and warmed them, which worked perfectly. If it is an inflammatory syndrome caused by evil heat and dryness of the lung, it should be treated with an agent that nourishes yin, clears the lungs, promotes body fluid and moisturizes the dryness, to achieve effective results.`,"麻疹过表变证补救 郑某之女，三岁，住四川会理县鹿厂观音桥":"Remedy for Measles Excessive Syndrome Zheng’s daughter, three years old, lives in Guanyin Bridge, Luchang, Huili County, Sichuan","麻疹过表变证补救 郑某之女，三岁，住四川会理县鹿厂观音桥。患儿于1913 年3月出疹，经某医诊治，服发表药三剂后，麻疹隐隐欲出未 出，发热嗜卧无神，两腮下忽而肿硬。延余诊视，认为服表药 过多，有伤气血，疹毒不得发越,遂凝结于腮下作肿。即以当 归补血汤合升麻葛根汤稍加薄荷服之。 北口芪24克，当归24克，升麻5克，杭白芍10克，葛根 6克，薄荷3克，甘草3克。 次日复诊，其疹已透出，色转红润，腮肿全消。照原方再 服一付后，全身疹已出齐，脉静身凉。继服黄芪建中汤二剂 调补而愈。按:此女体质较单弱，虽服表散之药较多，但幸未服寒凉之剂，故用大补气血，稍佐升提之岛，亦收显效。倘再误施表凉，则后患不堪设想。此后余诊治麻疹一症，均未敢过于表散，亦未敢骤施苦寒清凉与攻下之剂，而切实掌握辨证论治之精神，无不立见奇效。":"Remedy for Measles Excessive Syndrome: Zheng’s daughter, three years old, lives in Guanyin Bridge, Luchang, Huili County, Sichuan. The child developed a rash in March 1913. After being diagnosed and treated by a doctor, after taking three doses of the medicine, the measles appeared vague and lingering, with fever, sleepiness, and sudden swelling and hardness under the cheeks. After further examination, it was believed that taking too much topical medicine would damage the qi and blood, and the rash poison would not become more severe, so it condensed under the cheek and caused swelling. That is, take Angelicae Buxue Decoction and Cimicifuga Puerariae Decoction with a little mint. 24 grams of Beikou Qi, 24 grams of Angelica sinensis, 5 grams of Cimicifuga, 10 grams of white peony root, 6 grams of Pueraria lobata, 3 grams of mint, and 3 grams of licorice. After a follow-up visit the next day, the rash was revealed, the color turned rosy, and the swelling on the cheeks had completely disappeared. After taking another dose according to the original prescription, the rash appeared all over the body, the pulse was quiet and the body was cold. Then take two doses of Huangqi Jianzhong Decoction to replenish and heal the condition. Note: This woman's constitution is relatively weak. Although she took a lot of external powder medicine, she luckily did not take any cold or cooling medicine. Therefore, she used a large amount of qi and blood supplement, and a little bit of lifting island, and the effect was obvious. If you apply cold to the outside by mistake again, the consequences will be unimaginable. Since then, in the rest of the diagnosis and treatment of measles, I have not dared to overdo the superficial dispersion, nor have I dared to suddenly apply bitter cold and cooling agents, but I have truly grasped the spirit of syndrome differentiation and treatment, and all have achieved miraculous results immediately.","黄芪30g，党参20g，白术20g，茯苓25g，当归15g，丹参20g，赤芍15g，蒲公英25g，白花蛇舌草25g":"Astragalus 30g, Codonopsis pilosula 20g, Atractylodes 20g, Poria cocos 25g, Angelica 15g, Salvia miltiorrhiza 20g, Red peony root 15g, Dandelion 25g, Hedyotis diffusa 25g","黑豆、绿豆、赤小豆各30g，淡豆豉10g，生甘草6g":"30g each of black beans, mung beans and adzuki beans, 10g light tempeh, 6g raw licorice","鼻衄案 李某，14岁":"Epistaxis case Li, 14 years old","鼻衄案\\n李某，14岁。素患鼻衄，无他痛苦，故未用药调理。某日感客邪，身热恶寒，喜冷饮，脉浮细而数，主以麻杏石甘汤一剂霍然。异日外出，适值阴雨天寒，又复感冒而病，发热恶寒，头昏疼，肢体酸痛，不渴饮，脉反沉细而弱，主以麻黄细辛附子汤加桂尖、生姜一剂，服后汗出热退。次晨忽又鼻衄不止，用物塞鼻孔则血由口中溢出，似有不可止之状。头晕，腹痛，面色淡而无华，形弱神疲。复诊其脉迟缓而弱。此乃气血素亏，阴阳不相为守也。血虚散漫妄行，气虚则无力统摄血液，易致离经外溢。表邪虽解，气血尚虚，主以四逆当归补血汤：\\n附片50g，炮黑姜15g，砂仁6g，大枣3枚（烧黑存性），口芪15g，当归15g。\\n1剂衄血立止，再剂霍然。是夜因大便用力，起身时忽而气喘咬牙，昏厥欲绝，唇青，面色灰白，脉细迟无力。扶之使卧稍定，乃以四逆汤加上肉桂治之，连进4剂而痊。\\n按：此案先是身热恶寒，喜冷饮，判为表寒里热，主以麻杏石甘汤一剂霍然；继则发热恶寒，肢体酸痛，脉反沉细而弱，判为太少两感，主以麻黄细辛附子汤，服后汗出热退。两次虽有里热、阳虚不同表现，但一直都未离表证的处理，亦即“把好太阳关”之义。\\n表证解除后，所现鼻衄纯属里虚，用四逆汤合当归补血汤，扶阳兼顾气血。":`Epistaxis case\\nLi, 14 years old. I had always suffered from epistaxis and had no other pain, so I did not take any medication to treat it. One day, I felt a guest's evil spirit, had body heat and aversion to cold, liked cold drinks, and had a floating, thin and rapid pulse. I took a dose of Maxing Shigan Decoction. I went out the next day, it was rainy and cold, and I got sick again due to cold, fever, aversion to cold, dizziness and pain, sore limbs, no thirst for water, and a heavy and thin pulse. Mainly take Ephedra Asarum Fuzi Decoction plus a dose of cinnamon tip and ginger. After taking it, the fever will subside with sweating. The next morning, he suddenly had epistaxis that wouldn't stop. If he stuffed his nostrils with something, blood would flow out of his mouth, which seemed to be unstoppable. Dizziness, abdominal pain, pale complexion, physical weakness and mental fatigue. On further examination, his pulse was slow and weak. This is due to the deficiency of qi and blood elements, and the yin and yang do not maintain each other. Blood deficiency leads to loose and errant movement, while Qi deficiency makes it impossible to control the blood, which can easily cause menstrual leakage and overflow. Although the external evil has been resolved, the qi and blood are still deficient. The main treatment is Sini Danggui Buxue Decoction: \\n50g of Fu Pian, 15g of Paohei Jiang, 6g of Amomum villosum, 3 jujubes (burned black), 15g of Qi Qi, and 15g of Angelica sinensis. \\nOne dose will stop the bleeding immediately, and another dose will cause sudden pain. That night, due to straining to defecate, he suddenly gasped and gritted his teeth when he stood up, fainted, had blue lips, pale complexion, and a thready, slow and weak pulse. After helping the patient to lie still, he treated it with Sini decoction plus cinnamon. He was cured after taking 4 doses in a row. \\nNote: This case first developed body heat and aversion to cold, and a liking for cold drinks. It was judged that the patient was cold on the outside and hot on the inside. He was given a dose of Maxing Shigan Decoction for Huoran. Then he developed fever and aversion to cold, sore limbs, and a thin and weak pulse. He was judged to have two senses of too little. He was given Ephedra Asarum and Fuzi Decoction. After taking it, he sweated and the fever subsided. Although there were different manifestations of internal heat and yang deficiency in the two times, the treatment of external symptoms has always been the same, which means "keeping the sun closed". \\nAfter the superficial syndrome is resolved, the epistaxis is purely due to internal deficiency. Sini Decoction and Danggui Buxue Decoction can be used to support Yang and take into account Qi and blood.`,"鼻衄欲脱案 秦某，男，64岁":"Case of epistaxis and trying to escape Qin, male, 64 years old","鼻衄欲脱案\\n秦某，男，64岁。素多痰湿，咳嗽多年。昨因咳嗽气急上涌，忽然鼻血不止，注射止血针剂不效，延吴氏急诊：面色惨淡，鼻衄不止，冷汗淋漓，沉迷无神，气息低弱呈奄奄一息状。舌淡夹青而少血色，脉芤虚欲散，二三至而一止。辨为气虚不能摄血，阳虚不能守阴，复因咳嗽挣破血络而衄。病势颇危，有阳气外脱之势。急宜扶阳收纳，若能血汗均止，尚有生机，以参附汤加味急救：\\n附子30g，人参10g，炮姜6g，甘草3g，大枣2枚（烧黑存性）。\\n服1剂则效，衄减，神气转佳；再剂血汗均已得止。原方加黄芪24g，附子增为60g，连服2剂，唇舌色已红润，脉来和缓有神，继续调理而愈。\\n按：此症一派阳虚欲脱之象，辨之不难。难的是除炮姜一味外未用止血药，而以大剂附子扶阳为主，“血汗均已得止”，尽显火神派风格。":'He wanted to get out of the case of epistaxis\\nQin, male, 64 years old. Su has a lot of phlegm and dampness and has been coughing for many years. Yesterday, I suffered from shortness of breath due to coughing, sudden nosebleeds, and the injection of hemostatic injections was ineffective. I went to the emergency room at Yanwu Hospital with a pale complexion, persistent epistaxis, dripping cold sweat, lethargy, and weak breathing, as if dying. The tongue is pale and green with less blood color, and the pulse is soft and weak and wants to disperse, and stops after two or three times. It is diagnosed as qi deficiency, unable to absorb blood, yang deficiency, unable to maintain yin, and bleeding due to coughing and breaking of blood collaterals. The condition of the disease is quite critical, and there is a tendency for the yang energy to escape. If the blood and sweating can be stopped and there is still vitality, use Shenfu Decoction for first aid: 30g of aconite, 10g of ginseng, 6g of ginger, 3g of licorice, and 2 jujubes (burned black). \\nAfter taking one dose, the effect was effective, the bleeding was reduced, and the mood improved; after another dose, the sweating and sweating were stopped. Add 24g of astragalus and 60g of aconite to the original prescription. After taking 2 doses, the color of the lips and tongue has become rosy, and the pulse is gentle and energetic. Continue to regulate and the condition will heal. \\nNote: This disease is characterized by Yang deficiency and desire to escape, and it is not difficult to distinguish. The difficulty was that no hemostatic drugs were used except Paojiang, but a large dose of Aconite Fuzi was used to support Yang, and "the blood and sweat were stopped", which fully demonstrated the style of the Vulcan School.',"齿衄案 王某，男，32岁":"Teeth bleeding case Wang, male, 32 years old","齿衄案\\n王某，男，32岁。龈缝出血已久，牙床破烂，龈肉萎缩，齿摇松动，且痛而痒，屡服滋阴降火之品罔效。吴氏诊之，脉沉弱无力，舌质淡苔白滑，不思水饮。此系脾肾气虚，无力统摄血液以归其经。齿为骨之余属肾，肾气虚则齿枯而动摇；脾主肌肉，开窍于口，脾气虚而不能生养肌肉，则龈肉破烂而萎缩。气者，阳也；血者，阴也。阳气虚则阴不能潜藏而上浮，阴血失守而妄行于血脉之外。法当扶阳以镇阴，固气以摄血，俾阴阳调和则血自归经而不外溢矣。拟方潜阳封髓丹加黑姜、肉桂治之：\\n附子60g，砂仁20g（研），炮姜26g，肉桂10g（研末，泡水兑入），焦黄柏6g，炙甘草10g，龟甲13g（酥，打碎）。\\n服1剂稍效，3剂血全止，4剂后痛痒若失。连服10剂，牙肉已长丰满，诸症全瘳。\\n原按：附子、肉桂温补下焦命门真火，扶少火而生气；砂仁纳气归肾；龟甲、黄柏敛阴以潜阳；姜、草温中益脾，伏火互根，并能引血归经，故此方能治之而愈。余遇此等病症，屡治屡效。如见脉数饮冷，阴虚有热者，又须禁服也。":"Teeth bleeding case\\nWang, male, 32 years old. The gum line has been bleeding for a long time, the gums are tattered, the gums have atrophied, the teeth are loose, and the pain and itching occur. Repeated use of products that nourish yin and reduce fire have no effect. Wu's diagnosis showed that the pulse was weak and weak, the tongue was pale and had slippery coating, and he did not want to drink water. This is caused by spleen and kidney qi deficiency, which means that the blood cannot be absorbed and returned to its meridians. The teeth are bones and belong to the kidneys. If the kidney qi is deficient, the teeth will become dry and shaky. The spleen governs the muscles and opens the mouth. If the spleen is deficient and cannot grow muscles, the gums will be tattered and atrophied. Qi refers to Yang; blood refers to Yin. When Yang Qi is deficient, Yin cannot hide and floats up, and Yin blood loses control and travels outside the blood vessels. The method should support the yang to calm the yin, consolidate the qi to absorb the blood, and harmonize the yin and yang so that the blood will return to the meridians without overflowing. The proposed prescription is Qianyang Marrow Seal plus black ginger and cinnamon: 60g aconite, 20g amomum villosum (grind), 26g ginger, 10g cinnamon (grind, soak in water and mix), 6g burnt cypress, 10g burnt licorice, 13g tortoise shell (crisp, smash). \\nAfter taking 1 dose, it was slightly effective, and after 3 doses, the bleeding stopped completely. After 4 doses, the pain and itching disappeared. After taking 10 doses, the gums have grown plump and all symptoms have disappeared. \\nOriginal note: Aconite and cinnamon warm and tonify the real fire of the Jiao Ming Gate, supporting the less fire and energizing; Amomum villosum absorbs Qi and returns it to the kidney; Tortoise shell and Phellodendron astringe Yin to subdue Yang; Ginger and grass warm the spleen and subdue fire, and can lead blood to the menstruation, so it can be cured and cured. I have encountered this kind of disease, and it has been treated repeatedly with good results. If the pulse is rapid and the drink is cold, or there is heat due to yin deficiency, it is necessary to avoid taking it.","医案 {n}":"Cases {n}","著作 {n}":"Works {n}","共 {n} 卷":"Total {n} volumes","{a}。治以{b}，方用{c}。":"{a}. Treated with {b}, using {c}.","共 {n} 则医案":"Total {n} cases","本页收录“{d}”相关医案 {n} 则，逐案展示医案详情与医案来源。":'This page contains {n} cases related to "{d}", with details and sources shown case by case.',"医案 · {n}":"Case {n}","共 {n} 个病名":"Total {n} diseases","共 {n} 位名医":"Total {n} doctors","共找到 {n} 条与「{kw}」相关的{type}内容":'Found {n} results in {type} related to "{kw}"',"共 {n} 部著作":"Total {n} works","搜索病名、辨证、方剂、医家……":"Search disease, syndrome, formula, physician..."};export{e as default};
